#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "brush."
msgstr "scritch."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "planter with harvestable plant"
msgstr "jardinière contenant une plante prête à être récoltée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planter with harvestable plant"
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  This "
"one has a fully grown plant, and will need closer examination to harvest."
msgstr ""
"Une jardinière pleine de terre et bordée de lattes pour permettre un drainage "
"adéquat.  Celle-ci a une plante ayant fini son cycle de développement à "
"l'intérieur, examinez la jardinière pour la récolter."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "planter with mature plant"
msgstr "jardinière avec plante mature"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planter with mature plant"
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  This "
"one has a matured plant that should be ready for harvest before long."
msgstr ""
"Une jardinière pleine de terre et bordée de lattes pour permettre un drainage "
"adéquat.  Celle-ci a une plante mature poussant à l'intérieur qui devrait "
"être prête à être récoltée d’ici peu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "planter with seed"
msgstr "jardinière avec graines"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planter with seed"
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  This "
"one contains a planted seed, and will need attention to grow fully."
msgstr ""
"Une jardinière pleine de terre bordée de lattes pour permettre un drainage "
"adéquat.  Celle-ci contient une graine tout juste plantée et aura besoin "
"d’attention pour se développer pleinement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "planter with seedling"
msgstr "jardinière avec semis"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planter with seedling"
msgid ""
"A garden planter full of soil and slatted to allow adequate drainage.  This "
"one has a seed that has just begun to sprout its first roots."
msgstr ""
"Une jardinière pleine de terre bordée de lattes pour permettre un drainage "
"adéquat.  Celle-ci a une graine à l'intérieur qui vient tout juste de "
"commencer à germer ses premières racines."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "grain stook"
msgstr "crochets a grains"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "grain stook"
msgid ""
"Sheaves of cut grain have been stood upright in a self-supporting A-frame to "
"dry, keeping the seeds off the ground and out of reach of vermin."
msgstr ""
"Des gerbes de céréales coupées ont été placées debout dans un cadre en A "
"autoportant pour sécher, ce qui permet de garder les graines hors du sol et "
"hors de portée de la vermine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "stooking spot"
msgstr "Séchage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-domestic_plants.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stooking spot"
msgid ""
"A space has been cleared out here for grain drying.  Place fresh stalks of "
"grain in this spot and examine to set up a stook."
msgstr ""
"Un espace a été dégagé ici pour le séchage du grain. Placez des tiges de "
"céréales fraîches à cet endroit et examinez-les pour installer un séchoir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "spider egg sac"
msgstr "sac d’œufs d'araignée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spider egg sac"
msgid ""
"A sizable, off-white sac of large eggs.  Upon watching closer, you can see "
"them moving slightly.  Gross."
msgstr ""
"Un grand sac blanc grisâtre contenant de gros œufs.  En regardant de plus "
"près, vous pouvez les voir bouger légèrement.  Répugnant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spider egg sac"
msgid ""
"A bulbous mass of off-white spider eggs.  Upon watching closer, you can see "
"them moving a bit.  Really gross."
msgstr ""
"Une masse bulbeuse d’œufs d’araignée blanc grisâtre.  En regardant de plus "
"près, vous pouvez les voir bouger un peu.  C'est vraiment répugnant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spider egg sac"
msgid ""
"A gigantic sac of spider eggs, each one larger than your fist.  They're "
"definitely moving around.  Really gross, just seeing it makes your skin crawl."
msgstr ""
"Un gigantesque sac d’œufs d’araignée, chacun plus gros que votre poing.  Ils "
"bougent de façon perceptible.  C'est vraiment dégoûtant et le simple fait "
"d'observer ça vous donne la chair de poule."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ruptured egg sac"
msgstr "sac d’œufs d'araignée rompu"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-eggs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ruptured egg sac"
msgid ""
"A disgusting, ruptured sac of giant spider eggs.  The thought of all those "
"massive baby spiders pouring out of it is almost terrifying on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un sac dégoûtant et déchiré d’œufs d’araignée géante.  L’idée d'une vague "
"d'araignées énormes en ayant émergé est terrifiante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "swamp gas"
msgid "A pool of murky water that occasionally bubbles, releasing a mildly toxic gas."
msgstr ""
"Une mare d'eau trouble qui bouillonne occasionnellement, libérant un gaz "
"légèrement toxique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fog"
msgid "A misty cloud of fog."
msgstr "Un nuage brumeux de brouillard."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal grate"
msgstr "grille en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal grate"
msgid "A metal vent.  You can feel cool air seeping out of it."
msgstr ""
"Un conduit d'aération en métal. Vous pouvez ressentir de l'air froid s'en "
"échapper lentement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_cold_air2_blast"
msgid "A metal vent.  You can feel cold air blasting out of it."
msgstr ""
"Un conduit d'aération en métal. Vous pouvez ressentir des bourrasques d'air "
"froid s'en échapper."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_hot_air2_stream"
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_hot_air2_blast"
msgid "A metal vent.  You can feel hot air seeping out of it."
msgstr ""
"Un conduit d'aération en métal. Vous pouvez ressentir de l'air chaud s'en "
"échapper lentement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_toxic_leak"
msgid "A metal vent.  Toxic-looking clouds seep from it."
msgstr ""
"Un conduit d'aération en métal, vous observez des nuages de gaz ayant l'air "
"toxiques s'en échapper en petite bouffées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_toxic_belch"
msgid "A metal vent.  Toxic-looking clouds stream from it."
msgstr ""
"Un conduit d'aération en métal, vous observez des nuages de gaz ayant l'air "
"toxiques s'en déverser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_vent_rad_leak"
msgid "A metal vent."
msgstr "Une bouche d'aération en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-emitters.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_fog_breather"
msgid "A misty cloud of water vapor."
msgstr "Un nuage brumeux de vapeur d'eau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fakes.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ground crafting spot"
msgstr "espace d'artisanat"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fakes.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ground crafting spot"
msgid ""
"A cleared spot on the ground for crafting.  Slower than using a workbench or "
"holding a project in your hands, but readily available."
msgstr ""
"Un espace dégagé sur le sol pour bricoler. Plus lent que d'utiliser un établi "
"ou de tenir un projet dans vos mains, mais facilement accessible."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fireplace"
msgstr "cheminée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fireplace"
#. ~ Description of furniture "stone fireplace"
msgid ""
"A common fixture for safely hosting a fire indoors, with a chimney to vent "
"the smoke to the outside."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil courant pour allumer un feu en toute sécurité à l'intérieur, avec "
"une cheminée pour évacuer la fumée vers l'extérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "stone fireplace"
msgstr "cheminée en pierre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wood stove"
msgstr "poêle à bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wood stove"
msgid ""
"A simple metal stove for hosting wood-fueled fires.  Good for cooking or "
"heating food, and safe to use indoors."
msgstr ""
"Un simple poêle en métal pour des feux de bois.  Idéale pour cuisiner ou "
"réchauffer des aliments et peut être utilisé à l'intérieur sans problèmes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "brazier"
msgid_plural "braziers"
msgstr[0] "brasero"
msgstr[1] "braseros"
msgstr[2] "braseros"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "brazier"
msgid "A raised metal dish in which to safely burn things."
msgstr "Un plat métallique surélevé pour y brûler des objets en toute sécurité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "makeshift brazier"
msgid_plural "makeshift braziers"
msgstr[0] "brasero improvisé"
msgstr[1] "braseros improvisés"
msgstr[2] "braseros improvisés"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "makeshift brazier"
msgid ""
"A metal bucket with holes, in which you can safely start a fire.  It's too "
"small to fit any fuel item larger than some splintered wood."
msgstr ""
"Un seau en métal avec des trous à l'intérieur duquel vous pouvez allumer un "
"feu en sécurité.  Malheureusement les trous sont trop petits pour accepter "
"quoi que ce soit de plus large que des morceaux de bois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hobo stove"
msgid_plural "hobo stoves"
msgstr[0] "réchaud de clochard"
msgstr[1] "réchauds de clochard"
msgstr[2] "réchauds de clochard"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hobo stove"
msgid ""
"A small improvised wood stove, made from a metal can.  It's too small to fit "
"any fuel much larger than splintered wood."
msgstr ""
"Un petit poêle à bois improvisé, fabriqué à partir d'une boîte de conserve en "
"métal.  Trop petit pour contenir un combustible beaucoup plus gros que des "
"éclats de bois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "portable stove"
msgid_plural "portable stoves"
msgstr[0] "réchaud portable"
msgstr[1] "réchauds portables"
msgstr[2] "réchauds portables"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "portable stove"
msgid ""
"A foldable metal stove for hosting wood-fueled fires.  Good for cooking or "
"heating food, and safe to use indoors."
msgstr ""
"Un poêle pliable en métal pour accueillir des feux alimentés au bois. Idéal "
"pour cuisiner ou réchauffer des aliments, et peut être utilisé en toute "
"sécurité à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fire barrel (200 L)"
msgid_plural "fire barrels (200 L)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fire barrel (200 L)"
msgid ""
"A huge metal barrel used to safely contain a fire.  It has multiple holes "
"punched in the sides for air supply."
msgstr ""
"Un énorme tonneau en métal utilisé pour contenir un incendie en toute "
"sécurité. Il est doté de plusieurs trous percés sur les côtés pour "
"l'alimentation en air."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fire barrel (100 L)"
msgid_plural "fire barrels (100 L)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fire barrel (100 L)"
msgid ""
"A large metal barrel used to safely contain a fire.  It has multiple holes "
"punched in the sides for air supply."
msgstr ""
"Un grand tonneau en métal utilisé pour contenir un incendie en toute "
"sécurité. Il est doté de plusieurs trous percés sur les côtés pour "
"l'alimentation en air."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fire ring"
msgstr "anneau de feu"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fire ring"
msgid "A ring of stones to safely contain a fire."
msgstr "Un cercle de pierres pouvant contenir un feu en toute sécurité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "clay oven"
msgstr "four en terre cuite"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fireplaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "clay oven"
msgid ""
"A simple clay oven with a chimney, with a firebrick alcove in the middle that "
"can be used to cook food or just to contain a fire."
msgstr ""
"Un simple four en terre cuite doté d'une cheminée, avec une alcôve en briques "
"réfractaires au milieu qui peut être utilisée pour cuire des aliments ou "
"simplement pour contenir un feu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mutated poppy flower"
msgstr "fleur de pavot mutante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mutated poppy flower"
msgid ""
"These strange flowers have appeared in the wake of the Cataclysm, and their "
"buds can be used for medicinal purposes, like the buds of the mundane poppy "
"they're named after.  The dirt around it gently churns as its roots writhe "
"beneath the soil, and it's surrounded by an overwhelming floral smell that "
"makes you feel sleepy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dandelion"
msgid_plural "dandelion"
msgstr[0] "pissenlits"
msgstr[1] "pissenlits"
msgstr[2] "pissenlits"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dandelion"
msgid ""
"A common weed with a yellow flower.  Produces seeds that get carried on the "
"wind by thin, gray filaments."
msgstr ""
"Une mauvaise herbe commune avec une fleur jaune.  Produit des graines qui "
"sont transportées par le vent par de fins filaments gris."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "burdock"
msgid_plural "burdock"
msgstr[0] "bardane"
msgstr[1] "bardane"
msgstr[2] "bardane"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "burdock"
msgid ""
"A common weed with a purple thistle-like flower.  Its seeds tend to stick to "
"clothing and fur."
msgstr ""
"Mauvaise herbe commune avec une fleur violette ressemblant à un chardon.  Ses "
"graines ont tendance à coller aux vêtements et à la fourrure."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wild carrot"
msgstr "carottes sauvages"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wild carrot"
msgid "A common white wildflower which could be harvested for its root."
msgstr "Une fleur sauvage blanche commune pouvant être récoltée pour sa racine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "starry false Solomon's seal"
msgstr "maïanthème étoilé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "starry false Solomon's seal"
msgid ""
"The blossoms of this flower look like stars in the night sky.  Its crimson "
"berries are edible."
msgstr ""
"Les fleurs de cette plante ressemblent à des étoiles dans le ciel nocturne.  "
"Ses baies pourpres sont comestibles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "salsify"
msgstr "salsifis"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "salsify"
msgid "Tragopogon porrifolius, a ragged-looking purple flower with a nutritious root."
msgstr ""
"Tragopogon porrifolius, une fleur violette à l'apparence effilochée possédant "
"une racine nutritive."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chamomile"
msgstr "Camomille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chamomile"
msgid "A cute white flower with a yellow center, used to brew a soothing tea."
msgstr ""
"Une jolie fleur blanche au centre jaune pouvant être utilisée pour préparer "
"un thé apaisant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tulip"
msgstr "tulipe"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tulip"
msgid ""
"A bright, colorful flower with petals forming a small cup at its top.  It can "
"be poisonous to livestock."
msgstr ""
"Une fleur lumineuse et colorée avec des pétales formant une petite coupe à "
"son sommet.  Peut être toxique pour le bétail."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "spurge flower"
msgstr "fleur d'euphorbe"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spurge flower"
msgid "A yellow-green flower that grows in densely-packed bushes."
msgstr "Une fleur jaune-vert qui pousse dans des buissons denses."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cattails"
msgstr "quenouilles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cattails"
msgid ""
"This useful plant is available all year round.  Many parts of the plant are "
"edible."
msgstr ""
"Cette plante utile est pousse toute l’année et nombreuses sections de la "
"plante sont comestibles ou peuvent être utilisées d'autres façons."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black eyed Susan"
msgstr "Susan aux yeux noirs"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black eyed Susan"
msgid ""
"A mildly poisonous yellow flower with a dark ball in the middle.  Sometimes "
"known as an ox-eye daisy."
msgstr "Une fleur jaune légèrement vénéneuse avec une boule sombre au milieu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "lily"
msgstr "lys"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "lily"
msgid "A pretty flower that comes in a variety of colors."
msgstr "Une jolie fleur ayant une multitude de variétés de différentes couleurs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "lotus"
msgstr "lotus"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "lotus"
msgid ""
"A lovely flower that grows on the surface of bodies of fresh water.  A "
"traditional symbol of many Eastern cultures."
msgstr ""
"Une jolie fleur qui pousse à la surface des plans d’eau douce.  Un symbole "
"traditionnel de nombreuses cultures orientales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sunflower"
msgid_plural "sunflowers"
msgstr[0] "tournesol"
msgstr[1] "tournesols"
msgstr[2] "tournesols"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sunflower"
msgid ""
"A tall, wide-headed flower with a large dark center.  Produces many "
"nutritious seeds."
msgstr ""
"Une grande fleur à tête large avec un grand centre sombre.  Produit de "
"nombreuses graines nutritives."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Jerusalem artichoke plant"
msgstr "topinambour"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Jerusalem artichoke plant"
msgid "Looking similar to a sunflower, this tall plant has a nutritious tuber."
msgstr "Ressemble à un tournesol, une grande plante possèdant un tubercule nutritif."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "lilypad"
msgstr "nénuphar"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "lilypad"
msgid ""
"This lilypad doesn't look like it would support the weight of the things "
"you've heard croaking in the swamp."
msgstr ""
"Ce nénuphar n'a pas l'air de pouvoir supporter le poids des choses que vous "
"avez entendues coasser dans le marais."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bluebell"
msgstr "jacinthe des bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bluebell"
msgid "A common bluebell flower.  Pretty."
msgstr "Une jolie jacinthe des bois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dahlia"
msgstr "dahlia"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dahlia"
msgid "A puffy flower with many tightly-layered petals."
msgstr "Une fleur gonflée avec de nombreux pétales étroitement superposés."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chicory"
msgstr "chicorée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chicory"
msgid "A blue flower imported from Europe, also known as a cornflower."
msgstr "Une fleur bleue importée d’Europe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "datura"
msgstr "datura"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "datura"
msgid "A pretty moonflower."
msgstr "Une jolie fleur de lune."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of leaves"
msgstr "tas de feuilles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of leaves"
msgid ""
"A sizable pile of leaves.  You could sleep on it if you don't care about "
"comfort or warmth."
msgstr ""
"Un gros tas de feuilles.  Vous pourriez dormir dessus si vous ne vous souciez "
"pas du confort ou de la chaleur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mustard"
msgstr "moutarde"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mustard"
msgid ""
"A yellow flower known as Brassica Nigra.  Known for its seeds that can be "
"used for making table mustard."
msgstr ""
"Une fleur jaune connue sous le nom de Brassica Nigra.  Connue pour ses "
"graines pouvant être utilisées pour fabriquer de la moutarde de table."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wild sarsaparilla"
msgstr "sarsaparilla sauvage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wild sarsaparilla"
msgid ""
"A small, flowering plant known as 'Aralia nudicaulis'.  It is colored in "
"vibrant shades of orange and red in autumn, making it easy to spot."
msgstr ""
"Une petite plante à fleurs connue sous le nom d'Aralia nudicaulis.  Elle est "
"colorée dans des tons vibrants d’orange et de rouge en automne, ce qui la "
"rend facile à repérer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wintergreen"
msgstr "gaulthérie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wintergreen"
msgid ""
"A small shrub native to North America.  The leaves, which remain green even "
"in winter, are valued for medicinal purposes.  It produces edible and sweet "
"berries, too!"
msgstr ""
"Un petit arbuste originaire d'Amérique du Nord.  Les feuilles, qui restent "
"vertes même en hiver, sont appréciées pour leur utilité médicinale.  Produit "
"également des baies comestibles et sucrées!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Japanese knotweed"
msgstr "renouée du Japon"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Japanese knotweed"
msgid ""
"An invasive species originating from Japan.  The stem looks like it might "
"contain some water."
msgstr ""
"Une espèce envahissante originaire du Japon.  La tige semble contenir de "
"l’eau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fireweed"
msgstr "épilobe"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fireweed"
msgid ""
"Vibrant purple, it tends to be the first to appear after fires, hence its "
"name."
msgstr ""
"Une herbe d'un violet vibrant, elle a tendance à être la première à "
"apparaître après les incendies."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "common selfheal"
msgstr "brunelle commune"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "common selfheal"
msgid ""
"A small purple flower.  It got its name due to its usage in traditional "
"medicine."
msgstr ""
"Une petite fleur violette.  Elle tire son nom de son utilisation dans la "
"médecine traditionnelle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "spreading dogbane"
msgstr "apocyn à feuilles d'androsème"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spreading dogbane"
msgid ""
"It is not only toxic to dogs when eaten by them.  Humans and many other "
"animals are affected, too.  Its fibers sure are worth salvaging though.  "
"Despite its name, it is not actually spreading fast."
msgstr ""
"Ce n’est pas seulement toxique pour les chiens lorsqu’ils la mangent.  Les "
"humains et de nombreux autres animaux sont également susceptibles.  Ses "
"fibres valent certainement la peine d’être récupérées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "thistle"
msgstr "chardon"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "thistle"
msgid "A prickly and invasive small plant."
msgstr "Une mauvaise herbe épineuse et invasive."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "purple loosestrife"
msgstr "salicaire pourpre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "purple loosestrife"
msgid ""
"A pretty violet flower that likes water.  Unfortunately it is invasive and "
"does not benefit the environment."
msgstr ""
"Une jolie fleur violette qui aime l'eau.  Malheureusement, elle est "
"envahissante et n'est pas bénéfique à l'environnement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_grain.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wild rice"
msgid_plural "wild rice"
msgstr[0] "riz sauvage"
msgstr[1] "riz sauvage"
msgstr[2] "riz sauvage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wild rice"
msgid ""
"Also called Indian rice, Northern wild rice, or manoomin in Ojibwe, is a "
"species of rice that has been harvested and used by Native American tribes of "
"the northeast for hundreds of years.  It's similar to other types of wild "
"rice, offering a fiber-rich and healthy basis of a meal."
msgstr ""
"Également appelé riz indien, riz sauvage du Nord ou manoomin en ojibwé, c'est "
"une espèce de riz récoltée et utilisée par les tribus amérindiennes du "
"nord-est depuis des centaines d'années. Il est similaire aux autres types de "
"riz sauvage, offrant une base de repas riche en fibres et saine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "short hedge"
msgstr "haie courte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "short hedge"
msgid "A shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a squared shape."
msgstr "Une haie basse ayant été taillée jusqu'à atteindre une forme rectangulaire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tall hedge"
msgstr "haute haie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tall hedge"
msgid ""
"A tall shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a squared shape.  You "
"can't see past this thick hedgerow."
msgstr ""
"Une haie haute et épaisse ayant été taillée jusqu'à atteindre une forme "
"rectangulaire. Vous êtes incapable de voir à travers ou au dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "abstract topiary"
msgstr "topiaire abstrait"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "abstract topiary"
msgid "A tall shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a fanciful abstract shape."
msgstr ""
"Un haut buisson possédant des petites feuilles vertes ayant été taillé en une "
"forme abstraite et artistique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "animal topiary"
msgstr "topiaire animalistique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "animal topiary"
msgid "A tall shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into an animal shape."
msgstr "Un grand arbuste avec des petites feuilles vertes, taillé en forme d'animal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "animal topiary"
msgid "A tall shrub with small green leaves, trimmed into a dragon shape."
msgstr "Un grand arbuste avec des petites feuilles vertes, taillé en forme de dragon."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dam"
msgstr "barrage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/misc.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dam"
msgid ""
"A house that beavers built.  The entrance is underwater making it harder for "
"predators to access."
msgstr ""
"Une structure construite par des castors.  L'entrée est sous l'eau, rendant "
"l'accès plus difficile aux prédateurs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/misc.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "bonk."
msgstr "bonk."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "red algae"
msgstr "algues rouges"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "red algae"
msgid ""
"One of the thousands of species of grassy reddish marine plants that inhabit "
"intertidal zones the world over.  Its rubbery little fronds don't look "
"particularly edible."
msgstr ""
"L'une des milliers d'espèces de plantes marines herbeuses rougeâtres qui "
"peuplent les zones intertidales du monde entier. Ses petites frondes "
"caoutchouteuses ne semblent pas particulièrement comestibles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "splat."
msgstr "splat."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "squelch."
msgstr "squelch."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "green algae"
msgstr "algues vertes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "green algae"
msgid "A short patch of grassy green seaweed, wholly unremarkable."
msgstr "Une petite étendue d'algues vertes herbeuses, tout à fait banale."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sugar kelp"
msgid_plural "sugar kelp"
msgstr[0] "laminaire sucrée"
msgstr[1] "laminaire sucrée"
msgstr[2] "laminaire sucrée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sugar kelp"
msgid ""
"Also known as kombu, this brown algae grows in a single leaflike blade that "
"can reach more than twice the height of a man.  Young fronds make for "
"excellent soup stock and can even be eaten raw."
msgstr ""
"Également connue sous le nom de kombu, cette algue brune pousse en une seule "
"feuille pouvant atteindre plus de deux fois la taille d'un homme. Les jeunes "
"frondes constituent un excellent bouillon de soupe et peuvent même être "
"consommées crues."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sea lettuce"
msgid_plural "sea lettuce"
msgstr[0] "laitues de mer"
msgstr[1] "laitues de mer"
msgstr[2] "laitues de mer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sea lettuce"
msgid ""
"Sometimes known as green laver, this leafy algae from the Ulva genus grows in "
"leafy little patches around shallows and tide pools.  Though small, it makes "
"a tasty snack."
msgstr ""
"Parfois appelée algue verte, cette algue feuillue du genre Ulva pousse en "
"petites touffes feuillées autour des eaux peu profondes et des bassins de "
"marée. Bien que petite, elle constitue une collation savoureuse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bladderwrack"
msgid_plural "bladderwrack"
msgstr[0] "fucus"
msgstr[1] "fucus"
msgstr[2] "fucus"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bladderwrack"
msgid ""
"Named for the air bladders that grow all over its leafy fronds, this leafy "
"seaweed is technically edible and has a long history of use in folk medicine."
msgstr ""
"Nommée d'après les vessies d'air qui poussent partout sur ses frondes "
"feuillées, cette algue feuillue est techniquement comestible et a une longue "
"histoire d'utilisation en médecine populaire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sea anemone"
msgstr "anémone de mer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sea anemone"
msgid ""
"This sessile polyp waves its stinging tentacles with the motion of the tides, "
"hoping to capture a tiny fish or crab.  It's wholly inedible and poses no "
"danger to anything bigger than a shrimp."
msgstr ""
"Ce polype sessile agite ses tentacules urticants au gré des marées, dans "
"l'espoir de capturer un minuscule poisson ou un crabe. Il est totalement "
"immangeable et ne présente aucun danger pour les animaux plus gros qu'une "
"crevette."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sea sponge"
msgstr "éponge de mer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-flora_marine.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sea sponge"
msgid ""
"An immobile, lumpy little creature that looks nothing like a square kitchen "
"sponge.  Anchored to the sea floor, its porous body passively filters "
"plankton from the water that freely passes through it."
msgstr ""
"Une petite créature immobile et bosselée qui ne ressemble en rien à une "
"éponge de cuisine carrée. Ancrée au fond de la mer, son corps poreux filtre "
"passivement le plancton de l'eau qui le traverse librement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Marloss flower"
msgstr "fleur de Marloss"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Marloss flower"
msgid ""
"This flower looks mostly like the other flowers taken by the mushrooms, but "
"its bulb is a brilliant cyan color.  It emits an aroma that is both "
"overwhelming and strangely alluring."
msgstr ""
"Cette fleur ressemble beaucoup aux autres fleurs capturées par les "
"champignons, mais son bulbe est d'une couleur cyan brillante. Il dégage un "
"arôme à la fois envoûtant et étrangement séduisant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "poof."
msgstr "pouf."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fungal flower"
msgstr "fleur mycellaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fungal flower"
msgid ""
"This flower has been overgrown by gray, sinewy tendrils of fungus, and the "
"color has been leached from its petals and stem.  It gently sways of its own "
"volition, maintaining an unsettling rhythm."
msgstr ""
"Cette fleur est recouverte d'un réseau de filament mycellaires gris, et les "
"couleurs de ses pétales et de sa tige ont été asséchées.  Elle gigote "
"doucement de sa propre volonté, maintenant un rythme qui vous perturbe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fungal mass"
msgstr "masse fongique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fungal mass"
msgid ""
"Thick ropes of Mycal matter have covered the ground here completely.  It's "
"soft to the touch, but not firm enough to hold any weight."
msgstr ""
"D'épaisses cordes de matière Mycal ont entièrement recouvert le sol. C'est "
"doux au toucher, mais pas assez ferme pour supporter un poids quelconque."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fungal clump"
msgstr "touffe fongique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fungal clump"
msgid ""
"Alien mold and stems mingle tightly here, swaying around and weaving "
"together, creating a sort of fungal bush."
msgstr ""
"De la moisissure étrange et des tiges sont étroitement liées ici, se "
"balançant doucement et tissant ensemble une sorte de buisson fongique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fungal tangle"
msgstr "enchevêtrement fongique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-fungal.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fungal tangle"
msgid ""
"Thick, ropy tendrils of fungus have risen from the ground and gathered into "
"an impenetrable clump."
msgstr ""
"D'épaisses vrilles de champignons se sont élevées du sol et se sont "
"rassemblées en une touffe impénétrable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "stone slab"
msgstr "Dalle de pierre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stone slab"
msgid "A slab of heavy stone, with a reasonably flat surface."
msgstr "Une dalle de pierre lourde dotée d'une surface raisonnablement plate."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "headstone"
msgstr "stèle funéraire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "headstone"
msgid ""
"A large slab of stone, engraved with information on the deceased individual "
"buried beneath.  While only a solemn reminder of the uncountable losses of "
"the Cataclysm, a proper final resting place grants an odd sense of peace."
msgstr ""
"Une grande dalle de pierre, gravée d'informations sur la personne décédée "
"enterrée en dessous.  Bien qu'il ne s'agisse que d'un rappel solennel des "
"innombrables pertes du Cataclysme, un lieu de repos final approprié confère "
"un étrange sentiment de paix."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gravestone"
msgstr "pierre tombale"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gravestone"
msgid ""
"An upright slab of stone with information engraved on the face about whoever "
"lies beneath.  While only a solemn reminder of the countless casualties of "
"the Cataclysm, a proper final resting place grants an odd sense of peace."
msgstr ""
"Une dalle de pierre verticale avec des informations gravées sur l'une des "
"faces concernant la personne enterrée en dessous.  Bien qu'il ne s'agisse que "
"d'un rappel solennel des innombrables victimes du Cataclysme, un lieu de "
"repos convenable vous confère un étrange sentiment de paix."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "worn gravestone"
msgstr "pierre tombale usée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "worn gravestone"
msgid ""
"An aged and eroded gravestone, damaged to the point of rendering the "
"inscription illegible.  Whoever's buried here was probably lucky enough to "
"pass before all this chaos began."
msgstr ""
"Une pierre tombale vieillie et érodée, endommagée au point de rendre "
"l'inscription illisible.  Peu importe qui est enterré ici, il ont "
"probablement eu la chance de mourir avant que tout ce chaos ne commence."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "obelisk"
msgstr "obélisque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "obelisk"
msgid ""
"A magnificent carved statue with an engraved plaque fixed to the base.  It "
"serves to honor the passing of somebody significant, something one wishes was "
"still a practical goal."
msgstr ""
"Une magnifique statue sculptée avec une plaque gravée fixée au socle.  Elle "
"sert à honorer le décès d’une personne importante, et vous souhaiteriez que "
"ce genre de chose soit encore pratique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "thunk!"
msgstr "thunk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "battlefield cross"
msgstr "croix de champ de bataille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "battlefield cross"
msgid ""
"A makeshift memorial marker, made of a service rifle - buried in the dirt, or "
"nestled in a pair of boots - with a helmet perched on the stock.  A small way "
"to honor the dead."
msgstr ""
"Un monument commémoratif improvisé, constitué d'un fusil de service - enfoui "
"dans la terre ou niché dans une paire de bottes - avec un casque perché sur "
"la crosse.  Une façon d'honorer les morts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-graves.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_treesung.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "whack."
msgstr "whack."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chemical mixer"
msgstr "mixeur de produits chimiques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chemical mixer"
msgid ""
"A large vat with a motorized mixing device for combining large quantities of "
"chemicals."
msgstr ""
"Une grande cuve avec un mélangeur motorisé pour combiner de grandes quantités "
"de produits chimiques."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken generator"
msgstr "générateur cassé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken generator"
msgid "This generator is broken and will not help you produce usable electricity."
msgstr "Ce générateur est en panne et ne vous aidera pas à produire de l'électricité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Compact Advanced Sterling Radioisotope Generator"
msgstr "Générateur de radio-isotopes compact et avancé Sterling"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Compact Advanced Sterling Radioisotope
#. Generator"
msgid ""
"This hefty lump of steel and lead is the housing unit for a Stirling "
"generator powered by plutonium-238, originally designed by NASA and "
"repurposed by the military.  It is plastered with warning signs.  It's really "
"heavy owing to the thick armor plating, but you could take this down and use "
"it for your own purposes if you wanted."
msgstr ""
"Ce gros morceau d'acier et de plomb abrite un générateur Stirling alimenté au "
"plutonium 238, conçu à l'origine par la NASA et réutilisé par l'armée. Il est "
"recouvert de panneaux d'avertissement. Il est très lourd en raison de son "
"blindage épais, mais vous pouvez le démonter et l'utiliser à vos propres fins "
"si vous le souhaitez."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mobile antenna"
msgstr "antenne mobile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mobile antenna"
msgid ""
"A stark black directional antenna, seemingly part of a monitoring setup.  An "
"LED mounted on its back lights up with a lazy and irregular rhythm."
msgstr ""
"Une antenne directionnelle noire austère, qui semble faire partie d'un "
"dispositif de surveillance. Une LED montée à l'arrière s'allume avec un "
"rythme lent et irrégulier."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "light machinery"
msgstr "machines légères"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "light machinery"
msgid "Assorted light machinery.  You could scavenge it for parts."
msgstr ""
"Un assortiment de machines légères.  Vous pourriez en récupérer pour des "
"pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "heavy machinery"
msgstr "machines lourdes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy machinery"
msgid "Assorted heavy machinery.  You could scavenge it for parts."
msgstr "Un assortiment de machines lourdes.  Vous pourriez en récupérer des pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "old machinery"
msgstr "vieilles machines"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "old machinery"
msgid "Assorted old, rusty machinery.  You could scavenge it for parts."
msgstr ""
"Un assortiment de vieilles machines rouillées.  Vous pourriez en récupérer "
"des pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "electronic machinery"
msgstr "machines électriques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "electronic machinery"
msgid "Assorted electronic machinery.  You could scavenge it for parts."
msgstr ""
"Un assortiment de machines électroniques.  Vous pourriez en récupérer des "
"pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/funiture_heavy_industry.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "robotic arm"
msgstr "bras robotisé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/funiture_heavy_industry.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "robotic arm"
msgid ""
"An automated robotic arm used in assembly lines, which appears to be more "
"general-purpose than specially designed assemblers.  Despite being "
"functionless now, the parts could be useful."
msgstr ""
"Un bras robotique automatisé utilisé dans les chaînes de montage, qui semble "
"être plus polyvalent que les assembleurs spécialement conçus.  Même si cette "
"installation est ruinée, ceci pourrait avoir des pièces utiles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/funiture_heavy_industry.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "thunk."
msgstr "thunk."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ground cable"
msgstr "câble de terre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ground cable"
msgid "A bunch of loose cables snake along the floor."
msgstr "Un tas de câbles lâches serpentant au sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "shred!"
msgstr "shrraapp!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "thud!"
msgstr "bam!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "electrical conduit"
msgstr "conduit électrique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "electrical conduit"
msgid "A thick bundle of electrical wiring protected by a metal conduit."
msgstr "Un épais faisceau de câbles électriques protégé par un conduit métallique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "capacitor bank"
msgstr "batterie de condensateurs"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "capacitor bank"
msgid "A bank of heavy metal cylinders connected by large wires."
msgstr "Une banque de cylindres en métal lourd reliés par de gros fils."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/part_items.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/vehicles/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "control station"
msgid_plural "control stations"
msgstr[0] "poste de contrôle"
msgstr[1] "postes de contrôle "
msgstr[2] "postes de contrôle "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "control station"
msgid "Assorted electronic interfaces and screens.  You could scavenge it for parts."
msgstr ""
"Un assortiment d'interfaces et écrans divers.  Vous pourriez désassembler "
"cela pour des pièces d'électronique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nuclear fuel cell"
msgstr "cellule à combustible nucléaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-industrial.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nuclear fuel cell"
msgid ""
"This fuel assembly consists of cylindrical rods put into bundles.  A uranium "
"oxide ceramic is formed into pellets and inserted into Zircaloy tubes that "
"are bundled together.  The Zircaloy tubes are pressurized with helium to "
"minimize pellet-cladding interaction which can lead to fuel rod failure over "
"long periods.  This fuel cell is used in nuclear power stations to produce "
"heat to power turbines."
msgstr ""
"Cet assemblage combustible est constitué de crayons cylindriques disposés en "
"faisceaux. Une céramique d'oxyde d'uranium est formée en pastilles et insérée "
"dans des tubes en zircaloy regroupés. Les tubes en zircaloy sont pressurisés "
"à l'hélium pour minimiser l'interaction pastilles-gaine qui peut conduire à "
"une défaillance des crayons combustibles sur de longues périodes. Cette pile "
"à combustible est utilisée dans les centrales nucléaires pour produire de la "
"chaleur pour alimenter les turbines."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Autodoc Mk. XI"
msgstr "Autodoc Mk. XI"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Autodoc Mk. XI"
msgid ""
"A surgical apparatus used for the installation and removal of bionics.  The "
"term name 'Autodoc' is something of a misnomer, as it can only operate if "
"programmed beforehand, something that a plethora of labels warn against doing "
"without expertise."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil chirurgical utilisé pour l'installation et le retrait de "
"dispositifs bioniques. Le terme « Autodoc » est quelque peu impropre, car il "
"ne peut fonctionner que s'il a été programmé au préalable, ce qu'une "
"multitude d'étiquettes déconseillent de faire sans expertise."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Autodoc operation couch"
msgstr "bloc opératoire d'Autodoc"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Autodoc operation couch"
msgid ""
"A plush red sofa made less comfortable by the medical machinery directly "
"above it.  It has a single leather strap on the right armrest."
msgstr ""
"Un canapé rouge moelleux rendu moins confortable par les appareils médicaux "
"situés juste au-dessus. Il est doté d'une seule sangle en cuir sur "
"l'accoudoir droit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "autoclave"
msgstr "autoclave"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "autoclave"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled autoclave"
msgid ""
"A device that can steam its contents at high enough temperatures to "
"completely sterilize them, killing any possible contaminants."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil capable de chauffer les choses placées à l'intérieur à des "
"températures suffisamment élevées pour les stériliser complètement, éliminant "
"ainsi tout contaminant possible."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled autoclave"
msgstr "autoclave remplie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sample freezer"
msgstr "congélateur à échantillons"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sample freezer"
msgid ""
"A specialized freezer capable of maintaining temperatures of -80 Celsius, "
"best used for the preservation of delicate scientific samples."
msgstr ""
"Un congélateur spécialisé capable de maintenir des températures de -80 °C, "
"idéal pour la conservation d'échantillons scientifiques délicats."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "lab workbench"
msgstr "établi de laboratoire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "lab workbench"
msgid ""
"A metal storage cabinet topped with a durable resin countertop resistant to "
"most chemical spills and burns.  It has wired-in electrical and gas fittings."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire de rangement en métal surmontée d'un comptoir en résine durable "
"résistant à la plupart des déversements de produits chimiques et des "
"brûlures.  Elle dispose de raccords pour des câbles électriques et de la "
"tuyauterie à gaz."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fume hood"
msgstr "hotte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fume hood"
msgid ""
"A metal hood atop a lab workspace, with durable glass shutters.  A fan in the "
"hood draws fumes and smoke from dangerous chemicals up into a ventilation "
"duct."
msgstr ""
"Une hotte en métal au-dessus d'un espace de travail de laboratoire, avec des "
"volets en verre durables.  Un ventilateur dans la hotte aspire les vapeurs et "
"la fumée des produits chimiques dangereux vers un conduit de ventilation.  "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "shaker incubator"
msgstr "agitateur incubateur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "shaker incubator"
msgid ""
"A tool for keeping chemical broth nicely mixed and at just the right "
"temperature to grow bacteria.  Although more bacteria is probably the last "
"thing you need, considering the circumstances."
msgstr ""
"Un outil pour garder le bouillon chimique bien mélangé et à la bonne "
"température pour développer des bactéries.  Bien que davantage de bactéries "
"soient probablement la dernière chose dont vous avez besoin, compte tenu des "
"circonstances."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "emergency wash station"
msgstr "douches oculaires d'urgence"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "emergency wash station"
msgid ""
"A standing sink with a pair of nozzles, along with a large, brightly-colored "
"handle.  It is specially designed to quickly remove contaminants from the "
"eyes, and is easily usable without being able to see very well.  A sizable "
"notice warns against drinking the water it uses."
msgstr ""
"Un évier sur pied avec une paire de buses et une grande poignée aux couleurs "
"vives.  Spécialement conçu pour éliminer rapidement les contaminants des yeux "
"et aisément utilisable sans pouvoir très bien voir.  Une plaque de couleur "
"similairement vive met en garde contre la consommation de l'eau qu'il utilise."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "IV pole"
msgstr "Poteau à perfusion"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "IV pole"
msgid ""
"A tall wire frame on a set of small wheels used for holding an IV bag, useful "
"for unattended administration."
msgstr ""
"Un grand cadre métallique sur un ensemble de petites roues utilisé pour "
"maintenir un sac IV, utile pour une administration sans surveillance."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "high performance liquid chromatographer"
msgstr "appareil de chromatographie liquide à haute performance "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "high performance liquid chromatographer"
#. ~ Description of furniture "high-performance liquid chromatographer"
msgid ""
"This high-tech tool would, with electricity and an experienced user, be a "
"very useful way to separate chemicals in a liquid or aqueous phase, based on "
"their affinity, to the stationary phase in a tube.  At least, that's what the "
"label says."
msgstr ""
"Cet outil de haute technologie pourrait, avec de l'électricité et un "
"utilisateur expérimenté, constituer un moyen très utile de séparer les "
"produits chimiques en phase liquide ou aqueuse, en fonction de leur affinité, "
"de la phase stationnaire dans un tube. Du moins, c'est ce que dit l'étiquette."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "gas chromatographer"
msgstr "chromatographe à gaz"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gas chromatographer"
msgid ""
"This high-tech tool would, with electricity and an experienced user, be a "
"very useful way to separate chemicals in a gaseous phase, based on their "
"affinity, to a stationary phase in a tube.  At least, that's what the label "
"says."
msgstr ""
"Cet outil de haute technologie pourrait, avec de l'électricité et un "
"utilisateur expérimenté, constituer un moyen très utile de séparer des "
"produits chimiques en phase gazeuse, en fonction de leur affinité, en phase "
"stationnaire dans un tube. Du moins, c'est ce que dit l'étiquette."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mass spectrometer"
msgstr "spectromètre de masse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mass spectrometer"
msgid ""
"Inside this large white box is a carefully balanced set of electric field "
"generators that can precisely separate ionized particles based on their "
"charge-to-mass ratio, firing them into a detector that measures the exact "
"mass of the particle hitting it.  Invaluable for chemical analysis and other "
"advanced sciences, it's not as useful anymore."
msgstr ""
"À l’intérieur de cette grande boîte blanche se trouve un ensemble "
"soigneusement équilibré de générateurs de champ électrique capables de "
"séparer avec précision les particules ionisées en fonction de leur rapport "
"charge/masse, et de les envoyer vers un détecteur qui mesure la masse exacte "
"de la particule qui le frappe.  Inestimable pour l’analyse chimique et autres "
"sciences avancées, mais probablement pas très utile pour quelqu'un essayant "
"juste de survivre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nuclear magnetic resonance spectrometer"
msgstr "spectromètre à résonance magnétique nucléaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nuclear magnetic resonance spectrometer"
msgid ""
"A giant electromagnet with carefully tuned measurement equipment used to "
"observe how magnetic fields affect nuclear spins.  It is a common workhorse "
"for the discovery and study of chemical structures."
msgstr ""
"Un électro-aimant géant doté d'un équipement de mesure soigneusement réglé "
"utilisé pour observer la manière dont les champs magnétiques affectent les "
"spins nucléaires.  C’est un outil commun pour la découverte et l’étude des "
"structures chimiques."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "electron microscope"
msgstr "microscope électronique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "electron microscope"
msgid ""
"An enormous observational tool for studying the details of samples on an "
"immensely small scale."
msgstr ""
"Un énorme outil d’observation utilisé pour étudier les détails d’échantillons "
"à une échelle extrêmement précise."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "CT scanner"
msgstr "scanner de tomodensitométrie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "CT scanner"
msgid ""
"A massive piece of machinery used to take hundreds of X-ray images from 360 "
"degrees, often used for medical examinations."
msgstr ""
"Une machine massive utilisée pour prendre des centaines d'images "
"radiologiques à 360 degrés, utilisé souvent pour les tests médicaux "
"approfondis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "MRI machine"
msgstr "machine IRM"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "MRI machine"
msgid ""
"A massive tool used to take NMR images of a patient placed inside, providing "
"invaluable medical insight."
msgstr ""
"Un outil massif ayant été utilisé avant le Cataclysme pour prendre des images "
"RMN d’un patient placé à l’intérieur, fournissant ainsi des informations "
"médicales inestimables.  Maintenant plus ou moins inutile même si vous "
"possédiez les connaissances nécessaires pour comprendre les données s'en "
"provenant, ses puissants aimants ayants été ruinés dans le chaos, mais vous "
"pourriez probablement démonter ça pour en obtenir des pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "scanner bed"
msgstr "lit de scanneur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "scanner bed"
msgid ""
"A narrow, flat, and frankly uncomfortable bed for putting someone into an "
"imaging machine for medical observations."
msgstr ""
"Un lit étroit, plat et assez inconfortable utilisé pour insérer quelqu'un "
"dans une machine d'imagerie pour des tests médicaux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "anesthetic machine"
msgstr "appareil d'anesthésie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "anesthetic machine"
msgid ""
"A large machine with various tanks, tubes, and monitoring devices used to "
"maintain precise levels of anesthesia in a patient to ensure they, at least "
"ideally, remain asleep, unfeeling, but alive."
msgstr ""
"Une grande machine avec divers réservoirs, tubes et dispositifs de "
"surveillance utilisée pour maintenir des niveaux précis d'anesthésie chez un "
"patient afin de garantir qu'il reste, au moins idéalement, endormi et "
"insensible, mais vivant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dialysis machine"
msgstr "dialyseur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dialysis machine"
msgid ""
"A large machine for pumping and filtering the blood of somebody without the "
"function of their kidneys."
msgstr ""
"Une grande machine pour pomper et filtrer le sang d’une personne aux reins "
"absents ou inopérants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "medical ventilator"
msgstr "ventilateur médical"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "medical ventilator"
msgid ""
"A sizable box on a set of wheels that will pump air in and out of a patient's "
"lungs when they are incapable of breathing, though often only needed "
"temporarily."
msgstr ""
"Une boîte de grande taille sur un jeu de roues qui pompera l'air dans et hors "
"des poumons d'un patient lorsqu'il est incapable de respirer, bien que cela "
"ne soit souvent nécessaire que temporairement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "privacy curtain"
msgstr "rideau d'intimité"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "privacy curtain"
msgid "No peeking!"
msgstr "Pas de regards furtifs!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "swish!"
msgstr "swish!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clattering metal!"
msgstr "bruit de métal s'entrechoquant!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open privacy curtain"
msgstr "rideau d'intimité ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open privacy curtain"
msgid "Stop peeking!"
msgstr "Arrêtez de regarder!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_lab.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_lab.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "centrifuge"
msgstr "centrifuge"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "centrifuge"
msgid ""
"A centrifuge, a liquid separating device with an automated analyzer unit.  "
"For some reason, this one has an attached battery pack.  It could be used to "
"analyze a medical fluid sample, such as blood, if a test tube was placed in "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Une centrifugeuse, un dispositif de séparation de liquide avec une unité "
"d'analyse automatisée.  Pour une raison quelconque, celle-ci est équipée "
"d’une batterie.  Elle pourrait être utilisée pour analyser un échantillon de "
"liquide médical, tel que du sang, si un tube à essai y était placé.  "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "X-ray scanner"
msgstr "scanner rayons X"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "X-ray scanner"
msgid "A table with a movable head, often used for medical examinations."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dental X-ray machine"
msgstr "appareil de radiographie dentaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dental X-ray machine"
msgid "A device for creating radiographic images of the teeth."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "exam chair"
msgstr "chaise d'examen"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-medical.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "exam chair"
msgid "A medical exam chair with an overhead light, bolted to the floor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pallet of bricks"
msgstr "palette de briques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pallet of bricks"
msgid ""
"A massive, packed-together block of bricks wrapped with plastic packaging.  "
"It makes for easy storage of building materials for masonry constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un bloc de briques massif emballé dans du plastique.  Facilite le stockage "
"des matériaux de construction pour les constructions en maçonnerie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "bash!"
msgstr "Boom!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pallet of adobe bricks"
msgstr "palette de briques d'adobe"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pallet of adobe bricks"
msgid ""
"A massive, packed-together block of adobe bricks wrapped with plastic "
"packaging.  It makes for easy storage of building materials for masonry "
"constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un bloc massif de briques en adobe emballé dans du plastique.  Facilite le "
"stockage des matériaux de construction pour les constructions en maçonnerie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pallet of cement bags"
msgstr "palette de sacs de ciment"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pallet of cement bags"
msgid ""
"A massive, packed-together block of cement bags wrapped with plastic "
"packaging.  It makes for easy storage of building materials for masonry "
"constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un bloc massif de sacs de ciment emballé dans du plastique.  Facilite le "
"stockage des matériaux de construction pour les constructions en maçonnerie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "stack of wooden planks"
msgstr "pile de planches en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-pallet.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stack of wooden planks"
msgid ""
"Dozens of construction planks tied together for easier transport.  "
"Deconstruct to untie them."
msgstr ""
"Des douzaines de planches attachées ensemble pour un transport plus facile. "
"Démonter pour les détacher."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bathtub"
msgstr "baignoire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bathtub"
msgid ""
"An ordinary ceramic tub, with a now-functionless steel faucet and a plug "
"fixed over the drain.  Watertight and relatively clean, it would make for a "
"good water trough."
msgstr ""
"Une baignoire en céramique ordinaire, avec un robinet en acier désormais "
"inutilisable et un bouchon fixé sur le drain.  Étanche et relativement "
"propre, elle constituerait un bon abreuvoir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_druid.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "porcelain breaking!"
msgstr "bris de porcelaine!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/Backrooms/furniture_terrain.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_druid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "whunk!"
msgstr "whunk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "shower"
msgstr "douche"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "shower"
msgid ""
"A small enclosed ceramic room with a glass door and plumbing fixtures for "
"cleaning oneself.  Before it was a commonplace amenity, but now it's hard to "
"imagine wasting that much water."
msgstr ""
"Une petite pièce fermée en céramique avec une porte vitrée et des accessoires "
"de plomberie pour se nettoyer.  Avant, c'était une commodité courante, mais "
"aujourd'hui, il est difficile d'imaginer gaspiller autant d'eau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sink"
msgstr "évier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sink"
msgid ""
"A porcelain water basin with a water tap and drain, designed to be fitted "
"into an opening on a countertop."
msgstr ""
"Une vasque en porcelaine avec un robinet d'eau et un drain, conçue pour être "
"installée dans une ouverture sur un comptoir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sink with gravity-feed tank"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sink with gravity-feed tank"
msgid ""
"A water basin with flowing water, fed by a tank suspended above.  A luxury "
"when the water main is unavailable.  This one has a hand pump to refill from "
"groundwater."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "toilet"
msgstr "toilette"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "toilet"
msgid ""
"An invaluable fixture in any home, it would be a miracle to have one that "
"works.  The standing tank may hold a moderate amount of water, but while "
"better than anything that would be in the bowl, it would not be the cleanest."
msgstr ""
"Un accessoire inestimable dans n'importe quelle maison, ce serait un miracle "
"d'en avoir une qui fonctionne.  Le réservoir sur pied pourrait contenir une "
"quantité modérée d’eau, mais même s’il celle-ci serait meilleure que celle se "
"trouvant dans le bol, elle ne serait pas extrêmement potable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "water heater"
msgstr "chauffe-eau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "water heater"
#. ~ Description of furniture "family–sized water heater"
msgid ""
"An insulated metal tank with a small fire used to maintain near-boiling "
"temperatures.  There's no longer any way to power it, but any water left in "
"the large tank from before the power went out should be pretty clean, and it "
"could be used to store large quantities of other liquids too."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir métallique isolé avec un petit feu utilisé pour maintenir des "
"températures proches de l'ébullition.  Il n'y a plus aucun moyen de "
"l'alimenter, mais l'eau restant dans le grand réservoir avant la coupure de "
"courant devrait être assez propre, et il pourrait également être utilisé pour "
"stocker de grandes quantités d'autres liquides."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "family–sized water heater"
msgstr "chauffe-eau familial"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "water purifier"
msgid_plural "water purifiers"
msgstr[0] "purificateur d'eau"
msgstr[1] "purificateurs d'eau"
msgstr[2] "purificateurs d'eau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plumbing.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "water purifier"
msgid ""
"This device effectively sterilizes water.  You can plug it into a power grid "
"to use it."
msgstr ""
"Cet appareil stérilise efficacement l'eau.  Vous pouvez le brancher à un "
"réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "exercise machine"
msgid_plural "exercise machines"
msgstr[0] "machine d'exercice"
msgstr[1] "machines d'exercice"
msgstr[2] "machines d'exercice"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "exercise machine"
msgid ""
"A heavy set of weightlifting equipment for strength training, with a pair of "
"heavy weights affixed to opposite ends of a sturdy pipe.  You can adjust the "
"set by hand-picking the weights you wish to use."
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble lourd d'équipement d'haltérophilie pour l'entraînement en force, "
"avec une paire de poids lourds fixés aux extrémités opposées d'un tuyau "
"solide.  Vous pouvez ajuster l'ensemble en sélectionnant manuellement les "
"poids que vous souhaitez utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ball machine"
msgstr "machine à balles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ball machine"
msgid ""
"A simple machine for launching sports balls of various types, with a pair of "
"motorized wheels that, if spun up, would fling the ball at moderate speeds.  "
"Probably not the most effective ranged weapon against the undead."
msgstr ""
"Une machine simple capable de lancer des balles de sport de types variés, "
"avec une paire de roues motorisées qui, si alimentées, pourraient jeter "
"celles-ci à une vitesse modérée. Probablement pas le type de tourelle le plus "
"efficace contre les hordes de morts-vivants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "parkour bars"
msgstr "barres de parkour"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "parkour bars"
msgid "A complicated set of monkey bars, to be used by adults to train parkour."
msgstr ""
"Un assemblage compliqué de barres de singe en métal conçues pour permettre à "
"des adultes d'entraîner leurs muscles de bras et d'épaules."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "crack!"
msgstr "crac!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pool table"
msgstr "table de billard"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pool table"
msgid ""
"A large wooden table with green felt carpeting on top, and a set of "
"symmetrical holes that carry billiard balls to an opening on one side.  While "
"not a good substitute for a normal table, you could take it apart for a "
"substantial amount of wood."
msgstr ""
"Une grande table en bois avec un tapis en feutre vert sur le dessus et un "
"ensemble de trous symétriques qui transportent les boules de billard vers une "
"ouverture sur un côté.  Bien que ce ne soit pas un bon substitut à une table "
"normale, vous pouvez la démonter pour une quantité importante de bois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "diving block"
msgstr "plongeoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "diving block"
msgid ""
"A chunky plastic stool bolted onto the ground, intended as a safe way of "
"diving forward into a body of water."
msgstr ""
"Un tabouret en plastique épais boulonné au sol, destiné à servir de moyen sûr "
"de plonger vers l'avant dans un plan d'eau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "target"
msgstr "cible"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "target"
msgid ""
"A long sheet of metal, cut into a roughly human shape and held upright by a "
"pipe frame.  There are two bullseye targets painted onto it, a large one on "
"the torso, and a smaller one on the head.  It is peppered with small dents "
"and holes, and a large amount of the paint has flaked or chipped off."
msgstr ""
"Une longue feuille de métal, découpée en une forme grossièrement humaine et "
"maintenue verticalement par un cadre en tuyau.  Il y a deux cibles peintes "
"dessus, une grande sur le torse et une plus petite sur la tête.  Elle est "
"parsemée de petites bosses et de trous, et une grande partie de la peinture "
"s'est écaillée ou ébréchée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "arcade machine"
msgid ""
"A bulky upright arcade cabinet, brightly painted and slightly worn with age.  "
"Useless for its intended purpose without power, it's bound to have valuable "
"parts."
msgstr ""
"Une borne d'arcade verticale volumineuse, peinte de couleurs vives et "
"légèrement usée avec le temps.  Inutile pour l'usage auquel elle est destinée "
"sans alimentation, elle contient probablement des pièces utiles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pinball machine"
msgstr "flipper"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pinball machine"
msgid ""
"An iconic game, this machine has a brightly decorated background on its "
"intricate obstacle course, which is covered by a long sheet of glass.  While "
"inoperable without power, it's still impressive to look at, though probably "
"more useful if disassembled."
msgstr ""
"Un système de jeu emblématique, cette machine présente un arrière-plan aux "
"couleurs vives sur son parcours d'obstacles complexe, recouvert d'une longue "
"feuille de verre.  Bien qu'inutilisable sans alimentation, elle reste "
"impressionnante à regarder, mais renferme probablement des composants valant "
"quelque chose."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ergometer"
msgstr "ergomètre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ergometer"
msgid ""
"An exercise machine with a set of handles and plates meant to emulate rowing "
"a boat.  Without power it can't be operated, but it might have useful parts "
"to be scavenged."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil d'exercice avec un ensemble de poignées et de plaques destinés à "
"imiter l'aviron sur un bateau.  Sans électricité, il ne peut pas fonctionner, "
"mais il pourrait contenir des pièces utiles à récupérer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "mechanical ergometer"
msgid_plural "mechanical ergometers"
msgstr[0] "ergomètre mécanique"
msgstr[1] "ergomètres mécaniques"
msgstr[2] "ergomètres mécaniques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mechanical ergometer"
msgid ""
"An exercise machine with a set of handles and plates meant to emulate rowing "
"a boat.  This an older model with mechanical resistance adjustments, so it "
"works without power."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil d'exercice avec un ensemble de poignées et de plaques destinés à "
"imiter l'aviron d'un bateau.  Il s'agit d'un modèle plus ancien avec des "
"réglages de résistance mécaniques, capable donc de fonctionner sans "
"alimentation."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "treadmill"
msgstr "tapis roulant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "treadmill"
msgid ""
"A motorized conveyor belt with a control panel for running in place.  Without "
"power, it's an immense challenge to move the belt.  Regardless, you're "
"probably getting enough cardio on your own."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis roulant motorisé avec un panneau de commande pour courir sur place.  "
"Sans électricité, c'est un immense défi de déplacer la ceinture.  Quoi qu’il "
"en soit, vous faites probablement suffisamment de cardio juste en survivant "
"ces jours-ci."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "gravity treadmill"
msgid_plural "gravity treadmills"
msgstr[0] "tapis de course"
msgstr[1] "tapis de course"
msgstr[2] "tapis de course"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "gravity treadmill"
msgid ""
"A gravity-driven conveyor belt with a mechanical control panel for running in "
"place.  The belt is positioned on an adjustable incline, so it slides back "
"under your weight without needing to be powered."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis roulant à entraînement par gravité avec un panneau de commande "
"mécanique pour fonctionner sur place. Le tapis est positionné sur une "
"inclinaison réglable, de sorte qu'il glisse sous votre poids sans avoir "
"besoin d'être alimenté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "heavy punching bag"
msgid_plural "heavy punching bags"
msgstr[0] "sac de frappe lourd"
msgstr[1] "sacs de frappe lourds"
msgstr[2] "sacs de frappe lourds"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy punching bag"
msgid ""
"A hefty, oblong leather bag, suspended from a ceiling mount with a steel "
"chain.  It can be used for exercise and combat training, with the notable "
"advantage that it doesn't fight back."
msgstr ""
"Un sac en cuir massif et oblong, suspendu à un support de plafond grâce à une "
"chaîne en acier.  Il peut être utilisé pour des exercices et des "
"entraînements au combat, avec l'avantage notable de ne pas riposter."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "whud."
msgstr "bhum."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/decorative.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "piano"
msgid_plural "piano"
msgstr[0] "piano"
msgstr[1] "piano"
msgstr[2] "piano"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/decorative.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "piano"
#. ~ Description of "piano"
msgid ""
"An elegant piano, capable of producing beautiful music if used by a skilled "
"player.  A set of off-white and black keys are linked to a set of hammers, "
"which strike their corresponding tightly-coiled wire to produce sound."
msgstr ""
"Un piano élégant, capable de produire une belle musique s'il est utilisé par "
"un joueur expérimenté. Un ensemble de touches blanc cassé et noires sont "
"reliées à un ensemble de marteaux, qui frappent leur fil étroitement enroulé "
"correspondant pour produire un son."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a suffering piano!"
msgstr "un piano en souffrance!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "kerchang."
msgstr "karchang."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "speaker cabinet"
msgstr "enceinte de haut-parleur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "speaker cabinet"
msgid ""
"An upright wood-panel case of large speakers, built to produce a potentially "
"deafening volume level.  While it would be a terrible idea to use this now, "
"it could hold useful parts."
msgstr ""
"Un caisson vertical en panneaux de bois contenant de grandes enceintes, conçu "
"pour produire un niveau sonore potentiellement assourdissant. Même si ce "
"serait une très mauvaise idée de l'utiliser maintenant, il pourrait contenir "
"des pièces utiles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dancing pole"
msgstr "barre de danse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dancing pole"
msgid ""
"A tall steel pipe mounted vertically, securely fastened to the ceiling and "
"floor.  Usually used for various forms of dancing, often in adult-oriented "
"venues."
msgstr ""
"Un grand tube en acier monté verticalement, solidement fixé au plafond et au "
"sol. Généralement utilisé pour diverses formes de danse, souvent dans des "
"lieux réservés aux adultes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "roulette table"
msgstr "table de roulette"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "roulette table"
msgid ""
"A huge table specially made for a specific form of gambling, with a grid "
"painted onto the felt top, and a concave spinning wheel intended to give a "
"random selection of the inscribed possibilities."
msgstr ""
"Une immense table spécialement conçue pour une forme spécifique de jeu, avec "
"une grille peinte sur le dessus en feutre et une roue tournante concave "
"destinée à donner une sélection aléatoire des possibilités inscrites."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pipe organ"
msgstr "grande orgue"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pipe organ"
msgid ""
"A majestic pipe organ.  Dubbed \"the king of instruments\", it is capable of "
"producing powerful sound harmonies if used by a skilled player.  Rows of "
"off-white and black keys are linked to a set of iron pipes, which resonate at "
"a specific pitch when pressurized air is driven through them."
msgstr ""
"Un orgue à tuyaux majestueux. Surnommé « le roi des instruments », il est "
"capable de produire de puissantes harmonies sonores s'il est utilisé par un "
"joueur expérimenté. Des rangées de touches blanc cassé et noires sont reliées "
"à un ensemble de tuyaux en fer, qui résonnent à une hauteur spécifique "
"lorsque de l'air sous pression les traverse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a dramatic pipe organ!"
msgstr "un orgue à tuyaux dramatique!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "training dummy"
msgid_plural "training dummies"
msgstr[0] "mannequin d'entraînement"
msgstr[1] "mannequins d'entraînement"
msgstr[2] "mannequins d'entraînement"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "training dummy"
msgid ""
"A hand-made humanoid figure, useful for training in close quarters combat.  "
"This one is made from wood and has some duct tape to mark the striking "
"points.  It has been erected in the ground on its post."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine humanoïde fabriquée à la main, utile pour l'entraînement au "
"combat rapproché. Celle-ci est en bois et comporte du ruban adhésif pour "
"marquer les points de frappe. Elle a été érigée dans le sol sur son poteau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "armored training dummy"
msgid_plural "armored training dummies"
msgstr[0] "mannequin d'entraînement en armure"
msgstr[1] "mannequins d'entraînement en armure"
msgstr[2] "mannequins d'entraînement en armure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "armored training dummy"
msgid ""
"A hand-made humanoid figure, useful for training in close quarters combat.  "
"This one is covered in scrap armor and looks on guard.  It has been erected "
"in the ground on its post."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine humanoïde fabriquée à la main, utile pour l'entraînement au "
"combat rapproché. Celle-ci est recouverte d'une armure de rebut et semble sur "
"ses gardes. Elle a été érigée dans le sol sur son poteau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "box archery target"
msgid_plural "box archery targets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "box archery target"
msgid ""
"A soft target for archery consisting of tightly-packed cloth stuffed into a "
"cardboard box, with a bullseye marked on the front."
msgstr ""
"Une cible souple pour le tir à l'arc composée d'un tissu bien serré fourré "
"dans une boîte en carton, avec une cible marquée sur le devant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-rural.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "whish!"
msgstr "whish!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bale archery target"
msgid_plural "bale archery targets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-recreation.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bale archery target"
msgid ""
"A soft target for archery consisting of a bale of hay with a bullseye marked "
"on the front."
msgstr ""
"Une cible souple pour le tir à l'arc constituée d'une botte de foin avec une "
"cible marquée sur le devant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cell phone signal booster"
msgstr "amplificateur de signal de téléphone portable"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cell phone signal booster"
msgid ""
"A specialized piece of equipment that receives phone signals and amplifies "
"them to reach further destinations with more clarity.  Now that there's no "
"longer signals for them to boost, they're only good for parts."
msgstr ""
"Un équipement spécialisé qui reçoit les signaux téléphoniques et les amplifie "
"pour atteindre des destinations plus éloignées avec plus de clarté. "
"Maintenant qu'il n'y a plus de signaux à amplifier, ils ne sont plus bons que "
"pour les pièces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "womp!"
msgstr "womp!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "satellite dish"
msgstr "antenne parabolique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "satellite dish"
msgid ""
"A small sheet metal disc designed to receive radio waves from orbital "
"satellites.  Satellites that will assuredly continue to orbit, with nothing "
"to broadcast."
msgstr ""
"Un petit disque en tôle conçu pour recevoir les ondes radio des satellites en "
"orbite. Des satellites qui continueront assurément à orbiter, sans rien "
"émettre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chimney crown"
msgstr "couronne de cheminée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chimney crown"
msgid ""
"The top of a brick chimney, the opening is stained black with soot.  "
"Definitely too narrow to fit in."
msgstr ""
"Le haut d'une cheminée en brique, le trou d'aération est couvert de suie et "
"définitivement trop étroit pour passer à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "TV antenna"
msgstr "antenne TV"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "TV antenna"
msgid ""
"A simple metal antenna to increase the reception of non-cable television "
"broadcasts.  Almost wholly obsolete for years, only being good for parts "
"isn't new for this item."
msgstr ""
"Une ancienne antenne de télévision non câblée.  Plus ou moins obsolète depuis "
"des décennies, ce n'est pas que récemment qu'elle n'est plus utile que pour "
"ses composants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vent pipe"
msgstr "tuyau d'aération"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vent pipe"
msgid ""
"A sort of chimney spout for a building's internal ventilation system, this "
"can be used for circulation, venting fumes, and other such functions."
msgstr ""
"Une sorte de bec de cheminée pour le système de ventilation interne d'un "
"bâtiment, il peut être utilisé pour la circulation, l'évacuation des fumées "
"et d'autres fonctions similaires."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wind vane"
msgstr "girouette"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wind vane"
msgid ""
"A metal fin that swivels around a central pivot, indicating the direction of "
"prevailing wind."
msgstr ""
"Aileron métallique qui pivote autour d'un pivot central, indiquant la "
"direction du vent dominant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "roof turbine vent"
msgstr "évent de turbine de toit"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-roof.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "roof turbine vent"
msgid ""
"A rotary wind turbine that will catch the wind and pull out air from inside.  "
"It is most commonly used for improving air circulation, particularly in "
"poorly-ventilated areas like attics."
msgstr ""
"Une éolienne rotative qui capte le vent et extrait l'air de l'intérieur. Elle "
"est le plus souvent utilisée pour améliorer la circulation de l'air, en "
"particulier dans les zones mal ventilées comme les greniers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-rural.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bale of hay"
msgstr "rouleau de paille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-rural.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bale of hay"
msgid ""
"A massive packed-together block of hay, it makes for easy storage of straw "
"for livestock.  If your only other option is the floor, it makes a tolerable "
"bed."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un bloc de foin massif et compact qui facilite le stockage de la "
"paille pour le bétail. Si vous n'avez d'autre choix que le sol, il constitue "
"un lit acceptable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-rural.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of woodchips"
msgstr "pile de copeaux de bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-rural.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of woodchips"
msgid ""
"A large mound of piled wood chips.  Unpleasant to lay on, hard to walk "
"through, and a large fire hazard, it's probably best to shovel it out of the "
"way."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de copeaux de bois. Inconfortables comme option pour dormir dessus, "
"difficile à escalader, et un risque d'incendie, vous devriez probablement "
"juste trouver quelque chose pour vous en débarrasser, comme une pelle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bench"
msgstr "banc"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bench"
msgid ""
"A simple bench with wood slats nailed to a frame.  While uncomfortably flat "
"and just as cold as the ground, it could serve as a bed if needed."
msgstr ""
"Un banc en lamelles de bois attachées à un support en métal. Trop plat, dur "
"et froid pour être très comfortable comme option pour dormir, mais légèrement "
"mieux que le sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "armchair"
msgid_plural "armchairs"
msgstr[0] "fauteuil"
msgstr[1] "fauteuils"
msgstr[2] "fauteuils"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "armchair"
#. ~ Description of "armchair"
msgid ""
"A simple upholstered chair with armrests.  Soft and fairly warm, it "
"definitely beats the ground for sleeping on, though not by much."
msgstr ""
"Un fauteuil rembourré muni d'accoudoir. Doux et assez comfortable, ceci est "
"définitivement une meilleure alternative que de dormir à la dure, mais un "
"vrai lit serait beaucoup mieux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "airplane seat"
msgstr "siège d'avion"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "airplane seat"
msgid ""
"A cheaply-upholstered folding airplane seat, it has a simple across-the-lap "
"seatbelt.  You likely wouldn't be the first to sleep in this."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un siège d'avion pliant, rembourré et bon marché, doté d'une "
"simple ceinture de sécurité à enrouleur. Vous ne seriez sans doute pas le "
"premier à y dormir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden chair"
msgid_plural "wooden chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise en bois"
msgstr[1] "chaises en bois"
msgstr[2] "chaises en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden chair"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden chair with four legs, a seat, and a back.  It's nice to rest "
"your feet for once, and if coupled with a suitable table, you could eat a "
"meal properly and almost pretend that things were normal again."
msgstr ""
"Une simple chaise en bois avec quatre pieds, un siège et un dossier. C'est "
"agréable de reposer ses pieds pour une fois, et si on l'associe à une table "
"convenable, on peut manger un repas correctement et presque faire comme si "
"les choses étaient redevenues normales."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sofa"
msgstr "canapé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sofa"
msgid ""
"A wide upholstered bench, large enough for two people to comfortably sit "
"alongside one another, or for one person to lay down on.  It's not quite a "
"bed, but it's a hell of a lot more comfortable than the floor."
msgstr ""
"Un large banc rembourré, assez grand pour que deux personnes puissent "
"s'asseoir confortablement l'une à côté de l'autre, ou pour qu'une personne "
"puisse s'y allonger. Ce n'est pas tout à fait un lit, mais c'est beaucoup "
"plus confortable que le sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden stool"
msgid_plural "wooden stools"
msgstr[0] "tabouret en bois"
msgstr[1] "tabourets en bois"
msgstr[2] "tabourets en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden stool"
msgid ""
"A simple stool with four legs and a seat.  While it's a touch more "
"maneuverable to sit on, the lack of back support means it's significantly "
"less comfortable than a normal chair."
msgstr ""
"Un simple tabouret avec quatre pieds et un siège. S'il est un peu plus "
"maniable, l'absence de dossier le rend nettement moins confortable qu'une "
"chaise normale."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "camp chair"
msgid_plural "camp chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise de camping"
msgstr[1] "chaises de camping"
msgstr[2] "chaises de camping"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "camp chair"
msgid ""
"A somewhat uncomfortable folding chair, with fabric strung across a metal "
"frame.  Not the best, but better than nothing, and very easy to pack up for "
"transport."
msgstr ""
"Une chaise pliante quelque peu inconfortable, dont le tissu est tendu sur un "
"cadre métallique. Ce n'est pas ce qu'il y a de mieux, mais c'est mieux que "
"rien, et c'est très facile à emballer pour le transport."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "log stool"
msgid_plural "log stools"
msgstr[0] "tabouret-bûche"
msgstr[1] "tabourets-bûche"
msgstr[2] "tabourets-bûche"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "log stool"
msgid ""
"A short section of a tree trunk with one of the flat ends smoothed down.  "
"Makes for a decent place to sit, but not quite a real chair."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une courte section d'un tronc d'arbre dont l'une des extrémités "
"plates a été lissée. C'est un bon endroit pour s'asseoir, mais ce n'est pas "
"tout à fait une vraie chaise."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "deck chair"
msgid_plural "deck chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise longue"
msgstr[1] "chaises longues"
msgstr[2] "chaises longues"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "deck chair"
msgid ""
"A folding deck chair with fabric sheets mounted to a wooden frame.  While "
"it's built to handle outdoor conditions and is an improvement over the "
"ground, it's not particularly comfortable."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une chaise longue pliante dont les feuilles de tissu sont montées "
"sur un cadre en bois. Bien qu'elle soit conçue pour résister aux conditions "
"extérieures et qu'elle constitue une amélioration par rapport au sol, elle "
"n'est pas particulièrement confortable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal bench"
msgstr "banc métallique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal bench"
msgid "A bench made of metal.  Not the most comfortable furniture you've ever sat on."
msgstr ""
"Un banc en métal. Ce n'est pas le meuble le plus confortable sur lequel vous "
"vous êtes assis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "wooden bench"
msgstr "banc en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden bench"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden bench made of two thick, makeshift legs and a flat piece of "
"wood on top.  Certainly nowhere near as good as a bed, but sitting on it "
"makes you feel like you're out camping."
msgstr ""
"Un simple banc en bois composé de deux épais pieds de fortune et d'un morceau "
"de bois plat sur le dessus. C'est loin d'être aussi bien qu'un lit, mais en "
"s'asseyant dessus, on a l'impression de faire du camping."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "park bench"
msgstr "banc de parc"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "park bench"
msgid ""
"A wooden bench with a metal frame and a back support.  Cold and uncomfortable "
"to sleep on, but sitting on it is not terrible."
msgstr ""
"Un banc en bois avec une armature métallique et un dossier. Il est froid et "
"inconfortable pour dormir, mais s'asseoir dessus n'est pas terrible."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bar stool"
msgid_plural "bar stools"
msgstr[0] "tabouret de bar"
msgstr[1] "tabourets de bar"
msgstr[2] "tabourets de bar"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bar stool"
msgid ""
"A bar stool with a leather seat on a steel support.  Not practical for "
"sleeping at all, but it does feel nicer than sitting on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Un tabouret de bar avec un siège en cuir sur un support en acier. Ce n'est "
"pas du tout pratique pour dormir, mais c'est plus agréable que de s'asseoir "
"par terre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "folding chair"
msgid_plural "folding chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise pliante"
msgstr[1] "chaises pliantes"
msgstr[2] "chaises pliantes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "folding chair"
msgid ""
"A black foldable plastic chair on a steel frame.  Not particularly "
"comfortable, but at least you have something to sit on."
msgstr ""
"Une chaise pliante en plastique noir sur un cadre en acier. Ce n'est pas très "
"confortable, mais au moins on a de quoi s'asseoir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plywood chair"
msgid_plural "plywood chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise en bois contreplaqué"
msgstr[1] "chaises en bois contreplaqué"
msgstr[2] "chaises en bois contreplaqué"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "plywood chair"
msgid ""
"A simple chair made of plywood on a steel frame.  Quite uncomfortable, but it "
"works for sleeping if it's the only option available."
msgstr ""
"Une simple chaise en contreplaqué sur un cadre en acier. Elle est assez "
"inconfortable, mais elle permet de dormir si c'est la seule option disponible."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "black wooden chair"
msgid_plural "black wooden chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise en bois noire"
msgstr[1] "chaises en bois noires"
msgstr[2] "chaises en bois noires"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black wooden chair"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden chair with four legs, a seat, and a back.  It's nice to rest "
"your feet for once, and if coupled with a suitable table, you could eat a "
"meal properly and almost pretend that things were normal again.  This "
"particular chair is painted black."
msgstr ""
"A simple wooden chair with four legs, a seat, and a back. It's nice to rest "
"your feet for once, and if coupled with a suitable table, you could eat a "
"meal properly and almost pretend that things were normal again. This "
"particular chair is painted black."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "white wooden chair"
msgid_plural "white wooden chairs"
msgstr[0] "chaise en bois blanche"
msgstr[1] "chaises en bois blanches"
msgstr[2] "chaises en bois blanches"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "white wooden chair"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden chair with four legs, a seat, and a back.  It's nice to rest "
"your feet for once, and if coupled with a suitable table, you could eat a "
"meal properly and almost pretend that things were normal again.  This "
"particular chair is painted white."
msgstr ""
"Une simple chaise en bois avec quatre pieds, un siège et un dossier. C'est "
"agréable de reposer ses pieds pour une fois, et si on l'associe à une table "
"appropriée, on peut manger un repas correctement et presque faire semblant "
"que les choses sont redevenues normales. Cette chaise est peinte en blanche."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "barber chair"
msgstr "fauteuil de barbier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "barber chair"
msgid ""
"a stationary chair made of cloth and steel.  With adjustable height and the "
"ability to swing."
msgstr ""
"une chaise fixe faite de tissu et d'acier. Elle est réglable en hauteur et "
"peut se balancer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bean bag"
msgid_plural "bean bags"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-seats.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/seating.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bean bag"
#. ~ Description of "bean bag"
msgid "A large cushion filled with beads often used as a seat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bulletin board"
msgstr "tableau d'affichage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bulletin board"
msgid ""
"A wide wooden frame with a sheet of corkboard inside.  Good for pinning "
"various notices for other survivors to read."
msgstr ""
"Un large cadre en bois avec une feuille de liège à l'intérieur. Il permet "
"d'épingler divers avis que les autres survivants pourront lire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sign"
msgstr "pancarte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sign"
msgid ""
"A simple signpost made of wood.  Basically two planks alongside each other "
"nailed to another plank that holds them up."
msgstr ""
"A simple signpost made of wood.  Basically two planks alongside each other "
"nailed to another plank that holds them up."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "warning sign"
msgstr "panneau d'avertissement"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "warning sign"
msgid ""
"A triangular signpost painted white with a red border.  Designed to easily "
"catch the eye, signs of this nature seldom display anything but bad news."
msgstr ""
"Un panneau triangulaire peint en blanc avec une bordure rouge. Conçus pour "
"attirer facilement le regard, les panneaux de cette nature n'affichent que "
"rarement de mauvaises nouvelles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "evac shelter info board"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "evac shelter info board"
msgid ""
"A wide wooden frame surrounding a sheet of cork, on to which a number of "
"full-page notices have been neatly tacked.  Most seem to provide emergency "
"information, or instructions now woefully outdated considering the state of "
"things, but a map pointing to the nearest refugee center catches your eye.  "
"You should take a closer look."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_EVAC_BOARD_FALSE" in furniture "evac
#. shelter info board"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You study the board.  It shows a similar set of directions to the ones you "
"already have.  You cross-reference them and don't learn anything new."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_EVAC_BOARD" in furniture "evac
#. shelter info board"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You study the board.  One of the pages has a map and address for a nearby "
"refugee center alongside minutia you no longer need trouble yourself with now "
"that society has collapsed, like 'operating hours' and 'acceptable forms of "
"ID'.  You take careful note of the map on the board and mark down the "
"coordinates."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "stop sign"
msgstr "panneau stop"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-signs.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stop sign"
msgid "An octagonal red sign on a long metal pole, marked with the word STOP."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_treesung.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "bed"
msgstr "lit"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bed"
msgid ""
"A standard mattress on a sturdy wooden frame.  Even without blankets or "
"pillows, and despite being a completely ordinary mattress, it's a sight for "
"sore, tired eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un matelas standard sur un solide cadre en bois. Même sans couverture ni "
"oreiller, et bien qu'il s'agisse d'un matelas tout à fait ordinaire, c'est un "
"spectacle pour les yeux fatigués et endoloris."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/json/recipes/basecamps/base/fbmc_outpost/recipe_modular_outpost_normal.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Blueprint name of recipe crafting "faction_base_outpost_normal_bed_0"
msgid "bunk bed"
msgstr "lit superposé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bunk bed"
msgid ""
"A bunk bed with a sturdy wooden frame built to hold two single-person "
"mattresses above one another.  While these usually mean sleeping closer than "
"you'd like to somebody you wouldn't normally want to share a mattress with, a "
"bed's a bed."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un lit superposé doté d'un cadre en bois solide conçu pour "
"accueillir deux matelas pour une personne l'un au-dessus de l'autre. Bien que "
"cela signifie généralement que vous devez dormir plus près que vous ne le "
"souhaiteriez d'une personne avec laquelle vous ne voudriez normalement pas "
"partager un matelas, un lit est un lit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_treesung.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "down bed"
msgstr "lits en duvet"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "down bed"
msgid ""
"A down mattress on a sturdy wooden frame.  Even without blankets or pillows, "
"and despite being a completely ordinary mattress, it's a sight for sore, "
"tired eyes."
msgstr ""
"Un matelas en duvet sur un solide cadre en bois. Même sans couverture ni "
"oreiller, et bien qu'il s'agisse d'un matelas tout à fait ordinaire, c'est un "
"spectacle pour les yeux fatigués et endoloris."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "down bunkbed"
msgstr "lits superposés en duvet"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "down bunkbed"
msgid ""
"A bunk bed with a sturdy wooden frame built to hold two single-person "
"mattresses above one another.  While these usually mean sleeping closer than "
"you'd like to somebody you wouldn't normally want to share a mattress with, a "
"bed's a bed.  This one has two down mattresses."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un lit superposé doté d'un cadre en bois solide conçu pour "
"accueillir deux matelas pour une personne l'un au-dessus de l'autre. Bien que "
"cela signifie généralement que l'on dort plus près que l'on ne le "
"souhaiterait d'une personne avec laquelle on ne voudrait normalement pas "
"partager un matelas, un lit est un lit. Celui-ci a deux matelas en duvet."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "triple berth"
msgstr "triple couchette"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "triple berth"
msgid ""
"This bunk bed can hold three people at once - a perfect sleeping solution for "
"places where empty space is at a premium."
msgstr ""
"Ce lit superposé peut accueillir trois personnes à la fois - une solution de "
"couchage parfaite pour les endroits où l'espace est restreint."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bed frame"
msgstr "cadre de lit"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bed frame"
msgid ""
"A sturdy wooden bed frame built to hold most standard mattresses.  Despite "
"being one half of a bed, it's just about impossible to lay on by itself."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre de lit en bois robuste conçu pour accueillir la plupart des matelas "
"standard. Bien qu'il s'agisse de la moitié d'un lit, il est pratiquement "
"impossible de s'y allonger seul."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mattress"
msgid ""
"An ordinary mattress lying on the floor.  While it's not as comfortable as a "
"proper bed with a frame, it's pretty close.  If it's somewhere actually safe "
"to sleep, this is practically a luxury in and of itself."
msgstr ""
"Un matelas ordinaire posé sur le sol. Bien qu'il ne soit pas aussi "
"confortable qu'un vrai lit avec un cadre, il en est assez proche. S'il s'agit "
"d'un endroit où l'on peut dormir en toute sécurité, c'est un luxe en soi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "down mattress"
msgid ""
"A squishy, feather-stuffed mattress lying on the floor.  While it's not as "
"comfortable as a proper bed with a frame, it's pretty close.  If it's "
"somewhere actually safe to sleep, this is practically a luxury in and of "
"itself."
msgstr ""
"Un matelas mou, rembourré de plumes, posé sur le sol. Bien qu'il ne soit pas "
"aussi confortable qu'un vrai lit avec un cadre, il en est assez proche. S'il "
"s'agit d'un endroit où l'on peut dormir en toute sécurité, c'est un luxe en "
"soi."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/json/items/generic/bedding.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hammock"
msgid_plural "hammocks"
msgstr[0] "hamac"
msgstr[1] "hamacs"
msgstr[2] "hamacs"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hammock"
msgid ""
"A large sheet of cloth with ropes on two sides tied to nearby objects.  It's "
"quite comfortable to sleep in, but provides no warmth."
msgstr ""
"Un grand drap de tissu avec des cordes sur deux côtés attachées à des objets "
"proches. Il est assez confortable pour dormir, mais n'apporte aucune chaleur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "slap!"
msgstr "slap!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#: data/json/items/generic/bedding.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "net hammock"
msgid_plural "net hammocks"
msgstr[0] "hamac filet"
msgstr[1] "hamacs filets"
msgstr[2] "hamacs filets"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "net hammock"
msgid ""
"A large net with ropes on two sides tied to nearby objects.  It's quite "
"comfortable to sleep in, but provides no warmth."
msgstr ""
"Un grand filet avec des cordes sur deux côtés, attachées à des objets "
"proches. Il est assez confortable pour dormir, mais n'apporte aucune chaleur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "makeshift bed"
msgstr "lit improvisé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "makeshift bed"
msgid ""
"An improvised mattress on a flimsy wooden frame.  Almost as good as a normal "
"bed, albeit with a slightly lumpy mattress.  Considering the circumstances, "
"it's not too bad at all."
msgstr ""
"Un matelas improvisé sur un cadre en bois fragile. Presque aussi bien qu'un "
"lit normal, mais avec un matelas un peu lourd. Compte tenu des circonstances, "
"ce n'est pas si mal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "straw bed"
msgstr "lit de paille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-sleep.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "straw bed"
msgid ""
"An improvised bedding pile made of hay.  Better than nothing, but not "
"particularly comfortable, and quite itchy."
msgstr ""
"Une litière improvisée à base de foin. C'est mieux que rien, mais ce n'est "
"pas très confortable et ça gratte beaucoup."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bookcase"
msgstr "bibliothèque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bookcase"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden shelf for storing dozens of books.  While designed for books, "
"it does a decent job of storing anything else that'll fit."
msgstr ""
"Une simple bibliothéque en bois capable d'entreposer des dizaines de livres. "
"Bien que celle-ci à pour fonction de stocker des livres, ce n'est pas non "
"plus une mauvaise étagère pour tout ce qui est capable de tenir à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "entertainment center"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "entertainment center"
msgid ""
"While not quite as cool by itself as the name might imply, this large wooden "
"cabinet can store a variety of things, like a TV and media systems, with "
"shelving space and cupboards for anything that'll fit."
msgstr ""
"Même si elle n'est pas aussi cool que son nom l'indique, cette grande armoire "
"en bois permet de ranger une multitude d'objets, comme une télévision et des "
"systèmes multimédias, avec des étagères et des placards pour tout ce qui s'y "
"prête."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "coffin"
msgstr "cercueil"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "coffin"
msgid ""
"A humble wooden casket for the respectful burial of the dead.  While a "
"standard practice before this all happened, it is now a rare honor for one to "
"be given a proper final resting place.  An honor that countless many will "
"likely never receive."
msgstr ""
"Un humble cercueil en bois pour l'enterrement respectueux des morts. Bien "
"qu'il s'agisse d'une pratique courante avant que tout cela n'arrive, c'est "
"désormais un rare honneur pour quelqu'un de recevoir une dernière demeure "
"digne de ce nom. Un honneur que d'innombrables personnes ne recevront "
"probablement jamais."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/furniture-and-terrain/desert_terrain.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "wham!"
msgstr "bing!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying action message of furniture "coffin"
msgid "You wedge open the coffin."
msgstr "Vous ouvrez le cercueil."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying failure message of furniture "coffin"
msgid "You pry, but the coffin remains closed."
msgstr "Vous essayez de forcer l'ouverture, mais le cercueil reste fermé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open coffin"
msgstr "cercueil ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open coffin"
msgid ""
"A humble wooden casket for the respectful burial of the dead.  While a "
"standard practice before this all happened, it is now a rare honor for one to "
"be given a proper final resting place.  This one is open and unoccupied, and "
"gazing inside fills you with a sense of melancholic weariness."
msgstr ""
"Un humble cercueil en bois pour l'enterrement respectueux des morts. Bien "
"qu'il s'agisse d'une pratique courante avant que tout cela n'arrive, c'est "
"aujourd'hui un honneur rare que de recevoir une dernière demeure digne de ce "
"nom. Celui-ci est ouvert et inoccupé, et un regard à l'intérieur vous remplit "
"d'un sentiment de lassitude mélancolique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "crate"
msgstr "caisse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "crate"
msgid ""
"A sealed wooden storage container.  Lacking any labels, it could hold just "
"about anything inside.  If you don't have a proper tool to pry it open, "
"smashing it is an option, albeit one that risks destroying the contents."
msgstr ""
"Un conteneur de stockage en bois scellé. Dépourvu d'étiquettes, il peut "
"contenir à peu près n'importe quoi. Si vous ne disposez pas d'un outil "
"adéquat pour l'ouvrir, vous pouvez le casser, mais vous risquez de détruire "
"son contenu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying action message of furniture "crate"
msgid "You pop open the crate."
msgstr "Vous ouvrez la caisse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying failure message of furniture "crate"
msgid "You pry, but can't pop open the crate."
msgstr "Vous faites levier, mais vous n'arrivez pas à ouvrir la caisse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open crate"
msgstr "caisse ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open crate"
msgid ""
"An open wooden storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid "
"has been pried off and is leaned adjacent to it, and with a fresh set of "
"nails, could be sealed back shut."
msgstr ""
"Une boîte de rangement en bois ouverte, pouvant contenir un grand nombre de "
"choses. Le couvercle a été enlevé et est appuyé à côté, et avec une nouvelle "
"série de clous, il pourrait être refermé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/containers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "large cardboard box"
msgid_plural "large cardboard boxes"
msgstr[0] "grande boîte en carton"
msgstr[1] "grandes boîtes en carton"
msgstr[2] "grandes boîtes en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large cardboard box"
msgid ""
"A large box made of brown corrugated paper.  Could contain a number of "
"things, and you could even hide inside.  Considering it only has two small "
"flaps for carrying, it's very hard to see out of, and won't do anything to "
"protect you if you're found."
msgstr ""
"Une grande boîte en papier ondulé brun. Elle peut contenir un certain nombre "
"de choses, et vous pouvez même vous cacher à l'intérieur. Comme elle n'a que "
"deux petits rabats pour la transporter, il est très difficile de voir à "
"l'extérieur et elle ne vous protégera pas si on vous trouve."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "crumple!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/containers.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "reinforced large cardboard box"
msgid_plural "reinforced large cardboard boxes"
msgstr[0] "grande boîte en carton renforcée"
msgstr[1] "grandes boîtes en carton renforcées"
msgstr[2] "grandes boîtes en carton renforcées"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced large cardboard box"
msgid ""
"A large box made of brown corrugated paper that was doubled up for extra "
"strength.  Could contain a number of things, and you could even hide inside.  "
"Considering it only has two small flaps for carrying, it's very hard to see "
"out of, and won't do anything to protect you if you're found."
msgstr ""
"Une grande boîte faite de papier brun ondulé doublé pour plus de solidité. "
"Elle peut contenir un certain nombre de choses, et vous pouvez même vous "
"cacher à l'intérieur. Comme elle n'a que deux petits rabats pour la "
"transporter, il est très difficile de voir à l'extérieur et elle ne vous "
"protègera pas si on vous trouve."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dresser"
msgstr "commode"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dresser"
msgid ""
"A simple wooden cabinet with a column of short drawers.  While intended for "
"storing clothes, there's nothing stopping you from storing whatever fits."
msgstr ""
"Une simple armoire en bois avec une colonne de tiroirs courts. Bien qu'elle "
"soit destinée au rangement des vêtements, rien ne vous empêche d'y ranger ce "
"qui vous convient."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "glass front cabinet"
msgstr "armoire à façade vitrée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "glass front cabinet"
msgid ""
"A tall metal cabinet with a sheet of glass across the front for viewing the "
"contents.  Often used for displaying rare, visually pleasing, or otherwise "
"valuable goods, it's odd that it doesn't have a lock."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une haute armoire métallique dont la façade est recouverte d'une "
"feuille de verre permettant d'en voir le contenu. Souvent utilisée pour "
"exposer des objets rares, beaux ou précieux, il est curieux qu'elle ne soit "
"pas munie d'une serrure."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open gun safe"
msgstr "coffre à armes ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open gun safe"
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls, designed to securely store "
"firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Un grand et lourd conteneur aux parois métalliques épaisses, conçu pour "
"stocker en toute sécurité des armes à feu, des mods d'armes et des munitions. "
"Celui-ci est grand ouvert."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "screeching metal!"
msgstr "du métal qui crisse!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "closed gun safe"
msgstr "coffre à armes fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "closed gun safe"
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  This "
"one is closed, but not locked."
msgstr ""
"Un grand conteneur lourd aux parois métalliques épaisses et doté d'une "
"serrure à combinaison rotative, conçu pour stocker en toute sécurité des "
"armes à feu, des modulateurs d'armes et des munitions. Celui-ci est fermé, "
"mais pas verrouillé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "locked gun safe"
msgstr "coffre à armes verrouillé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "locked gun safe"
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  If "
"you had something to pick its lock with, you could probably open it."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un grand et lourd conteneur aux parois métalliques épaisses, doté "
"d'une serrure à combinaison rotative, conçu pour stocker en toute sécurité "
"des armes à feu, des mods d'armes et des munitions. Si vous aviez quelque "
"chose pour crocheter la serrure, vous pourriez probablement l'ouvrir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "locked gun safe"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gun safe door opens."
msgstr "Avec un clic satisfaisant, la serrure de la porte du coffre-fort s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "jammed gun safe"
msgstr "coffre à armes coincé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "jammed gun safe"
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and a rotary combination "
"lock, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  "
"Unfortunately, the lock is completely broken, and short of some pretty "
"serious machinery, you have no possible way of opening it."
msgstr ""
"Un grand et lourd conteneur aux parois métalliques épaisses et doté d'une "
"serrure à combinaison rotative, conçu pour stocker en toute sécurité des "
"armes à feu, des mods d'armes et des munitions. Malheureusement, la serrure "
"est complètement cassée et, à moins d'avoir recours à des machines très "
"puissantes, vous n'avez aucun moyen de l'ouvrir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "electronic gun safe"
msgstr "coffre à armes électronique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "electronic gun safe"
msgid ""
"A large, heavy container with thick metal walls and an electronic locking "
"system, designed to securely store firearms, weapon mods, and ammunition.  If "
"you had some way of hacking into it, you could probably crack it open."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un grand et lourd conteneur aux parois métalliques épaisses et "
"doté d'un système de verrouillage électronique, conçu pour stocker en toute "
"sécurité des armes à feu, des mods d'armes et des munitions. Si vous aviez un "
"moyen de le pirater, vous pourriez probablement l'ouvrir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "locker"
msgstr "casier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "locker"
msgid ""
"A tall sheet metal cabinet, useful for storing just about anything that'll "
"fit."
msgstr ""
"Une grande armoire en tôle, utile pour ranger à peu près tout ce qui peut "
"entrer dans l'armoire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mailbox"
msgstr "boîte aux lettres"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mailbox"
msgid ""
"A small metal box on top of a wooden post, designed to receive mail "
"deliveries.  Although considering the circumstances, it will likely never see "
"proper use again."
msgstr ""
"Une petite boîte métallique placée au sommet d'un poteau en bois, destinée à "
"recevoir les livraisons de courrier.  Compte tenu des circonstances, il est "
"probable qu'elle ne sera plus jamais utilisée pour sa fonction originelle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "clothing rail"
msgstr "portant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "clothing rail"
msgid ""
"A metal frame on a set of wheels used for hanging large amounts of clothes.  "
"Usually used in theater or retail environments, it's easy to use and quick to "
"access."
msgstr ""
"Cadre métallique sur roulettes utilisé pour suspendre de grandes quantités de "
"vêtements. Généralement utilisé dans les théâtres ou les magasins, il est "
"facile à utiliser et rapide d'accès."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "display rack"
msgstr "présentoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display rack"
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored."
msgstr ""
"Un rayonnage en tôle, dont les surfaces de stockage sont inclinées de manière "
"à mettre en valeur les articles stockés."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "locked display rack"
msgstr "présentoir verrouillé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "locked display rack"
msgid ""
"A sheet metal shelving unit, with the storage surfaces angled in such a way "
"as to show off the items stored.  Metal fasteners with a lock hold the items "
"securely to the rack."
msgstr ""
"Un rayonnage en tôle, dont les surfaces de stockage sont inclinées de manière "
"à mettre en valeur les articles stockés. Des attaches métalliques munies "
"d'une serrure maintiennent les articles en toute sécurité sur le rayonnage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "locked display rack"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock opens."
msgstr "Avec un clic satisfaisant, la serrure s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wooden rack"
msgstr "étagère en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden rack"
msgid ""
"A wooden shelving unit with angled storage surfaces designed to show off "
"whatever is stored on it."
msgstr ""
"Une étagère en bois avec des surfaces de rangement inclinées conçues pour "
"mettre en valeur ce qui y est rangé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "coat rack"
msgstr "porte-manteau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "coat rack"
msgid ""
"A tall wooden pole with a set of hooks used to store outdoor jackets and hats "
"to allow easy access."
msgstr ""
"Un long poteau en bois en haut duquel ont été placés plusieurs crochets "
"courbés auquel il est possible de pendre des manteaux et vestes pouvant être "
"facilement accédés à nouveau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "recycle bin"
msgstr "boîte de recyclage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "recycle bin"
msgid ""
"A large plastic bin painted green with a 'recycle' symbol emblazoned on it.  "
"While intended to store discarded things to be processed back into a factory, "
"the drastic change in priorities as of late means that these may hold "
"valuable materials."
msgstr ""
"Une grande poubelle en plastique peinte en vert et portant le symbole du "
"recyclage. Destinée à stocker des objets mis au rebut en vue de leur "
"transformation en usine, cette poubelle peut contenir des matériaux de valeur "
"en raison du changement radical de priorités intervenu ces derniers temps."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "safe"
msgstr "coffre-fort"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  This one isn't actually locked, just closed."
msgstr ""
"Une petite boîte métallique, lourde et presque inaccessible, munie d'une "
"serrure à combinaison rotative. Celle-ci n'est pas réellement verrouillée, "
"mais simplement fermée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "safe"
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock.  With something to listen really closely and a hell of a lot of time, "
"you might be able to crack it."
msgstr ""
"Une petite boîte en métal, lourde et presque inviolable, avec une serrure à "
"combinaison rotative. Avec une écoute très attentive et beaucoup de temps, "
"vous pourriez être en mesure de la forcer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open safe"
msgstr "coffre-fort ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open safe"
msgid ""
"A small, heavy, and near-unbreachable metal box with a rotary combination "
"lock, albeit significantly less secure with the door open."
msgstr ""
"Une petite boîte métallique, lourde et presque inaccessible, dotée d'une "
"serrure à combinaison rotative, mais nettement moins sûre lorsque la porte "
"est ouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/generic.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "trash can"
msgid_plural "trash cans"
msgstr[0] "poubelle"
msgstr[1] "poubelles"
msgstr[2] "poubelles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trash can"
msgid ""
"A plastic bin for storing discarded waste as to be disposed of later.  "
"Although, considering the circumstances, it might be worth seeing what's "
"inside."
msgstr ""
"Une poubelle en plastique pour stocker les déchets à éliminer plus tard. "
"Toutefois, compte tenu des circonstances, il peut être intéressant de voir ce "
"qu'il y a à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal trash can"
msgstr "poubelle en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal trash can"
msgid "A crude metal bin typically used to dispose of waste."
msgstr "Poubelle en métal brut généralement utilisée pour l'élimination des déchets."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wardrobe"
msgstr "armoire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wardrobe"
msgid ""
"A very large wooden cabinet for storing clothes, effectively an upright "
"closet.  Could technically be used to store anything else that would fit, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Une très grande armoire en bois pour ranger les vêtements, en fait un placard "
"vertical. Techniquement, elle peut être utilisée pour ranger tout ce qui peut "
"l'être."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "Torah Ark"
msgstr "Arche de Torah"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Torah Ark"
msgid ""
"An ornately-carved cabinet designed to hold a Torah scroll.  This one is "
"decorated with a tree motif, referencing Proverbs 3:18."
msgstr ""
"Armoire sculptée et ornée, conçue pour contenir un rouleau de la Torah. "
"Celui-ci est décoré d'un motif d'arbre, en référence à Proverbes 3:18."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filing cabinet"
msgstr "classeur de bureau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "filing cabinet"
msgid ""
"A rack of metal drawers designed to hold various files and paperwork.  "
"Paperwork that has more than likely lost all relevance and value by now."
msgstr ""
"Une étagère de tiroirs métalliques conçue pour contenir divers dossiers et "
"documents. Des documents qui ont probablement perdu toute pertinence et toute "
"valeur à l'heure actuelle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "utility shelf"
msgstr "simple étagères "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "utility shelf"
msgid ""
"A simple heavy-duty plastic and metal shelving unit, intended to store tools "
"and materials for easy access to workers."
msgstr ""
"Un simple rayonnage en plastique et en métal très résistant, destiné à ranger "
"les outils et les matériaux pour en faciliter l'accès aux travailleurs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "warehouse shelf"
msgstr "étagère d'entrepôt"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "warehouse shelf"
msgid "A huge, sturdy steel shelf for storing pallets of crates in warehouses."
msgstr ""
"Une énorme étagère en acier robuste pour stocker des palettes de caisses dans "
"les entrepôts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wooden keg"
msgstr "tonnelet en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden keg"
msgid ""
"A large standing wooden barrel, completely watertight.  Good for storing "
"liquids of all kinds."
msgstr ""
"Une énorme étagère en acier robuste pour stocker des palettes de caisses dans "
"les entrepôts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "display case"
msgstr "présentoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display case"
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass paneling on top.  "
"Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "display case"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock and the display case opens."
msgstr "Un cliquetis plaisant et le verrou et le couvercle de la vitrine s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open display case"
msgstr "vitrine ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open display case"
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass paneling on top.  "
"Useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off.  Not "
"actually as secure as it looks, as the display windows are easily broken.  "
"This one has had its lock picked and is open."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken display case"
msgstr "vitrine cassée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken display case"
msgid ""
"A secure wooden case at about waist-height, with glass paneling on top.  "
"Would be useful for storing valuable things while still showing them off, if "
"the glass hadn't been shattered.  Careful not to cut yourself when looting."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "map board"
msgstr "panneau de cartes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "map board"
msgid "A secure metal board with a locked glass panel used to display a map."
msgstr ""
"Un tableau métallique sécurisé avec un panneau en verre verrouillé utilisé "
"pour afficher une carte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "map board"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the locked glass panel opens."
msgstr "Avec un clic satisfaisant, le panneau de verre verrouillé s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open map board"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open map board"
msgid ""
"A successfully picked metal board with an open glass panel used to display a "
"map."
msgstr "Un panneau métallique avec une vitre ouverte, utilisé pour afficher une carte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken map board"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken map board"
msgid "A metal board with a smashed glass panel used to display a map."
msgstr ""
"Un tableau métallique avec un panneau de verre brisé utilisé pour afficher "
"une carte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armoire de pompier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fireman's cabinet"
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out, visibly holding tools behind a thin "
"panel of tempered glass."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire métallique peinte pour se démarquer, contenant visiblement des "
"outils derrière un mince panneau de verre trempé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of furniture "fireman's cabinet"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the cabinet opens."
msgstr "Avec un clic satisfaisant, la serrure de l'armoire s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armoire de pompier déverrouillée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "unlocked fireman's cabinet"
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its glass panel door was left "
"unlocked and slightly ajar."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire métallique peinte pour se démarquer. Sa porte vitrée est restée "
"déverrouillée et légèrement entrouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open fireman's cabinet"
msgstr "armoire de pompier ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open fireman's cabinet"
msgid ""
"A metallic cabinet painted to stand out.  Its protective glass panel lies "
"broken from some past emergency or looting attempt."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire métallique peinte pour se démarquer. Son panneau de verre "
"protecteur est brisé à la suite d'une urgence ou d'une tentative de pillage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "standing tank"
msgstr "réservoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "standing tank"
msgid "A huge metal tank that can be used to safely store large amounts of liquid."
msgstr ""
"Un énorme réservoir métallique qui peut être utilisé pour stocker en toute "
"sécurité de grandes quantités de liquide."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "bulk storage tank"
msgstr "réservoir de stockage en vrac"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bulk storage tank"
msgid ""
"A 2 meters high tank that can store up to 1500 liters of liquid.  That's a "
"lot."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir de 2 mètres de haut qui peut stocker jusqu'à 1500 litres de "
"liquide. C'est beaucoup."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fuel tank"
msgstr "réservoir d'essence"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
msgid "A tank filled with gasoline."
msgstr "Un réservoir remplie d'essence."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken fuel tank"
msgstr "réservoir de carburant brisé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with gasoline."
msgstr "Un réservoir cassé qui était rempli d'essence."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fuel tank"
msgid "A tank filled with diesel."
msgstr "Un réservoir rempli de diesel."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken fuel tank"
msgid "A broken tank which was filled with diesel."
msgstr "Un réservoir percé ayant été rempli de diesel."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "dumpster"
msgstr "benne à ordures"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "dumpster"
msgid ""
"A large metal dumpster that will likely not be getting picked up by the "
"city's waste management any time soon.  Despite the unpleasant nature of "
"climbing inside, it could make for a viable hiding spot."
msgstr ""
"Une grande benne métallique qui ne sera probablement pas ramassée par le "
"service de gestion des déchets de la ville de sitôt. Bien qu'il soit "
"désagréable de grimper à l'intérieur, elle pourrait constituer une cachette "
"intéressante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "butter churn"
msgstr "baratte à beurre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "butter churn"
msgid ""
"A metal tube with a built-in mixer for making butter.  Rather than needing "
"electricity, it is pedal-driven, allowing use without power."
msgstr ""
"Un tube métallique avec un mélangeur intégré pour faire du beurre. Il n'a pas "
"besoin d'électricité, il est actionné par une pédale, ce qui permet de "
"l'utiliser sans électricité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "riveted metal crate"
msgstr "caisse en métal rivetée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "riveted metal crate"
msgid ""
"This huge box is made of a dull metal, riveted together.  There is no obvious "
"opening mechanism, and the rivets don't match any of your tools.  The only "
"way in would be to smash it."
msgstr ""
"Cette énorme boîte est faite d'un métal terne, riveté ensemble. Il n'y a pas "
"de mécanisme d'ouverture évident, et les rivets ne correspondent à aucun de "
"vos outils. Le seul moyen d'entrer est de la briser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "sealed metal crate"
msgstr "caisse en métal scellée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "sealed metal crate"
msgid ""
"A huge, tightly sealed storage crate made from welded and riveted sheet "
"metal.  The sealing mechanism is too tight to open bare-handed and would need "
"some kind of prying instrument to release."
msgstr ""
"Une énorme caisse de stockage hermétiquement fermée, fabriquée à partir de "
"tôles soudées et rivetées. Le mécanisme de fermeture est trop serré pour être "
"ouvert à main nue et il faudrait un instrument d'ouverture pour le débloquer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying action message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
msgid "You wrench open the metal crate."
msgstr "Vous forcez la caisse en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Prying failure message of furniture "sealed metal crate"
msgid "The lid is sealed more tightly than you thought."
msgstr "Le couvercle de cette caisse est plus fermement en place que vous pensiez."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open metal crate"
msgstr "caisse en métal ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open metal crate"
msgid ""
"This large metal crate's lid is unsealed, and hinges open easily to reveal a "
"number of storage shelves inside.  Once open, the side panels also swing "
"wider for easy access."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wooden chest"
msgstr "coffre en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden chest"
msgid ""
"A sealed wooden storage container.  Lacking any labels, it could hold just "
"about anything inside.  It has a simple metal latch."
msgstr ""
"Un conteneur de stockage en bois scellé. Dépourvu d'étiquettes, il peut "
"contenir à peu près n'importe quoi. Il est muni d'un simple loquet en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "steel foot locker"
msgid_plural "steel foot lockers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "steel foot locker"
#. ~ Description of "steel foot locker"
msgid ""
"A steel storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid has a "
"small lock."
msgstr ""
"Boîte de rangement en acier, pouvant contenir un grand nombre d'objets. Le "
"couvercle est muni d'une petite serrure."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum foot locker"
msgid_plural "aluminum foot lockers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/furniture/storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum foot locker"
#. ~ Description of "aluminum foot locker"
msgid ""
"An aluminum storage box, capable of holding any number of things.  The lid "
"has a small lock."
msgstr ""
"Boîte de rangement en aluminium pouvant contenir un grand nombre d'objets. Le "
"couvercle est muni d'une petite serrure."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/containers/military.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "big collapsible drum"
msgid_plural "big collapsible drums"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "big collapsible drum"
msgid ""
"A black collapsible drum with a valve and D-Rings.  Yellow text on its top "
"clearly says \"FLAMMABLE\"."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "packed pallet"
msgstr "palettes en bois emballées"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "packed pallet"
msgid ""
"A wooden pallet loaded with cargo, wrapped with a watertight cover, and "
"belted to secure the contents."
msgstr ""
"Palette en bois chargée de marchandises, enveloppée d'une housse étanche et "
"ceinturée pour sécuriser le contenu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "rip!"
msgstr "rip!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "damaged pallet"
msgstr "palettes en bois endommagées"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "damaged pallet"
msgid ""
"A wooden pallet, containing cargo and possessing a torn cover.  You can reach "
"the contents, but it's awfully hard due to the belts still being in place."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#: data/json/items/tool/workshop.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Exodii kiln"
msgid_plural "Exodii kilns"
msgstr[0] "fourneau Exodii"
msgstr[1] "fourneaux Exodii"
msgstr[2] "fourneaux Exodii"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-storage.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Exodii kiln"
msgid "An imposing kiln produced by the Exodii, used to produce their ceramic armor"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "counter"
msgstr "comptoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "counter"
msgid ""
"A plain wooden countertop, either free-standing or affixed to a wall.  Makes "
"a decent surface for storage or crafting."
msgstr ""
"Comptoir en bois simple, indépendant ou fixé au mur. Il constitue une surface "
"décente pour le stockage ou le bricolage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cupboard"
msgstr "placard"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cupboard"
msgid "Store your cups.  Or other things, if you're feeling wild."
msgstr ""
"Un endroit où stocker vos assiettes, verres et tasses, ou tout autre chose "
"que vous voulez mettre à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "closed counter gate"
msgstr "porte de compteur fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "closed counter gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind "
"counters.  It's currently closed."
msgstr ""
"Porte battante en bois de qualité commerciale permettant de passer derrière "
"les comptoirs. Elle est actuellement fermée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open counter gate"
msgstr "porte de comptoir ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open counter gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial-quality swinging door made of wood that allows passage behind "
"counters.  It's open, allowing passage."
msgstr ""
"Une porte battante en bois de qualité commerciale qui permet de passer "
"derrière les comptoirs. Elle est ouverte, ce qui permet le passage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "desk"
msgstr "bureau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "desk"
msgid ""
"A wooden desk with drawers.  You could decorate it with trinkets, eat a meal "
"off it, use it as a workbench, read a book, write in a journal, put a laptop "
"on it, put your feet up, rest your head for a nap if you're sitting down… who "
"knew desks were so useful?"
msgstr ""
"Un bureau en bois avec des tiroirs. On peut le décorer avec des bibelots, y "
"prendre un repas, s'en servir comme établi, lire un livre, écrire dans un "
"journal, y poser un ordinateur portable, y mettre ses pieds, y reposer sa "
"tête pour une sieste si on est assis... qui aurait cru que les bureaux "
"étaient si utiles ?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "workbench"
msgstr "établi"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "workbench"
msgid ""
"A sturdy workbench built out of metal.  It is perfect for crafting large and "
"heavy things."
msgstr ""
"Un établi solide fait de métal. Il est parfait pour fabriquer des objets "
"larges et lourds. "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "leather tarp"
msgid_plural "leather tarps"
msgstr[0] "bâche de sol en cuir"
msgstr[1] "bâches de sol en cuir"
msgstr[2] "bâches de sol en cuir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "leather tarp"
msgid ""
"A large sheet of leather lying on the ground.  You could use it as a picnic "
"blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering as it does not "
"soak up blood."
msgstr ""
"Une grande feuille de cuir posée sur le sol. Vous pouvez l'utiliser comme "
"couverture de pique-nique, mais elle est plus utile comme surface de "
"boucherie car elle n'absorbe pas le sang."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "plastic groundsheet"
msgstr "bâche de sol en plastique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "plastic groundsheet"
msgid ""
"A large sheet of thick plastic lying on the ground.  It could be a useful "
"surface for butchering, perhaps."
msgstr ""
"Une grande feuille de plastique épais gît sur le sol. Ce pourrait être une "
"surface utile pour la boucherie, peut-être."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "whuff!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "crinkle."
msgstr "froissement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fiber mat"
msgid_plural "fiber mats"
msgstr[0] "tapis en fibre"
msgstr[1] "tapis en fibre"
msgstr[2] "tapis en fibre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fiber mat"
msgid ""
"A large mat woven from fibrous material.  You could use it as a picnic "
"blanket, but it's more valuable as a surface for butchering.  Too thin to be "
"used as a comfortable sleeping mat."
msgstr ""
"Un grand tapis tissé à partir d'un matériau fibreux. On peut l'utiliser comme "
"couverture de pique-nique, mais il est plus utile comme surface de boucherie. "
"Il est trop fin pour être utilisé comme tapis de couchage confortable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "folding table"
msgid_plural "folding tables"
msgstr[0] "table pliante"
msgstr[1] "tables pliantes"
msgstr[2] "tables pliantes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "folding table"
msgid ""
"A small metal folding table, ideal for off-road trips.  Can be used as a "
"workbench in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Une petite table pliante en métal, idéale pour les voyages hors route. Peut "
"servir d'établi en cas de besoin."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "table"
msgstr "table"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "table"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden table.  You could sit down at it to eat like a civilized "
"person."
msgstr ""
"Une table en bois standard. On peut s'y asseoir pour manger comme une "
"personne civilisée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/json/items/vehicle/tables.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fancy table"
msgid_plural "fancy tables"
msgstr[0] "table fantaisie"
msgstr[1] "tables fantaisie"
msgstr[2] "tables fantaisie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fancy table"
msgid ""
"A fancy table for a fancy person.  Functions as both a table and status "
"symbol."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "coffee table"
msgstr "table basse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "coffee table"
msgid ""
"A low table usually found in living rooms, it makes an ideal surface for "
"playing games, showing off some tasteful books, or presumably for putting "
"coffee cups on.  No one cares if you use a coaster anymore."
msgstr ""
"Cette table basse, que l'on trouve généralement dans les salons, constitue "
"une surface idéale pour jouer à des jeux, exposer des livres de bon goût ou, "
"vraisemblablement, poser des tasses à café. Plus personne ne se soucie de "
"savoir si vous utilisez un sous-verre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_habitat.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal table"
msgstr "table en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-surfaces.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal table"
msgid "A serviceable but simple table made of scrap metal."
msgstr "Une table simple mais utilisable, fabriquée à partir de ferraille."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tatami mat"
msgstr "tatami"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tatami mat"
msgid "A type of mat used as a flooring material in traditional Japanese-style rooms."
msgstr ""
"Type de tapis utilisé comme revêtement de sol dans les pièces traditionnelles "
"de style japonais."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pillow fort"
msgstr "châteaux en oreillers"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pillow fort"
msgid "A comfy place to hide from the world.  Not very defensible, though."
msgstr ""
"Un endroit confortable pour se cacher du monde. Mais il n'est pas très facile "
"à défendre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "paf!"
msgstr "paf!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cardboard fort"
msgstr "châteaux en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard fort"
msgid ""
"A fort built by tipping a cardboard box on its side, lining it with blankets, "
"and partly weather-sealing it with a plastic sheet."
msgstr ""
"Un fort construit en basculant une boîte en carton sur le côté, en la "
"tapissant de couvertures et en l'étanchéifiant partiellement avec une feuille "
"de plastique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cardboard wall"
msgstr "mur en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard wall"
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall."
msgstr ""
"Une pile de boîtes en carton qui ont été remplies de chiffons et de ferraille "
"et empilées comme des briques pour former un mur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cardboard floor"
msgstr "sol en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard floor"
msgid ""
"A flat floor made of sheets of cardboard duct-taped together, covering a "
"plastic sheet on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Un sol plat fait de feuilles de carton collées les unes aux autres, "
"recouvrant une feuille de plastique posée sur le sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cardboard roof"
msgstr "toit en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard roof"
msgid ""
"A sloped roof made of cardboard boxes, stuffed with scrap cardboard and paper "
"and layered atop each other.  Sheets of plastic are carefully arranged on top "
"to shed water.  It looks like it could last a season or two at least before "
"crumbling."
msgstr ""
"Un toit en pente fait de boîtes en carton, remplies de vieux cartons et de "
"papier et superposées les unes aux autres. Des feuilles de plastique sont "
"soigneusement disposées sur le toit pour évacuer l'eau. Il semble qu'il "
"puisse durer au moins une saison ou deux avant de s'effondrer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "cardboard door"
msgstr "porte en carton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been cut "
"open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is open."
msgstr ""
"Une pile de boîtes en carton remplies de chiffons et de bric-à-brac et "
"empilées comme des briques pour former un mur. Le plus grand carton a été "
"découpé et plié pour former une porte de fortune, qui est ouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "cardboard door"
msgid ""
"A pile of cardboard boxes that have been filled with rags and junk and "
"stacked together like bricks to form a wall.  The largest box has been cut "
"open and folded to form a makeshift door, which is closed."
msgstr ""
"Une pile de boîtes en carton qui ont été remplies de chiffons et de "
"bric-à-brac et empilées comme des briques pour former un mur. Le plus grand "
"carton a été ouvert et plié pour former une porte de fortune, qui est fermée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "beaded curtain"
msgstr "rideau de perle"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "beaded curtain"
msgid ""
"A curtain of wooden beads, thick enough that you can't see through them.  "
"They could be pulled aside effortlessly."
msgstr ""
"Un rideau de perles de bois, suffisamment épais pour qu'on ne puisse pas voir "
"à travers. On peut les écarter sans effort."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack"
msgstr "clickity clack… clack… clack"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clickity clack… clack"
msgstr "clickity clack… clack"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open beaded curtain"
msgstr "rideau de perle ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open beaded curtain"
msgid "A curtain of wooden beads that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Un rideau de perles en bois qui a été écarté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "clickity clack… clack… clack!"
msgstr "clickity clack… clack… clack!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "canvas floor"
msgstr "sol en toile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas floor"
msgid ""
"Flooring made out of stretched, waterproof cloth.  Helps keep dirt out of the "
"tent."
msgstr ""
"Plancher en tissu tendu et imperméable. Il empêche la saleté de pénétrer dans "
"la tente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "canvas wall"
msgstr "mur en toile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
msgid "A tent wall made of stretched, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "Un mur de tente composé d'une toile fine en tissu étanche."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas wall"
msgid "A tent wall made of stretched, heavy-duty, waterproof cloth."
msgstr "Une paroi de tente faite d'une toile tendue, résistante et imperméable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "large skin wall"
msgstr "long mur de peau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large skin wall"
msgid ""
"A large tent wall made out of stretched animal skin.  It'll keep the rain "
"out, but anything trying to get in could rip through it fairly easily."
msgstr ""
"Un grand mur de tente fait de peau d'animal tendue. Il empêchera la pluie de "
"pénétrer, mais tout ce qui essaiera d'y entrer pourra le déchirer assez "
"facilement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "large skin groundsheet"
msgstr "grand tapis de sol en peau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large skin groundsheet"
msgid "A large animal-skin groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the shelter."
msgstr ""
"Un grand tapis de sol en peau d'animal pour garder les pieds au sec à "
"l'intérieur de l'abri."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "large animalskin flap"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large animalskin flap"
msgid "A large animal-skin flap that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Un grand rabat en peau d'animal qui peut être tiré sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open animalskin flap"
msgstr "porte ouverte en peau de bête"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open animalskin flap"
msgid "A large animal-skin flap that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Un grand rabat en peau d'animal qui a été écarté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "canvas flap"
msgstr "porte en toile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
msgid "A canvas flap door that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Une porte à rabat en toile qui peut être tirée sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "open canvas flap"
msgstr "porte en toile ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
msgid "A canvas flap door that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Une porte à rabat en toile qui a été tirée sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "canvas flap"
msgid "A heavy canvas flap door that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Une porte à rabat en toile épaisse qui peut être tirée sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open canvas flap"
msgid "A heavy canvas flap door that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Une porte à rabat en toile lourde qui a été tirée sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "groundsheet"
msgstr "bâche de sol"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
msgid "A plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the tent."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis de sol en plastique pour garder les pieds au sec à l'intérieur de la "
"tente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
msgid "A large plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the tent."
msgstr ""
"Un grand tapis de sol en plastique pour garder les pieds au sec à l'intérieur "
"de la tente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "groundsheet"
msgid ""
"A government-issue plastic groundsheet to keep your feet dry, it was clearly "
"made by the lowest bidder."
msgstr ""
"Un drap de sol en plastique délivré par le gouvernement pour garder les pieds "
"au sec, qui a manifestement été fabriqué par le plus bas soumissionnaire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "animalskin wall"
msgstr "mur en peau de bête"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin wall"
msgid ""
"A tent wall made out of stretched animal skin.  It'll keep the rain out, but "
"anything trying to get in could rip through it fairly easily."
msgstr ""
"Un mur de tente fait de peau d'animal tendue. Il empêchera la pluie de "
"pénétrer, mais tout ce qui essaiera d'y entrer pourra le déchirer assez "
"facilement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "animalskin flap"
msgstr "porte en peau de bête"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin flap"
msgid "An animal-skin flap that can be pulled aside."
msgstr "Un rabat en peau d'animal qui peut être tiré sur le côté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "open animalskin flap"
msgid "An animal-skin flap that has been pulled aside."
msgstr "Rabat en peau d'animal qui a été écarté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "animalskin floor"
msgstr "sol en peau de bête"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "animalskin floor"
msgid "An animal-skin groundsheet to keep your feet dry inside the shelter."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis de sol en peau d'animal pour garder les pieds au sec à l'intérieur "
"de l'abri."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of rubble"
msgstr "tas de décombres"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rubble"
msgid ""
"A pile of various metals, bricks, and other building materials.  You could "
"clear it with a shovel."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de métaux, de briques et d'autres matériaux de construction. On peut "
"le déblayer avec une pelle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of rocky rubble"
msgstr "tas de gravats"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of rocky rubble"
msgid "A loose pile of rocks.  Useless?"
msgstr "Une pile de fragments de roches. Inutile?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of trashy rubble"
msgstr "pile de déchets"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of trashy rubble"
msgid ""
"A pile of trash topped with dirt and grass.  It smells gross, but one man's "
"trash…"
msgstr ""
"Un tas d'ordures recouvert de terre et d'herbe.  Ça sent mauvais, mais la "
"poubelle de quelqu'un…"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal wreckage"
msgstr "débris en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal wreckage"
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal wreckage from a plane"
msgid ""
"A pile of various bent and twisted metals.  Some of it looks pretty rusty, "
"you wouldn't want to cut yourself on this."
msgstr ""
"A pile of various bent and twisted metals.  Some of it looks pretty rusty, "
"you wouldn't want to cut yourself on this."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal wreckage from a plane"
msgstr "débris métalliques issus d'un avion"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_spaceship_machinery.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_spaceship_machinery.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "radioactive slag"
msgstr "débris radioactifs"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "radioactive slag"
msgid ""
"A pile of melted slag from a destroyed nuclear reactor.  What are you doing "
"looking at it?  Get the hell out of here, you nutcase!"
msgstr ""
"Un tas de scories fondues provenant d'un réacteur nucléaire détruit. "
"Qu'est-ce que tu fais à regarder ça ? Fous le camp d'ici, espèce de cinglé !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "pile of ash"
msgstr "tas de cendres"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "pile of ash"
msgid "A pile of ash, from wood or possibly corpses."
msgstr "Un tas de cendres, de bois ou peut-être de cadavres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "small boulder"
msgstr "petit rocher"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "small boulder"
msgid ""
"A big rock.  Should be easy to roll around, but too heavy to carry with you.  "
"It can be used as a primitive anvil, or broken into a bunch of smaller rocks."
msgstr ""
"Un gros rocher. Assez facile à pousser, mais trop lourd pour être porté. Vous "
"pourriez l'utiliser comme un enclume primitive, ou le briser en morceaux plus "
"petits."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "medium boulder"
msgstr "rocher moyen"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "medium boulder"
msgid ""
"A pretty big boulder, but still small enough to see and climb over.  It would "
"be a struggle to move it.  It can be used as a primitive anvil, or broken "
"into a bunch of smaller rocks."
msgstr ""
"Un rocher assez gros, mais suffisamment petit pour qu'on puisse le voir et "
"l'escalader. Il serait difficile de le déplacer. Il peut servir d'enclume "
"primitive ou être brisé en un tas de rochers plus petits."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "large boulder"
msgstr "grand rocher"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "large boulder"
msgid "A boulder that's taller than you.  Now how are you going to move this?"
msgstr "Un rocher plus grand que vous. Comment allez-vous le déplacer ?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "street light"
msgstr "réverbère"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "street light"
msgid ""
"A raised light source which used to illuminate streets and their surrounding "
"area, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr ""
"Une source de lumière surélevée qui servait à éclairer les rues et leurs "
"environs, mais qui ne sert à rien sans électricité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "traffic light"
msgstr "feu de signalisation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "traffic light"
msgid ""
"A signaling device positioned at road intersections and pedestrian crossings "
"to control the flow of traffic, but it's useless without electricity."
msgstr ""
"Un dispositif de signalisation placé aux intersections routières et aux "
"passages pour piétons pour contrôler le flux de la circulation, mais il est "
"inutile sans électricité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#: data/json/items/vehicle/cargo.json data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "bike rack"
msgid_plural "bike racks"
msgstr[0] "porte-vélo"
msgstr[1] "porte-vélos"
msgstr[2] "porte-vélos"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "bike rack"
msgid "A loop of metal in the shape of an upside down U used to securely park bikes."
msgstr ""
"Une boucle de métal en forme de U renversé utilisée pour garer les vélos en "
"toute sécurité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "flagpole"
msgstr "mât de drapeau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
msgid "A 6-meter tall metal flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr "Un mât métallique de 6 mètres de haut. On peut y hisser un drapeau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "flagpole"
msgid "A 5-meter tall wooden flagpole.  You could hoist up a flag here."
msgstr "Un mât en bois de 5 mètres de haut. On peut y hisser un drapeau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "utility pole"
msgstr "poteau électrique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "utility pole"
msgid ""
"A long wooden post which used to support overhead power lines and other "
"public utilities, but it doesn't work anymore."
msgstr ""
"Un long poteau en bois qui servait à soutenir les lignes électriques "
"aériennes et d'autres services publics, mais qui ne fonctionne plus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "scrap metal bridge"
msgstr "pont en ferraille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "scrap metal bridge"
msgid "A simple bridge made of riveted sheet metal."
msgstr "Un simple pont en tôle rivetée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "room divider"
msgstr "cloison de séparation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "room divider"
msgid "A tall piece of furniture used to divide rooms into separate areas."
msgstr "Un meuble haut utilisé pour diviser les pièces en zones distinctes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "short mound of dirt"
msgstr "petit monticule de terre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-terrains.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "short mound of dirt"
msgid ""
"An area of heaped dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr ""
"Un monticule de terre, assez difficile à traverser, mais un bon endroit ou "
"planter des graines."

