"An old machinery part, cut and smoothed to make a serviceable anvil, and "
"mounted to a heavy log stand."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "still"
msgid_plural "stills"
msgstr[0] "alambic"
msgstr[1] "alambics"
msgstr[2] "alambics"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "still"
msgid ""
"An essential component for brewing and chemistry that allows for refining "
"liquid mixtures."
msgstr ""
"Un composant essentiel pour la brasserie et la chimie qui permet d'affiner "
"les mélanges liquides."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "screw press"
msgid_plural "screw presses"
msgstr[0] "presse a vis"
msgstr[1] "presses a vis"
msgstr[2] "presses a vis"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "screw press"
msgid ""
"A large screw press for manually pressing oil out of fruit or seed paste.  "
"The paste is placed in wetted bags and pressed down by the force of the screw "
"mechanism."
msgstr ""
"Une grande presse à vis manuelle pour extraire l'huile de fruits ou de pâte "
"de graines. La pâte est placée dans des sacs humidifiés et pressée par la "
"force du mécanisme à vis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "charcoal kiln"
msgstr "four à charbon"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled charcoal kiln"
msgid ""
"A primitive rock kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into "
"charcoal in the absence of oxygen.  It isn't especially efficient compared to "
"a modern metal variant."
msgstr ""
"Un four primitif en pierre conçu pour brûler du bois et du matériel organique "
"en charbon de bois en l'absence d'oxygène. Il n'est pas particulièrement "
"efficace par rapport à une variante moderne en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled charcoal kiln"
msgstr "four à charbon rempli"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "Four à charbon en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal charcoal kiln"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgid ""
"A metal kiln designed to burn wood and organic material into charcoal in the "
"absence of oxygen.  Much more efficient than its archaic rock counterpart."
msgstr ""
"Un four à charbon de bois en métal conçu pour brûler du bois et du matériel "
"organique en charbon de bois en l'absence d'oxygène. Beaucoup plus efficace "
"que son équivalent archaïque en pierre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled metal charcoal kiln"
msgstr "four à charbon, en métal rempli"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "arc furnace"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled arc furnace"
msgid ""
"An arc furnace designed to burn a powdery mix of coke and limestone to create "
"calcium carbide."
msgstr "Four à arc électrique pour la production de carbure de calcium"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled arc furnace"
msgstr "four à arc électrique rempli"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "smoking rack"
msgstr "fumoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  "
"Works as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Un fumoir en bois conçu pour fumer les aliments afin de mieux les conserver "
"et d'améliorer leur goût. Fonctionne comme un fumoir à charbon de bois dans "
"la préparation des recettes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "spinning wheel"
msgid_plural "spinning wheels"
msgstr[0] "roue tournante"
msgstr[1] "roues tournantes"
msgstr[2] "roues tournantes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "spinning wheel"
msgid ""
"A large wooden device with a mechanical wheel used to combine fibers together "
"into a stronger material."
msgstr ""
"Un grand appareil en bois avec une roue mécanique utilisé pour combiner des "
"fibres en un matériau plus résistant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stationary scutcher"
msgid_plural "stationary scutchers"
msgstr[0] "teilleuse stationnaire"
msgstr[1] "teilleuses stationnaires"
msgstr[2] "teilleuses stationnaires"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "stationary scutcher"
msgid ""
"A bulky, simple-hinged wooden device to break up the hard parts of fiber "
"plants, with nail combs on the back for separating them out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active smoking rack"
msgstr "fumoir en cours d'utilisation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A wooden rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It "
"is lit and smoking."
msgstr ""
"Un fumoir en bois conçu pour fumer les aliments afin de mieux les conserver "
"et d'améliorer leur goût. Il est allumé et fume."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal smoking rack"
msgid_plural "metal smoking racks"
msgstr[0] "fumoir en métal"
msgstr[1] "fumoirs en métal"
msgstr[2] "fumoirs en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal smoking rack"
msgid ""
"A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  Works "
"as a charcoal smoker in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Un fumoir en métal conçu pour fumer les aliments afin de mieux les conserver "
"et d'améliorer leur goût. Fonctionne comme un fumoir à charbon de bois dans "
"la préparation des recettes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active metal smoking rack"
msgstr "Fumoir en métal actif"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active metal smoking rack"
msgid "A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste."
msgstr ""
"Un support métallique destiné à fumer les aliments pour une meilleure "
"conservation et un meilleur arôme."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rock forge"
msgstr "forge en pierre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rock forge"
msgid ""
"A metalworking station made of rock, typically used in combination with an "
"anvil.  Works as a charcoal forge in crafting recipes."
msgstr ""
"Une forge en pierre conçue pour permettre le travail des métaux et "
"normalement utilisée en tandem avec une enclume.  Fonctionne de façon "
"identique à une forge à charbon de bois dans les recettes de fabrication."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "clay kiln"
msgstr "four à argile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "clay kiln"
msgid "A kiln designed to bake clay pottery and bricks."
msgstr "Un four conçu pour cuire de la poterie en argile et des briques."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden stepladder"
msgid_plural "wooden stepladders"
msgstr[0] "escabeau en bois"
msgstr[1] "escabeaux en bois"
msgstr[2] "escabeaux en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden stepladder"
msgid ""
"A short, foldable wooden ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe "
"slow something down."
msgstr ""
"Une petite échelle en bois pliable. Peut vous aider à monter sur un toit ou "
"peut-être ralentir quelque chose."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum stepladder"
msgid_plural "aluminum stepladders"
msgstr[0] "escabeau en aluminium"
msgstr[1] "escabeaux en aluminium"
msgstr[2] "escabeaux en aluminium"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "aluminum stepladder"
msgid ""
"A short, foldable aluminum ladder.  Can help you climb to a rooftop, or maybe "
"slow something down."
msgstr ""
"Une petite échelle pliable en aluminium. Peut vous aider à monter sur un toit "
"ou peut-être ralentir quelque chose."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Beverly shear"
msgid_plural "Beverly shears"
msgstr[0] "cisaille stationnaire"
msgstr[1] "cisailles stationnaires"
msgstr[2] "cisailles stationnaires"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "Beverly shear"
#. ~ Description of "Beverly shear"
msgid ""
"A massive bench-mounted device with a short guillotine blade mounted to a "
"long lever.  Designed for making straight or curved cuts through sheet metal "
"up to 3 millimeters thick."
msgstr ""
"Un grand appareil de table avec une courte lame de guillotine montée sur un "
"long levier. Conçu pour effectuer des découpes droites ou courbes dans des "
"tôles de métal jusqu'à 3 millimètres d'épaisseur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "drill press"
msgid ""
"A powerful drill mounted on a slide that lets it drop precisely down.  Useful "
"in all kinds of projects from industrial fabrication to home woodworking.  "
"You can take this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"ne perceuse puissante montée sur un rail coulissant qui lui permet de "
"descendre précisément. Utile dans tous les types de projets, de la "
"fabrication industrielle au bricolage à la maison. Vous pouvez la démonter et "
"la brancher sur votre propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "firefly terrarium"
msgstr "terrarium à luciole"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "firefly terrarium"
msgid ""
"While many survivors would have focused on trying to bring back electric "
"lights, whoever lives here has apparently decided to make use of the changes "
"wrought by the Cataclysm to provide light.  This vivarium contains soil, "
"strange plants you don't recognize immediately, and most strikingly, a giant "
"mutant firefly."
msgstr ""
"Bien que la plupart des survivants aurait plutôt essayé d'utiliser des "
"lumières électriques, ceci est le fruit d'une exploitation astucieuse du "
"nouveau monde du Cataclysme pour illuminer les environs.  Ce vivarium "
"contient de la terre, des plantes étranges n'ayant pas l'air totalement "
"naturelles une énorme luciole mutant virevoltant ici et là."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "table saw"
msgid ""
"A rotating sawblade set into a large, flat table, for making straight "
"measured cuts.  It's a key tool in any carpenter's arsenal.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Une lame de scie circulaire montée sur une grande table plate, pour effectuer "
"des coupes droites mesurées. C'est un outil clé dans l'arsenal de tout "
"charpentier. Vous pouvez la démonter et la brancher sur votre propre réseau "
"électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mitre saw"
msgid ""
"A circular sawblade on an arm that can slide and rotate in several "
"directions, this is a staple tool for nearly any carpentry.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Une lame de scie circulaire montée sur un bras qui peut glisser et pivoter "
"dans plusieurs directions. C'est un outil indispensable pour presque tous les "
"travaux de menuiserie. Vous pouvez la démonter et la brancher sur votre "
"propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "band saw"
msgid ""
"A ribbonlike sawblade runs in a single direction in this tool, allowing "
"precise cuts at almost any angle.  You can take this down and plug it into "
"your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Une lame de scie en forme de ruban se déplace dans une seule direction dans "
"cet outil, permettant des coupes précises à presque tous les angles. Vous "
"pouvez la démonter et la brancher sur votre propre réseau électrique pour "
"l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "router table"
msgid ""
"This table has an inset router, a rotating motor with an exchangeable blade "
"head for cutting specific profiles and grooves and stuff.  You can take this "
"down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Cette table possède une fraiseuse à panneaux intégrée, un moteur rotatif avec "
"une tête de lame interchangeable pour découper des profils et des rainures "
"spécifiques. Vous pouvez la démonter et la brancher sur votre propre réseau "
"électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "planer"
msgid ""
"A hefty tool that will take in a board and cut it smooth and flat to a "
"specific width, particularly great if working with raw lumber stock, but also "
"good just for shaving wood down to size.  You can take this down and plug it "
"into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un outil robuste qui peut prendre une planche et la raboter pour lui donner "
"une surface lisse et plate à une largeur spécifique. Particulièrement utile "
"pour travailler avec du bois brut, mais aussi pour raboter du bois à la "
"taille souhaitée. Vous pouvez le démonter et le brancher sur votre propre "
"réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "jointer"
msgid ""
"A table-shaped tool with a rotating blade that will cut down, smooth out, and "
"square off a board to make it very smooth and nice indeed.  You can take this "
"down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Une table équipée d'une lame rotative qui peut raboter, lisser et équarrir "
"une planche pour lui donner un aspect très lisse et agréable. Vous pouvez la "
"démonter et la brancher sur votre propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
msgstr "réacteur de craquage catalytique déconnecté"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "disconnected catalytic cracking reactor"
msgid ""
"A makeshift extraction system, or as makeshift as you can consider something "
"that was purpose-built in a laboratory by a group of experts.  You can take "
"this down and plug it into your own power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un système d'extraction de fortune, ou aussi improvisé que vous pouvez "
"considérer quelque chose qui a été construit spécialement dans un laboratoire "
"par un groupe d'experts. Vous pouvez le démonter et le brancher sur votre "
"propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hydraulic press"
msgid ""
"If you really want to squash something a lot, this would be exactly the right "
"industrial tool for you.  You can take this down and plug it into your own "
"power grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Si vous voulez vraiment écraser quelque chose de manière importante, ce "
"serait exactement l'outil industriel idéal pour vous. Vous pouvez le démonter "
"et le brancher sur votre propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/fake.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "power lathe"
msgid_plural "power lathes"
msgstr[0] "tour à métaux"
msgstr[1] "tours à métaux"
msgstr[2] "tours à métaux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "power lathe"
msgid ""
"An industrial-grade lathe, for turning chunks of metal and other hard things "
"into round chunks of metal and other hard things."
msgstr ""
"Un tour à métaux industriel, pour transformer des morceaux de métal et "
"d'autres matériaux durs en morceaux ronds de métal et d'autres matériaux durs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "air compressor"
msgid ""
"This durable tank is topped with a motor that will cram as much air into the "
"tank as possible.  You can take this down and plug it into your own power "
"grid to use it."
msgstr ""
"Ce réservoir durable est surmonté d'un moteur qui va pousser autant d'air que "
"possible dans le réservoir. Vous pouvez le démonter et le brancher sur votre "
"propre réseau électrique pour l'utiliser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "manual tire changer"
msgid_plural "manual tire changers"
msgstr[0] "démonte-pneus manuel"
msgstr[1] "démonte-pneus manuels"
msgstr[2] "démonte-pneus manuels"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "manual tire changer"
msgid ""
"This floor-mounted machine contains all the levers, clamps and mounts "
"required to remove or fit a tire, plus an integrated foot pump to inflate it."
msgstr ""
"Cette machine montée au sol contient tous les leviers, pinces et supports "
"nécessaires pour retirer ou monter un pneu, ainsi qu'une pompe à pied "
"intégrée pour le gonfler."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "fermenting vat"
msgstr "cuve de fermentation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled fermenting vat"
msgid "A sealable 50-liter vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic brews."
msgstr ""
"Une cuve étanche de 50 litres pour la fermentation du vinaigre et de diverses "
"boissons alcoolisées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled fermenting vat"
msgstr "cuve de fermentation remplie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "cuve de fermentation en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wooden fermenting vat"
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled wooden fermenting vat"
msgid ""
"A sealable 50-liter wooden vat for fermenting vinegar and various alcoholic "
"brews."
msgstr ""
"Une cuve en bois de 50 litres pour la fermentation du vinaigre et de diverses "
"boissons alcoolisées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled wooden fermenting vat"
msgstr "cuve en bois remplie pour la fermentation."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "anaerobic digester"
msgstr "digesteur anaérobique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "anaerobic digester"
msgid "A 1000 L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "Un digesteur anaérobique de 1000L."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "filled anaerobic digester"
msgstr "digesteur anaérobique rempli"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "filled anaerobic digester"
msgid "A 1000L anaerobic digester."
msgstr "Un digesteur anaérobique de 1000L rempli."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "butchering rack"
msgstr "étal de boucher"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "butchering rack"
msgid "A wooden butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air."
msgstr "Étal de boucher en bois conçu pour suspendre une carcasse dans l'air."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal butchering rack"
msgid_plural "metal butchering racks"
msgstr[0] "étal de boucher en métal"
msgstr[1] "étal de boucher en métal"
msgstr[2] "étal de boucher en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "metal butchering rack"
msgid ""
"A metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It can be "
"deconstructed and folded for easy transportation."
msgstr ""
"Étal de boucher en métal conçu pour suspendre une carcasse dans l'air. Il "
"peut être démonté et plié pour un transport facile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "hanging meathook"
msgstr "crochet de boucher"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "hanging meathook"
msgid "A hefty hook suspended from a chain for stringing up corpses."
msgstr "Un crochet robuste suspendu à une chaîne pour pendre des cadavres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wind mill"
msgid_plural "wind mills"
msgstr[0] "moulin à vent"
msgstr[1] "moulins à vent"
msgstr[2] "moulins à vent"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "wind mill"
msgid "A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "Un petit moulin à vent capable de transformer des produits amylacés en farine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active wind mill"
msgstr "moulin à vent actif"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active wind mill"
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its "
"brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr ""
"Un petit moulin à vent capable de transformer des produits amylacés en "
"farine. Son frein a été retiré et il tourne."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "water mill"
msgid_plural "water mills"
msgstr[0] "moulin hydraulique"
msgstr[1] "moulins hydrauliques"
msgstr[2] "moulins hydrauliques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "water mill"
msgid "A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour."
msgstr "Un petit moulin à eau capable de transformer des produits amylacés en farine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active water mill"
msgstr "Moulin à eau actif"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active water mill"
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Its "
"brake has been removed and it is turning."
msgstr ""
"Un petit moulin à eau actif capable de transformer des produits amylacés en "
"farine."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "automated gas console"
msgstr "Console de gaz automatisée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "automated gas console"
msgid "An automated gas flow control console."
msgstr "Une console de contrôle de débit de gaz automatisée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken automated gas console"
msgstr "Une console de contrôle de débit de gaz automatisée en panne"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken automated gas console"
msgid ""
"An automated gas flow control console.  It's broken.  This is not a good "
"thing."
msgstr ""
"Une console de contrôle de débit de gaz automatisée en panne. Ce n'est pas "
"une bonne chose."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "reinforced vending machine"
msgstr "distributeur automatique renforcé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine"
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  That just makes "
"it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't it?"
msgstr ""
"Un peu plus difficile à ouvrir qu'un distributeur automatique ordinaire. Cela "
"le rend d'autant plus attrayant comme cible, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "reinforced vending machine (off)"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "reinforced vending machine (off)"
msgid ""
"A bit tougher to crack open than a regular vending machine.  Out of order, "
"for lack of power.  That just makes it all the sweeter of a target, doesn't "
"it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vending machine"
msgstr "distributeur automatique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  The goods inside can be "
"yours if you have money on a cash card."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire verticale en métal avec une porte transparente. Les biens à "
"l'intérieur peuvent être à vous si vous avez de l'argent sur une carte de "
"crédit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vending machine (off)"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vending machine (off)"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  Out of order, for lack of "
"power."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "broken vending machine"
msgstr "distributeur automatique cassé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "broken vending machine"
msgid ""
"An upright metal cabinet with a see-through door.  It's smashed open, so you "
"can take whatever you want for free."
msgstr ""
"Traduction :\n"
"\"Une armoire verticale en métal avec une porte transparente. Elle est grande "
"ouverte, vous pouvez donc prendre ce que vous voulez gratuitement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "grappling hook"
msgid_plural "grappling hooks"
msgstr[0] "grappin"
msgstr[1] "grappins"
msgstr[2] "grappins"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "grappling hook"
msgid ""
"A dangling piece of rope, hooked securely to something above you.  You could "
"climb up or take it down."
msgstr ""
"Une corde pendante, accrochée solidement à quelque chose au-dessus de vous. "
"Vous pouvez grimper ou la descendre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "vine leading up"
msgstr "liane grimpante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "vine leading up"
msgid ""
"A thick vine is rigidly anchored to something above you.  It looks quite "
"alive.  You could climb up or tear it down."
msgstr ""
"Une épaisse liane est solidement ancrée à quelque chose au-dessus de vous. "
"Elle a l'air très vivante. Vous pouvez grimper ou la déchirer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "twang."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "web leading up"
msgstr "une toile d'araignée qui s'éleve"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "web leading up"
msgid ""
"A thick, dangling strand of slightly sticky web, the other end is tied "
"securely to something above you.  You could use it to climb up."
msgstr ""
"Un épais fil de soie collant, suspendu dans l'air, avec l'autre extrémité "
"solidement attachée à quelque chose au-dessus de vous. Vous pourriez "
"l'utiliser pour grimper."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rope hoist"
msgstr "palan à corde"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rope hoist"
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, using a sturdy horizontal support as a basic "
"pulley.  While crude, it gives you some mechanical advantage for lifting "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Une boucle de corde pend ici, utilisant un support horizontal robuste comme "
"poulie de base. Bien qu'il soit rudimentaire, il vous offre un certain "
"avantage mécanique pour soulever des objets."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "rope and tackle hoist"
msgstr "Treuil à corde et poulie"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "rope and tackle hoist"
msgid ""
"A loop of rope hangs here, looped through a quality tackle to give a "
"significant mechanical advantage while lifting heavy objects."
msgstr ""
"Une boucle de corde pend ici, passée à travers un système de poulies de "
"qualité pour offrir un avantage mécanique significatif lors du levage "
"d'objets lourds."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "chain hoist"
msgstr "palan à chaîne"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-tools.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chain hoist"
msgid ""
"A sturdy chain and heavy tackle hang well-supported from the ceiling here, "
"ready to lift most heavy items you could think of using mechanical advantage."
msgstr ""
"Une chaîne robuste et un treuil lourd pendent solidement du plafond ici, "
"prêts à soulever la plupart des objets lourds que vous pourriez imaginer en "
"utilisant un avantage mécanique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "illuminating plant bulb"
msgstr "Ampoule végétale illuminée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "illuminating plant bulb"
msgid ""
"A small plant grows among the roots here, its green, onion-like bulb "
"illuminating the area around it."
msgstr ""
"A small plant grows among the roots here, its green, onion-like bulb "
"illuminating the area around it."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "brambles"
msgstr "ronces"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "brambles"
msgid ""
"A wall of tangled roots blocks the path here, you'd have destroy it to get "
"past."
msgstr ""
"Un mur de racines enchevêtrées bloque le passage ici. Vous devrez le détruire "
"pour passer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "composting midden"
msgstr "dépotoir à compost"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "composting midden"
msgid ""
"A hole has been dug into the roots here, and a pretty unpleasant smell emits "
"from it."
msgstr ""
"Un trou a été creusé dans les racines ici, et une odeur assez désagréable "
"s'en dégage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "active backup generator"
msgstr "générateur de secours allumé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "active backup generator"
msgid ""
"A ubiquitous piece of compact machinery meant for running anything from the "
"bathroom lights to electric stoves and other necessities when grid "
"electricity is unavailable.  This one is currently running.  You can hear it "
"humming slightly when you are very close."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil compact et omniprésent destiné à faire fonctionner n'importe "
"quoi, de l'éclairage de la salle de bain aux cuisinières électriques et "
"autres appareils indispensables lorsque le réseau électrique n'est pas "
"disponible. Celui-ci fonctionne actuellement. Vous pouvez l'entendre "
"bourdonner légèrement lorsque vous êtes très près."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "portable generator"
msgstr "générateur portable"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "portable generator"
msgid "A small, portable generator, one that people buy for a camp."
msgstr ""
"Un petit générateur portable communément utilisé par les campeurs préférant "
"un peu plus de comfort."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "diesel generator"
msgid "Big and powerful generator, used for street works."
msgstr ""
"Un large et puissant générateur fréquemment utilisé par les routiers et "
"travailleurs de chantier."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "military diesel generator"
msgid "Big and powerful generator, painted in camo."
msgstr "Un large et puissant générateur ayant été camouflé avec de la peinture."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_generators.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "powerful gasoline generator"
msgid "Big and powerful, yet portable generator."
msgstr ""
"Un large et puissant générateur, mais tout de même toujours d'une taille et "
"d'un poids raisonnablement transportable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "M224 mortar"
msgstr "mortier M224"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "M224 mortar"
msgid ""
"Deployed and ready to be used 60 mm mortar.  You are lucky you don't need to "
"scavenge actual firing tables, as they are clipped tightly to the mortar "
"itself.  However you can use it only for indirect fire, with a substantial "
"precision loss."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_military.json
#. ~ Message when furniture "M224 mortar"'s examine action fails its condition
msgid "You have absolutely no idea how to use this mortar."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ATM"
msgstr "distributeur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ATM"
msgid ""
"For your banking convenience, this Automated Teller Machine is fully capable "
"of operating autonomously in the event of complete network failure.  You can "
"deposit funds from cash cards and migrate all of your inflation-adjusted "
"earnings to a single card.  This thing has seen better days; there's been a "
"run on the bank, and this machine has the dents and cracks to prove it."
msgstr ""
"Pour votre confort bancaire, ce guichet automatique est entièrement capable "
"de fonctionner de manière autonome en cas de panne totale du réseau. Vous "
"pouvez déposer des fonds à partir de cartes de paiement et transférer tous "
"vos gains ajustés en fonction de l'inflation sur une seule carte. Cet "
"appareil a connu des jours meilleurs ; il y a eu une ruée sur la banque, et "
"cet appareil en porte les traces."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_misc.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ATM"
msgid ""
"Designed to withdraw money from your bank account, this machine is completely "
"dead now, both from having no more power, and having no internet connection "
"to do any withdraws.  While you can deconstruct it, it's effectively just a "
"big pile of metal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "decaying tube"
msgstr "tube en décomposition"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "decaying tube"
msgid "A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor."
msgstr "Une stalagmite de chair en décomposition s'étend du plafond jusqu'au sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "glowing decaying tube"
msgstr "tube en décomposition luminescent"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "glowing decaying tube"
msgid ""
"A decomposing fleshy stalagmite extends from the ceiling to the floor.  "
"Countless glowing spores weft from within, coating everything nearby."
msgstr ""
"Une stalagmite charnue en décomposition s'étend du plafond jusqu'au sol. "
"D'innombrables spores luminescentes s'en dégagent, recouvrant tout ce qui se "
"trouve à proximité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "beautiful nether lily"
msgstr "un lys du néant magnifique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "beautiful nether lily"
msgid ""
"A very tall, mesmerizing blood red flower.  Its beautiful, pristine form is "
"rooted firmly on the innards of the beast.  The flesh around it is decayed, "
"being consumed to feed its ornate, magnanimous body.  You feel an urge to sit "
"and admire this priceless miracle of life."
msgstr ""
"Une fleur d'un rouge sang, très haute et fascinante. Sa forme magnifique et "
"immaculée est enracinée fermement dans les entrailles de la bête. La chair "
"autour d'elle est en décomposition, consommée pour nourrir son corps orné et "
"magnanime. Vous ressentez une envie de vous asseoir et d'admirer ce miracle "
"de la vie sans prix."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a chilling scream!"
msgstr "un cri effroyable!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_floraxeno.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_floraxeno.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "squish!"
msgstr "squish!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You admire the lily.  Isn't it beautiful?"
msgstr ""
"Oui, la fleur est magnifique ! Son rouge sang et sa forme parfaite sont "
"vraiment impressionnants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You worship the lily, and feel truly fulfilled."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You bow to the lily, and gain immense satisfaction in having done so."
msgstr ""
"Vous vous inclinez devant le lys, et éprouvez une immense satisfaction à "
"l'avoir fait."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in effect in EoC "admire_lily_effect" in
#. furniture "beautiful nether lily"'s examine action
msgid "You focus on the lily and realize it truly is perfection *incarnate*."
msgstr ""
"Vous vous concentrez sur le lys et réalisez qu'il est véritablement la "
"perfection incarnée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether grass"
msgstr "herbe du néant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether grass"
msgid ""
"A bed of waist high segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"wade past, they react to your movement and always swivel to face you."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis de plantes bleues segmentées, hautes jusqu'à la taille, qui vous "
"rappellent de l'herbe. En y marchant, elles réagissent à vos mouvements et se "
"tournent toujours vers vous."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "tall nether grass"
msgstr "herbe haute du néant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "tall nether grass"
msgid ""
"A clump of tall, segmented blue plants that remind you of grass.  As you "
"approach, they bend towards you, hugging your body and making movement "
"difficult."
msgstr ""
"Un groupe de plantes bleues segmentées, hautes, qui vous rappellent de "
"l'herbe. En vous approchant, elles se penchent vers vous, vous enlaçant et "
"rendant le mouvement difficile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether patchwork"
msgstr "mosaïque du néant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether patchwork"
msgid ""
"A peculiar plant that is hard to distinguish, resembling a tangled mess of "
"different terrestrial flowers and weeds firmly wedged into the monstrous "
"flesh.  It pulses rhythmically as it rearranges its form into even weirder "
"shapes."
msgstr ""
"Une plante particulière difficile à distinguer, ressemblant à un "
"enchevêtrement de différentes fleurs terrestres et de mauvaises herbes "
"solidement coincées dans la chair monstrueuse. Elle pulse rythmiquement en "
"réorganisant sa forme en des formes encore plus étranges."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "nether lichen"
msgstr "lichen du néant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "nether lichen"
msgid ""
"A bed of orange, flowering lichen, covering the surface of the yellow ichor.  "
"Every now and then, a flower disappears into the liquid, but seems to "
"reappear the moment you look away."
msgstr ""
"Un tapis de lichen orange en fleurs recouvre la surface de l'ichor jaune. De "
"temps en temps, une fleur disparaît dans le liquide, mais semble réapparaître "
"dès que vous détournez le regard."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "refrigerator"
msgstr "réfrigérateur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "refrigerator"
msgid ""
"A standard household refrigerator.  If powered, it will cool its contents to "
"extend the time before they spoil.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it "
"to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "minifridge"
msgid ""
"A small fridge, often used in places where full-size fridge would be too big "
"or too much a hassle to transport, or when you only need a small amount of "
"items chilled.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "single glass door fridge"
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with a thick sheet of glass for a door, used in stores "
"to show off the goods while keeping them cool.  Deconstruct it if you want to "
"connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "double glass door fridge"
msgid ""
"A modern refrigerator with two glass doors, to fit twice as much goods for "
"consumers.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty fridge"
msgid ""
"A heavy, bulky refrigerator, used in professional kitchens.  Deconstruct it "
"if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display fridge"
msgid ""
"A big glass chamber, designed to display different food in multiple rows, "
"while cooling it at the same time.  Looks gorgeous, but has nothing good to "
"show to you.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "minifreezer"
msgid ""
"A small upright freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables long "
"term.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chest minifreezer"
msgid ""
"A small chest freezer, used to store a small amount of perishables for a long "
"time, if you're willing to dig them out each time that is.  Deconstruct it if "
"you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "chest freezer"
msgid ""
"A chest freezer.  Big and power efficient, this is the dream for every "
"Cataclysm survivor.  Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "heavy-duty freezer"
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty upright freezer, one that is used in a professional kitchen.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "glass door freezer"
msgid ""
"A commercial upright freezer, used to show ice creams, frozen veggies, pizza, "
"or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  Deconstruct it if "
"you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "display chest freezer"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_refrigeration.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "display chest freezer"
msgid ""
"A commercial chest freezer, used to show off ice creams, frozen veggies, "
"pizza, or anything else a consumer may want frozen and preserved.  "
"Conveniently tall enough for any curious child to gaze in at the sweets.  "
"Deconstruct it if you want to connect it to the grid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass figure"
msgstr "figure en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a someone frozen halfway through falling backwards, "
"and suspended on a single leg."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne figée à mi-chemin d'une "
"chute en arrière, suspendue sur une seule jambe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "tink."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of a person covering their face with their hands."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne se couvrant le visage "
"avec les mains."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of a child.  It is difficult to make out their facial "
"features, but it seems as if they are smiling."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant un enfant. Il est difficile de "
"distinguer ses traits faciaux, mais il semble sourire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of someone kneeling in prayer."
msgstr "Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne agenouillée en prière."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a firing posture.  Their jagged fingers "
"are frozen squeezing a trigger that isn't there."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne en position de tir. "
"Leurs doigts déchiquetés sont figés en train de serrer une gâchette qui n'est "
"pas là."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone leaning into the space to their right, their "
"fingers bent as if interlaced with someone else's."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne penchée vers l'espace à "
"sa droite, les doigts pliés comme si elle était entrelacée avec quelqu'un "
"d'autre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone clutching at their neck.  A delicate spray of "
"connected glass droplets emerges between their fingers."
msgstr ""
"Une silhouette en verre noir serrant son cou. Un délicat jet de gouttelettes "
"de verre reliées émerge entre ses doigts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"Most of a black glass human figure.  The face and much of the head is "
"missing, as if scooped out, and the inner surface is perfectly smooth."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant la majeure partie d'un humain. Le "
"visage et une grande partie de la tête manquent, comme si elles avaient été "
"évidées, et la surface intérieure est parfaitement lisse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid "A black glass figure of someone doubled over in laughter."
msgstr "Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne pliée en deux de rire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure.  Their features are too jagged to make out clearly, but "
"they remind you of someone you knew."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir. Ses traits sont trop irréguliers pour être "
"clairement distingués, mais ils vous rappellent quelqu'un que vous "
"connaissiez."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass figure"
msgid ""
"A black glass figure of someone in a fighting stance, their face twisted with "
"howls of rage and anger.  They're gripping some sort of weapon that isn't "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Une figurine en verre noir représentant une personne en position de combat, "
"le visage contordu par des hurlements de rage et de colère. Ils serrent une "
"sorte d'arme qui n'est pas là."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bed"
msgstr "lit en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bed"
msgid ""
"A black glass sculpture of a bed.  The rumpled covers are jagged, and "
"splinter at the touch."
msgstr ""
"Une sculpture en verre noir représentant un lit. Les draps froissés sont "
"déchiquetés et s'éclatent au toucher."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clink."
msgstr "clink."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bathtub"
msgstr "baignoire en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bathtub"
msgid ""
"A tub made from black glass, with a frozen column of onyx pouring from the "
"tap."
msgstr ""
"Une baignoire en verre noir, avec une colonne figée d'onyx qui coule du "
"robinet."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass shattering!"
msgstr "bris de verre!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clink!"
msgstr "clink!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dresser"
msgstr "commode en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dresser"
msgid ""
"A black glass cabinet with its doors slightly ajar.  Inside is a row of "
"hangers bearing neatly folded and entirely rigid clothing."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire en verre noir avec ses portes légèrement entrouvertes. À "
"l'intérieur se trouve une rangée de cintres portant des vêtements "
"soigneusement pliés et entièrement rigides."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass refrigerator"
msgstr "réfrigérateur en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass refrigerator"
msgid ""
"A black glass refrigerator, its door hanging open.  Inside is a seamless "
"surface with protrusions resembling fresh fruit and plastic bottles."
msgstr ""
"Un réfrigérateur en verre noir, sa porte pendante ouverte. À l'intérieur se "
"trouve une surface lisse avec des protubérances ressemblant à des fruits "
"frais et des bouteilles en plastique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass armchair"
msgstr "fauteuil en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass armchair"
msgid ""
"An armchair that was presumably once very plush and comfortable.  Now the "
"overstuffed cushions are hard, cold, and slippery."
msgstr ""
"Un fauteuil qui était probablement très moelleux et confortable autrefois. "
"Maintenant, les coussins trop rembourrés sont durs, froids et glissants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass chair"
msgstr "chaise en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass chair"
msgid ""
"A simple glass chair.  The seat is very thin, and crunches ominously under "
"any weight."
msgstr ""
"Une chaise en verre simple. L'assise est très fine et craque de manière "
"inquiétante sous n'importe quel poids."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass desk"
msgstr "bureau en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass desk"
msgid ""
"A glass desk.  There are a handful of shapes atop it that suggest pens, "
"paper, and miscellaneous knickknacks that are too jagged to identify."
msgstr ""
"Un bureau en verre. Il y a une poignée de formes sur le dessus qui suggèrent "
"des stylos, du papier et des babioles diverses, trop anguleuses pour être "
"identifiées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass locker"
msgstr "Casier en verre noir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass locker"
msgid ""
"A tall glass cabinet.  Whatever was inside will stay that way; the door is "
"seamless with the frame."
msgstr ""
"Une armoire en verre haute. Ce qui se trouve à l'intérieur restera ainsi ; la "
"porte est parfaitement intégrée au cadre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass crunching!"
msgstr "craquement de verre!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass oven"
msgstr "four en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass oven"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a gas oven.  Bristling from the burner is a crown of "
"jagged shards in the rough shape of an uncontrolled fire."
msgstr ""
"Une sculpture en verre d'un four à gaz. Des éclats déchiquetés, ressemblant à "
"un feu incontrôlé, s'élèvent du brûleur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass mailbox"
msgstr "boîte aux lettres en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass mailbox"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a mailbox.  The door is open; inside is a pile of "
"envelopes, all razor-edged."
msgstr ""
"Une sculpture en verre d'une boîte aux lettres. La porte est ouverte ; à "
"l'intérieur se trouve une pile d'enveloppes, toutes tranchantes comme des "
"rasoirs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass display rack"
msgstr "Présentoir en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass display rack"
msgid ""
"A glass sculpture of a shelving unit.  The angled shelves are covered in "
"jagged miscellany, most of which is firmly fused in place."
msgstr ""
"Une sculpture en verre d'une étagère. Les étagères inclinées sont recouvertes "
"d'un méli-mélo déchiqueté, dont la plupart est solidement fusionnée en place."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass sink"
msgstr "évier en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sink"
msgid ""
"A glass basin and tap.  The inside stops halfway down in sheet of concentric "
"ripples, with the tiny spire of a splashing droplet at the center "
msgstr ""
"Un lavabo en verre et un robinet. L'intérieur s'arrête à mi-hauteur avec une "
"nappe de rides concentriques, au centre de laquelle se trouve une petite "
"spire d'une gouttelette éclaboussante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass toilet"
msgstr "toilette en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass toilet"
msgid "A toilet made of black glass.  The lid, perhaps mercifully, is fused shut."
msgstr ""
"Une toilette en verre noir.  Le couvercle a, peut être heureusement, fusionné "
"avec le reste."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass cupboard"
msgstr "placard en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass cupboard"
msgid ""
"A black glass cupboard.  The doors are fused shut, but it presumably contains "
"glasses."
msgstr ""
"Un placard en verre noir fermé refusant de s'ouvrir.  Vous supposez que ce "
"qui est à l'intérieur est aussi en verre noir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass garden"
msgstr "jardinière en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass garden"
msgid ""
"A planter of dark glass.  Sharp, twisting glass sprouts emerge from the black "
"soil within."
msgstr ""
"Un pot de fleurs en verre noir. De pointes de verre tranchantes émergent du "
"sol noir à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass flower"
msgstr "fleur en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass flower"
msgid ""
"A delicate little thing; a wispy stem slightly bowed under the weight of "
"translucent petals.  The tiny barbs that line it are almost impossible to "
"see, until it crumbles in your fingers."
msgstr ""
"Une petite chose délicate ; une tige légère légèrement inclinée sous le poids "
"de pétales translucides. Les minuscules épines qui la bordent sont presque "
"impossibles à voir, jusqu'à ce qu'elle s'effrite entre vos doigts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "tinkle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "plink."
msgstr "plink."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bench"
msgstr "banc en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bench"
msgid ""
"A long, low slab of black glass.  You can't tell if the fissures here and "
"there on the surface are natural cracks, or carved names."
msgstr ""
"Une longue et basse plaque de verre noir. On ne peut pas dire si les fissures "
"ici et là sur la surface sont des fissures naturelles ou des noms gravés."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass washer"
msgstr "machine à linge en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass washer"
msgid ""
"A glass washing machine.  The inside is completely filled with black sand, "
"some of which has spilled onto the floor."
msgstr ""
"Une machine à laver en verre. L'intérieur est complètement rempli de sable "
"noir, dont une partie s'est répandue sur le sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dryer"
msgstr "sèche-linge en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dryer"
msgid ""
"A mechanical dryer of black glass.  The door hangs open, and inside, you can "
"see a jumble of what might once have been clothes, now smashed to pieces."
msgstr ""
"Un sèche-linge mécanique en verre noir. La porte est ouverte, et à "
"l'intérieur, vous pouvez voir un amas de ce qui aurait pu être des vêtements, "
"maintenant réduits en morceaux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass bookcase"
msgstr "bibliothèque en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
msgid ""
"A heavy bookshelf, laden with books fused into the shelves and each other.  "
"You can make out titles on the spines, but the alphabet they're written in is "
"unfamiliar."
msgstr ""
"Une lourde bibliothèque, chargée de livres fusionnés aux étagères et entre "
"eux. Vous pouvez distinguer des titres sur les dos des livres, mais "
"l'alphabet dans lequel ils sont écrits vous est inconnu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass counter"
msgstr "comptoir en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass counter"
msgid ""
"A thick cube of black glass.  On the surface, fused in place, are statues of "
"utensils and miscellany."
msgstr ""
"Un épais cube de verre noir. À la surface, fusionnées en place, se trouvent "
"des statues d'ustensiles et d'objets divers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass table"
msgstr "table en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass table"
msgid ""
"A slab of smooth black glass on four stout legs.  In a few places, there is "
"shallowly rounded mass, like liquid spilled on the surface."
msgstr ""
"Une dalle de verre noir lisse sur quatre pieds robustes. À quelques endroits, "
"il y a des masses légèrement arrondies, comme du liquide renversé sur la "
"surface."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass birdbath"
msgstr "vasque en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass birdbath"
msgid ""
"A glass pedestal and bowl.  Inside, frozen in the midst of washing itself in "
"the black sand, is the delicate figure of a bird."
msgstr ""
"Un piédestal en verre et un bol. À l'intérieur, figée en train de se laver "
"dans le sable noir, se trouve la délicate silhouette d'un oiseau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clunk."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass shower"
msgstr "douche en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass shower"
msgid ""
"From the head of this shower descend a dozen streams of thin black glass, "
"with frozen droplets strung from them like pearls."
msgstr ""
"Du pommeau de cette douche descendent une douzaine de filaments fins en verre "
"noir, avec des gouttelettes congelées suspendues comme des perles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass water heater"
msgstr "chaudière en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass water heater"
msgid ""
"A cylinder of thick black glass.  The top has burst apart, and rivulets of "
"black sand run down the side."
msgstr ""
"Un cylindre en verre noir épais. Le sommet a éclaté, et des ruisseaux de "
"sable noir coulent le long des côtés."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass fireplace"
msgstr "cheminée en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass fireplace"
msgid ""
"A fireplace of pitted glass bricks.  The fire inside has been frozen in glass "
"at the moment it began to leap beyond the grate."
msgstr ""
"Un foyer en briques de verre piquetées. Le feu à l'intérieur a été figé en "
"verre au moment où il commençait à s'échapper de la grille."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "ring of black stones"
msgstr "cercles de pierres noires"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "ring of black stones"
msgid ""
"A circle of smooth glass pebbles.  Inside are frozen tendrils of fire, "
"slightly translucent.  It seems colder as you approach."
msgstr ""
"Un cercle de galets en verre lisse. À l'intérieur, des filaments de feu "
"figés, légèrement translucides. Il semble plus froid à mesure que vous vous "
"en approchez."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass lantern"
msgstr "lanterne en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass lantern"
msgid ""
"A tall glass pole with a translucent shade atop it.  You know it could not "
"possibly turn on, but in the corner of your eye, you think you might see a "
"soft glow."
msgstr ""
"Un grand poteau en verre avec un abat-jour translucide au sommet. Vous savez "
"qu'il ne peut pas s'allumer, mais dans le coin de votre œil, vous pensez "
"apercevoir une douce lueur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "tink!"
msgstr "tink !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass box"
msgstr "boîte en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass box"
msgid "A box of thin black glass.  Its edges are glisteningly sharp."
msgstr "Une boîte en verre noir fin. Ses bords sont d'une netteté scintillante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass sofa"
msgstr "sofa en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass sofa"
msgid "A long bench, padded with cold glass cushions."
msgstr "Un long banc rembourré avec des coussins en verre froid."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "black glass dishwasher"
msgstr "machine à laver en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass dishwasher"
msgid ""
"A glass dishwasher, its door hanging open.  Inside, glass plates and utensils "
"are half buried in black sand."
msgstr ""
"Un lave-vaisselle, dont la porte est ouverte. À l'intérieur, des assiettes et "
"des ustensiles en verre sont à moitié enfouis dans le sable noir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "incomplete plush doll"
msgstr "poupée en peluche incomplète"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "incomplete plush doll"
msgid "A soft plush torso, empty of features, is lying on this sofa."
msgstr "Un torse en peluche, dépourvu de caractéristiques, est allongé sur ce canapé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/furniture_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "black glass bookcase"
msgid "This bookcase is missing a book."
msgstr "Il manque un livre à cette bibliothéque."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rocky coastline"
msgstr "côte rocheuse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rocky coastline"
msgid ""
"This is a section of eroded natural stone formations along the beach, the "
"water lapping and splashing at the edges."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une section de formations de pierres naturelles érodées le long "
"de la plage, l'eau clapotant et éclaboussant les bords."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tide pool"
msgstr "bassin de marée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-beach.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tide pool"
msgid "A shallow pool of salt water, often filled with interesting life."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "walkway"
msgstr "sentier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "walkway"
msgid ""
"A metallic bridge commonly used in industrial settings to meet specified "
"safety standards."
msgstr ""
"Pont métallique couramment utilisé dans l'industrie pour répondre à des "
"normes de sécurité spécifiques."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain_light_blue.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "dock"
msgstr "quai"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow bridge"
msgid "A wooden platform held by a support made of logs dug into the ground."
msgstr ""
"Une plate-forme en bois maintenue par un support fait de rondins creusés dans "
"le sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock pile"
msgstr "pieu de quai profond"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of wood extending all the way to the riverbed.  A frame "
"will be required to support a surface."
msgstr ""
"Un pieu solide en bois qui s'étend jusqu'au lit de la rivière. Un cadre est "
"nécessaire pour soutenir une surface."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock frame"
msgstr "cadre de quai profond"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
msgid ""
"A log frame secured atop a wooden pile.  Adding a wood surface will make this "
"into a proper dock section."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre en bois posé sur une pile de bois. L'ajout d'une surface en bois "
"permettra de créer une section de quai appropriée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "deep dock"
msgstr "quai profond"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
msgid ""
"A wooden platform held by a tall wooden pile that extend to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr ""
"Une plate-forme en bois soutenue par une haute pile en bois qui s'étend "
"jusqu'au lit de la rivière. Très robuste, elle a toutes les chances de vous "
"survivre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow bridge"
msgstr "pont bas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "pontoon bridge"
msgstr "ponton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pontoon bridge"
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over still water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross lakes."
msgstr ""
"Un pont flottant temporaire installé pour traverser une étendue d'eau calme, "
"similaire aux structures utilisées par des armées pour franchir des lacs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "river bridge"
msgstr "pont de rivière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "river bridge"
msgid ""
"A floating temporary bridge over flowing water, like the ones armies used to "
"make to cross rivers."
msgstr ""
"Un pont flottant temporaire installé pour traverser une étendue d'eau "
"courante, similaire aux structures utilisées par des armées pour franchir des "
"rivières."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge pavement"
msgstr "pavé de pont"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge pavement"
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal."
msgstr "Une section de pont faite de béton et de métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "concrete cracking and metal screeching!"
msgstr "craquement de béton et crissement de métal !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge yellow pavement"
msgstr "pavé jaune de pont"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge yellow pavement"
msgid "A bridge section made out of concrete and metal.  It's painted yellow."
msgstr "Une section de pont faite de béton et de métal. Il est peint en jaune."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bridge sidewalk"
msgstr "trottoir de pont"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-highways.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bridge sidewalk"
msgid "The sidewalk section of a concrete bridge."
msgstr "La section de trottoir d'un pont en béton."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dock"
msgid "A metal platform held by a support made of concrete set into the ground."
msgstr ""
"Une plate-forme métallique maintenue par un support en béton enfoncé dans le "
"sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock pile"
msgid ""
"A sturdy pile made of poured concrete extending all the way to the riverbed.  "
"A metal frame will be required to support a surface."
msgstr ""
"Un pieu solide en béton coulé s'étendant jusqu'au lit de la rivière. Un cadre "
"métallique sera nécessaire pour soutenir une surface."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock frame"
msgid ""
"A metal frame secured atop a concrete pile.  Adding a metal surface will make "
"this into a proper dock section."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre métallique fixé sur un pieu en béton. L'ajout d'une surface "
"métallique permettra de créer une section de quai appropriée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "deep dock"
msgid ""
"A metal platform held by a tall metal pile that extends to the riverbed.  "
"Very sturdy, and likely to outlast you."
msgstr ""
"Une plate-forme métallique soutenue par un haut pieu métallique qui s'étend "
"jusqu'au lit de la rivière. Très solide et probablement plus durable que vous."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floating dock"
msgstr "ponton flottant en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-bridges-docks.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floating dock"
msgid "A floating temporary dock, anchored to keep it from drifting away."
msgstr "Un ponton flottant temporaire, ancré pour l'empêcher de dériver."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed laminated glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre laminé fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed laminated glass door"
msgid ""
"A closed laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held "
"together by an interlayer."
msgstr ""
"Une porte fermée en verre pare-balle consistant de plusieurs couches de verre "
"laminé tenues ensemble par une couche intercalaire de plastique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open laminated glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre laminé ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open laminated glass door"
msgid ""
"A laminated glass door, composed of layers of glass and plastic held together "
"by an interlayer.  It's open."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ouverte en verre pare-balle consistant de plusieurs couches de "
"verre laminé tenues ensemble par une couche intercalaire de plastique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed ballistic glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre pare-balle fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed ballistic glass door"
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass."
msgstr "Une porte en verre pare-balle consistant de plusieurs couches de verre laminé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open ballistic glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre pare-balle ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open ballistic glass door"
msgid "A ballistic glass door, consisting of layers of laminated glass.  It's open."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ouverte en verre pare-balle consistant de plusieurs couches de "
"verre laminé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed reinforced glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre renforcé fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced glass door"
msgid ""
"A closed glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but "
"practical pattern."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en verre fermée, renforcée par des fils d'acier tressés dans un "
"motif à la fois élégant et pratique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open reinforced glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre renforcé ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced glass door"
msgid ""
"A glass door reinforced with woven steel wires in a stylish, but practical "
"pattern.  It's open."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ouverte en verre renforcée avec un réseau de tiges de ferre ayant "
"un motif stylé et pratique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très résistante. Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
msgid "You notice the door is unlocked, so you simply open it."
msgstr ""
"Vous remarquez que la porte n'est pas verrouillée, alors vous l'ouvrez "
"simplement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
msgstr "porte en bois fermée avec une serrure électronique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt electronic lock, so it's likely locked. "
" You could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock "
"the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très résistante. Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement. Celle-ci est équipée d'une serrure électronique à "
"pêne dormant, elle est donc probablement verrouillée. Vous pouvez l'ouvrir en "
"faisant levier, mais il est hors de question de deviner le code, ou "
"déverrouiller le pêne dormant de l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid "You pry open the door."
msgstr "Vous forcez l'ouverture de la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door with an electronic lock"
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid "You pry, but can't pry open the door."
msgstr "Vous faites levier, mais vous ne pouvez pas faire levier pour ouvrir la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one "
"has a deadbolt numpad, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open, "
"guessing the code is out of the question, or unlock the deadbolt from the "
"inside."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ordinaire en bois ordinaire, sauf que celle-ci est munie d'un "
"judas. Si vous l'examinez de plus près, vous pourrez jeter un coup d'œil à "
"travers le trou. Cette porte est munie d'un cadenas, elle est donc "
"probablement verrouillée. Vous pouvez faire levier, mais il est hors de "
"question de deviner le code, ou déverrouiller le pêne dormant de l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an electronic keypad, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open, guessing the code is out of the question."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très résistante.  Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement.  Celle-ci est équipée d'un clavier électronique, "
"elle est donc probablement verrouillée.  Il est possible de la forcer, mais "
"il est hors de question de deviner le code."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one is wide open."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très solide.  Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement.  Celle-ci est grande ouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door"
msgid ""
"A trashed wooden door, with a large hole in the middle that you can see right "
"through.  The doorknob is so messed up that it can't be opened anymore.  It "
"could be fixed up with a few planks."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois saccagée, avec un grand trou au milieu à travers lequel "
"vous pouvez voir.  La poignée est tellement abîmée qu'on ne peut plus "
"l'ouvrir.   Quelques planches suffiraient probablement à la réparer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty door frame"
msgstr "cadre de porte vide"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty door frame"
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made from planks and nails.  A variety of doors could be "
"constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre de porte vide construit à partir de planches et de clous.  Pourrait "
"accueillir une grande variété de portes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed glass door"
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door, clear enough that an animal or a particularly dumb "
"person could slam right into it.  This one is closed, so don't hurt yourself."
msgstr ""
"Une porte coulissante en verre, suffisamment claire pour qu'un animal ou une "
"personne particulièrement stupide puisse s'y heurter de plein fouet.  "
"Celle-ci est fermée, alors ne vous blessez pas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open glass door"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open frosted glass door"
msgid ""
"A sliding glass door that has been left open for all manner of things to "
"travel through."
msgstr ""
"Une porte coulissante en verre ayant été laissée ouverte pour permettre à "
"toutes sortes de choses de circuler."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "Section articulée fermée de la lentille d'un phare."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is on hinges and can "
"be opened for maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Un arrangement complexe de verre, conçu pour concentrer la lumière de "
"l'intérieur afin qu'elle soit visible sur de longues distances. Cette section "
"de la lentille est articulée et peut être ouverte pour la maintenance."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgstr "Section articulée ouverte de la lentille d'un phare."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open lighthouse lens hinged section"
msgid ""
"An intricate arrangement of glass, designed to focus light from within to be "
"visible over long distances.  This section of the lens is hinged and is "
"currently open."
msgstr ""
"Un arrangement complexe de verre, conçu pour concentrer la lumière de "
"l'intérieur afin qu'elle soit visible sur de longues distances. Cette section "
"de la lentille est articulée et peut être ouverte pour la maintenance."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wood door with peephole"
msgstr "porte en bois fermée avec judas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole."
msgstr ""
"Une porte classique faîte de bois ordinaire, mis à part qu'elle a un judas. "
"Si vous l'examinez de plus près, vous pourriez jeter un œil au travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgstr "porte en bois avec judas endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"The bad news is that the peephole is broken and you can't use it to look "
"through the door.  The good news is that the door is nearly broken down, so "
"there's nothing blocking the view.  Also, the doorknob is so messed up that "
"it can't be opened anymore.  A few planks, nails, and the right tools could "
"patch up all the damage."
msgstr ""
"La mauvaise nouvelle est que le judas est cassé et que vous ne pouvez pas "
"l'utiliser pour regarder à travers la porte.  La bonne nouvelle, c'est que la "
"porte est presque effondrée et qu'il n'y a donc rien qui bloque la vue.  De "
"plus, la poignée de la porte est tellement abîmée qu'elle ne peut plus être "
"ouverte.  Quelques planches, des clous et les bons outils suffiraient "
"probablement à réparer les dégâts."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wood door with peephole"
msgstr "porte en bois avec judas ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wood door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  No need "
"right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ordinaire en bois ordinaire, sauf que celle-ci est munie d'un "
"judas.  Si vous l'examinez de plus près, vous pourriez jeter un coup d'œil à "
"travers le trou.  Ce n'est pas nécessaire pour l'instant, puisque la porte "
"est de toute façon ouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed reinforced wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois renforcée fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"and an additional hinge for reinforcement.  It might be barricaded, but it's "
"still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""
"Comme les autres portes en bois, sauf que celle-ci comporte des couches de "
"planches clouées et une charnière supplémentaire pour la renforcer.  Elle est "
"peut être barricadée, mais celle-ci est toujours vulnérable au feu."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois renforcée endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "damaged reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Despite someone's best efforts at reinforcing this door, there are "
"splintering planks and visible holes in the wood, it could soon be smashed "
"apart completely if not repaired.  The doorknob is all messed up and the door "
"can't be opened until it's fixed."
msgstr ""
"Malgré tous les efforts déployés par quelqu'un pour renforcer cette porte, il "
"y a des planches qui se détachent et des trous visibles dans le bois, et elle "
"pourrait bientôt être complètement détruite si elle n'est pas réparée.  La "
"poignée de porte est abîmée et la porte ne peut pas être ouverte tant qu'elle "
"n'est pas réparée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open reinforced wood door"
msgstr "porte en bois renforcée ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open reinforced wood door"
msgid ""
"Just like other wooden doors, except this one has layers of nailed-on planks "
"for reinforcement.  It might be fortified, but it's still susceptible to "
"fire.  It's open, so it's not stopping anything right now."
msgstr ""
"Comme les autres portes en bois, sauf que celle-ci comporte des couches de "
"planches clouées et une charnière supplémentaire pour la renforcer. Elle est "
"peut être barricadée, mais celle-ci est toujours vulnérable au feu.  Celle-ci "
"est ouverte, donc elle n'arrête rien pour l'instant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très résistante.  Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement.  Elle a un trou de serrure supplémentaire, elle est "
"donc probablement verrouillée.  Vous pourriez la forcer ou crocheter la "
"serrure."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed wood door"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain ""
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the door opens."
msgstr ""
"Un cliquetis plaisant vous indique que la serrure de la porte est "
"déverrouillé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that doesn't look very resilient.  It'd probably burn "
"easily, too.  This one has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You "
"could pry it open or pick the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois standard qui n'a pas l'air très résistante.  Elle brûlerait "
"probablement facilement.  Celle-ci possède un trou de serrure à pêne dormant, "
"elle est donc probablement verrouillée.  Vous pouvez faire levier, crocheter "
"la serrure ou la déverrouiller de l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wood door"
msgid ""
"A regular door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  If you "
"examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the hole.  This one "
"has a deadbolt keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could pry it open or pick "
"the lock, or unlock the deadbolt from the inside."
msgstr ""
"Une porte ordinaire en bois ordinaire, sauf que celle-ci est munie d'un "
"judas.  Si vous l'examinez de plus près, vous pourriez jeter un coup d'œil à "
"travers le trou.  Elle possède aussi un trou de serrure à pêne dormant, elle "
"est donc probablement verrouillée.  Vous pourriez la forcer, crocheter la "
"serrure ou la déverrouiller de l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed door curtain"
msgstr "rideau de porte fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed door curtain"
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""
"Une paire de rideaux réutilisée provenant d'une fenêtre recouvrant un cadre "
"de porte.  Pourrait facilement être démonté pour être remplacé par une vraie "
"porte ou simplement placé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed makeshift door"
msgstr "porte improvisée fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed makeshift door"
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"vertically from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and "
"re-purposed."
msgstr ""
"Une porte improvisée constituée de planches reliées entre elles par de la "
"corde, suspendue verticalement au sommet de la porte.  Elle peut être "
"facilement démontée et réutilisée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "wham."
msgstr "bam."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open door curtain"
msgstr "rideau de porte ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open door curtain"
msgid ""
"Repurposed curtains from a window covering a door frame.  Could be easily "
"taken down for supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, "
"bundled, and tied next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"Des rideaux réutilisés provenant d'une fenêtre et recouvrant un cadre de "
"porte.  Pourrait facilement être retiré pour être remplacé par une porte plus "
"permanent ou simplement placés ailleurs.  Les rideaux sont ouverts, "
"empaquetés et attachés à côté de la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed grass curtain"
msgstr "rideau de porte en herbe fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed grass curtain"
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else."
msgstr ""
"Des feuilles de fil d'herbe recouvrent le cadre d'une porte. Elles peuvent "
"être facilement démontées pour être remplacées par d'autres ou placées "
"ailleurs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open grass curtain"
msgstr "rideau de porte en herbe ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open grass curtain"
msgid ""
"Sheets of grass yarn covering a door frame.  Could be easily taken down for "
"supplies or placed somewhere else.  The curtains are open, bundled, and tied "
"next to the doorway."
msgstr ""
"Des feuilles de fil d'herbe recouvrent le cadre d'une porte. Elles peuvent "
"être facilement enlevées pour être ravitaillées ou placées ailleurs. Les "
"rideaux sont ouverts, empaquetés et attachés à côté de la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open makeshift door"
msgstr "porte improvisée ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open makeshift door"
msgid ""
"A makeshift screen consisting of planks bound together with rope, hanging "
"from the top of the doorway.  Could be easily taken down and re-purposed.  "
"The planks have been rolled up and attached to the top of the doorway, "
"allowing free movement through."
msgstr ""
"Un assemblage de fortune de planches liées avec de la corde pendant du haut "
"du plafond. Vous pourriez aisément démanteler ceci est réutiliser les "
"matériaux pour quelque chose d'autre. Les planches ont été enroulés et "
"maintenues au plafond par des nœuds, ne posant aucun obstacle à la vision et "
"permettant un passage sans ralentissement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty metal door frame"
msgstr "seuil de porte en métal vide"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal door frame"
msgid ""
"An empty door frame made of steel and assorted metal.  A variety of doors "
"could be constructed here."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre de porte vide en acier et métaux divers.  Une variété de portes "
"pourraient être construites ici."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "empty metal window frame"
msgstr "cadre de fenêtre vide en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "empty metal window frame"
msgid ""
"An empty window frame constructed from assembled metal and carefully braced "
"with various hardware."
msgstr ""
"Un cadre de fenêtre vide construit à partir de métal assemblé et "
"soigneusement renforcé par diverses pièces de quincaillerie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up door"
msgstr "porte barricadée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door"
msgid ""
"A standard wooden door that has several planks across it, nailed down to "
"board it up and increase its durability.  It's still flammable, though."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois ordinaire à laquelle plusieurs planches de renforcement ont "
"été clouées. Toujours très inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgid "You pry the boards from the door."
msgstr "Vous arrachez les planches de la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged door"
msgstr "porte barricadée endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door"
msgid ""
"A boarded up wooden door, except that some of the planks are fractured or "
"coming loose.  Without repairs, it could be broken down easily."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois barricadée, mais dont certaines planches sont fracturées ou "
"se détachent.  Si celle-ci n'est pas réparée, elle pourrait être brisée "
"facilement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up door with peephole"
msgstr "porte barricadée avec judas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A boarded up door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole.  "
"Although it's been covered up in planks, you could still look through the "
"peephole if you were close enough."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois ordinaire à laquelle plusieurs planches de renforcement ont "
"été clouées et possédant un judas. Les planches laissent le judas dégagé et "
"il est toujours possible de l'utiliser pour voir ce qui se passe de l'autre "
"côté de la porte si vous êtes assez proche."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up reinforced door"
msgstr "porte barricadée renforcée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up reinforced door"
msgid ""
"An additionally reinforced door of layered planks that has been boarded up "
"with more wood to prevent it from opening.  It's still susceptible to fire."
msgstr ""
"Une porte renforcée à laquelle plusieurs planches ont été clouées pour la "
"consolider encore davantage, mais l'empêchant d'être ouverte. Toujours assez "
"inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgstr "porte barricadée renforcée endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged reinforced door"
msgid ""
"A battered and torn reinforced door with planks bursting from the joints.  "
"The boarded up planks are fragmented and in pieces, this doesn't look like an "
"easy repair."
msgstr ""
"Une porte renforcée, abîmée et déchirée, dont les planches sortent des "
"joints.  Les planches sont fragmentées et en morceaux, et n'a pas l'air "
"d'être quelque chose qui sera facile à réparer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgstr "porte barricadée avec judas endommagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "boarded up damaged door with peephole"
msgid ""
"A wrecked door made of ordinary wood, except this one has a peephole and some "
"partly-splintered boards nailed across it.  The peephole is damaged and can't "
"be used to see through."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en bois ordinaire renforcée avec des planches ayant vu de meilleurs "
"jours, possédant un judas et ayant des trous où ses panneaux et ses renforts "
"ont été brisés. Le judas est endommagé et ne peut plus être utilisé pour voir "
"ce qui ce passe de l'autre côté de la porte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_doors.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal door"
msgstr "porte en métal fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement résistante faite de pièces d'acier découpées et "
"martelées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed corrugated metal door"
msgstr "porte en tôle fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed corrugated metal door"
msgid "A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame."
msgstr "Une porte fine en tôle ondulée maintenue dans un cadre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal wall"
msgstr "mur en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal wall"
msgid ""
"An industrially fabricated thick sheet carefully positioned and joined "
"seamlessly with perimeter sealant, this wall is capable of resisting extreme "
"elements as well as hostile forces.  Blast load rated and extremely "
"fire-retardant, breaching it will require specialized tools or an industrial "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur, composé de plaques épaisses fabriquées industriellement, "
"soigneusement positionnées et assemblées de manière homogène à l'aide d'un "
"mastic d'étanchéité, est capable de résister au pire des éléments ainsi qu'à "
"des forces hostiles.  Résistant aux explosions et extrêmement ignifugé, il "
"vous faudra des outils spécialisés ou un véhicule industriel pour pouvoir "
"passer à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr "porte secrète ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of metal wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""
"Ce segment de métal à première vue normal s'est ouvert pour révéler un "
"passage secret."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete wall"
msgstr "mur en béton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
msgid ""
"A faux concrete wall positioned and joined seamlessly with the wall, this "
"wall is capable of resisting extreme elements as well as hostile forces.  "
"Blast load rated and extremely fire-retardant, breaching it will require "
"specialized tools or an industrial vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un mur en faux béton positionné et relié de façon homogène au mur, le rendant "
"capable de résister aux pire des éléments ainsi qu'à des forces hostiles.  "
"Résistant aux explosions et extrêmement ignifuge, il vous faudra des outils "
"spécialisés ou un véhicule industriel pour pouvoir passer à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open secret door"
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of concrete wall has opened to reveal a secret "
"passage."
msgstr ""
"Ce segment de mur en béton, apparemment normal, s'est ouvert pour révéler un "
"passage secret."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "thwack!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "electronic locked metal door"
msgstr "porte en métal verrouillée électroniquement"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "electronic locked metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It is locked by an electronic keypad."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement solide consistant d'un assortiment d'acier de qualité "
"sculpté et martelé pour lui donner une forme.  Celle-ci est verrouillée par "
"un clavier électronique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal door"
msgstr "porte en métal ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  It's open, so no tools are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement résistante, faîte d'acier assorti, creusée et frappée "
"dans sa forme actuelle. Elle est ouverte, donc pas besoin d'outils pour "
"pénétrer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open corrugated metal door"
msgstr "porte en tôle ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open corrugated metal door"
msgid ""
"A thin door made of corrugated steel held in a frame.  It's open, so no tools "
"are needed to break in."
msgstr ""
"Une porte fine en tôle ondulée maintenue dans un cadre.  Elle est ouverte, "
"vous n'aurez besoin d'aucun outil pour la forcer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal door with peephole"
msgstr "porte en métal fermée avec judas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door with peephole"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement solide consistant d'un assortiment d'acier de qualité "
"sculpté et martelé pour lui donner une forme.  En l'examinant de plus près, "
"vous pourriez utiliser le judas."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal door with peephole"
msgstr "porte en métal ouverte avec judas"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal door with peephole"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  If you examined it more closely, you'd be able to peek through the "
"peephole.  No need right now though, since the door is open anyway."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement résistante composée d'acier de différentes qualités, "
"sculptée et martelée pour lui donner une forme.  En l'examinant de plus près, "
"il serait possible de voir à travers le judas.  Ce n'est pas nécessaire en ce "
"moment, puisque la porte est ouverte de toute façon."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"A galvanized steel door, forged to withstand punishment and impede anyone or "
"anything.  Typically used in conjunction with automated electronic locking "
"mechanisms that require an external source to unlock."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en acier galvanisé, forgée pour résister aux abus et entraver "
"quiconque ou quoi que ce soit. Typiquement utilisé conjointement avec des "
"verrous électroniques automatiques nécessitant une source externe pour la "
"déverrouiller."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "You pry open the metal door."
msgstr "Vous forcez la porte en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain ""
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid "The metal door is too thick."
msgstr "La porte en métal est trop épaisse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of assorted steel, carved and pounded into "
"shape.  This one has an extra keyhole, so it's likely locked.  You could "
"probably pick the lock."
msgstr ""
"Une porte extrêmement résistante consistant d'un assortiment d'acier de "
"qualité sculpté et martelé pour lui donner une forme.  Elle a un trou de "
"serrure supplémentaire, elle est donc probablement verrouillée.  Vous "
"pourriez probablement la crocheter."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bar door"
msgstr "porte de bar fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism doesn't appear to be engaged."
msgstr ""
"Une porte de détention constituée de barres d'acier inoxydable entrecroisées. "
"Le mécanisme de verrouillage ne semble pas enclenché."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-windows.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_spaceship.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_spaceship.json
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed bar door"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "open wire gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "closed retractable gate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "chain link fence"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal post"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "railroad track"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "recessed railroad track"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "rebar cage"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "armored boarded up window"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window frame with metal bars"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal bars and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "window with metal grate and curtains"
#. ~ Hacksaw message of terrain "prison grating"
msgid "You finish cutting the metal."
msgstr "Vous finissez de couper le métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bar door"
msgstr "porte de bar ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  It's wide "
"open.  Freedom!"
msgstr ""
"Une porte de détention faite de barres d'acier inoxydable entrecroisées. Elle "
"est grande ouverte. Liberté !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid ""
"A detention door made up of crisscrossed stainless steel bars.  The locking "
"mechanism appears to be engaged.  You could pick it open with enough skill."
msgstr ""
"Une porte de détention constituée de barres d'acier inoxydable entrecroisées. "
"Le mécanisme de verrouillage semble enclenché. Il est possible de l'ouvrir "
"avec un peu d'habileté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "closed bar door"
msgid "The door swings open…"
msgstr "La porte s'ouvre…"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed frosted glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre givré fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed frosted glass door"
msgid "A sliding door of frosted white glass."
msgstr "Une porte coulissante en verre blanc dépoli."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open frosted glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre givré ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bulkhead door"
msgstr "porte de cloison fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bulkhead door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight and opened "
"using the fly wheel."
msgstr ""
"Porte extrêmement résistante en métal moulé, elle est étanche et s'ouvre à "
"l'aide d'un volant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bulkhead door"
msgstr "porte de cloison ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bulkhead door"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient door made of cast metal, it is watertight, or would be "
"if it was closed."
msgstr ""
"Porte extrêmement résistante en métal moulé, elle est étanche à l'eau, ou le "
"serait si elle était fermée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en briques avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en briques possède une embrasure vous permettant de tirer ou utiliser "
"des armes contre des ennemis à l'extérieur en offrant une couverture "
"significative."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en briques d'adobe avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "adobe wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This adobe brick wall has an embrasure that lets you shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the outside, while also protecting you."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en briques d'adobe possède une embrasure vous permettant de tirer ou "
"utiliser des armes contre des ennemis à l'extérieur en offrant une couverture "
"significative."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "stone wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en pierre avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "stone wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"The small opening on this stone wall allows you to shoot and use reach "
"weapons against enemies on the other side, while also providing cover for you."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en pierre possède une embrasure vous permettant de tirer ou utiliser "
"des armes contre des ennemis à l'extérieur en offrant une couverture "
"significative."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en bois avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This wooden wall has a hole that lets you shoot and use reach weapons against "
"enemies on the other side.  Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en bois possède une embrasure vous permettant de tirer ou utiliser des "
"armes contre des ennemis à l'extérieur en offrant une couverture "
"significative. Malheureusement très inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "paroi en bois avec une large ouverture"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall with a wide opening"
msgid ""
"This wooden wall previously had an embrasure, but the hole has been smashed "
"wide enough that you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  "
"Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en bois possédait auparavant une embrasure, mais le trou à été "
"tellement élargi que n'importe quoi pourrait juste passer à travers, le "
"rendant assez inutile en tant que mur. Malheureusement très inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "log wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur de rondins avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"This timber wall has a hole that lets you shoot through and use reach weapons "
"against enemies on the other side, while also protecting you.  Quite "
"flammable."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en rondins possède une embrasure vous permettant de tirer ou utiliser "
"des armes contre des ennemis à l'extérieur en offrant une couverture "
"significative. Assez inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "log wall with a wide opening"
msgstr "mur en rondins avec une large ouverture"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "log wall with a wide opening"
msgid ""
"This timber wall previously had an embrasure, but now the hole is so big that "
"you can climb through it, rendering it kind of pointless.  Quite flammable."
msgstr ""
"Ce mur en rondins possédait auparavant une embrasure, mais le trou à été "
"tellement élargi que n'importe quoi pourrait juste passer à travers, le "
"rendant assez inutile en tant que mur. Malheureusement très inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgstr "palissade avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"An age-old type of fortification consisting of hefty lumber staked into the "
"ground and cabled together.  This section in particular has an embrasure, so "
"you can shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un type de fortification très ancien composé de gros bois d'œuvre "
"plantés dans le sol et reliés entre eux par des câbles. Cette section en "
"particulier est dotée d'une embrasure, ce qui vous permet de tirer ou "
"d'utiliser des armes de portée à travers cette embrasure tout en restant en "
"sécurité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en béton avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall.  This one has an embrasure, so you can "
"shoot or use reach weapons through it while staying safe."
msgstr ""
"Un mur en béton solide et uniforme possédant une embrasure vous permettant de "
"tirer des armes à feu ou utiliser des armes longues comme des lances à "
"travers en restant bien à l'abri."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgstr "mur en béton armé avec embrasure"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-embrasures.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete wall with embrasure"
msgid ""
"A section of wall with a nice small hole, letting you shoot your machine gun "
"from the safety of your reinforced bunker."
msgstr ""
"Un pan de mur avec un joli petit trou, vous permettant de tirer à la "
"mitrailleuse en sécurité depuis votre bunker renforcé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "palisade gate"
msgstr "porte de palissade"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "palisade gate"
msgid ""
"A large doorway consisting of long logs cabled together, best used as part of "
"a longer wall.  Can act as a door if some type of pulley system were rigged "
"on an adjacent palisade wall."
msgstr ""
"Une grande porte constituée de longs rondins câblés ensemble, utilisée de "
"préférence dans le cadre d'un mur plus long. Peut servir de porte si un "
"système de poulie est installé sur un mur de palissade adjacent."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open palisade gate"
msgstr "porte de palissade ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open palisade gate"
msgid ""
"A hanging palisade gate, hoisted by a nearby pulley system.  You probably "
"shouldn't be underneath when it comes down."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière de palissade suspendue, hissée par un système de poulies situé à "
"proximité. Vous ne devriez probablement pas vous trouver en dessous "
"lorsqu'elle s'abaisse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "makeshift portcullis"
msgstr "herse improvisée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "makeshift portcullis"
msgid ""
"An immense gateway cobbled together from various bits of steel and metal "
"scraps."
msgstr ""
"Une immense passerelle bricolée à partir de divers morceaux d'acier et de "
"ferraille."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "locked wire gate"
msgstr "porte grillagée verrouillée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "locked wire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence.  This one has a locked padlock on the latch "
"system.  With the right tools, you could cut the metal fence or pick the "
"lock.  You could also examine the fence to see if it looks climbable."
msgstr ""
"Un portail pour une clôture à mailles losangées. Celui-ci est muni d'un "
"cadenas verrouillé sur le système de fermeture. Avec les bons outils, vous "
"pouvez couper la clôture métallique ou crocheter le cadenas. Vous pouvez "
"également examiner la clôture pour voir si elle semble pouvoir être escaladée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Boltcut sound of terrain "locked wire gate"
msgid "Gachunk!"
msgstr "Gachunk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked wire gate"
#. ~ Lockpick message of terrain "locked retractable gate"
msgid "With a satisfying click, the lock on the gate opens."
msgstr "Avec un clic satisfaisant, la serrure de la porte s'ouvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wire gate"
msgstr "porte grillagée fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wire gate"
msgid "A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Un portillon pour une clôture à mailles losangées avec un système de "
"verrouillage pour rester fermé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wire gate"
msgstr "porte grillagée ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chain link fence with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch "
"is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""
"Un portail pour une clôture à mailles losangées avec un système de loquet "
"pour rester fermé. Le loquet est défait, le portail est donc ouvert."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "locked retractable gate"
msgstr "barrière rétractible verrouillée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "locked retractable gate"
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate.  The latch on this one is locked.  With the "
"right tools, you could cut the metal fence or disable the lock."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière de sécurité rétractable. Le loquet de cette barrière est "
"verrouillé. Avec les bons outils, il est possible de couper la clôture "
"métallique ou de désactiver le verrou."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed retractable gate"
msgstr "barrière rétractible fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed retractable gate"
msgid "A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière de sécurité escamotable avec un système de verrouillage pour "
"rester fermée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open retractable gate"
msgstr "barrière rétractible ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open retractable gate"
msgid ""
"A retractable security gate with a latch system to stay closed.  The latch is "
"undone, so the gate has retracted up."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière de sécurité rétractable dotée d'un système de verrouillage pour "
"rester fermée. Le loquet est défait, la barrière s'est donc rétractée vers le "
"haut."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden gate"
msgstr "portail en bois fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgid "A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system."
msgstr "Un portail de qualité commerciale en bois avec un système de verrouillage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden gate"
msgstr "portail en bois ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden split rail gate"
#. ~ Description of terrain "open wooden privacy gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  The gate is wide "
"open, allowing anything to travel through."
msgstr ""
"Un portail de qualité commerciale en bois avec un système de verrouillage. Le "
"portail est grand ouvert, ce qui permet à n'importe quoi de  passer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed screen door"
msgstr "porte-moustiquaire fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed screen door"
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh."
msgstr "Une simple porte en bois avec un grillage."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "rattle!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open screen door"
msgstr "ouvrir la porte grillagée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open screen door"
msgid "A simple wooden doorway with screen mesh.  The door is open."
msgstr "Une simple porte en bois avec un grillage. La porte est ouverte."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed chickenwire gate"
msgstr "grillage fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed chickenwire gate"
msgid "A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed."
msgstr ""
"Un portillon pour une clôture en grillage avec un système de verrouillage "
"simple pour rester fermé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open chickenwire gate"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open chickenwire gate"
msgid ""
"A gate for a chickenwire fence with a simple latch system to stay closed.  "
"The latch is undone, so the gate has swung open."
msgstr ""
"Un portillon pour une clôture en grillage avec un système de verrouillage "
"simple pour rester fermé. Le loquet est défait, le portail s'est donc ouvert."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "picket fence"
msgstr "clôture"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "picket fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wood, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière en bois, rien de compliqué. Elle suggère seulement les endroits "
"où il ne faut pas aller."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "picket fence"
msgid "You pry out the fence post."
msgstr "Vous arrachez le poteau de clôture."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "woven wattle fence"
msgstr "Clôture en bois tressé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "woven wattle fence"
msgid "A flimsy barrier made of woven sticks.  Suitable for small animals."
msgstr "Une barrière fragile faite de bâtons tressés. Convient aux petits animaux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "narrow fence posts"
msgstr "poteaux de clôture étroits"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "narrow fence posts"
msgid "A set of narrow wooden posts for a woven wattle fence."
msgstr "Jeu de poteaux étroits en bois pour une clôture en bois tressé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chain link fence"
msgstr "grillage métallique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chain link fence"
msgid ""
"A tall fence made of woven wires.  There aren't any gaps big enough for you "
"to fit through, so you'll have to cut it, climb it, or find a way around."
msgstr ""
"Une haute clôture faite de fils de fer tressés. Il n'y a pas d'espace assez "
"grand pour que tu puisses passer, alors tu devras la couper, l'escalader ou "
"trouver un moyen de la contourner."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal post"
msgstr "poteau en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal post"
msgid "A set of metal posts that can hold more serious fences."
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble de poteaux métalliques qui peuvent supporter des clôtures plus "
"importantes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chickenwire fence"
msgstr "clôture en grillage à volaille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence"
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy fence made of planks and woven wire, suitable for "
"containing small livestock like chickens."
msgstr ""
"Clôture haute, plutôt fragile, faite de planches et de fil de fer tressé, "
"convenant pour contenir le petit bétail comme les poulets."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal rattling!"
msgstr "bruit métallique!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "screen mesh wall"
msgstr "mur moustiquaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "screen mesh wall"
msgid ""
"A tall, rather flimsy wall made of planks and screen mesh, suitable for "
"keeping the bugs out."
msgstr ""
"Un haut mur plutôt fragile constitué de planches et de treillis métallique, "
"adapté pour éloigner les insectes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chickenwire fence post"
msgstr "poteau de clôture en grillage galvanisé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chickenwire fence post"
#. ~ Description of terrain "fence post"
msgid ""
"A couple of posts that can support a fence.  They look lonely without the "
"fence."
msgstr ""
"Quelques poteaux pouvant supporter une clôture. Ils ont l'air solitaires sans "
"la clôture."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "fence post"
msgstr "poteau de clôture"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wire fence"
msgstr "grille fil de fer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wire fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of wire, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière en fil de fer, rien de compliqué. Elle suggère seulement les "
"endroits où il ne faut pas aller."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "barbed wire fence"
msgstr "fil barbelé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "barbed wire fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of sharp barbed wire.  The more persuasive brother of the wire "
"fence."
msgstr ""
"Barrière faite de fil de fer barbelé tranchant. Le frère plus persuasif de la "
"clôture en fil de fer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rope fence"
msgstr "barrière en corde"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rope fence"
msgid ""
"A barrier made of rope, it's nothing complicated.  Mildly suggests where not "
"to go."
msgstr ""
"Une barrière faite de corde, ce n'est rien de compliqué. Elle suggère "
"légèrement où ne pas aller.\""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "split rail fence"
msgstr "Clôture en rondins fendus"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "split rail fence"
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, suitable for containing "
"livestock like horses, cows and pigs."
msgstr ""
"Clôture assez solide faite de planches et de poteaux de clôture, convenant "
"pour contenir le bétail comme les chevaux, les vaches et les porcs."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "portail fermé à barreaux en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden split rail gate"
msgstr "portail ouvert à barreaux en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal fence"
msgstr "clôture métallique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal fence"
msgid "A simple metal fence."
msgstr "Une section de clôture en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed metal gate"
msgstr "portail en métal fermé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed metal gate"
msgid "A closed metal gate."
msgstr "Un portail en métal fermé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open metal gate"
msgstr "portail en métal ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open metal gate"
msgid "An open metal gate."
msgstr "Un portail en métal ouvert."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden privacy fence"
msgstr "clôture en bois pour la protection de la vie privée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden privacy fence"
msgid ""
"A rather stout fence made of planks and fence posts, it is tall enough to "
"prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'une clôture assez solide, composée de planches et de poteaux de "
"clôture, qui est suffisamment haute pour empêcher les gens de voir dans votre "
"cour."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "portail fermé en bois pour la protection de la vie privée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed wooden privacy gate"
msgid ""
"A commercial quality gate made of wood with a latch system.  It is tall "
"enough to prevent people from seeing into your yard."
msgstr ""
"Un portail de qualité commerciale en bois avec un système de verrouillage. Il "
"est suffisamment haut pour empêcher les gens de voir dans votre cour."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open wooden privacy gate"
msgstr "portail d'intimité en bois ouvert"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railing"
msgstr "rambarde"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railing"
msgid "A section of wooden railing."
msgstr "Section de garde-corps en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "glass railing"
msgstr "garde-fou en verre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "glass railing"
msgid "A section of railing made out of glass."
msgstr "Section de garde-corps en verre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "glass braking!"
msgstr "bris de verre!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-manufactured.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr "kar-rash!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal railing"
msgstr "garde-fou en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal railing"
msgid "A section of metal railing."
msgstr "Une section de garde-corps en métal."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete railing"
msgstr "garde-fou en béton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete railing"
msgid "A section of cemented concrete railing."
msgstr "Une section de garde-corps en béton."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "guard rail"
msgstr "garde-fou"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "guard rail"
msgid ""
"A section of metal railing, put in place to prevent people from falling or "
"taking the easy way out."
msgstr ""
"Une section de garde-corps en métal, installée pour empêcher les gens de "
"tomber ou de prendre le chemin le plus facile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "lowered boom barrier"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "lowered boom barrier"
msgid "A lowered boom barrier."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "cattle feeder"
msgstr "bac d'alimentation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fences-gates.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "cattle feeder"
msgid ""
"A section of tall steel with a solid base and feed spaces above to allow "
"livestock to reach the contained food."
msgstr ""
"Une section de métal haut avec une base solide et des espaces pour la "
"nourriture en hauteur, permettant au bétail d'atteindre la nourriture "
"contenue."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "overgrown floor"
msgstr "sol infesté"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown floor"
msgid ""
"A bare concrete floor, almost completely covered by twitching filaments of "
"gray flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en béton nu, presque entièrement recouvert de filaments gris de chair "
"qui s'agitent."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-fungal.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/json/snippets/snippets.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Snippet in category "<random_sound>"
msgid "SMASH!"
msgstr "SMASH!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "overgrown wall"
msgstr "mur envahi de chair"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flesh.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "overgrown wall"
msgid "A concrete wall overgrown by a grotesque grid of veins and knotted flesh."
msgstr "Un mur de béton recouvert d'un réseau grotesque de veines et de chair nouée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor that can support a roof, could still insulate "
"from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are "
"broken down."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls "
"are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un sol de béton nu et froid avec une trace de peinture jaune, pouvant encore "
"isoler de l'extérieur, mais avec un risque d'effondrement du toit si les murs "
"de soutien sont démolis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of red paint, could still "
"insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls "
"are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un sol de béton nu et froid avec une trace de peinture rouge, pouvant encore "
"isoler de l'extérieur, mais avec un risque d'effondrement du toit si les murs "
"de soutien sont démolis."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with painted stripes of black and yellow, "
"could still insulate from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if "
"supporting walls are broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en béton nu et froid, avec des bandes peintes en noir et jaune, peut "
"encore isoler de l'extérieur, mais l'effondrement du toit est possible si les "
"murs porteurs sont détruits."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a streak of yellow paint and a "
"still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above, could still insulate "
"from the outdoors but roof collapse is possible if supporting walls are "
"broken down."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en béton nu et froid, avec une trace de peinture jaune et une lampe "
"encore fonctionnelle fixée au plafond au-dessus, peut encore isoler de "
"l'extérieur, mais l'effondrement du toit est possible si les murs porteurs "
"sont détruits."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en béton, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"A bare and cold concrete floor with a still-functioning light attached to the "
"ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en béton nu et froid avec une lampe encore en état de marche fixée au "
"plafond au-dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en bois, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"Interlocking wooden tiles that are more than likely treated against fire, "
"with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Des carreaux de bois imbriqués qui sont probablement traités contre le feu, "
"avec une lumière encore fonctionnelle fixée au plafond au-dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick floor"
msgstr "sol en briques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick floor"
msgid "A relatively flat area made of tightly placed bricks.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Une zone relativement plate faite de briques serrées. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dirt floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en terre, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"A floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down, with a "
"still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un sol constitué de terre finement mélangée et tassée, avec une lampe encore "
"fonctionnelle fixée au plafond."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floor, with overhead light"
msgstr "sol métallique, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor, with overhead light"
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Sol métallique à damier de haute qualité et résistant pour réduire le risque "
"de glissade et de chute, avec une lumière encore fonctionnelle fixée au "
"plafond au-dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en béton résistant, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "strong concrete floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling above."
msgstr ""
"Un sol extrêmement résistant fait de barres d'armature soigneusement placées "
"et de béton coulé, avec une lumière encore fonctionnelle fixée au plafond "
"au-dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en linoléum gris, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gray linoleum floor, overhead light"
#. ~ Description of terrain "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgid ""
"Linoleum flooring with a still-functioning light attached to the ceiling "
"above."
msgstr "Sol en linoléum avec une lampe encore en état de marche fixée au plafond."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "white linoleum floor, overhead light"
msgstr "sol en linoléum blanc, plafonnier"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "small rebar roof cage"
msgstr "petit treillis de toit en barres d'armature"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small rebar roof cage"
msgid ""
"A series of structural supports crafted from rebar in order to allow the "
"pouring of concrete for a more stable floor and roof support."
msgstr ""
"Une série de supports structurels fabriqués à partir de barres d'acier pour "
"permettre le coulage du béton, offrant ainsi un support plus stable pour le "
"sol et le toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "SCRRRASH!"
msgstr "SCRRRASH!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "sol en béton armé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "reinforced concrete floor"
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient floor made from carefully placed rebar and poured "
"concrete, capable of providing protection from the elements.  It can support "
"a roof, but that still requires supporting walls, otherwise it may very well "
"cave in."
msgstr ""
"Un sol extrêmement résistant fabriqué à partir de ferraillage soigneusement "
"placé et de béton coulé, capable de fournir une protection contre les "
"éléments. Il peut supporter un toit, mais cela nécessite toujours des murs de "
"soutien, sinon il pourrait très bien s'effondrer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "fractured concrete floor"
msgstr "sol en béton fracturé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "fractured concrete floor"
msgid ""
"Thin strands of violet light shimmer in the air above this concrete floor, "
"like cracks upon a pane of glass.  It can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"De fins filaments de lumière violette scintillent dans l'air au-dessus de ce "
"sol de béton, comme des fissures sur une vitre. Il peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rebar roof cage"
msgstr "treillis de toit en barres d'armature"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rebar roof cage"
msgid ""
"A network of architecturally sound rebar in order to support a floor and roof "
"support, looks like it's missing the poured concrete."
msgstr ""
"Un réseau de ferraillage structurel solide pour soutenir un plancher et un "
"support de toit, semble manquer de béton coulé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
msgstr "sol en béton armé à moitié construit"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built reinforced concrete floor"
msgid ""
"An unfinished construction of rebar and poured concrete; the floor hasn't "
"been smoothed and the roof support isn't quite filled in yet."
msgstr ""
"Une construction inachevée en barres d'acier et en béton coulé ; le sol n'a "
"pas été lissé et le toit n'est pas encore complètement terminé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rock floor"
msgstr "sol en pierre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rock floor"
msgid ""
"A relatively flat area of rock and stone.  Looks stable enough to be mined "
"with the proper mining gear.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Une zone rocheuse relativement plate. Elle semble suffisamment stable pour "
"être exploitée avec l'équipement minier approprié. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "marble floor"
msgstr "sol en marbre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "marble floor"
msgid ""
"A smooth and flat flooring made of marble tiles.  Beautiful and expensive.  "
"Can support a roof."
msgstr "Un sol lisse et plat en marbre. Magnifique et coûteux. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "warped stone floor"
msgstr "sol en pierre déformé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "warped stone floor"
msgid ""
"A rough stone floor.  Its patterns constantly shift as if your mind can't "
"quite understand what it's really seeing.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en pierre rugueuse. Ses motifs changent constamment, comme si votre "
"esprit ne pouvait pas tout à fait comprendre ce qu'il voit réellement. Peut "
"supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal floor"
msgstr "sol en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_habitat_floor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered metal flooring to reduce the risk of slips "
"and falls.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Revêtement de sol en métal damier de haute qualité et résistant pour réduire "
"le risque de glissements et de chutes. Peut supporter un toit."

