msgid "Soft green carpet on a gray linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis vert doux sur un sol en linoléum gris. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "purple carpet"
msgid "Soft purple carpet on a gray linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis violet doux sur un sol en linoléum gris. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "Carpet"
msgid "Base white linoleum floor carpet!"
msgstr "Revêtement de sol en linoléum blanc de base"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "red carpet"
msgid "Soft red carpet on a white linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis rouge doux sur un sol en linoléum blanc. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow carpet"
msgid "Soft yellow carpet on a white linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis jaune doux sur un sol en linoléum blanc. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "green carpet"
msgid "Soft green carpet on a white linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis vert doux sur un sol en linoléum blanc. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "purple carpet"
msgid "Soft purple carpet on a white linoleum floor.  Can support a roof."
msgstr "Tapis violet doux sur un sol en linoléum blanc. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "linoleum tile"
msgstr "carreau de linoléum"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, rubbery material.  Colored a "
"simple white.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Une section de revêtement de sol en caoutchouc résistant, de couleur blanche "
"simple. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "linoleum tile"
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, gray, rubbery material.  Can "
"support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Une section de revêtement de sol en caoutchouc résistant, de couleur grise. "
"Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "painted waxed floor"
msgstr "sol peint et ciré"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "painted waxed floor"
msgid "This section of wax flooring has been painted yellow.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Cette section de plancher en cire a été peinte en jaune. Peut supporter un "
"toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "radiation platform"
msgstr "plateforme de radiation"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "radiation platform"
msgid ""
"A dual-purpose platform that exposes items placed on it to a radioactive "
"source by temporarily hoisting the radioactive material stored within, while "
"also safely containing all objects to avoid contaminating its surroundings.  "
"Operated from an external console."
msgstr ""
"Plate-forme à double fonction qui expose les objets qui y sont placés à une "
"source radioactive en soulevant temporairement les matières radioactives qui "
"y sont stockées, tout en contenant de manière sûre tous les objets afin "
"d'éviter de contaminer son environnement. Fonctionne à partir d'une console "
"externe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "junk metal floor"
msgstr "sol en ferraille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "junk metal floor"
msgid ""
"A simple roof of rusty scrap metal bolted and wire-tied to a makeshift frame. "
" Very fashionable in post-apocalyptic shantytowns.  Hope you like the sound "
"of rain on corrugated metal.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un toit simple en métal rouillé, boulonné et attaché avec du fil à un cadre "
"de fortune. Très à la mode dans les bidonvilles post-apocalyptiques. J'espère "
"que vous aimez le bruit de la pluie sur le métal ondulé. Peut supporter un "
"toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sidewalk"
msgstr "trottoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance, covered by a canvas floor.  May support a roof."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de béton coulé commune, endommagée par le soulèvement du gel et de "
"grandes fissures dues au manque d'entretien, recouverte d'un plancher en "
"toile. Peut supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/isherwood_spawnpoints.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dirt"
msgstr "terre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt"
msgid ""
"It's dirt.  Looks like some fine soil for tillage.  Could also be dug out for "
"construction projects.  Can support a roof."
msgstr ""
"C'est de la terre. Cela ressemble à un sol fin pour le labour. Il pourrait "
"également être creusé pour des projets de construction. Peut supporter un "
"toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sand"
msgstr "sable"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sand"
msgid ""
"A large area of fine sand that could be useful in a number of ways, if it was "
"extracted properly."
msgstr ""
"Une grande zone de sable fin qui pourrait être utile à plusieurs égards, s'il "
"était extrait correctement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mud"
msgstr "boue"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mud"
msgid "An area of wet, slick mud."
msgstr "Une zone de boue humide et glissante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "moss"
msgstr "mousse"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "moss"
msgid "A patch of moist, spongy moss."
msgstr "Une zone de mousse humide et spongieuse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "clay"
msgstr "argile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "clay"
msgid ""
"A large area of malleable clay, suitable for kiln firing if it was extracted "
"properly."
msgstr ""
"Une grande surface d'argile malléable, apte à la cuisson au four si elle a "
"été extraite correctement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of clay"
msgid "A mound of clay soil."
msgstr "Un monticule de terre argileuse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/tropical_terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_groundxeno.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "splosh!"
msgstr "splosh!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "burnt floor"
msgstr "sol brûlé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "burnt floor"
msgid ""
"Whatever this floor used to be made of, it's little more than charred remains "
"now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "twang!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "paper floor"
msgstr "sol en papier mâché"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "paper floor"
msgid ""
"A floor made of ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky wasp saliva.  It "
"has, or at least had, a roof of similar a material."
msgstr ""
"Un sol fait d'une matière pulpeuse ambiguë, recouvert de salive collante de "
"guêpe. Il avait, ou a peut-être encore, un toit du même matériau.\""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "paper floor"
msgid "A floor made of ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Un sol fait d'une matière pulpeuse ambiguë, recouvert de salive collante de "
"guêpe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "hard paper floor"
msgstr "sol en papier mâché durci"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "hard paper floor"
msgid ""
"A hardened cardboard floor made of chewed-up trees and resin mixed with wasp "
"saliva.  It has, or at least had, a roof of a similar material."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en carton durci, fait de morceaux d'arbres mâchés et de résine "
"mélangée à de la salive de guêpe. Il avait, ou a peut-être encore, un toit du "
"même matériau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "paper brood cap"
msgstr "bouchon de couvain en papier."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "paper brood cap"
msgid ""
"A thin paper floor, protecting the pupating wasp larva until it's ready to "
"emerge."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en papier fin, protégeant la larve de guêpe en cours de nymphose "
"jusqu'à ce qu'elle soit prête à émerger."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
