msgstr "L'ascenseur commence à bouger avant que vous ne puissiez toucher le panneau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_ROBOFAC_ELEVATOR_UP" in
#. terrain "elevator controls"'s examine action
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_ROBOFAC_ELEVATOR_DOWN" in
#. terrain "elevator controls"'s examine action
msgid ""
"The control panels' screen flashes before displaying \"UNAUTHORIZED\" in bold "
"red letters."
msgstr ""
"L'écran des panneaux de contrôle clignote avant d'afficher \" NON AUTORISÉ \" "
"en grosses lettres rouges."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "powerless controls"
msgstr "commandes débranchées"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "powerless controls"
msgid "The control face for an elevator.  It's currently unpowered."
msgstr "La face de contrôle d'un ascenseur. Il n'est actuellement pas alimenté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dark pedestal"
msgstr "piédestal noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dark pedestal"
msgid ""
"A dark stone pedestal covered in ancient, unintelligible symbols.  Looks "
"ominous."
msgstr ""
"Un piédestal de pierre sombre couvert de symboles anciens et inintelligibles. "
"Il a l'air inquiétant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "light pedestal"
msgstr "piédestal lumineux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "light pedestal"
msgid "A light stone pedestal covered in ancient, unintelligible symbols."
msgstr "Un léger piédestal de pierre couvert de symboles anciens et inintelligibles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "yellow switch"
msgstr "interrupteur jaune"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow switch"
msgid "A yellow switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interrupteur jaune. Est-ce une bonne idée de l'activer?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "cyan switch"
msgstr "interrupteur cyan"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "cyan switch"
msgid "A cyan switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interrupteur cyan. Est-ce une bonne idée de l'activer?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "purple switch"
msgstr "interrupteur violet"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "purple switch"
msgid "A purple switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interrupteur violet. Est-ce une bonne idée de l'activer?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "checkered switch"
msgstr "interrupteur à carreaux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "checkered switch"
msgid "A checkered switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interrupteur à damier. Est-ce une bonne idée de l'activer?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "nuclear reactor core"
msgstr "cœur de réacteur nucléaire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "nuclear reactor core"
msgid ""
"A naval A1B reactor, used in Gerald R. Ford-class aircraft carriers.  It can "
"produce enough steam to generate 125 megawatts of energy."
msgstr ""
"Réacteur naval A1B, utilisé dans les porte-avions de la classe Gerald R. "
"Ford. Il peut produire suffisamment de vapeur pour générer 125 mégawatts "
"d'énergie."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin wall"
msgstr "mur en résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin wall"
msgid ""
"A wall made of a glistening, nearly opaque, plastic-like substance.  Deep "
"within, you can barely see a network of pulsating green conduits, snaking "
"through it like blood vessels.  The material is hard, warm to the touch, and "
"slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Un mur fait d'une substance plastique scintillante, presque opaque. En "
"profondeur, on distingue à peine un réseau de conduits verts pulsants, "
"serpentant comme des vaisseaux sanguins. La matière est dure, chaude au "
"toucher et légèrement humide."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alienciv.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alienciv.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "boom!"
msgstr "boom!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin cage"
msgstr "cage en résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin cage"
msgid ""
"A resin wall that opens into a series of small honeycomb-like hexagons, "
"allowing the passage of air and light.  While still made of the same sturdy "
"material, it is thinner and more delicate in appearance."
msgstr ""
"Un mur en résine qui s'ouvre sur une série de petits hexagones en forme de "
"nid d'abeille, permettant le passage de l'air et de la lumière. Bien qu'il "
"soit toujours fabriqué dans le même matériau robuste, il est plus fin et "
"d'apparence plus délicate."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin floor"
msgstr "sol en résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
msgid ""
"A nearly opaque, plastic-like floor.  It has a gentle curve from wall to "
"wall, but in the central areas is quite flat.  The material is hard, warm to "
"the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Un sol presque opaque, semblable à du plastique. Il présente une légère "
"courbe d'un mur à l'autre, mais dans les zones centrales, il est plutôt plat. "
"Le matériau est dur, chaud au toucher et légèrement humide."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
msgid ""
"A nearly opaque, plastic-like floor that is smooth and flat.  The material is "
"hard, warm to the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Un sol presque opaque, semblable à du plastique, lisse et plat. Le matériau "
"est dur, chaud au toucher et légèrement humide."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin roof"
msgstr "toit en résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin roof"
msgid ""
"A wide, domed section of nearly opaque, plastic-like material.  When the "
"light hits it, a network of multicolored conduits like blood vessels can be "
"seen snaking through its glistening interior."
msgstr ""
"Une large section bombée d'un matériau presque opaque, semblable à du "
"plastique. Lorsque la lumière l'atteint, on peut voir un réseau de conduits "
"multicolores, comme des vaisseaux sanguins, serpenter à l'intérieur."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed resin portal"
msgstr "portail de résine fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed resin portal"
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is closed tightly, but it looks like a firm push would cause it to snap "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Une trappe tricuspide faite d'une sorte de matériau humide, flexible et "
"résineux. Celle-ci est fermée hermétiquement, mais il semble qu'une pression "
"ferme la ferait s'ouvrir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open resin portal"
msgstr "ouvrir portail de résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open resin portal"
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is open, the flaps held out by some sort of stringy mucus-like substance."
msgstr ""
"Une trappe tricuspide faite d'un matériau humide, flexible et résineux. "
"Celle-ci est ouverte, les volets sont maintenus écartés par une sorte de "
"substance muqueuse filandreuse."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "resin-lined hole"
msgstr "trou bordé de résine"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "resin-lined hole"
msgid "An open hole in the resin wall, large enough for you to crawl through."
msgstr "Un trou à travers le mur de résine assez large pour ramper à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass"
msgstr "verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass"
msgid ""
"An endless expanse of black glass.  It perfectly reflects the darkness around "
"it."
msgstr ""
"Une surface de verre noire interminable reflétant parfaitement les ombres "
"environnantes."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "perfect basalt wall"
msgstr "mur de basalt parfait"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "perfect basalt wall"
msgid ""
"Hexagonal columns of basalt spring from the dark floor.  Each a perfect copy "
"of the next."
msgstr ""
"Des colonnes hexagonales de basalte s'élèvent du sol sombre. Chacune est une "
"copie parfaite de la suivante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gravel"
msgstr "graviers"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gravel"
msgid ""
"An area of small, uniformly-sized stones.  Often used for roads, as railroad "
"ballast, and in many other applications."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de petites pierres de taille uniforme. Souvent utilisée pour les "
"routes, comme ballast ferroviaire, et dans de nombreuses autres applications."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad track"
msgstr "chemin de fer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm.  You could probably reclaim lengths of the track "
"itself with a metalcutting tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"Les trains roulaient autrefois sur ces rails. Ces voies ferrées sont "
"inutilisées depuis le Cataclysme. Vous pourriez probablement récupérer des "
"longueurs de la voie elle-même avec un outil de découpage des métaux comme "
"une scie à métaux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad tie"
msgstr "traverse de chemin de fer"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad tie"
msgid "A crosstie, used to support train rails."
msgstr "Une traverse, utilisée pour soutenir les rails de train."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm.  A crosstie sits underneath, supporting the rails.  "
"You could probably reclaim lengths of the track itself with a metalcutting "
"tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""
"Les trains roulaient autrefois sur ces rails. Ces voies ferrées sont "
"inutilisées depuis le Cataclysme. Une traverse de chemin de fer se trouve en "
"dessous, soutenant les rails. Vous pourriez probablement récupérer des "
"longueurs de la voie elle-même avec un outil de découpage des métaux comme "
"une scie à métaux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "buffer stop"
msgstr "heurtoir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "buffer stop"
msgid ""
"A tiny blockade on the train tracks, meant to signify the end of a track, or "
"mark a 'no-go' zone for trains."
msgstr ""
"Un petit barrage sur les voies ferrées, destiné à marquer la fin d'une voie "
"ou une zone interdite aux trains."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "railroad crossing signal"
msgstr "signal de passage à niveau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad crossing signal"
msgid ""
"Traffic lights meant to light and make noise when a train approaches, to "
"prevent people from turning into meaty mush while they cross the tracks.  "
"Won't stop people from turning into meaty mush by other means, though."
msgstr ""
"Feux de signalisation destinés à s'allumer et à émettre un bruit lorsqu'un "
"train approche, afin d'empêcher les gens de se transformer en purée de viande "
"en traversant les voies. Cependant, cela ne les empêchera pas de se "
"transformer en purée de viande par d'autres moyens."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture-plants.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clang."
msgstr "clang."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "crossbuck"
msgstr "croix de Saint-André"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "crossbuck"
msgid ""
"A traffic sign intended to indicate a level railway crossing.  If the trains "
"were still running."
msgstr ""
"Un panneau de signalisation destiné à indiquer un passage à niveau. Si les "
"trains circulaient encore."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "small railroad track"
msgid_plural "small railroad tracks"
msgstr[0] "rail de train miniature"
msgstr[1] "rails de train miniature"
msgstr[2] "rails de train miniature"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small railroad track"
msgid ""
"Like a railroad track, only smaller.  You could probably run a small vehicle "
"on this."
msgstr ""
"Comme une voie ferrée, mais plus petite. Vous pourriez probablement faire "
"circuler un petit véhicule dessus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "recessed railroad track"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "recessed railroad track"
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks sit flush with the "
"road.  You could probably reclaim lengths of the track itself with a "
"metalcutting tool like a hacksaw."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sandbox"
msgstr "bac à sable"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sandbox"
msgid ""
"Children used to play in this sandbox.  The population of lice probably "
"diminished considerably now that they no longer do."
msgstr ""
"Les enfants jouaient autrefois dans ce bac à sable. La population de poux a "
"probablement considérablement diminué maintenant qu'ils ne le font plus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "slide"
msgstr "toboggan"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "slide"
msgid "A children's slide.  It's too small for you to slide on comfortably."
msgstr "Un toboggan pour enfants.  Trop petit pour vous."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "monkey bars"
msgstr "série de barres parallèles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monkey bars"
msgid ""
"A set of monkey bars to be used by children to train their arm strength, or, "
"in happier days, to just have fun."
msgstr ""
"Un ensemble de barres parallèles pour que les enfants puissent s'entraîner à "
"la force des bras ou, dans les bons jours, simplement s'amuser."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "backboard"
msgstr "panier de basket"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
msgid "A basketball backboard."
msgstr "un panneau de panier de basketball."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
msgid "A metal backboard."
msgstr "Un panneau métallique."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rain gutter"
msgstr "gouttière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rain gutter"
msgid "Channels water from the roof towards the ground, it looks flimsy."
msgstr "Évacue l'eau du toit vers le sol, il a l'air fragile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "gutter drop"
msgstr "descente de gouttière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "gutter drop"
msgid ""
"A spot in the gutter where the water flows into a downspout.  It looks "
"flimsy.  You may be able to climb down here."
msgstr ""
"Un endroit dans la gouttière où l'eau s'écoule dans une descente de "
"gouttière. Il a l'air fragile. Vous pourriez peut-être y descendre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "downspout"
msgstr "descente de gouttière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "downspout"
msgid ""
"A length of gutter running from the roof to the ground, you could place a "
"container underneath it to collect rainwater.  It looks flimsy.  You may be "
"able to climb up here."
msgstr ""
"Un tronçon de gouttière allant du toit au sol, vous pourriez placer un "
"contenant en dessous pour recueillir l'eau de pluie. Il a l'air fragile. Vous "
"pourriez peut-être y monter."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "flat roof"
msgstr "toit plat"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit gris."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tar paper flat roof"
msgstr "toit plat en papier goudronné"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tar paper flat roof"
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop covered with tar paper."
msgstr "Une section de toit couverte de papier goudronné."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shingle flat roof"
msgstr "toit en bardeaux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shingle flat roof"
msgid "A flat section of rooftop covered with shingles."
msgstr "Une section de toit en ardoises."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "thatched roof"
msgstr "toit de chaume"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "thatched roof"
msgid "A section of roof made out of straw."
msgstr "Une section de toit en chaume."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal flat roof"
msgstr "toit en métal plat"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal flat roof"
msgid "A section of flat, sheet metal rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en tôle."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tile flat roof"
msgstr "toit en tuile plat"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tile flat roof"
msgid "A section of flat, tiled rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en tuiles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "skylight"
msgstr "puits de lumière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "skylight"
msgid "A giant sheet of glass inserted into the roof to let light pass through."
msgstr ""
"Une gigantesque plaque de verre insérée dans le toit pour laisser passer la "
"lumière."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "rock roof"
msgstr "toit en pierre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "rock roof"
msgid "A section of flat natural rock."
msgstr "Une section de paroi rocheuse plate servant de toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "warped roof"
msgstr "toit déformé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "warped roof"
msgid ""
"A section of flat, stone-like rooftop.  It is patterned with grooves and "
"lines that constantly shift."
msgstr ""
"Une section de toit en pierre inscrite de lignes et de rainures fines ayant "
"l'air de bouger constamment."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid "A flat surface made of ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Une surface plane faite de matière pulpeuse ambiguë, recouverte de salive "
"collante de guêpe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
msgid ""
"A flat surface made of hardened, ambiguous pulpy matter, covered in sticky "
"wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Une surface plane faite de matière pulpeuse durcie et ambiguë, recouverte de "
"salive collante de guêpe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "concrete roof"
msgstr "toit en béton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete roof"
msgid "A flat section of concrete rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en béton."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "wooden roof"
msgstr "toit en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden roof"
msgid "A flat section of wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Un section de toit en bois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "treated wooden roof"
msgstr "toit en bois traité"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "treated wooden roof"
msgid "A flat section of flame-resistant wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en bois ignifugé."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metal roof"
msgstr "toit en métal"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metal roof"
msgid "A high-quality and sturdy section of metallic rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en métal solide et de bonne qualité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "red metal roof"
msgstr "toit en métal rouge"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "red metal roof"
msgid ""
"A sturdy section of metallic rooftop, painted red for visibility and weather "
"resistance."
msgstr ""
"Une section robuste de toiture métallique, peinte en rouge pour la visibilité "
"et la résistance aux intempéries."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "sod roof"
msgstr "toit en tourbe"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sod roof"
msgid "A section of rooftop made out of sod."
msgstr "Un section de toit en tourbe."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brick roof"
msgstr "toit en briques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brick roof"
msgid "A section of brick rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toit en briques"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "canvas roof"
msgstr "toit en toile"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "canvas roof"
msgid "A section of canvas rooftop."
msgstr "Une section de toiture en toile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "treetop"
msgstr "canopée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "treetop"
msgid "The upper branches of a tree.  There's just enough room to perch here."
msgstr ""
"Les branches supérieures d'un arbre. Il y a juste assez de place pour se "
"percher ici."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dead treetop"
msgstr "sommet d'arbre mort"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dead treetop"
msgid ""
"The bare upper branches of a dead tree.  There's just enough room to perch "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Les branches supérieures nues d'un arbre mort. Il y a juste assez de place "
"pour se percher ici."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "giant fern top"
msgstr "sommet de fougère géante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "giant fern top"
msgid ""
"The top of some unearthly gigantic fern.  There is enough room to perch up "
"here, but only just."
msgstr ""
"Le sommet d'une gigantesque fougère d'un autre monde. Il y a juste assez de "
"place pour se percher ici."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow pit"
msgstr "trou peu profond"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow pit"
msgid ""
"A pit that could be dug even deeper or filled up.  Also useful as a starting "
"foundation for some constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un trou pouvant être creusé encore plus profondément ou rempli. Également "
"utile comme fondation de départ pour certaines constructions."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pit"
msgid ""
"A steep hole that could seriously injure something if it fell in, potentially "
"fatal if it was filled with sharp and dangerous things.  Deep enough for more "
"advanced construction projects, and possibly to reach groundwater if "
"constructed properly."
msgstr ""
"Un trou profond qui pourrait sérieusement blesser quelque chose s'il y "
"tombait, potentiellement fatal s'il était rempli de choses tranchantes et "
"dangereuses. Assez profond pour des projets de construction plus avancés, et "
"peut-être pour atteindre l'eau souterraine s'il était construit correctement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "corpse filled pit"
msgstr "fosse remplie de corps"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "corpse filled pit"
msgid ""
"A giant trench full of corpses, maybe even a mass graveyard.  The bodies "
"could be dug out, but nothing in here looks remotely usable."
msgstr ""
"Une grand trou rempli de cadavres.  Vous pourriez en sortir des corps mais "
"vous doutez que grand chose dessus soit en assez bon état pour être très "
"utile."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered pit"
msgstr "fosse recouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered pit"
msgid ""
"A deep pit with a plank placed across it, looks sturdy enough to cross "
"safely.  The plank could be removed to make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Un trou profond au dessus duquel une planche à été placée comme pont de "
"fortune ayant l'air assez solide pour traverser sans danger.  La planche "
"pourrait être retirée pour le rendre dangereux à traverser à nouveau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "spiked pit"
msgid "A narrow trench full of very pointy things that would easily puncture a body."
msgstr ""
"Une tranchée étroite remplie de choses très pointues qui pourraient "
"facilement percer un corps."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered spiked pit"
msgstr "fosse hérissée recouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered spiked pit"
msgid ""
"Menacing with sharp spears along the bottom, this pit has a plank across it "
"to allow someone or something to cross safely.  The plank could be removed to "
"make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Un trou profond hérissé de morceaux de bois pointus au dessus duquel une "
"planche à été placée comme pont de fortune ayant l'air assez solide pour "
"traverser sans danger.  La planche pourrait être retirée pour le rendre "
"dangereux à traverser à nouveau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "glass pit"
msgid ""
"Looks like a ton of broken glass was dumped into this pit.  Might not fatal "
"to fall in, but it wouldn't be pleasant to try to crawl out."
msgstr ""
"On dirait qu'une grande quantité de verre brisé à été jeté dans ce trou.  Ce "
"ne serait probablement pas fatal de tomber dedans, mais définitivement "
"douloureux à en sortir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "covered glass pit"
msgstr "fosse en verre recouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "covered glass pit"
msgid ""
"A plank has been placed carefully to allow traversal over this ditch full of "
"large glass shards.  The plank could be removed to make it dangerous again."
msgstr ""
"Une planche à été placée pour permettre de traverser ce trou rempli de verre "
"brisé.  La planche pourrait être retirée pour le rendre dangereux à traverser "
"à nouveau."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "dead drop pit"
msgstr "trou de point de chute"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "dead drop pit"
msgid ""
"A seemingly innocuous shallow pit.  Careful inspection reveals a black "
"canister half-buried in the exposed soil."
msgstr ""
"Un trou peu profond ayant l'air initialement inoffensif, mais un second coup "
"d'œil révélant un cylindre noir sortant à peine du sol."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_BEM_human_sample_deliver" in terrain
#. "dead drop pit"'s examine action
msgid "You prepare the drop as instructed"
msgstr "Vous préparez la goutte comme indiqué"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_BEM_human_sample_deliver" in
#. terrain "dead drop pit"'s examine action
msgid "You don't have anything to deliver."
msgstr "Vous n'avez rien à livrer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "small den"
msgstr "petite tanière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "small den"
msgid "A small den that burrowing animals such as groundhogs or hares call home."
msgstr "Une petite tanière probablement creusée par une marmotte ou un lièvre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "large den"
msgstr "large tanière"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "large den"
msgid "A large den that burrowing animals such as bears and foxes call home."
msgstr ""
"Une tanière de taille conséquente pouvant probablement accueillir un ours ou "
"un loup."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#: data/json/monsters/slimes.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "slime"
msgid_plural "slimes"
msgstr[0] "slime"
msgstr[1] "slimes"
msgstr[2] "slimes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "slime"
msgid ""
"A disgusting, slippery mess.  Could be used to stash things, because who'd "
"want to touch it?"
msgstr ""
"Une masse gluante et répugnante. Pourrait être utilisée pour cacher des "
"choses, car qui voudrait la toucher ?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "solid bark wall"
msgstr "mur d'écorce solide"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "solid bark wall"
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark, enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  It will "
"probably burn quite well."
msgstr ""
"Un mur solide d'écorce appartenant à un arbre énorme. Probablement très "
"flammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "chipped bark wall"
msgstr "mur d'écorce ébréché"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "chipped bark wall"
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  Some of it has "
"been broken away."
msgstr ""
"Un mur solide d'écorce appartenant au tronc d'un arbre énorme. Une bonne "
"partie a été arrachée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "broken bark wall"
msgstr "mur d'écorce cassé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "broken bark wall"
msgid ""
"A formerly solid wall of bark, now almost completely destroyed and waiting to "
"collapse."
msgstr ""
"Un mur de bois autrefois solide, maintenant presque complètement détruit et "
"prêt à s'effondrer."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "solid wood wall"
msgstr "mur en bois épais"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "solid wood wall"
msgid "A solid wall of naturally grown wood.  Likely very flammable."
msgstr ""
"Un mur solide de bois ayant poussé naturellement. Probablement très "
"inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bark"
msgstr "écorce"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bark"
msgid "A solid piece of bark covers the floor here."
msgstr "Une section d'écorce ininterrompue couvre le sol ici."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "branches with leaves"
msgstr "branches avec des feuilles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "branches with leaves"
msgid "Thin branches emerge here, covered with thick, large leaves."
msgstr "De fines branches émergent d'ici, recouvertes de feuilles épaisses et larges."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "root floor"
msgstr "sol racineux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_druid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "root floor"
msgid "A dirt floor covered with roots."
msgstr "Une section de sol couvert de racines."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "downward root slope"
msgstr "pente de racines descendante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "downward root slope"
msgid "A downward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Une pente descendante de sol couvert de racines."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "upward root slope"
msgstr "pente de racines montante"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "upward root slope"
msgid "An upward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Une pente ascendante de sol couvert de racines."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "closed bramble roots"
msgstr "racines de ronces fermées"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bramble roots"
msgid "A bramble of roots covering a large hole.  They could easily be pulled apart."
msgstr ""
"Un enchevêtrement de racines couvrant un trou assez large. Vous pourriez "
"facilement les écarter."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "open bramble roots"
msgstr "racines de ronces ouvertes"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "open bramble roots"
msgid "A bramble of roots, pulled apart to reveal a hole."
msgstr "Un enchevêtrement de racines ayant été écartées pour révéler un trou."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wall"
msgstr "mur"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wall"
msgid ""
"A standard wall consisting of a wooden support structure filled with "
"insulation and drywalled.  Painted a neutral off-white or cream color, it "
"could use some more vibrant paint.  Looks flammable."
msgstr ""
"Un mur standard composé d'une structure de support en bois isolée et plaqué "
"de plaques de plâtre. Peint dans une couleur neutre blanc cassé ou crème, il "
"pourrait utiliser une peinture plus vibrante. Semble inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "half-built wall"
msgstr "mur à moitié construit"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built wall"
msgid ""
"An incomplete wall of refined wood, dotted with carefully placed nails to "
"provide proper support.  It requires some more planks and nails before it'd "
"be considered a suitable wall."
msgstr ""
"Un mur inachevé en bois raffiné, parsemé de clous soigneusement placés pour "
"fournir un support approprié. Il nécessite quelques planches et clous "
"supplémentaires avant d'être considéré comme un mur convenable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "pony wall"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "pony wall"
msgid ""
"A short divider wall consisting of a wooden support structure with drywall.  "
"Painted an all-too-common and neutral off-white or cream color.  Looks "
"flammable."
msgstr ""
"Une courte cloison composée d'une structure de support en bois avec des "
"plaques de plâtre. Peinte dans une couleur neutre blanc cassé ou crème, trop "
"commune. Semble inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "wooden wall"
msgstr "mur en bois"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden wall"
msgid ""
"A finished wall of planks and support beams, capable of supporting an upper "
"level or roof.  Highly flammable."
msgstr ""
"Un mur fini en planches et poutres de support, capable de supporter un niveau "
"supérieur ou un toit. Hautement inflammable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete wall"
msgid ""
"An aesthetically pleasing design with simple lines, this type of concrete was "
"used with a weaker chemical mixture in order to have faster setting times.  "
"Not ideal for multi-story buildings, but still capable of supporting a roof."
msgstr ""
"Un design esthétique avec des lignes simples, ce type de béton a été utilisé "
"avec un mélange chimique plus faible afin d'avoir des temps de séchage plus "
"rapides. N'est pas idéal pour les bâtiments à plusieurs étages, mais peut "
"toujours supporter un toit."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "simple concrete wall"
msgstr "mur simple en béton"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "simple concrete wall"
msgid ""
"A durable and uniform concrete wall, quite drab without decoration.  More "
"than capable of supporting a roof, as well as keeping out most anything, save "
"for vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Un mur en béton solide et uniforme, assez terne sans décorations. Plus que "
"capable de supporter un plafond, ainsi que de garder plus ou moins quoi que "
"ce soit à l'extérieur n'ayant pas la force d'un véhicule lourd."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "red wall"
msgstr "mur rouge"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "red wall"
msgid "A wall, painted red."
msgstr "Une section de mur peint rouge."

