#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bone floor"
msgstr "sol osseux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bone floor"
msgid ""
"An impossibly hard, impregnable bone structure covers the internals of the "
"beast."
msgstr ""
"Une structure impossiblement solide et résistante ressemblant à de l'os "
"couvrant les sections internes de cette créature gigantesque."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bone wall"
msgstr "mur osseux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bone wall"
msgid ""
"An amazingly durable, impregnable wall of bone stands before you, forming the "
"outer shell of the eldritch monster."
msgstr ""
"Un mur d'os absurdement dur et impénétrable se dresse devant vous, la "
"coquille extérieure de cette créature abominable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "monster teeth"
msgid_plural "monster teeth"
msgstr[0] "dents de monstre"
msgstr[1] "dents de monstre"
msgstr[2] "dents de monstre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monster teeth"
msgid ""
"A fractal array of uncountable, bristling teeth that seem impossibly sharp, "
"even at a conceptual level.  An iridescent haze surrounds it, as if light "
"itself cannot help but be separated in their presence.  You surmise you could "
"extract some for your own use, if you had an appropriate tool to remove them "
"from the wall they're imbedded in."
msgstr ""
"Un tableau fractal de dents innombrables et hérissées, semblant "
"incroyablement acérées, même à un niveau conceptuel. Une brume irisée "
"l'entoure, comme si la lumière elle-même ne pouvait s'empêcher de se séparer "
"en leur présence. Vous supposez que vous pourriez en extraire quelques-unes "
"pour votre propre usage, si vous aviez un outil approprié pour les retirer du "
"mur dans lequel elles sont incrustées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "flesh floor"
msgstr "sol de chair"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh floor"
msgid ""
"Walking over the innards of this monstrous beast, you can still feel movement "
"underneath your feet."
msgstr ""
"Vous ressentez des choses toujours en mouvement sous vos pieds lorsque vous "
"marchez sur les entrailles de cette abomination."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#: data/json/monsters/zed_fusion.json
#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "flesh wall"
msgid_plural "flesh walls"
msgstr[0] "mur de chair"
msgstr[1] "murs de chair"
msgstr[2] "murs de chair"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid "Warm to the touch, the tainted flesh of this monstrous being still twitches."
msgstr ""
"Chaud au toucher, la chair pourrissante de cet être monstrueux se trémousse "
"encore."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid ""
"A thick wall of fleshy cartilage.  With the proper tools, you could smash "
"right through it."
msgstr ""
"Un mur épais de cartilage et de chair. Avec les outils appropriés vous "
"pourriez probablement percer à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "flesh wall"
msgid ""
"This section of flesh seems hollowed out.  You can see silky, translucent "
"larvae wriggling inside, consuming flesh at a prodigious pace."
msgstr ""
"Cette partie de la chair semble creusée. On y voit des larves soyeuses et "
"translucides s'agiter à l'intérieur, consommant la chair à un rythme "
"prodigieux."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "monster hemolymph"
msgstr "hémolymphe de monstre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "monster hemolymph"
msgid ""
"A shallow stream of glowing yellow ichor streaks through the beast.  Peering "
"into it, you can see dark shadows moving under the surface."
msgstr ""
"Un ruisseau peu profond d'ichor jaune luisant court à travers la bête, en "
"observant de plus près, vous observez des ombres obscures pullulant sous la "
"surface."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "cartilage"
msgstr "cartilage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "cartilage"
msgid "A thin, transparent cartilage webbing."
msgstr "Sangle cartilagineuse fine et transparente."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "Riiiiip!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "nether brain"
msgstr "cerveau du néant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_nether_monster.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "nether brain"
msgid "An oozing pile of wrinkled, decomposing flesh."
msgstr "Un amas suintant de chair ridée et en décomposition."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass ground"
msgstr "sol de verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass ground"
msgid ""
"A patch of black glass, roughly textured and entirely solid.  The little of "
"it you can see through reveals larger, darker pebbles underneath."
msgstr ""
"Une plaque de verre noir, grossièrement texturée et entièrement solide. Le "
"peu que l'on peut voir à travers révèle des cailloux plus gros et plus "
"sombres."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black grass"
msgstr "herbe noire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black grass"
msgid "A patch of thick, luxuriant midnight black grass.  Every blade is a razor."
msgstr ""
"Une parcelle d'herbe épaisse et luxuriante d'un noir de minuit. Chaque lame "
"est un rasoir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass floor"
msgstr "sol en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass floor"
msgid ""
"A floor of black glass, textured with the knots and whorls of old and "
"well-loved wood boards."
msgstr ""
"Un sol en verre noir, texturé par les nœuds et les spirales de vieilles "
"planches de bois bien aimées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass floor"
msgid "A black glass floor formed from tessellated octagonal tiles."
msgstr "Un sol en verre noir formé de carreaux octogonaux tessellés."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass wall"
msgstr "mur en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass wall"
msgid ""
"A heavy wall of black glass, textured with the knots and whorls of old and "
"well-loved wood boards."
msgstr ""
"Un lourd mur de verre noir, texturé avec les nœuds et les tourbillons de "
"planches de bois anciennes et bien-aimées."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "edge of a vastness"
msgstr "Bord de l'immensité"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "edge of a vastness"
msgid ""
"Beyond this point stretches an endless expanse of smooth black.  You are so "
"small, in comparison.  And why would you even want to leave?"
msgstr ""
"Au-delà de ce point s'étend une vaste étendue de noir lisse. Vous êtes si "
"petit en comparaison. Et pourquoi voudriez-vous même partir ?"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass door"
msgstr "porte en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass door"
msgid ""
"A door made from black glass, fused shut on useless hinges.  If you look very "
"closely, you can see the tiny ridges of fingerprints on the knob."
msgstr ""
"Une porte en verre noir, scellée sur des charnières inutiles. Si vous "
"regardez de très près, vous pouvez voir les minuscules crêtes des empreintes "
"digitales sur la poignée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black fiberglass fence"
msgstr "clôture en fibre de verre noire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black fiberglass fence"
msgid ""
"A network of delicate glass threads strung between thicker posts.  The wind "
"blowing across them produces a faint, eerie whine."
msgstr ""
"Un réseau de fils de verre délicats tendus entre des poteaux plus épais. Le "
"vent qui souffle à travers eux produit un faible et étrange sifflement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "sharp tinkling!"
msgstr "un tintement aigu !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "resonant tinkling!"
msgstr "un tintement résonnant !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "spined glasswire fence"
msgstr "clôture en fil de verre épineux"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "spined glasswire fence"
msgid ""
"Rolling coils of thin black glass covered in delicate barbs.  It's "
"reminiscent of snowflakes."
msgstr ""
"Des rouleaux de verre noir fin recouverts de délicates arêtes. Cela rappelle "
"les flocons de neige."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "translucent black glass wall"
msgstr "mur de verre noir translucide"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "translucent black glass wall"
msgid ""
"An area of black glass translucent enough to allow murky shapes to be seen "
"through it."
msgstr ""
"Une zone de verre noir translucide suffisamment pour permettre de voir des "
"formes indistinctes à travers."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass dust"
msgstr "poussière de verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass dust"
msgid ""
"A pile of glass ground so finely that the slightest breeze bears it aloft "
"into mesmerizing clouds."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de verre broyé si finement que la moindre brise le porte en l'air en "
"nuages envoûtants."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass curtains"
msgstr "rideaux en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass curtains"
msgid ""
"The shape of a window and trim, covered in drapings of black glass.  "
"Presumably it was once transparent; now the opaque curtains are solid and "
"immobile."
msgstr ""
"La forme d'une fenêtre et de ses moulures, recouverte de draperies de verre "
"noir. On suppose qu'elle était autrefois transparente ; maintenant, les "
"rideaux opaques sont solides et immobiles."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "jagged glass aperture"
msgstr "ouverture en verre dentelé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "jagged glass aperture"
msgid ""
"A ragged hole smashed through a thin portion of black glass.  The biggest "
"shards could probably be snapped off to make it safer to pass through."
msgstr ""
"Un trou déchiqueté s'est frayé un chemin à travers une fine portion de verre "
"noir. Les plus gros éclats pourraient probablement être cassés pour rendre le "
"passage plus sûr."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass pole"
msgstr "poteau en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass pole"
msgid ""
"A spar of glass fused into the ground, still bearing the jagged edges of the "
"structure it once supported."
msgstr ""
"Un éclat de verre se fondit dans le sol, portant encore les bords déchiquetés "
"de la structure qu'il soutenait autrefois."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass well"
msgstr "puit en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass well"
msgid ""
"This was formerly a well shaft and pump mechanism; it is now so obscured with "
"bubbles of black glass that only a faint outline of the original shape can be "
"seen."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agissait autrefois d'un puits et d'un mécanisme de pompe ; il est "
"maintenant tellement obscurci par des bulles de verre noir que l'on ne voit "
"plus qu'un faible contour de la forme originale."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass bars"
msgstr "barres de verre noire"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass bars"
msgid "Thick spars of black glass extending from floor to ceiling."
msgstr "D'épaisses barres de verre noir s'étendent du sol au plafond."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "a tremendous shattering!"
msgstr "un énorme fracas !"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Bashing failed sound
msgid "clonk!"
msgstr "clonk!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass column"
msgstr "colonne en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass column"
msgid "A tremendous spar of black glass."
msgstr "Une énorme flèche de verre noir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "shallow black pool"
msgstr "flaque noire peu profonde"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow black pool"
msgid ""
"At first glance, this looks like a smooth pool of black water.  Closer "
"examination reveals it to be fine glass dust."
msgstr ""
"À première vue, il s'agit d'une mare lisse d'eau noire. Un examen plus "
"approfondi révèle qu'il s'agit d'une fine poussière de verre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "tree of glass apples"
msgstr "arbre à pommes de verre"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "tree of glass apples"
msgid ""
"A flourishing tree, its branches heavy with apples.  Every black leaf is "
"razor-edged; every heavy fruit turns to dust at the touch."
msgstr ""
"Un arbre florissant, dont les branches sont chargées de pommes. Chaque "
"feuille noire est tranchante comme un rasoir, chaque fruit lourd se "
"transforme en poussière au toucher."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass tree"
msgstr "arbre en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass tree"
msgid "The glass skeleton of a once-leafy tree.  It looks more like coral, now."
msgstr ""
"Le squelette de verre d'un arbre autrefois feuillu. Il ressemble davantage à "
"du corail, maintenant."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass bush"
msgstr "buisson en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass bush"
msgid ""
"What was once a small shrub has grown wild, each of its branches twisting "
"into delicate glass spirals."
msgstr ""
"Ce qui était autrefois un petit arbuste a poussé de façon sauvage, chacune de "
"ses branches se tordant en délicates spirales de verre."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass stairs"
msgstr "escaliers en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass stairs"
msgid ""
"A set of smooth glass stairs, with countless years of bare footprints worn "
"into them."
msgstr ""
"Un escalier de verre lisse, marqué par d'innombrables années d'empreintes de "
"pieds nus."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass downspout"
msgstr "descente de gouttière en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass downspout"
msgid ""
"A drainpipe of black glass.  There are holes down its length, from which "
"occasionally trickle little dustings of black sand."
msgstr ""
"Une conduite d'évacuation en verre noir. Il y a des trous sur toute sa "
"longueur, d'où s'écoulent parfois de petites quantités de sable noir."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass roof"
msgstr "toit en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass roof"
msgid ""
"A roof of black glass tiles.  They are very smooth, and some break away at "
"the touch."
msgstr ""
"Un toit de tuiles de verre noir. Elles sont très lisses, et certaines se "
"détachent au toucher."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "black glass drain"
msgstr "gouttière en verre noir"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass drain"
msgid "A funnel of smooth glass, filled almost to the brim with sand."
msgstr "Un entonnoir en verre lisse, rempli presque à ras bord de sable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow black pool"
msgid ""
"At first glance, this looks like a rippling pool of black water.  Closer "
"examination reveals it to be fine glass dust, blown in slow waves by the "
"breeze."
msgstr ""
"À première vue, cela ressemble à un bassin d'eau noire ondulant. Un examen "
"plus attentif révèle qu'il s'agit de fines poussières de verre, soufflées par "
"la brise en lentes vagues."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "soft glass soil"
msgstr "terre en verre douce"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_vitrified.json
#: data/json/npcs/EOC_talkers/vitrified_farm.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "soft glass soil"
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This little mound of soil is unlike the jagged dirt around it.  It is smooth, "
"welcoming, and pleasant to the touch."
msgstr ""
"Ce petit monticule de terre est différent de la terre déchiquetée qui "
"l'entoure. Il est lisse, accueillant et agréable au toucher."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "swirling mist"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "swirling mist"
msgid ""
"A swirling, exotic pattern of shapes, floating in an ill-defined darkness.  "
"Staring at it too long hurts your brain."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_any.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "sparkling chasm"
msgid ""
"At a glance this just looks like darkness.  Then, gazing deeper, you think it "
"might be full of stars.  Still deeper, perhaps those stars are eyes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk0"
msgstr "Obélisque0"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk0"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk1"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk2"
#. ~ Description of terrain "Obelisk3"
msgid "Obelisk"
msgstr "Obélisque  "

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Thief's Pass.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a tall, olive green, metallic pillar covered in swirling patterns.  "
"As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  You have "
"learned the Thief's Passcode."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_0_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk0"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a tall, olive green, metallic pillar covered in swirling patterns.  "
"As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation on your skin.  "
"<ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of your own face, smirking; it's the "
"'Thief's Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk1"
msgstr "Obélisque1"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Circle of Wings Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a squat, angry-looking, indigo metallic pillar covered carved in "
"relief with the image of flying birds.  As you focus on it, you feel a "
"burning sensation on your skin.  You have learned the Circle of Wings "
"Passcode."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_1_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk1"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a squat, angry-looking, indigo metallic pillar covered carved in "
"relief with the image of flying birds.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you "
"feel a burning sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of "
"wings in a circle, running into themselves like an ouroboros; it's the "
"'Circle of Wings Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk2"
msgstr "Obélisque2"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Hard Nails Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a thick, powerful, gold-burnished pillar covered in what look like "
"deep fingernail scratches.  As you focus on it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  You have learned the Hard Nails Passcode."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_2_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk2"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a thick, powerful, gold-burnished pillar covered in what look like "
"deep fingernail scratches.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning "
"sensation on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a hand clawing "
"down a sheet of metal; it's the 'Hard Nails Passcode'.  "
"<ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "Obelisk3"
msgstr "Obélisque3"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_have" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid "You already know the Laughing Man Passcode.  The obelisk is inert."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_grant" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in "
"its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  You have learned the Laughing Man Passcode."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LS_Obelisk_3_firsttime" in terrain
#. "Obelisk3"'s examine action
msgid ""
"You see a beautiful pillar the color of roses or blood, absolutely perfect in "
"its proportions.  As your eyes are drawn to it, you feel a burning sensation "
"on your skin.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime1> a tattoo of a handsome man laughing.  "
"At first glance it appears charming and friendly, but the longer you examine "
"it, the more it appears to be inhumanly cold and cruel; it's the 'Laughing "
"Man Passcode'.  <ls_obelisk_firsttime2>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mysterious closed door"
msgstr "porte mystérieuse fermée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid ""
"A dark door of twisted metal, etched with symbols and writing that you can't "
"piece together."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Prying message of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid "With great effort, you pry open the door."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Prying failure of terrain "mysterious closed door"
msgid "You pry, but it seems like your tools will give out before the door does."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "mysterious open door"
msgstr "porte mystérieuse ouverte"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "mysterious open door"
msgid ""
"A dark door of twisted metal, etched with symbols and writing that you can't "
"piece together.  It has been swung open."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metallic wall"
msgstr "mur métallique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metallic wall"
msgid ""
"A durable wall of ordinary looking sheet metal, at first.  Staring closer, "
"the welds and joins seem to form strange fractal patterns."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal wailing!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "scrap metal wall"
msgstr "mur en ferraille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "scrap metal wall"
msgid ""
"A relatively simple wall made of cobbled-together scrap metal.  The wires and "
"bolts holding it together seem to be in just slightly different "
"configurations whenever you look back at it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "metal crying!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "metallic floor"
msgstr "sol métallique"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "metallic floor"
msgid ""
"Diamond-treaded metallic flooring.  Something seems off about the diamond "
"tread; you keep imagining that the bumps spell out words, but when you look "
"closer they're in very ordinary patterns."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "broken metal floor"
msgid ""
"Something has cratered this metal flooring.  It will be difficult to move "
"things across.  Through the cracks and dents emanates a faint eery glow."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "scrap metal floor"
msgstr "sol en ferraille"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "scrap metal floor"
msgid ""
"A floor assembled from various scraps of metal.  Though their placement seems "
"random, you keep seeing spots where they form faces."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "catwalk"
msgstr "passerelle"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "catwalk"
msgid "This catwalk extends over a deep chasm of swirling shadow."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "swirling metal roof"
msgstr "toit en métal tourbillonnant"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/netherum/terrain_labyrinth_cybernetic.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "swirling metal roof"
msgid ""
"A section of sturdy metal roofing that seems to swirl and twist with an "
"unfamiliar, ever-shifting pattern."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "brown laminate floor"
msgstr "sol laminé brun"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "brown laminate floor"
msgid ""
"A section of flooring made out of a tough, smooth material, colored in an "
"atrocious mottled brown."
msgstr ""
"Une section de sol faite d'un matériau résistant et lisse, de couleur marron "
"marbré atroce."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer roof"
msgstr "toit de remorque à balles"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer roof"
msgid "A smooth roof of gleaming chrome, slightly dusty from the road."
msgstr ""
"Un toit lisse aux chromes étincelants, légèrement poussiéreux à cause de la "
"route."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer exterior wall"
msgstr "mur extérieur de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer exterior wall"
msgid "A smooth wall of gleaming chrome, slightly dusty from the road."
msgstr "Un mur lisse de chrome brillant, légèrement poussiéreux à cause de la route."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "bullet trailer interior wall"
msgstr "mur intérieur de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "bullet trailer interior wall"
msgid "A simple wall paneled in a coarsely textured gray laminate of some sort."
msgstr "Un simple panneau mural en stratifié gris texturé grossièrement."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "f_bullettrailer_table_top"
msgid "A small trailer table, designed to convert into a bed when not in use."
msgstr ""
"Une petite table de caravane, conçue pour se transformer en lit lorsqu'elle "
"n'est pas utilisée."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer cabinets"
msgstr "cabinets de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer cabinets"
msgid ""
"Cramped trailer cabinets, with some inbuilt appliances taking up even more of "
"the limited space."
msgstr ""
"Armoires de caravane exiguës, certaines avec des appareils intégrés prenant "
"encore plus de place dans l'espace limité."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer sink"
msgstr "évier de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer sink"
msgid "A tiny metal sink and connected cabinet."
msgstr "Un minuscule évier en métal et un meuble connecté."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "mini desk"
msgstr "mini bureau"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "mini desk"
msgid "A small wooden desk with a little attached bookshelf."
msgstr "Un petit bureau en bois avec une petite bibliothèque attenante."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "trailer bathroom door"
msgstr "porte de salle de bain de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "trailer bathroom door"
msgid ""
"A gray textured door, rimmed in chrome, like a very tacky version of a ship's "
"hatch."
msgstr ""
"Une porte grise texturée, cerclée de chrome, comme une version très vulgaire "
"de l'écoutille d'un navire."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#: data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#. ~ Furniture name
#. ~ Item name
msgid "travel toilet"
msgid_plural "travel toilets"
msgstr[0] "toilette de voyage"
msgstr[1] "toilettes de voyage"
msgstr[2] "toilettes de voyage"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "travel toilet"
msgid ""
"A tiny plastic toilet for use in a travel trailer.  Unlike a normal toilet, "
"it doesn't store water locally for you to siphon out."
msgstr ""
"Des toilettes minuscules en plastique à utiliser dans une caravane. "
"Contrairement aux toilettes normales, elles ne stockent pas l'eau localement "
"pour que vous puissiez la siphonner."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Bashing sound
msgid "plastic cracking!"
msgstr "crac de plastique!"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer sofa"
msgstr "canapé de mobil-home"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer sofa"
msgid ""
"A folding trailer sofa with a durable, somewhat comfortable weave of coarse "
"red fabric."
msgstr ""
"Un canapé pliant pour remorque avec un tissu rouge grossier durable et assez "
"confortable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "trailer bed"
msgstr "lit de remorque"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "trailer bed"
msgid "A small but comfy-looking double bed."
msgstr "Un lit double, petit mais confortable."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "plywood sign for 'Dana's Bakery'"
msgstr "Panneau en contreplaqué pour \"Dana's Bakery\" (boulangerie de Dana)"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/bullet_trailer.json
#. ~ Description of furniture "plywood sign for 'Dana's Bakery'"
msgid "A spraypainted plywood sign reads 'Dana's Bakery' in red letters."
msgstr ""
"Une enseigne en contreplaqué peinte à la bombe indique \"Dana's Bakery\" en "
"lettres rouges."

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged aisle"
msgstr "allée noyée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged aisle"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged aisle.  It has started to degrade after some time spent "
"underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged board"
msgstr "panneau oxydé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged board"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged metal wall.  Keeps zombies outside the vehicle and prevents "
"people from seeing through it.  It has started to degrade after some time "
"spent underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged quarterpanel"
msgstr "aile oxydée"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged quarterpanel"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged half-height metal wall.  Keeps zombies outside the vehicle but "
"allows people to see over it.  It has started to degrade after some time "
"spent underwater.  Absolutely unrecoverable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged windshield"
msgstr "pare-brise noyé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged windshield"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged sheet of glass that lets you see outside the vehicle.  It has "
"started to degrade after some time spent underwater.  Absolutely "
"unrecoverable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "waterlogged frame"
msgstr "châssis oxydé"

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Description of terrain "waterlogged frame"
msgid ""
"A waterlogged metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on "
"it, and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  "
"It has started to degrade after some time spent underwater.  Absolutely "
"unrecoverable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/special_use/sunken_helicopter_furniture.json
#. ~ Furniture name
msgid "waterlogged bucket seat"
msgstr "siège baquet noyé"

