"A jumble of broken metal pieces that were removed during reconstructive "
"surgery."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de morceaux de ferraille ayant été retirés durant une opération de "
"reconstruction faciale."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Acidic Discharge CBM"
msgid_plural "Acidic Discharge CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Décharge Acide"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Décharge Acide"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Décharge Acide"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Acidic Discharge CBM"
msgid "A CBM that has been breached in several places.  Some acid is leaking from it."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC ayant été percé en plusieurs endroits et déversant une sorte d'acide "
"depuis ces trous."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Electrical Discharge CBM"
msgid_plural "Electrical Discharge CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Décharge Électrique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Décharge Électrique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Décharge Électrique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Electrical Discharge CBM"
msgid ""
"A formerly-functional CBM that is now a mess of naked wires and burnt "
"resistors."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC auparavant fonctionnel et maintenant rien qu'un amas de fils "
"électriques dénudés et de résistances carbonisées."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Electrical Drain CBM"
msgid_plural "Electrical Drain CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Siphon Électrique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Siphon Électrique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Siphon Électrique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Electrical Drain CBM"
msgid ""
"This CBM was wired incorrectly and would drain power from any system "
"connected to it."
msgstr ""
"Cet MBC a été mal câblé et ne ferait rien que de drainer tout système "
"électrique auquel il pourrait être attaché."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Itchy Metal Thing CBM"
msgid_plural "Itchy Metal Thing CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Bidule Métallique Démangeur"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Bidule Métallique Démangeur"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Bidule Métallique Démangeur"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Itchy Metal Thing CBM"
msgid ""
"You can't recognize what this is supposed to be, but you imagine it'd be a "
"very awkward thing to have in one's body."
msgstr ""
"Vous n'avez aucune idée ce que ceci est supposé être, mais vous pouvez "
"imaginer que ce n'est probablement pas quelque chose de désirable à avoir "
"encré en vous."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Glowy Thing CBM"
msgid_plural "Glowy Thing CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBCs - Bidouille Lumineux"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Bidouille Lumineux"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Bidouille Lumineux"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Glowy Thing CBM"
msgid "It's a… thing?  And it glows, at least it did when it was installed."
msgstr ""
"C'est… quelque chose?  Quelque chose qui brille?  Du moins quand c'est "
"attaché à un système électrique."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Leaky Bionic CBM"
msgid_plural "Leaky Bionic CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Implant Fuyant"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Implant Fuyant"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Implant Fuyant"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Leaky Bionic CBM"
msgid ""
"A mess of pierced pipes and broken seals, something unpleasant is leaking "
"from it."
msgstr ""
"Un chaos de tuyaux percés et de sceaux brisés, vous pouvez observer un "
"liquide douteux goutter de cet implant."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Noisemaker CBM"
msgid_plural "Noisemaker CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Émetteur de Bruit"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Émetteur de Bruit"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Émetteur de Bruit"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Noisemaker CBM"
msgid ""
"A malfunctioning bionic.  When installed, it occasionally emits a loud burst "
"of noise."
msgstr ""
"Un implant dysfonctionnel émettant occasionnellement un bruit tonitruant "
"lorsqu'il est installé."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Bionic Nostril CBM"
msgid_plural "Bionic Nostril CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Narines Bioniques"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Narines Bioniques"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Narines Bioniques"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Bionic Nostril CBM"
msgid "This thing was up someone's nose, they're probably glad to be rid of it."
msgstr ""
"Ceci était coincé dans le nez de quelqu'un probablement reconnaissant d'en "
"être débarrassé."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Bionic Visual Impairment CBM"
msgid_plural "Bionic Visual Impairment CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Handicap Visuel Bionique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Handicap Visuel Bionique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Handicap Visuel Bionique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Bionic Visual Impairment CBM"
msgid "A defective bionic that impairs vision."
msgstr ""
"Un implant défectueux ayant un effet négative sur la vision de son "
"utilisateur."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Power Overload CBM"
msgid_plural "Power Overload CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Surcharge Électrique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Surcharge Électrique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Surcharge Électrique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Power Overload CBM"
msgid "A bunch of defective power circuits that are prone to short-circuiting."
msgstr ""
"Un amas de circuits électriques défectueux ayant une tendance à "
"court-circuiter."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Bionic Short Circuit CBM"
msgid_plural "Bionic Short Circuit CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Court-Circuit Bionique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Court-Circuit Bionique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Court-Circuit Bionique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Bionic Short Circuit CBM"
msgid "This bionic is poorly wired and occasionally short-circuits."
msgstr "Cet implant est mal câblé et court-circuite occasionnellement."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Endocrine Enervator CBM"
msgid_plural "Endocrine Enervator CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Perturbateur Endocrinien"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Perturbateur Endocrinien"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Perturbateur Endocrinien"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Endocrine Enervator CBM"
msgid ""
"A malfunctioning bionic that causes sleepiness by altering the unfortunate "
"user's brain chemistry."
msgstr ""
"Un implant bionique défectueux qui provoque de la somnolence en altérant la "
"chimie du cerveau de l'utilisateur malchanceux."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Synaptic Regeneration System CBM"
msgid_plural "Synaptic Regeneration System CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Système de Regeneration Synaptique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Système de Regeneration Synaptique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Système de Regeneration Synaptique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Synaptic Regeneration System CBM"
msgid ""
"An electromagnetic stimulator surgically implanted on the back of the head "
"and along the spine, continually draining power.  As long as it's active, the "
"user will not suffer from sleep deprivation, although they may still feel "
"sleepy; if activated by a user that is already sleep-deprived, it will "
"gradually reduce the symptoms of lacking sleep."
msgstr ""
"Un stimulateur électromagnétique implanté chirurgicalement à l'arrière de la "
"tête et le long de la colonne vertébrale, drainant continuellement de "
"l'énergie. Tant qu'il est actif, son utilisateur ne souffrira pas de "
"privation de sommeil, bien qu'une somnolence légère soit possible; et en cas "
"de privation de sommeil déjà existante, l'implant réduira progressivement les "
"symptômes de manque de sommeil."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Motor Control Overstimulator CBM"
msgid_plural "Motor Control Overstimulator CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Hyperstimulateur de Contrôle Moteur"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Hyperstimulateur de Contrôle Moteur"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Hyperstimulateur de Contrôle Moteur"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Motor Control Overstimulator CBM"
msgid ""
"The result of poor configuration, this bionic module frequently causes "
"debilitating muscle spasms."
msgstr ""
"Résultat d'une mauvaise configuration, ce module bionique provoque "
"fréquemment des spasmes musculaires débilitants."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Wire-Induced Stiffness CBM"
msgid_plural "Wire-Induced Stiffness CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Rigidité Induite par Câbles"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Rigidité Induite par Câbles"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Rigidité Induite par Câbles"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Wire-Induced Stiffness CBM"
msgid "A length of poorly installed wiring that would cause stiffness."
msgstr "Une longueur de câblage mal installée qui provoquerait une rigidité."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Self-Locking Thumbs CBM"
msgid_plural "Self-Locking Thumbs CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Pouces Verrouillés"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Pouces Verrouillés"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Pouces Verrouillés"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Self-Locking Thumbs CBM"
msgid "A pair of faulty, self-locking thumb bionics."
msgstr ""
"Une paire d'implants de pouce défectueux capable de bloquer les pouces de "
"l'utilisateur de temps à autre."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Visual Disruptor CBM"
msgid_plural "Visual Disruptor CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Perturbateur Visuel"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Perturbateur Visuel"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Perturbateur Visuel"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Visual Disruptor CBM"
msgid ""
"A pair of defective ocular bionics that cause visual distortion and "
"pixelation."
msgstr ""
"Une paire d'implants oculaires défectueux causant des distortions visuelles "
"et de la pixellisation."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Voice Remodulator CBM"
msgid_plural "Voice Remodulator CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Remodulateur de Voix"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Remodulateur de Voix"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Remodulateur de Voix"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Voice Remodulator CBM"
msgid ""
"Part of the Autodoc's 'Cyborg Identity Package', this bionic gives the user a "
"creepy robot voice."
msgstr ""
"Composante du \" Pack d'Identité Cyborg\" d'Autodoc, cet implant bionique "
"donne à l'utilisateur une voix de robot effrayante."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Electromagnetic Leak CBM"
msgid_plural "Electromagnetic Leak CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Fuite Électromagnétique"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Fuite Électromagnétique"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Fuite Électromagnétique"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Electromagnetic Leak CBM"
msgid ""
"A broken implant that sends electromagnetic impulses that reduce other "
"implants' capacity to store charge."
msgstr ""
"Un implant cassé envoyant des impulsions électromagnétiques réduisant la "
"capacité des autres implants à stocker de l'énergie."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Oil Generator CBM"
msgid_plural "Oil Generator CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Générateur à Kérosène"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Générateur à Kérosène"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Générateur à Kérosène"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Oil Generator CBM"
msgid ""
"A CBM that generates power out of kerosene or motor oil.  It is fairly "
"efficient and can store up to 750 mL of fuel, but works somewhat slowly."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC qui génère de l'énergie à partir de kérosène ou d'huile de moteur. "
"Elle est assez efficace et peut stocker jusqu'à 750 ml de carburant, mais "
"fonctionne assez lentement."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Taste Fouler CBM"
msgid_plural "Taste Fouler CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Altération du Goût"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Altération du Goût"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Altération du Goût"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Taste Fouler CBM"
msgid ""
"A broken and mis-wired module that would cause food and drink to taste "
"terrible if installed."
msgstr ""
"Un implant cassé au câblage défectueux qui rendrait le goût des boissons et "
"de la nourriture infect si il était installé."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Radioactive Leak CBM"
msgid_plural "Radioactive Leak CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Fuite Radioactive"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Fuite Radioactive"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Fuite Radioactive"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Radioactive Leak CBM"
msgid ""
"A broken CBM that has been leaking radiation into its user.  The danger seems "
"to have been sealed off during the removal process, but you definitely "
"shouldn't put it back."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC défectueux qui a émis des rayonnements à l'intérieur de son "
"utilisateur. Le danger semble avoir été contenu lors du retrait, mais il ne "
"faut absolument pas le remettre en place."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Recoil Compensators CBM"
msgid_plural "Recoil Compensators CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Compensateurs de Recul"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Compensateurs de Recul"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Compensateurs de Recul"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Recoil Compensators CBM"
msgid ""
"A CBM that contains shock absorbers and kinetic braces which greatly reduce "
"the recoil of guns."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC qui contient des absorbeurs de chocs et des supports cinétiques qui "
"réduisent considérablement le recul des armes à feu."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Sleep Mode Shutdown CBM"
msgid_plural "Sleep Mode Shutdown CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Mise en Veille"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Mise en Veille"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Mise en Veille"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Sleep Mode Shutdown CBM"
msgid ""
"A CBM that completely shuts down all communication between the user's brain "
"and the rest of their body when they fall asleep, preventing them from waking "
"up under any circumstance until their natural sleep cycle completes.  An "
"inability to trigger its effects manually makes it useless as an anesthesia "
"substitute."
msgstr ""
"Un MBC qui coupe complètement la communication entre le cerveau de "
"l'utilisateur et le reste de son corps lorsqu'il s'endort, l'empêchant de se "
"réveiller en toute circonstance jusqu'à ce que son cycle de sommeil naturel "
"soit terminé. L'impossibilité de déclencher ses effets manuellement le rend "
"inutile en tant que substitut d'anesthésie."

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bionics_mainline_override.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/bionics_mainline_override.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/bionics_mainline_override.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Throwing Assist CBM"
msgid_plural "Throwing Assist CBMs"
msgstr[0] "MBC - Aide au Lancer"
msgstr[1] "MBCs - Aide au Lancer"
msgstr[2] "MBCs - Aide au Lancer"

#: data/json/items/bionics.json
#. ~ Description of "Throwing Assist CBM"
msgid ""
"The culmination of decades of research into hominid palaeoanthropology and "
"biomechanical modeling, the throwing assist CBM was brought to market to "
"revolutionize Beqball tournaments, soon becoming exhibitions of cybernetic "
"human effort and engineering.  A network of neurostimulators and sensors, "
"mostly in the arms and hands, work in tandem with the eyes for a significant "
"increase in throwing accuracy and precision.  When the Exodii came upon this "
"cybernetic enhancement suite, they found it to be an economical way to ensure "
"precise grenade placement in partial cyborgs."
msgstr ""
"Aboutissement de décennies de recherche en paléoanthropologie des hominidés "
"et en modélisation biomécanique, le MBC a été mis sur le marché pour "
"révolutionner les tournois de Beqball, devenant rapidement une exposition de "
"l'effort et de l'ingénierie cybernétiques de l'homme. Un réseau de "
"neurostimulateurs et de capteurs, principalement dans les bras et les mains, "
"travaille en tandem avec les yeux pour augmenter de manière significative la "
"précision du lancer. Lorsque les Exodii ont découvert cette suite "
"d'améliorations cybernétiques, ils ont estimé qu'il s'agissait d'un moyen "
"économique d'assurer un placement précis des grenades sur les cyborgs "
"partiels."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bird litter"
msgid_plural "bird litter"
msgstr[0] "fiente d'oiseau"
msgstr[1] "fientes d'oiseau"
msgstr[2] "fientes d'oiseau"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "bird litter"
msgid "Bird droppings, feathers, and soiled bits of rubbish."
msgstr ""
"Des déjections d'oiseaux mélangées avec des plumes et une variété d'autres "
"débris."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cow pie"
msgid_plural "cow pies"
msgstr[0] "bouse de vache"
msgstr[1] "bouses de vache"
msgstr[2] "bouses de vache"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "cow pie"
msgid "A fresh cow pie; this could probably be used to make some great fertilizer."
msgstr ""
"Une bouse de vache fraiche, vous pourriez probablement l'utiliser pour faire "
"du bon engrais."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dog dung"
msgid_plural "dog dungs"
msgstr[0] "merde de chien"
msgstr[1] "merdes de chien"
msgstr[2] "merdes de chien"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "dog dung"
msgid "Droppings from a canine."
msgstr "Excréments d'un chien."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "manure"
msgid_plural "manure"
msgstr[0] "fumier"
msgstr[1] "fumier"
msgstr[2] "fumier"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "manure"
msgid "Common manure, could probably be used to make some great fertilizer."
msgstr "fumier commun, pourrait certainement être utilisée pour faire un bon engrais. "

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "roach dirt"
msgid_plural "roach dirt"
msgstr[0] "excrément de cafard"
msgstr[1] "excréments de cafard"
msgstr[2] "excréments de cafard"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "roach dirt"
msgid "Large black pellets of rotting material."
msgstr "Grosses boulettes noires de matières en décomposition."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fetid goop"
msgid_plural "fetid goops"
msgstr[0] "bouillie fétide"
msgstr[1] "bouillies fétides"
msgstr[2] "bouillies fétides"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "fetid goop"
msgid ""
"A foul-smelling goop.  It has a disgusting texture and a powerful smell that "
"overwhelms every other smell around it."
msgstr ""
"Une bouillie nauséabonde. Sa texture est dégoûtante et son odeur puissante "
"écrase toutes les autres odeurs qui l'entourent."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chitin dust"
msgid_plural "chitin dust"
msgstr[0] "poussière de chitine"
msgstr[1] "poussière de chitine"
msgstr[2] "poussière de chitine"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "chitin dust"
msgid ""
"The dust left over by winged insects such as butterflies or moths.  It's "
"mostly chitin but may also contain dirt and other gross materials."
msgstr ""
"Poussière laissée par les insectes ailés tels que les papillons ou les mites. "
"Elle se compose principalement de chitine, mais peut également contenir de la "
"saleté et d'autres matières grossières."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "shed snakeskin"
msgid_plural "shed snakeskins"
msgstr[0] "mue de serpent"
msgstr[1] "mues de serpent"
msgstr[2] "mues de serpent"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "shed snakeskin"
msgid ""
"A small length of shed snakeskin.  It's thin and translucent but still bears "
"the distinct pattern of scales."
msgstr ""
"Un petit morceau de peau de serpent muée. Il est mince et translucide mais "
"porte toujours le motif distinct des écailles."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "shed snakeskin"
msgid ""
"The molted dermis of an adult snake.  This one is in one piece.  You can even "
"see the individual eyes."
msgstr ""
"La mue d'un serpent adulte. Elle est d'un seul tenant et on peut même "
"distinguer les yeux individuels."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "big shed snakeskin"
msgid_plural "big shed snakeskins"
msgstr[0] "large mue de serpent"
msgstr[1] "larges mues de serpent"
msgstr[2] "larges mues de serpent"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "big shed snakeskin"
msgid ""
"A very large shed snakeskin.  This didn't come from anything native, or "
"natural, to New England."
msgstr ""
"Une très grande mue de serpent. Celle-ci ne provient pas d'une espèce native "
"ou naturelle de la Nouvelle-Angleterre."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "gigantic shed snakeskin"
msgid_plural "gigantic shed snakeskins"
msgstr[0] "mue de serpent gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "mues de serpent gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "mues de serpent gigantesques"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "gigantic shed snakeskin"
msgid ""
"A complete shed snakeskin of tremendous size.  Whatever left it must be "
"getting even bigger.  You should not be, or return to, wherever you found "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Une mue de serpent complète et gigantesque. Ce qui l'a laissée doit être en "
"train de devenir encore plus grand. Vous ne devriez pas vous trouver, ni "
"retourner, là où vous avez trouvé cela."

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "gigantic snake scales"
msgid_plural "gigantic snake scales"
msgstr[0] "écaille de serpent gigantesque"
msgstr[1] "écailles de serpent gigantesques"
msgstr[2] "écailles de serpent gigantesques"

#: data/json/items/biosignatures.json
#. ~ Description of "gigantic snake scales"
msgid ""
"A handful of greatly oversized scales from a snake.  This is a troubling find "
"for a few reasons.  There's the size, obviously, but also the unusual "
"hardness in spite of the obvious decay, and the fact that snakes don't shed "
"individual scales like this."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'écailles de serpent anormalement grandes. Cette découverte est "
"troublante pour plusieurs raisons : la taille, bien sûr, mais aussi la dureté "
"inhabituelle malgré une décomposition évidente, et le fait que les serpents "
"ne muent pas leurs écailles individuellement."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "anesthetic"
msgid ""
"A variety of powerful hypnotic, analgesic, and stimulative drugs.  It's "
"intended for use in specialized medical equipment, and can't be administered "
"manually.  You can reload an anesthesia kit with it."
msgstr ""
"Une variété de puissantes drogues hypnotiques, analgésiques et stimulantes. "
"Elle est conditionnée pour être utilisée avec un équipement médical "
"spécialisé, et ne peut être administrée manuellement. Vous pouvez recharger "
"un kit d’anesthésiant avec cela."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fertility supplement"
msgid_plural "fertility supplement"
msgstr[0] "supplément de fertilité"
msgstr[1] "suppléments de fertilité"
msgstr[2] "suppléments de fertilité"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "fertility supplement"
msgid "A pill for those looking to have children.  It is of no use to you."
msgstr ""
"Une pilule pour celles qui veulent avoir des enfants. Elle ne vous est "
"d'aucune utilité."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sulfur"
msgid_plural "sulfur"
msgstr[0] "soufre"
msgstr[1] "soufre"
msgstr[2] "soufre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sulfur"
msgid ""
"A handful of pure sulfur.  Primarily used to make battery acid, sulfur is "
"sometimes used as fuel for explosives.  Can be burned to produce acidic smoke "
"that is deadly to bacteria and humans alike, or oxidized to make "
"paper-bleaching agents.  It also serves as a basis for many kinds of "
"fungicide."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de soufre pur. Principalement utilisé pour fabriquer de l'acide "
"de batterie, le soufre est également utilisé en tant que carburant pour "
"explosifs ou ingrédient pour une solution fongicide. Il est aussi possible de "
"le brûler pour relâcher des vapeurs toxiques fatales pour tout animal, plante "
"et bactérie y étant exposé(e)."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chunk of sulfur"
msgid_plural "chunks of sulfur"
msgstr[0] "morceau de soufre"
msgstr[1] "morceaux de soufre"
msgstr[2] "morceaux de soufre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "chunk of sulfur"
msgid "A chunk of pure sulfur.  Break it up to use it."
msgstr "Un morceau de souffre pur. Brisez le pour pouvoir l'utiliser."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cement powder"
msgid_plural "cement powder"
msgstr[0] "poudre de ciment"
msgstr[1] "poudre de ciment"
msgstr[2] "poudre de ciment"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "cement powder"
msgid ""
"Portland is most likely long gone, but its memory persists in cement.  This "
"ubiquitous binder can be used for all kinds of advanced masonry.  Just add "
"water."
msgstr "Un liant très utile pour la maçonnerie. Il faut juste y ajouter de l'eau."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "gravel"
msgid "A handful of gravel, smaller than pebbles but larger than sand."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de graviers, plus petits que des cailloux mais plus gros que du "
"sable."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "shredded rubber"
msgid_plural "shredded rubber"
msgstr[0] "caoutchouc déchiqueté"
msgstr[1] "caoutchouc déchiqueté"
msgstr[2] "caoutchouc déchiqueté"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "shredded rubber"
msgid "A handful of shredded rubber, usable as a mulch now."
msgstr "Une poignée de caoutchouc déchiqueté, utilisable comme paillis maintenant."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "limestone"
msgid_plural "limestone"
msgstr[0] "calcaire"
msgstr[1] "calcaire"
msgstr[2] "calcaire"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "limestone"
msgid ""
"A handful of small chunks of limestone.  Useful for experiments at science "
"fairs, but pretty useless as ammo.  Maybe something could be crafted from "
"this stuff…"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de morceaux de calcaire.  Utile pour des expériences "
"scientifiques, mais pas pour en faire des munitions.  Vous pourriez peut-être "
"en faire quelque chose…"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "quicklime"
msgid_plural "quicklime"
msgstr[0] "chaux vive"
msgstr[1] "chaux vive"
msgstr[2] "chaux vive"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "quicklime"
msgid ""
"The product of burning limestone, this white powder is a crucial ingredient "
"in making cement.  That said, it is also extremely caustic and will cause "
"severe burns to any tissue it comes in contact with.  This property could "
"probably be exploited."
msgstr ""
"Le résultat de la combustion du calcaire, cette poudre blanche est un "
"ingrédient indispensable pour le ciment.  La chaux vive est aussi extrêmement "
"corrosive et brûle les tissus qui entrent en contact avec.  Cette propriété "
"pourrait être exploitée…"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "slaked lime"
msgid_plural "slaked lime"
msgstr[0] "hydroxyde de calcium"
msgstr[1] "hydroxyde de calcium"
msgstr[2] "hydroxyde de calcium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "slaked lime"
msgid ""
" A handful of slaked lime, a white odorless powder with many uses.  Also "
"known as calcium hydroxide."
msgstr ""
" Une poignée de chaux éteinte, une poudre blanche inodore aux multiples "
"usages. Également connue sous le nom d'hydroxyde de calcium."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sand"
msgid ""
"A handful of New England sand.  If you had a stoked furnace, you could turn "
"it into glass.  Otherwise, it's only good for making cement."
msgstr ""
"Du sable. Avec un four alimenté vous pourriez en faire du verre. Sinon ce "
"n'est bon qu'a en faire du ciment."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soil"
msgid_plural "soil"
msgstr[0] "terre"
msgstr[1] "terre"
msgstr[2] "terre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "soil"
msgid ""
"A pile of loosely-packed, slightly damp loamy soil.  This mixture of sand, "
"silt and clay is ideal for growing plants."
msgstr ""
"Un tas de terreaux argileux légèrement humide. Ce mélange de sable, de limon "
"et d'argile est idéal pour la croissance des plantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "limestone shard"
msgid_plural "limestone shards"
msgstr[0] "éclat de calcaire"
msgstr[1] "éclats de calcaire"
msgstr[2] "éclats de calcaire"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "limestone shard"
msgid ""
"A small shard of limestone.  Pretty flimsy and not much of a weapon, but its "
"alkaline properties may yet find some use."
msgstr ""
"Un petit éclat de calcaire. Fragile et peu fiable en tant qu'arme, mes ses "
"propriétés alcalines pourraient être utiles."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rock salt"
msgid_plural "rock salt"
msgstr[0] "sel de roche"
msgstr[1] "sel de roche"
msgstr[2] "sel de roche"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "rock salt"
msgid "A handful of rock salt crystals.  Could be refined into table salt."
msgstr "Une poignée de sels gemme. Il pourrait être transformé en sel de table."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rhodonite"
msgid_plural "rhodonite"
msgstr[0] "rhodonite"
msgstr[1] "rhodonite"
msgstr[2] "rhodonite"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "rhodonite"
msgid ""
"A chunk of rhodonite.  It has manganese dioxide covering and going through it "
"in veins, which can be obtained using a chisel."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de rhodonite. Elle est recouverte de dioxyde de manganèse et "
"traversée par des veines que l'on peut obtenir à l'aide d'un ciseau."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "zincite"
msgid_plural "zincite"
msgstr[0] "zincite"
msgstr[1] "zincite"
msgstr[2] "zincite"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "zincite"
msgid ""
"A chunk of zincite.  Could be refined into zinc oxide, then into zinc by "
"reduction with a source of carbon."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de zincite. Il peut être raffiné en oxyde de zinc, puis en zinc "
"par réduction à l'aide d'une source de carbone."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bleach"
msgid_plural "bleach"
msgstr[0] "eau de Javel"
msgstr[1] "eau de Javel"
msgstr[2] "eau de Javel"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "bleach"
msgid "Sodium hypochlorite, a common household cleaning agent."
msgstr "De l'hypochlorite de sodium, un agent de nettoyage domestique commun."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Conditional name for "bleach" when FLAG matches DIRTY
msgid "bleach spill"
msgid_plural "bleach spills"
msgstr[0] "éclaboussure de javel"
msgstr[1] "éclaboussures de javel"
msgstr[2] "éclaboussures de javel"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "liquid ammonia"
msgid_plural "liquid ammonia"
msgstr[0] "ammoniaque liquide"
msgstr[1] "ammoniaque liquide"
msgstr[2] "ammoniaque liquide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "liquid ammonia"
msgid ""
"Anhydrous ammonia, a useful chemical compound.  It must be stored under "
"pressure or refrigerated.  Don't even think about drinking it."
msgstr ""
"De l'ammoniaque anhydre, un produit chimique utile. Doit être stocké sous "
"pression ou réfrigéré. Ne pensez même-pas à essayer de boire ceci."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ammonia solution"
msgid_plural "ammonia solution"
msgstr[0] "solution ammoniacale"
msgstr[1] "solution ammoniacale"
msgstr[2] "solution ammoniacale"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ammonia solution"
msgid "Ammonium hydroxide, a common household cleaning agent."
msgstr "De l'hydroxyde d'ammonium, souvent utilisé comme produit de nettoyage."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "liquid fertilizer"
msgid_plural "liquid fertilizer"
msgstr[0] "engrais liquide"
msgstr[1] "engrais liquide"
msgstr[2] "engrais liquide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "liquid fertilizer"
msgid "A nutrient-rich elixir for plants."
msgstr "Un liquide riche en nutriments conçu pour nourrir des plantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fermentable liquid mixture"
msgid_plural "fermentable liquid mixture"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "fermentable liquid mixture"
msgid ""
"A mixture of various organic wastes and water.  Wait about two months for "
"them to be fermented in a tank.  Also, biogas production will start after one "
"month."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange de divers déchets organiques et d'eau. Attendez environ deux mois "
"pour qu'ils fermentent dans un réservoir. De plus, la production de biogaz "
"commencera après un mois."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fermentable fish mixture"
msgid_plural "fermentable fish mixture"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "fermentable fish mixture"
msgid ""
"A mixture of fish, sugars, and water.  Wait about two months for them to be "
"fermented in an open tank."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange de poisson, de sucre et d'eau. Laissez fermenter environ deux mois "
"dans un réservoir ouvert."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "fermentable fish mixture"
msgid ""
"The overpowering smell of the fermenting fish liquid makes it clear that it "
"is not ready for use."
msgstr ""
"L'odeur puissante du liquide de poisson en fermentation indique clairement "
"qu'il n'est pas encore prêt à être utilisé."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fermented fertilizer liquid"
msgid_plural "fermented fertilizer liquid"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "fermented fertilizer liquid"
msgid ""
"A mixture of fermented biomass, will become liquid fertilizer after simple "
"treatment."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange de biomasse fermentée, qui deviendra un engrais liquide après un "
"simple traitement."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "commercial fertilizer"
msgid_plural "commercial fertilizer"
msgstr[0] "engrais commercial"
msgstr[1] "engrais commercial"
msgstr[2] "engrais commercial"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "commercial fertilizer"
msgid "Nutrient-rich granules for plants."
msgstr "Des granules riches en nutriments conçues pour nourrir des plantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "fungicide"
msgid_plural "fungicide"
msgstr[0] "fongicide"
msgstr[1] "fongicide"
msgstr[2] "fongicide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "fungicide"
msgid ""
"Agricultural-grade chemical anti-fungal powder designed to destroy infections "
"in plants."
msgstr ""
"Un agent chimique anti-fongique conçu éradiquer les infections fongiques "
"végétales."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "insecticide"
msgid_plural "insecticide"
msgstr[0] "insecticide"
msgstr[1] "insecticide"
msgstr[2] "insecticide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "insecticide"
msgid ""
"Agricultural-grade chemical insecticide powder designed to eradicate insect "
"pests."
msgstr "Un agent chimique insecticide conçu pour éradiquer les insectes nuisibles."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "salt water"
msgid_plural "salt water"
msgstr[0] "eau salée"
msgstr[1] "eau salée"
msgstr[2] "eau salée"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "salt water"
msgid "Water with salt added.  Not good for drinking."
msgstr "De l'eau avec du sel. Mauvais à boire."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soapy water"
msgid_plural "soapy water"
msgstr[0] "eau savonneuse"
msgstr[1] "eau savonneuse"
msgstr[2] "eau savonneuse"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "soapy water"
msgid "Water with soap added.  Not good for drinking."
msgstr "De l'eau avec du savon. Mauvais à boire."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sewage sample"
msgid_plural "sewage sample"
msgstr[0] "échantillon d'eau usée"
msgstr[1] "échantillons d'eau usée"
msgstr[2] "échantillons d'eau usée"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sewage sample"
msgid "A sample of sewage from a treatment plant.  Gross."
msgstr "Un échantillon d'eau usée obtenue dans une station d'épuration. Répugnant."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum powder"
msgid_plural "aluminum powder"
msgstr[0] "poudre d'aluminium"
msgstr[1] "poudre d'aluminium"
msgstr[2] "poudre d'aluminium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "aluminum powder"
msgid ""
"A handful of finely-ground aluminum powder.  This strong reducing agent was "
"used in combination with various oxidants for chemical welding and explosives "
"alike.  Just before the Cataclysm, however, it was the basis of virtually all "
"commercial metallic-hued paints and anti-corrosive coatings."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre fine d'aluminium. Ce fort agent réducteur était utilisé "
"avec divers oxydants pour la soudure chimique et les explosifs. Juste avant "
"le cataclysme, il servait dans les peintures métalliques et les revêtements "
"anti-corrosion."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nickel powder"
msgid_plural "nickel powder"
msgstr[0] "poudre de nickel"
msgstr[1] "poudre de nickel"
msgstr[2] "poudre de nickel"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "nickel powder"
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-white metallic powder composed of nickel.  Common "
"industrial uses include production of stainless steel as well as other alloys."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre métallique blanc argenté composé de nickel. Communément "
"utilisé en industrie pour fabriquer de l'acier inoxydable ainsi que d'autres "
"alliages."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "zinc powder"
msgid_plural "zinc powder"
msgstr[0] "poudre de zinc"
msgstr[1] "poudre de zinc"
msgstr[2] "poudre de zinc"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "zinc powder"
msgid ""
"A handful of zinc powder.  While commercially used mostly in cosmetics and "
"for paints, hobbyists used to mix it with sulfur to make basic rocket fuel or "
"a smokescreen.  When treated with a strong acid, it will produce hydrogen."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre de zinc. Commercialement utilisée pour la cosmétique et "
"les peintures, les amateurs l'utilisait avec du soufre pour en faire du "
"combustible à roquette ou des écrans de fumée. Si on le traite avec un acide "
"fort, il produit de l'hydrogène."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "zinc oxide"
msgid_plural "zinc oxide"
msgstr[0] "oxyde de zinc"
msgstr[1] "oxydes de zinc"
msgstr[2] "oxydes de zinc"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "zinc oxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of zinc oxide.  It can be reduced into zinc, or used for some other "
"reactions of its own."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'oxyde de zinc. Elle peut être réduite en zinc, ou utilisée pour "
"d'autres réactions qui lui sont propre."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "manganese dioxide"
msgid_plural "manganese dioxide"
msgstr[0] "dioxydes de manganèse"
msgstr[1] "dioxydes de manganèse"
msgstr[2] "dioxydes de manganèse"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "manganese dioxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of manganese dioxide powder.  Occurring naturally in the mineral "
"pyrolusite, it is used commercially in the production of alkaline and "
"zinc-carbon batteries."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre de dioxyde de manganèse. Se trouvant naturellement dans "
"le minerai de pyrolusite, elle est utilisée dans la production commerciale "
"des piles alcalines et des piles zinc-carbone."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgid_plural "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgstr[0] "pâte électrolytique acidique"
msgstr[1] "pâte électrolytique acidique"
msgstr[2] "pâte électrolytique acidique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acidic electrolyte paste"
msgid ""
"A moisturized mixture of zinc chloride and manganese dioxide, slightly "
"acidic.  It can be used in the production of zinc-carbon batteries."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange légèrement acidique de chloride de zinc et de dioxide de manganèse "
"ayant été humidifié. Utilisé pour produire des piles zinc-carbone."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ferric chloride"
msgid_plural "ferric chloride"
msgstr[0] "chlorure de fer"
msgstr[1] "chlorure de fer"
msgstr[2] "chlorure de fer"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ferric chloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of dark green crystalline powder, with a weak pungent smell similar "
"to that of hydrochloric acid.  Commonly used as a Lewis acid for catalyzing "
"various chemical reactions."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre crystalline vert foncé possédant une faible odeur "
"désagréable similaire à celle de l'acide hydrochlorique. Communément utilisé "
"come acide Lewis pour catalyser des réactions chimiques variées."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "antimony trichloride"
msgid_plural "antimony trichloride"
msgstr[0] "trichlorure d'antimoine"
msgstr[1] "trichlorure d'antimoine"
msgstr[2] "trichlorure d'antimoine"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "antimony trichloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of soft, colorless powder with a sharp pungent odor, also known as "
"butter of antimony.  It's a catalyst for polymerization, hydrocracking, and "
"chlorination reactions, and has some other niche uses."
msgstr ""
"Une poudre molle et incolore à l'odeur âcre, autrement connue sous le nom de "
"beurre d'antimoine. C'est un catalyseur pour les réactions de polymérisation, "
"d'hydrocraquage et de chloration, ainsi que d'autres utilisations plus niches."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium chloride"
msgid_plural "potassium chloride"
msgstr[0] "chlorure de potassium"
msgstr[1] "chlorures de potassium"
msgstr[2] "chlorures de potassium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium chloride"
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium chloride.  Although it occurs naturally in the mineral "
"sylvite, it can be produced as a byproduct of the reaction of saltpeter and "
"hydrochloric acid.  It can be used for making fertilizer, or potassium "
"hydroxide by way of electrolysis."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de chlorure de potassium. Bien que trouvable naturellement dans "
"la sylvine minérale, il peut être produit artificiellement par la réaction du "
"salpêtre et de l'acide chlorhydrique. Il peut est utilisé pour faire des "
"engrais, ou de l’hydroxyde de potassium par électrolyse."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium hydroxide"
msgid_plural "potassium hydroxide"
msgstr[0] "hydroxyde de potassium"
msgstr[1] "hydroxydes de potassium"
msgstr[2] "hydroxydes de potassium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium hydroxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of potassium hydroxide.  Commonly called caustic potash, it was "
"mainly used industrially for its caustic nature.  It can be used as an "
"electrolyte in alkaline batteries, among other applications."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'hydroxyde de potassium. Communément appelé potasse caustique, "
"il était principalement utilisé industriellement pour sa nature caustique. Il "
"peut être utilisé comme électrolyte dans des piles alcalines, parmi d'autres "
"utilisations."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sulfuric acid"
msgid_plural "sulfuric acid"
msgstr[0] "acide sulfurique"
msgstr[1] "acide sulfurique"
msgstr[2] "acide sulfurique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sulfuric acid"
msgid ""
"Sulfuric acid: viscous, foul-smelling and extremely corrosive, particularly "
"to organic matter and evil clowns.  Although used to prepare a number of "
"chemicals, it is mostly known as battery acid, due to its widest commercial "
"application."
msgstr ""
"Acide sulfurique: visqueux, nauséabond et très corrosif, particulièrement "
"avec les matières organiques et les mauvais clowns. Il est utilisé dans de "
"nombreuses formules chimiques mais est principalement connu pour son "
"utilisation en tant qu'acide de batterie."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hydrochloric acid"
msgid_plural "hydrochloric acid"
msgstr[0] "acide chlorhydrique"
msgstr[1] "acides chlorhydriques"
msgstr[2] "acides chlorhydriques"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hydrochloric acid"
msgid ""
"Hydrochloric acid, also known as muriatic acid.  It is a strong acid that has "
"a distinctive smell, important and frequently used ever since its discovery.  "
"It still has a vast multitude of uses."
msgstr ""
"Acide chlorhydrique, aussi appelé acide muriatique. C'est un acide puissant "
"qui a une odeur distincte, important et fréquemment utilisé depuis sa "
"découverte. Il a encore une multitude d'utilités."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetone"
msgid_plural "acetone"
msgstr[0] "acétone"
msgstr[1] "acétone"
msgstr[2] "acétone"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetone"
msgid ""
"Acetone, best known as the primary constituent of most nail polish removers.  "
"Flammable, and can be easily used for potent homemade explosives, as "
"demonstrated by the terrorist attacks of 2016."
msgstr ""
"De l'acétone, principalement connue pour ses propriétés de décapant. "
"Inflammable, elle peut facilement servir pour faire des explosifs, comme "
"l'ont démontré des attaques terroristes en 2016."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nitric acid"
msgid_plural "nitric acid"
msgstr[0] "a"
msgstr[1] "acide nitrique"
msgstr[2] "acide nitrique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "nitric acid"
msgid ""
"Nitric acid, a strong oxidant and an extremely corrosive material.  Mainly "
"used in the production of synthetic fertilizers, for the etching of circuit "
"boards, and in woodworking.  Remains quite useful both for making a vast "
"array of pyrotechnic and explosive agents and as a direct weapon: not many "
"beings enjoy being doused in nitric acid."
msgstr ""
"De l'acide nitrique, un oxydant puissant et extrêmement corrosif. "
"Principalement utilisé durant la production d'engrais synthétiques, pour "
"façonner des circuits électriques ainsi que du bois. Aussi remarquablement "
"utile pour fabriquer un sélection variée d'agents pyrotechniques et explosifs "
"mais aussi capable d'être utilisé comme une arme tel quel vu que la plupart "
"des choses que vous pourriez couvrir d'acide nitrique ne risquent pas de trop "
"apprécier."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chromium oxide"
msgid_plural "chromium oxide"
msgstr[0] "Oxyde de chrome"
msgstr[1] "oxyde de chrome"
msgstr[2] "oxyde de chrome"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "chromium oxide"
msgid ""
"A handful of chromium oxide.  This substance, typically known as the only "
"stable green pigment for paints, is also a mild oxidizer, which can be mixed "
"with aluminum powder to make thermite for welding.  If one had access to a "
"CVD machine and a laboratory worth of reagents, they might be able to produce "
"very durable ceramic layers."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée d'oxyde de chrome. Cette substance, connue comme le seul pigment "
"vert pour les peintures, et également utilisée comme comburant, qui mélangée "
"avec de la poudre d'aluminium peut produire de la thermite pour la soudure. "
"Celui qui a accès à un laboratoire avec les composants nécessaires pourrait "
"produire de la céramique très résistante."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbide premix"
msgid_plural "calcium carbide premix"
msgstr[0] "carbure de calcium pré-mixé"
msgstr[1] "carbure de calcium pré-mixé"
msgstr[2] "carbure de calcium pré-mixé"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide premix"
msgid ""
"A powdered mixture of coke and lime ready to be smelted into usable calcium "
"carbide in an arc furnace."
msgstr ""
"Un mélange en poudre de charbon et de chaux prêt à être fondu en carbure de "
"calcium dans un four à arc."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbide"
msgid_plural "calcium carbide"
msgstr[0] "carbure de calcium"
msgstr[1] "carbure de calcium"
msgstr[2] "carbure de calcium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbide"
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbide, giving off a faint, garlic-like smell.  "
"Commercially, calcium carbide was used for on-the-spot manufacture of "
"acetylene and historically to power acetylene lamps.  If mixed with water and "
"sealed, it will explode with little strength, but with a relatively loud "
"noise that might be useful as a distraction."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de carbure de calcium sentant légèrement l'ail. Utilisé pour "
"fabriquer de l'acétylène et alimenter les lampes à acétylène. Peut être "
"utilisé pour causer une petite explosion assez bruyante pouvant détourner "
"l'attention si mélangé avec de l'eau dans un récipient fermé."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "calcium carbonate"
msgid_plural "calcium carbonate"
msgstr[0] "carbonate de calcium"
msgstr[1] "carbonate de calcium"
msgstr[2] "carbonate de calcium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "calcium carbonate"
msgid ""
"A handful of calcium carbonate powder, typically derived from lime or shells. "
" Useful for a number of roles, such as sugar production, fracking, "
"construction, paint additives and antacid medicine."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre de carbonate de calcium, généralement dérivée de la "
"chaux ou de coquillages. Le carbonate de calcium est utile dans de nombreux "
"domaines, tels que la production de sucre, la fracturation, la construction, "
"les additifs de peinture et les médicaments antiacides."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hexamine"
msgid ""
"A handful of waxy hexamine tablets which could be broken up into smaller "
"crumbs if needed.  This ubiquitous fuel was used to start up almost every "
"garden grill, and no 'real' camping trip could do its cooking without it, "
"until the Cataclysm.  Nowadays, it is even more valuable than before, being "
"the key component in the preparation of several military-grade explosives."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de tablettes cireuses d'hexamine capable d'être cassées en plus "
"petits morceaux si nécessaire. Ce carburant omniprésent était utilisé pour "
"démarrer a peut prêt n'importe quel barbecue et aucune 'véritable' sortie "
"camping ne pouvais avoir lieu sans. Ceci est maintenant encore plus précieux "
"pour votre survie, d'autant plus qu'il est possible de préparer de nombreux "
"explosifs de qualité militaire ayant l'hexamine pour élément clé."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgid_plural "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgstr[0] "peroxyde d'hydrogène (concentré)"
msgstr[1] "peroxyde d'hydrogène (concentré)"
msgstr[2] "peroxyde d'hydrogène (concentré)"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hydrogen peroxide (concentrated)"
msgid ""
"Concentrated hydrogen peroxide is a powerful oxidant, violently decomposing "
"in contact with most reducing agents.  Can be used as rocket fuel or to make "
"high explosives.  Causes severe burns to any organic matter and may ignite it "
"on contact."
msgstr ""
"De l'eau oxygénée concentrée. Peut s'utiliser pour fabriquer du combustible à "
"roquettes ou des explosifs. Provoque de sérieuses brûlures sur les matières "
"organiques et peut même les enflammer au contact."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "plutonium"
msgid ""
"A chunk of unshielded plutonium.  You should probably get very far away from "
"this, if you enjoy not being irradiated."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de plutonium sans aucune protection. Vous devriez probablement "
"rester très loin de ceci si vous ne voulez pas être irradié(e)."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "uranium"
msgid ""
"Some uranium.  You should probably get very far away from this, if you enjoy "
"not being irradiated."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau d'uranium sans aucune protection. Vous devriez probablement rester "
"très loin de ceci si vous ne voulez pas être irradié(e)."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ammonium nitrate"
msgid_plural "ammonium nitrate"
msgstr[0] "nitrate d'ammonium"
msgstr[1] "nitrate d'ammonium"
msgstr[2] "nitrate d'ammonium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate"
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate.  This white, crystalline powder is commonly "
"used as a component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved "
"in water to sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this "
"quality in this new world?"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de nitrate d'ammonium. Cette poudre blanche cristalline est "
"couramment utilisée dans les fertilisants et les explosifs. On peut aussi la "
"dissoudre dans l'eau pour en diminuer nettement la température, mais est-ce "
"utile dans ce nouveau monde?"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgid_plural "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgstr[0] "granules de nitrate d’ammonium"
msgstr[1] "granules de nitrate d’ammonium"
msgstr[2] "granules de nitrate d’ammonium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ammonium nitrate pellets"
msgid ""
"A handful of ammonium nitrate pellets.  These pellets are commonly used as a "
"component of fertilizers and explosives.  Could also be dissolved in water to "
"sharply lower its temperature, but is there any use for this quality in this "
"new world?"
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de granules de nitrate d'ammonium. Communément utilisé dans la "
"fabrication d'engrais et d'explosifs. Vous pouvez aussi dissoudre ces "
"granules dans de l'eau pour en diminuer nettement la température, mais est-ce "
"ceci très utile dans ce nouveau monde?"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "saltpeter"
msgid_plural "saltpeter"
msgstr[0] "salpêtre"
msgstr[1] "salpêtre"
msgstr[2] "salpêtre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "saltpeter"
msgid ""
"A handful of saltpeter.  Sometimes used as a fertilizer, this ubiquitous "
"nitrate is the principal constituent of black gunpowder and simple rocket "
"propellants, such as rocket candy."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de salpêtre. Parfois utilisé comme fertilisant, ce nitrate "
"omniprésent est le composant principal de la poudre à canon et des "
"combustibles de simple fusées tel que le rocket candy."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#: data/mods/innawood/mining/furniture_and_terrain/veins.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Terrain name
msgid "niter"
msgid_plural "niter"
msgstr[0] "nitre"
msgstr[1] "nitre"
msgstr[2] "nitre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "niter"
msgid ""
"A large crystal of niter, the mineral form of potassium nitrate.  It can be "
"processed into saltpeter."
msgstr ""
"Un grand cristal de nitre, forme minérale du nitrate de potassium.  il peut "
"être raffiné en salpêtre."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "aluminum sulfate"
msgid_plural "aluminum sulfate"
msgstr[0] "sulfate d'aluminium"
msgstr[1] "sulfate d'aluminium"
msgstr[2] "sulfate d'aluminium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "aluminum sulfate"
msgid ""
"Several crystals of aluminum sulfate.  Historically, an agent for purifying "
"water and as molluscicide, due to the fact that it degenerates their slime.  "
"Just before the Cataclysm, its main uses were for adjusting the acidity of "
"soil and as an additive to baking powder.  If mixed with a strong acid, it "
"could be used to saturate soil with aluminum, causing all but the most "
"resistant of plants to wither and die."
msgstr ""
"Plusieurs cristaux de sulfate d'aluminium. Il sert notamment comme agent de "
"purification de l'eau et molluscicide. Avant le cataclysme cette substance "
"servait à ajuster l'acidité des sols et comme aditif pour certaines poudres "
"de cuisson. Mélangé à un acide puissant, vous pouvez l'utilisez pour saturer "
"une zone de sol en aluminium, empêchant toutes sauf les plus résistantes des "
"plantes de se développer."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetic acid"
msgid_plural "acetic acid"
msgstr[0] "acide acétique"
msgstr[1] "acide acétique"
msgstr[2] "acide acétique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetic acid"
msgid ""
"Concentrated acetic acid, typically used as a chemical reagent and antifungal "
"agent.  Despite its horrid smell, it was used to prepare several types of "
"perfumes, but would making perfume not be too fancy for post-apocalyptic New "
"England?"
msgstr ""
"Acide acétique concentré, généralement utilisé comme réactif chimique et "
"agent antifongique. Malgré son odeur nauséabonde, il était utilisé pour "
"préparer plusieurs types de parfums, mais la fabrication de parfums ne "
"serait-elle pas trop chic pour la Nouvelle-Angleterre post-apocalyptique ?"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "formaldehyde"
msgid_plural "formaldehyde"
msgstr[0] "méthanal"
msgstr[1] "méthanal"
msgstr[2] "méthanal"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "formaldehyde"
msgid ""
"Formaldehyde, here dissolved in water, was widely used before the Cataclysm "
"as a precursor to production of many chemicals and materials and as an "
"embalming agent.  Easily identifiable by its pungent odor.  Terribly toxic, "
"carcinogenic, and volatile."
msgstr ""
"Formaldéhyde, ici dissout dans l'eau, était largement utilisé avant le "
"Cataclysme comme précurseur à la production de nombreux produits chimiques et "
"matériaux ainsi que comme agent d'embaumement. Facilement identifiable à son "
"odeur âcre. Terriblement toxique, cancérigène et volatile."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "thermite"
msgid_plural "thermite"
msgstr[0] "thermite"
msgstr[1] "thermite"
msgstr[2] "thermite"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "thermite"
msgid ""
"A handful of silvery-greenish powder, produced by mixing aluminum and "
"chromium oxide.  This mixture, burning at a constant pace and at extremely "
"high temperature, was once used for on-the-spot welding.  Can be used as an "
"incendiary material in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un mélande d'aluminium et d'oxyde de fer. Il brûle à des températures "
"extrêmes, et s'utilisait pour les soudures. C'est une très bonne matière "
"incendiaire."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ANFO"
msgid_plural "ANFO"
msgstr[0] "ANFO"
msgstr[1] "ANFO"
msgstr[2] "ANFO"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ANFO"
msgid ""
"A handful of brownish pellets, made by allowing ammonium nitrate to absorb an "
"organic fuel.  This ammonium nitrate/fuel oil mixture, or ANFO, is a common "
"industrial explosive due to its stability and low price.  Burns fast, but "
"needs an explosive primer to detonate."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de boulettes brunâtres, fabriquées en laissant le nitrate "
"d'ammonium absorber un combustible organique. Ce mélange de nitrate "
"d'ammonium et de mazout, ou ANFO, est un explosif industriel courant en "
"raison de sa stabilité et de son faible prix. Il brûle rapidement, mais a "
"besoin d'une amorce explosive pour détoner."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "black gunpowder"
msgid_plural "black gunpowder"
msgstr[0] "poudre noire"
msgstr[1] "poudre noire"
msgstr[2] "poudre noire"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "black gunpowder"
msgid ""
"A handful of black gunpowder, a mix of saltpeter, charcoal, and sulfur.  "
"Pretty useless for making modern cartridges, as the soot produced when it "
"burns will quickly clog any firearm, but it could be used to make some "
"vicious bombs."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre noire, un mélange de salpêtre, de charbon de bois et de "
"soufre. Plutôt inutile pour fabriquer des cartouches modernes, car la suie "
"produite lors de la combustion encrasse rapidement n'importe quelle arme à "
"feu, mais elle peut être utilisée pour fabriquer des bombes vicieuses."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "RDX"
msgid ""
"Several off-white crystals of RDX, or hexogen: a military-grade, shelf-stable "
"high explosive.  Can be cast into shaped charges, or mixed with scrap to "
"pepper the blast area with high-velocity shrapnel."
msgstr ""
"Quelques cristaux blanchâtres de RDX, ou hexogène : un explosif de classe "
"militaire, soufflant et stable. Peut être moulé en charges formées, ou "
"mélangé avec de la ferraille pour poivrer la zone de shrapnels à "
"haute-vélocité."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "composition B"
msgid_plural "composition B"
msgstr[0] "composition B"
msgstr[1] "composition B"
msgstr[2] "composition B"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "composition B"
msgid ""
"Composition B is an explosive consisting of castable mixtures of RDX and TNT. "
" It is used as the main explosive filling in artillery projectiles, rockets, "
"land mines, hand grenades, and various other munitions."
msgstr ""
"La composition B est un explosif composé de mélanges coulables de RDX et de "
"TNT. Elle est utilisée comme principale charge explosive dans les projectiles "
"d'artillerie, les roquettes, les mines terrestres, les grenades à main et "
"diverses autres munitions."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "HMTD"
msgid_plural "HMTD"
msgstr[0] "HMTD"
msgstr[1] "HMTD"
msgstr[2] "HMTD"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "HMTD"
msgid ""
"Hexamine peroxide: this fine, yellowish powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, but best not store it for too long."
msgstr ""
"Peroxyde d'hexamine : cette fine poudre jaunâtre est un explosif primaire "
"puissant utilisé pour amorcer la détonation d'explosifs plus stables comme le "
"RDX. Relativement stable mais mieux vaut ne pas le stocker trop longtemps."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "APEX"
msgid_plural "APEX"
msgstr[0] "APEX"
msgstr[1] "APEX"
msgstr[2] "APEX"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "APEX"
msgid ""
"Acetone peroxide: this fine, white crystalline powder is a powerful primary "
"explosive, used to initiate detonation of more stable explosives, such as "
"RDX.  Relatively stable, with a fruit-like smell when pure."
msgstr ""
"Peroxyde d'acétone : cette fine poudre cristalline blanche est un puissant "
"explosif primaire, utilisé pour amorcer la détonation d'explosifs plus "
"stables, tels que le RDX. Relativement stable, elle dégage une odeur de fruit "
"lorsqu'elle est pure."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid_plural "improvised rocket fuel"
msgstr[0] "carburant de fusée improvisé"
msgstr[1] "carburant de fusée improvisé"
msgstr[2] "carburant de fusée improvisé"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "improvised rocket fuel"
msgid ""
"A chunk of a zinc powder-and-sulfur mixture, bound together by superglue, "
"that can be used as an impromptu rocket fuel."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau d'un mélange de poudre de zinc et de soufre, lié par de la "
"superglue, qui peut être utilisé comme carburant de fusée improvisé."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "water purification tablet"
msgid_plural "water purification tablets"
msgstr[0] "tablette de purification d'eau"
msgstr[1] "tablettes de purification d'eau"
msgstr[2] "tablettes de purification d'eau"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "water purification tablet"
msgid ""
"Intended for the clarification and disinfection of unsafe drinking water "
"while camping or traveling, this sodium dichloroisocyanurate-based "
"purification tablet removes dangerous contaminants using powerful chemicals.  "
"The label says to use one tablet per liter (4 units of water)."
msgstr ""
"Comprimé de purification à base de dichloroisocyanurate de sodium, destiné à "
"clarifier et désinfecter l'eau potable non sûre lors du camping ou des "
"voyages. Il élimine les contaminants dangereux grâce à des produits chimiques "
"puissants. L'étiquette indique d'utiliser un comprimé par litre (4 unités "
"d'eau)."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hickory root"
msgid_plural "hickory roots"
msgstr[0] "racine de caryer"
msgstr[1] "racines de caryer"
msgstr[2] "racines de caryer"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hickory root"
msgid "A root from a hickory tree.  It has an earthy smell."
msgstr "Un racine de caryer. Il à une senteur terreuse."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hickory nuts"
msgid_plural "hickory nuts"
msgstr[0] "noix de caryer"
msgstr[1] "noix de caryer"
msgstr[2] "noix de caryer"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "hickory nuts"
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a hickory tree, still in their shells."
msgstr "Une poignée de noix de caryer, encore dans leurs cosses."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pecans"
msgid_plural "pecans"
msgstr[0] "noix de pécan"
msgstr[1] "noix de pécan"
msgstr[2] "noix de pécan"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "pecans"
msgid "A handful of hard nuts from a pecan tree, still in their shells."
