msgstr[1] "eaux usées"
msgstr[2] "eaux usées"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sewage water"
msgid "Turbid liquid from the sewers with an awful stench."
msgstr ""
"Un échantillon de liquide d'égout possédant une puanteur conforme à son "
"origine."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "detergent"
msgid_plural "detergent"
msgstr[0] "détergent"
msgstr[1] "détergent"
msgstr[2] "détergent"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "detergent"
msgid "A popular pre-Cataclysm washing powder."
msgstr "Une poudre de lavage populaire avant le Cataclysme."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "soap flakes"
msgid_plural "soap flakes"
msgstr[0] "copeau de savon"
msgstr[1] "copeaux de savon"
msgstr[2] "copeaux de savon"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "soap flakes"
msgid ""
"A handful of flakes shaved off a bar of soap, suitable for use in a washing "
"machine."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de copeaux issus d'une barre de savon utilisables pour lancer une "
"machine à laver."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "lye"
msgid_plural "lye"
msgstr[0] "soude"
msgstr[1] "soude"
msgstr[2] "soude"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "lye"
msgid "A liquid form of sodium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with care."
msgstr ""
"Une solution liquide d'hydroxide de sodium. Hautement corrosive, à manipuler "
"avec précaution."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "potassium lye"
msgid_plural "potassium lye"
msgstr[0] "hydroxyde de potassium"
msgstr[1] "hydroxyde de potassium"
msgstr[2] "hydroxyde de potassium"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "potassium lye"
msgid ""
"A liquid form of potassium hydroxide.  It is highly corrosive; handle with "
"care."
msgstr ""
"Une solution liquide d'hydroxide de potassium. Hautement corrosive, à "
"manipuler avec précaution."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "nanomaterial canister"
msgid_plural "nanomaterial canisters"
msgstr[0] "baril de nano-matériel"
msgstr[1] "barils de nano-matériel"
msgstr[2] "barils de nano-matériel"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "nanomaterial canister"
msgid ""
"A steel canister containing carbon, iron, titanium, copper, and other "
"elements in specifically engineered atomic-scale configurations.  A "
"nanofabricator can assemble them into usable items."
msgstr ""
"Un bidon en acier contenant du carbone, du fer, du titane, du cuivre et "
"d'autres éléments dans des configurations spécifiquement conçues à l'échelle "
"atomique.  Une usine nanotechnologique peut les assembler pour en faire des "
"objets utilisables."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wood ashes"
msgid_plural "wood ashes"
msgstr[0] "cendres de bois"
msgstr[1] "cendres de bois"
msgstr[2] "cendres de bois"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wood ashes"
msgid ""
"A handful of almost-weightless residue left after the burning of some "
"substance."
msgstr "Le résidu presque sans poids laissé par la combustion d'un objet."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "corpse ashes"
msgid_plural "corpse ashes"
msgstr[0] "cendres de cadavre"
msgstr[1] "cendres de cadavre"
msgstr[2] "cendres de cadavre"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "corpse ashes"
msgid "The burnt remains of a person or animal."
msgstr "Les restes incombustibles d'une personne ou d'un animal."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "ether"
msgid_plural "ether"
msgstr[0] "ether"
msgstr[1] "ether"
msgstr[2] "ether"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "ether"
msgid ""
"A useful industrial solvent, and the first inhalative anesthetic in "
"widespread use.  Its uncomfortable side effects and tendency to explode "
"caused it to fall out of favor decades ago in the developed world.  If you "
"can't get the good stuff, however, it might make a passable substitute."
msgstr ""
"Solvant industriel utile et premier anesthésique inhalé d'usage courant. Ses "
"effets secondaires désagréables et sa tendance à exploser l'ont fait tomber "
"en disgrâce il y a plusieurs décennies dans les pays développés. Si vous ne "
"pouvez pas vous procurer le bon produit, il peut toutefois constituer un "
"substitut acceptable."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid_plural "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgstr[0] "diméthylsulfoxyde"
msgstr[1] "diméthylsulfoxyde"
msgstr[2] "diméthylsulfoxyde"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "dimethyl sulfoxide"
msgid ""
"Dimethyl sulfoxide, or DMSO, is a common and important aprotic solvent, "
"capable of dissolving a huge range of things.  It has the unusual property of "
"being absorbed very quickly through the skin, causing a garlic flavor in the "
"mouth, even if it touched your arm."
msgstr ""
"Le diméthylsulfoxyde, ou DMSO, est un solvant aprotique courant et important, "
"capable de dissoudre un grand nombre de choses. Il a la propriété "
"inhabituelle d'être absorbé très rapidement par la peau, provoquant un goût "
"d'ail dans la bouche, même s'il a touché votre bras."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "chloroform"
msgid_plural "chloroform"
msgstr[0] "chloroforme"
msgstr[1] "chloroforme"
msgstr[2] "chloroforme"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "chloroform"
msgid ""
"Famous for its properties as an illicit sedative, this substance is also a "
"very good solvent.  In particular, it's used a lot in nuclear magnetic "
"resonance spectroscopy."
msgstr ""
"Célèbre pour ses propriétés de sédatif illicite, cette substance est "
"également un très bon solvant. Elle est notamment très utilisée en "
"spectroscopie par résonance magnétique nucléaire."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "phenol"
msgid_plural "phenol"
msgstr[0] "phénol"
msgstr[1] "phénol"
msgstr[2] "phénol"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "phenol"
msgid ""
"A useful and potent solvent with a wide range of reactive applications.  It "
"can be used to make a huge number of plastics and polymers, it can be an "
"antiseptic, it can strip paint and break down epoxy, and it can burn your "
"skin away like tissue paper under a heat gun.  Wear gloves."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un solvant utile et puissant qui possède un large éventail "
"d'applications réactives. Il peut être utilisé pour fabriquer un grand nombre "
"de plastiques et de polymères, il peut être un antiseptique, il peut décaper "
"la peinture et décomposer l'époxy, et il peut brûler votre peau comme du "
"papier de soie sous un pistolet thermique. Portez des gants."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "benzene"
msgid_plural "benzene"
msgstr[0] "benzène"
msgstr[1] "benzène"
msgstr[2] "benzène"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "benzene"
msgid ""
"A colorless, highly flammable liquid with a sweet odor, one of the elementary "
"petrochemicals.  Being used primarily as a precursor to the manufacture of "
"chemicals with more complex structure, it's a major industrial chemical, but "
"finds limited use in consumer items because of its toxicity."
msgstr ""
"Liquide incolore, hautement inflammable et d'odeur douce, l'un des produits "
"pétrochimiques élémentaires. Utilisé principalement comme précurseur pour la "
"fabrication de produits chimiques de structure plus complexe, c'est un "
"produit chimique industriel majeur, mais dont l'utilisation est limitée dans "
"les produits de consommation en raison de sa toxicité."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "toluene"
msgid_plural "toluene"
msgstr[0] "toluène"
msgstr[1] "toluène"
msgstr[2] "toluène"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "toluene"
msgid ""
"A colorless, toxic, and highly flammable liquid which smells like paint "
"thinner.  It's predominantly used as an industrial feedstock and a solvent, "
"and is also used as an intoxicative inhalant in a manner unintended by "
"manufacturers."
msgstr ""
"Liquide incolore, toxique et hautement inflammable, dont l'odeur rappelle "
"celle du diluant pour peinture. Il est principalement utilisé comme matière "
"première industrielle et comme solvant, mais aussi comme produit d'inhalation "
"intoxicant d'une manière non voulue par les fabricants."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "glycerol"
msgid_plural "glycerol"
msgstr[0] "glycérol"
msgstr[1] "glycérol"
msgstr[2] "glycérol"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "glycerol"
msgid ""
"Also called glycerin, this clear, odorless liquid is both a handy skin "
"moisturizer and an ingredient necessary to make dynamite."
msgstr ""
"Également appelée glycérine, ce liquide clair et inodore est à la fois un "
"hydratant pour la peau utile et un ingrédient nécessaire à la fabrication de "
"la dynamite."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "peptone water powder"
msgid_plural "peptone water powder"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "peptone water powder"
msgid "A pre-mixed salty solution of protein and sugar meant for bacteria to eat."
msgstr ""
"Une solution saline pré-mélangée de protéines et de sucre destinée à nourrir "
"les bactéries."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "agar"
msgid_plural "agar"
msgstr[0] "agar"
msgstr[1] "agar"
msgstr[2] "agar"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "agar"
msgid ""
"Clear flakes of processed seaweed that can be dissolved in boiling water to "
"create a very sturdy, temperature-resistant gel.  Not only is it good for "
"making gels to separate molecules by size, but it's a great cheat ingredient "
"to make sure your jellies set properly."
msgstr ""
"Des flocons transparents d'algues transformées pouvant être dissous dans de "
"l'eau bouillante pour créer un gel très solide et résistant à la température. "
" Non seulement c'est bon pour fabriquer des gels pour séparer des molécules "
"par taille, mais c'est un excellent ingrédient de triche pour garantir que "
"vos gelées comestibles prennent correctement."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acrylamide"
msgid_plural "acrylamide"
msgstr[0] "acrylamide"
msgstr[1] "acrylamide"
msgstr[2] "acrylamide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acrylamide"
msgid ""
"A handful of highly carcinogenic white powder that can be readily polymerized "
"into a whole bunch of useful water-soluble gels."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée de poudre blanche hautement cancérigène facilement polymérisée "
"pour former une variété de gels utiles solubles dans l'eau."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "steel grille"
msgid_plural "steel grilles"
msgstr[0] "grille en acier"
msgstr[1] "grilles en acier"
msgstr[2] "grilles en acier"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "steel grille"
msgid "A metal grille.  It can be used as a framework for making a chemical catalyst."
msgstr ""
"Une grille métallique. Elle peut être utilisée comme cadre pour la "
"fabrication d'un catalyseur chimique."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid_plural "cobalt-60 pellets"
msgstr[0] "pastille de cobalt-60"
msgstr[1] "pastilles de cobalt-60"
msgstr[2] "pastilles de cobalt-60"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "cobalt-60 pellet"
msgid ""
"A piece of unshielded radioactive material that used to be a part of some "
"nuclear industry equipment.  You have yet to find some use for it, and you "
"probably shouldn't stand near it."
msgstr ""
"Un morceau de matière radioactive non-scellée qui faisait autrefois partie de "
"certains équipements de l'industrie nucléaire.  Vous ne pensez pas pouvoir en "
"faire quelque chose d'utile et vous ne devriez définitivement pas rester en "
"proximité avec."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden bead"
msgid_plural "wooden beads"
msgstr[0] "perle en bois"
msgstr[1] "perles en bois"
msgstr[2] "perles en bois"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wooden bead"
msgid ""
"A wooden bead.  It can be used to craft inscribable jewelry or create a "
"beaded curtain door."
msgstr ""
"Une perle en bois. Elle peut être utilisée pour fabriquer des bijoux "
"inscriptibles ou créer une porte de rideau en perles."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "rosin"
msgid_plural "rosin"
msgstr[0] "colophane"
msgstr[1] "colophane"
msgstr[2] "colophane"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "rosin"
msgid "A chunk of yellowish rosin, usable as a flux for soldering."
msgstr "Un morceau de colophane jaunâtre, utilisable comme fondant de soudure."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "acetylene"
msgid_plural "acetylene"
msgstr[0] "acétylène"
msgstr[1] "acétylène"
msgstr[2] "acétylène"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "acetylene"
msgid ""
"A flammable gas that explodes under pressure.  Combined with oxygen, "
"acetylene makes a great welding gas."
msgstr ""
"Gaz inflammable qui explose sous l'effet de la pression. Combiné à l'oxygène, "
"l'acétylène constitue un excellent gaz de soudage."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "formic acid"
msgid_plural "formic acid"
msgstr[0] "acide formique"
msgstr[1] "acide formique"
msgstr[2] "acide formique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "formic acid"
msgid ""
"Common in nature as an insect venom, this substance has a number of "
"industrial uses such as preservation and manufacturing."
msgstr ""
"Répandue dans la nature sous forme de venin d'insecte, cette substance a un "
"certain nombre d'utilisations industrielles telles que la conservation et la "
"fabrication."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "latex"
msgid_plural "latex"
msgstr[0] "latex"
msgstr[1] "latex"
msgstr[2] "latex"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "latex"
msgid "A liquid precursor to rubber found in some plants."
msgstr "Précurseur liquide du caoutchouc que l'on trouve dans certaines plantes."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "citric acid"
msgid_plural "citric acid"
msgstr[0] "acide citrique"
msgstr[1] "acide citrique"
msgstr[2] "acide citrique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "citric acid"
msgid ""
"A manufactured form of citric acid that is commonly used as an additive in "
"food, cleaning agents, and nutritional supplements."
msgstr ""
"Forme manufacturée d'acide citrique couramment utilisée comme additif dans "
"les aliments, les produits de nettoyage et les compléments alimentaires."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wasp venom gland"
msgid_plural "wasp venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glande venimeuse de guêpe"
msgstr[1] "glandes venimeuses de guêpe"
msgstr[2] "glandes venimeuses de guêpe"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "wasp venom gland"
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of wasp "
"venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with the right "
"know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un organe fragile frémissant légèrement ayant pour fonction la production et "
"le stockage du venin d'une guêpe.  Vous pourriez en extraire des produits "
"chimiques très utiles avec le bon savoir-faire, mais dépêchez-vous avant que "
"celle-ci pourrisse."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bee venom gland"
msgid_plural "bee venom glands"
msgstr[0] "glande venimeuse d'abeille"
msgstr[1] "glandes venimeuses d'abeille"
msgstr[2] "glandes venimeuses d'abeille"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "bee venom gland"
msgid ""
"A fragile, slightly quivering organ for the production and storage of "
"honeybee venom.  You could extract some very useful chemicals from it with "
"the right know-how, but only if you hurry."
msgstr ""
"Un organe fragile frémissant légèrement ayant pour fonction la production et "
"le stockage du venin d'une abeille.  Vous pourriez en extraire des produits "
"chimiques très utiles avec le bon savoir-faire, mais dépêchez-vous avant que "
"celle-ci pourrisse."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sac of paralytic venom"
msgid_plural "sacs of paralytic venom"
msgstr[0] "vésicule de venin paralytique"
msgstr[1] "vésicules de venin paralytique"
msgstr[2] "vésicules de venin paralytique"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sac of paralytic venom"
msgid ""
"A grayish, flexible vesicle filled to the brim with the potent paralytic "
"agent the triffids use to subdue still-moving fertilizer such as yourself.  "
"If you know your way around poisons you might be able to find a use for it."
msgstr ""
"Une vésicule grisâtre et flexible remplie à ras bord d'un puissant agent "
"paralysant que les triffides utilisent pour maîtriser les engrais immobiles "
"tels que vous. Si vous vous y connaissez en poisons, vous pourrez peut-être "
"lui trouver une utilité."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sac of triffid fungicide"
msgid_plural "sacs of triffid fungicide"
msgstr[0] "vésicule de fongicide triffide"
msgstr[1] "vésicules de fongicide triffide"
msgstr[2] "vésicules de fongicide triffide"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "sac of triffid fungicide"
msgid ""
"A triffid sac filled with what appears to be a triffid-produced antifungal "
"agent.  It will likely already work as an antifungal compound for more "
"offensive applications, but requires further refining before it can be used "
"as a medical drug."
msgstr ""
"Une poche de liquide antifongique ayant été produit par un organisme "
"triffide. Vous pourriez l'utiliser tel quel comme produit antifongique "
"offensif, mais vous allez devoir le raffiner un peu plus avant qu'il soit "
"raisonnable de l'utiliser comme médicament antifongique."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "concentrated venom"
msgid_plural "concentrated venom"
msgstr[0] "venin concentré"
msgstr[1] "Venins concentrés"
msgstr[2] "Venins concentrés"

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Description of "concentrated venom"
msgid ""
"A transparent, lightly greenish liquid, refined from the venom of bees and "
"wasps.  Active ingredients include (nor-)adrenaline, dopamine, histamine, and "
"protein toxins.  It is now relatively stable, but will require further "
"separation to be useful for anything other than killing you."
msgstr ""
"Un liquide transparent, légèrement verdâtre, obtenu en raffinant du venin "
"d'abeille ou guêpe ayant pour ingrédients actifs (nor-)adrénaline, dopamine, "
"histamine et plusieurs protéines toxiques. Rendu plus ou moins stable pour "
"l'instant, mais plus vous allez avoir besoin d'isoler certaines substances "
"pour fabriquer quelque chose à partir de ceci qui soit bon pour quoi que ce "
"soit d'autre qu'être un poison virulent."

#: data/json/items/chemicals_and_resources.json
#. ~ Item name
