#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de chasse à verrou"
msgstr[1] "fusils de chasse à verrou"
msgstr[2] "fusils de chasse à verrou"

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Description of "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"Featuring a handsome set of wooden furnishings, a classic design, and a no "
"nonsense .270 caliber chambering, this is a powerful hunting rifle.  With a "
"tried and proven pedigree dating back over 60 years, millions of such rugged "
"arms have been made, exported, and used throughout the United States and the "
"world at large.  Where hunting is concerned, this is a highly capable and "
"well proven weapon in all respects.  Fortunate, given that your prey in these "
"dark days may turn out to be a little bit more feisty than typical "
"White-Tailed deer, moose, and black bears."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid "Remington 700 .270 Win rifle"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .270 Win rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Remington 700 calibre .270 Win"
msgstr[1] "fusils Remington 700 calibre .270 Win"
msgstr[2] "fusils Remington 700 calibre .270 Win"

#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action hunting rifle" of gun "Remington 700
#. .270 Win rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Remington 700 .270 Win rifle" of item "bolt-
#. action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"A classic bolt-action rifle chambered for .270 Winchester, very popular among "
"hunters.  This is a CDL SF model with a forged, fluted, 416 stainless steel "
"barrel threaded into the receiver and a recessed bolt face.  It has checkered "
"walnut furniture and a recoil pad to reduce perceived recoil."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M2010 ESR"
msgid_plural "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[0] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[1] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[2] "M2010 ESR"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "M2010 ESR"
#. ~ Description of "M2010 ESR"
msgid ""
"A bolt-action, box-magazine-fed sniper rifle chambered in the powerful .300 "
"Winchester Magnum round.  The M2010 had completely replaced the M24 rifle "
"series by 2017."
msgstr ""
"Un fusil à verrou à chargeur de sniper chambré pour accueillir des cartouches "
"du puissant calibre .300 Winchester Magnum.  Ce modèle remplaça complétement "
"le M24 en 2017 pour l'armée américaine."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid_plural "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[0] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[1] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[2] "Weatherby Mark V"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Weatherby Mark V"
#. ~ Description of "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid ""
"The Weatherby Mark V is one of the world's finest bolt-action rifles.  "
"Designed in 1955 by Roy Weatherby and Fred Jennie, it has a strong action "
"designed to safely fire high-pressure cartridges.  These rifles were "
"presented to celebrities as part of a marketing campaign."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Winchester Model 70"
msgid_plural "Winchester Model 70s"
msgstr[0] "fusil Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[1] "fusils Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[2] "fusils Winchester Model 70"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester Model 70"
#. ~ Description of "Winchester Model 70"
msgid ""
"The Winchester Model 70 is a bolt-action sporting rifle.  It has an iconic "
"place in American sporting culture and has been held in high regard by "
"shooters since it was introduced in 1936."
msgstr ""
"Le Winchester Modèle 70 est un fusil de compétition avec mécanisme à verrou. "
"C'est une icône de la culture de tir sportif Américaine et populaire depuis "
"son introduction en 1936."

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Ruger Precision Rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Precision Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Fusil de Précision Ruger"
msgstr[1] "Fusils de Précision Ruger"
msgstr[2] "Fusils de Précision Ruger"

#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Precision Rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Ruger Precision Rifle"
msgid ""
"Originally introduced to the Ruger gun corporation's family of high-end "
"marksman rifles in 2015, the Ruger Precision Rifle is a modern and highly "
"modular long-range bolt-action weapon.  By incorporating a unique in-line "
"recoil path that manages recoil from the rear of the receiver to the "
"buttstock, as opposed to traditional bedding, the rifle offers maximal "
"accuracy potential, while the arm's additional bells and whistles, an "
"incorporated marksman's trigger, muzzle brake, and this particular rifle's "
"powerhouse chambering of .300 Win Mag, help to make the most from any "
"long-range engagement."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "BLR lever-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de chasse à verrou BLR"
msgstr[1] "fusils de chasse à verrou BLR"
msgstr[2] "fusils de chasse à verrou BLR"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Description of "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid ""
"A highly accurate lever-action hunting rifle chambered for the powerful "
".30-06 round.  Notable for using a detachable magazine instead of a "
"traditional tube."
msgstr ""
"Un fusil de chasse à levier reconnu pour sa précision exceptionelle et "
"chambré pour accueillir le calibre puissant .30-06. Cette arme à feu et aussi "
"notable pour son utilisation d'un chargeur détachable au lieu d'un tube de "
"charge plus traditionnel."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "BLR lever-action hunting rifle"
msgid "Browning BLR"
msgid_plural "Browning BLRs"
msgstr[0] "fusil Browning BLR"
msgstr[1] "fusils Browning BLR"
msgstr[2] "fusils Browning BLR"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "BLR lever-action hunting rifle" of gun "Browning
#. BLR"
#. ~ Description of variant "Browning BLR" of item "BLR lever-action hunting
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"The Browning BLR is notable for being a lever-action rifle, chambered in "
"calibers with spitzer bullets.  This is unusual for lever-actions, as a "
"spitzer bullet risks setting off other cartridges in a typical tube magazine. "
" The BLR gets around this issue by utilizing box magazines instead, making it "
"quite unique among other lever-action rifles.  This one is chambered for "
"30-06."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Garand battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Garand battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de combat Garand"
msgstr[1] "fusils de combat Garand"
msgstr[2] "fusils de combat Garand"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Garand battle rifle"
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic .30-06 battle rifle, developed to replace the M1903 "
"Springfield.  It didn't completely supplant the older bolt-action until after "
"World War II."
msgstr ""
"Un fusil de bataille semi-automatique chambré pour le calibre .30-06.  Conçu "
"pour remplacer le M1903 Springfield, les rigueurs de la Seconde Guerre "
"Mondiale empêchèrent une obsolescence complète avant la fin du conflit."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Garand battle rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M1 Garand"
msgid_plural "M1 Garand"
msgstr[0] "fusil M1 Garand"
msgstr[1] "fusils M1 Garand"
msgstr[2] "fusils M1 Garand"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Garand battle rifle" of gun "M1 Garand"
#. ~ Description of variant "M1 Garand" of item "Garand battle rifle"
msgid ""
"The M1 Garand is a widely celebrated battle rifle, being one of the most "
"mass-produced battle rifles in the world.  It saw widespread use in the US "
"military, being used extensively in WW2 and the Korean War.  While its "
"military use has dwindled down, being out of US service for more than 50 "
"years, some of its mechanical influence still remains through rifles such as "
"AKs or M14s.  It still sees widespread use in civilian spaces as an accurate "
"competition or hunting rifle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Springfield rifle"
msgid_plural "Springfield rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Springfield"
msgstr[1] "fusils Springfield"
msgstr[2] "fusils Springfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Springfield rifle"
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle chambered in .30-06, developed to replace the US "
"Army's older Krag rifle.  It served as the main American rifle in World War "
"I, was used alongside the M1 Garand in World War II, and was used as a sniper "
"rifle as late as the Vietnam War."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Springfield rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M1903 Springfield"
msgid_plural "M1903 Springfields"
msgstr[0] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[1] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[2] "M1903 Springfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Springfield rifle" of gun "M1903 Springfield"
#. ~ Description of variant "M1903 Springfield" of item "Springfield rifle"
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle originally chambered in .30-03 Springfield, "
"developed to replace the US Army's older Krag rifle.  It was quickly "
"rechambered into the .30-06 caliber with its spitzer bullet.  While an "
"American rifle produced and developed around WW1, manufacturing couldn't keep "
"up with demand, and saw service alongside the M1917 Enfield, a British rifle "
"rechambered for the American 30-06.  It saw service as a sniper rifle up to "
"the Vietnam War, but nowadays is mainly used by civilians, either as hunting "
"rifles or in collections."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "BAR rifle"
msgid_plural "BAR rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil BAR"
msgstr[1] "fusils BAR"
msgstr[2] "fusils BAR"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Description of "BAR rifle"
msgid ""
"This heavy rifle was designed near the end of World War I, and provided fire "
"support for the US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  "
"Too much firepower to serve as a battle rifle, but not enough to be an ideal "
"light machine gun, it still found a niche on the battlefield."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "BAR rifle"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgid_plural "Browning Automatic Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Fusil Automatique Browning"
msgstr[1] "Fusils Automatiques Browning"
msgstr[2] "Fusils Automatiques Browning"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "BAR rifle" of gun "Browning Automatic Rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Browning Automatic Rifle" of item "BAR rifle"
msgid ""
"Designed near the end of World War I, the BAR provided fire support for the "
"US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  Originally "
"developed to fill a now outdated role as an \"automatic rifle\", it was "
"pushed into service for use as a light machine gun.  Despite being heavy and "
"cumbersome, without filling its designed role, it saw service for over 50 "
"years.  While newer models have a slow and fast fully automatic setting, this "
"one is an older one, with just semi and full auto."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .30-06 rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Remington 700 calibre .30-06"
msgstr[1] "fusils Remington 700 calibre .30-06"
msgstr[2] "fusils Remington 700 calibre .30-06"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Remington 700 .30-06 rifle"
msgid ""
"A very popular and durable hunting or sniping rifle.  Popular among SWAT and "
"US Marine snipers.  Highly damaging, but perhaps not as accurate as the "
"competing Browning BLR."
msgstr ""
"Un fusil de chasse ou de sniper très populaire et très résistant. Commun dans "
"les rangs du SWAT ou chez les Marines snipers. Dévastateur mais peut-être pas "
"aussi précis que son rival le Browning BLR."

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger Guide rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Ruger Guide"
msgstr[1] "fusils Ruger Guide"
msgstr[2] "fusils Ruger Guide"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid ""
"This is a popular and sturdy long-range rifle that has been in production by "
"the Ruger gun company for several decades.  Using a bolt-action feed system, "
"the rifle features a four round capacity of .30-06 cartridges and has the "
"capability to dispatch said rounds with a level of accuracy that would make "
"comparable hunting rifles blush."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Ruger Guide rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Ruger Guide rifle"
msgid "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifle"
msgid_plural "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
msgstr[1] "fusils Ruger M77 Hawkeye"
msgstr[2] "fusils Ruger M77 Hawkeye"

#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Ruger Guide rifle" of gun "Ruger M77 Hawkeye
#. rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Ruger M77 Hawkeye rifle" of item "Ruger Guide
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"A popular bolt-action hunting rifle first introduced in 2006, the Ruger M77 "
"was originally intended to be a modernized Mauser 98-style long gun.  To this "
"end, the weapon features a Mauser-type fixed blade extractor and an angled "
"large screw that tightly beds the action into the stock.  This particular "
"rifle is a variant with additional features, a smoother trigger, and a "
"recontoured buttstock."
msgstr ""
"Un fusil de chasse à verrou populaire introduit au marché en 2006, le Ruger "
"M77 était originellement censé être une version modernisée d'un fusil long "
"dans le style du Mauser 98. À cette fin, cette arme à feu possède un "
"extracteur à cartouche fixé de type Mauser et une large vis coudée couchant "
"l'action de tir contre la crosse. Cette version spécifique du M77 est une "
"variante possédant plusieurs améliorations supplémentaires incluant une "
"détente plus fluide et une crosse reprofilée."

#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
