msgid_plural "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[0] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[1] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[2] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"

#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
#. ~ Description of gun "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
#. ~ Description of "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid ""
"A gas-operated rifle, with a short 5.5 inch barrel, built-in thin folding "
"stock, and full rail mount on the upper receiver.  This particular one is a "
"select-fire military version."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Enfield battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de combat Enfield"
msgstr[1] "fusils de combat Enfield"
msgstr[2] "fusils de combat Enfield"

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid ""
"An iconic weapon of both the First and Second World Wars, this bolt-action "
"rifle has seen deployment in the hands of Commonwealth troops across Europe "
"and beyond.  Firing the .303-caliber cartridge and making use of 10-round "
"Enfield magazines, the firearm's reputation precedes it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Enfield battle rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Enfield battle rifle"
msgid "SMLE No. 1 Mk III rifle"
msgid_plural "SMLE No. 1 Mk III rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil SMLE No. 1 Mk III"
msgstr[1] "fusils SMLE No. 1 Mk III"
msgstr[2] "fusils SMLE No. 1 Mk III"

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Enfield battle rifle" of gun "SMLE No. 1 Mk III
#. rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "SMLE No. 1 Mk III rifle" of item "Enfield battle
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"An English darling and icon of the First World War, the Short Magazine "
"Lee-Enfield Mk III was the standard issue battle rifle of the British "
"commonwealth from 1907.  Chambered for .303 ammunition, the rifle makes use "
"of ten-round detachable magazines.  With its full-length wooden handguard, "
"brass buttplate, and smooth action, the Lee-Enfield cuts a recognizable "
"profile in either the trenches of the Great War or the zombie-strewn "
"wastelands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#: data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "updated Enfield rifle"
msgid_plural "updated Enfield rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Enfield mis à jour"
msgstr[1] "fusils Enfield mis à jour"
msgstr[2] "fusils Enfield mis à jour"

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Description of gun "updated Enfield rifle"
#. ~ Description of "updated Enfield rifle"
msgid ""
"An evolution of Britain's First World War battle rifle, this bolt-action "
"firearm uses the same .303-caliber cartridge as its forerunner.  Much beloved "
"across the globe by collectors, rifles like this served as England's infantry "
"rifle well into the 1950s, with a specialized sniper variant remaining in "
"service until the early nineties."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "updated Enfield rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "updated Enfield rifle"
msgid "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I rifle"
msgid_plural "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I"
msgstr[1] "fusils Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I"
msgstr[2] "fusils Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I"

#: data/json/items/gun/303.json
#. ~ Description of variant "updated Enfield rifle" of gun "Lee-Enfield No. 4
#. Mk I rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Lee-Enfield No. 4 Mk I rifle" of item "updated
#. Enfield rifle"
msgid ""
"A Second World War progression of the British Commonwealth's Lee-Enfield "
"battle rifle, the No. 4 began its decades-long service life in 1939.  "
"Externally similar to its forefather, the rifle possesses a reinforced "
"receiver, an adjusted nose cap, and a heavier barrel.  Still chambered for "
"the same .303-caliber cartridge, the No. 4 represents one of the most "
"populous firearm imports in U.S. history."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Belgian battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Belgian battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de combat belge"
msgstr[1] "fusils de combat belges"
msgstr[2] "fusils de combat belges"

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Belgian battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Belgian battle rifle"
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, this gun is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Despite being labeled as obsolete, "
"its tunable gas system ensures both reliability and low recoil, allowing the "
"FAL to keep up even among modern competitors.  This is a semi-automatic clone "
"built by a domestic manufacturer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Belgian battle rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Belgian battle rifle"
msgid "DSA SA-58 rifle"
msgid_plural "DSA SA-58 rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil DSA SA-58"
msgstr[1] "fusils DSA SA-58"
msgstr[2] "fusils DSA SA-58"

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Belgian battle rifle" of gun "DSA SA-58 rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "DSA SA-58 rifle" of item "Belgian battle rifle"
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, the FAL is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Despite being labeled as obsolete, "
"its tunable gas system ensures both reliability and low recoil, allowing the "
"FAL to keep up even among modern competitors.  This is a semi-automatic clone "
"of the SA-58 pattern built by DSA."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "G3 battle rifle"
msgid_plural "G3 battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de combat G3"
msgstr[1] "fusils de combat G3"
msgstr[2] "fusils de combat G3"

#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
#. ~ Description of gun "G3 battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of "G3 battle rifle"
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic, domestically produced clone of an early battle rifle "
"developed after the end of WWII.  Known as the PTR 91, it is a fantastically "
"reliable, cheap to produce rifle that continues to serve in conflict regions. "
