#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle"
msgid_plural "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil anti-matériel semi-automatique"
msgstr[1] "fusils anti-matériel semi-automatiques"
msgstr[2] "fusils anti-matériel semi-automatiques"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of gun "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle"
#. ~ Description of "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle"
msgid ""
"A mahoosive rifle of military pedigree, fitted with a telescopic gun scope "
"peeking over its giant cocking mechanism and resting upon a bipod to control "
"recoil from the equally big .50-caliber munitions it is designed for.  "
"Originally employed for detonating unexploded ordnance in combat conditions "
"and defeating light vehicular and structural targets, in the post-Cataclysm "
"it serves as an admirable conduit of kinetic energy to the biggest and "
"baddest of the new world's critters."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un fusil militaire de grande taille, équipé d'une lunette de "
"visée télescopique qui dépasse de son gigantesque mécanisme d'armement et qui "
"repose sur un bipied afin de contrôler le recul des munitions de calibre 50 "
"pour lesquelles il a été conçu. Utilisé à l'origine pour faire exploser des "
"munitions non explosées dans des conditions de combat et pour détruire des "
"véhicules légers et des cibles structurelles, il sert, après le cataclysme, "
"d'admirable conduit d'énergie cinétique pour les créatures les plus grosses "
"et les plus méchantes du nouveau monde."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle"
msgid "Barrett M107A1"
msgid_plural "Barrett M107A1"
msgstr[0] "Barrett M107A1"
msgstr[1] "Barretts M107A1"
msgstr[2] "Barretts M107A1"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of variant "semi-automatic anti-materiel rifle" of gun
#. "Barrett M107A1"
#. ~ Description of variant "Barrett M107A1" of item "semi-automatic anti-
#. materiel rifle"
msgid ""
"A large, shoulder-fired, .50 caliber anti-materiel rifle.  Its large size, "
"recoil, and noise is offset by its damage and range."
msgstr ""
"Un gros fusil anti-matériel de calibre 50, tiré à l'épaule. Sa grande taille, "
"son recul et son bruit sont compensés par ses dégâts et sa portée."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
msgid_plural ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
msgstr[0] "mitrailleuse lourde calibre .50"
msgstr[1] "mitrailleuses lourdes calibre .50"
msgstr[2] "mitrailleuses lourdes calibre .50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of gun ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
#. ~ Description of ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
msgid ""
"Essentially a giant steel box with a long barrel peering from one end and "
"dual spade grips mounted upon the other, this venerable machine gun design "
"served the United States military since the First World War, mounted on "
"everything from tanks to patrol boats to aircraft, and even tripod-mounted "
"for stand-alone use.  Part and parcel with its size and munition payload of "
".50-caliber ammo belts, however, is the fact that, to operate it, one must "
"mount it upon suitable furniture, terrain features, or vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Essentiellement une boîte en acier géante avec un long canon dépassant d'une "
"extrémité et deux poignées à bêche montées à l'autre, cette vénérable "
"mitrailleuse a servi l'armée américaine depuis la Première Guerre mondiale, "
"montée sur toutes sortes d'objets, des chars aux patrouilleurs en passant par "
"les avions, et même montée sur trépied pour une utilisation autonome. Sa "
"taille et sa charge de munitions de calibre 50 font partie intégrante du fait "
"que, pour l'utiliser, il faut la monter sur des meubles, des éléments de "
"terrain ou des véhicules appropriés."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json data/mods/BombasticPerks/perkdata/old_guns.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
#. ~ Variant name of item ".50-caliber heavy machine gun"
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M2HB Browning HMG"
msgid_plural "M2HB Browning HMGs"
msgstr[0] "mitrailleuse lourde M2HB Browning"
msgstr[1] "mitrailleuses lourdes M2HB Browning"
msgstr[2] "mitrailleuses lourdes M2HB Browning"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of variant ".50-caliber heavy machine gun" of gun "M2HB
#. Browning HMG"
#. ~ Description of variant "M2HB Browning HMG" of item ".50-caliber heavy
#. machine gun"
msgid ""
"A heavy machine gun used by the US Military from its inception to the "
"Cataclysm, and even rarely by Cataclysm survivors.  Its massive size and "
"design make it impossible to use unless deployed or mounted to a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Une mitrailleuse lourde utilisée par l'armée américaine depuis sa création "
"jusqu'au Cataclysme, et même rarement par les survivants du Cataclysme. Sa "
"taille massive et sa conception la rendent impossible à utiliser à moins "
"d'être déployée ou montée sur un véhicule."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid ".50-caliber precision rifle"
msgid_plural ".50-caliber precision rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de précision calibre .50"
msgstr[1] "fusils de précision calibre .50"
msgstr[2] "fusils de précision calibre .50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of gun ".50-caliber precision rifle"
#. ~ Description of ".50-caliber precision rifle"
msgid ""
"Pin-point accurate out to one and a half kilometers and cycling its "
".50-caliber feed from detachable, 10-round magazines, this combat sniper's "
"weapon provides users with a comfortable window to engage targets at a "
"distance.  Its imposing bullets ensure that it is more than capable of "
"delivering an adequate account of itself at such ranges."
msgstr ""
"Précise jusqu'à un kilomètre et demi et alimentée en calibre 50 par des "
"chargeurs amovibles de 10 balles, cette arme de sniper de combat offre aux "
"utilisateurs une fenêtre confortable pour engager des cibles à distance. Ses "
"balles imposantes garantissent qu'elle est plus que capable de rendre un "
"compte adéquat d'elle-même à de telles distances."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun ".50-caliber precision rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item ".50-caliber precision rifle"
msgid "AI AS50"
msgid_plural "AI AS50"
msgstr[0] "fusil AI AS50"
msgstr[1] "fusils AI AS50"
msgstr[2] "fusils AI AS50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of variant ".50-caliber precision rifle" of gun "AI AS50"
#. ~ Description of variant "AI AS50" of item ".50-caliber precision rifle"
msgid ""
"Developed by Accuracy International, the AI AS50 is a semi-automatic .50 "
"caliber anti-materiel rifle produced for the British armed forces and the "
"United States Navy SEALs.  With a free-floated barrel, titanium frame, and an "
"accessory rail integrated into the weapon's receiver with two others mounted "
"on each side of the barrel shroud, the rifle features commendable ergonomics "
"and a notable level of modularity.  Providing operators with the capability "
"to engage targets at an estimated max range of 1500 meters, the firearm feeds "
"from 10-round box magazines."
msgstr ""
"Développé par Accuracy International, l'AI AS50 est un fusil anti-matériel "
"semi-automatique de calibre 50 produit pour les forces armées britanniques et "
"les Navy SEALs américains. Doté d'un canon flottant, d'une carcasse en titane "
"et d'un rail porte-accessoires intégré à la boîte de culasse de l'arme et de "
"deux autres montés de part et d'autre de la gaine du canon, le fusil présente "
"une ergonomie remarquable et un niveau de modularité notable. Offrant aux "
"opérateurs la possibilité d'engager des cibles à une distance maximale "
"estimée à 1500 mètres, l'arme à feu est alimentée par chargeur transversal de "
"10 balles."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action anti-materiel rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil anti-matériel à verrou"
msgstr[1] "fusils anti-matériel à verrou"
msgstr[2] "fusils anti-matériel à verrou"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle"
#. ~ Description of "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle"
msgid ""
"Serving both anti-materiel and high-priority sniping roles in their service "
"with various militaries, bolt-action rifles, such as this one, were known for "
"their long ranges of engagement, recoil, and armor-defeating ordinance.  "
"Essentially a step below light cannonry, as far as shoulder-arms are "
"concerned, this weapon's mix of power and accuracy meet hands to ensure that, "
"before the Cataclysm, one shot was synonymous with one very, very dead target."
msgstr ""
"Utilisés à la fois comme arme anti-matériel et comme arme de précision dans "
"diverses armées, les fusils à verrou, comme celui-ci, étaient connus pour "
"leurs longues distances d'engagement, leur recul et leurs munitions qui "
"détruisaient les armures. Essentiellement un cran en dessous de la canonnerie "
"légère, en ce qui concerne les armes d'épaule, le mélange de puissance et de "
"précision de cette arme se rencontre pour s'assurer qu'avant le Cataclysme, "
"un tir était synonyme d'une cible très, très morte."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle"
msgid "McMillan TAC-50"
msgid_plural "McMillan TAC-50"
msgstr[0] "fusil McMillan TAC-50"
msgstr[1] "fusils McMillan TAC-50"
msgstr[2] "fusils McMillan TAC-50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action anti-materiel rifle" of gun "McMillan
#. TAC-50"
#. ~ Description of variant "McMillan TAC-50" of item "bolt-action anti-
#. materiel rifle"
msgid ""
"A long-range anti-materiel and anti-personnel sniper rifle made by McMillan "
"Firearms, serving the Canadian Army since 2000 as the C15, and the Navy Seals "
"as the Mk 15 Mod 0.  This .50 caliber bolt-action rifle is capable of "
"defeating light vehicles, radar installations and crew-served weapons at "
"extreme distances.  It notably held the longest-range confirmed sniper kill, "
"as well as the 4th and 5th longest."
msgstr ""
"Fusil de précision anti-matériel et anti-personnel à longue portée fabriqué "
"par McMillan Firearms, utilisé par l'armée canadienne depuis 2000 sous le nom "
"de C15, et par les Navy Seals sous le nom de Mk 15 Mod 0. Ce fusil à verrou "
"de calibre 50 est capable d'abattre des véhicules légers, des installations "
"radar et des armes servies par l'équipage à des distances extrêmes. Il "
"détient notamment le record de la plus longue portée confirmée pour un tireur "
"d'élite, ainsi que les 4e et 5e records de longévité."

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "single-shot .50-caliber rifle"
msgid_plural "single-shot .50-caliber rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil de précision mono-coup calibre .50"
msgstr[1] "fusils de précision mono-coup calibre .50"
msgstr[2] "fusils de précision mono-coup calibre .50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of gun "single-shot .50-caliber rifle"
#. ~ Description of "single-shot .50-caliber rifle"
msgid ""
"Relatively trim as far as .50-caliber rifles go, this single-shot firearm was "
"a reasonably affordable entry-level gun for civilians wishing to play with "
"some very large, very punchy toys.  Now, at the world's Armageddon, it would "
"be wise to make that singular round-capacity count on some high-priority "
"craniums."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "single-shot .50-caliber rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "single-shot .50-caliber rifle"
msgid "Serbu BFG-50"
msgid_plural "Serbu BFG-50"
msgstr[0] "fusil Serbu BFG-50"
msgstr[1] "fusils Serbu BFG-50"
msgstr[2] "fusils Serbu BFG-50"

#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
#. ~ Description of variant "single-shot .50-caliber rifle" of gun "Serbu
#. BFG-50"
#. ~ Description of variant "Serbu BFG-50" of item "single-shot .50-caliber
#. rifle"
msgid ""
"A single-shot, bolt-action rifle made by Serbu Firearms, the BFG-50 was a "
"very affordable firearm for those wishing to shoot .50 BMG."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid ".500 Magnum revolver"
msgid_plural ".500 Magnum revolvers"
msgstr[0] "revolver calibre .500 Magnum"
msgstr[1] "revolvers calibre .500 Magnum"
msgstr[2] "revolvers calibre .500 Magnum"

#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
#. ~ Description of gun ".500 Magnum revolver"
#. ~ Description of ".500 Magnum revolver"
msgid ""
"The definition of 'overkill', this behemoth handgun puts large .44 caliber "
"revolvers to shame with its sheer size, power, and immense chambering.  "
"Firing the appropriately named .500 Magnum cartridge, the most powerful "
"handgun round in the world, the weapon has seen work in both sport shooting "
"and hunting roles.  A pistol for those of the 'bigger is better' mentality, a "
"high recoil junky's personal dream, and an all-around useless military "
"sidearm, should the urge to assault the Cataclysm in fine style grip you, "
"this giant provides you with 5 rounds with which to reduce a zombie into an "
"afterthought."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun ".500 Magnum revolver"
#. ~ Variant name of item ".500 Magnum revolver"
msgid "S&W 500 revolver"
msgid_plural "S&W 500 revolvers"
msgstr[0] "revolver S&W 500"
msgstr[1] "revolvers S&W 500"
msgstr[2] "revolvers S&W 500"

#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
#. ~ Description of variant ".500 Magnum revolver" of gun "S&W 500 revolver"
#. ~ Description of variant "S&W 500 revolver" of item ".500 Magnum revolver"
msgid ""
"The 5-shot Smith and Wesson 500 revolver fires the comparably-named .500 S&W "
"Magnum.  It's an impressive weapon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Russian AK rifle"
msgid_plural "Russian AK rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil AK russe"
msgstr[1] "fusils AK russes"
msgstr[2] "fusils AK russes"

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Russian AK rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Russian AK rifle"
msgid ""
"Flaunting classically iconic lines and a profile instantly recognizable to "
"any viewer, this American semi-automatic weapon is a replica of the AK-47 "
"rifle's technological descendant, the AK-74, a weapon with more notable "
"differences from its elder sibling than simply flipping the order of its "
"name's numbers.  Firing the rare, at least for the United States, 5.45x39mm "
"Soviet cartridge, this clone makes use of original 5.45mm banana magazines.  "
"Considering the scarcity of its munitions, you might be obliged to resort to "
"hand-loading your own ammunition."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Russian AK rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Russian AK rifle"
msgid "Kalashnikov AK-74"
msgid_plural "Kalashnikov AK-74 rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Kalashnikov AK-74"
msgstr[1] "fusils Kalashnikov AK-74"
msgstr[2] "fusils Kalashnikov AK-74"

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Russian AK rifle" of gun "Kalashnikov AK-74"
#. ~ Description of variant "Kalashnikov AK-74" of item "Russian AK rifle"
msgid ""
"A rifle of the Cold War, or at least a dead ringer for it, this weapon is a "
"semi-automatic clone of the Soviet Union's standard assault rifle following "
"1974.  Either a locally-built replica or produced from an imported, foreign "
"parts kit, fitted with a fixed wooden buttstock, a side-mounted optics rail, "
"and a barrel threaded for suppressors, the rifle's chambered for the Russian "
"5.45x39mm cartridge and feeds from AK-74 magazines.  A Communist gun built in "
"Capitalist America; bar hoofing it to eastern Europe, the weapon's likely the "
"closest you'll ever get to laying your palms on a Russian Kalashnikov."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Russian AK rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Russian AK rifle"
msgid "Kalashnikov AKS-74"
msgid_plural "Kalashnikov AKS-74 rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Kalashnikov AKS-74"
msgstr[1] "fusils Kalashnikov AKS-74"
msgstr[2] "fusils Kalashnikov AKS-74"

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Description of variant "Russian AK rifle" of gun "Kalashnikov AKS-74"
#. ~ Description of variant "Kalashnikov AKS-74" of item "Russian AK rifle"
msgid ""
"An American copy of a Soviet assault rifle, a strange piece of ordinance "
"using some weird proprietary Russian ammunition—all these terms and more can "
"describe this rifle: a semi-automatic clone of the Kalashnikov AKS-74, the "
"descendant of the iconic AKM.  Either a locally-built replica or produced "
"from an imported, foreign parts kit, the firearm possesses a triangular, "
"folding buttstock, a side-mounted optics rail, and a threaded barrel for "
"attaching muzzle devices.  The weapon fires the Soviet 5.45x39mm cartridge—a "
"unicorn even in the American gun wilderness—and feeds said unicorn ammunition "
"from AK-74 magazines."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Kord AK rifle"
msgid_plural "Kord AK rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Kord AK"
msgstr[1] "fusils Kord AK"
msgstr[2] "fusils Kord AK"

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Kord AK rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Kord AK rifle" of gun "Kord 6P67 rifle"
#. ~ Description of "Kord AK rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Kord 6P67 rifle" of item "Kord AK rifle"
msgid ""
"A special forces Russian rifle chambered in 5.45.  This version uses standard "
"Picatinny rails, has modern lightweight furniture and a unique complex recoil "
"balance system for high fire rate with minimal recoil.  It combines the "
"reliability of the AK series with the high-velocity, lightweight 5.45x39mm "
"cartridge and accepts standard AK-74M magazines."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "Kord AK rifle"
#. ~ Variant name of item "Kord AK rifle"
msgid "Kord 6P67 rifle"
msgid_plural "Kord 6P67 rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusil Kord 6P67"
msgstr[1] "fusils Kord 6P67"
msgstr[2] "fusils Kord 6P67"

#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "FN 5.7mm pistol"
msgid_plural "FN 5.7mm pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet FN calibre 5.7mm"
msgstr[1] "pistolets FN calibre 5.7mm"
msgstr[2] "pistolets FN calibre 5.7mm"

#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
#. ~ Description of gun "FN 5.7mm pistol"
#. ~ Description of "FN 5.7mm pistol"
msgid ""
"Firing the armor-piercing 5.7x28mm round, this lightweight handgun was "
"developed for NATO use as a sidearm capable of penetrating body armor.  Its "
"proprietary and nonprolific ammunition kept it comparatively rare among both "
"civilian and militant use, but the gun's ability to ignore most forms of "
"conventional ballistic armor can't be argued with.  Given that its tiny "
"bullets have next to no stopping power, its armor-penetrating capability "
"comes at a considerable trade-off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "FN 5.7mm pistol"
#. ~ Variant name of item "FN 5.7mm pistol"
