#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "M9 combat pistol"
msgid_plural "M9 combat pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet de combat M9"
msgstr[1] "pistolets de combat M9"
msgstr[2] "pistolets de combat M9"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#. ~ Description of "M9 combat pistol"
msgid ""
"A rugged, iconic, and long-serving 9mm handgun, the M9 is a sleek pistol that "
"has enjoyed fame in military, law enforcement, and civilian circles ever "
"since its inception.  Adopted as the primary service sidearm across all "
"United States armed branches from the early eighties until the late two "
"thousand and tens, the weapon has seen a great deal of popular media coverage "
"in both video games and television alike."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#. ~ Variant name of item "M9 combat pistol"
msgid "Beretta M9A1 pistol"
msgid_plural "Beretta M9A1 pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet Beretta M9A1"
msgstr[1] "pistolets Beretta M9A1"
msgstr[2] "pistolets Beretta M9A1"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of variant "M9 combat pistol" of gun "Beretta M9A1 pistol"
#. ~ Description of variant "Beretta M9A1 pistol" of item "M9 combat pistol"
msgid ""
"An iconic 9x19mm pistol, the M9 was the standard issue sidearm of the US "
"armed forces from 1985 until only recently.  It was formerly popular among "
"law enforcement before the advent of commercially available polymer-framed "
"handguns and the FBI's adoption of .40 S&W."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Variant name of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#. ~ Variant name of item "M9 combat pistol"
msgid "Beretta 90-two pistol"
msgid_plural "Beretta 90-two pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet Beretta 90-two"
msgstr[1] "pistolets Beretta 90-two"
msgstr[2] "pistolets Beretta 90-two"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of variant "M9 combat pistol" of gun "Beretta 90-two pistol"
#. ~ Description of variant "Beretta 90-two pistol" of item "M9 combat pistol"
msgid ""
"A more modern version of Beretta's popular 92 series of handguns, the 90-two "
"performs largely the same.  The main difference is a sleeker, almost "
"futuristic-looking design owed in large part to the polymer underbarrel rail "
"cover."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "Beretta Px4 Storm pistol"
msgid_plural "Beretta Px4 Storm pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet Beretta Px4 Storm"
msgstr[1] "pistolets Beretta Px4 Storm"
msgstr[2] "pistolets Beretta Px4 Storm"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta Px4 Storm pistol"
#. ~ Description of "Beretta Px4 Storm pistol"
msgid ""
"Lighter than Beretta's iconic 92 series of guns, the Px4 Storm was built by "
"utilizing light-weight polymer construction with steel inserts.  Its shape "
"was also optimized for concealed carry, while maintaining the reliability "
"that the 92 series is known for."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "STEN Luty submachine gun"
msgid_plural "STEN Luty submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "pistolet mitrailleur Luty STEN"
msgstr[1] "pistolets mitrailleurs Luty STEN"
msgstr[2] "pistolets mitrailleurs Luty STEN"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of gun "STEN Luty submachine gun"
#. ~ Description of "STEN Luty submachine gun"
msgid ""
"A Luty pattern makeshift smoothbore SMG crudely constructed out of various "
"steel parts using advanced powered hand tools; likely one of the most complex "
"guns that is feasible to make outside of a machine shop, but still very "
"unreliable.  This one is chambered for 9x19mm cartridges and accepts "
"STEN-compatible magazines."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "STEN Mk II submachine gun"
msgid_plural "STEN Mk II submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "pistolet mitrailleur STEN Mk II"
msgstr[1] "pistolets mitrailleurs STEN Mk II"
msgstr[2] "pistolets mitrailleurs STEN Mk II"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of gun "STEN Mk II submachine gun"
#. ~ Description of "STEN Mk II submachine gun"
msgid ""
"The standard issue 9mm submachine gun of the British military throughout most "
"of the Second World War.  The STEN is aesthetically far from pretty.  "
"Featuring an iconic side mounted magazine well and a design optimized for "
"mass production using unskilled labor, the STEN was developed to make up for "
"drastic supply shortages during the early days of the war.  Likely entering "
"the US prior to the 1960s, either as a war time holdover or a museum "
"purchase; you suppose that if you were to try and defend your nation, "
"whatever the cost may be, and fight the undead 'on the beaches, fight on the "
"landing grounds, fight in the fields and in the streets, fight in the hills; "
"and never surrender', then it might be the time for the STEN to come back "
"into frontline service."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Name of a gun
msgid "TEC-9 pistol"
msgid_plural "TEC-9 pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistolet TEC-9"
msgstr[1] "pistolets TEC-9"
msgstr[2] "pistolets TEC-9"

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#. ~ Description of gun "TEC-9 pistol"
#. ~ Description of "TEC-9 pistol"
msgid ""
"The TEC-9 is a semi-automatic 'pistol' made of cheap polymers and machine "
"stamped parts.  Its rise in popularity among criminals is largely due to its "
"intimidating looks, low cost and relative ease of converting to fully "
"automatic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
