msgstr "Vous allumez l'écran."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "cellphone"
msgid "The cellphone's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "La batterie du téléphone a besoin de plus de charge."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cellphone - Flashlight"
msgid_plural "cellphones - Flashlight"
msgstr[0] "téléphone portable - Lampe de poche"
msgstr[1] "téléphones portables - Lampe de poche"
msgstr[2] "téléphones portables - Lampe de poche"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cellphone - Flashlight"
msgid "You turn off the screen."
msgstr "Vous éteignez l'écran."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "directional antenna"
msgid_plural "directional antennas"
msgstr[0] "antenne directionnelle"
msgstr[1] "antennes directionnelles"
msgstr[2] "antennes directionnelles"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "directional antenna"
msgid ""
"An antenna designed to pick up signals better when pointed at the source.  "
"You could use this with a radio to receive faint signals."
msgstr ""
"Antenne conçue pour mieux capter les signaux lorsqu'elle est orientée vers la "
"source. Vous pouvez l'utiliser avec une radio pour recevoir des signaux "
"faibles."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "electronic handcuffs"
msgid_plural "electronic handcuffs"
msgstr[0] "menottes électroniques (paire)"
msgstr[1] "menottes électroniques (paires)"
msgstr[2] "menottes électroniques (paires)"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "electronic handcuffs"
msgid ""
"A pair of electronic handcuffs, used by police and riot bots to detain "
"captives.  Their continuous siren clearly identifies the wearer as an "
"arrested criminal and alerts human police.  Wait for their arrival, don't try "
"to escape or to remove the cuffs - they will administer an electric shock.\n"
"However, since the only police likely to respond are undead, you may have a "
"long wait ahead, unless you get creative…"
msgstr ""
"Une paire de menottes électroniques, utilisées par la police et les robots "
"anti-émeutes pour détenir les captifs. Leur sirène continue identifie "
"clairement le porteur comme un criminel arrêté et alerte la police humaine. "
"Attendez leur arrivée, n'essayez pas de vous échapper ou d'enlever les "
"menottes - ils vous infligeront une décharge électrique.\n"
"Cependant, comme les seuls policiers susceptibles de répondre sont des "
"morts-vivants, l'attente risque d'être longue, à moins que vous ne fassiez "
"preuve d'imagination..."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid_plural "e-ink tablet PCs"
msgstr[0] "tablette E-Ink"
msgstr[1] "tablettes E-Ink"
msgstr[2] "tablettes E-Ink"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid ""
"A tablet PC using an efficient color e-ink display.  Before the Cataclysm, "
"these were nifty gadgets; now, they are extremely useful tools.  Runs on "
"conventional batteries."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid "Turn on the screen"
msgstr "Allumer l'écran"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid "You power up the screen."
msgstr "Vous allumez l'écran."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid "The tablet batteries are dead."
msgstr "Les batteries de la tablette sont vides."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
msgid_plural "e-ink tablet PCs (on)"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
msgid "Turn off the screen"
msgstr "Éteindre l'écran"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
msgid "You power down the screen."
msgstr "Vous éteignez l'écran."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "USB drive"
msgid "A USB thumb drive.  Useful for holding electronic data."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "older USB drive"
msgid_plural "older USB drives"
msgstr[0] "disque USB obsolète"
msgstr[1] "disques USB obsolètes"
msgstr[2] "disques USB obsolètes"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "older USB drive"
msgid ""
"A USB thumb drive.  Maybe a decade out of date, but still useful for holding "
"electronic data."
msgstr ""
"Une clé USB ayant probablement été fabriquée il y a plus de dix ans, mais "
"tout de même toujours utile pour contenir une certaine quantité de données."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "portable hard drive"
msgid_plural "portable hard drives"
msgstr[0] "disque dur portable"
msgstr[1] "disques durs portables"
msgstr[2] "disques durs portables"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "portable hard drive"
msgid ""
"A portable external hard drive, the best in affordable mass storage.  Useful "
"for holding lots of electronic data."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "memory card"
msgid "A memory card, can be used to store data."
msgstr "Une carte mémoire pouvant être utilisée pour stocker des données."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "older memory card"
msgid_plural "older memory cards"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "older memory card"
msgid ""
"A memory card.  Maybe a decade out of date, but can still be used to store "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "memory card (XEDRA)"
msgid_plural "memory cards (XEDRA)"
msgstr[0] "carte mémoire (XEDRA)"
msgstr[1] "cartes mémoire (XEDRA)"
msgstr[2] "cartes mémoire (XEDRA)"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "memory card (XEDRA)"
msgid ""
"A memory card, can be used to store data.  This one has a label on which is "
"written 'XEDRA' followed by a long string of numbers."
msgstr ""
"Une carte mémoire pouvant être utilisée pour stocker des données. Celle-ci a "
"un label collé dessus sur lequel est écrit \"XEDRA\" suivi d'une longue série "
"de chiffres."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "electrohack"
msgid_plural "electrohacks"
msgstr[0] "électrohack"
msgstr[1] "électrohacks"
msgstr[2] "électrohacks"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "electrohack"
msgid ""
"This device has many ports attached, allowing it to connect to almost any "
"control panel or other electronic machine (but not computers).  With a little "
"skill, it can be used to crack passwords and more."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Geiger counter (off)"
msgid_plural "Geiger counters (off)"
msgstr[0] "compteur Geiger (éteint)"
msgstr[1] "compteurs Geiger (éteints)"
msgstr[2] "compteurs Geiger (éteints)"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "Geiger counter (off)"
msgid ""
"A tool for measuring radiation.  Using it will prompt you to choose whether "
"to scan yourself or the terrain, or to turn on continuous scan, which will "
"provide continuous feedback on ambient radiation.  It is currently off."
msgstr ""
"Outil de mesure des radiations. En l'utilisant, vous devrez choisir de vous "
"scanner ou de scanner le terrain, ou d'activer le balayage continu, ce qui "
"vous permettra d'obtenir des informations en continu sur les radiations "
"ambiantes. Il est actuellement désactivé."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Geiger counter (on)"
msgid_plural "Geiger counters (on)"
msgstr[0] "compteur Geiger (allumé)"
msgstr[1] "compteurs Geiger (allumés)"
msgstr[2] "compteurs Geiger (allumés)"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "Geiger counter (on)"
msgid ""
"A tool for measuring radiation.  It is in continuous scan mode, and will "
"produce quiet clicking sounds in the presence of ambient radiation.  Using it "
"allows you to turn it off, or scan yourself or the ground."
msgstr ""
"Outil de mesure des rayonnements. Il est en mode de balayage continu et "
"produit des cliquetis silencieux en présence de radiations ambiantes. Son "
"utilisation vous permet de l'éteindre ou de vous scanner vous-même ou le sol."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "Geiger counter (on)"
msgid "The Geiger counter's SCANNING LED turns off."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Otherworldly measuring device"
msgid_plural "Otherworldly measuring devices"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "Otherworldly measuring device"
msgid ""
"This strange contraption appears to be little more than a laminated box built "
"around a battery, a poorly backlit screen, and a wound spool of cloth "
"netting.  The letters \"X E D R A\" are emblazoned on the side.  To operate "
"the device, unfurl the netting and place it around the object to analyze.  "
"Despite not appearing to do anything, it consumes an enormous amount of "
"electricity and provides a brief numerical readout."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "NRE recorder"
msgid_plural "NRE recorders"
msgstr[0] "enregistreur NRE"
msgstr[1] "enregistreurs NRE"
msgstr[2] "enregistreurs NRE"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "NRE recorder"
msgid ""
"A strange apparatus, seemingly consisting of a glass-encased microphone "
"linked to a small thermal printer and digital screen.  The screen remains "
"perpetually blank, save for a battery indicator on its upper right, and on "
"its left side lies a single red button: \"PRINT DATA\"."
msgstr ""
"Un appareil étrange, apparemment constitué d'un microphone en verre relié à "
"une petite imprimante thermique et à un écran numérique. L'écran reste "
"perpétuellement vide, à l'exception d'un indicateur de batterie en haut à "
"droite, et sur le côté gauche se trouve un seul bouton rouge : \"PRINT DATA\"."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ "description" action message of item "NRE recorder"
msgid "Activate the recorder's printer."
msgstr "Activer l'imprimante de l'enregistreur."

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hand-crank charger"
msgid_plural "hand-crank chargers"
msgstr[0] "chargeur dynamo"
msgstr[1] "chargeurs dynamo"
msgstr[2] "chargeurs dynamo"

#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#. ~ Description of "hand-crank charger"
msgid ""
"A hand-powered battery charger.  It has an adjustable receptacle designed to "
"accept a wide variety of rechargeable battery cells."
msgstr ""
"Chargeur de batterie manuel. Il est doté d'une prise réglable conçue pour "
"accepter une grande variété de piles rechargeables."

