#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "paring knife" of item "small kitchen knife"
msgid ""
"A short-bladed knife with a sharp blade, made for fine controlled cuts to "
"vegetables without using a cutting board."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "large kitchen knife"
msgid_plural "large kitchen knives"
msgstr[0] "gros couteau de cuisine"
msgstr[1] "gros couteaux de cuisine"
msgstr[2] "gros couteaux de cuisine"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid "chef knife"
msgid_plural "chef knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de chef"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de chef"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de chef"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "chef knife" of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife.  The blade is wider than the handle, giving room "
"for the wielder's knuckles, and it has a characteristic curve for a fast "
"rocking action for chopping vegetables.  It makes an acceptable melee weapon, "
"but the wide blade is unwieldy for butchering."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid "carving knife"
msgid_plural "carving knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau à découper"
msgstr[1] "couteaux à découper"
msgstr[2] "couteaux à découper"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "carving knife" of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife with a thin, slightly curved blade for deftly "
"slicing meat either in flat sheets or around the bone.  It makes a decent "
"melee weapon, and is excellent for butchery."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid "bread knife"
msgid_plural "bread knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau à pain"
msgstr[1] "couteaux à pain"
msgstr[2] "couteaux à pain"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "bread knife" of item "large kitchen knife"
msgid ""
"This knife has quite a long blade with a scalloped edge for cutting bread.  "
"It's not that sharp, but its length and heft mean it could do a bit of damage "
"and cause some nasty tearing."
msgstr ""
"Ce couteau a une lame assez longue avec un tranchant dentelé pour couper le "
"pain. Elle n'est pas très tranchante, mais sa longueur et son poids lui "
"permettent de faire quelques dégâts et de provoquer de vilaines déchirures."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "huge kitchen knife"
msgid_plural "huge kitchen knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de cuisine énorme"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de cuisine énormes"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de cuisine énormes"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "huge kitchen knife"
msgid "butcher knife"
msgid_plural "butcher knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de boucher"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de boucher"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de boucher"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "butcher knife" of item "huge kitchen knife"
msgid ""
"A sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal item for "
"butchering corpses."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "cleaver"
msgid_plural "cleavers"
msgstr[0] "hachoir"
msgstr[1] "hachoirs"
msgstr[2] "hachoirs"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "cleaver"
msgid "meat cleaver"
msgid_plural "meat cleavers"
msgstr[0] "hachoir à viande"
msgstr[1] "hachoirs à viande"
msgstr[2] "hachoirs à viande"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "meat cleaver" of item "cleaver"
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square-shaped blade.  Its heft and "
"sharpness would make it a very effective melee weapon and an excellent "
"butchering tool."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau à l'allure menacante et à la pointe tronquée. Son poids et son "
"tranchant en font à la fois une arme redoutable et un outil de boucherie "
"efficace."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Variant name of item "cleaver"
msgid "vegetable cleaver"
msgid_plural "vegetable cleavers"
msgstr[0] "hachoir à légumes"
msgstr[1] "hachoirs à légumes"
msgstr[2] "hachoirs à légumes"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of variant "vegetable cleaver" of item "cleaver"
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square shaped blade, curved for fast "
"vegetable chopping.  Its heft and sharpness make it a decent weapon as well, "
"although not as good as a meat cleaver."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau à l'allure menaçante avec une large lame courbée ayant une pointe "
"tronquée conçue pour couper rapidement les légumes. Son poids et son "
"tranchant en font également une arme décente, mais moins efficace qu'un "
"hachoir à viande."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "copper knife"
msgid_plural "copper knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en cuivre"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en cuivre"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en cuivre"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "copper knife"
msgid ""
"A knife made of crudely-worked copper with a simple handle.  Primitive, but a "
"step above stone-age."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau en cuivre rudimentaire doté d'une garde. Un outil primitif, mais "
"meilleur qu'un outil néolithique."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze knife"
msgid_plural "bronze knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en bronze"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en bronze"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en bronze"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze knife"
msgid ""
"A cast bronze knife with a full tang, with a handle wrapped in cord and "
"leather, lovingly work-hardened and sharpened to a fine edge."
msgstr ""
"Un couteau en bronze forgé, équipé d'une poignée enrobée de cuir et de corde "
"et doté d'une lame affutée laborieusement."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "dive knife"
msgid_plural "dive knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de plongée"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de plongée"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de plongée"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "dive knife"
msgid ""
"A short, sturdy knife with a serrated edge for cutting lines and straps, and "
"a blunt tip for prying.  Used primarily by divers, this knife has been fitted "
"with cork to slow its descent if dropped underwater, so it takes up more "
"space than usual."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau solide dotée d'une lame dentelée utilisée pour couper à "
"travers des cordages ou des lignes de cable, sa pointe étant arrondie et "
"renforcée pour être utilisée comme outil de forçage. Principalement utilisé "
"par les plongeurs, un flotteur est attaché pour l'empécher de couler trop "
"vite lorsqu'il est lâché, le rendant un peu plus encombrant qu'attendu."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "honey scraper"
msgid_plural "honey scrapers"
msgstr[0] "grattoir à miel"
msgstr[1] "grattoirs à miel"
msgstr[2] "grattoirs à miel"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "honey scraper"
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used for harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un outil ressemblant à un couteau utilisé pour gratter le miel de morceaux de "
"ruche. Bien qu'il ne soit pas conçu pour, il peut être décemment utile comme "
"arme."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "pocket knife"
msgid_plural "pocket knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau de poche"
msgstr[1] "couteaux de poche"
msgstr[2] "couteaux de poche"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "pocket knife"
msgid ""
"A small pocket knife.  It isn't great for combat, but it's better than "
"nothing.  It's sharp enough to butcher with."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau de poche. ce n'est pas génial pour se battre avec, mais "
"c'est mieux que rien. Il est assez pointu pour vous aider à dépecer des corps."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone knife"
msgid_plural "stone knives"
msgstr[0] "couteau en pierre"
msgstr[1] "couteaux en pierre"
msgstr[2] "couteaux en pierre"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "stone knife"
msgid ""
"A sharpened stone set into a hollowed handle.  Not nearly as usable as a "
"proper knife, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "boxcutter knife"
msgid_plural "boxcutter knives"
msgstr[0] "cutter"
msgstr[1] "cutters"
msgstr[2] "cutters"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "boxcutter knife"
msgid ""
"A small knife designed for opening boxes.  It could cause some damage, but it "
"really should be used against inanimate objects.  It is too small to "
"effectively butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"Un petit couteau repliable, communément utilisé pour ouvrir des boites en "
"cartons. Bien que cet outil soit capable de blesser assez bien quelques "
"ennemis, il serait probablement une meilleure idée d'utiliser sa lame "
"uniquement contre des objets inanimés dû à sa petite taille et à sa "
"fragilité. La lame est trop courte pour être utilisée comme outil de "
"boucherie."

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone chopper"
msgid_plural "stone choppers"
msgstr[0] "hachoir en pierre"
msgstr[1] "hachoirs en pierre"
msgstr[2] "hachoirs en pierre"

#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
#. ~ Description of "stone chopper"
msgid ""
"A rock with sharpened edges, produced by knapping.  Works as a crude cutting "
"and butchering tool, if nothing else is available."
msgstr ""
"Une pierre dotée de bords pointus produits par taillage. Peut servir comme un "
"outil rudimentaire de boucherie ou pour couper quelque chose si vous n'avez "
"rien de mieux."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/weapon_copy_extensions.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "digging stick"
msgid_plural "digging sticks"
msgstr[0] "bâton-pelle"
msgstr[1] "bâton-pelles"
msgstr[2] "bâton-pelles"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "digging stick"
msgid ""
"A large stick with the end carved into a broad blade for digging.  It could "
"be used to dig shallow pits, but not deep ones."
msgstr ""
"Un gros bâton, la pointe ayant été taillée en une surface plate pour "
"rudimentairement imiter une pelle. Vous pourriez l'utiliser pour creuser un "
"trou peu profond mais pas plus."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "trowel"
msgid_plural "trowels"
msgstr[0] "déplantoir"
msgstr[1] "déplantoirs"
msgstr[2] "déplantoirs"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "trowel"
msgid "A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."
msgstr "Une petite pelle de jardinage, parfaite pour déterrer les larves et les vers."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "hoe"
msgid_plural "hoes"
msgstr[0] "houe"
msgstr[1] "houes"
msgstr[2] "houes"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "hoe"
msgid ""
"A farming implement.  You can use it to turn tillable land into a "
"slow-to-cross pile of dirt, or dig a shallow pit."
msgstr ""
"Un outil de jardinage. Vous pouvez l'utiliser pour créer un monticule de "
"terre ou un fossé peu profond à partir d'un terrain labourable."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze hoe"
msgid_plural "bronze hoes"
msgstr[0] "houe en bronze"
msgstr[1] "houes en bronze"
msgstr[2] "houes en bronze"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze hoe"
msgid ""
"A farming implement made from bronze.  The added heft and durability should "
"let you till soil for farming more easily as well."
msgstr ""
"Un outil de jardinage en bronze. Le poids additionnel de la tête comparément "
"à l'acier devrait rendre son utilisation pour labourer plus facile."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "wooden shovel"
msgid_plural "wooden shovels"
msgstr[0] "pelle en bois"
msgstr[1] "pelles en bois"
msgstr[2] "pelles en bois"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "wooden shovel"
msgid ""
"A crude shovel with a shovelhead made from wood, historically used as an "
"alternative to metal shovels when metal was too expensive.  It works passably "
"well, but really can't compare to a metal shovel."
msgstr ""
"Une pelle rudimentaire ayant une tête en bois, historiquement utilisée comme "
"alternative aux pelles en métal lors ce que celles-ci était trop chères. Bien "
"qu'elle soit décente pour creuser, une vraie pelle en métal serait préférable."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "metal rake"
msgid_plural "metal rakes"
msgstr[0] "râteau en métal"
msgstr[1] "râteaux en métal"
msgstr[2] "râteaux en métal"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "metal rake"
msgid "A sturdy metal rake, a must-have during autumn."
msgstr "Un râteau à feuilles solide en métal, un outil essentiel pour l'automne."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic rake"
msgid_plural "plastic rakes"
msgstr[0] "râteau en plastique"
msgstr[1] "râteaux en plastique"
msgstr[2] "râteaux en plastique"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic rake"
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic rake.  Will break quite quickly if used for anything other "
"than raking leaves."
msgstr ""
"Un râteau à feuilles bon marché en plastique. Il se cassera très vite si vous "
"décidez de l'utiliser pour quoi que ce soit d'autre que ramasser des feuilles."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "scythe"
msgid_plural "scythes"
msgstr[0] "faux"
msgstr[1] "faux"
msgstr[2] "faux"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "scythe"
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned farming tool used to cut tall grass.  Despite being a giant "
"blade on the end of a stick, it is incredibly awkward to use for anything but "
"its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Un vieil outil de moisson ou de désherbage. Bien que cet outil soit juste une "
"lame géante légèrement courbée attachée à un bâton, l'utiliser comme arme est "
"assez difficile."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "scythe"
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply-made replica of an old-fashioned farming tool used to cut "
"tall grass."
msgstr "Une réplique bon marché et émoussée d'un vieil outil de moissonnage."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_melee.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "grim reaper's scythe"
msgid_plural "grim reaper's scythes"
msgstr[0] "faux de la Faucheuse"
msgstr[1] "faux de la Faucheuse"
msgstr[2] "faux de la Faucheuse"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "grim reaper's scythe"
msgid ""
"A long, crooked tool used to reap souls, with a skull engraved in its blade.  "
"Let the harvest begin."
msgstr ""
"Un long outil avec un crâne engravé sur sa lame servant à faucher des âmes. "
"Que la moisson commence."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "shovel"
msgid_plural "shovels"
msgstr[0] "pelle"
msgstr[1] "pelles"
msgstr[2] "pelles"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "shovel"
msgid "A digging tool.  Use it to dig pits adjacent to your location."
msgstr ""
"Une pelle solide conçue pour creuser. Utilisez-la pour creuser un trou sur "
"l'une des cases adjacentes."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "snow shovel"
msgid_plural "snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pelle à neige"
msgstr[1] "pelles à neige"
msgstr[2] "pelles à neige"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "snow shovel"
msgid ""
"A sturdy metal shovel used for picking up snow and moving it somewhere else.  "
"It was useful before the Cataclysm, but now it's useless."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "plastic snow shovel"
msgid_plural "plastic snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pelle à neige en plastique"
msgstr[1] "pelles à neige en plastique"
msgstr[2] "pelles à neige en plastique"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "plastic snow shovel"
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic shovel used for picking up snow and moving it somewhere else. "
" It was useful before the Cataclysm, but now it's useless."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "stone sickle"
msgid_plural "stone sickles"
msgstr[0] "faucille en pierre"
msgstr[1] "faucilles en pierre"
msgstr[2] "faucilles en pierre"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "stone sickle"
msgid ""
"A primitive tool for cutting grass.  The sharp, crescent-shaped stone at the "
"end of the handle is barely good enough for the job."
msgstr ""
"Un outil primitif capable de moissonner ou désherber. La pierre affutée en "
"forme de croissant de lune affixée sur la poignée est à peine suffisante pour "
"remplir cette fonction."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json data/mods/MMA/swords_and_blades.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "sickle"
msgid_plural "sickles"
msgstr[0] "faucille"
msgstr[1] "faucilles"
msgstr[2] "faucilles"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "sickle"
msgid ""
"An old-fashioned farming tool for cutting tall grass.  Despite being a "
"massive curved blade on a handle, it is incredibly awkward to use for "
"anything but its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Un vieil outil de moisson ou de désherbage. Bien que cet outil est simplement "
"une lourde lame courbée attachée à une poignée, l'utiliser comme arme est "
"assez difficile."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bronze sickle"
msgid_plural "bronze sickles"
msgstr[0] "faucille en bronze"
msgstr[1] "faucilles en bronze"
msgstr[2] "faucilles en bronze"

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bronze sickle"
msgid ""
"A handheld grass-cutting tool with a cast bronze blade, fastened to a wood "
"handle wrapped with leather."
msgstr ""
"Un outil de moissonnage ou de désherbage possédant une lame en bronze forgé "
"attachée à une poignée enroulée de cuir."

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "bill"
msgid_plural "bills"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#. ~ Description of "bill"
msgid ""
"A long, slightly curved and hooked steel blade on the end of a sturdy shaft.  "
"Could be used to thoroughly ruin something's day, or cut branches and small "
"trees."
msgstr ""
