msgid "What do you see in your visions?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que vous voyez durant vos visions?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I must be seeing things again!  Stay away from me!"
msgstr "Je dois être en train de voir des choses encore!  Restez loin de moi!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "* eyes you menacingly with a scowl on his face.  \"What do you want?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi, <name_g>.  It's good to see you again."
msgstr "Salut <name_g>.  Content de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi, <name_g>.  Could I pat you on the shoulder?  I wanna be sure you're here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi, <name_g>.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut <name_g>.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you alright?"
msgstr "Vous allez bien?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Arturo, how are ya?"
msgstr "Salut Arturo, comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing, I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's alright, just take your time."
msgstr "Ce n'est pas grave, prenez votre temps."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What's hangin'?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've had a bad run of things.  I grew up real poor, in a bad part of town, "
"always got my nose where it shouldn't have been.  When I was about eighteen, "
"I started doing coke heavily.  Every two days, I'd get spaced out on the "
"stuff; started robbing gas stations and dumb <freaking> things like that for "
"a fix.  I went to jail, and I met the New England Church Community there.  I "
"joined up to find penance for my sins.  Another thing, stay off of that "
"<freaking> stuff; I messed up my brain real bad doin' that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They're not so hot.  The whole compound is always low on food, there's "
"<freaking> <zombies> out on the roads, and Helena's starting to panic a bit.  "
"She thinks I'm a holy visionary, with my episodes…  Sometimes I want to "
"believe her.  I usually take the Thorazine Jane has, but I've been getting it "
"less and less."
msgstr ""
"Tout ne ce passe pas exactement bien.  La communauté et constamment à court "
"de nourriture, il y a des <freaking><zombies> rôdant sur les routes, et "
"Helena commence à paniquer un peu.  Elle pense que je suis une sorte de "
"voyant sacré, avec mes épisodes…  De temps en temps je veux y croire aussi, "
"mais la plupart du temps je prends tout de même la chlorpromazine que Jane me "
"donne, mais il y en a de moins en moins."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, its an old church group that decided to become doomsday preppers.  I "
"don't know much else, except that they used to do a lot of charity work.  I "
"met them that way."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, c'est un vieux groupe d'église qui a décidé de se préparer à "
"l'apocalypse. Je ne sais pas grand-chose d'autre, sauf qu'ils faisaient "
"beaucoup de travail caritatif. Je les ai rencontrés de cette façon."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nah.  Not everything's perfect around here, but it's the only thing I've got "
"left."
msgstr "Non. Tout n'est pas parfait ici, mais c'est la seule chose qui me reste."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Arturo stares blankly for a moment.  \"The man in the mirror comes to me at "
"night, and whispers things in my ear.  Eyes on the walls, watching, watching… "
" The woman who crawls.\"  I'm sorry about that."
msgstr ""
"&Arturo regarde fixement pendant un moment. « L'homme dans le miroir vient à "
"moi la nuit et me murmure des choses à l'oreille. Les yeux sur les murs, "
"observant, observant... La femme qui rampe. » Je suis désolé pour ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Chill out man, I'm leaving."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&\"I'd be a lot better if you'd go away, I'm not up for talking right now.\"  "
"Arturo turns back his activities, ignoring you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Arturo_Maldonado.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine then, <name_b>, I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's it like living here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How've things been since <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you knit at all?  I noticed you have sewing needles."
msgstr "Vous tricotez? J'ai remarqué que vous aviez des aiguilles."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I have no interest in dealing with you, unnatural abomination.  Keep away "
"from me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What are you doing around here?  I don't want to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Theresa looks up from her knitting, with a sparkle in her eyes.  \"Come on "
"in, <granny_name_g>.  I'm glad to see you again, have a seat.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Praise the Lord.  It's good to see you're still around, <granny_name_g>."
msgstr "Dieu soit loué. C'est bon de vous voir <granny_name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome, <granny_name_g>.  I don't think I recognize you, I'm Theresa."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Theresa.  I'm <u_name>."
msgstr "Un plaisir de vous rencontrer Theresa.  Je m'appelle <u_name>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello, Theresa.  How are you doing?"
msgstr "Salut Theresa. Comment allez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the insults for?"
msgstr "A quoi servent les insultes?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck you then, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Allez-vous faire foutre de ce cas-là, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It is nice to meet you as well.  I reckon you got some questions about our "
"group."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just fine.  Nice of you to ask.  How's it going, <granny_name_g>?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm doing as well as can be expected.  How's everything, <granny_name_g>?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here about the scarf."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour l'écharpe."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here about the blanket."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour la couette."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here about the quilt."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour l'édredon."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're doing better than most, to put it mildly.  There's a reason for that, "
"as for everything.  Say, have I told you about my husband?  I'm sorry if I "
"already have, my memory's not what it used to be."
msgstr ""
"Nous nous en sortons mieux que la plupart, c'est le moins qu'on puisse dire. "
"Il y a une raison à cela, comme à tout. Dites, est-ce que je vous ai parlé de "
"mon mari ? Je suis désolée si je l'ai déjà fait, ma mémoire n'est plus ce "
"qu'elle était."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your husband."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de votre mari."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He was an exceptional man.  Ever since he was a child it was clear that there "
"was something special about him.  My husband had a way with people, and with "
"God too.  But, after all he was as human as you and I.  He was corrupted by "
"addiction.  One day, God appeared to him in a vision that turned his life "
"around, he had other plans for him.  From then on he didn't take his life for "
"granted.  He used his talent and newfound inspiration to better the people "
"around him."
msgstr ""
"C'était un homme exceptionnel. Depuis son enfance, il était évident qu'il "
"avait quelque chose de spécial. Mon mari avait un don pour les gens, et aussi "
"pour Dieu. Mais, après tout, il était aussi humain que vous et moi. Il était "
"corrompu par la dépendance. Un jour, Dieu lui est apparu dans une vision qui "
"a changé sa vie, il avait d'autres projets pour lui. Dès lors, il n'a plus "
"pris sa vie pour acquise. Il a utilisé son talent et sa nouvelle inspiration "
"pour améliorer les gens qui l'entouraient."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, he founded the community?"
msgstr "Alors, il a fondé la communauté?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about his visions."
msgstr "Dites-moi en plus au sujet de ses visions."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's right.  He wanted something to return for the guidance he received "
"when he was at the lowest point of his life.  He created a charity group "
"which, over the years, became what's now known as the New England Church "
"Community.  He lead them for many decades, until his death a few years before "
"his prophecy was fulfilled.  Now, our niece Helena leads the community."
msgstr ""
"Tout à fait.  Il voulait quelque chose en retour des conseils qu'il avait "
"reçus alors qu'il était au plus bas dans sa vie.  Il a créé un groupe "
"caritatif qui, au fil des ans, est devenu ce que l'on appelle aujourd'hui la "
"Communauté Chrétienne de Nouvelle Angleterre.  Il les a dirigés pendant "
"plusieurs décennies, jusqu'à sa mort, quelques années avant que sa prophétie "
"ne s'accomplisse.  Aujourd'hui, c'est notre nièce Helena qui dirige la "
"communauté."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He was a man of many secrets.  It would've been too personal to share, I'm "
"afraid.  On the other hand, there was a prophecy he was quite vocal about.  "
"In a way, he predicted <the_cataclysm> long before the first warning signs "
"appeared.  Thanks to him, we had the foresight to prepare.  Oh what a great "
"man he was…"
msgstr ""
"C'était un homme aux nombreux secrets. J'aurais eu peur de le partager avec "
"vous, mais il y avait une prophétie dont il parlait très ouvertement. D'une "
"certaine manière, il avait prédit <the_cataclysm> bien avant que les premiers "
"signes avant-coureurs n'apparaissent. Grâce à lui, nous avons eu la "
"clairvoyance de nous préparer. Oh, quel grand homme il était..."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh you don't have the time for that, do you now?  It's a long, long tale, "
"thank goodness.  I'm grateful, for I was blessed with a full life."
msgstr ""
"Oh, tu n'as pas le temps pour ça, n'est-ce pas ? C'est une longue, longue "
"histoire, Dieu merci. Je suis reconnaissante, car j'ai eu la chance d'avoir "
"une vie bien remplie."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's very sweet of you <granny_name_g>, but there's nothing I could "
"possibly want from this mortal world.  My life is now complete, I believe."
msgstr ""
"C'est très gentil de ta part <granny_name_g>, mais je ne peux rien désirer de "
"ce monde mortel. Ma vie est maintenant complète, je crois."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, I knit and sew in my spare time.  Its' helped keep my hands in good "
"shape over the years."
msgstr ""
"Oui, je tricote et je couds pendant mon temps libre. Cela m'a aidé à garder "
"mes mains en bonne forme au fil des ans."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you make something for me?"
msgstr "Est-ce que vous pourriez fabriquer quelque chose pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I suppose I could, in exchange for a few icons.  A scarf is five, a blanket "
"ten, a quilt thirty."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que je pourrais, en échange de quelques icônes. Une écharpe coûte "
"cinq, une couverture dix, une courtepointe trente."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a scarf."
msgstr "Je voudrais une écharpe."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a blanket."
msgstr "Je voudrais une couette."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a quilt."
msgstr "Je voudrais un édredon."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How long does it take you to make these?"
msgstr "Combien de temps vous faut-il pour les faire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've changed my mind.  How're you feeling?"
msgstr "J'ai changé d'avis. Comment te sens-tu ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_nevermind>  <end_talking_later>"
msgstr "<end_talking_nevermind>  <end_talking_later>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can knit a scarf ready by tomorrow, a blanket in two days, and a quilt in a "
"week."
msgstr ""
"Je peux tricoter une écharpe prête pour demain, une couverture en deux jours "
"et une courtepointe en une semaine."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hope you like it <granny_name_g>.  If you want anything else, just come "
"back."
msgstr ""
"J'espère que ça vous plaira <granny_name_g>. Si vous voulez autre chose, "
"revenez."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you, Theresa.  I'll put it to good use."
msgstr "Merci, Thérèsa. J'en ferai bon usage."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've grown tired, <granny_name_g>.  I haven't left here since we came, and "
"things outside are getting worse each day.  All my old aches and pains have "
"come back too; I can't see too good, and my muscles are always sore.  I don't "
"like where my niece is going either; she's ever more fanatical, and taking my "
"dear husband's prophecy to the extreme.  I'm content with my life, though.  "
"I've lived long and prospered by the grace of the Lord."
msgstr ""
"Je suis fatiguée, <granny_name_g>. Je ne suis pas sortie d'ici depuis notre "
"arrivée et les choses à l'extérieur empirent de jour en jour. Toutes mes "
"anciennes douleurs sont revenues ; je ne vois pas très bien et mes muscles "
"sont toujours endoloris. Je n'aime pas non plus où va ma nièce ; elle est de "
"plus en plus fanatique et pousse à l'extrême la prophétie de mon cher mari. "
"Je suis cependant satisfaite de ma vie. J'ai vécu longtemps et j'ai prospéré "
"par la grâce du Seigneur."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help?"
msgstr "Puis-je faire quelque chose pour aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You clearly have the mark of a sinner.  I've seen your kind out and about "
"after the Flood, killing and maiming like wild animals.  None of you are any "
"good, not even to God, and you're of no good to me either.  Run on back to "
"your sinful ways, now.  God has judged you already."
msgstr ""
"Vous portez clairement la marque d'un pécheur. J'ai vu des gens de votre "
"espèce errer après le déluge, tuant et mutilant comme des animaux sauvages. "
"Aucun d'entre vous n'est bon, pas même pour Dieu, et vous ne m'êtes d'aucune "
"utilité non plus. Retournez à vos mauvaises habitudes, maintenant. Dieu vous "
"a déjà jugés."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Aunt_Theresa.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You've done me poorly enough times now, I won't have any more of it.  Get out "
"of here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What are you doing here, go away!  I don't want to talk to you…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aw hey, it's you again, <u_name>.  How have you been?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aw hey, it's you again, <name_g>.  How have you been?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <u_name>, what's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <name_g>, what's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh… hi.  I don't know you.  My name's Chloe."
msgstr "Oh… salut.  Je ne vous connais pas.  Je m'appelle Chloé."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Chloe.  What's up?"
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer, Chloé."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Bonjour.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you wanna shoot the breeze?"
msgstr "Tu veux discuter ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just saying hello.  Keep safe."
msgstr "Je ne fait que dire bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay <name_b>, I'll leave."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Shoot."
msgstr "Tirer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Really, what's your story?"
msgstr "Sérieusement, quelle est ton histoire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How'd you and Sonia come to meet?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce que vous et Sonia se sont rencontrées?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How'd you and Sonia come to meet again?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce que vous et Sonia se sont rencontrées déjà?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Aren't you a bit young to be carrying a knife?"
msgstr "Vous n'êtes pas un peu jeune pour porter un couteau sur vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second though, let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Après réflexion, parlons d'autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things suck right now, but you know that anyway.  I don't even know why you "
"bother asking these stupid questions."
msgstr ""
"Les choses vont mal en ce moment, mais tu le sais déjà. Je ne sais même pas "
"pourquoi tu prends la peine de poser ces questions stupides."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm not a baby you know, I don't need a babysitter.  Sonia looks out for me "
"though.  She's not so weird, I guess.  She promised to give me guitar lessons "
"and she even signed me an autograph.  I know she's only nice to me because I "
"saved her, but that's okay; we're equal now."
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis pas un bébé, tu sais, je n'ai pas besoin d'une baby-sitter. Mais "
"Sonia veille sur moi. Elle n'est pas si bizarre, je suppose. Elle a promis de "
"me donner des cours de guitare et m'a même signé un autographe. Je sais "
"qu'elle est gentille avec moi uniquement parce que je l'ai sauvée, mais ce "
"n'est pas grave, nous sommes égales maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, that's enough for me."
msgstr "Ouais, ça me suffit."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Mes condoléances. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I grew up in the city.  My parents were always out of town on some "
"business meeting or another, so I had plenty of time to myself.  They're "
"great people; mom's a wonderful cook, she makes an amazing fish casserole.  "
"Dad's a hot shot for military contracts, he handled business deals for DARPA "
"and whatnot.  He's an ex-marine, and taught me how to defend myself with a "
"knife."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, j'ai grandi en ville. Mes parents étaient toujours en déplacement "
"professionnel, donc j'avais beaucoup de temps pour moi. Ce sont des gens "
"formidables ; ma mère est une cuisinière formidable, elle fait un excellent "
"ragoût de poisson. Mon père est un expert des contrats militaires, il a géré "
"des affaires pour la DARPA et d'autres choses du genre. C'est un ancien "
"marine, et il m'a appris à me défendre avec un couteau."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where do you think your parents are now?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que vous pensez que vos parents sont maintenant?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was home alone during the ongoing riots.  My parents chose the worst "
"possible time to reconnect, which sucks, but I'm also kinda happy for them.  "
"Anyway, they were part of the NECC people, so they knew about this place and "
"their plans and all.  Thing is, it was, like, really far away.  I kinda "
"didn't want to go alone but I also didn't want the rioters to eat me, so I "
"asked Sonia - my neighbor - to evacuate with me, I guess.  So that was fun; "
"escaping my hometown, walking down the country road, waiting for a horror to "
"ambush us.  Spoiler alert: we were attacked.  So this zombie shambles in "
"front of us and Sonia whacks it real hard with her guitar!  Its brain "
"splatters all over the pavement, I threw up 'cause it was so disgusting.  We "
"got here soon after that.  My parents weren't here, obviously.  Oh man, they "
"must worry about me so much…"
msgstr ""
"J'étais seul à la maison pendant les émeutes. Mes parents ont choisi le pire "
"moment possible pour reprendre contact, ce qui est nul, mais je suis aussi "
"plutôt content pour eux. Quoi qu'il en soit, ils faisaient partie des gens du "
"NECC, donc ils étaient au courant de cet endroit et de leurs plans et tout. "
"Le truc, c'est que c'était vraiment très loin. Je ne voulais pas y aller "
"seul, mais je ne voulais pas non plus que les émeutiers me dévorent, alors "
"j'ai demandé à Sonia - ma voisine - d'évacuer avec moi, je suppose. Donc "
"c'était amusant ; m'échapper de ma ville natale, marcher sur la route de "
"campagne, attendre qu'une horreur nous tende une embuscade. Alerte spoiler : "
"nous avons été attaqués. Alors ce zombie se traîne devant nous et Sonia le "
"frappe très fort avec sa guitare ! Son cerveau éclabousse partout sur le "
"trottoir, j'ai vomi parce que c'était tellement dégoûtant. Nous sommes "
"arrivés ici peu de temps après. Mes parents n'étaient pas là, évidemment. Oh "
"mon Dieu, ils doivent tellement s'inquiéter pour moi..."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the info.  Let's chat about something else."
msgstr "Merci pour l'information. Parlons d'autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the info."
msgstr "Merci pour l'information."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know.  They were going to a contract deal before the riots broke out, "
"at one of military bases I think.  I don't know what happened to them from "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas. Ils étaient sur le point de conclure un accord avant que les "
"émeutes n'éclatent, sur une base militaire, je crois. Je ne sais pas ce qui "
"leur est arrivé après cela."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll let you know if anything turns up."
msgstr "Je vous ferait savoir si il y a quelque chose de nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll let you know if anything turns up.  See you around."
msgstr "Je te ferai savoir si quelque chose se présente. À bientôt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aren't you a bit too old not to realize how dangerous the world is for a kid "
"like me?  I know how to handle one without hurting myself!  My dad taught me "
"everything, he's a real pro."
msgstr ""
"Tu n'es pas un peu trop vieux pour ne pas te rendre compte à quel point le "
"monde est dangereux pour un enfant comme moi ? Je sais comment m'en sortir "
"sans me faire mal ! Mon père m'a tout appris, c'est un vrai pro."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That makes sense."
msgstr "C'est logique."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "They're not dead."
msgstr "Ils ne sont pas morts."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I don't wanna talk about it right now."
msgstr "Je ne veux pas vraiment en parler là maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, let's change the subject."
msgstr "Changeons de sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I said to get lost, <name_b>!  I can't believe you really think everything's "
"alright, after all the shit you've done."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Chloe_Taylor_King.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright <name_b>, I'll leave."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are things, living here?"
msgstr "Comment ça se passe, vivre ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are the non-joinees treating you fairly?"
msgstr "Les non-membres vous traitent-ils équitablement ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What needs to be done?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui doit être accompli?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&Corrie briefly glances at you and shoots a glare.  \"What do you want?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey there, <name_g>.  Welcome to the losers club."
msgstr "Salut <name_g>. Bienvenue au club des losers."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just passing through."
msgstr "Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Corrie, you free?"
msgstr "Hé Corrie, tu es libre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Corrie.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Corrie.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well if that's the case, I don't suppose you could help out struggling "
"survivors, do you?"
msgstr ""
"Et bien, si c'est le cas, je suppose que vous ne pourriez pas aider les "
"survivants en difficulté, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, not interested."
msgstr "Pas intéressé(e), désolé(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, we're on the same boat, aren't we?"
msgstr "Eh, on est tous dans le même bateau, non?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just so you know, a lot of the folks here might not take to kindly to your "
"appearance.  I'm cool with it, though."
msgstr ""
"Juste pour que tu le saches, beaucoup de gens ici n'apprécieront peut-être "
"pas ton apparence. Mais ça ne me dérange pas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why would that be?"
msgstr "Pourquoi cela serait-il ainsi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you for your politeness and generosity.  I'll be seeing you."
msgstr "Merci pour votre politesse et votre générosité. A bientôt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure.  I can clear a few minutes of my oh-so hectic schedule."
msgstr "Bien sûr. Je peux libérer quelques minutes de mon emploi du temps si chargé."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry Corrie.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Désolé Corrie.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Corrie blankly stares at the wall for a moment.  \"Me and my friends were in "
"the cities when it hit, I was the only one to make it out.  Some gigantic "
"horror… devoured… everything in its way.  There was a memorial service and "
"all, organized by the church-goers.  By far the nicest thing they've done for "
"me.\""
msgstr ""
"&Corrie regarde le mur d'un air absent pendant un moment. « Mes amis et moi "
"étions dans les villes quand ça a frappé, j'étais la seule à m'en sortir. Une "
"horreur gigantesque... a dévoré... tout sur son passage. Il y a eu une "
"cérémonie commémorative et tout, organisée par les fidèles. De loin la plus "
"belle chose qu'ils aient faite pour moi. »"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Désolé·e d'avoir mentionné ça.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Désolé·e d'avoir remis ça dans votre tête.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Like second-class citizens, that's how they treat us."
msgstr "Comme des citoyens de seconde zone, voilà comment ils nous traitent."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm just here, really.  I'm the local mechanic around here, I just fiddle "
"with the machinery.  Just about all of it is a <freaking> <name_b>, older "
"than dirt and nearly unfixable.  They're running a wood-fire generator for "
"power, the <freaking> thing is the noisiest clunker I've ever heard."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How have things changed after that deal with Helena?"
msgstr "Comment les choses ont-elles changées après ce marché avec Helena?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No rest for the weary…"
msgstr "Pas de repos pour les braves…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not much.  I told you not to go for the icons."
msgstr "Pas grand chose. Je t'avais dit de ne pas aller chercher les icônes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry to hear that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Désolé·e d'entendre ça.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah they have.  I've noticed a change in attitude towards us, the new "
"guys.  Positive ones.  Things might be looking up, a little bit."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, ouais, ils l'ont fait. J'ai remarqué un changement d'attitude envers "
"nous, les nouveaux. Des changements positifs. Les choses pourraient "
"s'améliorer, un petit peu."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about some food as payment?"
msgstr "Est-ce que de la nourriture irait comme récompense?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glad to help.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Ravi·e d'avoir pu aider.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glad to help.  See you around, Corrie."
msgstr "Je suis ravie de pouvoir vous aider. À bientôt, Corrie."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, I completely forget.  Here you are."
msgstr "Oh, j'ai complètement oublié. Te voilà."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Basic repairs and upkeep, mostly.  The generator in the basement is on its "
"last legs, so I've been thinking about building a solar array for this place. "
" Helena's against it, but I want to change her mind.  All I need are a few "
"spare parts."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit principalement de réparations et d'entretien de base. Le générateur "
"du sous-sol est en fin de vie, alors j'ai pensé à construire un panneau "
"solaire pour cet endroit. Helena est contre, mais je veux la faire changer "
"d'avis. Tout ce dont j'ai besoin, ce sont quelques pièces de rechange."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can help you get the items you need."
msgstr "Je peux vous aider à trouver ce dont vous avez besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I'll come.  I hate staying here, and you've gone out of your way to "
"help me.  I appreciate that, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je viendrai. Je déteste rester ici, et tu as fait tout ton possible "
"pour m'aider. J'apprécie ça, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nearly everyone here went to a church that was a bit… out there, shall we "
"say.  They hate what they call \"mutants\", how some creatures and people "
"have physically changed inexplicably after everything went to shit.  I'm glad "
"they didn't kill you on the spot, not many people are left out there."
msgstr ""
"Presque tout le monde ici est allé dans une église qui était un peu… "
"excentrique, disons. Ils détestent ce qu'ils appellent les « mutants », la "
"façon dont certaines créatures et certaines personnes ont physiquement changé "
"de façon inexplicable après que tout soit parti en vrille. Je suis content "
"qu'ils ne t'aient pas tué sur le coup, il ne reste pas beaucoup de gens "
"là-bas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, thank's for telling me.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Merci d'avoir partagé cela avec moi.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wow.  This place is fucking crazy, I'm outta here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, not really.  It's not like I've got any business with you anyways."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the attitude for?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm outta here then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know freaking well what I'm upset about <name_b>.  Now go away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Corrie_Kaja_Dosia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you later <name_b>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that well…"
msgstr "Au sujet du puit…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/sadie.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/sadie.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are things here?"
msgstr "Comment vont les choses ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice farm you have here."
msgstr "C'est une bonne ferme que vous avez là."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Shove off, we've got no good words for each other."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Praise the Lord."
msgstr "Dieu soit loué."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/vampire_mentor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome back."
msgstr "Content de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Darryl.  Neat farm you have here."
msgstr ""
"Enchanté(e) de vous rencontrer aussi Darryl. C'est une assez jolie ferme que "
"vous avez ici."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Darryl.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Darryl.  Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Darryl.  Care to trade?"
msgstr "Salut Darryl.  Vous voulez troquer?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are the chickens?"
msgstr "Comment vont les poules?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the poor attitude about?"
msgstr "Quelle est cette mauvaise attitude?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck you <name_b>, I'm outta here."
msgstr "Va te faire foutre <name_b>, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I guess I can spare a few minutes.  What is it?"
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que je peux vous donner quelques minutes. De quoi voulez-vous "
"parler?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I buy anything?"
msgstr "Je peux acheter quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any family?"
msgstr "Vous avez de la famille?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This uncertainty is eating me inside, to be frank with you.  I'm a simple "
"man: I tend my farm, I scare off vermin, but even I can see somethin' ain't "
"right here.  I've talked to my wife, I had a word with Damien, they told me "
"to have more faith in God.  It's the last sliver of hope I have left, and I "
"was told that's enough."
msgstr ""
"Cette incertitude me ronge de l'intérieur, pour être franc avec vous. Je suis "
"un homme simple : je m'occupe de ma ferme, j'effraie les nuisibles, mais même "
"moi je vois que quelque chose ne va pas ici. J'ai parlé à ma femme, j'ai eu "
"une discussion avec Damien, ils m'ont dit d'avoir plus confiance en Dieu. "
"C'est la dernière lueur d'espoir qui me reste, et on m'a dit que c'était "
"suffisant."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I'd rather not get into my life before all this.  I have a farm to "
"maintain, after all.  Would be nice, sharing our tales while sipping cold "
"brew beer.  Not at a time like this.  Now if you'll excuse me, I'll be back "
"to work."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas vraiment le temps de parler de ma vie avant tout ça.  J'ai une "
"ferme à entretenir, après tout.  Ce serait sympa de partager nos histoires "
"tout en sirotant une bière bien fraîche, mais pas maintenant.  Bon, si vous "
"voulez bien m'excuser, je vais retourner au travail."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr "Il y a quelque chose que je pourrais faire pour vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll leave you to it."
msgstr "Je vous laisse faire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Took us three days and four hard-working hands to clear this humble little "
"land.  It's a far-cry from my old garden, it really is.  I heard theories, "
"from Tom of course, that really messed with my head.  You can never know "
"what's in one of them toxic clouds, can ya?  I suspect goo-puker blood.  That "
"putrid oil is a sure way to make any soil infertile, or so that nitwit says.  "
"Here I go again, ramblin' once more.  One of my bad habits."
msgstr ""
"Il nous a fallu trois jours et quatre mains travailleuses pour défricher "
"cette humble petite terre. C'est très loin de mon ancien jardin, vraiment. "
"J'ai entendu des théories, de Tom bien sûr, qui m'ont vraiment embrouillé la "
"tête. On ne peut jamais savoir ce qu'il y a dans un de ces nuages ​​toxiques, "
"n'est-ce pas ? Je soupçonne du sang gluant. Cette huile putride est un moyen "
"sûr de rendre n'importe quel sol infertile, du moins c'est ce que dit cet "
"idiot. Me revoilà, à radoter une fois de plus. Une de mes mauvaises habitudes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh, never would have thought you were interested in the fine art of farming. "
" Sure, I've got seeds I can say goodbye to… if you have the appropriate money "
"of course."
msgstr ""
"Huh, je n'aurais jamais pensé que vous vous intéresseriez à l'art subtil de "
"l'agriculture.  Bien sûr, j'ai des graines auxquelles je peux dire au revoir… "
"si vous avez l'argent nécessaire, naturellement."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's trade, then."
msgstr "Échangeons dans ce cas là."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's finished, and I've got eggs!  I'd be willing to sell ya some, a dozen "
"for seven icons."
msgstr ""
"C'est fini, et j'ai des œufs ! Je serais prêt à t'en vendre, une douzaine "
"pour sept icônes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy some."
msgstr "J'en veux bien un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's a bit rich for my blood.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "C'est un peu trop pour moi.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All right, this is what I've got:  I can give cucumber, barley or blackberry "
"seeds for one icon; carrot, buckwheat or cranberry seeds for two icons; oat, "
"sugar beet or potato seeds for three icons."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy cucumber seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de concombre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy barley seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines d'orge."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy blackberry seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de mûre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy carrot seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de carotte."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy buckwheat seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de sarrasin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy cranberry seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de canneberge."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy oat seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines d'avoine."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy sugar beet seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de betterave à sucre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy potato seeds."
msgstr "Je veux acheter des graines de pomme de terre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can't you just give them to me for free?  You said you didn't need them."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne pouvez pas juste me les donner gratuitement? Vous venez de dire que "
"vous n'en aviez pas besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Darryl."
msgstr "Merci, à plus tard Darryl."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It really isn't difficult to earn your money here.  Hard labor, like the rest "
"of us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've got a wife, Gemma.  She's a grand lady, should be around here somewhere. "
" She used to teach biology, and we both love gardenin'; that's how we met, ya "
"see.  She 'aint been herself lately, I'm startin' to worry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll check on her.  I hope everything works out for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, they passed a long time ago.  Wish they could've seen Gemma and I marry…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Salvor_Market/salvor_fabricator_talk.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Salvor_Market/salvor_fabricator_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss."
msgstr "Mes condoléances."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've heard of unnatural monsters such as yourself causing chaos after the "
"fall of civilization, and how men have transformed into horrors and gone mad "
"with sin.  This is the judgment of God upon you heathens for your wicked "
"ways, and I want nothing to do with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, I fucking well don't, not with you at least.  I ain't interested in "
"whatever you've got to say."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Darryl_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you later then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "godco_confessed"
msgid "Had a Confessional"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Had a Confessional"
msgid "You decided to take responsibility for your actions."
msgstr "Vous avez décidé d'assumer la responsabilité de vos actions."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Had a Confessional"
msgid "You finally got the weight off your chest."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm seeking forgiveness, Father.  I've made mistakes in my life that I can "
"never take back."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What brings you back here?  Come to exploit me again?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The Lord be with you…  You don't seem all too well, I pray for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The Lord be with you, brother."
msgstr "Que le Seigneur soit avec vous, mon frère."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you're still around, <u_name>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The Lord be with you, sister."
msgstr "Que le Seigneur soit avec vous, ma sœur."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Lord be with you, brother.  You seem new, nice to meet you.  Welcome, and "
"welcome aboard!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Lord be with you, sister.  You seem new, nice to meet you.  Welcome, and "
"welcome aboard!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Reverend."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer aussi Révérend."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to see you again, Reverend.  I wanted to talk."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking for work.  Can I do anything for your congregation?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis à la recherche de travail. Est-ce que je peux faire quelque chose "
"pour votre congrégation?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice meeting you, Reverend.  I'd best get going though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong with me, if you could say?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qui ne va pas avec moi si vous pouvez élaborer?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you talking about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What can I do for you?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where am I?"
msgstr "Où suis-je?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How may I help you, brother?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je vous aider mon frère?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How may I help you, sister?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je vous aider ma sœur?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where am I again?"
msgstr "Où suis-je déjà?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me a bit about this church?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet de cette église?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We all have, brother, we all have."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We all have, sister, we all have."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for your time, Reverend."
msgstr "Merci pour votre temps révérend."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is the New England Community Church, the congregation of it.  Praise the "
"Lord that we made it through!"
msgstr ""
"Ceci est l'Église Chrétienne de Nouvelle Angleterre, du moins sa "
"congrégation.  Louons le Seigneur que nous ayons réussi à nous en sortir!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
msgid "What are you doing out here?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que tu fais ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We all came out here when <the_cataclysm> rocked the world.  It's an old "
"retreat Helena bought in the hopes of renovating it, good thing we did."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I ask you a few more questions?"
msgstr "Puis-je vous poser quelque questions de plus?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I had a pretty comfortable life growing up.  My parents were florists, owned "
"a shop along the main street of town.  They were always so cheery, as if "
"nothing bad could phase them.  When I was about fifteen, I dreamt that the "
"Lord spoke to me; as if urging me to go and spread his Gospel, so I did.  I "
"took odd jobs at several churches for a while, before I went to seminary.  I "
"went between three different churches, before I found this one.  I've been "
"here since."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The full name is the New England Community Church.  Helena's father started "
"it about twenty years ago.  The flock may be small, but we've always helped "
"each other when times were tough; we're like a family now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about Helena?"
msgstr "Que pensez vous d'Helena?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Greenwood looks over his their shoulder, briefly glancing around before "
"speaking in a low whisper.  \"Don't tell anyone I said this, but I don't like "
"Helena at all.  Her father was a real nut, he'd rave on and on about an "
"apocalypse he'd prepared for.  He always thought that his church would be the "
"ark to weather the storm, that God would destroy the world by unleashing the "
"armies of Hell; and he wasn't talking about the Second Coming of Christ.  "
"Helena's just as fanatical as he was, and it reflects in her inadequate "
"leadership.  To be honest, I'm highly concerned for some of the people here; "
"they're obsessively zealous with Helena, and harbor a xenophobic hatred of "
"everything.  As in Matthew 15:14, 'They are blind guides.  And if one blind "
"person guides another, they will both fall into a pit'.\""
msgstr ""
"&Greenwood jète un coup d'œil autour de lui pour vérifier que personne ne "
"l'entend puis vous chuchote: \"Ne dites cela à personne, mais je n'aime pas "
"du tout Helena. Son père était cinglé et n'arrêtait pas d'hurler des sermons "
"au sujet d'une apocalypse à laquelle il se préparait. Il maintenait l'idée "
"que son église était une arche qui serait capable d'affronter la tempête, que "
"Dieu détruirait le monde et déchaînerait les armées infernales, et ce n'était "
"pas son interprétation du second avènement du Christ. Helena est aussi "
"fanatique qu'il était, et cela se reflète beaucoup dans son style de "
"leadership que je trouve franchement stupide. Honnêtement, les attitudes de "
"certains des membres de cette communité m'inquiète. Ils sont tellement zélés "
"et boivent les mots d'Helena comme du vin, et ont une haine xénophobe de tout "
"hors de la communauté. Matthieu 15:14 nous enseigne clairement que \"Ce sont "
"des aveugles qui conduisent des aveugles; si un aveugle conduit un aveugle, "
"ils tomberont tous deux dans une fosse\"."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, it's your appearance.  You're… how do I say, significantly different "
"than what most people are used to.  With the sudden appearance of strange "
"phenomenon following the Rapture, some have taken your changes as a mark of "
"demonic corruption, and won't be very kind to you either.  Be wary of this."
msgstr ""
"Disons juste que... c'est votre apparence. Vous êtes… comment dire, "
"significativement différent(e) de ce à quoi que la plupart des gens sont "
"habitués. Avec l'avénement de phénomènes bizarres après l'Enlèvement, "
"beaucoup ont commencés à attribuer des changements comme les vôtres comme une "
"preuve de corruption démoniaque, et ne seront pas très sympathiques avec vous "
"dû à cela. Prenez gare."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Ok.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the info, I'd best be going then."
msgstr "Merci pour l'info, je ferais mieux d'y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Father_Greenwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've already given you a second chance, and yet you kept right on abusing me. "
" I can't stand it any longer, and I want nothing to do with you.  I hope that "
"God will show you the light soon enough."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's your family?"
msgstr "Comment va votre famille?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/boann.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can do for you?"
msgstr "Il y a quelque chose que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's the manuscript coming?"
msgstr "Comment avance le manuscrit?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, go away.  I don't want to talk to you right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hi."
msgstr "Oh, bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, good to see you're still around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <u_name>, nice to see you."
msgstr "Hé <u_name>, ravi de te voir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hi there.  My name's Felicity, nice to see a new face."
msgstr ""
"Oh bonjour. Mon nom est Felicity, ça fait plaisir de rencontrez une nouvelle "
"personne."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Felicity?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "Felicity?  Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer.  Comment vont les choses pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Felicity.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Felicity.  Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's all that about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Felicity.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Felicity.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm always good for a talk.  It's nice to have company, even if we don't have "
"much else to offer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What's on your mind?"
msgstr "À quoi pensez vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "They're alright.  What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's nice to meet you, but I need to head out."
msgstr "C'était agréable de vous rencontrez, mais je doit y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They're alright, but they won't take kindly to someone with your… appearance. "
" What can i do for you?"
msgstr ""
"Ce ne sont pas de mauvaises personnes… Mais ils n'apprécieront probablement "
"pas quelqu'un avec votre… apparence. Que puis-je faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If that's the case, I'll leave."
msgstr "Si c'est comme ça je ferais mieux de m'en aller."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm actually from New England, Rhode Island specifically.  I grew up in "
"Providence, the state capital.  It was lovely there, I'd always walk to "
"school and stopped in the park on my way home.  Mom was an accountant for "
"various companies, she went to Rivtech back when it was a startup.  Dad was a "
"baker, ran a shop on the corner of Chalkstone and Mt Pleasant.  It smelled so "
"good when you walked by…  I always wanted to be a writer, but I wound up as a "
"proofreader for Stillwater, a publishing firm.  I met Tom at that office, we "
"got married about three years later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why'd you move out here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Tom and I wanted to get away from the city, so we found a home up here.  We "
"didn't move again until <the_cataclysm>, when we came here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've been through a lot without much help, it's been difficult to cope.  "
"Still, we put on a happy little face, and some of us pretend everything's all "
"right."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I suppose we do."
msgstr "Je suppose qu'il est nécessaire que certains fassent cela en effet."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  Au revoir Felicity."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My family's alright.  I have a wonderful daughter, Olwen; she's an "
"electronics nut, had a great job with it too.  My husband Tom is the crazy "
"one, always rambling on about conspiracy theories, secret agents, all that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about Tom?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'en dire plus au sujet de Tom?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about Olwen?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet d'Olwen?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Olwen's a bright girl, always has been.  She studied electricity and computer "
"science when she was in college, found a job with a research and development "
"firm.  My girl's a fiancee now, her and Julian were going to get married in a "
"few months.  She might teach you something, if you ask."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think about her love life with Julian in here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She is feeling down since her relationship with Julian seems to have been put "
"on pause by <the_cataclysm>, but I heard Julian talking about making a proper "
"confession with some rings and everything, maybe you could ask him about it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She is feeling great since receiving her ring from Julian, I can't stop "
"smiling seeing her flourishing here even after everything that happened…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I just helped her trying on her wedding dress!  She will look gorgeous in "
"that dress.  I can't wait to see her smile when the day arrives, she already "
"goes from here and there with a smile from ear to ear…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He wasn't always like this.  Olwen came not long after we married, he was a "
"great, caring father to her.  A few months before <the_cataclysm> is when he "
"lost it, got in some survivalist circle.  He'd stay up pouring over "
"newspapers and any documents he could find, and wound up quitting his job to "
"study it more.  We didn't see much of him for a while, always in the "
"basement, and took out a chunk of our savings to buy canned goods en masse."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way to get him out of it?"
msgstr "Il y aurait un moyen de le réveiller?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know.  I've tried talking to him, tried to convince him to give it "
"up.  I think he's stressed out with everything going on, and snapped because "
"of that.  I just want my husband back…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  Bye, Felicity."
msgstr "Je vais voir ce que je peux faire. Au revoir Felicity."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's finally finished!  Here, I want you to have a copy of it.  This is my "
"first time writing like this professionally, I hope you enjoy it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you, I'm sure it's lovely."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm still working on it.  I'll have it ready soon."
msgstr "Je suis toujours en train de travailler dessus. Je devrais avoir bientôt fini."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good luck with that."
msgstr "Bonne chance avec ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Overall, you've been quite unpleasent to us, and I've frankly had enough of "
"your prude nature.  I won't repeat myself more, go away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Felicity_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright <name_b>, I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What does a dorm leader do exactly?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que le leader de dormoir fait exactement?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I help you with anything?"
msgstr "Je peux vous aider avec quoi que ce soit?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I want to join the community."
msgstr "Je veux rejoindre la communauté."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm rather busy at the moment, I don't have the time to talk right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you're still around, <granny_name_g>."
msgstr "Contente que vous soyez toujours dans les environs, <granny_name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <u_name>.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "Bienvenue <u_name>.  Comment puis-je vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Great to see a new face.  I'm Gemma.  Will you be staying here with us?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer Gemma.  Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gemma.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer Gemma.  Je cherche asile."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm already staying here.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Gemma.  How're you doing?"
msgstr "Salut Gemma.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello, Gemma.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Gemma.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you sure?  I've got all the time in the world."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the harsh reception about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine then, screw you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Nice meeting you."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  Ravi·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I heard what it's like out there.  You must be weary from exploring this "
"unforgiving wasteland.  I'm sorry that you're leaving us this soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your "
"neighbors and we'll get along just fine, okay?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got it."
msgstr "Compris."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is the Decalogue?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que le Décalogue?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Its also called the Ten Commandments, if you've heard it by that.  A long "
"time ago, Moses lead the Israelites out of slavery in Egypt, towards the "
"Promised Land.  They broke their Covenant with God, and were cursed to wander "
"the desert for forty years, as opposed to the nineteen days it would normally "
"take.  On the way there, Moses went atop Mount Sinai to speak with God.  He "
"saw a burning bush, and heard the voice of the Lord; who engraved the "
"Decalogue on two tablets of stone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Gemma is in deep, silent thought for a moment, before clearing her throat.  "
"\"They read: 'I am the Lord your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of "
"the land of slavery.  You shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not "
"make for yourself a carved image, or any likeness of anything that is in "
"heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under "
"the earth.  You shall not take the name of the Lord your God in vain.  "
"Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it holy.  Honor your father and your "
"mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall not commit adultery.  You shall not "
"steal.  You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor.  You shall "
"not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're written in Exodus 20:1-17, for "
"future reference."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You are most welcome here.  In the good old days we would've held a ceremony "
"for you.  Oh well, times have changed.  Accept this blanket, you may choose "
"either bed by the window.  If you're hungry, you can go see Simon for a meal, "
"up to one per day."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Gemma."
msgstr "Merci, à plus tard Gemma."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "My story?  It's been told a thousand times."
msgstr "Mon histoire?  Je dois l'avoir racontée un millier de fois."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I always have things on the go: tidying, organizing, cleaning, but I don't "
"complain.  I never complain."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "There sure is.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Bien sûr.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm feeling great!  Even if the world's over, I always have myself and God "
"above."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm feeling alright, just working away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm happy to hear that, Gemma.  I'd best be going."
msgstr "Ça me fait plaisir d'entendre ça Gemma. Je ferais mieux d'y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_avatar.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_bye>"
#. ~ Avatar response indicated that the conversation is over via TALK_DONE.
msgid "I'll see you around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My flowers look a bit dehydrated, I'd appreciate it if you watered them for "
"me.  These indoor plants are the most calming reminders of life before "
"<the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I meant \"Are there any jobs you know of?\""
msgstr "Je voulais dire : « Y a-t-il des emplois que vous connaissez ? »"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "D'accord.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You certainly have the marks of one.  I don't understand how you can go "
"walking around looking like an abomination, cursed by God, and think "
"everything's alright.  I'm not interested in learning, either, so be gone "
"with you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Gemma_Johnstone.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you really want to know the truth, I;m quite upset with how you've been "
"acting as of late, and I don't want to talk to you.  Now please, leave me be."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What brings you here <name_b>?  You know we don't want anything to do with "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Blessings to you."
msgstr "Dieu vous bénisse."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Bless you, <u_name>."
msgstr "Dieu vous bénisse <u_name>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stranger, what brings you to our holy home?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you again."
msgstr "C'est un plaisir de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why might that be?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can't talk right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm Helena, the caretaker of this flock.  Who might you be, wanderer?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not doing much wandering, I'm staying here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just passing through.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Je ne fais que passer.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just like all the sinners, roaming through Hell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It certainly seems like it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See ya later, crazy lady."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you, I hope he shares that sentiment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Merci.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr "De quoi avez-vous besoin?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Corrie and I have finished that solar cart."
msgstr "Corrie et moi avons fini de construire le chariot solaire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Olwen's finished the radio transmitter she was working on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I am a prophet, like my uncle before me.  He saw <the_cataclysm>, the "
"righteous judgment of God and set about preparing an ark to save us.  He "
"passed before his visions could be fulfilled, and now I carry his righteous "
"banner."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He had many visions, and he had many secrets.  I don't know all of them, but "
"there was one he was highly vocal about, regarding <the_cataclysm>, that "
"according to him \"The spawn of Satan shall descend upon the Earth, and all "
"will be consumed in death and destruction\".  He never said much else about "
"it, and always had a mortified face whenever someone brought it up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks to my uncle's forethought, we've been blessed by God.  We have plenty "
"of food for ourselves, safety from the hordes of Hell, and the continued "
"protection of the Lord our God."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They denied us, they labeled us as a doomsday cult, threw sticks and stones "
"at us, and yet, we were standing resiliently.  Why?  Because we knew God was "
"on our side."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are all under God's protection here.  Our community, like all moral "
"civilizations, has a set of rules.  Obey the Decalogue, have respect for your "
"neighbors and we'll get along just fine.  Go see Gemma or Julian for a bed, "
"if one's available.  We do have limited space on our Ark, though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, I'll see about that.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Ok, je verrais.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Helena flips through her Bible before stopping.  \"They read: 'I am the Lord "
"your God, who brought you out of Egypt, out of the land of slavery.  You "
"shall have no other gods before me.  You shall not make for yourself a carved "
"image, or any likeness of anything that is in heaven above, or that is in the "
"earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth.  You shall not take "
"the name of the Lord your God in vain.  Remember the Sabbath day, and keep it "
"holy.  Honor your father and your mother.  You shall not murder.  You shall "
"not commit adultery.  You shall not steal.  You shall not bear false witness "
"against your neighbor.  You shall not covet your neighbors house.\"  They're "
"written in Exodus 20:1-17, for future reference."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I like what you and Corrie's put together.  I did promise payment for a "
"proof-of-concept, what'll it be?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have some icons."
msgstr "J'aimerais avoir des icônes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I want Corrie to have some extra rations."
msgstr "J'aimerais que Corrie reçoive des rations supplémentaires."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's negotiate some other time."
msgstr "Négocions plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Here's your money.  Don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "Voila votre argent. Ne dépensez pas tout en un seul coup."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A generous soul, are we?  That's not what I was expecting, but I'll see to it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, I was just informed of that.  I also heard that she found a large group "
"of people living out in an old evacuation center, who consider themselves "
"merchants.  That would be a good place to resume our spread of the Truth, "
"perhaps we could find others who were faithful before <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I presume you want me to pay a visit?"
msgstr "Je présume que vous voulez que je leurs rende visite?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, I've met them before!"
msgstr "Oh, je l'ai déjà rencontré·e!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's change the subject."
msgstr "Changeons de sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, you seem like a good fit for the job.  I'll pay you a small sum for "
"getting some information about them."
msgstr ""
"Oui, vous semblez être un bon candidat pour ce poste. Je vous paierai une "
"petite somme pour obtenir des informations sur eux."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll go and see what's up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Really?  I'd pay a small sum for information about them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, they're…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Helena_Misinter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You've been nothing but a leech and a stain on us, we don't want you here "
"anymore nor your \"services\" you might provide.  Now get out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Need any help?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'aide?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you provide any medical services?"
msgstr "Vous pourriez me fournir vos services médicaux?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might have some medicine for the community.  Anything you're missing?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you taking care of Arturo?"
msgstr "Vous veillez sur Arturo?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you want to come with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&Jane glaces at you, scowls, and ignores your presence."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How can I help you?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "<u_name>, what can I do for you?"
msgstr "<u_name>, que puis-je faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, I don't think we've met before.  My name's Jane, I'm the local doctor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Jane."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer aussi Jane."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Jane.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Jane.  Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, I don't see why not.  I've gotta keep my mind off stuff anyway."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm doing somewhat well, thanks to my occupation.  The other joinees, well, "
"they're barely scraping by.  It's been tense, and I'm not seeing it change "
"for the better."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a physician, one of the more unfortunate people who didn't call in sick "
"during the riots.  I remember it all so clearly, the cuts, bruises, deep "
"bites, then those oily black eyes, caustic yellow blood, spastic fungal "
"growths… it was terrible gnarly.  Then things descended into all-new levels "
"of fucked up, and some of my coworkers were preparing to just get the hell "
"out.  I followed them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Were you evaced'?"
msgstr "Vous avez été évacué(e)?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, not by the government."
msgstr "Non, pas par le gouvernement."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, not really.  I came here after I was split from my friends by a horde of "
"<zombies>.  They let me in after I gave away some food I found.  The church "
"distrusts my profession; I get by helping Kostas."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really don't, actually.  Even my help is thankless here.  Bandaging cuts, "
"setting bones, disinfecting wounds; who needs all that when they can pray "
"anything away?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any work available?"
msgstr "Vous avez du travail pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like to buy any supplies?"
msgstr "Voulez-vous acheter quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do what I can, but he's mostly beyond my skillset.  Coke's a <freaking> "
"<name_b>, really messes a person up.  Arturo was on it for several years "
"before he tried to get help, now he has auditory hallucinations; hears voices "
"from nowhere.  Traumatic experiences have a harsher effect on recovering "
"addicts, but <the_cataclysm> is worse than anything we've gone through before."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thorazine would go us a long way, but Arturo's having trouble getting it.  "
"They think he's the key and that my help would obstruct him.  Regardless, "
"there's just so much anti-medical sentiment here that I've given up on "
"prescribing anything."
msgstr ""
"De la chlorpromazine aiderait beaucoup, mais j'ai des problèmes à en fournir "
"assez à Arturo, les autres pense que ses hallucinations sont utiles et que le "
"traiter serait néfaste.  De toute façon il y a tellement d'opinions "
"anti-médicales ici que j'ai arrêté d'essayer de donner des prescriptions."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about Kostas?  The Church seems to trust him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He's an alright physician, but the Church massively overrates him.  They "
"think his 'natural medicine' can cure anything, like he's a magic medicine "
"man.  God created everything, so what on Earth isn't natural?!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do you feel about him personally?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Personally, I like him.  We've worked together for a few cases, but most "
"people refuse to let me work; they only want to see him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I've got some supplies on hand, just give me a minute and you'll be "
"right as rain.  It'll cost three icons."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can pay for quality work.  Here it is."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm up for it, Arturo's got enough medicine for two-and-half months.  It's "
"thankless work around here, so let's blow this joint."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'd like to leave, but I've got to take care of Arturo.  He's always low or "
"nearly out of antipsychotics, so I do what I can."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  Wanna chat?"
msgstr "Ok, vous voulez discuter?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I could always use more bandages, disinfectant, and the like.  What do you "
"have?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Je n'ai rien sur mon assiette là.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have anything right now.  I'll come back with something later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have <topic_item>."
msgstr "J'ai <topic_item>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fuck off <name_b>.  I've had it with your tormenting antics, I don't want "
"anything to do with you right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jane_Schulz.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine then, have it your way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your take on the situation here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are your parents like?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are your plans after <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "Quels sont vos plans après le/la/l'<the_cataclysm>?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Were could I find work around here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What are you doing around here <name_b>?  Get lost."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, look who's back."
msgstr "Eh, regardez qui est de retour."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey again <u_name>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hey, it's you again."
msgstr "Oh, c'est vous de nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, uh… you look new.  Didn't think we'd see new people here.  Hey."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just a traveler, kid.  I won't be staying here for long."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not exactly new here, kid."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Jerry.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with the attitude?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, kid.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I have a name, you know.  It's Jeremiah, but people just call me Jerry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, Jerry.  What's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, Jeremiah.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Désolé·e Jeremiah.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I thought asking about each other's emotions went out of style after "
"<the_cataclysm>.  Uhm, okay then.  I'm fine, I guess."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I noticed you're holding a D&D handbook.  Do you play much?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've convinced Kostas to take you on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My take?  You already know how things are.  People are dead, my friends are "
"dead, so yeah.  At least there's no school, the adults just love reminding me "
"that.  You know what?  I kinda miss school."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was in high school, like anyone else my age.  Then out of nowhere, my mom "
"pulled me out of school to \"save me\".  I got packed into a bus with my "
"parents and their old-timey friends.  We've been stuck here ever since.  "
"Actually, it's not all that bad.  I'm studying to be a herbalist like Kostas, "
"which is cool I guess."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your parents."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de vos parents."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I play.  I ran a campaign for a while with some of my friends, we'd "
"play after school.  I don't know where they are now, though.  Do you wanna "
"play some?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, I'm up for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No thanks.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Non Merci.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Jeremiah leans his head towards your ear, speaking in a low whisper.  \"To "
"be honest with you, I don't like my mom at all.  She's like a <freaking> "
"helicopter, always telling me what to do, where to go, who I can be with.  "
"She never thinks of me as an individual, only some idea of who she thinks I "
"am.  My dad's alright, he's the chef around here.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know, exactly.  I think I'll stay here and do what I can for the "
"community."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'd like to study herbology with Kostas, it seems like a useful skill these "
"days.  I do feel bad for Jane though, she's a skilled doctor and nobody here "
"cares, they all just think any illness can be prayed away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When do you plan on starting that apprenticeship?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well…  Kostas is a bit unsure about teaching me, for some reason.  If you "
"could change his mind, I'd pay you some \"icons\", what we've started using "
"for money around here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No thanks.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Non merci.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can do for you."
msgstr "Je vais voir ce que je peux faire pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's great!  Thanks <name_g>, here's the money."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "De rien."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Darryl should have something for you to do if you like gardening, Jane could "
"use some medical supplies, too.  If you like to be bossed around, Helena "
"probably has a few things that need doing.  I'd just ask around, really."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything you need?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know very well what I'm upset about.  Now do like I said earlier and get "
"lost."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Jeremiah_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine, whatever."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are the advantages of being a dorm leader?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Heard you and Olwen were some kind of lovebirds?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did Olwen receive the rings?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did Olwen like the dress?"
msgstr "Est-ce qu'Olwen aime la robe?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why did you join the Church?"
msgstr "Pourquoi avez-vous rejoint l'Église?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey…  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  Are you… planning on "
"sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Why are you still around, don't you have someone else to bother?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, <name_g>."
msgstr "Salut <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you again <u_name>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey, a new face.  I'm Julian, the guy in charge of this room.  You're "
"planning on sticking around or somethin'?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer Julian.  Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Julian.  I'm seeking asylum."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer Julian.  Je cherche asile."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm a joinee actually.  Nice to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, good to see you again."
msgstr "Salut, c'est un plaisir de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nope, just me and you pal.  What's the attitude about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello, Julian.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Julian.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you have complaints, please don't tell anyone."
msgstr "Si vous avez des problèmes, veuillez ne rien dire à qui que ce soit."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're still staying here, joinee?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Need anything, joinee?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Need anything?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Go on…"
msgstr "Continuez…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aight, here are the rules: don't commit sins, don't litter, and try not to "
"die.  Have some mutual respect, capiche?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "En fait, <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Of course, our relationship was going pretty well before <the_cataclysm>.  "
"Olwen seems to be under the weather lately, but I want to give her a great "
"surprise and make her smile again…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want me to help you with that surprise?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"With a big smile and her eyes wide open!  I can't thank you enough for "
"helping me with that, even so…  You could maybe lend your hand again to bring "
"even more happiness to this place?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She loved it!  I still can't believe I will be able to provide her with a "
"proper wedding even after everything that happened, you have been a real life "
"saver <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Listen, I have some bad news.  I don't personally have anything against you, "
"but many of the people here are very… discriminatory against those who look "
"like you.  I hate to say it, but I'll have to turn you away.  I'm sorry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, let's talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I get the picture, screw this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Your name is now on the books.  Here's your blanket, joinee.  Those two beds "
"next to the window, you can choose one of them.  It's safe, don't worry.  I'm "
"armed.  By the way, if you're hungry you can go bug Simon for a meal, up to "
"one in a day."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Julian."
msgstr "Merci, à plus tard Julian."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Julian suddenly appears disturbed, and looks away from you for a moment.  "
"\"It's a long story, and not an interesting one at that.  I was a cop before. "
" You must've heard about those riots and all that.  I'm glad we all managed "
"to make it out alive.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you make it out?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce que vous vous avez survécu?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I might as well be honest with you.  I ran mostly, ran like the devil "
"was chasin' me.  I was at one of the police stations in town, when we were "
"called out to handle a violent mob on the loose.  When we got there, the "
"people were crazy, smashing and killing everything in their way.  They had "
"these bloodshot eyes and a weird goo in their mouths.  We pulled out all the "
"stops to handle them.  When tear gas wouldn't work, the chief told us to draw "
"guns and kill them all.  We did…  There was so much blood…  That maneuver "
"killed a lot of them, but not all.  One snuck up behind a lady who worked "
"with us, tore a whole section of her spine out.  She never even had time to "
"scream, just slumped over the cruiser door…  So I jumped post and ran, never "
"looked back.  God, I can still hear the cries…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Maybe we should change the subject."
msgstr "Mes condoléances, peut être nous devrions changer de sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Mes condoléances.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Advantages?  All I do is work!"
msgstr "Des avantages? Ce n'est rien que du travail!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr "Quelque chose que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, it must be exhausting.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's been a struggle, trying to keep this bunch together.  Oh things could be "
"better here, of course.  It could always be, but sometimes we don't even "
"realize how good we have it here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"When I was younger, I used to go to church with my family.  When I started "
"growing up, I saw all this evil around me, people hating and persecuting "
"others, despite the teachings of Jesus; I just stopped going one day, decided "
"to make my own way.  I joined the NECC a few years back to rekindle my "
"relationship with God, get back to who I was."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'd rather not talk about it."
msgstr "J'aimerais ne pas en parler."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I can understand.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Ok, je comprends.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&\"You've messed me over a good bit, and I've had enough.  Goodbye.\"  Julian "
"goes back to his business and ignores you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Julian_Ray.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See ya later <name_b>."
msgstr "À plus tard <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Arturo?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet d'Arturo?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Corrie?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Corrie?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Jane?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Jane?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Sonia?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Sonia?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Zachary?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Zachary?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Simon?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Simon?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Jeremiah?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet de Jeremiah?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you do before <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "Que faisiez-vous avant <the_cataclysm>?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You don't seem to like the joinees very much.  Why is that?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know where I could find some work?"
msgstr "Vous savez où je peux trouver du boulot?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please go away, I'm not in the mood to talk right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "<u_name>, bless you."
msgstr "<u_name>, dieu vous bénisse."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Katherine.  How's it going?"
msgstr "Salut Katherine.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Katherine."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Katherine."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You sure, I've got plenty of time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, fuck you then."
msgstr "Très bien, allez vous faire foutre dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's always a pleasure.  How may I help you?"
msgstr "C'est toujours un plaisir. Comment puis-je vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just had some questions."
msgstr "J'avais juste quelques questions."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We have many things to pray for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "Nous avons beaucoup de raisons de prier j'ai bien peur."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I understand.  I don't have the answers you are looking for, I'm afraid."
msgstr "Je comprends. Je n'ai pas les réponses que vous cherchez j'ai bien peur."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "Je vais continuer mes voyages dans ce cas là."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Our prayers were heard.  We knew the day was coming, so we prepared.  Our "
"community stockpiled months' worth of canned goods, well enough until the "
"chaos ends.  With the food we have left, we could live peacefully, but we "
"foolishly didn't take extra people into consideration.  With so much at risk, "
"I don't think we can afford more people.  Though I'm not the one who makes "
"the decisions here, and it's probably for the better."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you can take in joinees once there's a vacancy?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I worked for the Church, organized charities and filed paperwork.  That's how "
"I met the Founder.  I did so much for everyone, yet they never noticed…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You're right, I don't.  They should've come when they had the chance.  Now "
"that our Ark has sailed, they want to jump aboard.  Such is the way of "
"sinners, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If there's a vacancy.  Even then, there's the decision of which joinee to "
"include.  Those people don't share or respect the same values as we do.  None "
"of them are promising candidates."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Jesus warned us about false prophets."
msgstr "Jésus nous a mis en garde au sujet des faux prophètes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She knows this and that about electronics.  The generator we have here was "
"made by her.  Nice to have one here, even though there's not much use for it "
"yet."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hear she knows this and that about electronics.    She keeps herself "
"occupied by doing menial tasks around the camp, looking for payment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's not an illness God can't cure.  Yet, by fate, we were given a doctor. "
" She's now taking care of Arturo, that poor thing.  Oh well, who am I to "
"question God's ways?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She occasionally plays her guitar in the hall, and she's quite good at it.  "
"Unsurprisingly, she doesn't know any hymns.  Wouldn't let her near my son."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My dear, sweet husband.  He worked as a cook for one of the homeless "
"shelters, that's how we met.  He's always liked to try new things.  He should "
"be in the dining hall, if you want to see him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He's my son, such a wonderful boy.  He's always been the light in my life, "
"and I've tried to teach him well.  We've been a bit distant as of late, but "
"I'm sure he'll come around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He can keep his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he's a bit more "
"useful than some of the others.  He helped Corrie make that generator."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm not planning to communicate with him, that's for certain.  He can keep "
"his distance with his smug nothingness.  At least he knows how to cut lumber."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you're here for an exciting story, you're talking with the wrong person.  "
"Ever since I was born I've lived very modestly.  Did I regret it?  No, it "
"will all be worth it in the end…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about the community."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de la communauté."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your family."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de votre famille."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've been a member of the New England Church Community for a quarter of a "
"century, took part in each and every sermon and gathering they held even "
"while I was carrying my boy Jeremiah.  Not to mention the countless times we "
"visited those filthy homeless shelters and prisons filled with sinners.  I "
"even met the Founder himself.  I can confidently say I'm more worthy to be "
"here than those impostors who leech on us at this camp."
msgstr ""
"Cela fait un quart de siècle que je suis membre de la Communauté Chrétienne "
"de Nouvelle-Angleterre, j'ai participé à chaque sermon et à chaque réunion "
"qu'elle organisait, même lorsque je portais mon fils Jeremiah.  Sans parler "
"des innombrables fois où nous avons visité ces immondes refuges pour "
"sans-abris et ces prisons remplies de pécheurs.  J'ai même rencontré le "
"Fondateur lui-même.  Je peux dire en toute confiance que je suis plus digne "
"d'être ici que tout les imposteurs qui nous sucent le sang dans ce camp."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The Founder?"
msgstr "Le Fondateur?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sure you've met my husband, Simon.  He was also a volunteer at a homeless "
"shelter, working as a cook.  We were brought together by the hands of fate as "
"some would say.  We have a son together, Jeremiah, the light in my life.  "
"Such a creative and well-behaved boy, I just wish we could find an "
"appropriate woman for him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He was quite reserved when I met him, seemed distant in his thoughts.  "
"Theresa has the answers you are looking for."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll talk to her then."
msgstr "Je lui parlerais dans ce cas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I'm rather upset and just need some time alone, okay?  I'm sure you're "
"very busy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have the time to wait, now can we get on with business?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Katherine scowls with anger at you.  \"This is the exact <freaking> reason I "
"don't want to talk to you, now go away!\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Katherine_Weaver.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck's sake <name_b>, I'm leaving!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have the pine needles you asked me for."
msgstr "J'ai les aiguilles de pin que vous m'avez demander de trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "You learn how to craft pine tea."
msgstr "Vous apprenez comment faire une tisane de pin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you do around here?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que vous faites ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A sin against God, did you know that's what you are?  Get away from me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Kostas looks up at you and scorns.  \"I'm rather busy right now with an "
"important project, go away please.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "<u_name>, how can I help you?"
msgstr "<u_name>, comment puis-je vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Kostas."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer aussi Kostas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard Jeremiah wanted to learn a few things from you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Kostas.  Care to trade?"
msgstr "Salut Kostas, vous voulez échanger quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, I think we've got some time to chat, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Kostas, find something interesting lately?"
msgstr "Salut Kostas, vous avez trouvé quelque chose d'intéressant récemment?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Kostas.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Kostas.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What the hell are you talking about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright then."
msgstr "Très bien alors."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm afraid I haven't gone out there for a while, maybe come back in "
"<interval>.  These are all I have, care to take a look?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry these are all I have.  However I'll be back from my next run in "
"<interval>.  Care to take a look in the meanwhile?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll take a look."
msgstr "Ok, j'y jetterai un coup d'œil."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, thanks for informing me.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What can I do for you, <name_g>?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que je peux faire pour vous <name_g>?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are there any jobs I could do?"
msgstr "Vous avez du travail pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My story?  I'm afraid it's not as gripping as the other tales around here.  "
"My father was an herbalist, my grandfather was an herbalist and - as "
"ancestral pressure would have it - I also became an herbalist.  I studied "
"from the best teachers and, through the years, a generation's knowledge "
"passed on to me.  I've spent a good portion of my life warning others of the "
"fakery that is plastic medicine and helping them rediscover the forgotten "
"beauty that lies in our surroundings.  I joined the New England Church "
"Community to express my gratitude towards the benevolence of nature.  This is "
"where it brought me."
msgstr ""
"Mon histoire?  Je crains qu'elle ne soit pas aussi passionnante que les "
"autres récits qui circulent ici.  Mon père était herboriste, mon grand-père "
"était herboriste et, comme le veut la pression ancestrale, je suis devenu "
"herboriste à mon tour.  J'ai étudié auprès des meilleurs professeurs et, au "
"fil des ans, le savoir d'une génération m'a été transmis.  J'ai passé une "
"bonne partie de ma vie à mettre en garde les autres contre l'imposture de la "
"médecine plastique et à les aider à redécouvrir la beauté oubliée qui se "
"trouve dans notre environnement.  J'ai rejoint la Communauté Chrétienne de "
"Nouvelle-Angleterre pour exprimer ma gratitude envers la bienveillance de la "
"nature.  Voici où cela m'a mené."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's been quiet and peaceful.  Nature is recovering, and so are we.  There's "
"something bittersweet about <the_cataclysm>, isn't there?  Our species was on "
"the path of destruction, but Mother Nature spared us.  A sign of mercy for a "
"creature that did not deserve it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You must be new to herbalism, no?  In short, I scavenge the land for herbs to "
"supply our humble community with medicine.  And that's just one part of my "
"job.  Say, are you interested in buying campsite gear?  I came across an "
"abandoned camp while foraging.  One can only wonder what happened to its poor "
"inhabitants…"
msgstr ""
"Vous devez être novice en matière d'herboristerie, non ? En bref, je cherche "
"des herbes dans la nature pour fournir des médicaments à notre humble "
"communauté. Et ce n'est qu'une partie de mon travail. Cela vous "
"intéresse-t-il d'acheter du matériel de camping ? Je suis tombé/e sur un "
"campement abandonné pendant que je cherchais de la nourriture. On ne peut que "
"se demander ce qu'il est advenu de ses pauvres habitant/es..."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Care to share your knowledge about herbalism?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Foraging is about recognizing the abundance that is around us all the time, "
"not seeking out rare species."
msgstr ""
"La cueillette consiste à reconnaître l'abondance qui nous entoure en "
"permanence, et non à rechercher des espèces rares."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'll need a good book to confidently identify edible and poisonous wild "
"foods.  I'd recommend the book 'Autobiography of a Mountain Man' for detailed "
"descriptions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Never eat any wild food without first being sure of its identity.  It only "
"takes one mistake."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The huge diversity of wild plants and fungi can be very daunting to the "
"novice forager.  Don't be too ambitious.  Try to enjoy the learning process "
"without getting frustrated or taking risks around uncertain identifications."
msgstr ""
"L'immense diversité des plantes et des champignons sauvages peut décourager "
"le cueilleur novice. Ne soyez pas trop ambitieux/se. Essayez d'apprécier le "
"processus d'apprentissage sans vous frustrer ni prendre de risques en raison "
"d'identifications incertaines."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can tell you this: pine needles make the best tea.  Perhaps I'll make you "
"one someday."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I try your pine needle tea?"
msgstr "Je peux goûter votre tisane au pin?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure.  Bring me a dozen pine boughs and I'll boil you some."
msgstr "Bien sûr, ramenez moi une douzaine de rameaux de pin et je vous en ferait une."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll be back soon."
msgstr "Je serais de retour bientôt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This recipe is a gemstone of my family heritage.  Lucky for us that the most "
"common evergreen tree in the U.S. is non-toxic.  Start by rinsing the "
"needles, and separating any woody parts from them.  Then, cut the pine "
"needles in half.  Add one bough's worth of chopped needles to a cup or mug "
"and fill it with boiling water.  Let the needles steep for ten minutes, until "
"they turn brownish and sink down to the bottom.  As a final step, you can "
"strain the needles, but then you'd be wasting precious calories.  A drink "
"like this is perfect for mid-winter colds."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "Merci, à plus tard Kostas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah…  I don't think he'd be a good fit for an herbalist.  He has a bad "
"habit of wandering off someplace, could get him killed one of these days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Jeremiah's a bright kid.  I'll just tell him to not wander as a stipulation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I know him pretty well, I'm sure he'll learn as he goes along."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you don't take him under your wings, I'll rip them off for you.  Capiche?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, I'm still certain about this.  Jeremiah just isn't a good fit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  See you around, Kostas."
msgstr "Ok.  À plus tard Kostas."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You think you're so tough <name_b>?  I'm not taking Jeremiah on, certainly "
"not when his representitive is so barbaric.  I don't know how he got such a "
"violent individual like yourself to do this, but I hope he can find someone "
"else in the future."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck you then, you judgmental <name_b>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm talking about you and your filthy, unnatural appearance.  I don't like "
"your kind, and neither does anyone else.  Go repent before the Lord for your "
"many sins, if he'll even listen to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck you, I'm blowing this joint."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Kostas becomes visibly angry now, glaring at you.  \"Feeling pushy today, "
"are we?  If you want to hear it plain, we're not on good terms at the moment "
"and I would appreciate it if you didn't bother me for a while.  Understand?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Kostas_Walsman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is everyone treating you fairly?"
msgstr "Tout le monde vous traite bien?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ahh!  What the hell are you?  Get the freaking away from me!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Buzz off <name_b>, I'm not interested in <freaking> chatting with you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <name_g>!  Nice to see you again!"
msgstr "Salut <name_g>!  Contente de vous revoir!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey <u_name>!  Nice to see you again!"
msgstr "Salut <u_name>!  Contente de vous revoir!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't think I've met you before, have I?  I'm Maria Serrano, it's nice to "
"see an new face."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you, Maria."
msgstr "C'est un plaisir de vous rencontrer Maria."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Maria.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Maria.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maria, why the sudden hostility?"
msgstr "Maria, pourquoi l'hostilité soudaine?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Maria.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Maria.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright, chill out, I'm leaving!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you sew something for me?"
msgstr "Pourriez-vous coudre quelque chose pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's my order going?"
msgstr "Comment va ma commande?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I arrived a bit later than everyone else, I was at my studio when "
"<the_cataclysm> came.  Had to dodge a big horde of <zombies> on my way out of "
"town, totaled my car, and hiked the rest of the way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I always wanted to be a fashion designer when I was young.  I used to have a "
"set of dolls, and I'd make dresses for them out of spare cloth I could find.  "
"I took up sewing in high school, and I was trying to get a job with Fashion "
"Nova before <the_cataclysm> screwed that up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things are alright, could be better.  I've been mending clothes and sheets "
"ever since I arrived, fixing this and that.  Theresa's been a big help in "
"those regards, we've traded quilt patterns and designs quite a bit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about Theresa?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet de Theresa?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She's a kind old lady, does a lot of knitting.  She could probably make you "
"something if you asked nicely."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah, they are.  I just wish my work was more appreciated."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What'll ya have?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous avez?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a t-shirt."
msgstr "Je voudrais un tee-shirt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a pair of pants."
msgstr "Je voudrais une paire de pantalons."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a leather jacket."
msgstr "J'aimerais une veste en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a dress."
msgstr "Je voudrais une robe."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a duster."
msgstr "Je voudrais un cache-poussières."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a trench coat."
msgstr "Je voudrais un trench-coat."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a backpack."
msgstr "Je voudrais un sac à dos."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a gambeson."
msgstr "Je voudrais un gambison."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What can you sew?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous coudre?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the price?"
msgstr "Quel est le prix?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you make more things with leather?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez fabriquer d'autre choses avec du cuir?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a set of pouches."
msgstr "J'aimerais un ensemble de pochettes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "J'aimerais une paire de pantalons en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a leather cloak."
msgstr "J'aimerais une cape en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a thicker leather jacket."
msgstr "J'aimerais une veste en cuir plus épais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a set of body armor."
msgstr "J'aimerais un ensemble pare-balles."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I've been busy lately, what did you ask for again?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a t-shirt."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un t-shirt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a pair of pants."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une paire de pantalons."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a leather jacket."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une veste en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a dress."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une robe."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a duster."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un cache-poussières."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a trench coat."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un trench-coat."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a backpack."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un sac à dos."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a gambeson."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un gambison."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a set of pouches."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un ensemble de pochettes."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a pair of leather pants."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une paire de pantalons en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a leather cloak."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une cape en cuir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a thick leather jacket."
msgstr "J'ai commandé une veste en cuir plus épais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I ordered a set of body armor."
msgstr "J'ai commandé un ensemble pare-balles."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I sure can!  For now, I can make t-shirts, pants, dresses, dusters, trench "
"coats, backpacks, jackets, and a gambeson; if that's your thing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's get to it."
msgstr "Mettons-nous y."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you make me something else with leather?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me fabriquer quelque chose avec du cuir?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses are four icons.  Dusters, trench coats, "
"and backpacks are eight icons.  A gambeson is sixteen."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"T-shirts, pants, jackets, and dresses take me just a day.  Dusters, trench "
"coats, and backpacks take four days, while a gambeson takes six days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"But of course!  Right now, I can make a set of pouches, pants, cloaks, "
"thicker jackets, or even a full set of body armor; it should be useful in "
"your travels."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I rather want something softer…"
msgstr "Je pense que je préfèrerais quelque chose de plus doux…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pouches and pants are eight icons.  Cloaks and thick jackets are twelve "
"icons.  A set of body armor is twenty-four."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pouches and pants take me two days.  Cloaks and thick jackets take four days, "
"while the set of body armor takes six days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alright, I'll get to it."
msgstr "Ok, je m'y mets."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Here it is, I hope you enjoy it.  If you want something else, just come to me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"'Cause your a <freaking> <name_b> is why!  You think you can just do what "
"fucking ever you want with no consequence!  I'm sick of this, I'm not talking "
"to you anymore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Maria_Serrano.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, <name_b>, piss on it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is your love life going in here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard you were handy with computers."
msgstr "J'ai entendu que vous aviez un truc pour les ordinateurs?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What in the world are you still doing around here, come back to screw me over?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You don't look too shabby, <u_name>."
msgstr "Vous n'avez pas l'air en trop mauvaise forme <u_name>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I definitely haven't met you yet.  Nice to meet you, I'm Olwen."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just a traveler."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Olwen.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Olwen.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Olwen.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Olwen.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I'll be on my way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You look somewhat interesting.  So, what's your story?"
msgstr "Vous avez l'air intéressant·e.  C'est quoi votre histoire?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here."
msgstr "Je cherche asile."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd rather not say.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to "
"wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any old port in a storm, I guess."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not many travelers come through here these days.  There's not much left to "
"wander too, besides a horde of <zombies>.  The people here won't be too "
"friendly with you either, so that sucks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure does."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I suppose a lot of us are these days, with all the nasty things wandering "
"around.  I hope you like it here, might not be the most comfortable, but "
"it'll do for me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They're alright, I suppose.  Helena's an asshole as usual, we're low on "
"supplies, and all scared to go twenty feet outside the gate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not much too it, really.  I came here on that bus with everyone else when "
"<the_cataclysm> happened to stroll by.  I've been servicing everyone's "
"electronics since then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about your past?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'en dire plus sur votre passé?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Why not?  Oversharing is kind of my thing anyway.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My dad's having a hard time letting go of the past.  Got any more interview "
"questions?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well…  Things were going pretty well between Julian and I before "
"<the_cataclysm>, but after everything that happened…  Ugh, I'm getting "
"depressed just thinking about it.  Let's just talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pretty well actually!  Julian just asked me to marry him!  With wedding rings "
"and everything!  I must be the happiest woman still alive!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm on cloud nine!  I just came back from trying on my wedding dress!  Julian "
"is so charming thinking of everything, I don't know how to repay him, I'm "
"really over the moon with the wedding."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I got a master's in computer science from the University of Rhode "
"Island.  Everyone around here comes to me when they want to keep their "
"computers running.  Corrie works more with the hardware portion of these "
"things; I'd recommend visiting her."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you teach me anything?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'apprendre quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, this is a really xenophobic bunch, and regard some of your, changes, as "
"a curse brought on by God.  I'm cool with you though, not like some of these "
"other <name_b>.  There are a few who wouldn't mind you, though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "In that case, I'd better get going."
msgstr "Dans ce cas là je ferais mieux de m'en aller."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You've been quite the <name_b> as of late, and I'm sick of it.  Now go away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Olwen_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll leave."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk about getting you those trophies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "Pourquoi n'allez vous pas collecter ces trophées vous-même?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why didn't you hunt these trophies yourself?"
msgstr "Pourquoi n'avez-vous pas simplement collecté ces trophées vous même?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "Vous avez vraiment besoin de ces trophées?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Get away from me, demon.  I shoot crazy sinners like you on a regular basis, "
"and my rifle's right here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Get away from me <name_b>.  I'm not interested in whatever <freaking> thing "
"you have to say right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Praise the Lord, <name_g>."
msgstr "Dieu soit loué, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Praise the Lord, <u_name>."
msgstr "Dieu soit loué, <u_name>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Greetings, <name_g><punc>  You okay?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh, so it was you over there.  It's always great to see a new face.  Name's "
"Russell, Russell Connelly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Russell, hey?  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "Russell?  Enchanté·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Russell.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Russell.  Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Russell.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Russell.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Chill out man, I'll leave you alone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's not often that we see new folks around the remnants of the New England "
"Community Church.  So, got any tales to share from the outside world?"
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas souvent qu'on voit de nouvelles personnes autour des vestiges de "
"Communauté Chrétienne de Nouvelle-Angleterre. Vous avez des histoires du "
"monde extérieur à partager?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "Je suis juste un voyageur curieux.  Qu'est-ce qui vous préoccupe?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What's up with you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Who cares what's up with me?  You're the new one here.  Let me put it another "
"way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking about the monsters that lurk "
"deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them with your very own eyes?"
msgstr ""
"On s'en fiche de ce qui se passe avec moi. C'est vous qui êtes nouveau ici. "
"Permettez-moi de le dire autrement : qu'avez-vous vu là-bas ? Je parle des "
"monstres qui se cachent au fond des bois. Les avez-vous vus de vos propres "
"yeux?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I wouldn't be here if I saw one.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "Je ne serais pas là si j'avais vu cela.  Pourquoi me demandez-vous ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've seen too many things out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "J'ai vu trop de choses là-dehors. Pourquoi voulez-vous savoir?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I won't let you leave just yet.  You're the new one here, I have so much to "
"ask.  Let me put it another way: what have you seen out there?  I'm talking "
"about the monsters that lurk deep in the woods.  Have you witnessed them with "
"your very own eyes?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne vous laisserai pas partir tout de suite.  Vous êtes le·a nouveau·elle "
"venu·e, j'ai tant de choses à vous demander.  Je vais vous le dire autrement: "
"qu'avez-vous vu·e loin d'ici?  Je parle des monstres qui se cachent au fond "
"des bois.  Les avez-vous vus de vos propres yeux?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've seen too much out there.  Why do you ask?"
msgstr "J'en ai trop vu.  Pourquoi cette question?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, let's just say I'm interested in rare game.  I've heard stories, rumors "
"and some tall tales about otherworldly beings out there in the wasteland.  "
"That's where you come in.  I want to see the evidence, something physical I "
"can collect as a trophy collection.  You seem to have experience, I was "
"hoping you could help me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Go and hunt them yourself.  You have a gun after all."
msgstr "Allez les chasser vous-même.  Vous avez une arme après tout."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got other things to deal with.  Do you really need these trophies?"
msgstr "J'ai d'autres chats à fouetter.  Avez-vous vraiment besoin de ces trophées ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can help.  Anyway, how are things?"
msgstr "Je peux vous aider.  Quoi qu'il en soit, comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Find somebody else, dude."
msgstr "Trouve quelqu'un d'autre, mec⸱euf."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've been better.  Having a hellish time keeping up with strange wildlife "
"that suddenly want us dead… hey, let's forget the world while we're talking.  "
"How's life treatin' ya?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai connu mieux.  J'ai du mal à suivre avec les nouvelles bêtes sauvages "
"étranges qui veulent soudainement notre peau… Oublions le monde pour un "
"moment pendant que nous parlons, comment va la vie?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion "
"happens to be collecting trophies.  I appreciate your help, by the way."
msgstr ""
"Écoutez, je suis juste un gars qui craint Dieu comme vous.  Il faut bien "
"avoir quelque chose pour se changer les idées.  Sinon, on devient fou.  Ma "
"passion est de collectionner des trophées.  J'apprécie votre aide comme même."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I'm just a regular God-fearing fella like you.  You gotta have "
"something to keep your mind off stuff.  You'd get mad otherwise.  My passion "
"happens to be collecting trophies."
msgstr ""
"Écoutez, je suis juste un gars qui craint Dieu, comme vous.  Il faut bien "
"avoir quelque chose pour se changer les idées.  Sinon, on devient fou.  Il se "
"trouve que ma passion est de collectionner des trophées."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your life, your escape mechanism…"
msgstr "Votre vie, votre mécanisme d'échappement…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh it's nothing new to me.  Livin' off the land, far from everyone - it's "
"just what I'm adjusted to.  I've kept in touch with the church folks, and "
"that was enough.  I had a loyal companion back home, Betsey, my rottweiler.  "
"Things have been very different since she passed away, though."
msgstr ""
"Oh, ce n'est pas nouveau pour moi.  Vivre de la terre, loin de tout le monde, "
"c'est ce à quoi je me suis habitué.  J'ai gardé le contact avec les gens de "
"l'église, et ça me suffisait.  J'avais une compagne fidèle à la maison, "
"Betsey, mon rottweiler.  Mais depuis sa mort, les choses ont beaucoup "
"changées."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you do now?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous faites maintenant?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about Betsey?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'en dire plus au sujet de Betsey?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hunt with most of my time these days.  Whatever game I spot, I bag and "
"donate.  Thing is, it's getting harder and harder.  Have you also noticed how "
"corruption is slowly overtaking the natural wildlife in this God-given "
"planet?  They think the flesh is just rotten.  No, it's mutated, become "
"something else."
msgstr ""
"Je chasse la plupart du temps ces jours-ci. Le gibier que j' attrape je "
"ramène ici et fait une donation. L'inconvénient et que ceci devient de plus "
"en plus compliqué. Vous avez remarqué que la nature sauvage de ce monde nous "
"ayant été donné par Dieu est en train d'être corrompue? Les autres pensent "
"que la chair est juste pourrie. Je pense qu'elle a mutée, qu'elle s'est "
"transformée en quelque chose d'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Russel's expression becomes somber, and he briefly stares at the wall.  "
"\"She was my dog, had her for seventeen years.  We used to go duck-hunting, "
"she'd swim out and get anything I shot.  She helped me track many a deer "
"through the woods…   When <the_cataclysm> hit, she saved me from some "
"<zombies> when we were skippin' town, but she died…  Then she came back, "
"wasn't herself…  I had to put her down.\""
msgstr ""
"&L'expression de Russel s'asombrit, et fixe brièvement le mur. \"C'était ma "
"chienne, cela faisait dix-sept ans que je l'avais. Nous allions souvent "
"chasser le canard et elle nageait pour ramener ce que j'avais réussi à "
"abattre. Elle m'a aussi aider à traquer un grand nombre de cerfs à travers "
"les bois… Lorsque <the_cataclysm> eu lieu, elle m'a sauvé d'un groupe de "
"<zombies> lorsque nous étions en train de nous enfuir de la ville où je "
"résidais, mais elle ne survécu pas à cela, revenant ensuite… mais ce n'était "
"pas elle… J'ai du l'achever.\""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Let's change the subject."
msgstr "Mes condoléances, changeons de sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I may be more skilled or better equipped but you, my friend, have something I "
"don't: experience.  A good hunter never leaves his hunting ground.  I sure "
"ain't gonna leave it!  Now you <name_g>, you know what it's REALLY like out "
"there!"
msgstr ""
"Peut être que j'ai plus de connaissances et d'équipement que vous, mais vous, "
"mon ami(e), avez quelque chose que je n'ai pas: de l'expérience de terrain. "
"Un bon chasseur ne quitte jamais son terrain de chasse et je n'ai pas "
"l'intention de le quitter! Mais vous, <name_g>, vous savez VRAIMENT comment "
"les choses sont en dehors de mon petit coin de nature!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I hate to break it to you, but I came here because I don't want to see the "
"world."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé⸱e de vous le dire, mais je suis venu⸱e ici parce que je ne "
"veux pas voir le monde."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm humbled by your words.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "And I hate to break it to you, but my point still stands."
msgstr "Et je suis désolé⸱e de vous le dire, mais mon point de vue reste valable."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're all desperately holding on to our stockpiles, but I can find something "
"for you.  I have some spare hides and pelts, if you're interested in buying."
msgstr ""
"Nous nous accrochons tous désespérément à nos réserves, mais je peux essayer "
"de trouver quelque chose pour vous. J'ai quelques peaux et fourrures en trop, "
"si cela vous intéresse."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Since I helped you out with your trophies, can I get a discount?"
msgstr ""
"Puisque je vous ai aidé avec vos trophées, est-ce que je peux avoir une "
"réduction?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's make a deal."
msgstr "Passons un marché."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't give a discount, but here's some meat instead.  Made by yours truly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Merci.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Russell_Connelly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see you around, Russell."
msgstr "Je vous remercie.  À bientôt, Russell."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Now that your guitar is fixed, could you play something for me?"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que votre guitare est réparée, pourriez-vous jouer quelque chose "
"pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's a nice guitar you have."
msgstr "C'est une belle guitare que vous avez."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Sonia glances at you harshly, then turns away.  \"Come back later, I'm busy "
"right now.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice of you to come around <u_name>."
msgstr "C'est gentil à vous d'être venu·e <u_name>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Good to see people like you in the world.  I'm Sonia, Sonia Greene.  I "
"entertain the people."
msgstr ""
"Ça fait plaisir qu'il y ait encore des personnes comme vous au monde. Je "
"m'appelle Sonia, Sonia Greene. Je divertit les gens."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sonia?  Nice to meet you, I'm <u_name>.  How are things here?"
msgstr "Sonia?  Enchanté·e, je m'appelle <u_name>.  Comment vous les choses?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Sonia.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Sonia.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey Sonia.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Sonia.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, see you later."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just playing some good ol' tunes.  There's so much negativity around here, "
"someone's gotta cheer people up, ya know?"
msgstr ""
"Je jouais juste quelques bons vieux morceaux.  Il y a tellement de négativité "
"par ici, il faut bien que quelqu'un remonte le moral des gens, vous savez?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothin' much, just sitting around and biding my time, getting any work I can. "
" I might play something to cheer everyone up, if my guitar wasn't busted."
msgstr ""
"Pas grand-chose, je reste assise sur mes fesses et j'attends mon heure, "
"travaillant autant que je peux quand il est possible d'aider.  Je pourrais "
"jouer quelque chose pour remonter le moral de tout le monde, si ma guitare "
"n'était pas cassée."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You're damn right.  I like its scars, makes it look like it has a history, "
"you know?  We've been through a lot.  Those pesky <zombies> forced me to harm "
"my sweet, sweet guitar, but I retaliated and bashed their heads in!  I lost a "
"part of me that day, but the guitar's alright.  Just a bit rusted from all "
"that blood and gore, that's all."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Now that's a wild story.  I owe my life to this kid Chloe, really.  I'll let "
"her tell the tale."
msgstr ""
"Ça, c'est est une histoire difficile à croire.  Je dois ma vie à cette "
"gamine, Chloé, vraiment.  Je la laisserai raconter l'histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was in an underground band - Taurists was our name - before all this.  "
"Performing gigs at local venues and jamming with my friends; that's all my "
"life was about.  Now, I'm a badass soloist with a war-torn guitar, a singer "
"of the old-world preserving the wonders of music and the Taurist legacy for "
"generations to come.  That's also a synonym for not having all that much "
"going on in my life."
msgstr ""
"Je faisais partie d'un groupe underground - Tauristes était notre nom - avant "
"tout cela.  Je donnais des concerts dans des salles locales et je jouais avec "
"mes amis, c'est tout ce qui comptait dans ma vie.  Aujourd'hui, je suis une "
"soliste à la guitare déchirée par la guerre, une chanteuse du monde d'avant "
"qui préserve les merveilles de la musique et l'héritage des Tauristes pour "
"les générations à venir.  C'est aussi une autre façon de dire que je ne sais "
"pas vraiment comment faire quoi que ce soit d'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, just fine.  A bit malnourished and all, but I can't really complain if "
"that's the worst of it, right?  My guitar makes our twisted little world a "
"bit more tolerable, though.  Takes my mind off stuff and muffles the screams "
"of the boogeyman, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, tout va bien.  Un peu sous-alimentée et tout ça, mais je ne peux pas "
"vraiment me plaindre si c'est ça le pire, non? Ma guitare rend notre petit "
"monde tordu un peu plus tolérable. Elle me permet de me changer les idées et "
"d'étouffer les cris du croque-mitaine, vous pigez?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fairly?  There's no such thing as fairness in the world.  The NECC wouldn't "
"give a damn if I starved to death on this very bench.  At least I have "
"friends here, ones that appreciate what I do.  I make music and that's all I "
"have left, it means everything to me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I can play you a tune or two that I know.  It will cost you a little "
"something, just one icon.  The artist doesn't want to starve, if you know "
"what I mean."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je peux vous jouer un ou deux airs que je connais.  Cela vous "
"coûtera un petit quelque chose, juste une icône.  L'artiste ne veut pas "
"mourir de faim, si vous voyez ce que je veux dire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, let's hear it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&Sonia doesn't say anything back, ignoring you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Sonia_Greene.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Walk away.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk about your goals."
msgstr "Parlons un peu de vos objectifs."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about yourself."
msgstr "Parle-moi de vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What the hell are you?  Get away from me!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's you again <u_name>, you have some nerve coming around after what you've "
"done."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, it's you again <u_name>!  Any news from the outside world?"
msgstr "Hé, alors c'est encore vous <u_name>!  Des nouvelles de monde extérieur?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Tom."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Tom."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Tom, got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Tom.  Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright, I'll leave you be."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Was it difficult to find us?  We haven't seen a single soul out there for so "
"long, I'm starting to lose my hope.  So, tell me about yourself."
msgstr ""
"Est-ce que ça a été difficile de nous trouver?  Nous n'avons pas vu une seule "
"âme depuis si longtemps et je commence à perdre espoir.  Parlez-moi de vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just a curious traveler.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr "Je ne suis qu'un·e voyageur·se curieux·se.  Et vous, comment allez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm seeking asylum here.  What about you, how are you doing?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey, that's nice of you to ask.  The people here are barely holding on.  "
"Malnutrition, sleepless nights, odd sounds from the woods, everyone turns a "
"little mad in these circumstances.  It's not their fault, I know, but they "
"did get what they wanted."
msgstr ""
"C'est gentil de demander.  Les gens d'ici tiennent à peine le coup.  "
"Malnutrition, nuits blanches, bruits étranges venant des bois, tout le monde "
"devient un peu fou dans ces circonstances.  Ce n'est pas de leur faute, je "
"sais, mais ils ont comme même obtenu ce qu'ils voulaient."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Please continue."
msgstr "Veuillez continuer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No rest for the weary.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "Pas de repos pour les braves.  À bientôt, Tom."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The sky has broken!  They received a rather passive-aggressive sign from God! "
" The wait is finally over.  Well, not for me.  So much is left unanswered, "
"and I know for a fact the answer's out there."
msgstr ""
"Le ciel s'est brisé!  Ils ont reçu un signe plutôt passif-agressif de la part "
"de Dieu!  L'attente est enfin terminée.  Enfin, pas pour moi.  Tant de choses "
"restent sans réponse, et je sais pertinemment que les réponses peuvent être "
"trouvées quelque part."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Perhaps it's not worth finding out."
msgstr "Peut-être que cela ne vaut pas la peine d'être découvert."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Try not to get stuck in the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "Essayez de ne pas rester figé dans le passé.  À bientôt, Tom."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Perhaps.  You don't wanna think about the stuff I'm thinking about, it would "
"spiral a newbie independent thinker into madness.  I don't blame you for "
"saying that."
msgstr ""
"Peut-être.  Vous ne voulez pas penser à ce à quoi je pense, cela ferait "
"sombrer un penseur indépendant néophyte dans la folie.  Je ne vais pas "
"prendre mal que vous ayez dit ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm currently in the middle of solving a pointless mystery for my own "
"entertainment.  Of course I have time!"
msgstr ""
"Je suis actuellement en train de résoudre un mystère inutile pour mon propre "
"divertissement.  Bien sûr que j'ai le temps!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I could help you with that mystery?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Désolé·e Tom.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I haven't got a story.  I'm an independent thinker.  Living out here, away "
"from the Man."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was nobody but an ordinary office drone.  Lived the average suburban life, "
"prepping for the inevitable.  Had the bright idea of purchasing a Last Man On "
"Earth shelter, but I decided to settle for less when I found out it cost five "
"times my annual salary.  That's how I ended up in a religious campground with "
"my family and a survival kit."
msgstr ""
"Je n'étais rien d'autre qu'un simple employé de bureau.  Je vivais une vie de "
"banlieue moyenne, me préparant à l'inévitable.  J'ai eu la brillante idée "
"d'acheter un abri du dernier homme sur terre, mais j'ai décidé de me "
"contenter de moins lorsque j'ai découvert que cela aurait coûté cinq fois mon "
"salaire annuel.  C'est pourquoi que je me suis retrouvé au milieu d'un camp "
"de religieux avec ma famille et un kit de survie."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All of us are here; me, Felicity, and Olwen.  We're so lucky, I feel like "
"crying tears of joy every time I see them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about Felicity?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que vous pouvez me dire au sujet de Felicity?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about Olwen?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet de Olwen?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She's my wife, we've been married for a while now.  We used to live in Rhode "
"Island, worked at a publishing firm, Stillwater.  She's always wanted to be a "
"writer, that's why we moved away.  We've been a bit distant as of late, I "
"don't think she's taking the \"whole end-of-the-world\" thing too well."
msgstr ""
"C'est ma femme, nous sommes mariés depuis un certain temps.  Nous vivions à "
"Rhode Island et travaillions dans une maison d'édition, Stillwater.  Elle a "
"toujours rêvé d'être écrivaine, c'est pourquoi nous avons déménagé.  Nous "
"avons été un peu distants ces derniers temps, je pense qu'elle ne prend pas "
"très bien cette histoire de fin du monde."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Olwen's a bright girl; she's fiddled with electronics and computers since she "
"was in high school.  She got a master's in it from the University of Rhode "
"Island.  Felicity's been a good mother for her, always been there for us.  "
"Olwen might be able to teach you a few things, she should be around here "
"somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Olwen est une fille brillante; elle bidouille avec l'électronique et "
"l'informatique depuis qu'elle est au lycée.  Elle a un master sur le sujet "
"accordé par l'université de Rhode Island.  Felicity a été une bonne mère pour "
"elle, elle a toujours été là pour nous.  Olwen pourrait vous apprendre "
"quelques trucs, elle devrait être dans le coin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I see that she is feeling down since <the_cataclysm> ruined their plans of "
"living together, but Julian was asking me the other day about my wedding with "
"Felicity so…  I can expect that to not last long."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I saw her big smile when receiving her ring from Julian, some days the smiles "
"of my family are what keeps me going after everything that happened…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She is constantly jumping from happiness after trying her wedding dress with "
"her mother…  I keep getting distracted from my investigation into "
"<the_cataclysm>, but seeing those two makes me smile so I can't stop seeing "
"their antics."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"New England Church Community is what they're called.  My wife was the first "
"in the family to come in contact with 'em.  She joined because of their "
"charity work and as for myself, well… you know why I was there.  Let me tell "
"you, being surrounded by like-minded folks was like a breath of fresh air.  "
"Even if the only belief we shared was paranoia, but you get what I'm saying.  "
"I tried everything to prep my family for the inevitable, I really did, but in "
"the end it wasn't me who saved us all."
msgstr ""
"On les appelle la Communauté Chrétienne de Nouvelle-Angleterre.  Ma femme a "
"été la première de la famille à entrer en contact avec eux.  Elle a adhéré à "
"cause de leurs œuvres caritatives et quant à moi, eh bien… vous savez "
"pourquoi j'étais là.  Laissez-moi vous dire que le fait d'être entouré de "
"personnes partageant les mêmes idées a été comme une bouffée d'air frais.  "
"Même si la seule croyance que nous partagions était la paranoïa, mais vous "
"voyez ce que je veux dire.  J'ai tout fait pour préparer ma famille à "
"l'inévitable, vraiment, mais en fin de compte, ce n'est pas moi qui nous ai "
"tous sauvés."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I want to find out the truth and preserve the past for the following "
"generation, so that they'll know some of what happened."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any progress?"
msgstr "Du progrès?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like an ambitious project.  Is there anything I can do to help you out?"
msgstr ""
"Ça m'a l'air d'un projet ambitieux. Je peux vous aider d'une manière ou d'une "
"autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good luck with that.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "Bonne chance.  À bientôt, Tom."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"So far?  Not so great.  Now that the Internet is down, I don't know.  Such "
"abundant hidden information - all gone!"
msgstr ""
"Jusqu'à présent?  Pas très bien.  Maintenant que l'Internet ne fonctionne "
"plus, je ne sais plus.  Une telle quantité d'informations cachées - tout est "
"perdu!"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Try not to glorify the past.  See you around, Tom."
msgstr "Essayez de ne pas glorifier le passé. Au revoir Tom."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Of course!  Just put all your literary findings on that chair over there.  "
"Remember, you're not only doing a favor for me, but for all of humanity as "
"well.  World heritage is what we're talking about!  I managed to get my hands "
"on a book called 'Zombie Survival Guide' while, uh… dumpster diving.  Imagine "
"how much this book alone reveals about our pre-Cataclysm culture!  Oh boy, "
"how wrong we were about everything."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I mean, can I help with the research?"
msgstr "Je veux dire, est-ce que je peux aider avec vos recherches?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No no no no no!  Thinking is one of the only thing I have left and you can't "
"take that away from me.  But, If you *really* want to make yourself useful, "
"relevant newspapers would help me piece out the puzzle."
msgstr ""
"Non, non, non, non, non!  La réflexion est l'une des seules choses qu'il me "
"reste et vous ne pouvez pas me l'enlever.  Mais si vous voulez vraiment vous "
"rendre utile, des journaux pertinents m'aideraient à reconstituer le puzzle."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Delivering <topic_item>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, I'm all out of them.  Now, I've got better things to do, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Tom_Powell.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay Tom, go ahead and be that way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you blow this joint and come with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're back?  Shove off <name_b>!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't worry, I'm not going to hurt you."
msgstr "N'aie pas peur, je ne vais pas te blesser."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I got here first, therefore this place belongs to me.  Them's the rules in "
"the <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Now that's an archaic belief.  I'll see you around."
msgstr "Eh bien voilà une croyance archaïque.  À bientôt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I ain't leaving, <name_g>.  Not until you or someone else has checked out "
"that nightmare for me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks, <name_g>.  I sure owe you one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I ain't leaving, <name_g>.  Not until that eldritch screeching nightmare is "
"dead 'n buried."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What nightmare?"
msgstr "Quel cauchemar?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see you around then."
msgstr "Je vous verrai plus tard dans ce cas-là"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Who I was is gone, dead… died when I put down the monsters wearing the face "
"of my friends.  Ever since then, I've felt nothing but disgust for myself.  "
"Let's not fuckin' reminisce."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They are nice people, lettin' us stay here 'n all.  I got friends here, and "
"while we may not be members we belong here.  We'll fight together if they "
"ever try to kick us out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It ain't so bad.  I got shelter, heat, and people to defend me if any "
"<zombie> shuffles its way in here.  If I want to eat then I'll be doin' "
"construction work all day."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas horrible. J'ai un toit au dessus de ma tête, il ne fait pas trop "
"froid et il y a d'autres personnes pour me défendre si un(e) <zombie> se "
"ramène. Et si j'ai besoin de manger je travaille."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Food is just the thing a starving man needs.  Thanks for the help, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"De la nourriture est ce dont l'homme affamé à besoin. Merci pour votre aide "
"<name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Je verrai ce que je peux faire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that <name_g>, but I don't feel like facing it either."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No chance!  Its not you, its the world out there I'm worried about.  All "
"those <freaking> monsters really give me the creeps, and as far as I know "
"this church is the last bastion of humanity in the <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/NPC_Zachary_Montes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's understandable."
msgstr "C'est compréhensible"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Could you be on your way, please?  We don't take kindly to sinners like you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Could you be on your way, please?  I'm rather busy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello again.  What do you need?"
msgstr "De nouveau bonjour.  De quoi avez-vous besoin?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*waves you over.  \"Hey <u_name>.  How's it going for you?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you?  Where am I right now?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous? Où suis-je?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/vampire_mentor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just passing through, don't mind me."
msgstr "Je ne fait que passer, ne me faites pas trop attention."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I have some food?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je pourrais avoir à manger?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard the joinees could get some food here."
msgstr "J'ai entendu que les nouveaux arrivants pouvaient reçevoir à manger ici."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, man.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Okay, shoot."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, what's up?"
msgstr "Ok, qu'est ce qu'il y a?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, let's chat."
msgstr "Ok, discutons."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are you holding up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way I could join the community?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about Katherine?"
msgstr "Que savez-vous au sujet de Katherine?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about Jeremiah?"
msgstr "Que savez-vous au sujet de Jeremiah?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've changed my mind, forget about it."
msgstr "J'ai changé d'avis, oubliez."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  See ya, <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is the New England Community Church, I should say it's one of their old "
"retreats.  I'm Simon, the head chef around here."
msgstr ""
"Ceci est la Communauté Chrétienne de Nouvelle-Angleterre, du moins un vieux "
"site de séminaire.  Je suis Simon, le chef de cuisine ici."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I used to volunteer as a cook in a homeless shelter.  I met the church "
"through that job; their missionaries would come by every so often and hand "
"out essentials to people living there, then give a sermon in one of the back "
"rooms.  Katherine and I wound up going to one of their sermons, and we've "
"stayed connected since.  Working in that shelter taught me to cook on a "
"shoestring budget; that's really useful these days, ya know."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where's your family now?"
msgstr "Où est votre famille en ce moment?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, <name_g>.  See you around."
msgstr "Merci, <name_g>.  À plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Katherine's probably in the bunks right now, and Jeremiah's next door.  Feel "
"free to say hello sometime."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who's Katherine?"
msgstr "Qui est Katherine?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who's Jeremiah?"
msgstr "Qui est Jeremiah?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "I'll do that."
msgstr "Je ferais ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's been a while since anyone gave out meals.  We're low on supplies around "
"here, I can't spare any.  I'm sorry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you accept any money for it?"
msgstr "Vous accepteriez de l'argent en échange?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Please?  I need it for my family."
msgstr "S'il vous plaît?  J'en ai besoin pour ma famille."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They can, but we're limited on the portions for now.  Hope you enjoy it, and "
"come back tomorrow for another."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, I wouldn't.  Like I said, we don't have any to spare."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It was worth a shot, I guess."
msgstr "Ça valait le coup d'essayer je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She's my wife, worked for the Church before <the_cataclysm>.  She used to "
"organize charities for the needy, now we're the ones in need of charity.  She "
"has a bit of a high horse these days, but a nice lady once you get to know "
"her.  We've been married for 28 years, and I couldn't ask for a better wife."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's good to hear.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's good to hear, but I gotta go."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Jeremiah is my son, he's a sweet boy and all grown up now.  We taught him "
"everything he knows, and we all had high hopes for how he could make it in "
"the world, before <the_cataclysm> took it away.  He doesn't like his mother, "
"Katherine, very much, and I've tried to help the two, but they can't seem to "
"properly get along."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why would they have an issue with each other?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Katherine is a bit overprotective of him, and ever since <the_cataclysm>, "
"she's become extremely worried for his safety.  He wants more independence, "
"seein' as how he's grown now, but she won't leave him be.  She tells me that "
"someone needs to keep an eye on him, so she took it upon herself to do so.  I "
"think she has the best intentions at heart, I know she loves him dearly, but "
"the boy needs to figure out some things on his own."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about Katherine?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous m'en dire plus au sujet de Katherine?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about Jeremiah?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous m'en dire plus au sujet de Jeremiah?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I have a family too.  I know how hard it is for you, but I've already "
"told you, rules are rules."
msgstr ""
"Écoutez, j'ai une famille aussi. Je sais que c'est difficile pour vous, mais "
"je comme j'ai déjà dit, les règles sont les règles."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess I'll starve."
msgstr "Je suppose que je vais mourir de faim."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Could be better, could be worse, but I'm not complaining.  I have everything "
"I need here; my family, a nice job, and roof over my head.  I only wish God "
"was as forgiving to others as to me."
msgstr ""
"Ça pourrait être mieux, ça pourrait être pire, mais je ne me plains pas.  "
"J'ai tout ce dont j'ai besoin ici: ma famille, un bon travail et un toit "
"au-dessus de ma tête.  J'aimerais seulement que Dieu soit aussi indulgent "
"envers les autres qu'envers moi."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to hear that."
msgstr "Ça fait plaisir à entendre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/cook.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'd have to talk to Gemma or Julian about that.  I'm sure there's a way, "
"though."
msgstr ""
"Vous allez devoir parler avec Gemma ou Julian pour ça. Je suis sûr qu'il "
"devrait y avoir un moyen pour vous d'arranger ça par contre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You better step away from me real quick, sinner.  I don't want your kind here."
msgstr ""
"Vous feriez mieux de vous éloigner de moi très vite, pécheur. Je ne veux pas "
"votre genre dans les environs."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What brings you around here <name_b>?  I don't want to see your face for a "
"while."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey there."
msgstr "Bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're back."
msgstr "Vous êtes de retour."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So…?"
msgstr "Donc…?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello.  What brings you around here?"
msgstr "Bonjour. Qu'est-ce qui vous amène?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just stopping by for a moment.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you again?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous déjà?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Care to talk for a bit?"
msgstr "Envie de discuter un peu?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright then, fuck you <name_b>."
msgstr "Très bien alors, allez vous faire foutre <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, what's happening?"
msgstr "Bien sûr, qu'est ce qu'il y a?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me a bit about yourself?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me raconter quelque chose à votre sujet?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you planning on doing in the future?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I borrow something from the stock?"
msgstr "Je peux emprunter quelque chose du stock?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be willing to buy any food?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Has anyone stolen from here?"
msgstr "Quelqu'un a déjà volé d'ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How much food do you have?"
msgstr "Quelle quantité de nourriture avez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can do to help you?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelque chose que je puisse faire pour vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Name's Eddie.  I'm making sure this stockpile is alright."
msgstr ""
"Le nom est Eddie. Je suis ici juste pour faire en sorte que ses réserves ne "
"soient pas dérangées."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you just chat for a bit?"
msgstr "Pourriez-vous discuter un peu ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nope, you can't do that.  I'd like to help you, but we've already got enough "
"mouths to feed."
msgstr ""
"Non, vous ne pouvez pas faire ça. J'aimerais vous aider, mais nous avons déjà "
"assez de bouches à nourrir."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could some money persuade you?"
msgstr "De l'argent pourrait vous persuader de changer d'avis?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can give these people one less mouth to feed, if you'd prefer that."
msgstr ""
"Je peux faire en sorte qu'au moins les gens ici n'ait plus jamais besoin de "
"vous nourrir, si vous préférez."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Très bien.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nobody's tried to yet.  It can get a little boring sometimes, standing around "
"and doing nothing."
msgstr ""
"Personne n'a essayé pour l'instant, c'est un peu ennuyant de temps en temps "
"de rester debout à ne rien faire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can understand that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I hope it isn't too boring.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's private info, <name_g>."
msgstr "Ce sont des informations privées <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nope, it couldn't.  Don't try and fuckin' bribe me again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Geez, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Ok. je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alright, alright.  Here's some food and water, <name_b>.  Get out of my sight."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keep that in mind."
msgstr "Gardez-ça en tête."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Okay, here's some food and water.  Don't tell anyone I gave you that."
msgstr ""
"Ok, voilà de l'eau et un peu de nourriture. Ne dites à personne que je vous "
"ai donné(e) ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I won't.  Pleasure doin' business."
msgstr "Je ne piperai pas un mot.  Un plaisir de faire affaire avec vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm just a regular guy, been with the Church for a while now.  I kept a good, "
"solid job before <the_cataclysm>, lived in a nice apartment on Chestnut "
"Street."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you do for a job before <the_cataclysm>?"
msgstr "Quel emploi occupiez-vous avant <the_cataclysm>?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any hobbies?"
msgstr "Avez-vous des hobbies?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I used to, me and my mother were pretty close.  I didn't know my father very "
"well for the first four years of my life, he was always out on deployment "
"with the Navy someplace.  Me and him got to know each other after he retired "
"from the service, we'd always go fishing on Sunday afternoons for years.  My "
"mother though, she was the sweetest lady you'd ever meet, always took care of "
"me and Dad.  Now they're gone, been that way for the last three years."
msgstr ""
"C'était le cas, ma mère et moi étions très proches. Je n'ai pas beaucoup "
"connu mon père pendant les quatre premières années de ma vie, car il était "
"toujours en déploiement dans la marine. Nous avons appris à nous connaître, "
"lui et moi, après qu'il a pris sa retraite, et nous sommes allés pêcher le "
"dimanche après-midi pendant des années. Ma mère, elle, était la femme la plus "
"douce que l'on puisse rencontrer, elle s'est toujours occupée de moi et de "
"papa. Aujourd'hui, ils ne sont plus là, et ce depuis trois ans."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're mother must've been very nice."
msgstr "Votre mère doit avoir été très gentille."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was your father like?"
msgstr "Comment était votre père?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"She sure was, helped me through some very hard times in my life.  I used to "
"be bullied in middle school, whenever I'd get beat up, she'd always help "
"clean me up and tell me I'd be alright.  She had this recipe for peach "
"casserole too, best one in the world.  It was hard for me when she passed, "
"but I found some solace right here in this Church.  We'd always been "
"religious, but this one just clicked for me, ya know?"
msgstr ""
"Elle m'a aidé à traverser des périodes très difficiles de ma vie. J'étais "
"victime de brimades au collège, et chaque fois que je me faisais battre, elle "
"m'aidait à me nettoyer et me disait que tout irait bien. Elle avait aussi une "
"recette de ragoût de pêches, la meilleure du monde. Cela a été dur pour moi "
"quand elle est décédée, mais j'ai trouvé un peu de réconfort ici, dans cette "
"église. Nous avons toujours été croyants, mais cette église a eu un déclic "
"pour moi, vous savez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is that why you joined the Church?"
msgstr "Est-ce pour cela que vous avez rejoint l'Église?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He was a nice fellow, taught me everything I know about firearms, wildlife, "
"and sailing.  We lived next to this big ol' lake, so we had plenty of "
"opportunities to catch bass and catfish.  He'd skin and filet them, and we'd "
"have it for dinner.  My mother always cooked them, and she was great at it."
msgstr ""
"C'était un homme sympathique, qui m'a appris tout ce que je sais sur les "
"armes à feu, la faune et la flore, et la navigation. Nous vivions à côté d'un "
"grand lac, ce qui nous donnait de nombreuses occasions d'attraper des perches "
"et des poissons-chats. Il les dépouillait et les découpait en filets, et nous "
"les mangions pour le dîner. Ma mère les cuisinait toujours, et elle était "
"excellente dans ce domaine."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're mother sounds very nice, what was she like?"
msgstr "Votre mère a l'air très gentille, comment était-elle ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, her death was hard on me.  I wound up goin' here one day, and I felt "
"something come over me, like I belonged here.  I haven't left since, and I've "
"been able to move on with them."
msgstr ""
"Oui, sa mort a été dure pour moi. J'ai fini par venir ici un jour, et j'ai "
"senti quelque chose m'envahir, comme si j'étais à ma place ici. Je ne suis "
"pas reparti depuis, et j'ai pu aller de l'avant avec eux."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I used to work for the U.S Postal Service, I was a mail carrier.  Delivered "
"all the letters, packages, and mail orders to the residents of <city>, "
"door-to-door.  It was pretty hard at times, but it kept me fit and on the "
"road."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really like to draw things, I primarily did landscapes in my spare time.  I "
"like paper-and-pencil sketches, but I have worked with watercolors and oil "
"canvases.  Never could get my head around the digital stuff, though, too "
"complex for me and I never had a good free hand with a stylus.  I also shot a "
"bit, went hunting a few times.  I mainly went to the gun range though, "
"shotguns were always my forte.  Besides that, I watched some TV and regular "
"ol' stuff.  I also like to read quite a bit, too."
msgstr ""
"J'aime beaucoup dessiner des choses, j'ai surtout fait des paysages pendant "
"mon temps libre. J'aime les croquis sur papier et au crayon, mais j'ai aussi "
"travaillé avec des aquarelles et des toiles à l'huile. Je n'ai jamais réussi "
"à me familiariser avec le numérique, trop complexe pour moi et je n'ai jamais "
"eu une bonne main libre avec un stylet. J'ai aussi tiré un peu, je suis allé "
"chasser quelques fois. J'allais surtout au stand de tir, les fusils de chasse "
"ont toujours été mon point fort. À part cela, j'ai regardé la télévision et "
"d'autres choses. J'aime aussi beaucoup lire."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess those shooting skills come in handy these days."
msgstr "Je suppose que ces compétences en matière de tir sont utiles de nos jours."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You must be a very good artist then.  Do you still have time to draw?"
msgstr ""
"Vous devez donc être un très bon artiste. Avez-vous encore le temps de "
"dessiner ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess they will.  I pray to God that I won't have to shoot someone, I never "
"want to be forced into deciding between life or death."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose qu'ils le feront. Je prie Dieu de ne pas avoir à tirer sur "
"quelqu'un, je ne veux jamais être obligé de décider entre la vie et la mort."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me about your hobbies again?"
msgstr "Pourriez-vous me parler à nouveau de vos hobbies?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm alright at it, I guess.  I'm no Van Gough or Botticelli, but I get along "
"with it and do my best.  I've started using the desk up here to work on these "
"days, I just need to keep my firearm close and one eye on the door."
msgstr ""
"Je me débrouille bien, je crois. Je ne suis pas Van Gough ou Botticelli, mais "
"je me débrouille et je fais de mon mieux. J'ai commencé à utiliser le bureau "
"d'ici pour travailler ces jours-ci, je dois juste garder mon arme à feu à "
"proximité et un œil sur la porte."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know anymore, to tell you the truth.  I was planning on settling down "
"and having kids, but now that everyone's dead and the judgment of God has "
"come to pass, I'll seek His truth and try to keep on living.  One day, when "
"this is all over, I'll fly away to Heaven's pearly gates and be with the "
"angels.  As for the Earth, I'd rather not think about the things that have "
"come to pass."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/members/foodguard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I'd be willing to purchase some.  I'll have to work up the money with "
"Helena, but I'm sure we've got it.  I'd prefer canned, and preserved goods.  "
"How much are you talkin'?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je serais prêt à en acheter. Je vais devoir trouver l'argent avec "
"Helena, mais je suis sûr que nous l'avons. Je préférerais des conserves et "
"des produits préservés. De combien parlez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*looks up at you in uninterested fashion.  \"What do you want?  I'm working."
msgstr ""
"*regarde vers vous d'un air désintéressé. « Qu'est-ce que tu veux ? Je "
"travaille."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, uh, sorry."
msgstr "Oh, euh, pardon."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here to pick up a delivery."
msgstr "Je suis venu chercher une livraison."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back for the records, and I have the money."
msgstr "Je suis de retour pour les enregistrements, et j'ai l'argent."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back for your records."
msgstr "Je suis de retour pour vos archives."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The boss wants your accounting papers, I need them."
msgstr "Le patron veut vos documents comptables, j'en ai besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh nothing, I must have the wrong person."
msgstr "Oh rien, je dois me tromper de personne."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "They're not ready yet, you'll have to come back later."
msgstr "Ils ne sont pas encore prêts, vous devrez revenir plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll just take them as is, thanks.  Everything can be finalized later."
msgstr "Je les prends tels quels, merci. Tout peut être finalisé plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We both know that's a lie.  Hand them over, or else."
msgstr "Nous savons tous les deux que c'est un mensonge.  Donnez-ça, ou bien…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I get them for a price?"
msgstr "Pourrais-je les obtenir à un certain prix ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When will they be ready?"
msgstr "Quand seront-ils prêts?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, see ya."
msgstr "D'accord, à plus."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just two more days is all I need with them, then the boss can do whatever.  "
"Is that good?"
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai besoin que de deux jours de plus avec eux, après quoi le patron peut "
"faire ce qu'il veut. Est-ce que c'est bien ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll be back then."
msgstr "D'accord, je reviendrai alors."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I need them now."
msgstr "Non, j'en ai besoin maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know what the hell you want them for, but I sure don't care.  Take "
"'em, <name_b>."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas pourquoi vous les voulez, mais je m'en fiche. Prenez-les, "
"<name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, <name_b>."
msgstr "Merci <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How much are you thinking?"
msgstr "À combien pensez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does $5 sound good?"
msgstr "Est-ce que 5 $, ça vous va ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about $20?"
msgstr "Que diriez-vous de 20 $ ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll give you $50, my best offer."
msgstr "Je vous propose 50 $, ma meilleure offre."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*holds their abdomen as they nearly keel over from laughter.  \"You better be "
"glad that I think you're funny, anyone else would find it an insult.  $150 is "
"more like it to me."
msgstr ""
"*Il se tient l'abdomen alors qu'il manque de s'écrouler de rire. « Tu ferais "
"mieux d'être content que je te trouve drôle, n'importe qui d'autre trouverait "
"ça insultant. Pour moi, 150 dollars, c'est plutôt ça."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, here it is."
msgstr "Très bien, le voici."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't take kindly to your jokes, <name_b>.  Hand 'em over or else."
msgstr "Je n'aime pas vos plaisanteries, <name_b>. Remettez-les moi, ou bien."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*seems to get lost in thought for a moment, before looking back at you.  "
"\"Alright, you have a deal."
msgstr ""
"*Il semble se perdre dans ses pensées pendant un moment, avant de se tourner "
"à nouveau vers vous. « D'accord, vous avez un marché."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pleasure doing business."
msgstr "Ça a été un plaisir de faire affaire avec vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*seems to get lost in thought for a moment, before looking back at you.  "
"\"Nah, I think $150 would be a better price."
msgstr ""
"*Il semble se perdre dans ses pensées pendant un moment, avant de vous "
"regarder à nouveau. « Nan, je pense que 150$ serait un meilleur prix."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about I don't give you any money instead?  Hand 'em over or else."
msgstr "Et si je ne vous donnais pas d'argent?  Donnez-moi tout ça, sinon…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds great to me."
msgstr "Cela me semble très bien."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I think you can go a bit higher, $150 and the records are yours."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que vous pouvez aller un peu plus haut, 150 $ et les disques sont à "
"vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC makes sound in effect in EoC "EOC_BRIBE_20_FALSE_EFFECT"
#. ~ NPC makes sound in effect in EoC "EOC_BRIBE_50_FALSE_EFFECT"
#. ~ NPC makes sound in effect in EoC "EOC_BRIBE_150_FALSE_EFFECT"
msgid "Come back later when you have the money, then we'll talk."
msgstr "Revenez plus tard lorsque vous avez l'argent, et l'on pourra parler."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_GUARD_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC makes sound in effect in EoC "EOC_BRIBE_LATER_TRUE_EFFECT"
msgid "A pleasure doin' business with you."
msgstr "Un plaisir de faire affaire avec vous."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything suspicious, you're "
"outnumbered here and we're well armed, and my boss will know what happens "
"soon enough."
msgstr ""
"Bien, bien, bien, un autre voyageur. Ne tentez rien de suspect, vous êtes "
"plus nombreux que nous et nous sommes bien armés, et mon patron saura ce qui "
"se passe bien assez tôt."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you threatening me?"
msgstr "Vous essayez de m'intimider?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your deal here?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui se passe ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I won't try anything if you don't.  Just passing through."
msgstr "Je n'essaierai rien si vous ne le faites pas. Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have anything to trade?"
msgstr "Vous avez des choses à échanger?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your prices seem awfully high."
msgstr "Vos prix semblent terriblement élevés."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing much.  Just passing through."
msgstr "Pas grand chose.  Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, not at all.  Just being cautious.  You know how it gets out here.  We're "
"not looking for trouble.  In fact, if you've got anything worthwhile, maybe "
"we could do a little trading."
msgstr ""
"Non, pas du tout. Je suis juste prudent. Vous savez comment ça se passe ici. "
"Nous ne cherchons pas les ennuis. En fait, si vous avez quelque chose "
"d'intéressant, nous pourrions peut-être faire un peu de commerce."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, let's trade."
msgstr "Ok, faisons un peu de troc."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That suits me fine.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's it?  What's your story?"
msgstr "C'est tout ? Quelle est votre histoire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's interesting.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "C'est intéressant.  Eh bien, échangeons."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me directions to any of these other survivor groups?"
msgstr ""
"Pouvez-vous m'indiquer comment me rendre dans l'un de ces autres groupes de "
"survivants ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for chatting.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci pour la discussion.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers "
"directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr ""
"Ne le prenez pas mal, mais mes clients n'aimeraient certainement pas que je "
"donne à des étrangers des indications sur leurs cachettes. Vous devrez les "
"trouver par vos propres moyens."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can understand that.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Je peux comprendre cela.  Eh bien, échangeons."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Heh, always good to do business."
msgstr "Eh, toujours un plaisir de faire du business."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "En fait, je croix que j'ai encore quelques trucs à échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You got anything else?"
msgstr "Vous avez autre chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  What were we talking about before?"
msgstr "Merci.  De quoi parlions-nous auparavant?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for that.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well, not right now.  Try again after around <interval>."
msgstr "Pas tout de suite. Réessayez après environ <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay.  About other things…"
msgstr "D'accord.  À propos d'autres choses…"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  I'd like to buy something."
msgstr "Ok.  J'aimerais acheter quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think you're full of shit.  I know you're gouging for your own benefit, and "
"wouldn't it be a shame if this information were to get out?"
msgstr ""
"Je pense que vous êtes un escroc. Je sais que vous vous enrichissez sur le "
"dos des autres, et ne serait-il pas dommage que cette information soit "
"divulguée?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/vampire_mentor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  What were we talking about before?"
msgstr "D'accord.  De quoi parlions-nous avant?"

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Woah woah woah, cool your jets.  I can't let this spread about me, so name "
"your price and keep quiet, and I might give you a discount."
msgstr ""
"Wow wow wow calmos. Je ne veux pas qu'une rumeur comme ça se répande à mon "
"sujet, alors dites-moi ce que vous voulez pour la boucler, et peut être que "
"je peux vous offrir des offres au rabais."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "50 merch and you have a deal."
msgstr "50 merch et marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know what, I don't want your <freaking> dirty money.  Go fuck yourself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What proof do you have <name_b>?  Nothing is what you got, and your the only "
"one here who's full of shit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you don't wanna cooperate, I'll stop this by force."
msgstr "Si vous ne voulez pas coopérer, j'y mettrai fin par la force."

#: data/json/npcs/godco/visitors/TALK_CARAVAN_MERCHANT_PREDATORY.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Get out of here, <name_b>."
msgstr "Sortez d'ici, <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Fenceman"
msgstr "Receleur"

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#. ~ Job description of "Fenceman" NPC class
msgid "I sell illegal things."
msgstr "Je vends des choses illégales."

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/npc.json
#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic quartermaster for the Hell's Raiders.
#. ~ Old guard quatermaster
msgid "Quartermaster"
msgstr "Intendant"

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#. ~ Job description of "Quartermaster" NPC class
msgid "I manage garrison supplies."
msgstr "Je gère les provisions."

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Bandit Leader"
msgstr "Leader de Bandits"

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/classes.json
#. ~ Job description of "Bandit Leader" NPC class
msgid "I lead a bandit clan."
msgstr "Je dirige un clan de bandits."

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/npc.json data/mods/No_Hope/NPC/npc.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic pistol/rifle focused guard for the Hell's Raiders faction.
#. ~ The boss of a local raider clan.
#. ~ Generic trader for the Hell's Raiders.
msgid "Bandit"
msgstr "Bandit"

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/npc.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ EOC-specific, should not spawn outside of trigger events.
msgid "assassin"
msgstr "assassin"

#: data/json/npcs/hells_raiders/npc.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Automotive specialist for the Hells Raiders.
msgid "Mechanic"
msgstr "Mécano"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A survivor raising rabbits, all by themselves. Give special quests to
#. give rabbits to player
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ This is a unique NPC who doesn't get randomly selected background traits
msgid "Mr. Lapin"
msgstr "Mr. Lapin"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ A survivor raising rabbits, all by themselves. Give special quests to
#. give rabbits to player
msgid "Warrener"
msgstr "Éleveur de Lapins"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Job description of "Mr. Lapin" NPC class
#. ~ This is a unique NPC who doesn't get randomly selected background traits
msgid "I raise rabbits."
msgstr "J’élève des lapins."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are you here to protect us?"
msgstr "Êtes-vous ici pour nous protéger?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Pleased to meet you."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just trying to get by."
msgstr "J'essaie juste de survivre."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Heard anything about the outside world?"
msgstr "Vous avez entendu quelque chose sur le monde extérieur?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You look different?"
msgstr "Vous semblez différent·e?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I can help with?"
msgstr "Je peux aider avec quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that work…"
msgstr "Au sujet de ce boulot…"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you need any resources?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did you get that giant firefly terrarium?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que vous avez trouvé ce terrarium à luciole géante?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Getting by will do for now."
msgstr "Juste survivre est assez pour moi pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess it has to."
msgstr "Je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I raise my rabbits, I seem to have more in common with them every day."
msgstr ""
"J'élève mes lapins, j'ai l'air d'avoir de plus en plus de choses en commun "
"avec eux chaque jour."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, then…"
msgstr "Dans ce cas…"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"People come to me to learn how to keep rabbits.  They learn and they go.  I "
"like to think I'm making the world better."
msgstr ""
"Les gens viennent à moi pour apprendre à élever des lapins. Ils apprennent et "
"s'en vont. J'aime penser que je rends le monde un peu moins horrible."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anyone nearby I should meet?"
msgstr "Il y a quelqu'un dans les environs que je devrais rencontrer?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds optimistic?"
msgstr "Ceci sonne assez optimiste?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is a family of nearby farmers that I trade with.  I'd appreciate it if "
"you could go check on them."
msgstr ""
"Il y a une famille de fermiers dans les environs avec qui je troque. "
"J'apprécierais si vous pouviez allez vérifier qu'ils vont bien."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Seems like a deal to me."
msgstr "Ça m'a l'air raisonnable."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems rather dangerous, I think I'll pass."
msgstr "Ceci semble un peu trop dangereux, je pense que je vais décliner."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It can be quite a hike depending on your transportation.  Lot of bad news "
"between here and there."
msgstr ""
"Ça peut être un petit bout de chemin entre ici et là-bas dépendant de votre "
"mode de transportation avec beaucoup de dangers potentiels sur le chemin."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't worry, I'll be careful."
msgstr "Ne vous inquiétez pas, je serais prudent."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a walk in the woods."
msgstr "Juste une marche à travers les bois."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If I teach one hundred people how to raise rabbits, that's potentially a "
"hundred communities given food and fur before those people teach anyone else."
msgstr ""
"Si j'apprends à cent personnes à élever des lapins, c'est potentiellement "
"cent communautés auxquelles je peux donner de la nourriture et de la "
"fourrure, et ceci est avant que mes élèves apprennent à qui que ce soit "
"d'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's the most hopeful thing I've heard so far."
msgstr "C'est la chose la plus optimiste que j'ai entendue jusqu'à présent."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A traveler brought this to me in return for some rabbits.  Said that he'd "
"gotten it from a scientist out in the swamps but it took up too much space in "
"his car."
msgstr ""
"Une personne me l'a donné en échange de lapins, me disant qu'elle l'avait "
"reçue de la part d'un scientifique dans les marais mais qu'il prenait trop de "
"place dans sa voiture."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's quite unique!"
msgstr "C'est assez unique!"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Same way you got yours, I bet."
msgstr "De la même manière que vous avez obtenu le vôtre, je parie."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "CRISPR?  Radiation?  Something in the water?  Maybe it was bunnies."
msgstr ""
"CRISPR? Radiation? Quelque chose dans l'eau potable? Peut être même que "
"c'était des lapins de ce que je sais."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So it goes."
msgstr "C'est ainsi que les choses se passent."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're disgusting."
msgstr "Vous êtes dégueulasse "

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm very sorry to tell you this, but you should look in a mirror."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé⸱e de vous dire cela, mais vous devriez-vous regarder dans un "
"miroir."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Insulting people who could help you is unlikely to aid survival."
msgstr ""
"Insultez ceux qui pourrait vous aider n'est probablement pas une bonne "
"tactique de survie."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The bunnies and I love adding some diversity to the menu and I always need "
"materials for patching fences."
msgstr ""
"Les lapins et moi aimons ajouter de temps à autre de la diversité au menu et "
"j'ai toujours besoin de matériaux pour réparer les clôtures."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's all for now.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's all for now.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Timber!"
msgstr "Timber!"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Timber!"
msgid "Bring five logs."
msgstr "Ramenez cinq bûches."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
msgid "I need 5 logs for fences."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 5 bûches pour construire des barrières."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
msgid ""
"I need to build fences and ditches around my rabbits.  Could you find about… "
"five logs for me?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai besoin de construire des clôtures et des fossés autour de mes lapins.  "
"Pourriez vous trouvez… cinq bûches pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
msgid "There's a lot of places to look.  Trees are pretty common."
msgstr ""
"Il y a beaucoup d'endroits où vous pourriez en trouver, il ne manque pas "
"d'arbres."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Timber!"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Big Game Hunting"
msgid "How is the search going?  Have you found'em?"
msgstr "Comment va votre recherche? Vous avez trouvé ce que je vous ai demandé?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Sweets"
msgstr "Bonbons"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Sweets"
msgid "Find 25 blackberries."
msgstr "Trouvez 25 mûres"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
msgid "I need 25 blackberries."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 25 mûres"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
msgid "Fruits would let me break the monotony of grains and meats."
msgstr ""
"Un peu de fruits devrait m'aider à rompre la monotonie des féculents et de la "
"viande."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
msgid ""
"Thanks for accepting this task.  Otherwise I might kill a stranger for some "
"oranges.  Just kidding."
msgstr ""
"Merci d'avoir accepter cette tâche, ou j'aurais peut être tué un inconnu pour "
"des oranges. Je plaisante bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
msgid "Find someone growing berries or an orchard."
msgstr "Trouvez quelqu'un faisant pousser des baies ou possédant un verger."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
msgid "Have you found the fruit?"
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé les fruits?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sweets"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bread"
msgid "Thank you for your help.  Here's your reward."
msgstr "Merci pour votre aide. Voilà votre récompense."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Visit the Isherwoods"
msgstr "Visitez les Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
msgid ""
"There is a family nearby that I'd like you to check in on.  After you talk to "
"all of them, come back to me and tell me how they are doing."
msgstr ""
"Il y a une famille dans les environs que j'apprécierais si vous pouviez "
"vérifier si tout va bien pour eux.  Après avoir parlé à tout le monde, "
"revenez me voir et dites-moi comment ils vont."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
msgid "Have you checked on them?"
msgstr "Vous les avez visités?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
msgid "Good, that's one less thing to worry about."
msgstr "Bien, une préoccupation de moins"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
msgid "I'm glad to hear they are fine.  Why haven't they been by then?"
msgstr "Je suis heureux d'apprendre qu'ils vont bien. Pourquoi ne l'ont-ils pas fait ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Mr_Lapin.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/draco_dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Visit the Isherwoods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Go check out this island"
msgid "At least you came back with your life…"
msgstr "Au moins, vous êtes revenu·e vivant·e…"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ Hunter with indigenous ancestry and big ideas.
msgid "Glooscap"
msgstr "Glouscap"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you again, how can I help you?"
msgstr "Ça fait plaisir de vous revoir, qu'est-ce que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know storms?  Used to be more.  Took me a lot of work, but there aren't "
"as many now.  That was me, I did that.  Fewer storms, pretty good.  There's a "
"big eagle, it's a long story really.  I'm good with rope though."
msgstr ""
"Vous connaissez les tempêtes ? Il y en avait plus avant. Ça m'a demandé "
"beaucoup de travail, mais il n'y en a plus autant maintenant. C'est moi qui "
"l'ai fait. Moins de tempêtes, c'est pas mal. Il y a un grand aigle, c'est une "
"longue histoire. Mais je sais me servir d'une corde."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's decided then.  I will be Glooscap.  Who will you be?"
msgstr "C'est décidé. Je serai Glooscap. Qui seras-tu ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glooscap?  That's a funny name.  Is it foreign?"
msgstr "Glooscap ? C'est un drôle de nom. Est-ce un nom étranger ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 11]  Like the Wabanaki myth?"
msgstr "[INT 11]  Comme la figure mythologique Wabanaki?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So.  You're dressed like a hunter.  Are you a hunter?"
msgstr "Vous êtes habillé comme un chasseur. Êtes-vous un chasseur ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you had any luck out there?"
msgstr "Avez-vous eu de la chance ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Whatever, I don't have time for whatever this is.  Try not to get your face "
"eaten I guess."
msgstr ""
"Peu importe, je n'ai pas le temps pour ce que c'est. Essayez de ne pas vous "
"faire manger la figure, je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, my name has been a name here for a very long time too."
msgstr "Non, mon nom a été un nom ici pendant très longtemps aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I just made it up."
msgstr "Non, je viens de l'inventer."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, I just got here.  What's happening?"
msgstr "Oui, je viens d'arriver. Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know about names, let's talk about something more interesting."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas ce qu'il en est des noms, parlons plutôt de quelque chose de "
"plus intéressant."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know the real people's stories?  Yes, a lot like that."
msgstr ""
"Vous connaissez les histoires de personnes réelles ? Oui, beaucoup de choses "
"comme ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cool, cool.  So you like myths and stuff?"
msgstr "Cool, cool. Tu aimes les mythes et tout ça ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 14] Do you have a twin named Malsumis?"
msgstr "[INT 14] Avez-vous un jumeau appelé Malsumis?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yes, I'm a very smart survivor of the apocalypse.  <end_talking_leave>  Later "
"Glooscap."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Beer] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some drinks with me, "
"want to have some?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer India Pale Ale] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some "
"drinks with me, want to have some?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Cigarettes] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have some "
"cigarettes, want one with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Joint] I am extremely into your smile yes.  I have something to smoke, "
"want to have some with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You seem cool but I don't have anything fun.  I'll try and find something and "
"come back so we can share."
msgstr ""
"Tu as l'air cool mais je n'ai rien d'amusant. Je vais essayer de trouver "
"quelque chose et je reviendrai pour qu'on puisse partager."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PRETTY] That smile is very nice.  It makes me smile too."
msgstr "[JOLI] Ce sourire est très beau. Il me fait sourire aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[GLORIOUS] Worship my beauty."
msgstr "[GLORIOUS]  Vénérez ma beauté."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[TERRIFYING] Fear me!  I am disgusting!"
msgstr "[TERRIFYANT] Craignez-moi ! Je suis dégoûtant !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[TERRIFYING] Destroy me!"
msgstr "[TERRIFIANT] Détruisez-moi!"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 14] I'll look out then, thanks.  Of course if you were Malsumis you "
"probably wouldn't admit it because no one likes Malsumis.  Who would your "
"twin say you are?"
msgstr ""
"[INT 14]  J'y veillerai, merci. Bien sûr, si vous étiez Malsumis, vous ne "
"l'admettriez probablement pas, car personne n'aime les Malsumis. Qui votre "
"jumeau dirait-il que vous êtes ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know you're not really Glooscap right?  You're joking right?"
msgstr "Vous savez que vous n'êtes pas vraiment Glooscap non? Vous rigolez juste?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Of course, that all makes as much sense as anything I guess.  So you have "
"crazy supernatural powers then?  Can you stop whatever is happening and make "
"it like before?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, c'est tout à fait logique, je suppose. Vous avez donc des pouvoirs "
"surnaturels ? Tu peux arrêter ce qui se passe et faire en sorte que tout "
"redevienne comme avant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know what Malsumis would say, Malsumis is very tricky.  I always tell "
"the truth, it's very boring."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas ce que Malsumis dirait, Malsumis est très délicat. Je dis "
"toujours la vérité, c'est très ennuyeux."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 14] I think you're Malsumis.  Where is Glooscap?"
msgstr "[INT 14] Je pense que vous êtes Malsumis. Où est Glooscap ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 14] Yes, that all makes sense to me.  Forget I asked."
msgstr "[INT 14] Oui, tout cela me semble logique. Oubliez ma question."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I don't have time for this.  I have serious survival business to do.  I am a "
"serious survival business person."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas le temps pour cela. J'ai des choses sérieuses à faire pour "
"survivre. Je suis un homme d'affaires sérieux."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fight me Malsumis!"
msgstr "Combattez-moi, Malsumis !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[SKILLED LIAR] Then you're definitely not Malsumis and everything is cool.  "
"So Malsumis wants to kill everybody right?  I guess they're feeling pretty "
"great right now huh?"
msgstr ""
"[MENTEUR HABILE] Alors vous n'êtes pas Malsumis et tout va bien. Alors "
"Malsumis veut tuer tout le monde, c'est ça ? Je suppose qu'ils se sentent "
"bien en ce moment, hein ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Haha, good one Glooscap.  So funny.  Love that.  Let's move on."
msgstr "Haha, bien joué Glooscap. Très drôle. J'adore ça. Passons à autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This is awkward.  I need to leave."
msgstr "Tout cela est assez embarrassant.  Je pense qu'il est temps que je m'en aille."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe.  Is it worse to be unhappy with a goal or to be unhappy without a "
"goal?  You're all right, I feel like we get each other."
msgstr ""
"Peut-être. Est-il pire d'être malheureux avec un objectif ou d'être "
"malheureux sans objectif ? Vous allez bien, j'ai l'impression que nous nous "
"comprenons."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I feel the same way best friend."
msgstr "Je ressens la même chose, mon meilleur ami."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No idea what you mean."
msgstr "Aucune idée de quoi vous parlez."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Haha, right.  What would Glooscap be doing in the sunrise lands at the "
"beginning of the fourth age?  That's silly.  I'm probably some Wabanaki that "
"got hit on the head or something.  And who turns into a beaver?  Haha.  You "
"got me.  Just a normal human made out of trees like the rest."
msgstr ""
"Haha, c'est vrai. Que ferait Glooscap dans les terres du soleil levant au "
"début du quatrième âge ? C'est idiot. Je suis probablement un Abénaquis qui a "
"reçu un coup sur la tête ou quelque chose comme ça. Et qui se transforme en "
"castor ? Haha. Tu m'as eu. Juste un humain normal fait d'arbres comme les "
"autres."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No problem, a lot of people are going through some hard times right now.  "
"Honestly, you're doing better than most.  You should follow me, I have a "
"pretty good handle on reality."
msgstr ""
"Pas de problème, beaucoup de gens traversent des moments difficiles en ce "
"moment. Honnêtement, vous vous en sortez mieux que la plupart. Vous devriez "
"me suivre, j'ai une bonne maîtrise de la réalité."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm not made out of trees, I'm made out of awesome.  Follow me and you will "
"grow fat and rich."
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis pas fait d'arbres, je suis fait de merveilles. Suivez-moi et vous "
"deviendrez gros et riche."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You shouldn't follow me, but I guess I can't stop you."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne devriez pas me suivre, mais je suppose que je ne peux pas vous "
"arrêter."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Another world is going and a new world is coming.  I hope this new one is "
"better than the last, a new golden age.  So far not great."
msgstr ""
"Un autre monde s'en va et un nouveau monde arrive. J'espère qu'il sera "
"meilleur que le précédent, un nouvel âge d'or. Pour l'instant, ce n'est pas "
"terrible."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure sure.  So are you on drugs?"
msgstr "Bien sûr.  Vous êtes drogué non?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Whatever, I don't have time for creepy stuff."
msgstr "Quoi qu'il en soit, je n'ai pas le temps de m'occuper de choses effrayantes."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, thank you for sharing with me.  So what are you doing here?  What are "
"you trying to accomplish?"
msgstr ""
"Oui, merci de partager avec moi. Que faites-vous ici ? Qu'essayez-vous "
"d'accomplir ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 14] I'm trying to understand what happened and see if I can make "
"something better happen."
msgstr ""
"[INT 14] J'essaie de comprendre ce qui s'est passé et de voir si je peux "
"améliorer les choses."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm trying to become more powerful than whatever else is out there."
msgstr "J'essaie de devenir plus puissant que toute les choses rôdant par ici."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm trying to make a survivor settlement.  You should join!"
msgstr ""
"J'essaie de mettre en place un règlement pour les survivants. Vous devriez "
"vous joindre à nous !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe some day.  If you can survive for long enough I may decide to come and "
"stay with you."
msgstr ""
"Peut-être un jour. Si tu peux survivre assez longtemps, je déciderai "
"peut-être de venir et de rester avec toi."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not enough given what's happening."
msgstr "Ce n'est pas suffisant compte tenu de ce qui se passe."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Whoah whoah, calm down.  Yikes.  Yeah fine, we're good.  Just stop trying to "
"spook me, I don't like it."
msgstr ""
"Whoah whoah, calmez-vous. Yikes. Oui, c'est bon. Arrête d'essayer de me faire "
"peur, je n'aime pas ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, that worked great."
msgstr "Oui, cela a très bien fonctionné."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We are not good and I'm done talking to you."
msgstr "Nous ne sommes pas bons et j'ai fini de vous parler."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Among other things, sure.  I have some extra I might be willing to trade, but "
"I only trade with my friends and I don't have a lot of those left."
msgstr ""
"Entre autres choses, bien sûr. J'en ai d'autres que je serais prêt à "
"échanger, mais je n'échange qu'avec mes amis et il ne m'en reste plus "
"beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Beer] I don't know about friends, but I have some drinks with me, want "
"to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[Offrez de la Bière] Je ne peux pas aider avec des amis, mais j'ai quelque "
"chose à boire sur moi, vous en voulez?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer India Pale Ale] I don't know about friends, but I have some drinks "
"with me, want to have some?"
msgstr ""
"[Offrez de l'India Pale Ale] Je ne peux pas aider avec des amis, mais j'ai "
"quelque chose à boire sur moi, vous en voulez?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Cigarettes] I don't know about friends, but I have some cigarettes, "
"want one with me?"
msgstr ""
"[Offrez des Cigarettes] Je ne peux pas aider avec des amis, mais j'ai "
"quelques cigarettes sur moi, vous en voulez?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Offer Joint] I don't know about friends, but I have something to smoke, want "
"to have some with me?"
msgstr ""
"[Offrez un Joint] Je ne peux pas aider avec des amis, mais j'ai quelque chose "
"à fumer sur moi, vous en voulez?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You seem cool and I'd like to talk more but I don't have anything fun.  I'll "
"try and find something and come back so we can share."
msgstr ""
"Tu as l'air sympa et j'aimerais parler plus longuement mais je n'ai rien "
"d'amusant. Je vais essayer de trouver quelque chose et je reviendrai pour que "
"nous puissions partager."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PRETTY] I think we're going to be great friends, don't you agree?"
msgstr "[JOLIE] Je pense que nous allons être de grandes amies, tu n'es pas d'accord ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Whoah whoah, calm down.  Yikes.  Yeah fine, we're good.  Just stop making "
"that face, it's too much for me.  Gives me feelings."
msgstr ""
"Whoah whoah, calmez-vous. Yikes. Oui, c'est bon. Arrête de faire cette tête, "
"c'est trop pour moi. Ça me donne des sentiments."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I don't think so.  I'm pretty good at hunting though."
msgstr "Je ne pense pas. Je me débrouille bien à la chasse par contre."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/NC_GLOOSCAP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess that's something."
msgstr "Je suppose que c'est quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor trying to stay safe
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor completely unwilling to talk
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor that gave up on life
#. ~ A rural holdout survivor willing to trade items
msgid "Survivor cowboy"
msgstr "Survivant cowboy"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/vampire_mentor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello again."
msgstr "Rebonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ayuh, I was thinkin' it's just another monstah skulkin' about.  Who are you?"
msgstr ""
"Je pensais que c'était un autre monstre qui rôdait dans les parages. Qui "
"êtes-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a survivor, looking around.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Juste un survivant explorant les environs.  Que faites-vous ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you before all this?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous faisiez avant tout ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there something I can do for you?"
msgstr "Puis-je faire quelque chose pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about we travel together?"
msgstr "Et si nous voyagions ensemble ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with the accent?"
msgstr "C'est quoi votre accent?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's hope it will."
msgstr "Espérons que ce sera le cas."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Can't say I can think of summin' specific right now.  Gotta say though, maybe "
"it oughta be a good idea for us ta travel togetha' - safety in numbers an' "
"all that."
msgstr ""
"Je ne peux pas dire que je pense à quelque chose de précis pour l'instant. Je "
"dois dire que ce serait peut-être une bonne idée que nous voyagions ensemble "
"- la sécurité par le nombre et tout ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll think about it."
msgstr "J'y réfléchirais."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is it a good idea to trust a stranger like me this easily?"
msgstr ""
"Vous pensez que c'est une bonne idée pour vous de faire confiance à un(e) "
"inconnu(e) aussi rapidement?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like a good idea - want to join me, then?"
msgstr "Ça m'a l'air d'être une bonne idée - vous voulez vous joindre à moi donc?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Wicked.  Been around the old road long enough ta know how ta handle myself in "
"a pinch.  Knew my way around a gun ever since my da taught me when I was a "
"kid, so ya don't have ta worry about me doing my part."
msgstr ""
"Mauvais. J'ai fait le tour de la route assez longtemps pour savoir comment me "
"débrouiller en cas de besoin. Je sais me servir d'une arme depuis que mon "
"père me l'a apprise quand j'étais enfant, alors tu n'as pas à t'inquiéter de "
"savoir si je fais ma part du travail."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On a second thought, let me think about it a bit more"
msgstr "Après réflexion, permettez-moi d'y réfléchir un peu plus."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great!  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Fantastique!  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Don't have much of a choice, do I?  On my own, a monstah will get lucky "
"sooner or later, and even if I kill it, bleedin' out in some alley is not "
"summin' I fancy.  Plus, we just had a nice, civil chat where no one tried ta "
"kill the otha', so I reckon we're off to ah' good start, all things "
"considered."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas vraiment le choix, n'est-ce pas ? Seul, un monstah aura de la "
"chance tôt ou tard, et même si je le tue, me vider de mon sang dans une "
"ruelle n'est pas quelque chose que j'aime. De plus, nous venons d'avoir une "
"discussion agréable et civile au cours de laquelle personne n'a essayé de "
"tuer l'autre, alors je pense que nous sommes bien partis, tout compte fait."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough.  Want to travel with me, then?"
msgstr "C'est très bien. Tu veux voyager avec moi, alors ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can't say I really agree.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Wha', nevah been ta Boston 'ave ya?  Hope you're not 'avin a hahd time "
"keepin' up with me, but if ya get used ta it, wicked good fun, let me tell ya."
msgstr ""
"Quoi, tu n'as jamais été à Boston, n'est-ce pas ? J'espère que tu n'as pas "
"beaucoup de mal à me suivre, mais si tu t'y habitues, tu t'amuseras beaucoup, "
"je te le dis."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I like it."
msgstr "J'aime ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I hate it."
msgstr "Je déteste ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Friendly.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay then."
msgstr "D'accord, alors."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey!  Stop right there!  This here is private property!  Not one step closer, "
"you got it?!"
msgstr ""
"Hé ! Arrêtez-vous là ! C'est une propriété privée ! Pas un pas de plus, "
"compris ? !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Whoa, calm down, no reason to get heated."
msgstr "Calmez-vous, il n'y a pas de raison de s'énerver."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You better calm down right now."
msgstr "Tu ferais mieux de te calmer tout de suite."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does private property even exist anymore?"
msgstr "La propriété privée existe-t-elle encore ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah that's right!  And don't bother me again, you hear?!"
msgstr "Oui, c'est ça ! Et ne me dérangez plus, vous entendez ? !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I said stay away!  Don't get any closer or I swear I will kill you."
msgstr ""
"Je t'ai dit de ne pas t'approcher ! Ne t'approche pas ou je jure que je te "
"tue."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't threaten me or you will regret it."
msgstr "Ne me menace pas ou tu le regretteras."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I really just want to talk - I mean no harm."
msgstr "Je veux juste parler - je ne veux pas faire de mal."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Ok, je pars."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "For the last goddamn time, leave or I will defend myself!  I will kill you!"
msgstr "Pour la dernière fois, partez ou je me défendrai ! Je vous tuerai !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to see you try."
msgstr "J'aimerais vous voir essayer."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Did you just fucking threaten me?!  This is your last chance to piss off or I "
"swear I will end you!"
msgstr ""
"Est-ce que tu viens de me menacer ? ! C'est ta dernière chance de dégager ou "
"je jure que je vais te tuer !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright, I'm going."
msgstr "Ok, ok, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It does on my property!  Now blow off!"
msgstr "C'est le cas sur ma propriété ! Maintenant, dégagez !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, I'll leave."
msgstr "Okay, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Hostile.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just want to talk."
msgstr "Je veux juste discuter."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah?"
msgstr "Ouais?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh.  Hey there."
msgstr "Oh. Bonjour, vous êtes là."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thought I heard someone.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "J'ai cru entendre quelqu'un. Qu'est-ce que vous faites ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like to come with me?"
msgstr "Voulez-vous venir avec moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_main_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you around."
msgstr "À la prochaine."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait, 'we'?"
msgstr "Attendez, \"nous\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  Okay."
msgstr "C'est vrai. D'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm sorry for your loss.  But you still can't give up.  You have a lot to "
"live for!"
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé pour votre perte. Mais vous ne pouvez pas abandonner. Vous "
"avez beaucoup de raisons de vivre !"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We all lost someone.  No reason to sit down and die."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons tous perdu quelqu'un. Il n'y a pas de raison de s'asseoir et de "
"mourir."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You can't let yourself be consumed by grief.  It will get better."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne pouvez pas vous laisser envahir par le chagrin. La situation "
"s'améliorera."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No one gets out alive.  Always been that way.  So we keep going."
msgstr "Personne n'en sort vivant. Il en a toujours été ainsi. Alors nous continuons."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sure your loved one would want you to live on for them."
msgstr "Je suis sûr que votre proche voudrait que vous continuiez à vivre pour lui."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I… I mean… huh.  I guess."
msgstr "Je… Je veux dire… huh.  J'imagine."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good.  Take care."
msgstr "C'est une bonne chose. Prenez soin de vous."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's a start."
msgstr "C'est déjà un début."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just leave me alone."
msgstr "Just laissez-moi tranquille."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright.  Take care."
msgstr "D'accord. Prenez soin de vous."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I dunno.  Waiting.  Seeing if something happens I guess."
msgstr "Je ne sais pas. Attendre. Voir si quelque chose se passe, je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You do realize there is an apocalypse going on, right?"
msgstr "Vous réalisez qu'une apocalypse est en cours, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah.  I do."
msgstr "Oui, c'est vrai."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So shouldn't you be more concerned?  Trying to survive?"
msgstr "Ne devriez-vous pas être plus inquiet ? Essayer de survivre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"For how long?  You've seen what's out there.  If we survive today, we'll die "
"the day after.  Or the day after that.  And if we live beyond that, we'll "
"just see everyone we care about die.  All of them.  Might as well get it over "
"with."
msgstr ""
"Pour combien de temps ? Vous avez vu ce qu'il y a dehors. Si nous survivons "
"aujourd'hui, nous mourrons le lendemain. Ou le jour suivant. Et si nous "
"vivons plus longtemps, nous verrons mourir tous ceux qui nous sont chers. "
"Tous. Autant en finir."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So you're just going to give up?"
msgstr "Vous allez donc abandonner ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeah.  I think I will."
msgstr "Oui, je pense que je le ferai."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I dunno.  Maybe.  Might give me something to do while I think about all this."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas. Peut-être. Ça pourrait me donner quelque chose à faire "
"pendant que je réfléchis à tout ça."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It will.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Ça sera fait. <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Nihilist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On a second thought, wait here a while."
msgstr "Tout compte fait, attendez un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey!  Who goes there?"
msgstr "Hé!  Qui va là?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just another survivor.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Juste un autre survivant. Que faites-vous ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm you, from the future.  I've come to warn you."
msgstr "Je suis vous, du futur.  Je suis venu vous avertir."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I am a ghost.  I died here 37 years ago, yet I cannot depart this mortal "
"realm."
msgstr ""
"Je suis un fantôme. Je suis mort ici il y a 37 ans, mais je ne peux pas "
"quitter ce royaume mortel."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there something I can help you with?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelque chose que je puisse faire pour vous aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Worked as a salesman - high end farming equipment.  Now I know, it may not "
"sound that fancy, but you'd be shocked at how pricy those machines can get.  "
"I was lucky enough to be on a fairly remote farm when everything went to "
"shit.  In a way, being a salesman saved me and the experience from the job "
"might allow me to make a living in the apocalypse, bartering for gear and "
"trinkets, so I got that going for me, I suppose."
msgstr ""
"J'ai travaillé comme vendeur de matériel agricole haut de gamme. Je sais que "
"cela n'a rien d'extraordinaire, mais vous seriez surpris de voir à quel point "
"ces machines peuvent coûter cher. J'ai eu la chance d'être dans une ferme "
"assez éloignée lorsque tout est parti en vrille. D'une certaine manière, le "
"fait d'être vendeur m'a sauvé et l'expérience acquise dans le cadre de ce "
"travail pourrait me permettre de gagner ma vie pendant l'apocalypse, en "
"faisant du troc pour obtenir du matériel et des babioles, alors je suppose "
"que c'est un avantage pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Speaking of which, I'd like to see your wares."
msgstr "En parlant de ça, j'aimerai voir ce que vous avez en stock."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not a bad way to live."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hah, real cute.  Seem the End times didn't take your sense of humor, eh, "
"stranger?"
msgstr ""
"Haha, mignon. On dirait que la fin du monde ne vous a pas enlevé le sens de "
"l'humour hein ?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have my moments.  So what are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah, not much really.  Passing through, trying to make a living by trading "
"with folk.  If you're interested, I got a lot of good things on sale, "
"stranger."
msgstr ""
"Ah, pas grand-chose en fait. Je suis de passage, j'essaie de gagner ma vie en "
"faisant du commerce avec les gens. Si vous êtes intéressé(e), j'ai beaucoup "
"de bonnes choses en vente, étranger(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You do?  Let me take a look."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You seem like a decent sort, but I'm not really looking for company right "
"now.  Think I'm better off on my own."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air d'un type bien, mais je ne cherche pas vraiment de compagnie "
"en ce moment. Je pense que je suis mieux tout seul."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you think so."
msgstr "Si vous pensez cela."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fair enough.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "D'accord.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgstr "Trouvez un fusil à pompe Remington 870 Express"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "Well, now that you mention it…"
msgstr "Eh bien, maintenant que vous en parlez…"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid ""
"You see, some time ago, I ran into this guy who offered me a substantial "
"payment in exchange for a Remington 870 Express.  I asked if he'd like "
"another weapon, since nowadays, any gun will do, but for some reason, he's "
"dead set on that particular model.  If you could obtain one for me, well, I'd "
"be quite grateful."
msgstr ""
"Il y a quelque temps, j'ai rencontré un homme qui m'a proposé un paiement "
"substantiel en échange d'une Remington 870 Express. Je lui ai demandé s'il "
"voulait une autre arme, car de nos jours, n'importe quelle arme fait "
"l'affaire, mais pour une raison que j'ignore, il tient absolument à ce modèle "
"particulier. Si vous pouviez m'en procurer un, je vous en serais "
"reconnaissant(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "Great!  Let me know when you get it, and I'll try to get in touch with him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "Suit yourself.  Ain't a rush."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid ""
"Well, a gun store is a solid bet, but the model is common enough.  Maybe you "
"can find one in a police station, or a store with hunting gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "Any news on that Remington?"
msgstr "Des nouvelles de ce Remington?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid ""
"Fantastic!  I'll try and get it to the buyer, if he's still alive.  If not, "
"well, still a good gun to sell.  Now, how would you like to be compensated?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "How did you even get this option to display the hell."
msgstr "Comment est-ce que vous êtes arrivé à faire apparaitre cette option?"

#: data/json/npcs/holdouts/Rural-Cowboy_Trader.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain a Remington 870 Express shotgun"
msgid "Then where is it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Barry!  You're okay!"
msgstr "Barry!  Tu va bien!"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh god, oh thank god.  Let's get Barry out of here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What's up?  Change of plans?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Everything OK?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not really a good time for a chat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't believe this is happening."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We've got him, let's get out of here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  Let's do this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You got it, let's go!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/Isherwood_Rescue_NPC_Duplicates.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not yet, just give me a minute."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer the Isherwood family.  Duplicate copy for the rescue mission
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dairy farmer the Isherwood family.
msgid "Carlos Isherwood"
msgstr "Carlos Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Carlos Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm Jesse's husband, part of the Isherwood family."
msgstr "Je suis le mari de Jesse, un membre de la famille Isherwood."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer of the Isherwood family.  Duplicate for the rescue mission.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dairy farmer of the Isherwood family.
msgid "Eddie Isherwood"
msgstr "Eddie Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Eddie Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm a dairy farmer, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Je suis un producteur laitier, membre de la famille Isherwood."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Dairy farmer's son in the Isherwood family.  Duplicate for the rescue
#. mission.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Dairy farmer's son in the Isherwood family.
msgid "Luke Isherwood"
msgstr "Luke Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Luke Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm Eddie's son, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Le fils d'Eddie, membre de la famille Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Horse trainer for the Isherwood family.  False copy for the Barry resue
#. mission
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Horse trainer for the Isherwood family.
msgid "Jesse Isherwood"
msgstr "Jesse Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Jesse Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm a horse trainer, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Je suis un membre de la famille Isherwood et un dresseur de chevaux"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.  False copy for the Barry resue mission.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.
msgid "Lisa Isherwood"
msgstr "Lisa Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Lisa Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "Part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Une membre de la famille Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.  False copy for the Barry resue mission.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Part of the Isherwood family.  Does not spawn until you get a mission
#. from Carlos to track him down.
msgid "Chris Isherwood"
msgstr "Chris Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPCS_Isherwood_Rescue_Duplicates.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Chris Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm Jesse and Carlos' son, part of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Je suis le fils de Jesse et Carlos, un membre de la famille Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A naked prisoner, from the isherwood faction trapped in a horrifying
#. cage, watching horrible things happen.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Barry Isherwood"
msgstr "Barry Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Barry Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "Missing member of the Isherwood family."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*crouches on the bottom of his cell, shivering, then looks up as you "
"approach.  He blinks a few times, then stands up.  He's totally nude, and his "
"tanned body is covered in tiny, precise-looking scars of varying ages.  \"I "
"can't believe my eyes.  Please get me outta here…\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you Barry Isherwood?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll get you out of here, just stay calm.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""
"Je vais vous sortir d'ici, j'ai juste besoin que vous restiez calme.  "
"<lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm Luke Skywalker, I'm here to rescue you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You just hold tight here for a second."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What?\"  The naked, traumatized man stares at you blankly, as though he'd "
"never seen Star Wars, which is clearly ridiculous.  \"Rescue me?  Yes, oh "
"please yes!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay then, your family's outside.  Let me go get them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's go."
msgstr "Allons-y."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hang on.  I've got questions."
msgstr "Attends. J'ai des questions."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just hold on a little longer, okay?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gulps.  \"I sure as hell am.  Did my family send you?  Please, we gotta go.  "
"There are more of those things.  They're everywhere.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, they did, I'll go get them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, Chris did, we're taking you home."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*switches, abruptly, to pure white-hot rage.  \"DOES THIS LOOK LIKE A TIME "
"FOR FUCKING QUESTIONS?\"  He stops, shaking, and returns to how he was "
"before.  \"I'm sorry.  I'm so sorry.  Oh god, I'm sorry.  I need to get out "
"of here.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, me too, let's go."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right, we're leaving, but you better not test me again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, me too.  I'll go get your family."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"All right, we're leaving, but you better not test me again.  I'll be back "
"with your family."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pff.  If you're gonna treat me like that, you can stay here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let's get back to the farm, as fast as possible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What farm?"
msgstr "Quelle ferme?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That shouldn't take long, your family's outside waiting.  I'll be back with "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That shouldn't take long, I brought some of your family with me.  Let's get "
"you home."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"\"Oh, so my family didn't send you then.\"  Barry looks downtrodden for a "
"brief moment.  \"Look, we just need to get out of here first, I'll tell you "
"about it later.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, sounds good to me.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry about the Luke Skywalker joke."
msgstr "Désolé pour la blague Luke Skywalker."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey buddy, feel like talking about what you saw in that tower?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What farm were you going to tell me about earlier?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've thought about it some more, and I'd like to have the directions to your "
"farm."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe let's talk about you a little bit.  What's your role in this family?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Come on, let's get out of here while we still can.  I don't want to spend any "
"longer around here then we need too."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*lights up as you approach, but also looks wary.  \""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, Jedi.\""
msgstr "Salut, Jedi.\""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, <name_g>.\""
msgstr "Salut <name_g>.\""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't wait to get back home and see everyone.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*nods.  \"Of course, what'd you want to ask?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I think we need to talk about it, but I'm not ready yet.  Let me "
"reclaim my life for a while."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds good, Barry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"It was terrible timing, but I have to admit, you don't see many "
"situations that perfect for that reference.  Sorry I didn't get it at the "
"time.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I ask you some questions?"
msgstr "Je peux vous poser quelques questions?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's still a bit fresh, but okay.  Yeah.  Let me sit down first.\"  Barry "
"takes a seat, his hands shaking even at the prospect of discussing the tower "
"and the things he saw.  \"What should we talk about?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to you in there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second thought, I think you should recover more."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shivers, though the room is warm, and moves his mouth wordlessly for a few "
"seconds.  \"It's hard to remember details.  The air in that place messes with "
"your brain, makes it all feel like some kind of dream.  Makes it so you can't "
"fight back.  Not that I could have anyway.\"  He stares into space for a "
"moment, then swallows hard.  \"They cut into me, over and over.  I don't "
"think they took anything out.  They just opened me up, poked around.  I was "
"awake for all of it, as awake as for anything else.  Sometimes I felt pain, "
"other times they did something to me so I could feel it but it didn't hurt.  "
"There were big, pale ones that did the cutting.\"  His voice gets "
"increasingly detached as he speaks, and his shaking grows worse.  You're not "
"sure it would be wise for him to go further."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Let him continue.]"
msgstr "[Laissez-le continuer.]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's enough for now, Barry."
msgstr "Ça suffit pour l'instant Barry."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shudders, looking like he might vomit.  \"What did they want?  Why me?  "
"Every time, they'd put me back together again, seal it up and make it look "
"almost like nothing happened.\"  He yanks up his shirt to show the scars.  "
"\"But I know what happened, it was REAL, goddammit!\"  He drops the shirt, "
"bends forward, and dry heaves for a few seconds.  Wordless, he hides his face "
"in his hands, and stops responding."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Leave.]"
msgstr "[Partir.]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.  Yeah.\"  He takes a long, shaky breath.  \"Yeah, you're right.  This "
"isn't going anywhere good.  Claire's been talking about making some dandelion "
"wine,\" he says with a hollow smile.  \"Maybe I'll go see if she needs help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How about we change the subject instead?  What's your role in this family?"
msgstr "Et si on changeait plutôt de sujet ? Quel est votre rôle dans cette famille ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good idea."
msgstr "Bonne idée."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He wipes his hand across his face, tension leaving him as he runs his "
"fingers through his hair.  \"Yeah, okay.  To be honest, years ago I was the "
"black sheep.  Moved off the family farm, lived out in Bunyan.  Went to "
"college, thought I'd get a job in computers.\"  He shuffles in his chair, "
"smiling half-heartedly.  \"I did sysadmin stuff for a while, back when the "
"internet was fairly new.  Then my dad died.  Carlos and Jesse had just gotten "
"married, and at the time it looked like they might be getting some land of "
"their own, and Eddie was out finding himself.  My dad and I had never got "
"along, but Jack…\" he stops.  \"Sorry, I don't think you were looking for my "
"life story.  What did you ask, again?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, go on."
msgstr "Non, continuez."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're right.  I was asking something different."
msgstr "Vous avez raison. Je demandais autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's okay, I'm going to head out."
msgstr "C'est bon, je vais partir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fair enough, you asked for it.\"  He stretches his arms out.  \"Jack and I "
"stayed close, even after my old man and I fell out, so when it looked like he "
"was going to be saddled with the entire farm to run, I took a good long look "
"at my life and realized I hated it.  It was never the farm I was trying to "
"get away from, you know?  I packed up my things, quit my job, and came out to "
"help Jack.  Never looked back.\"  He chuckles.  \"Damn hard finding a partner "
"for a guy like me out here though.  I was in a long-term relationship when I "
"left, but that fell apart.  I haven't been too lonely though, I've got my "
"people."
msgstr ""
"Ok, tu l'as bien cherché ». Il s'étire les bras. « Jack et moi sommes restés "
"proches, même après que mon père et moi nous soyons brouillés, alors quand il "
"a semblé qu'il allait devoir gérer toute la ferme, j'ai bien regardé ma vie "
"et j'ai réalisé que je la détestais. Ce n'était pas la ferme dont je voulais "
"m'éloigner, vous savez ? J'ai fait mes valises, j'ai quitté mon travail et je "
"suis venu aider Jack. Je n'ai jamais regardé en arrière ». Il s'esclaffe. « "
"C'est difficile de trouver un-e partenaire pour un gars comme moi ici. "
"J'avais une relation à long terme quand je suis parti, mais ça n'a pas duré. "
"Mais je ne me sens pas trop seul, j'ai mes amis."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PER 9] Was your choice in partners part of the problem with your father?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for taking the time to talk to me.  I had some other questions."
msgstr "Merci d'avoir pris le temps de me parler. J'ai d'autres questions. "

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the story.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci pour l'histoire. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&His eyebrows shoot up, briefly surprised, then he smiles.  \"You nailed it "
"in one.  Yeah, we're talking about a rural farmer in the nineties, here.  My "
"dad never understood me, even before he knew, and he did find out, although I "
"tried to keep the closet door closed.  Jack, though, he always saw me for me. "
" Never let it change our relationship.  That's real love, and that's what "
"made me come back when he needed me.  Meanwhile, the man I thought I'd marry, "
"back in Bunyan, he couldn't be assed even to come out and see the family "
"farm, let alone think about moving here.  He was dead weight, and I've never "
"doubted that decision.\"  He shrugs.  \"There's folks like me wherever you "
"go, I've had a few relationships since then.  Just nothing that stuck, and "
"I'm okay with that.  If nothing else, it proved what I already knew: aside "
"from my old man, none of my family treated me or them any different for it.  "
"They're good people.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, yeah, now I remember.  That farm I was talking about is where I live, "
"almost the whole Isherwood family lives there, including me.  I just wanted "
"to get back home as fast as possible so I can see everyone again, and so "
"everyone knows that I'm okay."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me some directions to it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's pretty cool.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "C'est plutôt cool.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, can I please see your map?\"  Barry takes your map, orients himself, "
"and points out a route to the farm.  \"Once we've done that, I'll head on "
"myself so everyone won't be surprised by you coming.  Sound good?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds good to me, let's hit the road."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to think about it some more."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Barry_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return Barry to Isherwood's farm."
msgstr "Ramenez Barry à la ferme des Isherwood."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, looks like you are building a forge setup."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Jack and Claire suggested I come talk to you about a job."
msgstr "Bonjour, Jack et Claire m'ont suggéré de venir vous parler d'un emploi."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is an older middle-aged man, well-muscled and darkly tanned, with worried "
"lines around the corners of his eyes and mouth.  He looks up as you get close"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", and then puts his hand on the butt of the rifle slung across  his back.  "
"\"I see that badge, I think you need to keep on walking, straight off this "
"property.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then smiles distantly.  \"Hello Sir, what brings you here?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then smiles distantly.  \"Hello Ma'am, what brings you here?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I'm a Marshal, what are you going to do about it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…[Leave.]"
msgstr "…[Partir.]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"* glares at you, his hand moving again to his gun.  \"I see that badge, I "
"think you need to keep on walking, straight off this property.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rolls his eyes.  \"I'm not an idiot.  You think if you don't wear your "
"badge, I won't know who you're working for?  Get out of here.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Look, I took it off to show I'm not here as a marshal.  I'm just here as a "
"traveler, someone who can maybe help you out.  I know you've got problems "
"bigger than you can handle right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*looks up warily as you approach"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  \"Yeah?\""
msgstr ". \"Ouais ?\""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, right… [Leave.]"
msgstr "Ah, oui…  [Partez.]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*struggles to think of a reply for a moment, then drops his hand from his "
"gun.  \"We've got that under control, but you're not wrong.  An extra pair of "
"hands wouldn't hurt, just now.  Just keep that damn badge out of my sight.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  Thanks.  Tell me more about what happened to Barry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It is coming together.  I want to make our own tools, repair our items and "
"even create some weapons and ammunition reloading."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard about Barry, can you tell me what captured him?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was pink and really fast, it had lots of limbs, definitely not human.\"  "
"Carlos rubs the back of his hand idly, staring into space.  \"It easily kept "
"up with us when we tried to escape, horrifying stuff.  Barry just dropped to "
"the ground, and the thing swept him away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You all just gonna leave him out there to his fate?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*frowns at you.  \"Of course not.  We tracked it for a while, but lost the "
"trail.  Right now we don't have the resources to try to rescue him.  My son, "
"Chris, has been trying to pick up the trail again and figure out a rescue "
"plan.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could help.  Where did Chris go?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shakes his head.  \"Leave Chris be, he knows what he's doing.  Give him some "
"time.  Calling more attention to him could get both of you killed.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The big item I need is an anvil, once I have that I can get a lot of repairs "
"done.\"  He smiles briefly.  \"Can't exactly head to town to get it done "
"anymore, but I learned a bit of old world metalwork from my granddad."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gestures around the workspace, which looks more set up.  \"I'm figuring "
"things out, getting it worked out.  It's been a while since I did this kind "
"of metalwork."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, it's coming along nice.\"  He slaps the surface of the anvil.  \"Thanks "
"for this, I'm still getting my skills back up, but it's going to be real "
"helpful."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Chris is hiking the perimeter of our land, planning some defense options.\"  "
"He looks you up and down.  \"Best just let him be."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks at you curiously.  \"Should be where you saw him last.  He's not "
"missing again, is he?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is your forge operational?"
msgstr "Votre forge fonctionne?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where can I find Chris?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que je devrais commencer a chercher Chris?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find an anvil"
msgstr "Trouvez une enclume"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "I need an anvil to do advanced metal work."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'une enclume pour faire de la métallurgie avancée."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "I could really use an anvil."
msgstr "J'ai vraiment besoin d'une enclume"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "You might be able to find one in a hardware store or similar."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "Thanks anyway, we'll find the time to make it ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "If you can't find one, maybe you can make one for me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid "Do you have the anvil?"
msgstr "Vous avez l'enclume?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an anvil"
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, this will really make a difference, here's some horse armor "
"I've been working on.  Eventually I'll have the whole herd outfitted."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgstr "Trouvez Chris Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid ""
"Chris hasn't come back from his latest search for Barry, I'm getting "
"concerned."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid "Can you go find my son and tell him to check in with us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid "Oh well.  I hope he turns up soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid ""
"He might be on the property somewhere, maybe by that old cabin near the "
"entrance, sometimes he camps there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid ""
"Thanks, I was getting ready to go look myself.  Now that I have the anvil, "
"I've been working on new armor for the horses, take this prototype I made."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Carlos_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Chris Isherwood"
msgid "I hope he didn't meet Barry's fate…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hi, your dad asked me to come find you, said you've been looking for your "
"uncle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, said you had some interesting ideas about the "
"world ending.  Is it tied to Barry's abduction?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, what have you been up to lately."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I hear your ideas about the world ending, now that we saved Barry?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you had any ideas for what your family could do?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you think we're ready to try this again?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got some SWAT gear that should work for the assault."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got enough SWAT gear to set everyone up for the assault."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[LIE] I tried to get the SWAT gear, but it looks like someone looted it "
"before I could get there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got enough bags to set up a defensive wall."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a young man, perhaps in his early twenties or late teens.  He eyes you up "
"and down.  \""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I see that badge.  You need to leave our land, my relatives have no fondness "
"for Marshals.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi, what's up?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, they are always worried about us, I prefer to survey the land and try "
"to track the changes.  I'm thinking about fixing up this cabin for some peace "
"and quiet…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like you are restless, why not leave?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What sort of changes have you seen?"
msgstr "Quel types de changements avez-vous observés?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, said you had some interesting ideas about the "
"world ending."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I surveyed the land, and I am trying to track the changes.  I fixed up this "
"cabin for some peace and quiet… you can settle here if you want"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you think, monsters that kidnaped Barry are responsible for end of the "
"world?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/sadie.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/cyrus_whately.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/milly_whately_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/prepnet_dialogue.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/sadie.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/whately_generic_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Parlons de quelque chose d'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/boann.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd better get going."
msgstr "Je devrais y aller, au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My family is convinced that if we stay here, we'll be able to weather this "
"catastrophe.  Since technology has failed, they've doubled down on older "
"traditions.  I think we need to get out there and find some answers before "
"settling on a path."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"In one of my longer trips looking for Barry, I saw something out in a field.  "
"I didn't get close but I swear unbelievable monsters were coming out of it.  "
"It kinda shimmered, almost like it wasn't quite there.  I've been tracking "
"those monsters for a while…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you find?"
msgstr "Qu'avez-vous trouvé?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I doubt that, other monsters and zombies attacked them way too often"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They made their way to this weird spire like structure, I've never seen "
"anything like it, it glistened in the sun like something organic.  I think "
"they could be holding Barry there, I've seen them arrive and leave with other "
"humans."
msgstr ""
"Ils se sont dirigés vers une structure bizarre qui ressemble à une flèche.  "
"Je n'ai jamais rien vu de tel, elle brillait au soleil comme quelque chose "
"d'organique.  Je pense qu'ils y détiennent Barry, je les ai vus arriver et "
"repartir avec d'autres humains."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might be able to help you get Barry back, but we've got to plan this out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, wildlife is more hostile and I've seen gigantic insects around, never "
"mind all these monsters.  I've also found mysterious dead spots and mutated "
"vegetation.  I don't think staying on a farm is sustainable forever, there "
"are big planet wide changes occurring."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You should leave before my family sees you."
msgstr "Vous devriez partir avant que ma famille ne vous voie."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your dad asked me to come find you, said you've been looking for your uncle."
msgstr ""
"Votre père m'a dit de vous trouver, il disait que vous étiez à la recherche "
"de votre oncle."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I was talking to Luke earlier, he said you had some interesting ideas about "
"the world ending."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Chris looks you up and down, and nods.  \"I'm definitely not going to say no "
"to a willing body, and you look like you know what's up.\"  He sighs.  \"To "
"be honest with you, I've been a bit stuck.  I can't tackle that thing alone, "
"and I'm not willing to bring my dad or Uncle Eddie in either.  Dad's got a "
"bum knee - don't tell him I said that - and Eddie's not that great a shot.  "
"Luke's still too young for something like this… you get the idea.\"  He leans "
"forward, self-consciously running his hand through his hair.  \"I think if we "
"work together maybe we'd stand a chance.  I don't have a great plan though.  "
"That tower doesn't look like something a person could just storm up to "
"full-frontal style.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I was just planning to go in by myself.  I've handled worse."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've got my own team here, we'll take this.  You stay back here, keep the "
"family safe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, I think we should work together on this.  Do you mind if I take the "
"lead?  I've probably got more experience."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks at you with obvious doubt.  \"You sure you know what you're getting "
"into?  I can't stop you if you plan on going in solo, but it seems like a "
"terrible idea.  Those things mean business.  I won't be able to go in and "
"help you if you get trapped too.  It's probably better we pair up.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Trust me.  See you in a bit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you insist, yeah, we could team up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, bringing your own people in is reasonable.  Still, the more the better. "
" It's my uncle in there, I'm more than willing to help out.  I know my way "
"around, I won't get in your way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right.  As long as you follow my lead, we could use another pair of hands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It's all right.  We've got this, you get things ready for when we return with "
"Barry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*nods.  \"I'm fine following your lead.  I'm a good scout and hunter, but "
"I've never done anything like this before.  When you set the time, I'll head "
"out and wait near the scout tower for you with the best gear I can get.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right.  Let's kick some alien butt."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anyone else around here that could help us?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You mentioned that Carlos, Eddie and Luke probably can't help in a firefight. "
" Is there any other way we could use them?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Like I said, I don't really think my dad or uncle should help, and I think "
"Luke's more likely to get injured than be helpful."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about Lisa?  She seems like she could handle herself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, I guess it's just us.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*blinks.  \"My… yeah, of course Lisa could come.  Damn, she'd smack me if she "
"knew I didn't think of that myself.  Mind if I go talk to her about it?  I'll "
"get her to come out with me and we'll meet you together, if she's willing.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Okay, I'll give you about an hour to talk with her about it.  I'll be back "
"soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Probably.  They'd want to, for sure.\"  He looks thoughtful.  \"I'm sure we "
"could use more help, but this isn't my strong suit.  Let me think about it.  "
"If you have any ideas, run them by me.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK.  Let's talk about it again in a bit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.  I think they should cover our exit.  We've got an old truck they could "
"set up as a platform, where Dad can put down covering fire without his knee "
"being an issue.  Eddie can drive, instead of shoot, and Luke or Mom can be "
"ready with some first aid supplies.  Then when we get out, we've got an easy "
"getaway set up, and there's less chance of us getting flanked while we're in "
"there looking for Barry.\"  He looks at you, suddenly nervous.  \"Is that a "
"good plan?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Seems like a good plan to me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think it's better we take my vehicle, and just leave them out of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I don't think one farmer with a hunting rifle is going to be enough to keep "
"our backs safe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think we need some kind of secure fallback point for the family, maybe a "
"defensive wall?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We're going to need some way to breach the tower itself, possibly some form "
"of explosives.  Do you know anyone who could help us with that?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks crestfallen for a moment, then straightens up.  \"All right.  Yeah, "
"maybe better not to put them at risk I guess.  So we're back to going in "
"without them.  Maybe that's better, I don't want to lose anyone else.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Can you think of anything else we might need, or should we put this into "
"action?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's go get your uncle back."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've changed my mind.  I think it's better we take my vehicle, and just leave "
"them out of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm a bit worried about defenses.  Do you folks have any armor or equipment "
"to help keep yourselves safe?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks thoughtful.  \"Well, we can wear our usual wrangling gear, but you're "
"right.  It's no good against those claws.\"  He sighs.  \"I don't want to "
"delay, but I don't want to lose another family member either.  If we could "
"get our hands on some riot gear, that might give us a better chance to fend "
"off the monsters.  Not too far away, our corrupt-as-hell local cops kept "
"enough of that gear on hand to easily set our family up.  As if they needed "
"it in this place.  Just used it to keep the boot on, y'know?\"  He spits on "
"the ground.  \"I can show you where their stores were, it'd feel nice to put "
"that stuff to good use.  Of course, any riot gear would do, if you happen to "
"have already looted some.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think you're right, that would take too long.  We'll have to count on "
"offense being our best defense."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Show me where, and I'll try to get some riot gear for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles slightly.  \"Awesome, getting our team kitted out better will go a "
"long way to making this possible.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 Riot Armor] I've got enough riot armor for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 Riot Helmet] These crowd control helmets should help a lot."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 Riot Arm Guard] I hope these armguards won't interfere with people's aim."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[5 Riot Leg Guard] I've got these leg guards to keep people from getting "
"hobbled."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We have enough full sets of riot control armor to cover everyone, head to toe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*nods intently, looking at the assembled pile of equipment.  \"Like I said, "
"I'll get this distributed to everyone who's coming.  It's starting to feel "
"more real, but less impossible.  Thanks for doing this.\""
msgstr ""
"*hoche la tête intensément, regardant la pile de matériel assemblée. « Comme "
"je l'ai dit, je vais distribuer cela à tous ceux qui viendront. Cela commence "
"à sembler plus réel, mais moins impossible. Merci d'avoir fait ça. »"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Before you get on to that, I wanted to talk about something else."
msgstr "Avant d’en arriver là, je voulais parler d’autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll let you get on that."
msgstr "Je te laisse t'en charger."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Désolé·e.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry.  I'm going to go take care of a few more things."
msgstr "Je suis désolé. Je vais m'occuper de quelques petites choses encore."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Good idea.  A sandbag wall would be easy enough, we've had to do those a few "
"times when we've had flooding and everyone knows the drill.  Back then we "
"just grabbed supplies from the hardware store, though.  Maybe you'd be able "
"to make a run for those?  Something like 20 canvas bags would probably do it. "
" We can fill them up in advance and toss them out of the truck to get a "
"decent barricade."
msgstr ""
"Bonne idée. Un mur de sacs de sable serait assez facile à construire, nous "
"avons dû le faire plusieurs fois lors d'inondations et tout le monde connaît "
"la procédure. À l'époque, nous allions simplement chercher des fournitures "
"dans une quincaillerie. Peut-être que vous pourriez vous en procurer ? "
"Quelque chose comme 20 sacs de toile ferait probablement l'affaire. Nous "
"pouvons les remplir à l'avance et les jeter hors du camion pour obtenir une "
"barricade décente."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think this is going to take too long, honestly.  Let's just stick with the "
"truck."
msgstr "Je pense que ça va prendre trop de temps, honnêtement. Restons-en au camion."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I know where to find those canvas bags, I'll go get them."
msgstr "Je sais où trouver ces sacs en toile, je vais les chercher."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All right.  I think that's everything we need.  Let me get it out to the "
"family and we'll have it all prepped by tomorrow."
msgstr ""
"Très bien. Je pense que c'est tout ce dont nous avons besoin. Je vais le "
"remettre à la famille et nous aurons tout préparé pour demain."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Before I go, let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Avant de partir, parlons d'autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll let you get on that, I've got my own preparations to take care of."
msgstr "Je te laisse t'en charger, j'ai mes propres préparatifs à faire."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"* looks thoughtful for a moment, then becomes a bit nervous.  \"Wait, won't "
"that run the risk of injuring Barry, or possibly collapsing the tower?  I "
"don't want him hurt during this, or anyone else if this bomb sends back a "
"bunch of shrapnel.  What do you think about it?\""
msgstr ""
"* semble pensif pendant un moment, puis devient un peu nerveux. « Attendez, "
"cela ne risque-t-il pas de blesser Barry, ou peut-être de faire s'effondrer "
"la tour ? Je ne veux pas qu'il soit blessé pendant cela, ni personne d'autre "
"si cette bombe renvoie un tas d'éclats d'obus. Qu'en pensez-vous ? »"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Don't worry, I know what I'm doing.  I've taken a look at these sorts of "
"towers before, and I know that the structure itself is pretty solid.  If we "
"tune it right, then the tower won't fall over."
msgstr ""
"Ne vous inquiétez pas, je sais ce que je fais. J'ai déjà vu ce genre de tours "
"et je sais que la structure elle-même est assez solide. Si nous la réglons "
"correctement, la tour ne s'effondrera pas."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I trust you on this.  If you need a good hand with chemistry, go see "
"Luke about it.  He knows a lot, you'd be surprised.  \" He pauses for a "
"moment, and thinks as if trying to recall something.  \"Luke should be over "
"in the old outbuilding near the dairy, that's on the other end of the "
"property."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, je te fais confiance. Si tu as besoin d'un bon coup de main en "
"chimie, va voir Luke. Il en sait beaucoup, tu serais surpris. \" Il s'arrête "
"un instant et réfléchit comme s'il essayait de se rappeler quelque chose. \" "
"Luke devrait être dans la vieille dépendance près de la laiterie, c'est à "
"l'autre bout de la propriété."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That sounds great, I'll go talk to him about it.  Let's talk about something "
"else first, though."
msgstr "Ça a l'air génial, je vais lui en parler. Mais parlons d'autre chose avant."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds great, I'll go talk to him about it."
msgstr "Ça a l'air génial, je vais lui en parler."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you think we're ready, I think we can try another go.  Even… even if it's "
"too late for Uncle Barry, I think we've got to try to take that damn tower "
"out of commission."
msgstr ""
"Si tu penses que nous sommes prêts, je pense que nous pouvons réessayer. Même "
"si c'est trop tard pour l'oncle Barry, je pense que nous devons essayer de "
"mettre cette foutue tour hors service."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgstr "Libérez Barry de la mystérieuse structure"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid ""
"We need to investigate the alien encampment and try to find out what happened "
"to Barry."
msgstr ""
"Nous devons enquêter sur le campement extraterrestre et essayer de découvrir "
"ce qui est arrivé à Barry."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid "I can take you to the structure, I tracked them to it."
msgstr "Je peux t'emmener à la structure, je les ai suivis jusqu'à elle."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid "Awesome, I want some answers!"
msgstr "Génial, je veux des réponses!"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid "Thanks anyway, I'll keep my eye on it, maybe I'll find a way one day."
msgstr ""
"Merci quand même, je vais y prêter attention, peut-être que je trouverai un "
"moyen un jour."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid ""
"I feel like we are underprepared if they see us, I marked the location for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"J'ai l'impression que nous ne sommes pas préparés s'ils nous voient, je t'ai "
"marqué l'emplacement."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid "You ready?"
msgstr "Es-tu prêt?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid ""
"It's taller then I remember, we should look for prisoners.  I left a note for "
"my family before we left.  If we survive, the cabin should be fixed up and "
"ready for you to move in if you want to stay."
msgstr ""
"C'est plus haut que dans mes souvenirs, nous devrions chercher des "
"prisonniers. J'ai laissé un mot à ma famille avant de partir. Si nous "
"survivons, la cabane devrait être réparée et prête à vous accueillir si vous "
"souhaitez rester."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Free Barry from the mysterious structure"
msgid "Well it was here…"
msgstr "Et bien c'était ici…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Retrieve 5 sets of riot armor for the Isherwoods"
msgstr "Récupérez 5 ensembles d'armures anti-émeute pour les Isherwoods"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Chris_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Retrieve Canvas Bags for Chris"
msgstr "Récupérer des sacs en toile pour Chris"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Matriarch of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Claire Isherwood"
msgstr "Claire Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Claire Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm the matriarch of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Je suis la matriarche de la famille Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Is that a U.S. Marshal's badge you're wearing?"
msgstr "Est-ce un badge d'U.S. Marshal que vous portez?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi, what brings you here?"
msgstr "Bonjour, qu'est ce qui vous amène?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, I'm a marshal."
msgstr "Oui, je suis un marshal."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, nice farm you have here."
msgstr "Bonjour, c'est une bonne ferme que vous avez là."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Jack suggested I stop by and say hello."
msgstr "Salut, Jack m'a suggéré de venir dire bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_ARDELIA.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_HELEN_TAVREL.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's trade."
msgstr "Faisons du commerce."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, when would more of this stuff be ready?"
msgstr "Hé, quand est-ce que plus de ce genre de choses seront prêtes ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Around <interval>."
msgstr "Autour <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright then, bye."
msgstr "Très bien, au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I live here with my husband, Jack.  He is working out in his shop."
msgstr "Je vis ici avec mon mari, Jack. Il travaille dans son atelier."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You are lucky to have your family still together."
msgstr "Vous avez de la chance de toujours avoir votre famille au complet."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Must be nice, to have the quiet place amid so much madness."
msgstr "Ça doit être bien d'avoir un endroit calme au milieu de toute cette folie."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You don't need as much luck if you are prepared and work together.  We've had "
"our losses, my brother in law, Barry, was our best hunter but things are so "
"different now…"
msgstr ""
"Il n'est pas nécessaire d'avoir autant de chance si vous êtes préparés et "
"travaillez ensemble. Nous avons eu des pertes, mon beau-frère, Barry, était "
"notre meilleur chasseur, mais les choses sont si différentes maintenant…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to Barry?"
msgstr "Qu'est-il arrivé à Barry?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A farm must be a pretty safe place these days."
msgstr "Une ferme doit être un endroit assez sûr de nos jours."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, nice to meet you.  I imagine Jack was boasting about my herbal "
"remedies, he's proud of what we've put together here."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, ravi de vous rencontrer. J'imagine que Jack se vantait de mes "
"remèdes à base de plantes, il est fier de ce que nous avons mis au point ici."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "He did mention you make remedies, are they effective?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I have always studied and made some natural remedies, but now they are more "
"essential than ever.  Who knows the next time we'll see a trained doctor.  "
"These remedies aren't always as effective, but they can do the job in a pinch."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Some of their cows were killed before we realized what was happening, Barry "
"and Carlos went into the forest to find the predator but it was like nothing "
"they'd ever seen.  Carlos may be willing to tell you more."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've always tried to live a quiet life out here, I suppose we are doing "
"better than most."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Jack and I have been together for 40 years.  He's been my anchor through all "
"of this chaos."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Jesse and her family live up at the horse farm.  They may have some jobs for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Jesse et sa famille vivent à la ferme équestre. Ils peuvent avoir des emplois "
"pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Eddie's dairy is at the end of the road.  He's may have some jobs for you if "
"you are interested."
msgstr ""
"La laiterie d'Eddie se trouve au bout de la route. Il pourrait avoir des "
"emplois pour vous si vous êtes intéressés."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You should get off our land, you have no business here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ask away."
msgstr "Demandez-moi."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your husband, is he around?"
msgstr "Au sujet de votre mari, il est dans les environs?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your daughter lives down the road?"
msgstr "Votre fille vit un peu plus loin?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where is your brother's place?"
msgstr "Votre frère habite où?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgstr "Trouvez 50 pissenlits"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid "I could use some help foraging ingredients."
msgstr "J'aurais besoin d'un peu d'aide pour cueillir des ingrédients."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid ""
"I could use some fresh dandelions for the next batch of wine.  Can you bring "
"me 50 dandelions?"
msgstr ""
"J'aurais besoin de pissenlits frais pour ma prochaine production de vin, "
"pouvez-vous m'en trouver 50?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid "Thank you, I'll put these to good use."
msgstr "Merci, j'en ferais bon usage."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid "Oh well.  Maybe some other time, thanks."
msgstr "Eh bien. Peut-être une autre fois, merci."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid "You can find them in the fields during the spring and summer months."
msgstr "Vous pouvez en trouver dans les champs durant le printemps et l'été."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid "Thanks.  Here's a small reward to show my appreciation for your help."
msgstr "Merci. Voilà une petite récompense pour vous montrer ma gratitude."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 50 dandelions"
msgid "I wonder if the wildlife ate all the greens…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgstr "Trouvez 20 poignées de graines de mélisse"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid "I could use some seeds from the forest."
msgstr "J'aurais besoin de graines issues de la forêt."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid ""
"We could use some seeds for the next planting season.  Can you bring me 20 "
"bee balm seeds?"
msgstr ""
"On aurait besoin de graines pour la prochaine saison de semaille. Pouvez-vous "
"me trouver 20 poignées de graines de mélisse?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid "Thank you.  It's important to have a good stock before the flu season hits."
msgstr ""
"Merci. C'est important d'avoir un bon stock avant que la saison de la grippe "
"ne commence."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid ""
"You should search through the forest, make sure to check in the underbrush "
"for bee balm and then harvest its seeds."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid ""
"Wow, perfect.  Here are some of my own remedies and if those don't work try "
"my other gift."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 20 bee balm seeds"
msgid "I'll have to find someone more at home in the forest…"
msgstr "J'ai besoin de trouver une personne qui se sens à la maison dans la forêt…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find and capture a cat"
msgstr "Trouvez et capturez un chat"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "I could use a barn cat to keep the mice down."
msgstr ""
"J'aurais besoin d'un chat de ferme pour garder la population de rongeurs "
"locale sous contrôle."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "I saw some feral cats out by the old cabin.  Can you capture one for me?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai vu des chats sauvages pas loin de la vieille cabane. Vous en captureriez "
"un pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid ""
"Thank you!  Please hurry back!  Take this cage so you have a chance of "
"capturing one."
msgstr ""
"Merci ! S'il-vous plait dépêchez-vous! Prenez cette cage avec vous pour avoir "
"une chance d'en capturer un."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "I didn't want to use chemicals on these rats."
msgstr "Je ne voulais pas utiliser du poison pour tuer ces rats."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid ""
"Take this pet carrier; if you can get close to a cat, you can put it inside.  "
"If you're having problems, try befriending it with cat food."
msgstr ""
"Prenez cette caisse de transport. Si vous arrivez à vous rapprocher d'un "
"chat, vous pouvez le mettre dedans. Si vous avez des soucis, essayez de "
"l'amadouer avec de la nourriture pour chat."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "Have you found a cat?"
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé un chat?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid ""
"Thank you so much, I want you to have this copy of my natural remedy journal. "
" I'll name this handsome fellow Joshua."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "What?!  You're lying, I can tell!  Did you even bring back my cage?"
msgstr "Quoi?! Tu mens, je peux le dire! As-tu même ramené ma cage?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Claire_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find and capture a cat"
msgid "Oh no!  I guess they are too nimble for you…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice dairy, must be tough keeping it running."
msgstr "Une bonne ferme laitière, cela doit être difficile à maintenir ces jours-ci."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When will your cows produce again?"
msgstr "Quand vos vaches produiront à nouveau ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a sun-worn, middle-aged man with crows feet and graying hair.  He looks "
"up as you approach, "
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"then sneers as he spots the Old Guard Marshal badge gleaming on your chest.  "
"\"I already told your kind not to come around here.  You need to keep on "
"walking, straight off this property.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "then gives you a little greeting wave.  \"Hello Sir, what brings you here?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "then gives you a little greeting wave.  \"Hello Ma'am, what brings you here?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Luke said you guys have some issues with the Old Guard.  What's up with that?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*glares at your marshal badge.  \"I said, keep *walking*, G-man.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*spits on the ground, glancing at where your marshal badge would have been, "
"and shaking his head.  \"Nice try.  You can take off the badge, but I know "
"what you are, I'm not some country rube.  Get out.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"<color_green>[Social 3]</color> I swear, I'm not here to cause trouble.  I "
"just volunteer with those guys to help travelers, things like that.  I don't "
"speak for them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"<color_yellow>[Social <3]</color> I took it off man, what more do you want "
"from me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine, I'm gone."
msgstr "Bien, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", looking at your marshal badge immediately.  \"Nope.  Agreement or not, I'm "
"not talking to you while you're wearing their sign, and I don't appreciate "
"the disrespect.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", his eyes darting to the spot where your marshal badge would be.  \"What "
"now?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the deal with you and the Old Guard, anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*spits on the ground.  \"Didn't much care for the government and the cops "
"before everything happened, care for them quite a bit less now.  We've had a "
"run-in or two with the folks calling themselves the 'Old Guard'.  That's all "
"I care to say about it.  They'll never be welcome on my land and I don't "
"believe for a second that they didn't cause all this in the first place.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for telling me.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Merci de m'avoir dit ça.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*grimaces.  \"Fine, I'll give you a chance, but you don't mess with me or my "
"family, you understand?  This is our land, not yours.  Or theirs.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for hearing me out."
msgstr "Merci de m'avoir écouté(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  I'll give you space for now."
msgstr "Merci. Je vous laisse tranquille maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I feel like maybe you didn't hear me right.  Get.  Off.  My.  Land."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You can't make me."
msgstr "Vous ne pouvez pas m'y forcer."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If the cows don't get anything nasty it should be around <interval>."
msgstr "Si les vaches n'attrapent rien de gênant, ça devrait être vers <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cheers, bye."
msgstr "Allez, salut."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I run this dairy with my son, Luke.  It's been a tough job keeping the herd "
"together, hasn't left a lot of time for other projects."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I heard about Barry, such a tragedy.  Can you tell me more about what "
"happened?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu au sujet de Barry, une tragédie. Pouvez-vous m'en dire plus sur "
"ce qui c'est passé?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*speaks in a quiet monotone, like he's reading off a page.  \"Barry and "
"Carlos went to hunt down something that killed our livestock, they tracked it "
"into the forest.  It grabbed Barry and ran off, you might be able to get "
"Carlos to tell you the story, if he can bring himself to share what happened.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I could use some help getting materials.  I want to outfit that old "
"building across the road with some kilns.  We want to make our own jars and "
"pottery so we aren't dependent on scavenging."
msgstr ""
"Oui, je pourrais avoir besoin d'aide pour trouver des matériaux. Je veux "
"équiper ce vieux bâtiment de l'autre côté de la route avec des fours. Nous "
"voulons fabriquer nos propres poteries pour être moins dépendants de ce que "
"nous arrivons à trouver et échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That is a good idea, what do you need?"
msgstr "C'est une bonne idée, de quoi avez-vous besoin?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not interested right now.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Je ne suis pas intéressé·e pour le moment.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Luke was going to start college this year, now everything is upside down.  He "
"is adaptable though, had an idea to begin manufacturing our own jars and "
"pottery.  He's out in the old outbuilding right now, cleaning up the place."
msgstr ""
"Luke était censé commencé l'université cette année, mais maintenant tout est "
"foutu en l'air. Il est tout de même adaptable, et à eu l'idée de fabrique nos "
"propres contenants en argile en premier. Il est dans le vieux bâtiment en ce "
"moment, vidant l'endroit pour libérer de la place pour les fours."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Jesse manages the horses and other livestock, she is amazing with animals."
msgstr ""
"Jesse gère les chevaux et autres animaux d'élevage, elle est incroyable avec "
"les animaux."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Carlos will be in his workshop if he isn't out hunting.  He is trying to get "
"a forge set up."
msgstr ""
"Carlos sera dans son magasin s'il n'est pas à la chasse. Il essaye de mettre "
"en place une forge."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your son helps with the dairy?"
msgstr "Votre fils aide dans la ferme laitière?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, Jesse runs the horse farm?"
msgstr "Jesse gère la ferme équestre donc?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where can I find Carlos?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que je peux trouver Chris?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgstr "Trouvez 120 Cailloux"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "We need to build some kilns."
msgstr "Nous avons besoin de construire des fourneaux."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "I could use 120 rocks to construct some kilns."
msgstr "J'aurais besoin de 120 cailloux pour construire des fours."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "You can break up some larger stones, or gather them up from the fields."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez éclater de plus grosses pierres pour en trouver, ou simplement en "
"trouver ici et là."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "Thanks anyway, we'll find the time to get them ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Merci quand même, on pourra toujours trouver un peu de temps pour le faire "
"nous-même."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 75 Rocks"
msgid "Mining would always be an option if you had the resources."
msgstr "Vous pouvez aussi juste miner et acquérir les cailloux comme cela."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "Do you have the stone?"
msgstr "Vous avez les pierres?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 120 Rocks"
msgid "I appreciate it, this will make Luke happy."
msgstr "J’apprécie, Luke sera content."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgstr "Trouvez 2000 unités de sable"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgid "I do have some resource gathering I could use help with."
msgstr ""
"J'ai un peu de collecte de ressources avec laquelle je pourrai avoir besoin "
"d'aide."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgid ""
"Now that the forge is set up, we could use 2000 units of sand to get "
"production going."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que la forge est opérationnelle, nous aurions besoin de 2000 "
"unités de sable pour commencer notre production."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid "Oh well.  I'll try to find time to get it myself, thanks."
msgstr "Pas grave, j'essaierai de trouver le temps d'aller le faire moi même."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgid ""
"You can find it along river banks, or maybe landscaping supplies and hardware "
"stores."
msgstr ""
"Vous pourrez probablement en extraire d'une berge de rivière, ou en trouver "
"déjà emballé dans un magasin de jardinage ou de bricolage."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
msgid "Thanks, now Luke can get started.  Here's a token of my thanks."
msgstr "Merci, maintenant Luke peut s'y mettre. Voici un geste pour vous remercier."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 2000 units of sand"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid "I wonder where all the sand went…"
msgstr "Je me demande où tout le sable à pu aller…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgstr "Rassemblez 100 unités d'argile"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid "I do have some resource gathering I could use help if you have time."
msgstr ""
"J'ai un peu de collecte de ressources avec laquelle je pourrai avoir besoin "
"d'aide si vous avez le temps."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid ""
"Now that the clay kiln is set up, we could use 100 units of clay to get "
"production going."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que le four à argile est construit, nous aurions besoin de 100 "
"unité d'argile pour commencer notre production."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid "You can find it along river banks, or maybe look for deposits in the forest."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez le trouver le long des berges des rivières, ou peut-être chercher "
"des gisements dans la forêt."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Gather 100 units of clay"
msgid ""
"Thanks, now Luke can get started making jugs, We'd like to give you a cow, "
"Here's Daisy, take good care of her and she'll provide you with milk."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Eddie_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/snippets/snippets.json
#. ~ Nickname for creature 'mon_cow' in an effect
#. ~ Snippet in category "<dog_name>"
msgid "Daisy"
msgstr "Daisy"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Patriarch of the Isherwood family.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Jack Isherwood"
msgstr "Jack Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Job description of "Jack Isherwood" NPC class
msgid "I'm the patriarch of the Isherwood family"
msgstr "Je suis le patriarche de la famille Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here to deliver some resources."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour fournir des ressources."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This is a lot of land, you been here since the collapse?"
msgstr ""
"Ceci est une large propriété, vous êtes restés ici depuis que tout s'est "
"effondré?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I live here with my wife, this is our family's land.  My daughter's family "
"and son live down the road."
msgstr ""
"Je vis ici avec ma femme, ce sont les terres familiales. La famille de ma "
"fille vivent en bas de la route."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your whole family survived?"
msgstr "Toute votre famille a survécu?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've had our losses… now we stay close to home, preparing for trouble.  "
"We've always taken disaster preparedness seriously, but we didn't expect "
"anything like this though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even out here we've had some attacks and seen… other things.  We have been "
"working on our defenses, but it takes time.  We've been able to keep up with "
"the crops and animals though so we won't have to risk our necks for supplies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What sort of defenses do you want?"
msgstr "Quelle sorte de défenses voulez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We want to put up more fencing and build some look out spots, maybe lay some "
"traps for the monsters.  We could use some extra resources.  If you want to "
"bring me logs, sand, clay, wire, nails, wood planks, and metal chunks, I'll "
"give you signed chits you can use to buy goods from any of the family."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds reasonable, I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Ça semble raisonnable, je vais voir ce que je peut faire."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Claire and I have been together for 40 years now, couldn't run this place "
"without her.  She's quite the herbalist too, been real useful lately.  She is "
"probably in the house, you should stop in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Jesse and her family live up at the horse farm.  Her husband, Carlos, may "
"have some jobs for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Eddie's dairy is at the end of the road.  It's just him and his son since "
"Barry was taken by that thing in the woods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You should get off my land, the government proved its incompetence with this "
"catastrophe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your wife, is she around?"
msgstr "Au sujet de votre femme, elle est dans les environs?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Excellent.  What've you brought us?"
msgstr "Excellent. Que nous avez-vous apporté ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 10 3 L jars"
msgstr "Trouvez 10 bocaux de 3L"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
msgid "I could use some help scavenging."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
msgid ""
"We could use some 3 liter jars to preserve our produce.  Can you bring me 10 "
"large three liter jars?  I'll give you some preserves in exchange."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
msgid "Thank you.  It's important to preserve foods while we can."
msgstr "Merci.  Il est important de conserver nos denrées tant que nous le pouvons."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
msgid "Oh well.  I'll see if I can find another way, thanks."
msgstr ""
"Pas très grave. Je vais voir si je peux trouver un autre moyen de m'en "
"procurer, merci pour l'effort."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
msgid "Grocery stores, house kitchens, there's plenty of places to look."
msgstr "Épiceries, cuisines de maison, il y a de nombreux endroits où chercher."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgid "Wow, perfect.  Thanks.  Here's your reward."
msgstr "Wow, parfait. Merci beaucoup. Voilà votre récompense."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 10 3 L jars"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid "I wonder where all the jars went…"
msgstr "Je me demande où toute les bocaux sont allés…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgstr "Trouvez 100 poignées de graines de blé"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgid "I do have some more scavenging for you."
msgstr "J'ai plus de choses que vous pourriez trouver pour nous."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgid ""
"We could use some seeds for the next planting season.  Can you bring me 100 "
"wheat seeds?  I'll give you some fresh produce."
msgstr ""
"Nous aurions besoin de graines pour la prochaine semée. Pouvez vous m'amener "
"100 poignées de grains de blé? Je vous donnerait des produits frais de notre "
"ferme en échange."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgid "Thank you.  It's important to preserve healthy foods while we can."
msgstr ""
"Merci, ceci nous aidera vraiment à assurer que la prochaine récolte soit "
"bonne."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid "Oh well.  I'll see if I can find another supplier, thanks."
msgstr ""
"Pas très grave. Je vais voir si je peux trouver quelqu'un d'autre pour m'en "
"procurer, merci pour l'effort."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jack_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 100 wheat seeds"
msgid "I wonder where all the seeds went…"
msgstr "Je me demande où toute les graines sont allées…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Leave our property, Marshal."
msgstr "Quittez notre propriété Marshal."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello.  We don't see many people these days."
msgstr "Bonjour. On ne voit pas beaucoup de monde ces jours-ci. "

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, it looks like you are doing well here."
msgstr "Salut, on dirait que vous vous débrouillez bien ici."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Jack and Claire suggested I come down here and meet you."
msgstr "Salut, Jake et Claire m'ont suggéré de descendre vous rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It would be a lot harder without family.  Keeping the animals safe is "
"essential to our future."
msgstr ""
"Ce serait beaucoup plus difficile sans la famille.  Garder les animaux en "
"sécurité est essentiel pour notre avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like you are betting on civilization not coming back."
msgstr ""
"On dirait que vous misez sur le fait que notre civilization ne se remettra "
"pas sur ses pieds."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any animal care tips?"
msgstr "Vous avez des astuces sur l'élevage?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can't wait for someone else to fix things, we need to take care of "
"ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Nous ne pouvons pas attendre que quelqu'un d'autre arrange les choses, nous "
"devons prendre soin de nous-mêmes."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Horses make good all around companions.  They can get places that cars can't "
"and also help when all the engines fail.  They become very trusting if you "
"feed them some nice fodder."
msgstr ""
"Les chevaux sont des bons compagnons à avoir. Ils peuvent passer là ou un "
"véhicule ne peut pas ou lorsque trouver des pièces de rechanges n'est pas "
"pratique. Vous pouvez probablement gagner la confiance d'un cheval en leur "
"donnant du bon fourrage."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh good, I'm sure Jack wanted to put you to work.  If you're interested, I "
"could use a hand clearing out the woods.  My son, Chris has his hands full "
"trying to keep the predators under control."
msgstr ""
"Oh bien, je suis sûr que Jack voulait vous mettre au travail. Si ça vous "
"intéresse, j'aurais besoin d'un coup de main pour débroussailler les bois. "
"Mon fils, Chris, a les mains pleines en essayant de garder les prédateurs "
"sous contrôle."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to speak with Carlos too about some work."
msgstr "J'aimerais aussi parler avec Carlos, voir si il a du boulot pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is Chris around?  I'd like to know what he's run into out in the woods."
msgstr ""
"Chris est dans les environs? J'aimerais savoir sur quoi il est tombé dans les "
"bois."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What needs killing?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qui a besoin d'être tué?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "He's out back in the workshop."
msgstr "Il est dans l'atelier."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He's out doing some surveying, we are planning on adding a fence line and "
"some defenses."
msgstr ""
"Il est en train d'étudier le terrain, nous voulons ajouter une barrière et "
"des défenses."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You should get off my farm, I won't deal with a government stooge."
msgstr ""
"Vous ferait mieux de ficher le camp de ma ferme, je ne rien avoir à faire "
"avec un larbin du gouvernement."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Looks like you are doing well here."
msgstr "On dirait que vous vous débrouillez bien ici."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Jack and Claire suggested I come talk to you."
msgstr "Jack et Claire ont suggéré que je vienne vous parler."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is Chris around?"
msgstr "Chris est dans les environs?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Kill wolves"
msgstr "Tuez des loups"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
msgid "We could use some help killing some wolves."
msgstr "On aurait besoin d'aide pour tuer quelque loups."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
msgid ""
"There's been some wolves that keep scaring our chickens and horses, I'd be "
"grateful if you can kill them."
msgstr ""
"Il y a des loups qui n'arrêtent pas d'effrayer nos poules et chevaux, vous "
"auriez ma reconnaissance si vous pouviez nous en débarrasser."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
msgid "Wonderful, let me know when it is done."
msgstr "Merveilleux, dites-moi quand ce sera fait."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "Thanks anyway, we will try some traps."
msgstr "Merci quand même, on va essayer d'installer des pièges."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "A gun will probably help."
msgstr "Une arme à feu aidera beaucoup je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "Did you kill it?"
msgstr "Vous les avez tués?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, I've got this old saddle I want you to have.  I'll be happy "
"to put a horse under it if you want to do some more heroics."
msgstr ""
"J'apprécie vraiment, j'ai cette vieille selle que je veut que vous ayez. Je "
"serais. Je serais heureux d'y ajouter un cheval si vous vous sentez capable "
"d'accomplir une autre chose pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill wolves"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "Show me the bodies."
msgstr "Montrez-moi les corps."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Kill monsters"
msgstr "Tuez des monstres"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "We could use some help killing some monsters."
msgstr "Nous aurions besoin de votre aide pour tuer quelques monstres."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid ""
"We could use some help killing a pack of monsters.  I don't know what they "
"are, but they're very fast, I'm willing to outfit you with a horse if you "
"succeed."
msgstr ""
"Nous aurions besoin d'aide pour tuer un groupe de monstres. Je ne sais pas "
"exactement ce qu'ils sont, mais ils sont très rapides. Je serais heureux de "
"vous donner un cheval si vous réussissez."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid "Be ready for anything."
msgstr "Soyez prêt(e) à tout."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill monsters"
msgid ""
"I appreciate it, this will help keep our animals safe.  This is, Steve, he's "
"a good, steady horse.  You should talk to Carlos about some armor for him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Jesse_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Nickname for creature 'mon_horse' in an effect
msgid "Steve"
msgstr "Steve"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I see that badge, I think you need to keep on walking, straight off this "
"property."
msgstr ""
"J'ai vu votre badge, je pense que vous devez passer votre chemin, directement "
"hors de cette propriété."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, this is a nice farm, your family lives here?"
msgstr "Salut, c'est une belle ferme, votre famille vit dessus?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, I'm looking for Jesse."
msgstr "Salut, je suis à la recherche de Jesse."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, I'm looking for Chris."
msgstr "Salut, je suis à la recherche de Chris."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I talked to Chris about rescuing Barry.  He thinks you might be able to help."
msgstr "J'ai parlé à Chris pour secourir Barry. Il pense qu'il pourrait nous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My family owns all the land around here, my parents are out in the barn and "
"my other family is down the road."
msgstr ""
"Ma famille possède les terres par ici, mes parents sont à la ferme et le "
"reste de ma famille sont en bas de la route."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok, I'll go find them."
msgstr "Ok, je vais les trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Mom is in her office, in the barn.  Be careful that you don't let our horses "
"out."
msgstr ""
"Ma mère est dans son bureau, dans la grange.  Faites attention à ne pas "
"laisser nos chevaux sortir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Chris is out hunting or something right now."
msgstr "Chris est dehors en train de chasser ou quelque chose comme ça là maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, ok."
msgstr "Oh, ok."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Or something?"
msgstr "Ou quelque chose comme ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice talking to you, bye."
msgstr "Ravi⸱e d'avoir parlé avec toi, au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, he's supposed to be hunting, but since you've been talking to Luke, I "
"bet he mentioned Chris wants to learn more about the end of the world.  "
"Sometimes he'll take off for a few days and I end up patching him up so my "
"parents don't know he left the property."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, Chris talked to me a minute ago.\"  She touches the shoulder strap on "
"her rifle.  \"I can't believe he's not trying to talk me out of it, really, "
"but I'd do anything to save Uncle Barry.  I'll be ready at the tower, when "
"you need me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great.  I'll see you there."
msgstr "Super. On se voit là-bas."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He did?\"  She touches the shoulder strap on her rifle.  \"Like, action?  "
"Yeah, I'm a pretty good shot, and I'd do anything to save Uncle Barry.  I'm "
"surprised Chris didn't try to go all protective older brother on me.  What's "
"the plan?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Explain the plan.]"
msgstr "[Expliquez le plan.]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Lisa_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&She listens intently as you explain.  \"All right.  I'll be ready at the "
"tower when you need me.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a young man in his mid teens, wearing threadbare but clean work trousers "
"and a plain shirt with a few holes in it.  He looks you up and down as you "
"approach"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then scowls as he spots the Old Guard Marshal badge gleaming on your chest. "
" \"I see that badge.  You should leave before my father spots it.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", and nods once when he sees you've taken off your marshal badge.  \"Tread "
"carefully around here, we don't have a lot of respect for your type of "
"lawman.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then raises a hand to greet you.  \"Hello.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then raises his hand to his forehead in an old fashioned hat-tipping sort "
"of gesture.  \"Hello.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong with me being a marshal?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qui ne va pas avec mon titre de marshal?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your dad said you were out here fixing up this place."
msgstr "Votre père m'a dit que vous étiez en train de retaper cette endroit."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are those books doing for you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Chris and I have a little project for you that we've cooked up, if you're "
"interested."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We've got the truck, what's next?"
msgstr "On a le camion, c'est quoi la suite ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got the dynamite you requested, I can't wait to see how this works out."
msgstr "J'ai la dynamite que vous vouliez, hâte de voir ce qu'elle peut faire."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, what are you doing out here?"
msgstr "Hey, qu'est-ce que vous faites ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't see how it's much of your business what our story is.  You can try "
"asking my dad, Eddie, if you really want.  Just don't start acting like some "
"little piece of tin in your pocket means you can come in like you own the "
"place."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I work on it when I have the time.  I can't leave the farm too long, so "
"I can't find some things I need."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I can help out.  What do you need?"
msgstr "Peut être que je peux aider.  De quoi avez vous besoin?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Must be tough having the world fall apart when you had you future to look "
"forward to."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gestures to where they sit on a shelf.  \"I've been trying to look at them, "
"but I can't focus too much right now.\"  He smiles sadly.  \"Hope to get to "
"them soon.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Because of Barry?"
msgstr "À cause de Barry?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*winces a little at the name.  \"Yeah.  Because of Barry.\"  You can see he'd "
"rather not pursue the topic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles.  \"Bit early to tell, but I've been doing some night time reading "
"and trying a few things out.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles brightly.  \"Real great, thanks!  I've learned a lot from them "
"already.  Tried my hand at some basic stuff, it's fun to learn new things.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gestures around at the worn down shed surrounding you.  \"I've been cleaning "
"up this old building to make it into a workshop.  I want to put up a pottery "
"kiln and forge.  My dad doesn't want me leaving the farm to find some things"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", says it is too dangerous.  After what happened with Barry, well, I tend to "
"agree with him.\"  He smiles thinly.  \"Don't want you to have to run out "
"saving another one of us, right?\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", says it's too dangerous.  I used to think he was being a pain in the butt, "
"but lately…\" he stops abruptly, and says nothing more."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I know all the grown-ups worry about us, but I think we can adapt better than "
"them in the long run.  Chris - my cousin - has some interesting thoughts on "
"the matter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What sort of ideas does Chris have?"
msgstr "Quel genre d’idées a-t-il?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&His shoulders slump a little at the question.  \"Things have been tough for "
"my dad since Barry was captured.  He works till he falls asleep most nights…\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks around, then leans in just a little closer.  \"He's doing OK now that "
"Barry's home, but, well, things still aren't the same.  I imagine that'll "
"take time.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*goes a bit pale.  \"I shouldn't have said that.  Not my place to talk to a "
"stranger about it.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I already know Barry got captured.  I just wanted to know a bit more about "
"it.  Maybe I can help."
msgstr ""
"Je sais déjà que Barry a été capturé.  Je veux juste savoir un peu plus.  "
"Peut être que je peux aider."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might be able to help, though."
msgstr "Je pourrais peut être aider."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*frowns.  \"I don't know how much I can tell you.  Your best bet is to talk "
"to Uncle Carlos.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really… okay.  Maybe ask my grandma, Claire.  She'll know if it's okay to "
"talk about."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Chris is a little older than me, he's up at the horse farm with his parents "
"and sister, Lisa."
msgstr ""
"Chris est un peu plus vieux que moi, il est dans le haras avec ses parents et "
"sa sœur, Lisa."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, he doesn't agree that what we're doing here will last.  He thinks "
"things will only get worse.\"  Luke shrugs, as if to say he doesn't have a "
"strong opinion on the matter.  \"It's tough to get the adults to listen "
"though, much less agree with his solution.  You can go talk to him more about "
"it if you want."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You won't find any help here."
msgstr "Vous ne trouverez pas d'aide ici."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your dad."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de votre père."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How does this all come together?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, we are going to turn this truck into a bomb that'll give us a big "
"enough opening in the tower to let out some of the heat and gas.  But small "
"enough that it won't kill Barry unless it's right next to him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are you serious?  This is your brother we are risking here!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Exactly, and I wouldn't do anything to risk him unnecessarily."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"OK so I have an idea on how we can breach that tower.  We need a truck and "
"some dynamite.  I've heard about some bandits in a truck robbing people "
"nearby.  If you can take care of the bandits I'll pick up the truck later"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I can manage two bandits."
msgstr "Je pense que je peu m'occuper de deux bandits."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Surely we can think of a better way in."
msgstr "Je suis certain(e) qu'on peut trouver une meilleure solution."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"So now that we've got the truck we need the boom.  See if you can find some "
"dynamite at the old mines?  Once we got the dynamite I'll rig that up to a "
"kitchen timer and we'll have a bomb on wheels.  I'll need 50lbs to light that "
"truck up like the 4th of July!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "This is gonna rad as heck as long as it works."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not doing it."
msgstr "Je fais pas ça."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I've got everything I need to make this breaching truck for us.  Thanks!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[heck yeah]"
msgstr "[oh yeah]"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
msgstr "Trouvez une copie de L'art du Soufflage de Verre"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
msgid "I need more knowledge to get the glass blowing started."
msgstr ""
"J'ai besoin d'apprendre un peu plus de choses avant de pouvoir commencer à "
"souffler du verre."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
msgid ""
"I could really use a book on glass blowing.  With the internet gone, I don't "
"have any handy references."
msgstr ""
"J'aurais vraiment besoin du livre traitant de soufflage de verre. Avec "
"l'internet mort, je n'ai rien à quoi me référer."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "Fantastic, I'm not supposed to leave our land."
msgstr "Fantastique, je ne suis pas vraiment censé sortir de nos terres."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "Oh well, figured I'd have to do a lot of practice anyway."
msgstr ""
"Dommage, je supposait que j'aurais besoin de beaucoup d'entraînement de toute "
"façon."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
msgid "A library, bookstore or a glass blower's studio should have one."
msgstr ""
"Vous pourriez peut être en trouver un dans un atelier de souffleur, un "
"libraire ou une bibliothéque."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_foreman.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of Homebrewer's Bible"
msgid "Do you have the book?"
msgstr "Vous avez le livre?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "I appreciate it, this will make my life so much easier."
msgstr "J'apprécie vraiment, ceci me rendra la vie beaucoup plus facile."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "I don't see a book…?"
msgstr "Je ne vois pas de livre…?"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find The Art of Glassblowing book"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "At least you escaped with your life…"
msgstr "Au moins vous vous en êtes tiré·e en vie…"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgstr "Trouvez une copie du Compendium du Bricoleur"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "I need more knowledge to get better pottery."
msgstr ""
"J'ai besoin d'apprendre un peu plus de choses afin de produire de la "
"meilleure poterie."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid ""
"I could really use the book, DIY Compendium.  With the internet gone, I don't "
"have any handy references."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of DIY Compendium"
msgid "A library, bookstore should have one, schools are another good idea."
msgstr ""
"Un libraire, une bibliothéque ou peut être une école pourraient en avoir une "
"copie."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Retrieve the Truck for Luke Isherwood"
msgstr "Ramenez la Voiture à Luke Isherwood"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Retrieve the Truck for Luke Isherwood"
msgid "Kill the two bandits for Luke Isherwood to get their truck."
msgstr "Tuez deux bandits pour Luke Isherwood et ramenez leur véhicule."

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Retrieve Some Dynamite for Luke"
msgstr "Trouvez de la dynamite pour Luke"

#: data/json/npcs/isherwood_farm/NPC_Luke_Isherwood.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Retrieve Some Dynamite for Luke"
msgid ""
"Get 50 pounds of dynamite for Luke Isherwood to make a bomb.  There's a known "
"shipment at a mine in the region."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
msgid "prisoner"
msgstr "prisonnier(ère)"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
msgid "gatekeeper"
msgstr "gardien(ne)"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
msgid "leader of prisoners"
msgstr "leader des prisonniers"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Skills intentionally kept low.  This character should probably have a
#. higher chance of having insanity type traits eventually.
msgid "Prisoner"
msgstr "Prisonnier(ère)"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Job description of "Prisoner" NPC class
msgid "I'm here to kick ass."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour botter des culs."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Get the fuck out of here."
msgstr "Barrez-vous d'ici putain."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok, sorry, I'm already leaving!"
msgstr "Ok, pardon, je m'en vais déjà!"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, fuck you, <name_b>!"
msgstr "Hé, va te faire foutre, <name_b> !"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Do I need to repeat myself?  Get outta here, <name_b>."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de me répéter ? Dégage de là, <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I got it.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "C'est bon, j'ai compris. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just wanted to ask if you have a job for me."
msgstr "Je voulais juste vous demander si vous aviez du boulot pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just hungry, and I thought you might give me some food for some job."
msgstr ""
"J'ai juste faim, je pensais que tu pourrais me filer de la bouffe en échange "
"d'un boulot."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can we just talk it over?"
msgstr "Est-ce qu'on peut juste en parler ?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Get out, loser."
msgstr "Dégage, loser."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Do I have a <freaking> exclamation sign over my <freaking> head, like I'm a "
"<freaking> quest-giver from some <freaking> video game?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, of course not!  Sorry, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Non bien sûr que non!  Désolé·e, je m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Disappear, <name_b>."
msgstr "Disparais, <name_b>."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok, sorry, I promise I won't bother you anymore."
msgstr "Ok, désolé, je promets de ne plus vous déranger."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Gee, what's the matter with you?  Okay, okay, I'm leaving."
msgstr "Putain, c'est quoi ton problème ? Ok ok, je pars."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It would be you who will regret talking to me like that."
msgstr "C'est toi qui va regretter de m'avoir parlé comme ça."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not so fast, I think you need to pay for breaking your promise and bothering "
"me.  Give me your shit, now!"
msgstr ""
"Pas si vite, je crois que tu dois me payer pour avoir brisé ta promesse et "
"pour m'avoir emmerdé. File moi tes affaires, maintenant !"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Please don't hurt me!  Take all that you want."
msgstr "Ne me faites pas de mal! Prenez tout ce que vous voulez."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What, <no>!"
msgstr "Quoi, <no>!"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I have nothing more to say to you.  Get the fuck out of here."
msgstr "J'ai rien de plus à te dire. Casse toi."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, what are you waiting for?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous attendez?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You are what you eat, as they say."
msgstr "Vous êtes ce que vous mangez, dit le dicton."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's you again."
msgstr "Vous de nouveau?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hello there.  Haven't seen you around before.  You must be from the other "
"wing.  Managed to survive, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I've been through situations far worse than that."
msgstr "Ouais, j'ai survécu des situations bien pires que ça."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It was a nightmare, lots of <zombies>, blood everywhere!  Thank god I'm among "
"living people again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[CANNIBAL] It's hard to die of hunger when there's so many tasty corpses "
"lying around."
msgstr ""
"[CANNIBALE] Difficile de mourir de faim avec autant de corps frais dans les "
"environs."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I want to get out of this <freaking> prison.  I hoped you could help me with "
"that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm on my way."
msgstr "J'y vais."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know if I'll take your advice, but thanks nevertheless."
msgstr "Je ne sais pas si je vais suivre vos conseils, mais merci quand même."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Wait, what?  A <freaking> can of beans?!  I went through hell to get this "
"<freaking> thing for you, and all you give me as reward is a <freaking> can "
"of beans?!  I demand something more substantial."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice talking to ya.  Farewell."
msgstr "Ravi⸱e d'avoir parlé avec vous.  Au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh, even so?  I'm not saying I approve your… tastes, but I definitely "
"respect people who use all possibilities life has to offer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, we share the same opinions on this matter."
msgstr "Ouais, on a la même opinion là-dessus."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, that's a boastful statement.  Not that I don't believe it, it's just….  "
"Ah, nevermind.  Let's get to the point.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hold the horses, pal.  Nobody allowed you to stay here - yet."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Please!  I don't want to go back there!  I'm tired and hungry!  I just need "
"time to rest!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Shit!  Looks like I'm on my own now.  Thanks for nothing.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We don't have much space, and there's not much food.  Besides, I don't know "
"you at all, and something tells me you won't survive another day."
msgstr ""
"Nous n'avons pas beaucoup d'espace, et pas beaucoup de nourriture. De plus, "
"nous ne vous connaissons pas du tout, et quelque chose me dit que vous "
"n'allez pas survivre longtemps."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[STR 11] I'm tougher than it seems!"
msgstr "[STR 11] Je suis plus coriace que j'en ai l'air!"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Survival 2] I have some survival expertise!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess I need to find some other place…"
msgstr "J'imagine que je dois trouver un autre endroit…"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The answer is still no.  In fact it might be better for us to kill you right "
"away - you know, the less mouths to feed, the better.  But I'm in a good mood "
"today, so I've decided to help you get out of this island."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok, I'm listening."
msgstr "Ok, j'écoute."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know, I think I'll manage without your help.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I need you to retrieve some stuff from a locked safe.  Interested?"
msgstr ""
"J'aurais besoin que vous me récupériez des choses d'un coffre-fort "
"verrouillé. Êtes-vous intéressé(e)?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Show the military ID card.] You mean this stuff?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's in the safe?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qu'il y a dans le coffre-fort?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What for do you need it?"
msgstr "Pourquoi vous en avez besoin?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
msgid "Yeah, sure."
msgstr "Ouais, bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have a bad feeling about this.  Sorry, I'll pass."
msgstr "J'ai un mauvais présentiment. Désolé(e), mais sans moi."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As I said, that's the thing I need.  You don't need to know what's that "
"exactly.  Just grab all things you find in the safe, and call it a day."
msgstr ""
"Comme je l'ai dis, c'est ce dont j'ai besoin. Tu n'as pas besoin de savoir ce "
"que c'est exactement. Tu prends juste tout ce qui est dans le coffre fort, et "
"ça sera bon."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's weird."
msgstr "C'est bizarre."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let's say that's none of your <freaking> business.  Other questions?"
msgstr "On va dire que c'est pas ton <freaking> de problème. D'autres questions ?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, where did you get it?  Nevermind, just give it to me.  Right now."
msgstr "Eh, où t'as eu ça ! En fait on s'en fou, file-le moi. Maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, no need to be hostile.  Here you go, I don't need it anyway."
msgstr "Hé, pas besoin d'être hostile. Tiens, j'en ai pas besoin de toute façon."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I went through incredible hardships to get it.  Please, can I keep this to "
"myself?"
msgstr "J'ai vraiment galéré à l'avoir. S'il te plait, je peux le/la garder ?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I killed tons of <zombies> while I was trying to get this thing.  Do you "
"really think you and your handful of losers pose a threat to me?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai tué des tonnes de <zombies> en essayant d'obtenir ce truc. Tu penses "
"vraiment que toi et ta poignée de losers représentez une menace pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay.  It was convincing.  I'll still get what I want, one way or another.  "
"You better watch your back from now on."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. C'était convaincant. J'aurais quand même ce que je veux, d'une "
"manière ou d'une autre. Tu ferais mieux de surveiller tes arrières à partir "
"de maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Noted.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "C'est noté. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm afraid you're not in the position to demand anything from me, <name_b>.  "
"You're done here, leave."
msgstr ""
"Je crains que tu ne sois pas en position de demander quoi que ce soit, "
"<name_b>. T'es fini ici, pars."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, fuck you, <name_b>!  You'll regret that!"
msgstr "Hé, va te faire foutre, <name_b> ! Tu vas le regretter !"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, fine.  Cheapskate!"
msgstr "Ok, bien. Radasse !"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgstr "Récupérer La Chose, du bureau du chef"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid "Here's the job…"
msgstr "Voici le job…"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid ""
"My snitch whispered in my ear that the thing I need is located in the chief's "
"safe in his office.  You need to crack it open and bring the contents to me.  "
"Don't try to use anything you find in there!  Just bring all the stuff to me, "
"and I'll help you.  Deal?"
msgstr ""
"Mon informateur m'a chuchoté à l'oreille que la chose dont j'ai besoin se "
"trouve dans le coffre-fort du chef, dans son bureau. Vous devez l'ouvrir et "
"m'en apporter le contenu. N'essayez pas d'utiliser ce que vous trouverez "
"là-dedans ! Apporte-moi tout ce qu'il y a dedans et je t'aiderai. C'est "
"d'accord ?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid ""
"Great!  Don't forget that I need all stuff from the safe, try not to lose a "
"thing."
msgstr ""
"Super ! N'oublie pas que j'ai besoin de tout ce que tu trouvera dans le "
"coffre, ne perds rien. "

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid "Fine, I'll get the thing in any case, sooner or later."
msgstr "Bien, j'aurais la Chose dans tous les cas, tôt ou tard."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid ""
"The chief's office is on the other side of the prison.  I think the road "
"there is full of <zombies>, so you better find a weapon.  Also you probably "
"will need some tools to crack the safe open."
msgstr ""
"Le bureau du chef est de l'autre côté de la prison. Je pense que la route "
"là-bas est pleine de <zombies>, donc vous devriez trouver une arme. Vous "
"aurez aussi probablement besoin d'outils pour ouvrir le coffre."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid "Did you get the stuff already?"
msgstr "Vous avez ce que je vous ai demandé?"

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid ""
"At last!  Give me a few moments to check if it isn't damaged.  Here, take "
"this for your troubles."
msgstr ""
"Enfin ! Laisse-moi vérifier s'il n'est pas endommagé. Prends ça pour tes "
"ennuis."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid "Huh.  This isn't going to work like I thought."
msgstr "Hunh. Ça ne s'est pas passé comme je l'aurais pensé."

#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get The Thing from the chief's office"
msgid "You're useless.  I should've killed you when I met you."
msgstr ""
"Vous êtes totalement inutile. J'aurais du vous tuer le moment ou j'ai posé "
"mes yeux sur vous."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hiya darlin', welcome to the shop."
msgstr "Salut chéri(e), bienvenu(e) au magasin."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, killer!  How's it going?"
msgstr "Hey tueur ! Comment ça va ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Still the apocalypse out there, huh?"
msgstr "C'est toujours l'apocalypse là-dehors?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "See anything you like?"
msgstr "Il y a quelque chose qui vous plaît?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that contract…"
msgstr "Au sujet de ce contrat…"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with all the weapons and armor?"
msgstr "Pourquoi toute les armes et pièces d'armure?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you and Jay close?"
msgstr "Est-ce que vous et Jay sont… proches?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Motion to the sketches.] What is it that you are working on?"
msgstr "[Mouvement vers les esquisses.] Vous travaillez sur quoi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Motion to the sketches.] You seem more excited about this stuff recently."
msgstr ""
"[Pointez vers les dessins.] Vous avez l'air beaucoup plus enthousiaste sur le "
"sujet de ces trucs récemment."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to know more about some of your 'special' projects."
msgstr "J'aimerais en apprendre un peu plus au sujet de vos \"projets spéciaux\"."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Show the nomad jumpsuit blueprint.] Hey - I met a group with some "
"interesting ideas for armor design.  Is any of this of use to you?"
msgstr ""
"[Montrez les plans pour la combinaison de nomade.] J'ai rencontré un groupe "
"avec des idées intéressantes pour concevoir des armures. Ça vous serait utile "
"?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[100 merch] I'd like to become a member of the co-op."
msgstr "[100 merch] J'aimerais rejoindre la coopérative."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About those contracts…"
msgstr "Au sujet de ces contrats…"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why do you hate merch?"
msgstr "Pourquoi est-ce que vous n'aimez pas la merch?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you make me a suit of armor?"
msgstr "Vous pourriez me fabriquer une armure?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you make me a weapon?"
msgstr "Vous pourriez me fabriquer une arme?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my armor coming?"
msgstr "Comment va mon armure?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my weapon coming?"
msgstr "Comment va mon armure?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned you'd need some special materials to make that nomad armor?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez mentionné que vous auriez besoin de matériaux spéciaux pour me "
"fabriquer cette armure de nomade?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Interesting.  When would be the next batch of merchandise ready?"
msgstr "Intéressant. Quand est-ce que le prochain lot de marchandises sera prêt ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I heard you might want some metal…"
msgstr "J'ai entendu que vous pourriez apprécier une livraison de métal…"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "With how the things are goin'? <interval>."
msgstr "Vu comment les choses se passent ? <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll leave you to your work then.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Je vous laisse travailler alors. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm Cody, was an engineer before everything went to hell.  I guess I still "
"am, but I don't have to consult anymore, so I consider that a plus at least."
msgstr ""
"Je m'appelle Cody, j'étais ingénieur avant que tout ne parte en vrille. Je "
"suppose que je le suis toujours, mais je n'ai plus besoin d'être consultant, "
"alors je considère que c'est au moins un avantage."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know if you've met Jay yet, but he and I split a garden out here.  We "
"both work - well, worked - in technology, and we were convinced the world was "
"ending so we both got property outside town.  We met when he moved in next "
"door.  So this is our little homestead with a few upgrades.  We aren't really "
"sweating property lines at this point."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas si vous avez déjà rencontré Jay, mais lui et moi partageons un "
"jardin ici. Nous travaillons tous les deux - enfin, nous avons travaillé - "
"dans le domaine de la technologie, et nous étions convaincus que la fin du "
"monde était proche, si bien que nous avons tous les deux acheté une propriété "
"en dehors de la ville. Nous nous sommes rencontrés lorsqu'il a emménagé à "
"côté. Voici donc notre petite propriété, avec quelques améliorations. Nous ne "
"nous préoccupons pas vraiment des limites de propriété à ce stade."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I make them myself!  I've always loved traditional armaments and am a proud "
"member of the SCA!  Figured now that everything has gone to hell I can make "
"it a full-time thing.  Lots of survivors in need of a big ol' hammer or some "
"armored guards to keep the biters off."
msgstr ""
"Je les fabrique moi-même ! J'ai toujours aimé les armes traditionnelles et je "
"suis un fier membre de la SCA ! Je me suis dit que maintenant que tout est "
"parti en vrille, je pouvais en faire une activité à plein temps. Il y a "
"beaucoup de survivants qui ont besoin d'un bon vieux marteau ou de gardes en "
"armure pour éloigner les mordeurs."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It must take some serious equipment to make all this."
msgstr "Il doit y avoir besoin d'équipements sérieux pour faire tout ça."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, what can I say, I had lots of disposable income.  Kept me busy and all "
"that.  So yeah, I've got a pretty impressive shop in the back."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, que puis-je dire, j'avais beaucoup de revenus disponibles. Ça "
"m'occupait et tout ça. Alors oui, j'ai un magasin assez impressionnant à "
"l'arrière."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 8] Still this is a lot of equipment.  Wouldn't it have been easier to "
"buy this stuff from a manufacturer?"
msgstr ""
"[INT 8] Il s'agit tout de même d'une grande quantité d'équipement. "
"N'aurait-il pas été plus facile d'acheter ce matériel auprès d'un fabricant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can anyone use the workshop?"
msgstr "Est-ce que n'importe qui peut utiliser cet atelier?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Honey, I have a hard time finding a bra that fits.  Good luck finding a "
"breastplate."
msgstr ""
"Mon chou, j'ai du mal à trouver un soutien-gorge qui me convienne. Bonne "
"chance pour trouver un plastron qui aille."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell me about it, finding anything that fits in this apocalypse has been a "
"nightmare."
msgstr ""
"Parlez-moi de cela, trouver quelque chose qui fonctionne dans cette "
"apocalypse a été un cauchemar."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, uh.  Right, uh."
msgstr "Oh, euh. Bien, euhh."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, not *anyone*, but I've always been a believer in community.  The shop "
"is run as a co-op, so if you want access you'll have to buy a share.  As a "
"partial owner, you will have full access to the shop.  Shares are currently "
"100 merch; I hate the currency but it's the closest thing we've got to a "
"representation of labor."
msgstr ""
"Enfin, pas *tout le monde*, mais j'ai toujours cru en la communauté. La "
"boutique est gérée comme une coopérative, donc si vous voulez y avoir accès, "
"vous devrez acheter une part. En tant que propriétaire partiel, vous aurez un "
"accès complet à la boutique. Les parts sont actuellement de 100 merch ; je "
"déteste cette monnaie mais c'est ce qui se rapproche le plus d'une "
"représentation du travail."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[100 merch] Yeah, I can do that."
msgstr "[100 merch] Ok, ça me va."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There yah go, one co-op membership with your name on it.  Shop's in the back, "
"keep it tidy and share if anyone else is around workin'.  Just as a heads-up, "
"you'll need to bring your own charcoal.  There's a kiln in there too, so if "
"you got things to burn, just throw 'em in there and light up."
msgstr ""
"Et voilà, une adhésion à la coopérative à votre nom. Le magasin est à "
"l'arrière, gardez-le en ordre et partagez si quelqu'un d'autre travaille dans "
"le coin. Pour information, vous devez apporter votre propre charbon de bois. "
"Il y a aussi un four, alors si vous avez des choses à brûler, jetez-les là et "
"allumez-les."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Money is part of what got us into this mess in the first place."
msgstr "L'argent est ce qui nous a mis dans cette galère en premier lieu."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PER 8] Is that why you don't carry any cash?"
msgstr "[PER 8] C'est pour ça que tu ne portes pas de cash sur toi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "B-I-N-G-O.  If you bring it, I'll take it, but that's about it."
msgstr "B-I-N-G-O. Si vous l'apportez, je le/la prendrai, mais c'est à peu près tout."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, we've always got along great.  He comes over for supper every Friday.  "
"Have a few drinks, maybe take some guns out.  Or, well… we used to.  A little "
"while ago, we had a huge fight.  It was right after this stuff got real bad… "
"I'm fuzzy on the details or what I said, all I remember was being so angry "
"that I could kill him.  We haven't talked much since."
msgstr ""
"Oui, nous nous sommes toujours bien entendus. Il vient dîner tous les "
"vendredis. On boit quelques verres, on sort peut-être quelques armes. Ou, "
"bien... nous avions l'habitude. Il y a peu de temps, on a eu une grosse "
"dispute. C'était juste après que les choses aient dégénéré... Je ne me "
"souviens plus très bien des détails ou de ce que j'ai dit, tout ce dont je me "
"souviens, c'est que j'étais tellement en colère que j'aurais pu le tuer. Nous "
"n'avons pas beaucoup parlé depuis."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you apologized?"
msgstr "Vous vous êtes excusée?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can do?"
msgstr "Est-ce que que je peux faire quoi que soit ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It just seemed like it wouldn't be enough.  I know it's silly but I have to "
"do more than that."
msgstr ""
"J'avais l'impression que cela ne suffirait pas. Je sais que c'est idiot, mais "
"je dois faire plus que cela."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you're offering.  Before everything went to hell, Jay was talking about "
"going to some gun show.  There was a guy there who had managed to sneak some "
"Russian gun into the US.  It was a massive deal for Jay, it was all he could "
"talk about.  I know it's a long shot, but maybe that guy was already at the "
"gun show?  If you find the gun you can keep it, but it would mean a lot to "
"Jay if he could take a look.  All he wanted was to pull it apart and put it "
"back together."
msgstr ""
"Si vous le proposez. Avant que tout ne parte en vrille, Jay parlait d'aller à "
"un salon de l'armement. Il y avait là un type qui avait réussi à faire entrer "
"en douce des armes russes aux États-Unis. C'était une affaire énorme pour "
"Jay, il ne parlait que de ça. Je sais que c'est peu probable, mais peut-être "
"que ce type était déjà présent à la foire aux armes ? Si vous trouvez l'arme, "
"vous pouvez la garder, mais cela compterait beaucoup pour Jay s'il pouvait y "
"jeter un coup d'œil. Tout ce qu'il voulait, c'était la démonter et la "
"remonter."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll bring you back a souvenir."
msgstr "Je vous ramènerai un souvenir."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not really interested."
msgstr "Ça ne m'intéresse pas vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, honey!  I'm always in need of more material!  What's the price, though?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr! J'ai toujours besoin de plus de matières premières. Par contre, "
"quel est votre prix?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, how about 100 merch for every 70 pounds of metal…"
msgstr ""
"100 merch pour chaque 32 kilos de métal que vous êtes capable de me ramener, "
"ça vous va?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, I don't really have the time to work on something like that.  I've got "
"lots of pieces for sale on the shelves."
msgstr ""
"Désolée, mais je n'ai pas vraiment le temps de travailler sur un projet aussi "
"large. Mais si vous voulez j'ai beaucoup de pièces individuelles à offrir sur "
"mes étagères."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_avatar.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_line.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_nevermind>"
#. ~ Avatar response indicated that the conversation is over.
#. ~ Snippet in category "<no>"
#. ~ Generally emphatic negative responses to a request or command
msgid "Forget it."
msgstr "Oubliez."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[350 merch, 1.2mm] I'd prefer to just have chainmail."
msgstr "[350 merch, 1.2mm] Je préfèrerais juste de la maille."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[400 merch, 2mm] I like to stay light."
msgstr "[400 merch, 2mm] J'aime voyager léger."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[500 merch, 4mm] A middle ground would be good."
msgstr "[500 merch, 4mm] Je préfère un bon compromis."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[600 merch, 6mm] Never skimp on protection."
msgstr "[600 merch, 6mm] Je ne lésine jamais sur l'épaisseur."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alright, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm, so the next question "
"is time.  Currently, it's the classic problem: if you want quality, you gotta "
"wait.  Two processes I could offer that you would be hard-pressed to find "
"anywhere else are either really great high carbon steel, or I can go through "
"the lengthy process of tempering.  High carbon will take three weeks to "
"process and do the work, and tempering will take me four."
msgstr ""
"Ok, <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm d'épaisseur donc, la "
"seconde question que j'ai pour vous est combien de temps vous voulez me "
"donner. Pour l'instant c'est un problème classique, si vous voulez de la "
"qualité, cela me prendra plus de temps à fabriquer. Deux services que je peux "
"offrir que vous aurez probablement des difficultés à trouver qui que ce soit "
"d'autre pouvant le faire, est de vous fournir de l'armure en acier très riche "
"en carbone, ou de l'armure ayant été passée à travers le travail long et "
"difficile du trempage. L'armure riche en carbone me prendra trois semaines à "
"fabriquer, l'armure trempée quatre."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"  For five I could, I think, create a suit of that nomad armor.  It would "
"incorporate climate control, help you support more weight, and it'll have a "
"jumpsuit built in, but you won't be able to wear normal clothes with it."
msgstr ""
" Pour cinq merchs, je pense que je pourrais créer une armure nomade. Elle "
"comprendrait un système de régulation thermique, vous aiderait à supporter "
"plus de poids et comporterait une combinaison, mais vous ne pourriez pas "
"porter de vêtements normaux avec."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 weeks, great protection] High steel sounds great."
msgstr ""
"[3 semaines, très bonne protection] De l'acier de haute qualité sonne bon "
"pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 weeks, exceptional protection] I'll wait for the best you can do."
msgstr ""
"[4 semaines, qualité de protection exceptionnelle] Je peux attendre pour le "
"meilleur que vous pouvez produire."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 weeks, CBM-integrated protection] I'd like nomad armor."
msgstr "[5 semaines, protection avec interface MBC] J'aimerais une armure de nomade."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made of the best high steel a woman can scavenge.  If you're good with that, "
"I'll take the merch up front and we can start taking some very invasive "
"measurements."
msgstr ""
"D'accord, il s'agira d'une armure "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm faite du meilleur acier qu'une "
"femme puisse trouver. Si cela vous convient, je prendrai les merchs à "
"l'avance et nous pourrons commencer à prendre des mesures très invasives."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made with some of the best fabrication techniques the world has ever seen.  "
"If you're good with that, I'll take the merch up front and we can start "
"taking some very invasive measurements."
msgstr ""
"Donc, ce sera une armure de <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm "
"d'épaisseur avec l'acier le plus solide pouvant être fabriqué. Si cela vous "
"va, je peux prendre la merch à l'avance et nous pouvons commencer à prendre "
"des mesures très invasives."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alright, so it'll be <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm armor "
"made with some of the best fabrication techniques the world has ever seen, as "
"well as help from some extradimensional friends.  I'd be lying if I said I "
"wasn't excited.  If you're good with that, I'll take the merch up front and "
"we can start taking some very invasive measurements."
msgstr ""
"Donc, ce sera une armure de <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_thickness>mm "
"d'épaisseur avec l'acier le plus solide pouvant être fabriqué et de l'aide de "
"la part d'amis extradimensionnels. Je serais une menteuse si je disais que je "
"ne suis pas un peu excitée de commencer. Si cela vous va, je peux prendre la "
"merch à l'avance et nous pouvons commencer à prendre des mesures très "
"invasives."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_armor_cost> merch] Sounds good.  See you "
"in <u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_wait> weeks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Um… wait, I don't have that kind of money right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's all done!  Sorry for the long wait; hopefully it's worth it.  If you "
"need it refitted, let me know."
msgstr ""
"C'est prêt! Désolée pour la longue attente; j'espère que l'armure valait la "
"peine d'attendre et n'oubliez pas de me dire si vous avez besoin de l'ajuster."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Still working on it."
msgstr "Je suis toujours en train de travailler dessus."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you when it's done."
msgstr "On se reverra quand ce sera fini. "

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh wow, this is really interesting, huh?  The way they balance weight for "
"travel is genius.  If you wanted a real suit of armor for a traveling "
"warrior, I think I could do it with this.  I'll need one of each of these "
"wire kits, though, for each set I make.  Bring some to me if you want me to "
"use them."
msgstr ""
"Oh wow, c'est vraiment intéressant, hein ? La façon dont ils équilibrent le "
"poids pour le voyage est géniale. Si vous vouliez une véritable armure pour "
"un ou une guerrière itinérante, je pense que je pourrais le faire avec ça. "
"Mais il me faudra un exemplaire de chacun de ces kits de fils pour chaque "
"ensemble que je fabriquerai. Apportez-m'en si vous voulez que je les utilise."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have some right now.  [Hand over a CBM interface wire kit and an external "
"climate control kit.]"
msgstr ""
"J'en ai en ce moment. (Tend un kit de câbles d'interface MBC et un kit de "
"contrôle de la température externe)."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll try and find some."
msgstr "Je vais essayer d'en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Here you go.  [Hand over a CBM interface wire kit and an external climate "
"control kit.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_fabricate.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not right now."
msgstr "Pas maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, these.  With the end of the world, Jay and I had been talking about some "
"new projects for the wasteland warriors.  Anyways, it doesn't matter anymore "
"since… well, it doesn't matter."
msgstr ""
"Oh, ça.  Avec la fin du monde, Jay et moi avions parlé de nouveaux projets "
"pour les guerriers de l'apocalypse.  De toute façon, ça n'a plus d'importance "
"puisque… eh bien, ça n'a plus d'importance."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sure we'll fix things soon!"
msgstr "Je suis sûre que nous allons bientôt arranger les choses !"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah!  I feel a lot better now that Jay and I are talking again, and we've "
"been putting some serious work into this stuff.  If you wanted to help source "
"parts and do some testing, we could definitely get some prototypes made."
msgstr ""
"Oui ! Je me sens beaucoup mieux depuis que Jay et moi nous parlons à nouveau "
"et que nous travaillons sérieusement sur ce projet. Si vous voulez nous aider "
"à trouver des pièces et à faire des tests, nous pourrons certainement "
"fabriquer des prototypes."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm already working on something for you.  I only got two hands and 24 hours "
"in a day."
msgstr ""
"Je travaille déjà sur quelque chose pour vous. Je n'ai que deux mains et 24 "
"heures par jour."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm still working on it, can't rush perfection."
msgstr ""
"Je suis toujours en train de travailler dessus, la perfection ne peut pas "
"être pressée."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, what would you like to know more about?"
msgstr "Bien sûr, que voudriez-vous savoir de plus ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you work on one of these projects for me?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous travailler sur ces projets pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Motion to the picture of some kind of rifle.] What's the 'OBREZ'?"
msgstr "[Pointez vers une photo d'une sorte de fusil.] Qu'est ce que \"l'OBREZ\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is the Obrez finished?"
msgstr "L'Obrez est fini?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Motion to the picture of a switchblade.] What's the 'PRESSIN'?"
msgstr ""
"[Mouvement vers l'image d'un couteau à cran d'arrêt.] Qu'est-ce que le « "
"PRESSIN » ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is the Pressin finished?"
msgstr "Le Pressin est fini?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Motion to the picture of a mace styled with fire on the head.] What's the "
"'LOUVERTURE'?"
msgstr ""
"(Mouvement vers l'image d'une masse stylisée avec du feu). Qu'est-ce que la « "
"LOUVERTURE » ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is the Louverture finished?"
msgstr "Louverture est finie?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Motion to the picture of a sledge hammer with a piston jutting from one face "
"of the head.] What's the 'DISORDER'?"
msgstr ""
"(Mouvement vers l'image d'un marteau de forgeron avec un piston dépassant "
"d'une face de la tête). Qu'est-ce que le « DISORDER» ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is the Disorder finished?"
msgstr "Le Disorder est terminé ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Obrez is a classic Mosin-Nagant that someone has cut down and removed the "
"stock of.  The idea was that in some parts of the world a surplus rifle was "
"easier than finding a pistol to conceal.  Way I see it, a sturdy classic gun "
"like that with a bit of reinforcement could make a great mace.  You find me a "
"functioning Mosin - any variant will do - and 50 merch for parts, and I can "
"get this one working in a week."
msgstr ""
"L'Obrez est un Mosin-Nagant classique dont quelqu'un a coupé et enlevé la "
"crosse. L'idée était que dans certaines régions du monde, il était plus "
"facile de se procurer un fusil de surplus que de trouver un pistolet à "
"dissimuler. De mon point de vue, un pistolet classique et robuste comme "
"celui-là, avec un peu de renfort, pourrait faire une excellente masse. "
"Trouvez-moi un Mosin en état de marche - n'importe quelle variante fera "
"l'affaire - et 50 merch pour les pièces, et je pourrai faire fonctionner "
"celui-ci en une semaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Mosin-Nagant M44, 50 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[Mosin-Nagant M44, 50 merch] On se voit la semaine prochaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Mosin-Nagant 1891/30, 50 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[Mosin-Nagant 1891/30, 50 merch] On se voit la semaine prochaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about another project?"
msgstr "Qu'en est-il d'un autre projet ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll check in later."
msgstr "Je reviendrai plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The gun is done, looking pretty sleek if you ask me.  All loaded and ready to "
"cave in a zombie."
msgstr ""
"L'arme est terminée, elle a l'air plutôt élégante si vous voulez mon avis. "
"Tout est chargé et prêt à faire tomber un zombie."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Pressin was a self defense weapon for politicians in Spain.  It was a "
"small breach loaded handheld pistol that could fit in a glasses case and be "
"fired subtly.  I figure that we can improve on the design by adding a "
"retracting blade while keeping the surprise shots.  To get this working I'm "
"gonna need a .32 gun like a Kel-Tec P-32, or a Walther PPK.  I'll also need a "
"switchblade, 20 merch, and a week."
msgstr ""
"Le Pressin était une arme de défense personnelle pour les politiciens en "
"Espagne. C'était un petit pistolet à chargement par la culasse, suffisamment "
"compact pour tenir dans un étui à lunettes et être tiré discrètement. Je "
"pense qu'on peut améliorer le design en ajoutant une lame rétractable tout en "
"gardant les tirs surprises. Pour que ça fonctionne, il me faudra un pistolet "
"en calibre .32, comme un Kel-Tec P-32 ou un Walther PPK. Il me faudra aussi "
"un couteau à cran d'arrêt, 20 unités de marchandise, et une semaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PPK, switchblade, 20 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[PPK, couteau à cran d'arrêt, 20 merch] On se voit la semaine prochaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[P-32, switchblade, 20 merch] See you in a week."
msgstr "[P-32, couteau à cran d'arrêt, 20 merch] On se voit la semaine prochaine."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The gun's done.  Mind the safety on the side, this guy is pretty dangerous."
msgstr ""
"L'arme est prête. Attention à la sécurité sur le côté, cette arme est plutôt "
"dangereuse."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, that's one of my sillier ideas.  Jay is convinced it'll never work but I "
"really want to give it a shot.  A traditional mace with gas-venting ports and "
"an ignition system for mini bursts of fire.  Maybe I've just played too many "
"RPGs, but it seems worth a shot.  To get this one working I'm gonna need a "
"real deal mace -  something that can handle the pressure - as well as a "
"military grade flamethrower.  Fabrication will definitely take two weeks on "
"this one."
msgstr ""
"Oh, c'est une de mes idées les plus stupides. Jay est convaincu que ça ne "
"marchera jamais, mais j'ai vraiment envie d'essayer. Une masse traditionnelle "
"avec des orifices d'évacuation de gaz et un système d'allumage pour des "
"mini-balles de feu. J'ai peut-être joué à trop de RPG, mais ça vaut le coup "
"d'essayer. Pour que celui-ci fonctionne, je vais avoir besoin d'une véritable "
"masse - quelque chose qui puisse supporter la pression - ainsi que d'un "
"lance-flammes de qualité militaire. La fabrication prendra certainement deux "
"semaines."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Mace, flamethrower] See you in 2 weeks."
msgstr "[Masse d'arme, lance-flammes] On se revoit dans 2 semaines."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The mace is done.  It honestly works pretty great too.  Hope you get some "
"good use out of it."
msgstr "La masse est fini. Elle a l'air parfaite. J'espère que vous l'utiliserez bien."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Disorder is already kind of a real thing.  I got the idea from a viral "
"video I saw of a guy making something similar with a baseball bat for hitting "
"home runs.  Takes a sledge hammer with a center mounted piston that you can "
"arm with .22 caliber blanks.  When you hit a zombie with that sweet spot… "
"boom.  The blank goes off and sends the piston straight down into whatever "
"poor fucker you hit it with.  I'll need a sledge hammer, 80 merch, and at "
"least 20 .22 LR rounds.  Fabrication will definitely take two weeks on this "
"one."
msgstr ""
"Le Désordre est déjà en quelque sorte quelque chose ayant existé. J'ai eu "
"l'idée d'une vidéo virale que j'ai vu d'un gars ayant fabriqué quelque chose "
"de similaire avec une batte de baseball pour marquer des home runs. Ça "
"demande un marteau de démolition équipé d'un piston au centre pouvant être "
"poussé par des cartouches à blanc de calibre .22. Lorsque vous frapper un "
"zombie fort avec... boom. La cartouche à blanc explose et propulse la masse "
"directement dans ce que vous frappez. J'aurais besoin d'un marteau de "
"démolition, 80 merch, au moins 20 cartouches de .22 LR et définitivement deux "
"semaines pour fabriquer cela."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Sledge hammer, 80 merch, 20 .22 LR] See you in 2 weeks."
msgstr "[Masse, 80 merch, 20 cartouches de .22 LR] On se revoit dans 2 semaines."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_prototype.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The beast is done!  Really heavy-duty, but really packs a punch.  Be careful "
"with your fingers.  I'm serious, this thing could tear 'em off."
msgstr ""
"La bête est terminée ! Très résistante, elle a du punch. Attention à vos "
"doigts. Je suis sérieux, cette chose pourrait les arracher."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Do you still want to order your "
"<item_name:<u_val:general_artisans_blacksmith_weapon>> or would you like to "
"choose something else?"
msgstr ""
"Voulez-vous commander votre "
"<item_name:<u_val:general_artisans_blacksmith_weapon>> ou bien voulez-vous "
"choisir quelque chose d'autre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, I want to order it."
msgstr "Oui, je veux passer commande."

#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200 merch, 3 days] I need a mace."
