msgstr "[<item_name:wooden_post_long>, $1.5 par pièce, max 100]"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[<item_name:wood_panel>, $8 a piece, max 100]"
msgstr "[<item_name:wood_panel>, $8 par pièce, max 100]"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[<item_name:wood_sheet>, $16 a piece, max 100]"
msgstr "[<item_name:wood_sheet>, $16 par pièce, max 100]"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[<item_name:wood_beam>, $25 a piece, max 50]"
msgstr "[<item_name:wood_beam>, $25 par pièce, max 50]"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[<item_name:log>, $5 a piece, max 100]"
msgstr "[<item_name:log>, $5 par pièce, max 100]"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<color_light_red>[Reset.]</color>"
msgstr "<color_light_red>[Remise à zéro.]</color>"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"<color_light_green>[$<npc_val:number_fabricate_price>] That's all.  I'm ready "
"to pay.</color>"
msgstr ""
"<color_light_green>[<npc_val:number_fabricate_price>$] C'est tout. Je suis "
"prêt(e) à payer.</color>"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LUMBERMILL_FABRICATE_ordered" in
#. nested EOCs on true condition in an effect
msgid ""
"Your order will be ready in <npc_val:number_fabricate_wait> days.\n"
"Come back in that time to pick up your lumber."
msgstr ""
"Votre commande sera prête dans <npc_val:number_fabricate_wait> jours.\n"
"Revenez à ce moment pour récupérer votre bois."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I don't want to place an order."
msgstr "En fait, je ne veux pas passer de commande."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let me check…  <u_name>…  Yes, all your lumber are ready, you can pick it up."
msgstr ""
"Laissez-moi vérifier…  <u_name>…  Oui, votre bois est prêt, vous pouvez le "
"récupérer."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Your order?  No, sorry, we're still working on it."
msgstr "Votre commande ? Non, pardon, elle n'est pas terminée."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_fabricate.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Merci. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello there.  Nice to see you, <name_g>."
msgstr "Salut toi. C'est chouette de te voir, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A stranger out here?  Who are you?"
msgstr "Un(e) étranger(e) ici ? Qui êtes-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_combat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<hands_up>"
#. ~ Mostly hostile NPCs say these things in preparation for mugging an
#. unarmed avatar.
msgid "Hands up, <name_b>!"
msgstr "Mains en l'air, <name_b>!"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pleasure to see you again."
msgstr "C'est un plaisir de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Do you need something?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I wonder if you've heard "
"anything about it?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis à la recherche d'un bâtiment spécifique et étrange. Je me demande si "
"vous en avez entendu parler."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do things work around here now?"
msgstr "Comment ça marche par ici maintenant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nah, see ya."
msgstr "Nan, à plus."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The logger "
"considers for a moment"
msgstr ""
"&Vous décrivez l'entrepôt du mieux que vous pouvez. Le bûcheron réfléchit un "
"instant"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh well.  Thanks anyway.  I'll go ask around."
msgstr "Ok. Merci quand même. Je vais me renseigner."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You mean you're still looking for wood?  Crazy… but we had a suspicion folks "
"might show up in an emergency.  Talk to the manager if you want to make an "
"order."
msgstr ""
"Vous voulez dire que vous cherchez encore du bois?  C'est fou… mais on se "
"doutait que des gens pourraient se présenter en cas d'urgence.  Parlez au "
"directeur si vous voulez passer une commande."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, the machinery works just fine.  We were always self-sufficient and "
"<the_cataclysm> only really made that more apparent.  So if you want to place "
"an order and help keep the operation running, talk to the manager.  We'll "
"trade you for our wood."
msgstr ""
"La machinerie fonctionne très bien. Nous avons toujours été autosuffisants et "
"<the_cataclysm> n'a fait que le mettre en évidence. Donc si vous voulez "
"passer une commande et aider à faire fonctionner l'entreprise, parlez-en au "
"directeur. Nous vous échangerons notre bois."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I'm a logger here.  Seasonal work but good pay… or it was, at least.  "
"Before that first <zombie> showed up and made it clear how bad things were "
"really getting."
msgstr ""
"Je suis bûcheron·ne ici.  Un travail saisonnier mais bien payé… du moins, "
"c'était le cas.  Avant que le premier <zombie> n'apparaisse et nous fasse "
"comprendre à quel point les choses allaient mal."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm a lumberjack out here.  Things were quiet for a long time.  We're pretty "
"far out in the woods so it was kind of a shock to find out just how bad it'd "
"gotten in civilization.  We had a couple close run-ins ourselves.  My friend "
"over there almost got eaten!  But we still have resources that I'm sure "
"people can use."
msgstr ""
"Je suis bûcheron(e) ici. Les choses sont restées calmes pendant longtemps. "
"Nous sommes assez loin dans les bois, alors ça a été un choc de découvrir à "
"quel point la situation s'était détériorée dans la civilisation. Nous avons "
"nous-mêmes frôlé la catastrophe à plusieurs reprises. Mon amie là-bas a "
"failli se faire manger ! Mais nous avons toujours des ressources que les gens "
"peuvent utiliser, j'en suis sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My comrades and I were lucky to be in the right place at the right time, I "
"suppose.  We keep really busy out here, so we didn't expect <the_cataclysm> "
"to land right in our lap like that.  Luckily these axes can chop more than "
"wood.  They'll take a good chunk out of anything nasty that threatens our "
"mill."
msgstr ""
"Mes camarades et moi avons eu la chance d'être au bon endroit au bon moment, "
"je suppose. Nous sommes très occupés ici, alors nous ne nous attendions pas à "
"ce que <the_cataclysm> nous tombe dessus comme ça. Heureusement, ces haches "
"peuvent couper bien plus que du bois. Elles sont capables de couper un bon "
"morceau de tout ce qui menace notre moulin."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I work here.  Welcome to the mill.  Used to be trucks in and out of "
"here all the time but you're the first face we've seen in a while."
msgstr ""
"Je travaille ici. Bienvenue à l'usine. Il y avait des camions qui entraient "
"et sortaient tout le temps, mais vous êtes le premier visage que nous voyons "
"depuis un moment."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_logger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hope it goes well."
msgstr "J'espère que tout ira bien."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello there.  Nice to see you again."
msgstr "Bonjour, content(e) de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "A new face at the mill?  Who might you be?"
msgstr "Un nouveau visage à la scierie? Qui êtes vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_combat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<hands_up>"
#. ~ Mostly hostile NPCs say these things in preparation for mugging an
#. unarmed avatar.
msgid "Hands up!"
msgstr "Mains en l'air!"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, what's up?"
msgstr "Alors, quoi de neuf?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When will you have new stuff in stock?"
msgstr "Quand les nouveaux produits seront-ils en stock ?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I order a batch of lumber?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my order going?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I use the gate?  I'd like to bring a vehicle for trade."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll tell the guys to open one of the gates, but you gotta promise to be "
"careful.  We've got a simple rule here: You break it, you buy it!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll be careful."
msgstr "Je ferais attention."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Workers will bring in a new shipment of lumber in <interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I mean, I don't remember a whole lot about this job I had, I just know that I "
"managed this lumbermill and sold wood to… somebody.  I think it was some sort "
"of company.  I'm just glad I remember my coworkers here, my <name_g>s.  "
"They're helping me to try and remember who I was before all this.  You see, "
"that's the weird thing; I remember what my job was and how to do it the right "
"way, but I don't know where I learned that, or who taught me.  I just know "
"that we're in this together, and we're gonna make it through Hell if we have "
"too."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the manager here at the mill.  It's a tight-knit crew, unionized "
"operation.  When <the_cataclysm> broke out, we were all running scared when "
"some <zombies> broke onto the yard, had to fight them off.  Now, we've just "
"held up here.  I imagine any folks left out there might be needing our "
"machinery and skills to keep civilization alive.  Might make new customers "
"yet."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/TALK_lumbermill_merchant.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hm."
msgstr "Hmm."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "logger"
msgstr "bûcheron"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "manager"
msgstr "manager"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
#. ~ Job description of "Lumberjack" NPC class
msgid "I felled trees before the apocalypse.  Zombies shouldn't be as tough."
msgstr ""
"J'ai abattu des arbres avant l'apocalypse. Les zombies ne devraient pas être "
"aussi coriaces."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Drive Belts"
msgstr "Trouvez des Courroies de Transmission"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Obtain 3 drive belts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr ""
"Obtenez 3 courroies de transmission en échange d'un crédit auprès des "
"bûcherons."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "I need three drive belts."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 3 courroies de transmission."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid ""
"Some of our machinery received some damage before <the_cataclysm> and we were "
"waiting on replacement parts.  Now everything's changed and those parts are "
"more important than ever.  Get us three drive belts and I'll give you some "
"credit with us."
msgstr ""
"Certaines de nos machines ont été endommagées avant <the_cataclysm> et nous "
"attendions des pièces de rechange. Maintenant, tout a changé et ces pièces "
"sont plus importantes que jamais. Trouvez-nous trois courroies de "
"transmission et je vous accorderai un certain crédit."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Someone's got to do it."
msgstr "Quelqu'un doit le faire."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid ""
"If you can't find actual drive belts on engines, a good replacement can be "
"made from a belt and some duct tape.  Nothing difficult."
msgstr ""
"Si vous ne trouvez pas de courroies d'entraînement sur les moteurs, vous "
"pouvez en fabriquer une bonne à partir d'une courroie et d'un peu de ruban "
"adhésif. Rien de bien compliqué."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Do you have the belts?"
msgstr "Vous avez les courroies?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Wonderful!  Thanks, <name_g>, we'll be fine for a long while from now."
msgstr "Merveilleux ! Merci, <name_g>, nous nous en sortirons encore longtemps."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Where are they?  I don't believe you."
msgstr "Où sont-ils?  Je ne vous crois pas."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to do it."
msgstr ""
"C'est dommage. Je suppose que nous devrons trouver quelqu'un d'autre pour le "
"faire."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgstr "Trouvez 1000 Clous"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Obtain 1,000 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Trouvez 1000 clous pour obtenir un crédit avec les bucherons."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "I need 1,000 nails."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 1000 clous."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid ""
"Along with those drive belts, we were waiting for some nails for structural "
"repairs.  Due to <the_cataclysm>, we obviously never received them.  So, I "
"need you to get us 1,000 nails.  We'll pay you fairly."
msgstr ""
"En plus de ces courroies de transmission, nous attendions des clous pour des "
"réparations structurelles. En raison du <the_cataclysm>, nous ne les avons "
"évidemment jamais reçus. J'ai donc besoin que vous nous fournissiez 1 000 "
"clous. Nous vous paierons équitablement."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Taking apart some furniture in town should get what you need."
msgstr ""
"Démonter quelques meubles en ville devrait vous permettre d'obtenir ce dont "
"vous avez besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Do you have the nails?"
msgstr "Vous avez les clous?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Our warehouse was about to fall apart.  These will be extremely helpful to us."
msgstr ""
"Notre entrepôt était sur le point de s'effondrer. Ces produits nous seront "
"d'une grande utilité."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgstr "Trouvez 6800 Clous"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Obtain 6,800 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Trouvez 6800 clous pour obtenir un crédit avec les bucherons."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "I need 6,800 nails."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 6800 clous."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid ""
"While fairly sturdy, the metal fence around this place won't hold out for "
"long.  So, we've decided to replace it with a wall.  However, the nails we "
"had were used to repair our existing structures, and they weren't nearly "
"enough.  After some calculations, we need 6,800 nails to do it.  That may "
"seem like a lot, but we're willing to give you a TON of credit for it."
msgstr ""
"Bien que relativement solide, la clôture métallique qui entoure cet endroit "
"ne tiendra pas longtemps. Nous avons donc décidé de la remplacer par un mur. "
"Cependant, les clous dont nous disposons ont été utilisés pour réparer nos "
"structures existantes, et ils sont loin d'être suffisants. Après quelques "
"calculs, nous avons besoin de 6 800 clous. Cela peut sembler beaucoup, mais "
"nous sommes prêts à vous accorder une TONNE de crédit pour cela."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Well, I suppose that's reasonable."
msgstr "Je suppose que c'est raisonnable."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid ""
"You might have to do more than just scrapping a bunch of furniture.  "
"Dismantling a building somewhere in town could get you what you need."
msgstr ""
"Vous devrez peut-être faire plus que mettre à la ferraille un tas de meubles. "
"Le démantèlement d'un bâtiment quelque part en ville pourrait vous permettre "
"d'obtenir ce dont vous avez besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "That's absolutely amazing!  I can't thank you enough for this!"
msgstr "C'est absolument génial ! Je ne saurais trop vous en remercier !"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "You're a fucking scammer, <name_b>!"
msgstr "Vous êtes un putain d'escroc, <name_b>!"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 6 Blankets"
msgstr "Trouvez 6 Couettes"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "Obtain 6 blankets or quilts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr "Trouvez 6 couvertures ou couettes pour obtenir un crédit avec les bucherons."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "I need 6 blankets."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de 6 couettes."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid ""
"Now that we should be safe from harm, I decided to start adding a few things "
"to this place.  Right now, we don't have anywhere to comfortably sleep, so "
"we're building a small sleeping quarter.  We just need 6 big, warm blankets "
"or quilts to finish our project."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que nous sommes à l'abri du danger, j'ai décidé de commencer à "
"ajouter quelques éléments à cet endroit. Pour l'instant, nous n'avons pas "
"d'endroit où dormir confortablement, c'est pourquoi nous construisons un "
"petit dortoir. Nous avons juste besoin de 6 grandes couvertures ou couettes "
"chaudes pour terminer notre projet."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "I figure any hotel or motel in town should have lots of blankets."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que tout hôtel ou motel de la ville devrait disposer de nombreuses "
"couvertures."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "Did you find us some bedding yet?"
msgstr "Avez-vous trouvé les couettes que je vous ai demandées?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid ""
"Thanks!  Feel free to sleep here if you want.  It's the least we can do for "
"the help."
msgstr ""
"Merci d'avance ! N'hésitez pas à dormir ici si vous le souhaitez. C'est le "
"moins que l'on puisse faire pour vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "How is this supposed to help us?"
msgstr "En quoi cela est-il censé nous aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Establish trade relations between the loggers and a refugee center, and bring "
"back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr ""
"Établir des relations commerciales entre les exploitants forestiers et un "
"centre de réfugiés, et rapporter un document de l'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"While some of us were out scavenging, we spotted an old evac shelter that "
"looks like it might have some people inside.  I want you to go over there, "
"find whoever runs the joint, and see if we can make a deal with them for some "
"processed lumber.  This will be invaluable to our survival."
msgstr ""
"Alors que certains d'entre nous étaient en train de faire les poubelles, nous "
"avons repéré un vieil abri d'évacuation qui semble avoir des occupants à "
"l'intérieur. Je veux que vous alliez là-bas, que vous trouviez la personne "
"qui gère l'endroit et que vous voyiez si nous pouvons passer un accord avec "
"eux pour obtenir du bois transformé. Cela nous sera d'une aide précieuse pour "
"notre survie."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Please give it a try?  This is really important to us."
msgstr "Vous voulez essayer ? C'est très important pour nous."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "What did they say about the deal?"
msgstr "Qu'ont ils dit au sujet de notre offre?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Thank you!  We're set for life on this one!"
msgstr "Merci ! Nous sommes prêts pour la vie !"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "How does this help us?"
msgstr "En quoi cela nous aide-t-il?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to trade with."
msgstr ""
"C'est dommage. Je suppose que nous devrons trouver quelqu'un d'autre avec qui "
"échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A member of the Gray Moose Lodge, trying to safe in their isolated
#. location
msgid "Militia Guard"
msgstr "Garde de la Milice"

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ Job description of "Guard" NPC class
msgid "I'm a local guard."
msgstr "Je suis un(e) garde local."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm busy on watch duty.  Talk to the Boss upstairs."
msgstr "Je suis de garde. Allez parler au patron à l'étage."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm on watch duty.  Talk to the Boss.  He's upstairs."
msgstr "Je suis de garde. Parlez au patron. Il est en haut."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there.  Hate to have to kill you after you've already died."
msgstr ""
"Soyez prudents. Je ne voudrais pas avoir à vous tuer après que vous soyez "
"déjà mort."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A member of the Gray Moose Militia, trying to safe in their isolated
#. location
msgid "Darby Sutton"
msgstr "Darby Sutton"

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Welcome to our camp.  Behave yourself while you are here.  What can I do for "
"you?"
msgstr ""
"Bienvenue à notre camp. Comportez-vous correctement quand vous êtes ici et "
"nous ne devrions pas avoir de problèmes. Qu'est-ce que je peux faire pour "
"vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Salvor_Market/uica_vehicle_marchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Salvor_Market/uica_vehicle_marchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you do here?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous faites ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the story behind this place?"
msgstr "Qu'elle est l'histoire derrière cette communauté?"

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Time for me to leave"
msgstr "Il est temps pour moi de partir je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the most senior member at this point so I'm what passes for the leader "
"here now.  I'm just trying to make plans to keep us alive since everything "
"fell apart."
msgstr ""
"Je suis le membre avec le plus de séniorité maintenant donc je suppose que je "
"suis ce qui peut compter comme un leader ici pour l'instant.  J'essaie juste "
"de planifier comment nous garder en vie maintenant que tout s'est écroulé."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, that's a long story.  We are what's left of the Grey Moose militia.  We "
"had plans for when things went south cause of crazy politicians or war, but "
"we didn't expect people to go crazy then turn zombie.  Only a handful of our "
"members actually made it through all that madness.  What's worse is that we "
"lost so much of our supplies and gear due to military checkpoints and trigger "
"happy soldiers.  It didn't matter that half of us were former military the "
"checkpoint guards just saw weapons, panicked and then confiscated everything "
"but the clothes on our back.  So here we are at our planned escape location "
"with not even a fraction of our manpower or supplies."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, c'est une longue histoire.  Nous sommes ce qui reste de la milice "
"Élan Gris.  Nous avions des plans sur ce que nous devrions faire si des "
"politiques cinglés lançaient une guerre ou une dictature ou quelque chose "
"comme ça, mais on était pas vraiment préparé à ce que tout le monde perde la "
"boule avant de devenir des mort-vivants.  Donc seulement quelques-uns de nos "
"membres se sont sorties de tout cela est nous avons perdu la majorité de nos "
"ressources et armes que nous avions préparées dû soit au chaos soit à des "
"fouilles lorsque nous sommes passés par des barrages policiers et militaires. "
" Peu importe que la plupart d'entre nous était des vétérans, les gardes de "
"checkpoint ont paniqué systématiquement lorsqu'ils ont vu nos armes lourdes "
"et tout confisqué jusqu'à ce que nous n'avions plus ou moins plus que nos "
"vêtements.  Donc nous voilà au bastion que nous avions préparé avec une "
"fraction dérisoire de nos membres et possessions."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can't say I can think of anything at the moment.  Our remoteness is our "
"defense.  We want to keep a low profile and try to keep out of any trouble in "
"this isolated location.  We are willing to trade for weapons and ammo though. "
" Keeping the nearby area clear and hunting is always eating away at our "
"supplies."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai rien que vous pourriez faire pour le moment.  Notre isolation est "
"notre principale défense.  Nous voulons garder un profil bas et évitez tout "
"problèmes ici.  Nous serions néanmoins plus que content d'acheter des armes "
"et munitions.  Garder les environs sûrs et chasser pour nous nourrir entame "
"comme même nos stocks limités."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keeping a low profile is good."
msgstr "Garder un profile bas est une bonne idée."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there.  Not enough of us are around anymore."
msgstr "Prenez garde dehors. Pas assez d'entre nous encore vivants."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former miner, poor fellow succumbed to spiral madness.
msgid "miner"
msgstr "mineur"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Miner"
msgstr "Mineur"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Job description of "Miner" NPC class
msgid "Spirals."
msgstr "Spirales."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Spirals?"
msgstr "Spirales?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello there!"
msgstr "Salut!"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr "Je m'en vais. Au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Poor fellow - looks like you're out of your mind.  Can't help you, sorry.  "
"I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr ""
"Le pauvre, on dirait que vous avez perdu la tête. Je ne peux pas vous aider, "
"désolé. Je m'en vais. Au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, what?"
msgstr "Désolé(e), quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you repeating 'spirals' over and over again?"
msgstr "Pourquoi répétez-vous le mot \"spirales\" encore et encore?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you nuts?"
msgstr "Est-ce que vous êtes cinglé(e)?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm afraid I can't talk now."
msgstr "J'ai peur de ne pas avoir le temps de discuter pour le moment."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there."
msgstr "Restez en sécurité."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella"
msgstr "Bienvenue au camp Arabella"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm supposed to direct all questions to my leadership."
msgstr "Je suis censé poser toutes les questions à mes supérieurs."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you're looking to trade you'll need to talk to the quartermaster."
msgstr "Si vous souhaitez faire du commerce, vous devez vous adresser à l'intendant."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
msgid "Duhring"
msgstr "Duhring"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Officer"
msgstr "Officier"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Job description of "Officer" NPC class
msgid "I'm an officer for FOB Arabella"
msgstr "Je suis un(e) officier/officière de FOB Arabella"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have any use for you right now.  You will be informed if I need you, "
"soldier."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas besoin de vous pour l'instant. Vous serez informé(e) si cela "
"change soldat(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about yourself?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me parler de vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "Understood."
msgstr "Compris."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If it wasn't clear, you are dismissed soldier."
msgstr "Si je n'était pas assez clair(e), vous êtes excusé(e) soldat(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I am clearly busy, soldier."
msgstr "Je suis manifestement occupé, soldat."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I just ask you some questions?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux juste vous poser quelques questions?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Go. Away."
msgstr "Partez. Tout de suite."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If I have to tell you one more time so help me god…"
msgstr "Si je dois vous le dire encore une fois, que Dieu me vienne en aide…"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Pilot"
msgstr "Pilote"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
#. ~ Job description of "Pilot" NPC class
msgid "I'm a pilot."
msgstr "Je suis un(e) pilote."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella, What will it be?"
msgstr "Bienvenue au camp Arabella, que voulez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the camp quartermaster.  Come and see me if you have anything valuable to "
"trade."
msgstr ""
"Je suis le quartier-maître du camp. Venez me voir si vous avez quelque chose "
"d'utile à échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you're looking to trade you've come to the right place."
msgstr "Si vous êtes ici pour échanger vous êtes au bon endroit."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "pizzaiolo"
msgstr "pizzaiolo"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I got the cake.  Shall we move, <name_g>?"
msgstr "J'ai le gâteau. Allons-y <name_g>?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you still want to travel with me, let's go."
msgstr "Si tu veux toujours voyager avec moi, allons-y."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Lead the way, <name_g>."
msgstr "Montrez le chemin <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are we there yet, my <name_g>?"
msgstr "Sommes-nous déjà arrivés, mon <name_g> ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're here, <name_g>.  Let's celebrate."
msgstr "Nous sommes là, <name_g>. Faisons la fête."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Be patient.  We'll be there soon, <name_g>"
msgstr "Soyez patients. Nous serons bientôt là, <name_g>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[*NOM-NOM*]"
msgstr "[*NOM-NOM*]"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Mmm, delicious.  You know, you are good friend, and a good cook.  I'm glad "
"that I'm with you at the day like this.  Say, what do you think about me "
"going with you?  As you can see, my restaurant is thrashes, my house ruined, "
"the only option left is to travel somewhere, and it's better if I do it with "
"someone."
msgstr ""
"Mmm, délicieux. Tu sais, tu es un bon ami et un bon cuisinier. Je suis "
"content d'être avec toi en ce moment. Dis, qu'est-ce que tu penses du fait "
"que je vienne avec toi ? Comme tu peux le voir, mon restaurant est en ruine, "
"ma maison aussi, la seule option qui me reste est de voyager quelque part, et "
"c'est mieux si je le fais avec quelqu'un."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, <name_g>.  <end_talking>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgstr "Pizzaiolo Enragé"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Bring the pizzaiolo to <color_light_blue>their rival's house</color> and "
"don't forget to <color_yellow>bring at least 200 units of gasoline</color>.  "
"After you got there, talk to the pizzaiolo to start burning the house."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"I'm so angry!  I have an enemy that ruined my life, and I want revenge for "
"it!  I don't care about <the_cataclysm>, I just want to burn his <freaking> "
"restaurant!  Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Good.  Let's go to his restaurant and fucking burn it!  Oh, by the way, could "
"you bring gasoline with you, <name_g>?  I was so angry I forgot to bring it "
"with me…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "What?!  Why do you… ah, forget it."
msgstr "Quoi?!  Pourquoi vous… ah, oubliez-ça."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid "Maybe we can find some gasoline at gas station."
msgstr "Peut être que nous pouvons trouver du carburant à une station essence."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Sweet, sweet revenge!  It smells so nice!  His restaurant burns, his legacy "
"is now ruined!  Even if he became a <zombie>, it still good."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgstr "Trouvez le vrai Foodperson"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid "Help pizzaiolo find TrueFoodperson and kick his ass."
msgstr "Aidez pizzaiolo à trouver le vrai Foodperson et à lui botter le cul."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"Ah, it's you, <name_g>.  Wanna continue on my revenge to all American "
"<name_b>s?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"Good.  Next stop, Foodplace.  I always hated that place, especially that "
"<freaking> <name_b> in his idiotic mask.  I know he's still alive, hiding in "
"his dumb parody of a restaurant.  Take this bat.  Let's take a visit to him, "
"<name_g>, and kick his <freaking> ass!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"I heard that these 'restaurants' use some kind of locking system for staff "
"room, so we would need to find a way to get there."
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu dire que ces \"restaurants\" utilisaient une sorte de système de "
"verrouillage pour la salle du personnel, de sorte que nous devions trouver un "
"moyen d'y accéder."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "I'm waiting."
msgstr "J'attends."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid "Another one bite the dust!  We did good, <name_g>."
msgstr "Un autre a mordu la poussière ! Nous avons bien travaillé, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pizza parlor"
msgstr "Pizzeria"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "Help pizzaiolo take back his restaurant."
msgstr "Aidez le pizzaiolo à reprendre possession de sa pizzeria."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid ""
"I need to make a last step to achieve my revenge, and the step is - my pizza "
"parlor.  Before <the_cataclysm>, the bank took my place, and now, some "
"<freaking> <name_b>s occupied it and made it their base!  Just unbelievable, "
"I tell ya.  It's time for me to fight back, deal with this <freaking> "
"<name_b>s and regain my honor.  Are you with me, <name_g>?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "Very good.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "These <name_b>s might be heavily armed, so we need to prepare to face them."
msgstr ""
"Ces <name_b> pourraient être lourdement armés, nous devons donc nous préparer "
"à les affronter."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid ""
"Nice, very fucking nice.  Fuck, this placed is thrashed.  <freaking> "
"<name_b>s thrashed my restaurant!  Okay, calm down, calm down, will ya… At "
"least I retrieved my place.  Thank you, <name_g>.  I couldn't make it without "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Family house"
msgstr "Maison de Famille"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Family house"
msgid "First bring pizzaiolo some chocolate cake then lead him to his family house."
msgstr ""
"Amenez d'abord un gâteau au pizzaïolo puis guidez-le vers sa maison de "
"famille."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid ""
"Now, as my competitors dead, their places are ruined, it's time to relax… I "
"know, let's celebrate it!  Lead me to my house.  Also, we need a cake for "
"that.  What celebration without a cake, right?  I can teach you how to cook "
"it, if you want."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que mes concurrents sont morts, leurs entreprises en ruine, il est "
"temps de se relaxer ou même… célébrer! Ramenez-moi chez moi. Aussi, nous "
"avons besoin d'un gâteau pour ça. Ce ne serait pas une vraie célébration sans "
"un gâteau non? Je peux vous apprendre comment le cuisiner, si vous voulez."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "Good.  Bring me chocolate cake and talk to me."
msgstr "Bien. Amenez-moi un gâteau au chocolat et parlez avec moi."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid ""
"If you listened to me very closely, it wouldn't be hard for you to make it.  "
"Good luck, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"Si vous avez bien écouté ce que je vous ai dit, il ne devrait pas être dur "
"pour vous d'en cuisiner un. Bonne chance <name_g>. "

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "You learn how to craft cake."
msgstr "Vous apprenez comment cuisiner un gâteau au chocolat."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are we there yet, <name_g>?  I can't wait to burn that building!"
msgstr "On y est déjà, <name_g> ? J'ai hâte de brûler ce bâtiment !"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/missiondef.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're here.  Let's do it!"
msgstr "Nous sommes ici. C'est parti !"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Be patient, <name_g>, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "Ayez un peu de patience, <name_g>, nous sommes presque là."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Finally, someone who isn't part of those <zombies>."
msgstr "Enfin quelqu'un qui ne fait pas partie de ces <zombies>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, today's your lucky day.  Hand over your stuff, or you'll be one "
"yourself."
msgstr ""
"Oui, c'est votre jour de chance. Remettez vos affaires, ou vous en serez un "
"vous-même."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, nice to meet you."
msgstr "Salut, enchanté·e de vous rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<greet>"
msgstr "<greet>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous exactement?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wanna buy something, maybe sell off what you don't need?"
msgstr ""
"Vous voulez acheter quelque chose, voire vendre ce dont vous n'avez pas "
"besoin ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I buy one of your pets?"
msgstr "Je pourrais acheter l'un de vos animaux?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's quite noble of you, but how do you take care of so many animals?"
msgstr ""
"C'est très noble de votre part, mais comment faites-vous pour vous occuper "
"d'autant d'animaux ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be honest with you, it's been pretty difficult.  I sneak out at night or "
"whenever there's an opening to grab whatever I need and come back before "
"something notices me.  I've been held up for quite a while whenever a horde "
"decides to pass by.  Good thing we had some spare bookcases lying around, or "
"I'd be a goner by now."
msgstr ""
"Pour être honnête avec vous, c'est assez difficile. Je sors furtivement la "
"nuit ou dès qu'il y a une ouverture pour prendre ce dont j'ai besoin et je "
"reviens avant que quelqu'un ne me remarque. Il m'est arrivé d'être bloqué "
"pendant un bon moment lorsqu'une horde décidait de passer par là. "
"Heureusement que nous avions des bibliothèques en réserve, sinon je serais "
"déjà mort."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Interesting."
msgstr "Intéressant."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hate to see them go, but I think you'd be able to take better care of one "
"than I can right now.  I can sell you a cat or dog of your choosing, for $25 "
"and $50, respectively."
msgstr ""
"Je déteste les voir partir, mais je pense que vous seriez capable de mieux "
"vous occuper de l'un d'entre eux que je ne peux le faire actuellement. Je "
"peux vous vendre un chat ou un chien de votre choix, pour 25 et 50 dollars "
"respectivement."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've changed my mind, let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Oubliez, parlons d'autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a dog."
msgstr "J'aimerais un chien."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a cat."
msgstr "J'aimerais un chat."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hand over your stuff!  Don't make any sudden moves, or you die!"
msgstr ""
"Remettez vos affaires ! Ne faites pas de mouvements brusques, ou vous mourrez "
"!"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What brings you around here?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui vous amène ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be interested in trading at all?"
msgstr "Vous seriez intéressé(e) à faire du troc?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I stay here for a while?"
msgstr "Je peux rester ici un petit moment?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr "Vous voulez venir avec moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why would someone leave a gun store open in all this chaos?"
msgstr "Pourquoi quelqu'un laisserait-il un magasin d'armes ouvert dans ce chaos ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, they weren't really around to lock it up.  Whoever got here first blew "
"their head off with a 12-gauge, but they were up and movin', tried to kill me "
"too.  They're out in the dumpster now."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, ils n'étaient pas vraiment là pour la fermer. Celui qui est arrivé "
"le premier leur a explosé la tête avec un calibre 12, mais ils étaient debout "
"et bougeaient, ils ont essayé de me tuer aussi. Ils sont dans la benne à "
"ordures maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that.  Maybe we should change the subject."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Freeze you <freaking> <zombies>!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "&Hold up your hands.  \"Don't worry, I'm not going to hurt you\""
msgstr "Levez les mains. \"Ne vous inquiétez pas, je ne vais pas vous faire de mal."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you doing in this deathtrap?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous faites dans ce traquenard?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wow."
msgstr "Wow."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<greet>."
msgstr "<greet>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glad to see you too.  Now, hand over your things."
msgstr "Heureux de vous voir aussi. Maintenant, remettez vos affaires."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_TECHNO_KID.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey <name_g>."
msgstr "Hey <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just wandering, <name_g>."
msgstr "J'errais dans le coin, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'll make this real simple for you.  Hand over your stuff, and no one gets "
"hurt, capiche?"
msgstr ""
"Je vais vous simplifier la tâche. Vous me donnez vos affaires, et personne "
"n'est blessé, capiche ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I purchase any of your liquor?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux acheter votre alcool?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's a bit dangerous to be out here alone.  Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr "C'est un peu dangereux d'être seul ici. Pourquoi ne viens-tu pas avec moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I could do for you?"
msgstr "Il y a quelque chose que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be interested in bartering?"
msgstr "Vous voulez faire du troc?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I guess you could borrow one of the spare beds, just don't hog it.  I "
"kept a few in case someone else joined me, but no one I knew came here."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que vous pouvez emprunter un des lits d'appoint, mais ne le "
"monopolisez pas. J'en ai gardé quelques-uns au cas où quelqu'un d'autre me "
"rejoindrait, mais personne que je connaissais ne venait ici."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't come any closer!"
msgstr "Ne faîtes pas un pas de plus!"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qu'il y a?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/camp_start.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's stay here, then.  I trust your decisions."
msgstr "Restons ici, alors. Je fais confiance à vos décisions."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "meteorologist"
msgstr "météorologiste"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Meteorologist"
msgstr "Météorologiste"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Job description of "Meteorologist" NPC class
msgid "Meteorologist."
msgstr "Météorologiste."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Run, I need to run, where to run…"
msgstr "Courir, j'ai besoin de courir, où courir…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I can help you with your problem?"
msgstr "Peut être que je peux vous aider avec votre problème?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I need more time.  Come back later."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de plus de temps. Revenez plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "No problem."
msgstr "Pas de problème."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, you can relax now."
msgstr "Oui, vous pouvez vous relaxer maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't worry, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "Ne vous inquiétez pas, nous arrivons bientôt."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank you.  I will never forget your kindness, <name_g>.  Take this book as "
"token of my gratitude."
msgstr ""
"Merci, je n'oublierais jamais votre générosité <name_g>. Veuillez accepter ce "
"livre comme un gage de ma gratitude."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Me too."
msgstr "Moi aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Trouvez de la ferraille pour le météorologiste"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 50 pieces of scrap."
msgstr "Le météorologiste m'a demandé de lui apporter 50 morceaux de ferraille."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need scrap metal to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "J'ai besoin de ferraille pour assembler un drone…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"I've been sitting here for a long time, and all that time I was wondering how "
"bad everything is outside.  I want to build a drone that I can use to fly "
"over New England, check the air condition, take a few pictures from above to "
"get a glimpse of how is it.  There were a lot of things in our back room that "
"could be useful, but still I'm missing a lot of things.  You look like an "
"experienced survivalist.  Can you help me?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis assis ici depuis longtemps, et pendant tout ce temps, je me suis "
"demandé si tout allait bien à l'extérieur. Je veux construire un drone que je "
"pourrais utiliser pour survoler la Nouvelle-Angleterre, vérifier l'état de "
"l'air, prendre quelques photos d'en haut pour avoir un aperçu de l'état des "
"lieux. Il y avait beaucoup de choses dans notre arrière-boutique qui "
"pourraient être utiles, mais il me manque encore beaucoup de choses. Vous "
"avez l'air d'un survivaliste expérimenté. Pouvez-vous m'aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Good.  I just need a little stuff: 50 scrap, 6 medium batteries, 5 small "
"high-quality lenses and a radio remote control.  Bring the scrap for now, but "
"don't forget about the rest."
msgstr ""
"Bien. Je n'ai besoin que de quelques trucs: 50 morceaux de ferraille, 6 "
"batteries moyennes, 5 petites lentille haute qualité de caméra et une télé. "
"Ramenez-moi la ferraille pour l'instant, mais n'oubliez pas le reste de la "
"liste."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe another time…"
msgstr "Peut être un autre jour…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"I don't think this is a difficult task.  Surely there is a lot of it "
"underfoot."
msgstr ""
"Je ne pense pas que ce soit une tâche difficile. Il y en a certainement "
"beaucoup sous les pieds."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "How's it going?"
msgstr "Comment allez vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm starting to work on it…"
msgstr "Super, je commence à travailler dessus…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "Why do you say that?"
msgstr "Pourquoi dites-vous cela ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Trouvez des batteries pour le météorologiste"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 6 medium batteries."
msgstr "Le météorologiste m'a demandé de lui apporter 6 batteries moyennes."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need batteries to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Nous avons besoin de batteries pour assembler un drone…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, batteries.  6 medium batteries would be "
"enough."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, ce qui vient ensuite sur la liste… oui, des piles.  6 piles moyennes "
"suffiraient."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "I'm waiting for you."
msgstr "J'attendrais votre retour."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "Try looking for some battery-powered trinkets and take them apart."
msgstr "Essayez de trouver des bibelots fonctionnant avec des piles et démontez-les."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm continue to work on it…"
msgstr "Très bien, je vais continuer à travailler dessus…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Trouvez des lentilles de haute qualité pour le météorologiste"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 5 small high-quality lenses."
msgstr ""
"Le météorologue a demandé à ce qu'on lui apporte 5 petits objectifs de haute "
"qualité."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need small high quality lenses for our drone…"
msgstr "Nous avons besoin de petites lentilles de haute qualité pour notre drone…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, lenses.  5 small high-quality lenses "
"would be enough."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, quelle est la prochaine étape sur la liste… oui, les lentilles.  5 "
"petites lentilles de haute qualité suffiraient."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "Try looking for telescopes or microscopes to dismantle."
msgstr "Essayez de démonter des télescopes ou microscopes pour en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm continuing to work on it…"
msgstr "Super, je continue à travailler dessus…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Trouver un contrôleur radio pour le météorologue"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him a radio controller."
msgstr "Ramenez une télécommande au météorologiste."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need an RC to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Trouver un contrôleur radio pour le météorologue"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, radio control.  Any kind will do, but "
"the simplest one is better, so I can easily reconfigure it for my drone."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, quelle est la prochaine étape sur la liste… oui, la radiocommande.  "
"N'importe quel type fera l'affaire, mais le plus simple est le mieux, pour "
"que je puisse facilement le reconfigurer pour mon drone."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "I advise you to search in a store, such as electronics or toy store."
msgstr ""
"Je vous conseille de chercher dans un magasin, par exemple un magasin "
"d'électronique ou de jouets."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Great, very little work left.  I need a few days to finish all this, and to "
"try it in work.  I hope everything will work fine!  While I'm working on the "
"drone, you can read this book.  Maybe you can learn something new from it."
msgstr ""
"Très bien, il reste très peu de travail. J'ai besoin de quelques jours pour "
"terminer tout cela, et pour l'essayer au travail. J'espère que tout "
"fonctionnera bien ! Pendant que je travaille sur le drone, tu peux lire ce "
"livre. Tu pourras peut-être y apprendre quelque chose de nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgstr "Trouvez le drone écrasé du météorologiste."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him his crashed drone."
msgstr "Le météorologiste vous a demandé de lui ramener son drone écrasé."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "I've lost the drone, we should find out what happened…"
msgstr "J'ai perdu le drone, nous devrions vérifier ce qui s'est passé…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"I'm glad that you are alive and that you haven't forgot about me.  The drone "
"turned out to be great, it managed to take off and even was able to fly "
"several hundred meters!  Unfortunately, after that, I lost control of it… I "
"don't know what happened to it, though.  Maybe you can check?  I'm a little "
"afraid to go out there…"
msgstr ""
"Je suis content que tu sois en vie et que tu ne m'aies pas oublié. Le drone "
"s'est avéré génial, il a réussi à décoller et même à voler sur plusieurs "
"centaines de mètres ! Malheureusement, après cela, j'en ai perdu le "
"contrôle... Mais je ne sais pas ce qu'il est devenu. Peut-être pourriez-vous "
"vérifier ? J'ai un peu peur de sortir de là..."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"I don't know quite what happened.  Maybe something noticed my drone and tried "
"to bring it down.  Be careful."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas vraiment ce qui s'est passé. Peut-être que quelque chose a "
"remarqué mon drone et a essayé de le faire tomber. Soyez prudent."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"Hmm, I see that the drone is not with you.  Maybe at least the memory module "
"remains?  Okay, show it to me… hmm, situation is worse than I expected, much, "
"much worse… I'm not feeling good.  I don't feel safe in this place anymore.  "
"I have to run, run somewhere.  But where to run if these monsters are "
"everywhere…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing to it.  Before <the_cataclysm>, it didn't take much to find yourself "
"here.  And I guess it just made sense to stay.  We seem to be doing better "
"than most, anyway."
msgstr ""
"Rien à voir. Avant <the_cataclysm>, il ne fallait pas grand-chose pour se "
"retrouver ici. Et je suppose qu'il était logique de rester. Nous avons l'air "
"de nous en sortir mieux que la plupart des gens, de toute façon."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Surviving, as I always have.  Is that what you mean?"
msgstr "Survivre, comme je l'ai toujours fait. C'est ce que vous voulez dire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you?  Would you like to trade?"
msgstr "Qui êtes vous? Voulez-vous échanger?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where might your friends be?"
msgstr "Où se trouvent vos amis?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I stay here?"
msgstr "Je peux rester ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I purchase some of your wares?"
msgstr "Je peux acheter quelques-uns de vos produits?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's that smoker coming along?"
msgstr "Comment se porte le fumoir?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Making ends meet, even in the worst circumstances.  We've been camping out "
"here now, trading with whoever passes by.  If something catches your eye, let "
"me know."
msgstr ""
"Joindre les deux bouts, même dans les pires circonstances. Nous campons "
"maintenant ici, échangeant avec tous ceux qui passent. Si quelque chose "
"attire votre attention, faites-le moi savoir."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We got tired of being out on the road and decided to stay here for a bit.  "
"We've found a lot of useful stuff out and about, so if you see anything you "
"need I'll make you a deal."
msgstr ""
"Nous en avons eu assez d'être sur la route et avons décidé de rester ici un "
"peu. Nous avons trouvé beaucoup de choses utiles, alors si vous voyez quelque "
"chose dont vous avez besoin, je vous propose un marché."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They should be around here somewhere.  We usually go out in teams to "
"scavenge, and they haven't told me about anything yet.  They might have "
"something for you to do."
msgstr ""
"Ils devraient être quelque part par ici. D'habitude, nous sortons en équipe "
"pour fouiller, et ils ne m'ont encore rien dit. Ils pourraient avoir quelque "
"chose à vous faire faire."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I don't see anything wrong with it.  We should have a spare bed in that "
"tent you could sleep on.  Just don't cause any trouble."
msgstr ""
"Je n'y vois pas d'inconvénient. Nous devrions avoir un lit d'appoint dans "
"cette tente sur lequel vous pourriez dormir. Mais ne causez pas de problèmes."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure!  It turned out well enough for us, and it's one of the few fresh meats "
"we can find.  I'll pay fairly for it."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr ! Il s'est avéré assez bon pour nous, et c'est l'une des rares "
"viandes fraîches que nous pouvons trouver. Je paierai le prix juste."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have nothing."
msgstr "Je n'ai rien."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have nothing.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Je n'ai rien.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's wonderful!  We've been preserving a lot more of what we manage to "
"scavenge so we won't have to worry about our food going bad for a while.  "
"We'd be willing to sell some of the excess, if you want."
msgstr ""
"C'est merveilleux ! Nous conservons beaucoup plus de ce que nous parvenons à "
"récupérer afin de ne pas avoir à nous soucier de la dégradation de notre "
"nourriture pendant un certain temps. Nous serions prêts à vendre une partie "
"de l'excédent, si vous le souhaitez."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'll buy 10 slices.  [$20]"
msgstr "Je voudrais acheter 10 tranches.  [$20]"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think 20 slices would be alright?  [$40]"
msgstr "Je pense que j'aimerais en acheter 20. [40$]"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take 50 slices of the stuff.  [$100]"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'en donner 50? [100$]"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you, and what are you doing here?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous, et que faites-vous ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you.  I mean no harm."
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer.  Je ne vous veux aucun aucun mal."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with that guy in the tent?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui se passe avec ce type dans la tente ?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want to trade?"
msgstr "Vous voulez faire du troc?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, they're right over there, and one of us is in that tent over there.  They "
"handle any stuff we manage to scavenge, so feel free to trade for what you "
"want."
msgstr ""
"Oh, ils sont juste là, et l'un d'entre nous est dans la tente là-bas. Ils "
"s'occupent de tout ce que nous parvenons à récupérer, alors n'hésitez pas à "
"échanger ce que vous voulez."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks for the offer, but I don't have anything to spare right now.  One of "
"my buddies over in that tent handles stuff like this, though.  You might find "
"something."
msgstr ""
"Merci pour l'offre, mais je n'ai rien à dépenser pour l'instant. L'un de mes "
"amis dans cette tente s'occupe de ce genre de choses. Vous trouverez "
"peut-être quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, they were the brightest of us when all hell broke loose.  They managed "
"to get us some food and weapons early on.  I guess that just kinda made them "
"the leader."
msgstr ""
"Ils étaient les plus brillants d'entre nous lorsque l'enfer s'est déchaîné. "
"Ils ont réussi à nous procurer de la nourriture et des armes très tôt. Je "
"suppose que cela a fait d'eux les leaders."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Sticky Situation"
msgstr "Situation Gluante"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Kill some slimes in exchange for credit with some of the traders and bring "
"back six of their slime scraps."
msgstr ""
"Tuez des slimes en échange de crédit avec certains des marchands et "
"ramenez-leurs six de leurs globes de gelée."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "I need some help."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'aide."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"We've had some trouble with slimes not far from us.  It's been hard going "
"through there with all them around, so I want you to go take care of it."
msgstr ""
"On a eu des problèmes avec des slimes dans les environs, et c'est difficile "
"de se déplacer là où ils sont, donc ça serait sympa si vous pouviez vous en "
"débarrasser de quelque uns."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "I'll be here when you get back."
msgstr "Je serai là à votre retour."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "No problem.  I'm sure one of us will get to it anyway."
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a pas de problème. Je suis sûr que l'un d'entre nous s'en chargera de "
"toute façon."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Sure, they can be cut, but I'd say it's better to splatter them with "
"something large and heavy."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, on peut les couper, mais je dirais qu'il vaut mieux les écraser  "
"avec quelque chose de gros et de lourd."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "Are those slimes dead yet?"
msgstr "Ces slimes sont morts?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll just take those off your hands.  Might be good for greasing the "
"bike chains and door hinges around here even though it is a bit… abnormal."
msgstr ""
"Parfait.  Je vais vous en débarrasser.  Cela pourrait être utile pour "
"graisser les chaînes de vélo et les charnières de porte par ici, même si "
"c'est un peu… anormal."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "You don't look nearly as sticky as you're supposed to.  Get back to it."
msgstr "Tu n'as pas l'air aussi collant que tu le devrais. Retournez-y."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "Did they give you the slip?  It's worse than I thought, then."
msgstr "Ils t'ont fait faux bond ? C'est pire que ce que je pensais."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Arthropod Hunting"
msgstr "Chasse aux Arthropodes"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"Kill some ants and bring back ten slices of their meat in exchange for credit "
"with some of the traders."
msgstr ""
"Tuez des fourmis et ramenez dix morceaux de leur viande en échange de crédit "
"avec certains des marchands."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"The last time we went out scouting we found some gargantuan ants crawling "
"around.  We thought we might see how they taste, if they could be cooked and "
"whatnot.  I want you to go kill one and bring back some of its meat."
msgstr ""
"La dernière fois que nous sommes partis en reconnaissance, nous avons trouvé "
"des fourmis gargantuesques qui rampaient autour de nous. Nous avons pensé "
"voir quel goût elles avaient, si elles pouvaient être cuisinées, etc. Je veux "
"que vous alliez en tuer une et que vous rameniez un peu de sa viande."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "Alright, I can understand that."
msgstr "Pas grave, je comprends."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "A shotgun of some sort might work well."
msgstr "Un fusil à pompe ou quelque chose de similaire ferait des merveilles."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "Do you have the meat?"
msgstr "Vous avez la viande?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll get these cooked up.  Who knows, we might want some more in the "
"future."
msgstr ""
"C'est bien. Je vais les préparer. Qui sait, nous pourrions en vouloir "
"d'autres à l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "You sure?  I don't see my meat anywhere."
msgstr "Vous êtes sûr(e)? Je ne vois ma viande nulle part."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Ah, well.  It's no big deal."
msgstr "Oh, ce n'est pas très grave."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments"
msgstr "Rénovations"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments"
msgid "Obtain 100 planks."
msgstr "Trouvez 100 planches."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
msgid ""
"My buddies and I have decided to stay here for a while.  This is about the "
"only safe place out here, and it's kinda become our home.  Anyway, we're "
"going to build a wall.  Our old logs have provided a bunch of the wood, but "
"we still need quite a few planks.  About 100 of them.  If you could get it "
"for us, I'd be grateful."
msgstr ""
"Mes amis et moi avons décidé de rester ici pendant un certain temps. C'est à "
"peu près le seul endroit sûr ici, et c'est un peu devenu notre maison. Quoi "
"qu'il en soit, nous allons construire un mur. Nos vieux troncs ont fourni une "
"bonne partie du bois, mais il nous faut encore pas mal de planches. Une "
"centaine. Si vous pouviez nous en procurer, je vous en serais reconnaissant."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll be sure to compensate your efforts."
msgstr "Merci, nous compenserons vos efforts gracieusement."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Alright, I can understand that.  I guess I'll have to get it myself."
msgstr "D'accord, je comprends. Je suppose que je vais devoir me le procurer moi-même."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid ""
"Any nearby forest should have all you need.  Otherwise, you might try "
"breaking down some furniture in town."
msgstr ""
"Les forêts avoisinantes devraient vous fournir tout ce dont vous avez besoin. "
"Sinon, vous pouvez essayer de casser quelques meubles en ville."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid "Do you have my lumber?"
msgstr "Vous avez le bois?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll start right away."
msgstr "Je vous remercie. Nous allons commencer tout de suite."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "I can tell you're lying.  I don't see shit."
msgstr "Je peux dire que vous mentez. Je ne vois rien."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgstr "Rénovations II"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid "Obtain 150 planks."
msgstr "Trouvez 150 planches."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid ""
"Now that we've got the wall done, we decided to move out of these old tents.  "
"We still have some leftover nails but we need more wood.  So, if you could "
"get us 150 planks, we'd be grateful."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que le mur est terminé, nous avons décidé de quitter ces vieilles "
"tentes. Il nous reste quelques clous, mais nous avons besoin de plus de bois. "
"Si vous pouviez nous procurer 150 planches, nous vous en serions "
"reconnaissants."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgstr "Rénovations III"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Obtain 6 ropes."
msgstr "Trouvez 6 cordes."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid ""
"Our entrance is wide open so we're building a gate over it.  Problem is we "
"don't have any ropes.  If you could find some for us, we'll pay you."
msgstr ""
"Notre entrée est totalement ouverte, nous voulons donc construire une porte, "
"mais n'avons aucune corde. Si vous pouviez nous en fournir, nous serions "
"disposés à vous payer."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid ""
"If you can't find any rope around, one of our books should have something on "
"rope-making.  Most plants can be woven into a halfway decent rope."
msgstr ""
"Si vous ne trouvez pas de corde dans les environs, l'un de nos livres devrait "
"contenir des informations sur la fabrication de cordes. La plupart des "
"plantes peuvent être tressées en une corde à peu près convenable."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Do you have my ropes?"
msgstr "Vous avez les cordes?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgstr "Rénovations IV"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Obtain a wood saw."
msgstr "Trouvez une scie à bois."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid ""
"We appreciate all of your help but we can't rely on everyone else to do "
"things for us.  I'd be willing to buy a wood saw of some kind from you so we "
"can cut our own wood as needed."
msgstr ""
"Nous apprécions votre aide, mais nous ne pouvons pas compter sur les autres "
"pour faire les choses à notre place. Je serais prêt à vous acheter une sorte "
"de scie à bois pour que nous puissions couper notre propre bois si nécessaire."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "A hardware store or lumbermill should have one."
msgstr "Un magasin de bricolage ou une scierie devrait probablement en avoir une."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Do you have my saw?"
msgstr "Vous avez la scie?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Thank you.  Pick what you want from our stash."
msgstr "Merci. Prenez ce que vous voulez de notre pile de choses."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgstr "Rénovations V"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Obtain a shovel."
msgstr "Trouvez une pelle."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid ""
"Our sanitation here has become… problematic.  We've mostly just been going "
"outside the walls to piss.  Not only is it kinda unhealthy, but the last time "
"I wandered out I almost got eaten!  So, if you'd get us a shovel, we could "
"make a latrine for ourselves.  We'll pay you fairly, as usual."
msgstr ""
"Nos standards sanitaires ici sont devenus un peu… problématiques. Jusqu'ici "
"nous ne faisions que sortir des murs pour pisser, mais maintenant, en plus du "
"fait que cela n'est pas exactement propre, c'est devenu dangereux, la "
"dernière fois que je suis sorti(e) je me suis presque fait dévorer! Donc, si "
"vous nous trouviez une pelle, nous pourrions nous creuser une latrine. Comme "
"d'habitude nous ferons en sorte de bien vous compensé pour l'embarras."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "A hardware store should have one lying around."
msgstr "Vous pourriez probablement en trouver une dans un magasin de bricolage."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Do you have the shovel?"
msgstr "Vous avez la pelle?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Thank you.  We're eternally grateful to you."
msgstr "Merci.  Nous vous sommes éternellement reconnaissants."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "I'll do it myself, then."
msgstr "Je le ferai moi-même dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgstr "Rénovations VI"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Obtain a charcoal smoker."
msgstr "Trouvez un fumoir au charbon de bois."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid ""
"Turns out that ant meat you got us wasn't actually too bad.  A little tough, "
"sure, but perfectly edible.  The problem now is we need a way of preserving "
"it.  One of those portable charcoal smokers would be really great.  Heck, you "
"might even wanna buy some."
msgstr ""
"Ont dirait que la viande de fourmi que vous nous avez ramenée n'est pas trop "
"mauvaise. Un peu coriace, mais parfaitement mangeable. Le problème maintenant "
"et que nous avons besoin d'un moyen de la conserver. L'un de ces fumoirs à "
"charbon serait probablement parfait. Nous serions totalement disposés à vous "
"vendre notre production après cela si vous en voulez."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid ""
"Maybe try a farm?  I bet those rural folks were pretty invested in preserving "
"their food."
msgstr ""
"Essayez de fouiller une ferme? Je parierai qu'il est probable que de fermier "
"avait de la nourriture à preserver sans frigos."

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Do you have the charcoal smoker?"
msgstr "Vous avez le fumoir à charbon?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll get started right away."
msgstr "Merci, on s'y met tout de suite."

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A person from elsewhere.
msgid "Involuntary Traveler"
msgstr "Voyageur Involontaire"

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_bye_portal_person>"
msgid "Pfum."
msgstr "Pfum."

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Job description of "No class" NPC class
msgid "I'm from another world."
msgstr "Je viens d'un autre monde."

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Dell hastro bovice?  Arand natick res?"
msgstr "Dell hastro bovice? Arand natick res?"

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What?"
msgstr "Comment?"

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Jand rawdle?  Ignate hasture."
msgstr "Jand rawdle?  Ignate hasture."

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I guess there's no reason to expect an interdimensional traveler to speak "
"English."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose qu'il n'y a aucune raison qu'un voyageur d'une autre dimension "
"parle ma langue."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My god, you've got to get me out of here.  The things… the things they've "
"done… please help."
msgstr ""
"Mon Dieu, vous devez me sortir de là.  Les choses… les choses qu'ils ont "
"faites… s'il vous plaît, aidez-moi."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aren't you a little short to be a stormtrooper?"
msgstr "Vous êtes pas un peu petit pour être un stormtrooper?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me."
msgstr "Aidez-moi, s'il vous plaît."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Can you get me out of this hell hole?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me tirer de cet enfer?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you?  Are you real?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous? Je ne suis pas en train de vous halluciner?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Can you please save me?  I have to get out of here."
msgstr "Vous pouvez me sauver? J'ai besoin de m'échapper d'ici."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hallelujah, rescue!"
msgstr "Alléluia, mon salut!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't believe my eyes.  Thank you, thank you!"
msgstr "Je ne peux pas y croire.  Merci, merci!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're… you're actually real!"
msgstr "Vous êtes, vous êtes réel(le)!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come with me, if you want to live."
msgstr "Suivez-moi si vous voulez survivre."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've no use for weaklings.  Run.  Now."
msgstr "Je n'ai pas besoin de faibles. Barrez-vous. Maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have anything that you'd like to sell?"
msgstr "Vous avez des choses que vous voulez vendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did you say you were going again?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que vous disiez que vous voyager vers déjà?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you found anything out of the ordinary out in the wastes?"
msgstr "Vous avez rencontré quoi que ce soit sortant de l'ordinaire sur la route?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What's in that RV of yours?  Couldn't be anything you need, so hand over your "
"stuff."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to meet you too.  What are you doing out here?"
msgstr "Le plaisir est partagé.  Que faites vous ici au milieu de nul part?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  <npc_name> "
"considers for a moment"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", nodding along.  \"Yeah, I remember something like that a while back.  "
"Pretty memorable building, I think it's what you're looking for.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm going south.  Hopefully somebody down there fared better than the people "
"I knew up here.  Besides, I won't have to worry about freezing my <freaking> "
"butt off when winter comes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm going west, see how things are out there in tumbleweed territory.  You "
"see, the Midwest didn't have a whole lot of people in it compared the East "
"Coast, so there logically shouldn't be as many <zombies> as there are here.  "
"I just hope that everything hasn't collapsed, that someone's still holding on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "ERROR: DIRECTION PARAMETERS EITHER NOT PICKED OR OUT OF BOUNDS"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When will you be leaving?"
msgstr "Quand partez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll be gone here in a day or two, just stopping long enough to get some "
"supplies and fix anything wrong with the camper."
msgstr ""
"Je serai parti/e d'ici un jour ou deux, je m'arrêterai juste le temps "
"d'acheter quelques provisions et de réparer ce qui ne va pas dans le "
"camping-car."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have a whole lot, but I've got a few things that I could stand to be "
"rid of, too much weight tanks the gas mileage.  I could always use more fuel, "
"food, and clean water if you have any to spare.  Entertainment is also "
"appreciated, it's pretty fucking boring looking at nothing but road for 10 "
"hours a day."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas grand-chose, mais j'ai quelques objets dont je pourrais me "
"débarrasser, car trop de poids nuit à la consommation d'essence. Je pourrais "
"toujours avoir besoin de plus de carburant, de nourriture et d'eau potable si "
"vous en avez à revendre. Les divertissements sont également appréciés, c'est "
"assez ennuyeux de ne regarder que la route pendant 10 heures par jour."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's take a look."
msgstr "Regardons-ça."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that farm?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je me rendre à cette ferme?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that cabin?"
msgstr "Comment atteindre cette cabine?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where were they at?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ah, that's nothing new to me.  Thanks anyway though."
msgstr "Ah, ce n'est pas nouveau pour moi. Merci quand même."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
msgid "Be careful.  Seems like a rough place to me."
msgstr "Faites attention, ça m'a l'air d'être un endroit assez sinistre."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
msgid "Sweet."
msgstr "Sympa."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
msgid "That's unfortunate."
msgstr "Regrettable."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that desolate barn"
msgstr "Visitez cette grange désolée"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "Garde de Caravane"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/obsoletion_and_migration_0.I/obsolete_npc_class.json
#. ~ Job description of "Trader" NPC class
msgid "I'm collecting gear and selling it."
msgstr "Je collecte de l'équipement pour le vendre."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, if "
"you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's plenty "
"of that on the roads already."
msgstr ""
"Nous ne sommes que des voyageurs qui font une halte. Nous pourrions être "
"disposés à échanger un peu, si vous avez quelque chose à partager. Nous ne "
"cherchons pas les ennuis, il y en a déjà beaucoup sur les routes."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're with a larger group of survivors, working out of one of the old FEMA "
"bunkers.  Folks have taken to calling us Free Merchants, although that sounds "
"kinda on the nose to me.  We know about a few survivor groups and we make "
"regular trips around, sharing supplies back and forth and bringing them home. "
" We're on the way back now."
msgstr ""
"Nous faisons partie d'un grand groupe de survivants et travaillons dans l'un "
"des anciens bunkers de la FEMA. Les gens ont pris l'habitude de nous appeler "
"\"Free Merchants\" (marchands libres), même si cela me semble un peu exagéré. "
"Nous connaissons quelques groupes de survivants et nous nous déplaçons "
"régulièrement pour échanger des fournitures et les ramener à la maison. Nous "
"sommes sur le chemin du retour."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where is 'home'?"
msgstr "Où se trouve le \"chez soi\" ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if you're "
"the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"Je vais l'indiquer sur votre carte. N'hésitez pas à venir faire du commerce, "
"ou si vous êtes du genre, nous pourrions avoir besoin de vos services en tant "
"que mercenaire."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Merci.  Eh bien, échangeons."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "Il est toujours bon de faire un peu de commerce."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "Je croix que j'ai un peu plus à échanger encore."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the "
"trader."
msgstr ""
"Sup ? Content de voir un survivant. Si vous êtes ici pour affaires, parlez au "
"commerçant."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "Merci pour l'astuce."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "Rebonjour.  Vous voulez quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "Vous cherchez du boulot? Je recrute peut être."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "Non, je ne fais que dire bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try to "
"find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr ""
"Je suis gardien de caravane et je travaille pour les marchands libres. Mais "
"je suis un entrepreneur indépendant. Je pense que c'est un bon moyen "
"d'assurer la sécurité par le nombre et d'essayer de trouver un endroit sûr "
"pour s'installer."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "Vous travaillez donc pour eux, mais vous n'êtes pas l'un d'entre eux ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything like "
"that?"
msgstr ""
"Les marchands libres ? Ont-ils une sorte d'avant-poste commercial ou quelque "
"chose comme ça ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's a living, eh?  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the early "
"part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone else "
"join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those traders "
"need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, ces gars ont récupéré une sorte de bunker d'évacuation de la FEMA au "
"début de <the_cataclysm> et gardent l'espace. Ils ne laissent personne "
"d'autre les rejoindre, mais ils ont besoin de provisions, alors ils envoient "
"des commerçants, et ces commerçants ont besoin de protection, alors ils "
"envoient des gars comme moi."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "Comment s'y rendre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr ""
"C'est bon pour l'instant, mais vous pouvez généralement trouver un mercenaire "
"ou deux qui attendent entre deux boulots, à la base des marchands libres."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci pour le conseil ! <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "Bien sûr, je peux l'indiquer sur votre carte si vous le souhaitez. Ici."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Merci pour le conseil ! <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  Hey, "
"I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr ""
"*relève son chapeau de ses yeux et vous regarde d'un air sombre. \"Huh ? Hey, "
"j'essaie de dormir ici. J'étais de garde la nuit."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "John Bailey"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up at you, taking a moment to place your face, then grins broadly.  He "
"looks about the same as when you last saw him, perhaps a little more fit.  "
"\"So, you're still playing on the 'living' team, huh?  Glad to see you're "
"still kicking around.  Always good to run into a familiar face nowadays.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il lève les yeux vers vous, prend un moment pour situer votre visage, puis "
"affiche un large sourire. Il a l'air d'être le même que la dernière fois que "
"vous l'avez vu, peut-être un peu plus en forme. \"Alors, tu joues toujours "
"dans l'équipe des 'vivants', hein ? Je suis content de voir que tu es "
"toujours là. C'est toujours bon de croiser un visage familier de nos jours.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He is "
"a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair graying and his face "
"flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly "
"scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until "
"recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He "
"presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's "
"Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Bonjour John.  Qu'est-ce que vous faites ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi John.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut John. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can "
"do for you, friend?\""
msgstr ""
"*hoche la tête à votre approche, puis sourit et s'étire nonchalamment. \"Je "
"peux faire quelque chose pour vous, mon ami ?\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "Que savez-vous de cet endroit ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "Vous cherchez de la main d'œuvre?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking for a very specific building in the wilderness.  Have you seen it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "Pas pour le moment, mais merci."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Like I said,\" John shrugs.  \"I'm just checking "
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  Might "
"see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is right."
msgstr ""
"et faire un peu de shopping. Ensuite, je reprendrai la route. Je verrai "
"peut-être s'ils ont des travaux à faire avant, si le prix est correct."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "Que cherchez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "En route\" où ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "Quel type de travail recherchez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "Vous avez un moment pour m'apprendre quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a "
"stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't "
"use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a "
"lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to loot "
"a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where they're "
"going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas vraiment. Les stocks de nourriture ne sont pas trop mauvais "
"pour moi et les miens, j'ai trouvé un stock de conserves assez tôt qui nous "
"permettra de tenir un certain temps. Je n'utilise pas d'arme à feu si je peux "
"l'éviter, c'est trop bruyant. J'ai remarqué que ces types semblent garder "
"beaucoup de matériaux de construction, et essayer de prendre un véhicule en "
"ville pour piller une quincaillerie ou un chantier de construction est du "
"suicide, alors je pense que c'est là qu'ils vont prendre mon argent. Je me "
"demande s'ils livrent."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "Quelle est votre prochaine destination ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "Qui est \"vous et les vôtres\" ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "Vous êtes à la recherche d'un emploi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  John listens "
"intently"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then shakes his head.  \"I don't believe I've heard about anything like "
"that, no.  Sorry.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"I can't guarantee it, but I'm pretty sure I've seen "
"something like that.  It was far away, and the weather was bad.  Could've "
"been a church or something, but it didn't look right for that.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh well, thanks John.  I'll go ask around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of "
"them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make "
"it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of "
"them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been "
"through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people though, "
"so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be done, then "
"move on."
msgstr ""
"Vous feriez mieux d'en parler aux gens d'ici. Il semble qu'un certain nombre "
"d'entre eux se soient rassemblés ici au début du <the_cataclysm> et qu'ils "
"aient réussi à s'en sortir. C'est le plus grand groupe de survivants que j'ai "
"trouvé jusqu'à présent, mais la plupart d'entre eux se terrent dans le "
"sous-sol. Je comprends cette envie. Nous avons tous vécu beaucoup trop de "
"choses. Ils disent qu'ils n'ont pas de place pour plus de gens, alors je suis "
"juste ici pour faire quelques courses, voir s'il y a du travail à faire, puis "
"repartir."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "\"Move on\" where?"
msgstr "\"Bouge\" où ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how this "
"trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my hideout "
"and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr ""
"Qui peut le dire, vraiment ? Je n'ai pas vraiment de plan précis. Tout "
"dépendra de la façon dont ce voyage se déroulera. Une fois que mon véhicule "
"sera plein, il faudra que je retourne à ma cachette et que je prenne des "
"nouvelles de tout le monde. Je n'aime pas m'absenter trop longtemps."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "Qui est \"tout le monde\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the "
"really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she "
"told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an "
"unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  "
"Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things "
"were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left "
"on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a "
"lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one "
"thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out "
"for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and "
"scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr ""
"Euh, pour faire court, je suis sorti de ma ville au tout debut des emeutes, "
"avant qu'elles deviennent vraiment des émeutes en fait, dû au fait que ma "
"femme a une très bonne intuition, et au fait que je me suis dit qu'au pire ce "
"serait des vacances au milieu du printemps dans la veille cabine de mon père. "
"Apparemment, faire confiance à ma femme nous à tous sauvés et extirpes des "
"semaines de cauchemar au debut du  Cataclysme. Tout n’était pas rose, mais de "
"ce que j'ai pu entendre d'autre visiteurs, je suis probablement le seul a "
"avoir une famille nucléaire complète dans le nord-est des Etats-Unis, je me "
"sens toujours un peu coupable pour ça, et j'ai comme même probablement perdu "
"la plupart de ma famille étendue. Bref, de fil en aiguille, plusieurs "
"personnes ont décidé de vivre avec nous et font leur part ici. Mon pote "
"Darius par example m'accompagne quand je pars explorer et on surveille les "
"arrières de l'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "Où êtes-vous situés ? Est-ce que je peux vous rejoindre aussi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "Dites-moi ce que vous savez au sujet de Darius."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "Comment saviez-vous que les choses allaient mal tourner ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "Cela semble être une histoire assez improbable."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous me conseiller ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "Que faisiez-vous avant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Changeons de sujet. Qu'avez-vous dit que vous faisiez ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my people, "
"okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some scary "
"fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite your "
"face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's end is "
"a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't really "
"welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you and I "
"get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr ""
"Je vais être franc avec vous, je ne veux pas vous en dire trop sur mon "
"peuple, d'accord ? Tu as l'air d'aller bien, ne te méprends pas, mais j'ai vu "
"des gens effrayants, qui paraissent normaux et qui essaient de t'arracher le "
"visage quand ils te trouvent seul. Chaque personne réagit différemment à la "
"fin du monde. Les choses sont stables avec mon peuple maintenant, mais nous "
"n'accueillons plus vraiment de nouveaux visages. J'aimerais que ce ne soit "
"pas le cas. Peut-être que si toi et moi apprenons à mieux nous connaître un "
"jour, je changerai d'avis."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "L'ensemble de votre histoire semble peu vraisemblable."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he "
"won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, "
"hey?  Anyway.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days "
"without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so "
"he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr ""
"Parlez à Darius si vous voulez en savoir plus sur Darius. C'est un homme bon, "
"et il ne mordra pas - ugh, désolé, c'est une tournure de phrase que nous "
"devrions probablement retirer, hé ? Quoi qu'il en soit. Je ne sais pas si "
"nous aurions passé les premiers jours sans lui. Depuis les émeutes, il est un "
"peu nerveux avec les foules, alors il surveille nos affaires."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going to "
"go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, as "
"much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it out. "
" When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up in the "
"Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a getaway "
"anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get out to the "
"cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It wasn't so much "
"knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck that we trusted "
"our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr ""
"Parfois, je me demande pourquoi d'autres personnes n'ont pas su que les "
"choses allaient mal tourner. Le recul, c'est vingt fois vingt, je suppose. "
"Pour être honnête, même si j'aimerais me féliciter, ce n'est pas moi qui l'ai "
"compris. Lorsque les premières émeutes ont commencé, même si elles se "
"déroulaient dans le Midwest, ma femme a eu un mauvais pressentiment. Nous "
"avions envisagé une escapade de toute façon, et j'avais un peu de temps "
"libre, alors nous avons pris cela comme une excuse pour aller à la cabane et "
"attendre que tout se calme. Et nous y sommes. Ce n'est pas tant que nous "
"savions comment les choses allaient se dérouler, mais plutôt que nous avons "
"fait confiance à notre - *son* - instinct au bon moment et que nous avons eu "
"de la chance."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do "
"gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie "
"hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the "
"unlikely thing.\""
msgstr ""
"*chuckles. \"Heureusement pour moi, ça n'a pas d'importance si tu me crois. "
"Je dois dire que c'est marrant que toi et moi, deux vrais chasseurs de "
"zombies, nous parlions face à face et que tu penses que mon histoire de "
"survie est improbable.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand, "
"but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of "
"help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find "
"for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a "
"lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough "
"as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos "
"out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little things "
"I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't put me in "
"too much danger."
msgstr ""
"Je fais des petits boulots si les gens ont besoin d'aide.  Ce n'est pas du "
"bénévolat, vous comprenez, mais j'essaie de ne pas être injuste non plus.  De "
"nos jours, beaucoup de gens ont besoin d'un peu d'aide, souvent pour de "
"petites choses qu'un pilleur comme moi peut trouver pour eux.  Il est facile "
"pour des gens comme vous et moi de sous-estimer la peur qu'ont beaucoup de "
"gens de retourner à l'extérieur.  La situation est déjà assez grave, mais ce "
"genre de personnes se sont réfugiés lorsque c'était un véritable chaos.  Il y "
"a beaucoup de traumatismes à évacuer.  Quoi qu'il en soit, s'il y a des "
"petites choses que je peux faire pour eux, j'essaie d'aider là où je peux, "
"tant que cela ne me met pas trop en danger."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill "
"count?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air de vous débrouiller pas mal. Combien de zombies avez-vous "
"tués?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "J'ai besoin de quelqu'un comme toi. Tu veux voyager avec moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "Vous semblez en savoir beaucoup sur les sentiments des gens."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez raison. Les gens comme vous et moi sont faits d'une étoffe plus "
"solide."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand "
"everything to them."
msgstr ""
"Les gens devraient apprendre à se débrouiller seuls, et ne pas se contenter "
"de vous demander de tout leur donner."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, "
"doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human "
"though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, "
"especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help it.\""
msgstr ""
"*Rire un peu penaud. \"Il me semble déplaisant de garder une trace de ce "
"genre de choses, n'est-ce pas ? Il touche une série d'encoches sur son "
"<mywp>. \"Mais je suis humain. J'en suis à <npc_val:zkc_john> pour l'instant. "
"Ça me semble beaucoup, surtout que j'essaie d'éviter d'engager l'ennemi si je "
"peux m'en empêcher.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a "
"good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially "
"these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to "
"watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il vous regarde de haut en bas et secoue tristement la tête. \"Darius et moi "
"avons une bonne relation, et une troisième personne serait difficile à "
"justifier, surtout de nos jours. La confiance est difficile à obtenir. Je "
"suis désolé. J'espère que tu as quelqu'un pour surveiller tes arrières, mais "
"ça ne peut pas être moi.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of "
"stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"C'est dommage. Nous ferions une bonne équipe. Les gens comme toi et moi sont "
"plus forts que toi."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "C'est tout à fait vrai. Les gens devraient apprendre à se débrouiller seuls."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, "
"especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  "
"Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time "
"judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr ""
"Oui, je connais un peu ce genre de choses. Difficile de ne pas compatir, "
"surtout quand je sais que je ne suis pas aussi dur que les autres, par pure "
"chance. D'ailleurs, nous sommes si peu nombreux maintenant. A quoi bon perdre "
"son temps à juger les autres pour leur difficulté à supporter la fin du monde "
"?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "On dirait que vous avez un certain passé. Vous voulez en parler ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just say "
"I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr ""
"Pas vraiment, non. Ce sont de vieilles histoires, et il y en a assez. Disons "
"simplement que je ne suis pas étranger à la perte, que ce soit la mienne ou "
"celle des autres."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about "
"thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure, "
"not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe home, "
"too.\""
msgstr ""
"*Un sourcil se lève. \"Je ne sais pas ce qu'il en est.  Vous devriez faire "
"attention à ne pas penser que les gens ne faisant pas les mêmes choix sont "
"inférieurs.  Bien sûr, tout le monde n'est pas fait pour être pilleur, mais "
"les pilleurs apprécient avoir quelque part où revenir.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "C'est de la foutaise. Les gens devraient apprendre à se débrouiller seuls."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be "
"independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than "
"the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into "
"civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're "
"doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr ""
"*Il se frotte la barbe, l'air pensif. \"Je reconnais qu'il est important "
"d'être indépendant, mais n'oublie pas que c'est en travaillant ensemble que "
"nous sommes meilleurs que les morts-vivants. C'est comme ça que nous sommes "
"sortis des arbres et des champs, et que nous sommes entrés dans la "
"civilisation. Quoi qu'il en soit, je ne veux pas vous parler de philosophie. "
"Si vous vous débrouillez bien tout seul, bravo !\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"C'est pour les faibles. Les gens comme vous et moi sont faits d'une étoffe "
"plus solide."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "Je ne sais pas, les zombies semblent travailler ensemble."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best "
"to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and "
"it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr ""
"*chuckles. \"Si on peut appeler ça comme ça, bien sûr. Alors peut-être "
"devrions-nous faire de notre mieux pour être meilleurs que les zombies dans "
"ce domaine. Ça me semble assez raisonnable, et c'est une barre assez basse à "
"franchir.\""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you "
"can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever "
"possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I "
"try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have "
"the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid so "
"we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high "
"ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with "
"spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes "
"instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we can "
"take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are "
"suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to "
"the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and "
"try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that "
"little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, "
"zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a "
"crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can avoid "
"it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  We get a "
"lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, where if "
"there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je suppose. Je ne sais pas si je sais quelque chose que vous ne "
"savez pas, vous semblez pouvoir vous débrouiller tout seul. Je suis arrivé "
"jusqu'ici en ne m'engageant pas chaque fois que c'était possible. Je "
"n'arriverai jamais à tuer tous les zombies. Darius et moi essayons de ne pas "
"nous battre si nous pouvons l'éviter, et si nous ne le pouvons pas, nous "
"essayons de toujours avoir l'avantage. Le nombre, l'armement, le terrain. Les "
"zombies sont maladroits et stupides, alors nous les menons à travers des "
"buissons et des choses qui les font trébucher. Nous prenons les hauteurs et "
"les laissons s'enfoncer dans les échelles comme des idiots pendant que nous "
"leur assénons des coups de lance depuis le haut. Mais surtout, nous essayons "
"de ne pas être vus. Nous utilisons des vélos plutôt que des voitures parce "
"qu'ils ne font pas de bruit et n'ont pas besoin d'essence, et parce que nous "
"pouvons emprunter des sentiers forestiers et éviter les embouteillages. C'est "
"du suicide. Nous essayons d'éviter les villes, et quand nous nous en "
"approchons, nous restons à la périphérie et nous attaquons les maisons "
"isolées. Dans ces dernières, nous restons accroupis et essayons de pénétrer "
"rapidement dans le bâtiment, ou de descendre au sous-sol, afin que les petits "
"bruits ne portent pas beaucoup et que personne de l'extérieur ne puisse nous "
"voir. De plus, les zombies étant des idiots, fermer les stores est une "
"excellente idée. J'ai toujours un pied de biche pour ouvrir les portes et les "
"fenêtres, mais j'essaie de ne pas l'utiliser si je peux l'éviter. Darius peut "
"crocheter les serrures, ce qui est plus lent mais ne fait pas de bruit. Nous "
"obtenons beaucoup plus de résultats en attaquant des stations-service et "
"d'autres sites ruraux, où s'il y a quelques zombies, nous pouvons "
"généralement les faire fuir."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "Qu'en est-il des choses autres que les zombies ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen "
"some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we "
"don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  "
"One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a "
"cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started "
"hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  "
"Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to travel "
"these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we turn around "
"and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't outrun."
msgstr ""
"Oh, bon sang, oui. Le monde est vraiment parti en couille, n'est-ce pas ? "
"J'ai vu des trucs bizarres d'extraterrestres. Notre règle est la suivante : "
"\"Mieux vaut être effrayé que mort\". Si nous ne savons pas ce qu'est une "
"chose et comment la tuer, nous nous en éloignons. Une fois, j'ai vu un globe "
"oculaire enflammé au loin, alors que j'étais en repérage depuis une tour de "
"téléphonie mobile. Il m'a regardé dans les yeux et j'ai commencé à avoir des "
"hallucinations. Darius m'a empêché de tomber de la tour. C'est pour ce genre "
"de choses que je pense qu'il faut être un peu fou pour voyager de nos jours, "
"sauf si on n'a pas le choix. Tout ce que nous ne connaissons pas, nous le "
"tournons et nous pédalons fort. Jusqu'à présent, nous n'avons rien rencontré "
"que nos vélos ne puissent dépasser."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  My "
"dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop quite "
"a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of work, but "
"then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and electrical "
"work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering degree, then "
"decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time doing freelance "
"electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a startup that was "
"designing and programming medical equipment.  I was supposed to be a general "
"technician, but through a weird series of events I wound up in sales, then "
"management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big nest egg from my share "
"stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  That was a dumb move, I "
"was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and started doing on-call "
"teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things like that at a college "
"and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent the rest of my time "
"outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr ""
"C'est une question plus difficile qu'il n'y paraît. J'ai eu une vie bien "
"remplie. Mon père était mécanicien et, quand j'étais jeune, j'aidais souvent "
"à l'atelier. J'ai commencé par penser que j'allais faire ce métier, mais je "
"me suis laissé distraire et j'ai fini par m'intéresser à l'informatique et à "
"l'électricité pendant longtemps. J'ai passé une partie de mon diplôme "
"d'ingénieur électricien, puis j'ai décidé que ce n'était pas pour moi et j'ai "
"abandonné. J'ai passé un peu de temps à faire de l'électricité et de la "
"programmation en free-lance, puis j'ai été recruté par une start-up qui "
"concevait et programmait des équipements médicaux. J'étais censé être un "
"technicien général, mais par une étrange série d'événements, je me suis "
"retrouvé dans la vente, puis dans la gestion. Je détestais la gestion et "
"j'avais accumulé un gros pécule grâce à mes actions, alors j'ai tout plaqué "
"et j'ai essayé de prendre ma retraite jeune. C'était une décision stupide, je "
"m'ennuyais à mourir, alors j'ai terminé mon diplôme et j'ai commencé à "
"enseigner sur demande l'atelier, l'informatique, les mathématiques et "
"d'autres choses du même genre au niveau du collège et du lycée. Je passais le "
"reste de mon temps à l'extérieur, à faire des randonnées, etc."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr "C'est une sacrée vie.  Vous devez avoir des compétences utiles à enseigner."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'd be happy to.  I can't spare a lot of free time, but for a little trade, "
"I'll tell you about whatever I can help with."
msgstr ""
"J'en serais ravi. Je n'ai pas beaucoup de temps libre, mais en échange d'un "
"peu d'argent, je vous parlerai de tout ce que je peux faire pour vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting "
"outside."
msgstr ""
"Désolé, mais c'est tout ce que j'ai le temps de faire pour le moment.  Darius "
"attend dehors."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr "Bien sûr, parlons commerce."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Je m'en souviendrai. Qu'avez-vous dit que vous faisiez ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Merci, je vais y réfléchir.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr "Je pourrais vous prendre au mot, mais pour l'instant, je dois y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, can direct you to the free merchants and nearest FEMA camp.
#. ~ Random NPC, can be recruited away.
#. ~ Random NPC, demands heroin and can accept.
msgid "refugee"
msgstr "réfugié(e)"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please don't hurt us, we're just trying to get to safety."
msgstr "Ne nous faites pas de mal, nous essayons juste de nous mettre à l'abri."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your situation here?"
msgstr "Quelle est votre situation ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I don't mean any harm.  I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I "
"wonder if you've heard anything about it?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne veux pas faire de mal. Je cherche un bâtiment spécifique et étrange. Je "
"me demande si vous en avez entendu parler."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have time for zombie bait like you."
msgstr "Je n'ai pas le temps de m'occuper d'appâts à zombies comme vous."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I don't have any."
msgstr "Non je n'en ai pas."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just trying to find a safe place right now.  I think there's a FEMA "
"camp nearby that should have room for us."
msgstr ""
"Nous essayons juste de trouver un endroit sûr pour le moment. Je pense qu'il "
"y a un camp de la FEMA à proximité qui devrait avoir de la place pour nous."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good luck with that.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Bonne chance avec ça. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The refugee nods "
"along"
msgstr "&Vous décrivez l'entrepôt du mieux que vous pouvez. Le/la réfugié(e) acquiesce"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then frowns.  \"Nope, not ringing any bells, sorry.\""
msgstr ", puis fronce les sourcils. « Non, ça ne me dit rien, désolé(e) »."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just "
"used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found "
"another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been killed, "
"all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all the way "
"to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us there was no "
"room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more room and "
"supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr ""
"Nous nous sommes retrouvés dans la même petite cabane d'évacuation, mais elle "
"était en désordre, avec des préservatifs usagés, des bouteilles cassées et "
"des inscriptions au rouge à lèvres sur les murs. Nous avons trouvé un autre "
"groupe de réfugiés comme nous sur la route, mais ils avaient tous été tués, "
"tout déchiquetés, du sang partout. Nous avons pris leur nourriture et sommes "
"allés jusqu'à un grand centre de réfugiés, mais quelqu'un armé nous a dit "
"qu'il n'y avait pas de place et que nous allions dans un camp de la FEMA. Ils "
"devraient avoir plus de place et de matériel. Rien n'est garanti, mais c'est "
"une chance."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to that FEMA camp?  I want to go there too if it's "
"so great."
msgstr ""
"Pouvez-vous m'indiquer le chemin de ce camp de la FEMA ? Je veux y aller "
"aussi si c'est si génial."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai jamais été dans un centre de réfugiés. Pouvez-vous me dire où il se "
"trouve ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Of course, we're all in this together.  Let me mark that on your map."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, nous sommes tous dans le même bateau. Permettez-moi de l'indiquer "
"sur votre carte."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the information.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci pour l'information. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Things must be better at the camp…"
msgstr "Les choses doivent aller mieux au camp…"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "We're all in this together, looking forward to meeting you there."
msgstr "Nous sommes tous dans le même bateau, et nous avons hâte de vous y rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Everything is going to be all right."
msgstr "Tout va bien se passer."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "No worries friend, good luck to you."
msgstr "Pas de souci mon ami, bonne chance à toi."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "The hard part is getting there."
msgstr "Le plus difficile, c'est d'y arriver."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Any progress on getting to the camp?"
msgstr "Des progrès ont-ils été réalisés en ce qui concerne l'accès au camp ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Well, success I guess."
msgstr "Eh bien, je pense que c'est une réussite."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Such a disappointment…"
msgstr "Une vraie déception…"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  I wouldn't bet they'll treat you any "
"differently than us though.  You might try and bring something to trade, they "
"like that."
msgstr ""
"Tenez, je vais l'indiquer sur votre carte. Je ne parierais pas qu'ils vous "
"traiteront différemment de nous. Vous pourriez essayer d'apporter quelque "
"chose à échanger, ils aiment ça."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me directions to where you're going too?  I love cartography."
msgstr " Pouvez-vous aussi m'indiquer où vous allez ? J'adore la cartographie."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Looking good there.  I like your whole setup.  What's your story?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air en forme. J'aime bien l'ensemble de votre installation. "
"Quelle est votre histoire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice.  Good to see you again.  What do you want from me?"
msgstr "C'est bien. C'est bon de vous revoir. Qu'est-ce que tu veux de moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You should come with me instead."
msgstr "Tu devrais plutôt venir avec moi."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You should definitely come with me instead."
msgstr "Tu devrais vraiment venir avec moi."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing, just saying hi."
msgstr "Rien, je ne fais que dire bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So you're not attached right now?"
msgstr "Vous n'êtes donc pas attaché pour l'instant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why, where were you before?"
msgstr "Pourquoi, où étiez-vous avant?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not interested.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Pas intéressé(e). <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, I'm not really with them.  We just got stuck together in the same messed "
"up evacuation place.  This one guy was really nice, but they wouldn't let us "
"stay.  They got there first so they told us we needed to find our own place, "
"but if we got anything they wanted they'd trade some of the stuff they have.  "
"I tried to talk them into helping but they were so cold to me."
msgstr ""
"Non, je ne suis pas vraiment avec eux. On s'est juste retrouvés coincés "
"ensemble dans le même lieu d'évacuation pourri. Ce type était vraiment sympa, "
"mais ils ne voulaient pas nous laisser rester. Ils sont arrivés les premiers, "
"alors ils nous ont dit que nous devions trouver notre propre endroit, mais "
"que si nous obtenions quelque chose qu'ils voulaient, ils échangeraient "
"certaines de leurs affaires. J'ai essayé de les convaincre de nous aider, "
"mais ils ont été très froids."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I guess it's hard all over.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Oui, j'imagine que c'est difficile partout. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is the beginning of a beautiful thing.  I'm with you."
msgstr "C'est le début d'une belle chose. Je suis avec vous."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr "Oui!"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Actually, I think I'm on the right track here, but you might have some luck "
"finding a little something something back at the Free Merchant base.  They "
"seemed pretty desperate."
msgstr ""
"En fait, je pense que je suis sur la bonne voie, mais vous pourriez avoir de "
"la chance de trouver un petit quelque chose à la base des marchands libres. "
"Ils ont l'air assez désespérés."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Of course.  How do I get there?"
msgstr "Bien entendu.  Comment puis-je m'y rendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes.  I'll be on my way then."
msgstr "Oui, j'y vais."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey man.  Do you have any heroin?  I'm in a bit of a bind."
msgstr "Hé, mec. Tu as de l'héroïne ? Je suis un peu dans le pétrin."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never, that heroin is for me and me alone."
msgstr "Jamais, cette héroïne est pour moi et moi seule."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think you might need it even more than me.  Here you go."
msgstr "Je pense que tu en as encore plus besoin que moi. Voilà, c'est parti."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I love you."
msgstr "Je vous adore."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, uh, thanks.  I guess."
msgstr "Oh, hum, merci.  Je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No thank you."
msgstr "Non merci."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/missiondef_free_merchants.json
#: data/mods/classic_zombies/missiondef.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Reach Refugee Center"
msgstr "Atteignez le Centre de Réfugiés"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Full"
msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr "Ce mendiant a l'air d'avoir eu quelque chose à manger récemment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Reena Sandhu"
msgstr "Reena Sandhu"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Teacher"
msgstr "Institutrice"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ All the beggars have been camping inside the evac shelter because they're
#. too weak and unskilled to make it on their own.
#. ~ This is the only beggar with some skills, sort of the leader.
msgid "Beggar"
msgstr "Mendiant"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, any luck with convincing the others to come on your crazy adventure yet?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez réussi à convaincre les autres de vous suivre dans votre aventure "
"folle?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you again.  I really appreciate the food."
msgstr "Merci encore. J'apprécie vraiment la nourriture."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food.  Aren't you their sheriff?  Can't you help me?"
msgstr ""
"S'il vous plaît, aidez-moi. J'ai besoin de nourriture. N'êtes-vous pas leur "
"shérif ? Vous ne pouvez pas m'aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food."
msgstr "Aidez-moi, s'il vous plaît. J'ai besoin de nourriture."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've talked to the others, and they're all willing to come.  So, you joining "
"us?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai parlé aux autres et ils sont tous prêts à venir. Alors, vous vous "
"joignez à nous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, here, I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "J'ai peut-être de la nourriture pour vous. Laissez-moi vérifier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Get away from me."
msgstr "Éloignez-vous de moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They won't let me in.  They say they're too full.  I'm allowed to camp out "
"here as long as I keep it clean and don't make a fuss"
msgstr ""
"Ils ne me laissent pas entrer. Ils disent qu'ils sont trop pleins. J'ai le "
"droit de camper ici tant que je reste propre et que je ne fais pas d'histoires"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but I'm reduced to begging to survive."
msgstr ", mais j'en suis réduit(e) à faire la manche pour survivre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but I'm so hungry."
msgstr ", mais j'ai tellement faim."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you scavenge your own food?"
msgstr "Pourquoi est-ce que vous n'essayez pas de trouver votre propre nourriture?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "J'ai peut être quelque chose à manger pour vous. Laissez-moi chercher."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got some more food, if you want it."
msgstr "J'ai un peu plus de nourriture, si vous en voulez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr "Je suis désolé, je ne peux pas vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you so much."
msgstr "Merci tellement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I ask you something else first?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux vous demander autre chose d'abord?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry, I was wrong.  I can't help you."
msgstr "Je suis désolé, j'avais tort, je ne peux pas vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Here, you can have this <topic_item>."
msgstr "Voila, vous pouvez avoir ce <topic_item>."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."
msgstr "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Pas de problème. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Where else?  I can't fight those things out there.  I'm in terrible physical "
"condition, don't have any useful skills, and I'm terrified of <zombies> and "
"violence.  How am I supposed to find a safe place?"
msgstr ""
"Où d'autre ? Je ne peux pas me battre contre ces choses-là. Je suis en très "
"mauvaise condition physique, je n'ai aucune compétence utile et je suis "
"terrifié par les <zombies> et la violence. Comment puis-je trouver un endroit "
"sûr ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better than "
"living here."
msgstr ""
"Viens avec moi. Tu n'es peut-être pas un grand aventurier, mais c'est mieux "
"que de vivre ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  You could come there.  There aren't "
"many people left, we could use anyone regardless of skills."
msgstr ""
"J'ai mon propre camp, loin d'ici. Vous pourriez y venir. Il ne reste plus "
"beaucoup de monde, nous avons besoin de tout le monde, quelles que soient les "
"compétences."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, people "
"who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances begging for "
"scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make room for me, "
"thanks."
msgstr ""
"Là-bas ? C'est du suicide ! Les gens qui sortent ne reviennent pas, les gens "
"qui tiennent le coup... pas comme moi. Je préfère tenter ma chance en "
"mendiant des miettes et en attendant que quelqu'un au centre meure pour me "
"faire de la place, merci."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe you can't scavenge, but we "
"can use any warm bodies that can lift a tool.  You'd be safer and better fed "
"there."
msgstr ""
"J'ai mon propre camp, loin d'ici. Vous ne pouvez peut-être pas faire les "
"poubelles, mais nous pouvons utiliser tous les corps chauds qui peuvent "
"soulever un outil. Vous serez plus en sécurité et mieux nourris là-bas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a high school math teacher.  It was a good job, I loved it.  Funny "
"enough, it's not super applicable after the end of the world.  I mean, at "
"some point people are going to need a teacher again, but right now they just "
"want food, shelter, and clothing."
msgstr ""
"J'étais professeur de mathématiques dans un lycée. C'était un bon travail, "
"j'aimais ça. C'est amusant, mais ce n'est pas vraiment applicable après la "
"fin du monde. Je veux dire qu'à un moment donné, les gens auront à nouveau "
"besoin d'un professeur, mais pour l'instant, ils veulent juste de la "
"nourriture, un toit et des vêtements."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe they can't use your skills "
"here, but I could."
msgstr ""
"J'ai mon propre camp, loin d'ici. Peut-être qu'ils ne peuvent pas utiliser "
"vos compétences ici, mais je pourrais le faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a kind offer of you, but I think I'd rather take my chances here than "
"risking it out there again.  I remember <the_cataclysm>, I'm not in any hurry "
"to face that again."
msgstr ""
"C'est gentil de votre part, mais je crois que je préfère tenter ma chance ici "
"plutôt que de me risquer à nouveau là-bas. Je me souviens de <the_cataclysm>, "
"je ne suis pas pressé d'y faire face à nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's quite the offer, but I don't think I'd survive the trip.  I don't "
"think you realize how useless I am in this world."
msgstr ""
"C'est une belle offre, mais je ne pense pas que je survivrais au voyage. Je "
"ne pense pas que tu réalises à quel point je suis inutile dans ce monde."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm sorry, I'm too hungry to make a big decision like that."
msgstr "Je suis désolée, j'ai trop faim pour prendre une décision aussi importante."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can keep you safe.  I'll take you there myself."
msgstr "Je peux vous mettre en sécurité. Je t'y emmènerai moi-même."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really appreciate everything you've done for me, but I don't think you get "
"it.  I can't go out there.  I will die.  I know it's horrible camping out "
"here, but I just can't face that nightmare again."
msgstr ""
"J’apprécie vraiment tout ce que vous avez fait pour moi, mais je ne suis pas "
"sur que vous comprenez bien, je n'arriverais jamais à survivre dehors. C'est "
"une situation horrible de crever de faim ici, mais je ne peux pas survivre le "
"cauchemar dehors."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I hope you'll reconsider eventually.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "J'espère que vous y repenserez à un moment.  <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "OK.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, I'll talk to them too."
msgstr "Ok, je vais essayer de les convaincre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right!  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Très bien ! <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Schizophrenic beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Dino Dave"
msgstr "Dino Dave"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We've done it!  We've solved the list!"
msgstr "Nous avons réussi ! Nous avons résolu la liste !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How's things with you?  My cardboard collection is getting quite impressive."
msgstr ""
"Comment ça se passe chez vous ? Ma collection de cartons devient assez "
"impressionnante."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Have I told you about cardboard, friend?  Do you have any?"
msgstr "T'ai-je parlé du carton, mon ami ? En as-tu ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that shopping list of yours…"
msgstr "Au sujet de votre liste de shopping…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr "Je peux faire quelque chose pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you going to do with all that cardboard now?"
msgstr "Qu'allez-vous faire avec tout ce carton maintenant?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We've done it, Dave!  Smokes says you can build yourself a house up on the "
"roof if you want.  You've got to keep it nice and clean, and help out the "
"people down here by looking out for zombies, but you can still use the "
"washrooms and things downstairs when you need to.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""
"On l'a fait, Dave ! Smokes dit que tu peux te construire une maison sur le "
"toit si tu veux. Tu devras la garder propre et bien entretenue, et aider les "
"gens en bas en surveillant les zombies, mais tu pourras toujours utiliser les "
"toilettes et tout ce qu'il y a en bas quand tu en auras besoin. Qu'est-ce que "
"tu en dis ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cardboard?"
msgstr "Du carton?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you sitting out here?"
msgstr "Pourquoi es-tu assis ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you seriously wearing a dinosaur costume?"
msgstr "Est-ce que vous êtes sérieusement en train de porter un costume de dinosaure?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you need something to eat?"
msgstr "Vous voulez quelque chose à manger?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh nice.  Crunchings and munchings.  That's a cool, a cool thing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can tell when it has stuff in it, it's got a sandy texture.  But this "
"doesn't.  Thanks again."
msgstr ""
"Je peux dire que lorsqu'il contient des substances, il a une texture "
"sablonneuse. Mais ce n'est pas le cas. Merci encore."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Pas de problème. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm building a house out of cardboard.  The sandman doesn't want me to, but I "
"told him to go fuck himself."
msgstr ""
"Je construis une maison en carton. Le marchand de sable ne veut pas, mais je "
"lui ai dit d'aller se faire foutre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why cardboard?"
msgstr "Pourquoi du carton?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The sandman?"
msgstr "Le marchand de sable?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like me to give you some cardboard?"
msgstr "Voulez-vous que je vous donne du carton?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me "
"safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it "
"hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Il y en a tellement maintenant, et les zombies en ont peur. Ça m'a permis de "
"rester en sécurité jusqu'à présent. Les rayons bêta proviennent du point "
"central du zombie, ils frappent donc le carton et ne peuvent pas pénétrer. La "
"réflexion peut arrêter tout dommage supplémentaire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Kind of a question's that?  Yeah man, you got cardboard, I got a whole… a "
"whole shopping list.  Got it here."
msgstr ""
"C'est une question?  Ouais mec, t'as du carton, j'ai toute une… toute une "
"liste de courses.  Je l'ai là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's next on the list?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qu'il y a sur la liste après ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you don't know who he is, I definitely can't tell you.  He talks to "
"everyone, if you didn't hear him that means you can't be trusted, except to "
"help me out."
msgstr ""
"Si vous ne savez pas qui il est, je ne peux certainement pas vous le dire. Il "
"parle à tout le monde, si tu ne l'as pas entendu, c'est qu'on ne peut pas te "
"faire confiance, sauf pour m'aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…<done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "…<done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"These cowards are afraid of me.  They won't let me into their base.  I'm "
"going to build my new house and I won't let them in."
msgstr ""
"Ces lâches ont peur de moi. Ils ne me laisseront pas entrer dans leur base. "
"Je vais construire ma nouvelle maison et je ne les laisserai pas entrer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You said you were building a house?"
msgstr "Vous disiez que vous étiez en train de construire une maison?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I… I can see you wearing it.  Why are you wearing that?"
msgstr "Je… Je vous vois le porter.  Pourquoi portez-vous ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was that about cardboard?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que c'est que cette histoire de carton ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You ask me what I can see, but I don't tell you what you see.  Sometimes we "
"have shields up, to protect ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Vous me demandez ce que je vois, mais je ne vous dis pas ce que vous voyez. "
"Parfois, nous levons des boucliers pour nous protéger."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well… I had it all pretty together, "
msgstr "C'est que… Je me débrouillais plutôt pas mal,"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "but the others have left, and "
msgstr "mais les autres sont partis"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "and I feel bad with all the help you've given me already, but "
msgstr "et je me sens coupable dû à toute l'aide que vous m'avez déjà donnée, mais"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"now the masters won't let me build my sanctuary.  I know I can't build it in "
"here, they wouldn't allow it.  They won't listen to me when I ask for a safe "
"place.  They just want me to disappear, like the others.  Can you help me "
"figure them out?"
msgstr ""
"maintenant les maîtres ne veulent pas me laisser construire mon sanctuaire. "
"Je sais que je ne peux pas le construire ici, ils ne me laisserait pas le "
"faire, mais ils ne veulent pas m'écouter lorsque je leur demande un endroit "
"sûr. Ils veulent juste que je disparaissent, comme les autres. Pouvez-vous "
"m'aider à leur faire entendre raison?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why don't you leave this place?  Come with me, I could use some help out "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Qu'est-ce que ça vous dit de partir d'ici? Venez avec moi, je pourrais "
"utiliser quelqu'un comme vous à l'extérieur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a "
"place to go."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr Dave. Une dernière faveur, je pense que je peux convaincre Smokes de "
"vous trouver un endroit où aller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to think on that, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "Je vais devoir y réfléchir, Dave, j'en ai déjà fait beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  I can hardly believe it!  This will be a "
"nicer house than I had before everything went funny.  I can watch out, I'm "
"happy to do that.  And it'll be nice to still have a bathroom!  Come see me "
"there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"Le toit ! Si haut ! Si haut ! J'ai du mal à y croire ! Ce sera une plus belle "
"maison que celle que j'avais avant que tout ne devienne bizarre. Je peux "
"faire attention, je suis heureux de le faire. Et ce sera bien d'avoir encore "
"une salle de bains ! Viens me voir, mon ami. Je ne te décevrai pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see you on the rooftop.  Good luck, Dave."
msgstr "Je vous verrais sur le toit. Bonne chance Dave."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No!  I just got everything together.  I am not leaving, not now.  "
"Everything's finally coming together!"
msgstr ""
"Non ! Je viens de tout rassembler. Je ne pars pas, pas maintenant. Tout se "
"met enfin en place !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about "
"finding you a place to go."
msgstr ""
"Bon, d'accord, Dave. Une dernière faveur, je pense que je peux parler à "
"Smokes pour te trouver un endroit où aller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to think on it, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "Je dois y réfléchir Dave, j'ai déjà fait beaucoup pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Ramenez 40 petites boîtes en carton"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em."
msgstr ""
"Il faut commencer petit, n'est-ce pas ? Des petits pour garder les petites "
"choses en sécurité. Je pourrais les utiliser."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em.  I need a bunch of 'em.  Little ones, you know?  Can you bring "
"me like… like… forty?"
msgstr ""
"Il faut commencer petit, n'est-ce pas ? Des petits pour garder les petites "
"choses en sécurité. Je pourrais les utiliser. J'en ai besoin d'un tas. Des "
"petits, tu sais ? Tu peux m'en apporter une quarantaine ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much my friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "Merci beaucoup, mon ami. Tu ne le regretteras pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "I didn't think so."
msgstr "Je ne crois pas que ce soit le cas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Watch out, he's looking for it too."
msgstr "Attention, il la cherche aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid "Got the little ones yet?"
msgstr "Vous avez déjà des enfants ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid "Oh this is so great, so great!"
msgstr "Oh, c'est vraiment génial, vraiment génial !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Oh, that's too bad.  Guess they're eating it all."
msgstr "Oh, c'est dommage. Je suppose qu'ils mangent tout."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgstr "Trouvez un rouleau de ruban adhésif (200 charges)"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side."
msgstr ""
"Ceux-ci sont bons, bons. Ils ont besoin de quelque chose pour, vous savez, "
"les lier ensemble. Les entourer, le côté clair, le côté obscur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side.  Bring me the Force!"
msgstr ""
"Ceux-ci sont bons, bons. Ils ont besoin de quelque chose pour, vous savez, "
"les lier ensemble. Entourez-les, côté lumineux, côté obscur. Apportez-moi la "
"Force !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid "It's all around us… but did you get it in a crude matter form?"
msgstr ""
"Elle est partout autour de nous… mais l'avez-vous reçue sous forme de matière "
"brute?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Amenez 10 boîtes en carton"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well."
msgstr ""
"Dix plus gros maintenant, s'il vous plaît. La liste ne ment pas. Vous avez "
"bien travaillé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well.  I "
"got a little more on the list, but we're more than half there."
msgstr ""
"Dix plus gros maintenant, s'il vous plaît. La liste ne ment pas. Vous avez "
"bien travaillé. J'en ai un peu plus sur la liste, mais nous en sommes à plus "
"de la moitié."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Any luck?  Bigger ones?"
msgstr "Des trouvailles?  Des plus grosses boîtes?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "I'm so happy now!"
msgstr "Je suis si heureux maintenant!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgstr "Trouvez 10 grandes feuilles de plastique"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I "
"guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger."
msgstr ""
"Si je peux l'installer ici, je n'en aurai pas besoin, mais ils pourraient me "
"chasser, alors je suppose que j'ai besoin de plastique, juste au cas où. Je "
"n'aime pas ça, le marchand de sable peut sentir à travers le plastique, mais "
"je pense que le carton est plus fort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I "
"guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger.  Please bring "
"me some plastic sheets."
msgstr ""
"Si je peux l'installer ici, je n'en aurai pas besoin, mais ils pourraient me "
"chasser, alors je suppose que j'ai besoin de plastique, juste au cas où. Je "
"n'aime pas ça, le marchand de sable peut sentir à travers le plastique, mais "
"je pense que le carton est plus fort. S'il vous plaît, apportez-moi des "
"feuilles de plastique."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "We're almost there, now."
msgstr "Nous y sommes presque."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "They keep a lot of this stuff in hardware stores and lumber yards."
msgstr ""
"Les quincailleries et les parcs à bois conservent une grande partie de ces "
"produits."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"I really feel bad sending you on this one, it's dangerous.  Have you found "
"anything?"
msgstr ""
"Je me sens vraiment mal de vous envoyer sur ce terrain, c'est dangereux. "
"Avez-vous trouvé quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "Nice, this will do perfectly!"
msgstr "Joli, cela fera parfaitement l'affaire !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "Oh, that's too bad."
msgstr "Oh… c'est bien dommage.  "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Trouvez 5 grandes boîtes en carton"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts "
"myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five "
"more really big cardboard boxes?"
msgstr ""
"C'est la dernière chose dont j'ai besoin de votre part. J'ai récupéré les "
"autres pièces moi-même, c'est plus facile avec plus de carton. Pouvez-vous "
"m'apporter cinq autres très grands cartons ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts "
"myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five "
"more really big cardboard boxes?  Five more cardboard boxes, as big as it "
"gets.  I have a few already stored up, that should be all I need."
msgstr ""
"C'est la dernière chose dont j'ai besoin de votre part. J'ai récupéré les "
"autres pièces moi-même, c'est plus facile avec plus de carton. Pouvez-vous "
"m'apporter cinq autres très gros cartons ? Cinq cartons de plus, aussi grands "
"que possible. J'en ai déjà quelques-unes en réserve, ça devrait suffire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Yes!  The home stretch!"
msgstr "Oui!  La dernière ligne droite!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Oh man, but we're so close!"
msgstr "Oh mec, mais nous sommes si proches !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Try looking in cargo storage areas."
msgstr "Essayez de regarder dans les espaces de stockage de la cargaison."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Did you bring me those last few boxes?"
msgstr "Tu m'as apporté les dernières boîtes ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Brilliant!  You're a true hero.  I'll see if I can find a place to set these "
"up now."
msgstr ""
"Brillant ! Vous êtes un véritable héros. Je vais voir si je peux trouver un "
"endroit pour les installer maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "No!  Oh god, no, this can't be happening…"
msgstr "Non!  Oh mon Dieu, non, ça ne peut pas arriver…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
msgstr "Discutez avec Smokes pour trouver un endroit ou Dave pourrait rester."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me."
msgstr ""
"Je l'ai, j'ai tout, mais je ne trouve pas d'endroit où le mettre. Allez-vous "
"demander aux maîtres ? Peut-être ? J'ai essayé, mais ils m'ignorent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me.  I just need a place to "
"put it all, a place I can be safe, and not make anyone upset."
msgstr ""
"Je l'ai, j'ai tout, mais je ne trouve pas d'endroit où le mettre. Allez-vous "
"demander aux maîtres ? Peut-être ? J'ai essayé, mais ils m'ignorent. J'ai "
"juste besoin d'un endroit où mettre tout ça, un endroit où je peux être en "
"sécurité et où je ne dérange personne."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Thank you!  I'm sorry, I thought we were done, but we can do this!"
msgstr ""
"Merci ! Je suis désolée, je pensais que c'était fini, mais nous pouvons le "
"faire !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Maybe somewhere they can't see me?  Where I can just be me?"
msgstr ""
"Peut-être dans un endroit où ils ne peuvent pas me voir ? Où je peux juste "
"être moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Did you ask the masters?"
msgstr "Avez-vous demandé aux maîtres ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not "
"disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"Le toit ! Si haut ! Si haut ! Viens me voir là-bas, mon ami. Je ne vous "
"décevrai pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/missiondef.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Power Storage CBM"
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr "Je ne comprends pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "insulted_luo"
msgid "Insulted"
msgstr "Insulté(e)"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Insulted"
msgid "Oh, you went there."
msgstr "Oh, vous y êtes allé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Luo Meizhen"
msgstr "Luo Meizhen"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Mycologist"
msgstr "Mycologue"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yo.  Anyone else keen on moving from this bus stop to your tent city?"
msgstr ""
"Yo. Quelqu'un d'autre a envie de quitter cet arrêt de bus pour rejoindre son "
"village de tentes ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey there.  Good to see you again."
msgstr "Bonjour à tous. C'est un plaisir de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Careful, I'm getting hangry again and am not totally responsible for my own "
"actions."
msgstr ""
"Attention, j'ai de nouveau la fringale et je ne suis pas totalement "
"responsable de mes actes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't bother with these assholes."
msgstr "Ne vous embêtez pas avec ces connards."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "J'ai peut être quelque chose à manger pour vous. Vous avez faim?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're cool.  Sorry for insulting you earlier."
msgstr "Oublions tout. Désolé de vous avoir insulté(e) tout à l'heure."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I found a sample of alien fungus for you."
msgstr "J'ai trouvé un échantillon de champignon extraterrestre pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok… see ya."
msgstr "Ok… à plus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Actually yeah, I'm always hungry these days.  I don't like taking handouts, "
"but I wouldn't say no."
msgstr ""
"En fait, oui, j'ai toujours faim ces jours-ci. Je n'aime pas l'assistanat, "
"mais je ne dirais pas non."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks, I really appreciate this."
msgstr "Merci, j'apprécie vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "They're 'too full'.  Won't share fuck-all."
msgstr "Ils sont \"trop pleins\". Ils ne veulent rien partager."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you living here then?"
msgstr "Alors, pourquoi vivez-vous ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, they might not share, but I can.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "Bon, ils ne veulent pas partager, mais je peux. Vous avez faim?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even without them helping, it's the safest place to squat.  As long as we "
"keep it clean up here and don't cause sanitation problems, they don't mind us "
"sitting around the entryway.  So kind and generous of them, to let us sit "
"here and slowly starve."
msgstr ""
"Même sans leur aide, c'est l'endroit le plus sûr pour squatter. Tant que nous "
"restons propres et que nous ne causons pas de problèmes sanitaires, ils ne "
"voient pas d'inconvénient à ce que nous nous asseyions à l'entrée. C'est "
"tellement gentil et généreux de leur part de nous laisser nous asseoir ici et "
"de nous laisser mourir de faim."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, same old story at first.  I got evacuated on to the local concentration "
"center, then picked up on a repurposed school bus and dragged out here.  Then "
"the chick processing me to get in saw my face and Chinese name and "
"conveniently 'lost' my paperwork.  I was sent out here to wait for further "
"processing, while I watched busloads of people get processed and taken in.  "
"By the time they 'found' it, the place was full up, wouldn't ya know it.  Now "
"I'm stuck out here and they won't consider letting me in."
msgstr ""
"Au début, c'était la même histoire. J'ai été évacué vers le centre de "
"concentration local, puis embarqué dans un bus scolaire réaménagé et traîné "
"jusqu'ici. Ensuite, la fille qui s'occupait de mon admission a vu mon visage "
"et mon nom chinois et a commodément \"perdu\" mes papiers. On m'a envoyé ici "
"pour attendre la suite du processus, tout en regardant des bus remplis de "
"gens se faire enregistrer et emmener. Le temps qu'ils \"retrouvent\" mes "
"papiers, l'endroit était plein, et vous ne vous en doutez pas. Maintenant, je "
"suis coincé ici et ils ne veulent pas me laisser entrer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think you were treated like that because of your race?"
msgstr "Vous pensez que vous avez été traité de la sorte à cause de votre race ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does that mean you were part of that back room evacuation I heard about?"
msgstr ""
"Cela signifie-t-il que vous avez participé à l'évacuation des locaux dont "
"j'ai entendu parler ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why stay out here then?"
msgstr "Pourquoi rester ici alors ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  No paperwork required.  Want to "
"come?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai un camp à moi loin d'ici. Pas de paperasse requise pour être admis. Vous "
"voulez venir?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, that was a hell of a shitstorm.  We were waiting back there for "
"'processing' for hours and hours, with the sick and wounded.  One guy died, "
"we all thought he was sleeping until he got back up.  That started a panic, "
"gunshots in a closed area, that kind of stuff.  In just a few minutes, a "
"bunch more people were dead.  Then the assholes called it an 'outbreak' and "
"tried to barricade us in… took us way too long to convince the panicking "
"guards that we were alive and needed to get out.  I'll give the one guy "
"credit, Sean: when he found out they'd locked living people in with zombies, "
"he came in himself, as some of the newly dead were starting to get back up, "
"and he held them off for us to escape.  That… that was probably the only "
"actual good thing I've seen since before the end of the world: he owned his "
"error and he put himself in harm's way to make up for it.  Massive respect to "
"that guy.  So, of course, he's a zombie now.  Fuck, thanks for reminding me "
"of all that sunny fun."
msgstr ""
"Oh oui, c'était une sacrée tempête de merde. Nous avons attendu des heures et "
"des heures à l'arrière pour le \"traitement\", avec les malades et les "
"blessés. Un homme est mort, nous pensions tous qu'il dormait jusqu'à ce qu'il "
"se relève. Cela a déclenché une panique, des coups de feu dans une zone "
"fermée, ce genre de choses. En l'espace de quelques minutes, d'autres "
"personnes sont mortes. Il nous a fallu beaucoup trop de temps pour convaincre "
"les gardes paniqués que nous étions vivants et que nous devions sortir. Je "
"reconnais le mérite d'un type, Sean : quand il a découvert qu'ils avaient "
"enfermé des personnes vivantes avec des zombies, il est entré lui-même, alors "
"que certains des nouveaux morts commençaient à se relever, et il les a "
"retenus pour nous permettre de nous échapper. C'est probablement la seule "
"bonne chose que j'ai vue depuis avant la fin du monde : il a assumé son "
"erreur et s'est mis en danger pour la réparer. J'ai beaucoup de respect pour "
"ce type. Alors, bien sûr, c'est un zombie maintenant. Putain, merci de me "
"rappeler tout ce plaisir ensoleillé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up. What were you saying?"
msgstr "Désolé de l'avoir évoqué. Que disiez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure.  My grandparents were from China.  That means I'm obviously personally "
"responsible for all this.  Do you think there's some other reason they let "
"hundreds of other educated people in and I'm sitting out here?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr. Mes grands-parents venaient de Chine. Cela signifie que je suis "
"personnellement responsable de tout cela. Pensez-vous qu'il y ait une autre "
"raison pour laquelle ils ont laissé entrer des centaines d'autres personnes "
"instruites et que je reste assis ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't care if you're Chinese.  You can travel with me if you want."
msgstr "Je me fiche que vous soyez chinois. Tu peux voyager avec moi si tu veux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I mean, racism could definitely be a part of it… but you are visibly in poor "
"shape.  They need strong survivor material."
msgstr ""
"Je veux dire, le racisme pourrait certainement en faire partie… mais vous "
"êtes visiblement en mauvais état.  Ils ont besoin de survivants solides."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's awful kind of you, but look at me.  I'm not traveling material, I've "
"managed to stay fifty pounds overweight on a diet of pine nuts and wilted "
"rhubarb, and I scream and shake uncontrollably at the sight of blood."
msgstr ""
"C'est très gentil de votre part, mais regardez-moi. Je n'ai pas l'étoffe "
"d'une voyageuse, j'ai réussi à conserver un surpoids de quinze kilos en me "
"nourrissant de pignons de pin et de rhubarbe flétrie, et je hurle et tremble "
"de façon incontrôlable à la vue du sang."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It'd be temporary.  I have a base set up.  There are only a few of us "
"survivors left, we need to work together"
msgstr ""
"Ce serait temporaire. J'ai installé une base. Il ne reste que quelques "
"survivants, nous devons travailler ensemble."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, yeah, that's a bit of a problem.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Ok, ouais, c'est un peu un problème. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It may not be much, but we've got a little community.  We can't live like "
"this forever, but we're safer than out there, and we look out for each other. "
" One way or another we'll shake things out to something better."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est peut-être pas grand-chose, mais nous avons une petite communauté. "
"Nous ne pourrons pas vivre éternellement comme ça, mais nous sommes plus en "
"sécurité qu'ailleurs et nous veillons les uns sur les autres. D'une manière "
"ou d'une autre, nous parviendrons à améliorer les choses."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You sound more optimistic than usual."
msgstr "Vous avez l'air plus optimiste que d'habitude."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, about that doctorate of yours…"
msgstr "Au sujet de votre doctorat…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Don't get me wrong, I hate this place and this situation, and especially the "
"selfish racist fucks that landed me here… but these other losers that landed "
"out here with me?  I like them.  We might be miserable, but we're miserable "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Ne vous méprenez pas, je déteste cet endroit et cette situation, et surtout "
"les putains de racistes égoïstes qui m'ont fait atterrir ici... mais ces "
"autres losers qui ont atterri ici avec moi ? Je les aime bien. On est "
"peut-être malheureux, mais on est malheureux ensemble."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks for saying it.  So, what brings you around?"
msgstr "Merci de l'avoir dit. Alors, qu'est-ce qui vous amène ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just wanted to get square.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Tempting offer, but I don't know how much I trust a random stranger offering "
"me a place to live.  Call me crazy."
msgstr ""
"Offre tentante, mais je ne sais pas si je fais confiance à un inconnu qui me "
"propose un logement. Traitez-moi de fou."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, come on.  I'm not a random stranger anymore, I brought you that crazy "
"mushroom didn't I?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, allez, je ne suis plus un inconnu. Je ne suis plus un inconnu, je t'ai "
"apporté ce champignon fou, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What better choice do you have?  It's not like it would be just you and me, "
"the others out here can come too."
msgstr ""
"Quel meilleur choix avez-vous ? Ce n'est pas comme s'il n'y avait que toi et "
"moi, les autres peuvent venir aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Like I said, sorry, it's just not happening.  It's not that I don't trust "
"you, it's just that I don't really trust you."
msgstr ""
"Like I said, sorry, it's just not happening. It's not that I don't trust you, "
"it's just that I don't really trust you."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aw damn, I was worried you'd say that.  Okay, listen: you've got yourself a "
"deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've gotta get me hooked up with a "
"microscope as soon as you can.  This could be the beginning of something "
"really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying that I'm not coming unless "
"you can find a place for my friends here in your base.  I'm sure you "
"anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It should be easy, "
"they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr ""
"Bon sang, j'avais peur que tu dises ça. Ok, écoutez : vous avez un marché. Je "
"viendrai à ta base, mais tu dois me brancher sur un microscope dès que "
"possible. Ça pourrait être le début de quelque chose de vraiment cool. Oh, et "
"il va sans dire que je ne viendrai pas si vous ne trouvez pas de place pour "
"mes amis dans votre base. Je suis sûr que vous l'avez prévu. Parlez-leur d'y "
"aller et je suis partant. Ça devrait être facile, c'est une bande d'idiots au "
"grand cœur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, before <the_cataclysm> ended I was working at a university bookstore.  "
"I know a little bit about a lot of things, I guess you could say.  I kinda "
"loved the job, to be honest."
msgstr ""
"Avant la fin du <the_cataclysm>, je travaillais dans une librairie "
"universitaire. Je m'y connais un peu en beaucoup de choses, on peut dire ça "
"comme ça. Pour être honnête, j'aimais bien ce travail."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What had you working at the university bookstore in the first place?  Are you "
"an academic yourself?"
msgstr ""
"Qu'est-ce qui vous a poussé à travailler à la librairie de l'université ? "
"Êtes-vous vous-même universitaire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's this I hear about you having a doctorate?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que j'entends dire à propos de votre doctorat ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah, it's all very glamorous.  Sure, I trained in the great ivory "
"tower, got my PhD in mycology.  Did my dissertation on signaling pathways in "
"hyphae formation, and a postdoc in plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  "
"Then I got the job at the bookstore because there wasn't a ton of work for a "
"doctor of mycology, although I'd had a few nibbles before things really got "
"crazy.  Now, people are just breaking down my door to get my sweet sweet "
"knowledge of mold to help them fight the incoming zombie threat."
msgstr ""
"Oui, oui, tout cela est très prestigieux. Bien sûr, j'ai été formé dans la "
"grande tour d'ivoire, j'ai obtenu mon doctorat en mycologie. J'ai fait ma "
"thèse sur les voies de signalisation dans la formation des hyphes, et j'ai "
"fait un post doctorat  sur la communication entre les plantes et les "
"champignons dans les rhizomes. Ensuite, j'ai trouvé un emploi à la librairie "
"parce qu'il n'y avait pas beaucoup de travail pour un docteur en mycologie, "
"même si j'ai eu quelques opportunités avant que les choses ne deviennent "
"vraiment folles. Aujourd'hui, les gens se bousculent à ma porte pour obtenir "
"mes douces connaissances en matière de moisissures afin de les aider à lutter "
"contre la menace zombie qui se profile."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know about the fungal zombies though?"
msgstr "Connaissez-vous les zombies fongiques ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Heh.  Yeah, that was a great use of my time.  As you can see it really helped "
"my employment prospects.  Yeah, I have a PhD in mycology.  Did my "
"dissertation on signaling pathways in hyphae formation, and a postdoc in "
"plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  Then I got the job at the bookstore "
"because there wasn't a ton of work for a doctor of mycology, although I'd had "
"a few nibbles before things really got crazy.  Now, people are just breaking "
"down my door to get my sweet sweet knowledge of mold to help them fight the "
"incoming zombie threat."
msgstr ""
"Heh. Oui, j'ai bien utilisé mon temps. Comme vous pouvez le voir, cela a "
"vraiment amélioré mes perspectives d'emploi. Oui, j'ai un doctorat en "
"mycologie. J'ai fait ma thèse sur les voies de signalisation dans la "
"formation des hyphes, et j'ai fait un postdoc sur la communication entre les "
"plantes et les champignons dans les rhizomes. Ensuite, j'ai trouvé un emploi "
"à la librairie parce qu'il n'y avait pas beaucoup de travail pour un docteur "
"en mycologie, bien que j'aie eu quelques opportunités avant que les choses ne "
"deviennent vraiment folles. Aujourd'hui, les gens se bousculent à ma porte "
"pour obtenir mes douces connaissances en matière de moisissures afin de les "
"aider à lutter contre la menace zombie qui se profile."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, no I don't, and I'd appreciate you not leaving me hanging on that.  There "
"are fungal zombies?"
msgstr ""
"Non, non, je ne sais pas, et j'apprécierais que vous ne me laissiez pas en "
"suspens sur ce point. Il y a des zombies fongiques ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Encroaching alien mushrooms, fungal towers, tough mycelium invading ground "
"and trees, zombies taken over by aggressive mold… Yeah.  It's ugly stuff."
msgstr ""
"Des champignons extraterrestres envahissants, des tours fongiques, du "
"mycélium coriace envahissant le sol et les arbres, des zombies capturés par "
"de la moisissure agressive…  Pas des bonnes choses."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, you've got my attention.  Listen, do you think you could bring me some "
"kind of sample of these things?"
msgstr ""
"Ok, vous avez mon attention. Ecoutez, pensez-vous pouvoir m'apporter une "
"sorte d'échantillon de ces choses ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It'd be dangerous.  What kind of benefit is there from taking a risk like "
"that?"
msgstr "Ce serait dangereux. Quel avantage y a-t-il à prendre un tel risque ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you get me a sample, I'll join your crazy camp expedition.  Hell, if you "
"bring me a sample maybe I'll help you set up a lab to study this stuff.  "
"Almost anything could work, but if this stuff is as dangerous as you make it "
"sound, maybe make sure it's not a sporulating body."
msgstr ""
"Si vous m'apportez un échantillon, je me joindrai à votre expédition dans un "
"camp de fous. Si vous m'apportez un échantillon, je vous aiderai peut-être à "
"monter un labo pour étudier ce truc. Presque tout pourrait fonctionner, mais "
"si ce truc est aussi dangereux que tu le dis, assure-toi que ce n'est pas un "
"corps sporulant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I dunno, scientific interest?  If you don't bring me anything, no worries.  "
"I'm positively swimming in entertainment here, as you can see."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas, un intérêt scientifique ? Si vous ne m'apportez rien, ne vous "
"inquiétez pas. Comme vous pouvez le constater, je nage dans le divertissement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It just so happens I have a chunk of fungal matter on me right now."
msgstr "Il se trouve que j'ai un morceau de matière fongique sur moi en ce moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, I'd better get going.  I'll see if I can find you something."
msgstr "Sure, I'd better get going. I'll see if I can find you something."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well.  Well, well, well.  This is really interesting.  Look, you can see "
"reticulations here, it looks sort of like an enlarged piece of a stipe from a "
"basidiocarp… but look at this, these fibers are clearly unlike anything I've "
"seen before.  I wonder if they're motile?\n"
"\n"
"Okay, listen: you've got yourself a deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've "
"gotta get me hooked up with a microscope as soon as you can.  This could be "
"the beginning of something really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying "
"that I'm not coming unless you can find a place for my friends here in your "
"base.  I'm sure you anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It "
"should be easy, they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... Eh bien, eh bien, eh bien. Ceci est vraiment intéressant. "
"Regardez, vous pouvez voir des réticulations ici, cela ressemble à un morceau "
"agrandi d'un stipe d'un basidiocarpe... mais regardez ça, ces fibres sont "
"clairement différentes de tout ce que j'ai vu auparavant. Je me demande si "
"elles sont mobiles.\n"
"\n"
"Bon, écoutez : vous avez un marché. Je viendrai à votre base, mais vous devez "
"m'équiper d'un microscope dès que possible. Ça pourrait être le début de "
"quelque chose de vraiment cool. Oh, et il va sans dire que je ne viendrai pas "
"si vous ne trouvez pas de place pour mes amis dans votre base. Je suis sûr "
"que vous l'avez prévu. Parlez-leur d'y aller et je suis partant. Ça devrait "
"être facile, c'est une bande d'idiots au grand cœur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great!  I'll go see what I can do about that."
msgstr "C'est très bien ! Je vais voir ce que je peux faire à ce sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well.  Well, well, well.  This is really interesting.  Look, you can see "
"reticulations here, it looks sort of like an enlarged piece of a stipe from a "
"basidiocarp… but look at this, these fibers are clearly unlike anything I've "
"seen before.  I wonder if they're motile?\n"
"\n"
"Sorry.  I could stare at this all day.  I owe you one, a big one.  Thanks for "
"this.  Let me know if you ever need a favor from a chubby beggar woman."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... Eh bien, eh bien, eh bien. Ceci est vraiment intéressant. "
"Regardez, vous pouvez voir des réticulations ici, cela ressemble à un morceau "
"agrandi d'un stipe d'un basidiocarpe... mais regardez ça, ces fibres sont "
"clairement différentes de tout ce que j'ai vu auparavant. Je me demande si "
"elles sont mobiles.\n"
"\n"
"Je suis désolé. Je pourrais regarder ça toute la journée. Je vous en dois "
"une, une grosse. Merci pour ça. Faites-moi savoir si vous avez besoin d'une "
"faveur de la part d'une mendiante grassouillette."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Glad you like it.  If I think of something you can do in return, I'll let you "
"know."
msgstr ""
"Je suis heureux que cela vous plaise. Si je pense à quelque chose que vous "
"pouvez faire en retour, je vous le ferai savoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well good.  Let's get going, I want to see some more of these crazy mushrooms."
msgstr "Très bien. Allons-y, je veux voir d'autres de ces champignons fous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Sickly beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Brandon Garder"
msgstr "Brandon Garder"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter2.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Sickly beggar in the refugee center.
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#. ~ Construction skill trainer
msgid "Carpenter"
msgstr "Charpentier"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, are you a big fan of survival of the fittest?"
msgstr "Êtes-vous un grand fan de la survie du plus fort ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why do you ask?"
msgstr "Pourquoi cette question?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to see you too, what's up?"
msgstr "Ravi de te voir aussi, quoi de neuf ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to see you.  I gotta be going though."
msgstr "C'est un plaisir de vous voir. Mais je dois y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh you know, the usual: sittin' out here until I starve to death, playin' "
"cards with Dave, that kinda thing."
msgstr ""
"Oh vous savez, la routine : rester ici jusqu'à ce que je meure de faim, jouer "
"aux cartes avec Dave, ce genre de choses."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Because I sure ain't fit, so I'm sittin' out here until I starve to death.  "
"Help a poor sickly soul out?"
msgstr ""
"Parce que je ne suis pas en forme, alors je reste ici jusqu'à ce que je meure "
"de faim. Aider une pauvre âme malade ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could maybe help you out… want something to eat?"
msgstr "Je pourrais peut-être vous aider… Vous voulez manger quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong with you?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qui va mal?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They won't let you in because you're sick?"
msgstr "Ils ne vous laissent pas entrer parce que vous êtes malade ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you even get here if you're so sick?"
msgstr "Comment es-tu arrivé ici si tu es si malade ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you camped out here if they won't let you in?"
msgstr "Pourquoi campez-vous ici s'ils ne vous laissent pas entrer ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's awful kind of you, you really are a wonderful person."
msgstr "C'est très gentil de votre part, vous êtes vraiment une personne merveilleuse."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's good to know there are still people like you in the world, it really is."
msgstr ""
"Il est bon de savoir qu'il y a encore des gens comme vous dans le monde, "
"vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you up to?"
msgstr "Que faites-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You name it!  Asthma, diabetes, arthritis.  Diabetes hasn't been so bad since "
"I stopped, y'know, eating regularly.  Well, I assume it hasn't.  Not like I "
"can check that ol' whatchamacallit, the blood test the docs used to bug me "
"about every couple months."
msgstr ""
"Vous n'avez que l'embarras du choix ! Asthme, diabète, arthrite. Le diabète "
"n'est pas si grave depuis que j'ai cessé de manger régulièrement. Enfin, je "
"suppose que ce n'est pas le cas. Ce n'est pas comme si je pouvais vérifier ce "
"vieux \"whatchamacallit\", le test sanguin pour lequel les docteurs avaient "
"l'habitude de m'embêter tous les deux mois."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem awfully happy considering the situation."
msgstr "Vous semblez très heureux compte tenu de la situation."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They got enough mouths to feed that can pull their own weight.  I got a lot "
"of weight and I'm too weak to pull it, so I'm out here."
msgstr ""
"Ils ont suffisamment de bouches à nourrir qui peuvent tirer leur épingle du "
"jeu. J'ai beaucoup de poids et je suis trop faible pour le tirer, alors je "
"suis ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Came with a small group quite a while ago.  The others were young and fit, "
"they got in.  They were some of the last ones to get in actually.  I didn't "
"make the cutoff."
msgstr ""
"Came with a small group quite a while ago. The others were young and fit, "
"they got in. They were some of the last ones to get in actually. I didn't "
"make the cutoff."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is a mercy.  I get shelter, light, and heat, and those guards will help "
"us if any zombies show up.  It ain't so bad.  If I was out on my own I'd have "
"none of this and still have to look for food… in other words, I'd be dead as "
"a doornail.  Or I guess undead."
msgstr ""
"This is a mercy. I get shelter, light, and heat, and those guards will help "
"us if any zombies show up. It ain't so bad. If I was out on my own I'd have "
"none of this and still have to look for food… in other words, I'd be dead as "
"a doornail. Or I guess undead."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What's the alternative?  You take the hand you're dealt.  I've given eulogies "
"for two of the people I love most on this earth, and the third wrote me off.  "
"I've already been through the end of the world.  Came out the other side with "
"my bits intact.  And you know, I've been pretty lonely since my wife passed.  "
"Here I've got friends.  We might be hungry but we're close.  Reena's been "
"teaching me math and science, Luo is one of the smartest folks I've ever met "
"- she's got a doctorate you know - and Yusuke is the only one here that can "
"beat me at poker.  And Dave, well, he's Dave.  There's more goin' on under "
"the surface there, mark my words.  We may be unfit, but we aren't worthless."
msgstr ""
"Quelle est l'alternative ? On prend la main qu'on a reçue. J'ai fait l'éloge "
"funèbre de deux des personnes que j'aime le plus sur cette terre, et la "
"troisième m'a laissé tomber. J'ai déjà vécu la fin du monde. Je suis sorti de "
"l'autre côté avec mes morceaux intacts. Et vous savez, je me suis senti très "
"seul depuis le décès de ma femme. Ici, j'ai des amis. On a peut-être faim, "
"mais on est proches. Reena m'apprend les mathématiques et les sciences, Luo "
"est l'une des personnes les plus intelligentes que j'aie jamais rencontrées - "
"elle a un doctorat, vous savez - et Yusuke est le seul ici à pouvoir me "
"battre au poker. Et Dave, c'est Dave. Il y a d'autres choses qui se passent "
"sous la surface, croyez-moi. Nous sommes peut-être inaptes, mais nous ne "
"sommes pas sans valeur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I used to be a roofer, but I had a bad fall and wrecked my back around "
"'06.  Tried to get into other kinds of carpentry but I just don't have the "
"head for it.  My wife managed to support both of us with the extra bit I made "
"from odd jobs, but she had a stroke in 2016 and left me on my own the last "
"few years slowly draining my savings dry while I work whatever junk jobs I "
"can handle.  Couple days before <the_cataclysm> I got the notice that the "
"bank was going to foreclose on my crappy little trailer."
msgstr ""
"J'étais couvreur, mais j'ai fait une mauvaise chute et je me suis cassé le "
"dos vers 2006. J'ai essayé de me lancer dans d'autres types de menuiserie, "
"mais je n'ai pas la tête à ça. Ma femme a réussi à nous faire vivre tous les "
"deux avec le peu que je gagnais en faisant des petits boulots, mais elle a eu "
"un accident vasculaire cérébral en 2016 et m'a laissé seul ces dernières "
"années, vidant peu à peu mes économies pendant que je faisais les petits "
"boulots que je pouvais faire. Quelques jours avant <the_cataclysm>, j'ai reçu "
"l'avis que la banque allait saisir ma petite caravane minable."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You have any kids?"
msgstr "Vous avez des enfants?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Would you like to travel with me?  Someone good with a trade could be "
"helpful, and it's got to be better than wasting away here."
msgstr ""
"Voulez-vous voyager avec moi ? Quelqu'un de doué pour le commerce pourrait "
"être utile, et c'est toujours mieux que de perdre son temps ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp.  It's a damn sight better than those place, and there are "
"regular meals.  Someone with your trades experience would be welcome, even if "
"you can't do the big jobs anymore."
msgstr ""
"J'ai un camp. C'est bien mieux que ces endroits, et il y a des repas "
"réguliers. Quelqu'un avec votre expérience des métiers serait le bienvenu, "
"même si vous ne pouvez plus faire les gros travaux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, we had two.  My daughter died of an OD right at the start of that "
"fentanyl stuff.  It did a real number on my son - they were twins you see - "
"and he cut ties to me and my wife.  Wasn't even there for her funeral.  I "
"can't blame him, it messed us all up pretty fierce.  As far as I'm concerned "
"he's still out there with my grandkids, hiding away somewhere safe.  These "
"days, no news is good news."
msgstr ""
"Oui, nous en avons eu deux. Ma fille est morte d'une overdose au début de "
"l'affaire du fentanyl. Cela a fait beaucoup de mal à mon fils - ils étaient "
"jumeaux - et il a coupé les ponts avec moi et ma femme. Il n'a même pas "
"assisté à ses funérailles. Je ne peux pas lui en vouloir, ça nous a tous mis "
"dans un sale état. En ce qui me concerne, il est toujours avec mes "
"petits-enfants, caché dans un endroit sûr. Ces jours-ci, aucune nouvelle "
"n'est une bonne nouvelle."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's sweet of you to say that, but I'm just not up to the wandering life, not "
"with these knees."
msgstr ""
"C'est gentil de dire ça, mais je ne suis pas prêt à vivre une vie d'errance, "
"pas avec ces genoux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's awful nice of you.  Tell you what: if you can help Dave get himself "
"sorted out, so I don't feel like I've gotta stay here keeping an eye on the "
"poor fella, then I'll come along."
msgstr ""
"C'est très gentil de votre part. Je vais vous dire : si vous pouvez aider "
"Dave à s'en sortir, pour que je n'aie pas l'impression de devoir rester ici à "
"surveiller le pauvre gars, alors je viendrai."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think I've sorted Dave out pretty well, don't you?  Would you consider "
"coming with me now?"
msgstr ""
"Je pense que j'ai bien arrangé Dave, n'est-ce pas ? Voudriez-vous venir avec "
"moi maintenant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Golly.  I didn't expect that, but I'm as good as my word.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Mutant beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Yusuke Taylor"
msgstr "Yusuke Taylor"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Mutant beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Computer Technician"
msgstr "Technicien Informatique"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I couldn't help but notice, you're covered in fur."
msgstr "Je n'ai pas pu m'empêcher de remarquer que vous êtes couvert de fourrure."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like something to eat?"
msgstr "Voulez-vous manger quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I live here.  Too mutant to join the cool kids club, but not mutant enough to "
"kill on sight."
msgstr ""
"Je vis ici, trop mutant pour être accepté par le groupe, mais pas assez "
"mutant pour être tiré dessus à vue."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why live out here?"
msgstr "Pourquoi vivre ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem like you can hold your own.  Why not travel with me?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air de pouvoir vous débrouiller. Pourquoi ne pas voyager avec moi "
"?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's safer than making my own home.  I head out and forage when I have to.  "
"As long as we keep it clean and do our part when a zombie comes, they let us "
"squat here as an extra defense.  They don't like that I've been bringing food "
"for the other squatters though… I think they are trying to slowly starve us "
"out, and even though I can't keep everyone's bellies full, I've been able to "
"bring back enough to keep these folk in better shape.  I suspect they'll find "
"an excuse to kick me out eventually."
msgstr ""
"C'est plus sûr que de faire sa propre maison. Je sors et je cherche de la "
"nourriture quand il le faut. Tant que nous restons propres et que nous "
"faisons notre part quand un zombie arrive, ils nous laissent squatter ici "
"comme une défense supplémentaire. Ils n'aiment pas que je ramène de la "
"nourriture pour les autres squatters... Je pense qu'ils essaient de nous "
"affamer lentement, et même si je ne peux pas remplir le ventre de tout le "
"monde, j'ai pu ramener assez de nourriture pour que ces gens soient en "
"meilleure forme. Je pense qu'ils finiront par trouver une excuse pour me "
"mettre dehors."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Gross, isn't it?  Feels like pubes.  I just started growing it everywhere a "
"little while after the Cataclysm.  No idea what caused it.  I can't blame "
"them for hating it, I hate it."
msgstr ""
"Ma fourrure est dégoutante non? On dirait du poil pubien. Ça à commencé à "
"pousser quelque jours après le Cataclysme. Aucune idée quelle en est la "
"cause. Je peux pas blamer les réfugiés d'être repoussés par la fourrure par "
"contre, je la déteste aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do okay for myself actually.  I eat a lot of things close to spoilage while "
"I'm foraging.  If you've got food to spare, please give it to my friends."
msgstr ""
"J'ai pas besoin de nourriture. Je mange beaucoup de choses au point de "
"pourrir quand je sors trouver de la nourriture. Si vous avez de la nourriture "
"à partager, donnez-la à mes amis."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing too exciting.  I was in trade college, learning to be a computer "
"technician.  Those skills aren't too helpful, but when I was a kid I was an "
"Eagle scout.  I learned all kinds of useful stuff about plants and foraging, "
"and that's come in pretty handy."
msgstr ""
"Rien de trop excitant. J'étais dans une école de métiers, je voulais devenir "
"un/e technicien/ne informatique. Ces compétences ne sont plus très utile "
"maintenant, mais quand j'étais un gamin/e j'étais scout. Et ce que ça m'a "
"appris au sujet des herbes, plantes et champignons sauvages, ça c'est utile."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about your family, stuff like that?"
msgstr "Et votre famille?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't want to think about it.  I grew up in Rhode Island, they're still "
"there.  I haven't heard from them since the insanity with the Governor and "
"that secession stuff.  All communication lines got closed off.  I haven't met "
"anyone who knows what happened to the people there but I don't have much hope."
msgstr ""
"Je ne veux pas y penser. J'ai grandi à Rhode Island, ils y sont encore. Je "
"n'ai pas entendu parler d'eux depuis la folie du gouverneur et cette histoire "
"de sécession. Toutes les lignes de communication ont été fermées. Je n'ai "
"rencontré personne qui sache ce qui est arrivé aux gens là-bas, mais je n'ai "
"pas beaucoup d'espoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you go back there?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ne pas y retourner ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about what happened with Rhode Island?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez m'en dire plus sur ce qui c'est passé sur Rhode Island?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Same reason as I'm stuck here… it's way too dangerous, for one thing.  Almost "
"a hundred miles, through zombie infested territory, on foot, to get to the "
"shoreline?  No, thank you.  And then, how would I get from the shore to Block "
"Island?  My family moved out there when Dad retired, and I get the impression "
"the ferry probably isn't running anymore.  Even if I got there, I don't know "
"what I'd find, and I think maybe that scares me the most."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You don't know?  The governor went nuts, like a lot of people did leading up "
"to the end, only he had a lot more power to work with.  One day he just "
"showed up to work with a militia of rowdies and loyalists and staged a coup, "
"taking over the government completely, killing those that opposed him, and "
"moving as many people as he could get behind him onto the islands.  The "
"rumors I've heard is that most of them survived the Cataclysm and are still "
"running the show there, but that seems kind of impossible to me."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne savez pas ? Le gouverneur est devenu fou, comme beaucoup de gens "
"l'ont fait jusqu'à la fin, mais il avait beaucoup plus de pouvoir pour "
"travailler. Un jour, il s'est présenté au travail avec une milice de voyous "
"et de loyalistes et a organisé un coup d'État, prenant le contrôle total du "
"gouvernement, tuant ceux qui s'opposaient à lui et déplaçant sur les îles "
"autant de personnes qu'il pouvait en avoir derrière lui. La rumeur que j'ai "
"entendue est que la plupart d'entre eux ont survécu au Cataclysme et qu'ils "
"sont toujours aux commandes, mais cela me semble impossible."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you think you'd go back and look for your family?"
msgstr "Pensez-vous que vous y retourneriez pour rechercher votre famille ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've spoken to all your friends, and except for Dave, they're good to go.  "
"Dave wants to stay here.  How about you?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai parlé à tous vos amis, et à l'exception de Dave, ils sont prêts à "
"partir. Dave veut rester ici. Et toi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh.  Getting those three to sign on to a suicide mission is quite the feat… "
"sounds like you're pretty dedicated to this.  OK, I'm with you.  Let's round "
"up the others and hit the road."
msgstr ""
"Huh… Faire signer ces trois-là pour une mission suicide, c'est un exploit… On "
"dirait que vous voulez vraiment faire ça.  OK, je suis avec vous.  "
"Rassemblons les autres et prenons la route."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Bien. <lets_go>"

