#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm not a kid, okay?  I'm fourteen."
msgstr "Je ne suis pas une enfant, d'accord ? J'ai quatorze ans."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I didn't mean anything by it.  What's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I didn't mean anything by it.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just standing around here waiting, like a bunch of idiots.  We're "
"supposedly waiting to go downstairs to the shelter, but it's been over a "
"month.  I don't think it's happening.  I don't know what we're doing here.  "
"I've read all the books, and there's zombies outside so we're stuck in here.  "
"We can hear them at night."
msgstr ""
"Nous restons là à attendre, comme une bande d'idiots. Nous sommes censés "
"attendre de descendre au refuge, mais cela fait plus d'un mois. Je ne pense "
"pas que ce soit le cas. Je ne sais pas ce que nous faisons ici. J'ai lu tous "
"les livres, et il y a des zombies dehors, alors on est coincés ici. On les "
"entend la nuit."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know what's up.  I'm not sure what we're even doing here.  They say "
"we're supposed to wait until we can be moved to the shelter downstairs, but "
"we've been here days and there's no word on how long we'll be waiting.  It's "
"all so stupid, and nobody can tell me anything.\"  She glances at the "
"shuttered windows.  \"Jenny figures they're never going to let us go down "
"there, so I guess we're going to sort it out up here, one way or another.  "
"It's not fair, but 'fair' doesn't mean much in my life anymore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*narrows her eyes, her words coming out hoarse and clipped.  \"You can't just "
"go asking people questions like that nowadays.  I'm a teenaged girl alone in "
"an evacuation center after, like, literally everyone in the world died and "
"came back as zombies.  What do you think my story is?  My entire family died, "
"came back as zombies, and I somehow wound up here.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle fronce les yeux, ses mots sont rauques et coupés. \"On ne peut pas "
"poser ce genre de questions aux gens de nos jours. Je suis une adolescente "
"seule dans un centre d'évacuation après que tout le monde soit mort et revenu "
"sous forme de zombies. Quelle est mon histoire, à votre avis ? Toute ma "
"famille est morte, elle est revenue sous forme de zombies, et j'ai atterri "
"ici d'une manière ou d'une autre.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who takes care of you here?"
msgstr "Qui s'occupe de vous ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nobody really.  I'm old enough to work and get merch for my rations.  Jenny "
"and Rhy look out for me though.  They think I don't notice that they're "
"looking out for me, but I do.  It's okay, they're both cool."
msgstr ""
"Personne vraiment. Je suis assez grand pour travailler et obtenir des "
"marchandises pour mes rations. Jenny et Rhy veillent sur moi. Ils pensent que "
"je ne remarque pas qu'ils veillent sur moi, mais c'est le cas. Ce n'est pas "
"grave, elles sont toutes les deux cool."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have much of a hot take besides what I just said.  It's shit.  Not "
"enough to do to stay busy, not enough to eat, and even if I had internet, all "
"the YouTubers I follow are dead."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas grand-chose à dire à part ce que je viens de dire. C'est la "
"merde. Pas assez de choses à faire pour rester occupé, pas assez à manger, et "
"même si j'avais Internet, tous les YouTubers que je suis sont morts."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What YouTubers did you follow?"
msgstr "Quel YouTubers étiez-vous abonnée à?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks you up and down, an uncharacteristic glint of humor in her eyes.  "
"\"Why, you thinking of subscribing?  I don't think you'd have heard of them, "
"and even if you had, there's definitely no way for them to get any new "
"content out.  Not anything worth watching anyway.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle vous regarde de haut en bas, avec une lueur d'humour inhabituelle dans "
"les yeux. \"Pourquoi, tu penses à t'abonner ? Je ne pense pas que tu aies "
"entendu parler d'eux, et même si c'était le cas, il n'y a aucun moyen pour "
"eux de diffuser du nouveau contenu. Rien qui vaille la peine d'être regardé "
"en tout cas.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Alonso Lautrec"
msgstr "Alonso Lautrec"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "al_relaxed"
msgid "Relaxed with Alonso"
msgstr "S'est détendu·e avec Alonso"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Relaxed with Alonso"
msgid "You spent some pleasant time relaxing with someone."
msgstr "Vous avez passé un agréable moment de détente avec quelqu'un."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Miss message of effect type "Relaxed with Alonso"
msgid "You feel relaxed."
msgstr "Vous vous sentez relaxé·e."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem a little forward…"
msgstr "Vous avez l'air un peu trop pressé⋅e…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[PER 10] What is up with you?  What's with the fake accent, and speaking in "
"the third person?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why aren't you wearing any pants?"
msgstr "Pourquoi est-ce que vous ne portez pas de pantalon?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About those special pants a sexy clown hid in a shop for mysterious reasons…"
msgstr ""
"À propos de ce pantalon spécial qu'un clown sexy a caché dans une boutique "
"pour des raisons mystérieuses…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[PRETTY] Remember that nice thing I did for you?  Can you do something nice "
"for me?"
msgstr ""
"[PRETTY]Tu te souviens de la chose gentille que j'ai faite pour toi ? Peux-tu "
"faire quelque chose de gentil pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So about those condoms.  I thought of a good use for them…"
msgstr "A propos de ces préservatifs.  J'ai trouvé un bon usage pour eux…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[UGLY] I'm desperate.  You're my only chance."
msgstr "[UGLY] Je suis désespéré. Tu es ma seule chance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is an uncharacteristically well-groomed young man, his hair trim and slicked "
"back.  In this stark setting, he looks like a cartoon character on a "
"live-action set piece.  \""
msgstr ""
"*Il s'agit d'un jeune homme inhabituellement soigné, aux cheveux bien coupés "
"et lissés en arrière. Dans ce décor austère, il ressemble à un personnage de "
"dessin animé sur un plateau de tournage. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh my, it's good to see such a strong and handsome fellow around here"
msgstr "Oh mon Dieu, c'est bon de voir un homme si fort et si beau par ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh my, you're a beautiful lady, so nice to see you"
msgstr "Oh mon Dieu, vous êtes une belle dame, c'est un plaisir de vous voir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".\"  He slides his hand through his hair and smiles, his eyes half-lidded.  "
"\"They call me Alonso.\""
msgstr ""
".\" Il passe la main dans ses cheveux et sourit, les yeux mi-clos. \"Ils "
"m'appellent Alonso.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Alonso."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Alonso."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Alonso, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Alonso, enchanté·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Alonso.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Alonso.  Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Alonso.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Alonso.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice to meet you too.  Very nice.  It gets so lonely here in the center."
msgstr ""
"Enchanté de vous rencontrer également. Très agréable. On se sent si seul ici, "
"au centre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well, it's a lot better now that you're here.  Nice to see a familiar face."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, c'est beaucoup mieux maintenant que tu es là. C'est bien de voir un "
"visage familier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Now that you are here, everything.  Is there anything Alonso can… *do for "
"you*?"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que vous êtes là, tout.  Y a-t-il quelque chose qu'Alonso puisse…  "
"*faire pour vous*?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know me, I gotta be me, right?"
msgstr "Vous me connaissez, je dois être moi-même, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alonso cannot help himself, in the face of someone so fine as you."
msgstr "Alonso ne peut pas s'en empêcher, face à quelqu'un d'aussi fin que vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aw man"
msgstr "Oh mec/meuf"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aw come on"
msgstr "Oh allez là"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", why you gotta be like that?  I'm just tryin' to get an air of mystery okay? "
" Nobody wants to be with a slutty guy from Brooklyn, but Alonso the "
"mysterious is another story."
msgstr ""
"Pourquoi es-tu comme ça ? J'essaie juste d'avoir un air mystérieux, d'accord "
"? Personne n'a envie d'être avec une salope de Brooklyn, mais Alonso le "
"mystérieux, c'est une autre histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And how is that working out for you?"
msgstr "Et comment cela se passe-t-il pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Better'n you'd maybe think, okay?  Can we drop it?"
msgstr "C'est mieux que ce que vous pensez, d'accord ? On peut laisser tomber ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just stop talking like that around me, maybe?  It's really obnoxious."
msgstr "Arrêtez de parler comme ça autour de moi, peut-être ? C'est vraiment odieux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know what?  You do you.  It's all good."
msgstr "Vous savez quoi ? Tu le fais. Tout va bien."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll leave you to it then."
msgstr "Je vous laisse faire ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Fine.  As a favor to you, I'll be a guy from Brooklyn."
msgstr "Très bien. Pour te rendre service, je serai un gars de Brooklyn."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alonso thanks you for your kindness, and will remain his glorious self."
msgstr "Alonso vous remercie pour votre gentillesse, et restera lui-même."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm tryin' ta forget, y'know?  Don't like thinkin' about the past.  Better to "
"plan for the future, even if the future looks grim."
msgstr ""
"I'm tryin' ta forget, y'know?  Don't like thinkin' about the past.  Better to "
"plan for the future, even if the future looks grim."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alonso has many a tale to tell, all slow and drawn-out like, a sensual "
"seduction of the -- how you say?  Ears.  There are dark days ahead, but "
"perhaps together we can bring a little light?  Or at least a little heat.  "
"This is a science joke I make for you.  Friction, it is the joke."
msgstr ""
"J'essaie d'oublier, vous savez ? Je n'aime pas penser au passé. Il vaut mieux "
"préparer l'avenir, même s'il est sombre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I fucked up and got drunk at a kiddy party I crashed, broke into a van "
"with the party clown I was seein' (hey don't judge me, it took me a long time "
"to make that happen, clowns are very givin' lovers) and I lost my pants, "
"includin' all my money and all my triple magnum condoms I stole off a dead "
"priest at a bar.  I'd be mad, but at least I'm safe, I made it here.  But I "
"got no game here y'know?  I look like the clown when I should be knee deep in "
"hotness here.  Look around, it's straight hotties!"
msgstr ""
"Ouais, j'ai merdé et je me suis saoulé à une fête d'enfants que j'ai ratée, "
"je me suis introduit dans une camionnette avec le clown de la fête que je "
"voyais (ne me jugez pas, ça m'a pris du temps pour y arriver, les clowns sont "
"des amoureux très généreux) et j'ai perdu mon pantalon, y compris tout mon "
"argent et tous mes préservatifs triple magnum que j'ai volés à un prêtre mort "
"dans un bar. Je serais furieux, mais au moins je suis en sécurité, j'ai "
"réussi à venir ici. Mais je n'ai pas de jeu ici, tu sais ? J'ai l'air d'un "
"clown alors que je devrais être dans le feu de l'action jusqu'aux genoux. "
"Regarde autour de toi, il y a des chaudes hétéros !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Why were you looking though?  I kid, I know she is hard to miss!  In English, "
"the special package she is a woman no?  No.  I see.  And so do you it seems.  "
"Yes.  There was such a clown, a clown of enormous physical beauty.  The pale, "
"perfect skin, the ruby red lips, amazing hair, and what a sense of humor.  I "
"laugh still, though I have lost everything.  My pants, my money, my many "
"illegal imported triple magnum condoms I stole from a priest.  All lost to "
"that one beautiful night.  The candles, the balloons, the singing.  It was "
"the most romantic children's birthday party you could hope to imagine.  I "
"would do it all again, and there was so much we did.  It was the end of that "
"party, but the beginning of something beautiful, for several hours in that "
"open minivan we found.  But you do not want to hear of such pleasures, I do "
"not want to get you excited, for what can I do when I look so foolish, and "
"lack the protection needed for more serious excitement.  Though and you must "
"understand, Alonso's tongue is good for more than just the telling of long "
"and saucy stories yes?"
msgstr ""
"Mais pourquoi cherchiez-vous ? Je plaisante, je sais qu'il est difficile de "
"la rater ! En anglais, le paquet spécial, c'est une femme, non ? Non. Je "
"vois. Et vous aussi, semble-t-il. Oui. Il y a eu un clown, un clown d'une "
"énorme beauté physique. Une peau pâle et parfaite, des lèvres rouges comme le "
"rubis, une chevelure étonnante, et quel sens de l'humour. Je ris encore, bien "
"que j'aie tout perdu. Mon pantalon, mon argent, mes nombreux préservatifs "
"triple magnum importés illégalement que j'ai volés à un prêtre. Tout a été "
"perdu lors de cette belle nuit. Les bougies, les ballons, les chants. C'était "
"la fête d'anniversaire d'enfant la plus romantique que l'on puisse imaginer. "
"Je referais tout cela, et nous avons fait tellement de choses. Ce fut la fin "
"de cette fête, mais le début de quelque chose de magnifique, pendant "
"plusieurs heures, dans ce minivan ouvert que nous avions trouvé. Mais tu ne "
"veux pas entendre parler de ces plaisirs, je ne veux pas t'exciter, car que "
"puis-je faire quand j'ai l'air si stupide et que je n'ai pas la protection "
"nécessaire pour une excitation plus sérieuse. Mais vous devez comprendre que "
"la langue d'Alonso ne sert pas qu'à raconter de longues histoires grivoises, "
"n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I help you out?"
msgstr "Je peux vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Could be better.  I don't really got any friends here in the center, but "
"seeing travelers like you always brightens my day."
msgstr ""
"Cela pourrait être mieux. Je n'ai pas vraiment d'amis ici au centre, mais "
"voir des voyageurs comme vous illumine toujours ma journée."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Here in the center, Alonso is a bit lonely.  We get a few brave, strong "
"travelers like yourself, though, and seeing them brightens Alonso's day.  "
"Normally I am more popular, but something seems to be troubling the spirits "
"of these people during these terrible times."
msgstr ""
"Ici, au centre, Alonso se sent un peu seul. Nous recevons quelques voyageurs "
"courageux et forts comme vous, et les voir illumine la journée d'Alonso. "
"Normalement, je suis plus populaire, mais quelque chose semble troubler les "
"esprits de ces gens en ces temps terribles."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgstr "Alonso a besoin de son pantalon spécial"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid "Find Alonso's leather pants in the 'toy shop' Alonso has marked on your map."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez le pantalon en cuir d'Alonso dans le \"magasin de jouets\" qu'Alonso "
"a indiqué sur votre carte."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid "I think I might know where those special pants might be though…"
msgstr "Je pense savoir où se trouve ce pantalon spécial…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"This clown was into some of the different things, not the vanilla, you "
"understand me?  Yes.  I think you will find my valuables in a toy shop not so "
"far."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"You make me so happy I could give you little kisses, and some big kisses, and "
"then something else maybe."
msgstr ""
"Tu me rends si heureuse que je pourrais te donner de petits baisers, de gros "
"baisers et peut-être autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"I know that you cannot resist me long.  I will wait, and perhaps some other "
"pretty thing will help me instead?"
msgstr ""
"Je sais que vous ne pourrez pas me résister longtemps. J'attendrai, et "
"peut-être qu'une autre jolie chose m'aidera à la place ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"It may be crowded no?  A popular place before, maybe is better to visit at "
"night.  Sounds like Alonso's apartment no?"
msgstr ""
"Il y a peut-être du monde, non ? C'est un endroit populaire avant, peut-être "
"vaut-il mieux le visiter la nuit. On dirait l'appartement d'Alonso, non ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"Have you found what it is that you seek?  There may be something in it for "
"you no?  Something big, but we take it slow yes?"
msgstr ""
"Avez-vous trouvé ce que vous cherchez ? Il y a peut-être quelque chose pour "
"vous, non ? Quelque chose de grand, mais il faut y aller doucement, oui ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"This is the best news since those lonely teachers asked me to be a nude model "
"at the college for the blind.  Alas, the special condoms have all been used.  "
"This is not a surprise, few could resist this seductive clown.  You find a "
"condom, I find a use for it.  Safety, she was never more important than now, "
"in *so* many ways."
msgstr ""
"C'est la meilleure nouvelle depuis que ces professeurs solitaires m'ont "
"demandé d'être un modèle nu au collège pour aveugles. Hélas, les préservatifs "
"spéciaux ont tous été utilisés. Ce n'est pas une surprise, peu de gens ont pu "
"résister à ce clown séducteur. Vous trouvez un préservatif, je lui trouve une "
"utilité. La sécurité n'a jamais été aussi importante que maintenant, à bien "
"des égards."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid "You give me confidence.  I trust you.  I do not know why this is."
msgstr "Tu me donnes confiance. J'ai confiance en vous. Je ne sais pas pourquoi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Alonso must have his special pants"
msgid ""
"Disaster, but I thank you for to try.  You want a backrub some time, it will "
"happen for sure.  And maybe you give me a rub too?"
msgstr ""
"Désastre, mais je vous remercie d'avoir essayé. Si tu veux te faire masser le "
"dos un jour, ça arrivera, c'est sûr. Et peut-être que tu me feras un massage "
"aussi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "My jewel of the New England, I give to you my biggest prize."
msgstr "Mon joyau de la Nouvelle-Angleterre, je te donne mon plus grand prix."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"\"\n"
"\n"
"Liam gives you a sly wink, heads to the door, theatrically produces a sock "
"from - somewhere, you're not sure where - slides it on the doorknob, and "
"leaves the room."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sigh.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All done.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "C'est fait. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yeeeeah it's on!"
msgstr "Ouaiiiiis c'est parti !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I give to you what of I got.  And this is Alonso so I mean it's a lot."
msgstr ""
"Je vous donne ce que j'ai. Et c'est Alonso, alors je veux dire que c'est "
"beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Ouais. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"\"\n"
"\n"
"After shooting Alonso a smile of genuine respect, Liam gives you a sly wink, "
"heads to the door, theatrically produces a sock from - somewhere, you're not "
"sure where - slides it on the doorknob, and leaves the room."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sorry kid, you're younger than my little sister was.  Seems wrong."
msgstr "Désolé, tu es plus jeune que ma petite soeur. Ce n'est pas normal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alonso thinks maybe we should wait a few years?"
msgstr "Alonso pense que nous devrions peut-être attendre quelques années ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sigh."
msgstr "Soupir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sorry.  I… saw things back there, when it all went sideways.  I can't go "
"back, not for anything."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolée. J'ai… vu des choses là-bas, quand tout a dérapé.  Je ne peux "
"pas y retourner, pour rien au monde."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Alonso, alas, is sorry, but he cannot sully his hands with blood.  It is not "
"that he does not wish to prove his strength, but he… he is not strong enough."
msgstr ""
"Alonso, hélas, est désolé, mais il ne peut pas salir ses mains avec du sang.  "
"Ce n'est pas qu'il ne veuille pas prouver sa force, mais il… il n'est pas "
"assez fort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks anyway.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Merci tout de même. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, thanks anyway."
msgstr "Hé bien, merci quand même."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Boris Borichenko"
msgstr "Boris Borichenko"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Boris, I'm sorry, but I could only find two people willing to help.  Can I "
"pitch in myself?  [Spend 5 hours helping]"
msgstr ""
"Boris, je suis désolée, mais je n'ai trouvé que deux personnes prêtes à "
"m'aider. Est-ce que je peux m'impliquer moi-même ? [Spend 5hours helping]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Boris, I'm sorry, but I could only find three people willing to help.  Can I "
"pitch in myself?  [Spend 4 hours helping]"
msgstr ""
"Boris, je suis désolée, mais je n'ai trouvé que deux personnes prêtes à "
"m'aider. Est-ce que je peux m'impliquer moi-même ? [Spend 4 hours helping]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I spoke with everyone I could, but only four people agreed to help.  I can "
"pitch in if you want."
msgstr ""
"J'en ai parlé à tout le monde, mais seules quatre personnes ont accepté de "
"m'aider. Je peux participer si vous le souhaitez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything I can help you out with?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelque chose que je puisse faire pour vous aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got anything else I can help out with?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose que je peux vous aider avec?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, have you had a chance to get that laptop working and look at it yet?"
msgstr ""
"Avez-vous déjà eu l'occasion de faire fonctionner votre ordinateur portable "
"et de l'examiner ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Now that you've got your tools and shop set up, do you think you could teach "
"me a thing or two about construction?"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que vous avez installé vos outils et votre atelier, pensez-vous "
"pouvoir m'enseigner une ou deux choses sur la construction ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You don't seem to be doing great."
msgstr "Vous n'avez pas l'air d'aller très bien."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ah, another new face.  Hello.  I am Boris."
msgstr "Ah, encore un nouveau visage. Bonjour. Je suis Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Boris."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Boris, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Boris, enchanté·e."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*stares at you for a moment before nodding in recognition.  \""
msgstr ""
"*Il vous regarde un instant avant de hocher la tête en signe de "
"reconnaissance. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Boris.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Boris. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Boris.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Boris.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*nods at you, his eyes lighting up a little as you approach.  \""
msgstr ""
"*Il vous fait un signe de tête, ses yeux s'illuminent un peu lorsque vous "
"vous approchez. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to see you, Boris.  Are things looking up for you at all?"
msgstr "Content de te voir, Boris. Les choses vont-elles mieux pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It is nice to meet you too.  To what do I owe the pleasure?"
msgstr "Je suis également ravie de vous rencontrer. Que me vaut ce plaisir ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm just a traveler, taking the chance to have some living human company.  "
"What's up in your life these days?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis qu'un voyageur qui profite de la chance d'avoir de la compagnie "
"humaine vivante. Que se passe-t-il dans votre vie ces jours-ci ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just wanted to say hi.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Je voulais juste dire salut. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What is 'up'?  Less than I would like, it seems.  I am better when I am busy, "
"and I am not at all busy."
msgstr ""
"Qu'est-ce que le \"haut\" ? Moins que je ne le souhaiterais, semble-t-il. Je "
"suis meilleur quand je suis occupé, et je ne le suis pas du tout."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*forces a bit of a smile through his bushy beard, though it doesn't reach his "
"eyes.  \"It is good to see you too.  I would not say things are looking 'up' "
"yet, but they are not so much looking down perhaps.  I am keeping a bit "
"busier."
msgstr ""
"*forces a bit of a smile through his bushy beard, though it doesn't reach his "
"eyes. \"It is good to see you too. I would not say things are looking 'up' "
"yet, but they are not so much looking down perhaps. I am keeping a bit busier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want to talk about it a little?"
msgstr "Vous voulez en parler un peu ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a carpenter.  I like to keep my hands busy, especially when I am "
"stressed.  Now, here I am, picking my nose and stuck thinking about my "
"problems and all that I've lost."
msgstr ""
"J'étais charpentier. J'aime avoir les mains occupées, surtout quand je suis "
"stressé. Maintenant, je suis là, à me curer le nez et à penser à mes "
"problèmes et à tout ce que j'ai perdu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What have you lost, if it's okay for me to ask?"
msgstr "Qu'avez-vous perdu, si je peux me permettre de vous le demander ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It seems like carpentry work would be something the Free Merchants need.  Why "
"are you so bored?"
msgstr ""
"Il semblerait que les marchands libres aient besoin d'un travail de "
"charpentier. Pourquoi t'ennuies-tu autant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you teach me something about carpentry?"
msgstr "Pourriez-vous m'apprendre quelque chose sur la menuiserie ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Now that things are cleaned up in the back, is there anything holding you "
"back from working?"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que tout est rentré dans l'ordre, y a-t-il quelque chose qui vous "
"empêche de travailler ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, not great.  Like all here, I have lost too much.  I do not feel I can "
"ever come back from it.  Can anyone be strong enough?"
msgstr ""
"Non, pas très bien. Comme tout le monde ici, j'ai trop perdu. Je ne pense pas "
"pouvoir en revenir un jour. Quelqu'un peut-il être assez fort ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I would rather talk about what I have left: my husband, Stan, and his brother "
"Garry, my best friend.  Without them, I'd be lost myself.  What we've lost is "
"more than anyone should have to think about."
msgstr ""
"Je préfère parler de ce qui me reste : mon mari, Stan, et son frère Garry, "
"mon meilleur ami. Sans eux, je serais moi-même perdue. Ce que nous avons "
"perdu, c'est plus que ce que n'importe qui devrait avoir à penser."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Désolé·e.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Désolé·e.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"…Ash.  His name was Ash, and he was ten years old.  Such a light, a spark.  I "
"wanted to see the man he would grow into.  I… now I can barely say his name.  "
"I miss him so much, every instant.  If I did not have Stan, I would walk out "
"through the barbed wire and join the walking dead."
msgstr ""
"...Ash. Il s'appelait Ash et avait dix ans. Une telle lumière, une telle "
"étincelle. Je voulais voir l'homme qu'il deviendrait. Je... maintenant je "
"peux à peine dire son nom. Il me manque tellement, à chaque instant. Si je "
"n'avais pas Stan, je passerais à travers les barbelés et rejoindrais les "
"morts-vivants."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Tell me more about Ash."
msgstr "Toutes mes condoléances.  Parlez-moi d'Ash."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We've all lost a lot of people.  You can either let yourself die, or learn to "
"survive."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons tous perdu beaucoup de gens. On peut soit se laisser mourir, soit "
"apprendre à survivre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm so sorry, man.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Je suis vraiment désolé/e mec. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I could talk forever, but it's hard to make the words come.  He was so "
"*smart*.  Always on the computer, writing stories and programming silly games "
"in Scratch.  He had a little robotics toy he made walk around and do funny "
"dances.  It was a challenge to make him play with his friends sometimes, he "
"would get so far into himself and buried in that thing.  So tough to be a "
"parent, you know?  It is good for him to write, to learn, but he also needs "
"to socialize and have friends.  He'll grow out… he…"
msgstr ""
"Je pourrais parler indéfiniment, mais c'est difficile de faire venir les "
"mots. Il était si *intelligent*. Toujours sur l'ordinateur, à écrire des "
"histoires et à programmer des jeux idiots en Scratch. Il avait un petit jouet "
"robotique qu'il faisait marcher et danser. C'était parfois un défi de le "
"faire jouer avec ses amis, car il se renfermait tellement sur lui-même qu'il "
"s'enfonçait dans ce jouet. C'est tellement difficile d'être parent, vous "
"savez ? C'est bien qu'il écrive, qu'il apprenne, mais il a aussi besoin de "
"socialiser et d'avoir des amis. Il grandira... il..."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any of his writing?"
msgstr "Avez-vous un de ses écrits ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Of course, yes.  I know this, but it is not so easy, is it?  So many are "
"gone, and I do not know which of the two I would prefer, just yet."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, oui. Je le sais, mais ce n'est pas si facile, n'est-ce pas ? Il y "
"en a tant qui sont partis, et je ne sais pas encore lequel des deux je "
"préférerais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, fine.  Just wallow in it.  I'm out."
msgstr "Oui, d'accord. Il suffit de se vautrer là-dedans. Je me retire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No.  In the evacuation shelter, distracted by grief, I forgot it.  We were "
"rushed onto the bus so quickly, and… well, I don't remember much of that "
"time.  His work was all saved on the hard drive, we thought we could download "
"it from the cloud when we arrived but, well, there is no cloud now.  Even if "
"there were, it would only have his writing, not his little games, his silly "
"voice recordings."
msgstr ""
"Non. Dans l'abri d'évacuation, distraite par le chagrin, je l'ai oublié. Nous "
"avons été précipités dans le bus si rapidement, et... eh bien, je ne me "
"souviens pas de grand-chose de cette période. Son travail était sauvegardé "
"sur le disque dur, nous pensions pouvoir le télécharger à partir du cloud à "
"notre arrivée, mais il n'y a plus de cloud. Même s'il y en avait un, il ne "
"contiendrait que ses écrits, pas ses petits jeux, ni ses enregistrements "
"vocaux idiots."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, now that you mention it, with the back bay cleared I could probably set "
"up back there and start work.  I don't know if I can handle it.  The last "
"time I was back there was the last time I saw… if… if someone were to clean "
"up back there, wipe away some memories, then I could start renovating it into "
"a better living space."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que vous le dites, si la baie arrière est dégagée, je pourrais "
"probablement m'y installer et commencer à travailler. Je ne sais pas si je "
"peux le faire. La dernière fois que j'y suis allé, c'est la dernière fois que "
"j'ai vu... si... si quelqu'un nettoyait l'arrière, effaçait quelques "
"souvenirs, alors je pourrais commencer à le rénover pour en faire un meilleur "
"espace de vie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There isn't much to do with a hammer and a saw here indoors, and working "
"outside is too dangerous.  If we had enough space for me to do some shuffling "
"around, I could build some privacy walls in here.  I tried to set up a bit of "
"a shop in the garage space, but I had to keep taking everything down for "
"caravan loading and unloading and couldn't get anything done.  The caravans "
"bring food, so they get priority, I can't argue with that."
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a pas grand-chose à faire avec un marteau et une scie à l'intérieur, "
"et il est trop dangereux de travailler à l'extérieur. Si nous avions assez "
"d'espace pour que je puisse me déplacer, je pourrais construire des murs "
"d'intimité ici. J'ai essayé d'installer un petit magasin dans le garage, mais "
"j'ai dû tout démonter pour charger et décharger les caravanes et je n'ai rien "
"pu faire. Les caravanes apportent de la nourriture, elles ont donc la "
"priorité, je ne peux pas le nier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you need to get things cleaned up?  Can I help?"
msgstr "De quoi avez-vous besoin pour faire le ménage ? Puis-je vous aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We could put together a little clean up group, but everyone here has terrible "
"memories of that place.  I could not ask anyone here to go back and see the "
"leftovers of people we knew.  Still, it's a big job.  Who here might be able "
"to do it?"
msgstr ""
"Nous pourrions mettre en place un petit groupe de nettoyage, mais tout le "
"monde ici a de terribles souvenirs de cet endroit. Je ne peux pas demander à "
"quiconque ici d'y retourner et de voir les restes de personnes que nous "
"connaissions. Mais c'est un gros travail. Qui ici pourrait s'en charger ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sure there's someone.  Would you like me to ask around?"
msgstr "Je suis sûr qu'il y a quelqu'un. Voulez-vous que je me renseigne ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I am afraid I cannot teach you right now.  Not only do I have no shop, but I "
"do not think I am in a good place for anything so taxing."
msgstr ""
"Je crains de ne pas pouvoir vous enseigner pour le moment. Non seulement je "
"n'ai pas d'atelier, mais je ne pense pas être en état de faire quelque chose "
"d'aussi exigeant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything more I can do to help?"
msgstr "Il y a quelque chose de plus que je peux faire pour vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great!  Let's get started."
msgstr "Parfait!  Commençons."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Let's do this later."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave> Faisons ça plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Everyone agrees this is bad.  Sleeping on a cot on the floor, crowded in with "
"strangers"
msgstr ""
"Tout le monde s'accorde à dire que ce n'est pas bien. Dormir sur un lit de "
"camp à même le sol, entassé avec des inconnus"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but it is a bit better since we cleaned up our dead"
msgstr "mais c'est un peu mieux depuis que nous avons nettoyé nos cadavres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", woken by zombies in the night"
msgstr "réveillé par des zombies dans la nuit"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  To me, though, that is all just a drop in the bucket"
msgstr ". Pour moi, tout cela n'est qu'une goutte d'eau dans l'océan"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  What is killing me is being forced to sit with nothing but my thoughts of "
"what I've lost."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  I have spent so much time, just regretting what I have lost.  Thank you "
"for bringing back what little you could."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was difficult at first, but yes, I did.  It hurts, but it is good.  I am "
"so proud of him.  Would you like to see some… some of what you brought me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, my friend.  I'd love to hear you brag about your boy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds a bit heavy for me right now, let's talk about something else"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not today, I have to get going.  Just glad I was able to help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Boris boots up the laptop and opens a folder labeled 'ART'.  He shows you "
"simple digital paintings, clearly done by an adolescent.  There's nothing "
"terribly remarkable about them except the number: Ash was a prolific creator. "
" Boris goes through several, proudly showing how his son learned little "
"lighting tricks, or reminiscing on the time his son showed him the art.  "
"After a while, he stops commenting and just continues quietly clicking "
"through photos.  He seems different in the glow of the screen, like several "
"years dropped away from his face, despite the deep sadness still etched there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Boris boots up the laptop and opens a folder labeled 'STORY 1'.  In it are "
"numerous text files containing smatterings of stream-of-conscious notes, "
"copy-and-pasted bits of fanfictions, notes about how to write a novel, and "
"more.  The story itself is a handful of poorly fleshed out chapters written "
"with the quality level you'd expect from a grade schooler.  Nonetheless it's "
"quite impressive that there's this much stuff on a single topic.  Boris talks "
"for a while about dinner conversations for weeks that would focus on Ash's "
"ideas for his stories.  After a while, he trails off and just continues "
"flipping through the files, reading silently."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Boris boots up the laptop and opens the videos folder.  He shows you several "
"self-made videos that follow a loose blog style, of an awkward young man "
"talking about his favorite games, interspersed with comments about art and "
"writing.  Boris comments on little events and laughs a few times, before "
"becoming engrossed in his reminiscence."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Leave Boris alone for now.]"
msgstr "[Laisser Boris seul pour le moment]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh.  Right.  It's been a long apocalypse.  What were you saying?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Sorry.  I didn't notice which dialogue option I was selecting.  I'll just "
"back away slowly now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, let's get to work."
msgstr "Ok, mettons-nous au travail."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to hear.  I'm sure everyone will appreciate that place being cleaned up."
msgstr ""
"Ça fait du bien d'entendre ça. Je suis sûr que tout le monde appréciera que "
"cet endroit soit nettoyé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgstr "Trouvez quelqu'un pour nettoyer l'arrière du centre de réfugiés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid ""
"Boris in the refugee center is looking for at least five people to help clean "
"up the back bay."
msgstr ""
"Boris de l'abri du centre de réfugiés veut assembler au moins cinq personnes "
"pour sécuriser le garage à l'arrière."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid ""
"Find a few people able to help clean the back, people without too much trauma "
"there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid ""
"Yes, please.  If you can ask around for someone who can help, I can gather "
"the tools they will need and some payment for them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "You are a kind soul."
msgstr "Vous êtes une âme aimable."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "Ah well.  I can ask around myself, perhaps."
msgstr "Ah ok. Je peux aller demander moi-même, peut-être."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid ""
"Those of us here in the back have too many bad memories, but perhaps someone "
"who didn't come with the original refugee groups would be less burdened."
msgstr ""
"Celleux d'entre nous qui sont à l'arrière ont trop de mauvais souvenirs, mais "
"peut-être que quelqu'un qui n'est pas venu avec les premiers groupes de "
"réfugiés serait moins éprouvé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid "Greetings, my friend.  Have you found anyone?"
msgstr "Bienvenue, mon ami-e. Avez-vous trouvé quelqu'un ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid ""
"This has great promise.  Perhaps something to keep me busy will help.  Here, "
"I found some small money to thank you."
msgstr ""
"C'est très prometteur. Peut-être que quelque chose pour m'occuper m'aidera. "
"J'ai trouvé ici un peu d'argent pour vous remercier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
msgid "I see….  Well I shall get things in order!"
msgstr "Je vois. Et bien je devrais remettre les choses en ordre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid "No worries.  Let me know if you want to try again."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgstr "Ramenez une scie circulaire à Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid ""
"Find a circular saw for Boris.  Smokes might be selling one if it's available "
"in stock."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid "Find a circular saw for Boris."
msgstr "Trouvez une scie circulaire pour Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid ""
"We now have a space to work in, and I have wood and nails to spare.  All I "
"need is a saw.  I would love a table saw and mitre saw, but I can work with a "
"hand held circular saw for now.  I have looked, and what we have is garbage.  "
"Can you bring me a good one?"
msgstr ""
"Nous disposons maintenant d'un espace de travail et j'ai du bois et des clous "
"à revendre. Tout ce dont j'ai besoin, c'est d'une scie. J'aimerais avoir une "
"scie à table et une scie à onglets, mais je peux me contenter d'une scie "
"circulaire manuelle pour l'instant. J'ai cherché, et ce que nous avons est "
"merdique. Pouvez-vous m'en apporter une bonne ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid ""
"It is not hard to find.  I have even seen them for sale at the merchants, but "
"they save them as trade goods and will not give me as a gift."
msgstr ""
"Il n'est pas difficile à trouver. J'en ai même vu en vente chez les "
"marchands, mais ils les gardent comme biens d'échange et ne veulent pas m'en "
"faire cadeau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid "Greetings, my friend.  Have you found a saw I can use?"
msgstr "Bienvenue mon ami-e. Avez-vous trouvé une scie que je pourrais utiliser ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
msgid ""
"Ah, good.  VonWalt is good brand, I had a saw like this at home.  Now I shall "
"set to work, and make myself a shop back there.  Oh yes, here is a little "
"payment I saved."
msgstr ""
"Ah, c'est bien. VonWalt est une bonne marque, j'avais une scie comme ça à la "
"maison. Maintenant, je vais me mettre au travail et me faire un magasin "
"là-bas. Ah oui, voilà un petit paiement que j'ai économisé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgstr "Apportez à Boris les écrits perdus de son fils."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "Find Boris' son's laptop in the evac shelter marked on your map."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez l'ordinateur portable du fils de Boris dans l'abri d'évacuation "
"indiqué sur votre carte."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "Find Boris' son's laptop."
msgstr "Trouvez l'ordinateur portable du fils de Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid ""
"My son, Ash, had a laptop on which he kept his writing.  If you can find it, "
"it would mean so much to me.  I will give you directions to the shelter where "
"he left it.  It was barely a shelter, broken and torn apart.  It should just "
"be on the floor where it was dropped."
msgstr ""
"Mon fils, Ash, avait un ordinateur portable sur lequel il conservait ses "
"écrits. Si vous pouvez le retrouver, cela signifierait beaucoup pour moi. Je "
"vous indiquerai comment vous rendre au refuge où il l'a laissé. C'était à "
"peine un abri, cassé et déchiré. Il devrait juste être sur le sol, là où il a "
"été laissé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "You can tell it is his because he covered it in stickers."
msgstr "Vous pourrez le reconnaître facilement, il est couvert de stickers."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "I know it is a hard thing to hope, but were you able to find Ash's laptop?"
msgstr ""
"Je sais que c'est difficile d'y croire, mais avez-vous réussit à trouver "
"l'ordinateur portable d'Ash ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid ""
"It is so strange to see this again, like a little piece of my old life.  I "
"don't know if I can bring myself to read what's on it yet, but having this "
"piece of him is a great comfort."
msgstr ""
"C'est tellement étrange de le revoir, comme un petit morceau de mon ancienne "
"vie. Je ne sais pas encore si je peux me résoudre à lire ce qu'il y a dessus, "
"mais avoir ce fragment de lui est d'un grand réconfort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
msgid "Even that you tried means a lot to me."
msgstr "Déjà, que vous ayez essayer compte beaucoup pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Ash's laptop computer"
msgid_plural "Ash's laptop computers"
msgstr[0] "ordinateur portable de Ash"
msgstr[1] "ordinateurs portables de Ash"
msgstr[2] "ordinateurs portables de Ash"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Description of "Ash's laptop computer"
msgid ""
"A small, somewhat worn-out laptop computer.  The flip-top is decorated with "
"various stickers."
msgstr ""
"Un petit ordinateur portable un peu usé. Le flip-top est décoré de divers "
"autocollants."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Dana Nunez"
msgstr "Dana Nunez"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I spoke to the foreman over at Tacoma Ranch.  If you're willing to put in the "
"work, they'll find some work for you over there."
msgstr ""
"J'ai parlé au contremaître du Tacoma Ranch. Si vous êtes prêt à travailler, "
"ils vous trouveront du travail là-bas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I spoke to your husband about getting you a job at the Tacoma Ranch.  What "
"would you think about that?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai parlé à votre mari de vous trouver un emploi au Tacoma Ranch. Qu'en "
"pensez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Your husband said to ask you what you'd think about getting out of this place "
"and coming to work for me at my own camp."
msgstr ""
"Votre mari m'a dit de vous demander ce que vous penseriez de quitter cet "
"endroit et de venir travailler pour moi dans mon propre camp."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You seem pretty unhappy about the quality of your bread.  Is there something "
"I can do to help?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air peu satisfaite de la qualité de votre pain. Est-ce que je "
"pourrais vous aider avec quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got your sourdough."
msgstr "J'ai votre culture de levain."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got any more bread I can trade flour for?"
msgstr "Vous avez plus de pain à échanger contre de la farine?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a pale woman with a broad, friendly face.  She seems to start opening "
"with a wide grin, then notices her somber surroundings and dials it back to a "
"pleasant smile.  \"Hi there.  I'm Dana, Dana Nunez.  Nice to see a new face.\""
msgstr ""
"*une femme pâle au visage large et amical.  Elle semble commencer par un "
"large sourire, puis remarque que son les conditions laissant à désirer et le "
"ramène à un sourire agréable.  \"Bonjour.  Je suis Dana, Dana Nunez.  Ravie "
"de voir un nouveau visage.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Dana, hey?  Nice to meet you.  How are things here?"
msgstr "Dana, hein?  Ravi⸱e de vous rencontrer.  Comment vont les choses ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Dana.  What's your story?"
msgstr "Ravi⸱e de vous rencontrer, Dana.  Quelle est votre histoire?  "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Dana, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Dana, ravi-e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*beams at you as you approach.  \""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*turns from her conversation with Pablo, and smiles as she sees you.  \""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello, nice to see you again.  What brings you around today?"
msgstr "Bonjour, ravi-e de vous revoir. Qu'est-ce qui vous amène aujourd'hui ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's good to see you're still around."
msgstr "C'est chouette de voir que vous êtes toujours dans le coin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Dana, nice to see you too.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Dana, content-e de vous voir également. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was working in a nice restaurant as a baker, until <the_cataclysm>.  I was "
"pregnant, and it was getting close to time to go on mat leave; lots of time "
"on my feet, getting up stupid-early to make pastries, you know.  Because of "
"the pregnancy we were evacuated early and shipped out this way, but our bus "
"was attacked in the chaos.  We managed to escape, but had to hike the rest of "
"the way, with the Singhs and a few other refugees that didn't make it.  I "
"lost the baby.  It wasn't a good time."
msgstr ""
"Je travaillais dans un bon restaurant en tant que boulangère, jusqu'à  "
"<the_cataclysm>. J'étais enceinte, et le moment de partir en congé de "
"maternité approchait ; j'ai passé beaucoup de temps debout, à me lever très "
"tôt pour préparer des pâtisseries, vous savez. En raison de ma grossesse, "
"nous avons été évacués plus tôt que prévu et envoyés par ici, mais notre bus "
"a été attaqué dans le chaos. Nous avons réussi à nous échapper, mais nous "
"avons dû faire le reste du chemin à pied, avec les Singhs et quelques autres "
"réfugiés qui n'ont pas survécu. J'ai perdu le bébé. Ce n'était pas une bonne "
"période."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you done any baking lately?"
msgstr "Vous avez cuit quelque chose récemment?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Bye, Dana."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  Au revoir Dana."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 flour] That sounds like a great deal, here's some flour for you."
msgstr "[8 unités de farine] Ça me semble être une bonne affaire, voilà votre farine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 merch] I got two merch for you."
msgstr "[2 merch] J'ai deux merch pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 flour] Thanks for cutting me a deal, here's the six cups of flour."
msgstr "[6 unités de farine]  Merci pour l'affaire, voilà six tasses de farine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 merch] All right, one merch as agreed."
msgstr "[1 merch] Une merch comme l'on s'était mis d'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not since I last saw you, sorry.  Come by tomorrow and I'll try to keep a "
"loaf set aside for you, but they disappear fast."
msgstr ""
"Pas depuis la dernière fois que je vous ai vu, désolée. Passez demain et "
"j'essaierai de vous réserver un pain, mais ils disparaissent vite."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I sure do, if you've got the flour or the merch for me, I'd be happy to trade "
"you another loaf."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, si vous avez de la farine ou des merch pour moi, je serais heureuse "
"de vous échanger un autre pain."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do a bit.  I got a sourdough starter going almost as soon as I arrived, and "
"it's making passable bread already.  I cooked some up yesterday actually, I "
"could probably trade a loaf of fresh bread for, say, about eight cups of "
"flour, or two merch."
msgstr ""
"Je le fais un peu. J'ai démarré un levain presque dès mon arrivée, et il fait "
"déjà du pain passable. J'en ai fait cuire un peu hier en fait, je pourrais "
"probablement échanger une miche de pain frais contre, disons, environ huit "
"tasses de farine, ou deux merchs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[BARTER] Is that the lowest you can go?  I'd love some bread, but I can't "
"quite make that."
msgstr ""
"[MARCHANDAGE] Vous ne pouvez pas baisser le prix un peu plus? J'aimerais bien "
"acheter du pain, mais je ne peux pas vraiment à ce prix."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[BARTER] Aw, c'mon.  I rescued Landough, can't you cut me a little deal?"
msgstr ""
"[MARCHANDAGE] Je ne peux pas avoir une petite réduction après avoir sauvé "
"Landough?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, can we talk about something else?"
msgstr "Merci, peut-on parler d'autre chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll look into that.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Je vais regarder ça. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, it's not something I can bend on.  I don't make a big profit off this, "
"I use what I get to make more bread.  If I cut you a deal, I'll run out of "
"supplies."
msgstr ""
"Désolé, ce n'est pas quelque chose que je peux négocier. Je ne fais pas de "
"gros bénéfices avec ça, j'utilise ce que j'obtiens pour faire plus de pain. "
"Si je vous fais un marché, je serai à court de provisions."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, but I think I'll pass.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Merci, mais je vais passer mon tour. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, fine.  Six cups of flour, or one merch.  I'm not going any lower, I got a "
"business to run here."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. Six tasses de farine, ou un merch. Je ne descendrai pas plus bas, "
"j'ai une affaire à gérer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know, I think I changed my mind.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Vous savez, je crois que j'ai changé d'avis. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's kind of you to say.  I'm doing my best to move on… it hurts, but in "
"the scale of things it could be worse.  Pablo and I still have each other, "
"that's a lot more than most."
msgstr ""
"C'est gentil de votre part.  Je fais de mon mieux pour aller de l'avant… ça "
"fait mal, mais dans le contexte actuel, ça pourrait être pire.  Pablo et moi "
"sommes toujours là l'un pour l'autre, c'est beaucoup plus que la plupart des "
"gens."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great, here's a loaf of the best damn sourdough bread in the world.  I used "
"to make that claim as a joke, but I feel like now there's a fighting chance "
"nobody else can beat me."
msgstr ""
"Super, voici une miche du meilleur pain au levain du monde. J'avais "
"l'habitude de faire cette affirmation en plaisantant, mais j'ai l'impression "
"que maintenant, il y a une chance que personne d'autre ne puisse me battre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice.  Enjoy the mighty bounty of Landough Calrisean."
msgstr "Joli. Profitez de l'abondance du Landough Calrisean."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Here you go, from the family recipe."
msgstr "Et voilà, avec la recette familiale."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hope you enjoy it as much as I do, this is the best damn bread in the world "
"now."
msgstr ""
"J'espère que vous l'apprécierez autant que moi, c'est le meilleur pain du "
"monde maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great, here's a loaf of my locally-famous, not-very-mature sourdough.  It's "
"not too bad honestly.  Everyone here seems to like it."
msgstr ""
"Super, voici un pain de mon fameux levain local, pas très mature. "
"Honnêtement, il n'est pas trop mauvais. Tout le monde ici semble l'aimer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It smells awesome.  <end_talking_leave>  Thanks!"
msgstr "Ça sent super bon. <end_talking_leave> Merci !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure.  If you really like this second-rate bread, you could risk your life "
"for something actually worth it.  I left my actual sourdough starter back in "
"the bakery where I worked.  That baby is a hundred years old, and has been in "
"my family for generations… if you can bring him to me, I'll bake you the "
"finest bread you've ever had."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr. Si vous aimez vraiment ce pain de seconde zone, vous pouvez risquer "
"votre vie pour quelque chose qui en vaut la peine. J'ai laissé mon véritable "
"levain à la boulangerie où je travaillais. Ce bébé a cent ans, il est dans ma "
"famille depuis des générations... si tu peux me le ramener, je te ferai le "
"meilleur pain que tu n'aies jamais mangé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why not?  I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Pourquoi pas?  Je verrai ce que je peux faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe not right now.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Peut-être pas maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Take care of yourself out there.\"  She jots down directions to her bakery "
"and hands them to you.  \"His name is Landough, Landough Calrisean.  He'll be "
"in the right-hand fridge, in a jar with a picture of the Millennium Falcon on "
"it.  And listen, when you bring my sourdough back, I don't want to see a "
"scratch on him, you understand?"
msgstr ""
"Prenez soin de vous dehors.\" Elle note les indications pour se rendre à sa "
"boulangerie et vous les tend. \"Son nom est Landough, Landough Calrisean. Il "
"sera dans le frigo de droite, dans un bocal avec une image du Faucon "
"Millenium dessus. Et écoutez, quand vous me ramènerez mon levain, je ne veux "
"pas qu'il ait une seule égratignure, vous comprenez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  Sure."
msgstr "Ok. Bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"All right, old buddy.  You know, I know what he means to you.  I'll take good "
"care of him, so that he won't get a scratch."
msgstr ""
"D'accord, mon vieux. Je sais ce qu'il représente pour toi. Je prendrai bien "
"soin de lui, pour qu'il n'ait pas une égratignure."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*takes the jar from you eagerly, studying it with care.  \"He's been through "
"a lot, hasn't he.  Poor guy.  Aw man.\"  She turns back to you, beaming.  "
"\"Oh, you will not regret this.  He may not look like much, but he's got it "
"where it counts, kid.  It's gonna take me a few days to revive him after "
"being abandoned so long, but he'll be operational soon and then you can come "
"back for some real bread.\"  She frowns.  \"I don't really have much to give "
"you in return, but I'll cut you a deal on bread if that helps.\""
msgstr ""
"*prend le pot avec impatience et l'étudie avec soin. \"Il a traversé beaucoup "
"d'épreuves, n'est-ce pas ? Mon pauvre ami. Oh là là.\" Elle se retourne vers "
"vous, rayonnante. \"Oh, vous ne le regretterez pas. Il n'a peut-être pas "
"l'air de grand-chose, mais il en a là où ça compte, petit. Il va me falloir "
"quelques jours pour le ranimer après avoir été abandonné si longtemps, mais "
"il sera bientôt opérationnel et tu pourras revenir pour du vrai pain.\" Elle "
"fronce les sourcils. \"Je n'ai pas grand-chose à te donner en échange, mais "
"je te propose un arrangement sur le pain si ça peut t'aider.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll hold you to that."
msgstr "Je vous le promets."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just glad to help."
msgstr "Juste content·e d'avoir pu aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, not quite yet.  Landough was in pretty rough shape.  No fault of "
"yours, it was no good having him cooped up in a dank fridge for that long… "
"and I think my apprentice baker may have fucked with him before the Cataclysm "
"too.  He'd better hope he's a zombie now, because if I see him alive… anyway, "
"it's gonna take a few more feeds before I can get him ready for prime time, "
"check back in a couple days."
msgstr ""
"Désolée, pas tout à fait. Landough était dans un sale état. Ce n'est pas de "
"votre faute, ce n'était pas bon de le laisser enfermé dans un frigo pendant "
"si longtemps... et je pense que mon apprenti boulanger l'a peut-être aussi "
"bousillé avant le Cataclysme. Il ferait mieux d'espérer qu'il soit un zombie "
"maintenant, parce que si je le vois vivant... Quoi qu'il en soit, il va "
"falloir attendre encore un peu avant qu'il soit prêt pour le prime time, "
"revenez dans quelques jours."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things are tense at the best of times.  We didn't choose this crowd, so not "
"all of us really get along.  I like Jenny and Fatima, and the three of us are "
"kind of lucky to have friends here, but that doesn't make up for us being a "
"bunch of unfamiliar faces crammed into a tiny space.  Someone's gonna murder "
"someone soon, mark my words."
msgstr ""
"Les choses sont tendues dans le meilleur des cas. Nous n'avons pas choisi ce "
"groupe et nous ne nous entendons pas tous. J'aime bien Jenny et Fatima, et "
"nous avons toutes les trois de la chance d'avoir des amis ici, mais cela ne "
"compense pas le fait que nous sommes une bande de visages inconnus entassés "
"dans un espace minuscule. Quelqu'un va bientôt assassiner quelqu'un, "
"croyez-moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh.  I've made a few friends here, but not so much as I'd stick around here "
"with no future prospects, hoping someone downstairs dies to make room for me. "
" It does sound nice, if they're looking for more workers."
msgstr ""
"Hum. Je me suis fait quelques potes ici mais pas au point de rester ici sans "
"perspectives d'avenir, en espérant que quelqu'un en bas meure pour me faire "
"de la place. Ça a l'air sympa, s'ils cherchent plus de travailleurs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Dana_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll look into that.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Je vais regarder ça. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All right.  I've taken some time to think about it, and I'm willing to go.  "
"I'm sure they'll have use for a baker over there, after all, and if I don't "
"get out of this place there's a very real chance I'm going to snap.  You can "
"go let Pablo know first hand, if you want; he's been pretty excited about the "
"idea."
msgstr ""
"D'accord. J'ai pris le temps d'y réfléchir et je suis prête à partir. Je suis "
"sûr qu'ils auront besoin d'une boulangère là-bas, après tout, et si je ne "
"sors pas d'ici, il y a de fortes chances que je craque. Tu peux informer "
"Pablo directement, si tu veux ; il a été très enthousiaste à l'idée."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, I'll go tell him.  Cool!"
msgstr "Bien sûr, je vais lui dire. Cool !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pablo's a little quicker on the trigger than I am.  We're trying to have a "
"baby, did you know that?  It's a bit crazy in this world, but I won't change "
"those plans.  Tell you what: if your camp has access to a doctor and some "
"medical facilities, in case I actually can get pregnant again, I would "
"consider getting out of here and signing up."
msgstr ""
"Pablo est un peu plus rapide que moi sur la gâchette. Nous essayons d'avoir "
"un bébé, le saviez-vous ? C'est un peu fou dans ce monde, mais je ne "
"changerai pas ces plans. Je vais vous dire : si votre camp a accès à un "
"médecin et à des installations médicales, au cas où je pourrais à nouveau "
"tomber enceinte, j'envisagerais de partir d'ici et de m'inscrire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgstr "Trouvez la culture de levain familiale de Dana"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid "I could get my real sourdough starter…"
msgstr "Si seulement je pouvais récupérer ma culture de levain familiale…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"If you really like this second-rate bread, you could risk your life for "
"something actually worth it.  I left my actual sourdough starter back in the "
"bakery where I worked.  That baby is a hundred years old, and has been in my "
"family for generations… if you can bring him to me, I'll bake you the finest "
"bread you've ever had."
msgstr ""
"Si vous aimez vraiment ce pain de seconde zone, vous pourriez risquer votre "
"vie pour quelque chose qui en vaille la peine. J'ai laissé mon véritable "
"levain dans la boulangerie où je travaillais. Ce bébé a cent ans, il est dans "
"ma famille depuis des générations... si tu peux me le ramener, je te ferai le "
"meilleur pain que tu n'aies jamais mangé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"Take care of yourself out there.  And listen, when you bring my sourdough "
"back, I don't want to see a scratch on him, you understand?"
msgstr ""
"Prenez soin de vous. Et écoutez, quand vous me ramènerez mon levain, je ne "
"veux pas voir une seule égratignure sur lui, vous comprenez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"I can understand why you think you wouldn't want to risk your life for a "
"bread starter.  You haven't tried that bread."
msgstr ""
"Je peux comprendre que vous pensiez ne pas vouloir risquer votre vie pour une "
"levure de pain. Vous n'avez pas encore essayé ce pain."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"He'll be in the right-hand fridge, in a jar with a picture of the Millennium "
"Falcon on it."
msgstr ""
"Il sera dans le réfrigérateur de droite, dans un bocal avec une photo du "
"Faucon Millenium dessus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid "So, you seen my sourdough starter?"
msgstr "Alors, tu as vu mon levain ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"Oh, you will not regret this.  He may not look like much, but he's got it "
"where it counts, kid.  It's gonna take me a few days to revive him after "
"being abandoned so long, but he'll be operational soon and then you can come "
"back for some real bread."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne le regretterez pas. Il n'a peut-être pas l'air de grand-chose, mais "
"il en a là où ça compte, petit. Il me faudra quelques jours pour le ranimer "
"après avoir été abandonné si longtemps, mais il sera bientôt opérationnel et "
"tu pourras alors revenir pour du vrai pain."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid "This ain't it."
msgstr "C'est pas ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Dana's family sourdough culture"
msgid ""
"I am not sure if I'm gonna make it through the Cataclysm without my special "
"jar of goop."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas si je vais réussir à traverser le Cataclysme sans mon bocal "
"spécial de pâte."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Dana's family sourdough starter"
msgid_plural "Dana's family sourdough starter"
msgstr[0] "Levain familial de Dana"
msgstr[1] "Levain familial de Dana"
msgstr[2] "Levain familial de Dana"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Description of "Dana's family sourdough starter"
msgid ""
"This crusty old jar has a glow-in-the-dark Millennium Falcon decal on the "
"side, and a label that reads, \"Landough Calrisean.  Dana's.  Do not touch on "
"pain of death\".  It's been abandoned for some time and doesn't look like it "
"could be readily salvaged as a sourdough culture, but maybe an experienced "
"sourdough baker could manage it."
msgstr ""
"Ce vieux bocal rouillé est orné d'une décalcomanie du Faucon Millenium "
"phosphorescente sur le côté et d'une étiquette sur laquelle on peut lire « "
"Landough Calrisean. À Dana. Ne pas toucher sous peine de mort ». Il a été "
"abandonné depuis un certain temps et ne semble pas pouvoir être récupéré "
"comme culture de levain, mais peut-être qu'un boulanger au levain expérimenté "
"pourrait y arriver."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Dana's sourdough bread"
msgid_plural "Dana's sourdough bread"
msgstr[0] "Levain de Dana"
msgstr[1] "Levain de Dana"
msgstr[2] "Levain de Dana"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#. ~ Description of "Dana's sourdough bread"
msgid "This round loaf of bread has a thick, dark crust, and smells very enticing."
msgstr ""
"Le pain au levain de Dana. Ce pain rond a une croûte épaisse et foncée, et "
"son odeur est très alléchante."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*sits in a surprisingly well-built room made of lovingly assembled cardboard "
"boxes.  The area is quite clean and cozy.  The whole building is built on top "
"of cargo pallets, insulated with scraps, and waterproofed with plastic.  It "
"shows an unexpected amount of design prowess.  \"Hello, my noble knight "
"errant,\" Dave intones, his voice solemn."
msgstr ""
"*s'assoit dans une pièce étonnamment bien construite, faite de cartons "
"assemblés avec amour. L'endroit est assez propre et confortable. L'ensemble "
"du bâtiment est construit sur des palettes de marchandises, isolé avec des "
"chutes et imperméabilisé avec du plastique. Il témoigne d'une prouesse "
"inattendue en matière de design. « Bonjour, mon/ma noble chevalier-e errant-e "
"», dit Dave d'une voix solennelle."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "  \"We hope our gift to you will help repay our great debt.\""
msgstr ""
" \"Nous espérons que notre cadeau vous aidera à rembourser notre grande "
"dette.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"  \"We owe you a great debt for your actions of the past.  Some day, we shall "
"repay it.  Until then, you are welcome here, now and always.\""
msgstr ""
"\"Nous avons une grande dette envers vous pour vos actions passées. Un jour, "
"nous la rembourserons. En attendant, vous êtes les bienvenu-es ici, "
"maintenant et toujours.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Dave.  You seem different."
msgstr "Salut Dave.  Vous semblez différent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are things going up here on the roof?"
msgstr "Comment ça se passe sur le toit?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Always good to catch up, Dave.  Keep on being you."
msgstr "Toujours un plaisir de se revoir, Dave. Continue à être toi-même."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You said something about a gift?"
msgstr "Vous avez dit quelque chose à propos d'un cadeau ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*nods deeply.  \"We are, for where we once were in chaos, now we are at "
"peace.  In time, this shall bring wisdom, but we must ponder on these great "
"changes.\""
msgstr ""
"*hoche la tête fortement. \"Nous sommes, car là où nous étions dans le chaos, "
"nous sommes maintenant en paix. Avec le temps, cela nous apportera la "
"sagesse, mais nous devons réfléchir à ces grands changements.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Were you like this, uh, before?  Did you use to have a doctor or anything?"
msgstr "Étiez-vous comme ça, euh, avant ? Aviez-vous un médecin ou autre chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We were… I… we can scarcely remember those times.\"  Dave looks pained.  "
"\"No, we had no doctor.  We didn't need one.  We had a job and… and… we don't "
"like to talk about this."
msgstr ""
"Nous étions… je… nous nous souvenons à peine de cette époque.\"  Dave a l'air "
"peiné.  \"Non, nous n'avions pas de médecin.  Nous n'en avions pas besoin.  "
"Nous avions un travail et… et… nous n'aimons pas en parler."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come on, Dave.  We're friends.  I won't use this against you or anything."
msgstr ""
"Allez Dave. Nous sommes des amis. Je n'utiliserais pas ça contre vous ou "
"quelque chose comme ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*winces.  \"It is true.  You have earned some truth, but we… we find it hard "
"to give.  We had a job, an education.  Prestige.  It is all very faint now.\" "
" He touches a stainless steel ring on his pinky finger, looking lost in "
"thought.  \"We don't know why that man left, and this one remains.  Perhaps "
"that is some wisdom that will come with time, or perhaps it is a door best "
"left closed.\""
msgstr ""
"*winces. \"C'est vrai. Vous avez mérité une certaine vérité, mais nous... "
"nous avons du mal à la donner. Nous avions un travail, une éducation. Du "
"prestige. Tout cela s'est évanoui maintenant. \"Il touche une bague en acier "
"inoxydable à son petit doigt, l'air perdu dans ses pensées. \"Nous ne savons "
"pas pourquoi cet homme est parti et pourquoi celui-ci est resté. Peut-être "
"est-ce une sagesse qui viendra avec le temps, ou peut-être est-ce une porte "
"qu'il vaut mieux laisser fermée.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*gestures about his new home.  \"We have everything we wanted.  They cannot "
"see us here, and our mind is at peace.  We go outside as we need, and the "
"safety we have received here stays with us, as long as we are careful about "
"it.  In time, perhaps we will again have need of your noble services.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il montre sa nouvelle maison. \"Nous avons tout ce que nous voulions. Ils ne "
"peuvent pas nous voir ici, et nous avons l'esprit tranquille. Nous sortons "
"quand nous en avons besoin, et la sécurité que nous avons reçue ici reste "
"avec nous, tant que nous y prenons garde. Avec le temps, nous aurons "
"peut-être à nouveau besoin de vos nobles services.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem different."
msgstr "Vous semblez different."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You know, this place is surprisingly nice, for a cardboard fortress."
msgstr ""
"Vous savez, cet endroit est étonnamment agréable pour une forteresse en "
"carton."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*bows deeply.  \"Thank you.  Our expertise with the most sacred of materials "
"comes from a past long gone.\"  He gazes off into the distance, lost in "
"thought.  You wait, but he doesn't talk again."
msgstr ""
"*s'incline profondément. « Merci. Notre expertise avec les matériaux les plus "
"sacrés vient d'un passé lointain. » Il regarde au loin, perdu dans ses "
"pensées. Vous attendez, mais il ne parle plus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Uh, you there?"
msgstr "Euh, vous êtes là?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You've given us an idea, a way we could repay a small fraction of your aid.  "
"Come back in a day, and your blessing will be here for you."
msgstr ""
"Vous nous avez donné une idée, un moyen de rembourser une petite fraction de "
"votre aide. Revenez dans un jour, et votre bénédiction sera là pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you in a day, then."
msgstr "On se voit dans un jour, donc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Make sure you don't let the sandman in.  He can't be trusted."
msgstr ""
"Veillez à ne pas laisser entrer le marchand de sable. On ne peut pas lui "
"faire confiance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Indeed, my knight.  I was hesitant to grant you this power, but you have "
"proven your worth and fealty many times over.  Make sure it does not fall "
"into the wrong hands.  May it help you on your journey."
msgstr ""
"En effet, mon/ma chevalier/ère. J'hésitais à t'accorder ce pouvoir, mais tu "
"as prouvé ta valeur et ta loyauté à maintes reprises. Veille à ce qu'il ne "
"tombe pas entre de mauvaises mains. Qu'il t'aide dans ton voyage."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Take the gift.]"
msgstr "[Prend le cadeau.]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Draco Dune"
msgstr "Draco Dune"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well now, good to see another new face!  Welcome to the center, friend, I'm "
"Draco."
msgstr "Ça fait plaisir de voir un nouveau visage! Bienvenue au centre, je suis Draco."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Draco."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Draco."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Draco, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Draco, ravi·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Draco, how are you doing?"
msgstr "Salut Draco. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi again, Draco, nice to see you too."
msgstr "Rebonjour Draco, ça me fait aussi du bien de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Draco, nice to see you too.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Draco, ravi/e de te voir également."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nice to meet you too.  What brings you to these parts?  Got any stories to "
"share?  Happy ones, hopefully… we've had our fill of sadness around here."
msgstr ""
"Enchanté de vous rencontrer également. Qu'est-ce qui vous amène ici?  Vous "
"avez des histoires à partager?  Des histoires heureuses, j'espère… nous avons "
"eu notre dose de tristesse ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about you, how're you doing?"
msgstr "Et vous? Comment allez-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, it's tough everywhere.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Ouais, c'est dur par ici. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, look at you.  Asking after random folks like some sort of shepherd!  "
"No, don't take offense now… I mean it well.  We could use more folks askin' "
"after other folks.  I figure it makes the world go round, now, more than "
"ever.  I'm well, friend, considering I have both of my legs and much of my "
"health left to me.  A bit of pain in the back, but can't really complain much "
"if that's the worst of it, right?  You look like you've had a story of your "
"own to tell, just getting here.  I'm writing it in my imagination right now.  "
"Fought through countless hordes, run ragged, chased at every turn, yeah, no "
"thank-you any more of that for me!"
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, regarde-toi. Demander des renseignements à des gens au hasard comme "
"une sorte de berger ! Non, ne vous offusquez pas... Je suis sincère. Nous "
"aurions besoin de plus de gens qui s'occupent d'autres gens. Je pense que ça "
"fait tourner le monde, maintenant, plus que jamais. Je vais bien, mon ami/e, "
"si l'on considère qu'il me reste mes deux jambes et une bonne partie de ma "
"santé. J'ai un peu mal au dos, mais je ne peux pas vraiment me plaindre si "
"c'est le pire, n'est-ce pas ? Vous avez l'air d'avoir une histoire à "
"raconter, rien que pour arriver ici. Je l'écris en ce moment même dans mon "
"imagination. Se battre contre d'innombrables hordes, courir à toutes jambes, "
"se faire pourchasser à chaque tournant, ouais, plus de merci pour moi !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about you, what's your story?"
msgstr "Et vous? Quelle est votre histoire?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No more indeed."
msgstr "Pas plus en effet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh you don't have time for all that, do you?  Well, I'll give you the short "
"version.  I've gotten kinda tired of it in the telling.  Frankly, it's not as "
"heroic, not as inspiring, not as tragic, and certainly not as funny as some "
"of the tales around here.  But it's mine, ya know?  I'm a musician.  Guitar's "
"my baby.  You like folk and the blues, friend?  Well, that was my bag and I "
"sure could please my own ear with em, anyway.  Folks who's bein' generous "
"might also say it pleased theirs.  Problem is, I seem to be between guitars "
"right now, you know?  Temporarily guitar-light, if you get my saying.  "
"Problem is, in the run for my life, I had to use old Jasmine as a bit of a "
"billy club.  Had to curb some rowdy dudes on my way here.  It was her or me, "
"you understand?  You wouldn't begrudge a man breakin' his instrument to save "
"his life, would ya?"
msgstr ""
"Oh, vous n'avez pas le temps pour tout cela, n'est-ce pas ? Eh bien, je vais "
"vous donner la version courte. Je me suis un peu lassé de cette histoire. "
"Franchement, ce n'est pas aussi héroïque, pas aussi inspirant, pas aussi "
"tragique et certainement pas aussi drôle que certains des récits que l'on "
"trouve ici. Mais c'est la mienne, vous savez ? Je suis musicien. La guitare "
"est mon bébé. Tu aimes le folk et le blues, mon ami ? Eh bien, c'était mon "
"domaine et je pouvais certainement plaire à mon oreille avec eux, de toute "
"façon. Les gens qui sont généreux pourraient aussi dire que ça leur plaisait. "
"Le problème, c'est que j'ai l'impression d'être entre deux guitares en ce "
"moment. Temporairement à court de guitare, si vous voyez ce que je veux dire. "
"Le problème, c'est que dans la course à la vie, j'ai dû me servir du vieux "
"Jasmine comme d'une sorte de gourdin. J'ai dû freiner des gars turbulents sur "
"mon chemin. C'était elle ou moi, vous comprenez ? Vous ne reprocheriez pas à "
"un homme de briser son instrument pour sauver sa vie, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I would've done the same.  Nobody around here has a guitar?"
msgstr "Je pense que j'aurais fait pareil. Personne dans le coin n'a de guitare ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, yes I would… you monster."
msgstr "Oui oui je le ferais… monstre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Would you believe that they don't!  Not a one in the whole place.  Well, "
"maybe downstairs, but that's a different matter, isn't it?  Say, you're not "
"planning on sticking around, right?  You're a free-roller, not a settler, "
"seems like to me.  Don't know if I could beg or cajole you into maybe keepin' "
"an ear out for a new guitar for me?  There gotta still be plenty out there "
"not gettin' any love these days.  Whattya say?  Help an old man play some "
"blues?  Would be good to have some real music around this place.  Be good for "
"PEOPLE, you know what I'm sayin'?"
msgstr ""
"Croyez-moi, ils n'en ont pas ! Pas un seul dans tout cet endroit. Enfin, "
"peut-être en bas, mais c'est une autre histoire, non ? Vous n'avez pas "
"l'intention de rester ici, n'est-ce pas ? Vous êtes un resquilleur, pas un "
"colon, il me semble. Je ne sais pas si je pourrais vous supplier ou vous "
"cajoler pour que vous soyez à l'affût d'une nouvelle guitare pour moi ? Il "
"doit y en avoir encore beaucoup qui ne sont pas aimées en ce moment. "
"Qu'est-ce que tu en dis ? Aider un vieil homme à jouer du blues ? Ce serait "
"bien d'avoir de la vraie musique ici. Ce serait bon pour les gens, tu vois ce "
"que je veux dire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where would we be without music?"
msgstr "Où en serions nous sans musique ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You're aware that the world has ended, right?  I've got real problems to deal "
"with.  You're on your own."
msgstr ""
"Vous êtes au courant que c'est la fin du monde ? J'ai des vrais problèmes à "
"gérer. Tu es seul(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Let me ask you something.  What type are you?"
msgstr "Laisse-moi te poser une question. Tu es de quel type ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Uhh, what do you mean?"
msgstr "Euh, qu'est-ce que tu veux dire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll tell you what type I am."
msgstr "Je te dirai de quel type je suis."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, not playing this game."
msgstr "Non, je ne vais pas jouer à ce jeu là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know, what kinda person are you?  What motivates you?"
msgstr "Tu sais, quel genre de personne es-tu ? qu'est-ce qui te motive ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Leaving."
msgstr "Je pars."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So then, what type are you?"
msgstr "Et donc, tu es de quel type ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The 'just getting by' type."
msgstr "Le type \"je passe juste par là\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The serious type."
msgstr "Le type sérieux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The zany type."
msgstr "Le genre loufoque."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I fight stuff."
msgstr "Je combat des trucs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I want to see it all."
msgstr "Je veux tout voir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The 'doesn't have time for this' type."
msgstr "Le type \"j'ai pas le temps pour ça\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me too!  You can understand how folks be wantin' some liveliness in these "
"times.  Some music sure would help with that.  Damn, I miss it.  All I hear "
"is those MP3 players with their tin-can drum machines and whiny vocals.  Help "
"me find a guitar and we'll really get this place smokin'!"
msgstr ""
"Moi aussi ! On peut comprendre que les gens aient envie d'un peu de vie par "
"les temps qui courent. Un peu de musique y contribuerait certainement. Bon "
"sang, ça me manque. Tout ce que j'entends, ce sont ces lecteurs MP3 avec "
"leurs boîtes à rythmes en fer-blanc et leurs voix pleurnichardes. Aide-moi à "
"trouver une guitare et on va vraiment faire chauffer cet endroit !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could be persuaded."
msgstr "Je pourrais être persuadé·e."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's called dub-step and I like it.  Goodbye, old man."
msgstr "Ça s'appelle de la dub-step et j'aime ça. Au revoir, vieux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me too!  Times are hard for folks and that's no laughing matter.  People need "
"some normality in these times.  Some reminders of how things used to be.  I "
"think a sing-along or two could do folks good."
msgstr ""
"Moi aussi ! Les temps sont durs pour les gens et il n'y a pas de quoi rire. "
"Les gens ont besoin d'un peu de normalité dans ces moments-là. Des rappels de "
"ce qu'étaient les choses autrefois. Je pense qu'un ou deux chants pourraient "
"faire du bien aux gens."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Couldn't hurt."
msgstr "Ça ne peut pas faire de mal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't need to hear amateur-hour karaoke around here.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Je n'ai pas besoin d'entendre du karaoké d'amateur ici. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me too!  I did stand-up comedy at a club once.  Well, outside a club anyway.  "
"You know what'd be funny?  Next time one of those stupid ferals starts "
"running around chasing after a squirrel or something, if I had me a guitar I "
"could play the Benny Hill tune and get everybody crackin' up.  Places needs "
"some laughter badly."
msgstr ""
"Moi aussi ! J'ai fait du stand-up dans un club une fois. Enfin, en dehors "
"d'un club en tout cas. Tu sais ce qui serait drôle ? La prochaine fois qu'un "
"de ces stupides animaux sauvages se met à courir après un écureuil ou quelque "
"chose comme ça, si j'avais une guitare, je pourrais jouer l'air de Benny Hill "
"et faire craquer tout le monde. Les lieux ont vraiment besoin de rire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That'd be awesome."
msgstr "Ça serait super."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, wouldn't be so funny when Zed heard all the sound and broke in.  Be "
"responsible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me too.  It's fight a stay afloat in these times.  Some music would lift all "
"spirits, though, don't you think?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you play heavy metal on an acoustic guitar?"
msgstr "Est-ce que tu sais jouer du heavy-métal sur une guitare acoustique ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Boring.  I'm going to go destroy something."
msgstr "Chiant. Je vais détruire un truc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me too!  For now, anyway, that's not really possible for me.  I mean, I guess "
"you know better than me about that.  Man, I used to travel all around.  Saw "
"halfa the States with my guitar on my back.  Now, though, well, I think I'll "
"stay inside til this all flies over."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I could help with something?"
msgstr "Je pourrais peut-être aider avec quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well then, I'll leave you here where it's safe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Man, just imagine what I could do with a new guitar."
msgstr "Dommage, imaginez juste ce que je pourrais faire avec une nouvelle guitare."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk about getting you that guitar."
msgstr "Parlons de te trouver cette guitare."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've been thinking about that deal you mentioned."
msgstr "J'ai réfléchi à ce deal que vous avez mentionné."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything you buying or selling, by chance?"
msgstr "Tu as quelque chose à vendre ou à acheter, par chance ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know any tunes good to dance to?"
msgstr "Est-ce que tu connais des sons sur lesquels danser ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you around, Draco."
msgstr "À la prochaine, Draco."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well now, my friend-o!  You just asked a mighty fine question.  Folks have "
"been missing the little things in life.  New shoes, new cellphones, can't "
"exactly go shopping, or, well, I guess you sorta can, if you mind the broken "
"glass.  I left my wallet in an outdoorsman's store when I 'bought' this "
"warmer coat.  Figured that's kinda it, you know?  It didn't matter anymore.  "
"I don't think my insurance's going to pay out for any health care I get now.  "
"I did what you see in the movies though, I rolled a joint with a hundred "
"dollar bill.  Ended up coughing and rerolling it in regular paper though.  "
"Was too harsh.  Just letting you know in case you get the smart idea of "
"trying it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Go on."
msgstr "Continue."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Say, I don't mean to get you in any trouble or nothing, if any folks still "
"care about that, but you haven't seen any green around town, have ya?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "WHAT."
msgstr "QUOI."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh yeah, some people've been growing it in their basements."
msgstr "Oh oui, certaines personnes on fait pousser dans leur sous-sols."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not comfortable with where this is going."
msgstr "Je ne suis pas à l'aise avec là où ça va."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh.  Uh, sure."
msgstr "Oh. Euh, bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Right, of course I knew that!  There's tons of the stuff out there for the "
"taking."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nope, sorry."
msgstr "Non, désolé(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not doing this."
msgstr "Je ne ferais pas ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey, don't get all serious on me all of a sudden.  It helps me relax.  "
"Lubricates my joints.  Eases the pain, ya know?  Makes every day a bit more "
"bearable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can help."
msgstr "Je peux aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, no worries, though.  I'm good at the moment.  Ask me again later and "
"maybe I'll have scrounged up some more cash for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Amazing!  My lucky day.  Let's see here.  What can I offer… I can scrounge up "
"some merch bucks for, say, five joints or joints-worth of the good stuff."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You have yourself a deal.  Here's the marijuana."
msgstr "C'est une affaire.  Voici de l'herbe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You have yourself a deal.  Here's some joints."
msgstr "C'est une affaire.  Voici des joints."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, alright.  I'll be back later with the goods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second thought, maybe later."
msgstr "En y réfléchissant, peut-être plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well, let me know when you have.  I'm not going anywhere."
msgstr "Bah dis moi quand tu en as. Je ne vais nul part."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure."
msgstr "Ok."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not your drug dealer, buddy."
msgstr "Je suis pas ton dealer/ ta dealeuse, mec."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem, Draco."
msgstr "Pas de problème Draco."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're welcome.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "De rien. <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a sec, got something I need to do first."
msgstr "Une seconde, j'ai un truc à régler avant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Shuffle back and forth a little.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Do a little dance.]"
msgstr "[Exécutez une petite danse.]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Perform a decent dance.]"
msgstr "[Exécutez une danse passable.]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Perform an impressive dance.]"
msgstr "[Exécutez une danse impressionnante.]"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Perform a masterful dance.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Perform a legendary dance.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not in the mood to dance, huh?  Or perhaps you should try wearing something "
"less encumbering.  You know, if you want to."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll consider it.  Thanks for the tunes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, later."
msgstr "Merci, à plus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ah yes, that's the spirit!  This place could sure use more dancing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cheers!"
msgstr "Santé!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cheers!  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr "Santé ! <end_talking_bye>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh my oh my.  That was impressive!  Sweet moves!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh wow.  I didn't even know the human body could move like that.  I don't "
"know what to say.  That was amazing!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgstr "Ramenez une guitare acoustique"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid ""
"Yeah, sure, imagine how things would be if we had some live music around "
"here?  I don't know how much I could thank you, though, if you're looking for "
"payment.  You'd sure be improving the mood, though."
msgstr ""
"Ouais, bien sûr, imaginez comment les choses seraient si nous avions de la "
"musique live par ici ? Je ne sais pas à quel point je pourrais vous "
"remercier, si vous cherchez à être payé. C'est certain, vous amélioreriez "
"l'ambiance en tous cas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid ""
"I just want a functional acoustic guitar.  Preferably one that hasn't been "
"used to cave in any zombie skulls."
msgstr ""
"Je veux juste une guitare acoustique en bonne état. De préférence une qui n'a "
"pas était utilisé pour casser des crânes de zombies.  "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid "Great!  We'll be makin' music in no time!"
msgstr "Super ! on va très bientôt faire de la musique !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid "Oh well.  I understand your reluctance… I guess."
msgstr "Bon ok… Je comprends votre réticence… je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid ""
"Well, I'll let you in on a little secret.  Guitars COULD be found at a music "
"store.  Let that one sink in a bit."
msgstr ""
"Je vais vous révéler un petit secret. Les guitares PEUVENT être trouvées dans "
"un magasin de musique. Prenez le temps d'y réfléchir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid "How's my guitar comin', friend?"
msgstr "Alors, ma guitare arrive l'ami/e ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid ""
"Hell yeah, bud!  You just made a lot of people really happy!  In thanks, I'll "
"have enough cash to offer you more recompense for our little dealings."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, mon/ma pote ! Tu viens de rendre beaucoup de gens très heureux ! En "
"remerciement, j'aurai assez d'argent pour t'offrir une meilleure compensation "
"pour notre petite affaire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid "Huh.  This… is something, isn't it."
msgstr "Ouh là.  C'est… quelque chose, n'est pas?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring an acoustic guitar"
msgid "No worries.  They don't grow from trees, but we have time."
msgstr "Ne t'inquiète pas. Elles ne poussent pas dans les arbres, mais on a le temps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Fatima al Jadir"
msgstr "Fatima al Jadir"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you wind up here at the center?"
msgstr "Comment est-tu arrivé ici au centre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, you free for a bit of teaching?"
msgstr "Hé, dispo pour une séance d'apprentissage ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a fit young woman dressed in smudged coveralls.  She looks at you with "
"interest and concern.  \"Oh, hey, a new face.  Hi, I'm Fatima.  Just visiting "
"I hope?  It's nice to meet new people but there are no beds to share.\""
msgstr ""
"*est une jeune femme en pleine forme, vêtue d'une combinaison de travail "
"maculée. Elle vous regarde avec intérêt et inquiétude. \"Oh, hey, un nouveau "
"visage. Bonjour, je suis Fatima. Vous n'êtes que de passage, j'espère ? C'est "
"sympa de rencontrer de nouvelles personnes mais il n'y a pas de lits à "
"partager.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Fatima.  I'm just passing through."
msgstr "Enchanté·e, Fatima.  Je ne fais que passer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Fatima.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Enchanté·e également, Fatima.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*futilely dusts a bit of grime on her coveralls, then looks at you.  \""
msgstr ""
"*futilement, elle époussette un peu de crasse sur sa combinaison, puis vous "
"regarde. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you're still around."
msgstr "C'est cool de voir que vous êtes encore dans le coin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Fatima.  How are things?"
msgstr "Bonjour Fatima. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Fatima.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Fatima.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well, cool.  Anything I can help you with?"
msgstr "Ok, cool. Il y a quelque chose que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, you know, the usual.  Trapped in a tight space with a bunch of strangers "
"getting along tenuously at best.  Good times, good times."
msgstr ""
"Oh, vous savez, comme d'habitude. Coincée dans un espace restreint avec une "
"bande d'étrangers qui s'entendent au mieux de façon ténue. Du bon temps, du "
"bon temps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Before <the_cataclysm> I had just finished welding school actually, and was "
"about to start looking for a job.  That was fun, being a young Muslim woman "
"in a Massachusetts trade college, let me tell you."
msgstr ""
"Avant <the_cataclysm>,  je venais de terminer l'école de soudure et j'étais "
"sur le point de commencer à chercher un emploi. C'était amusant d'être une "
"jeune musulmane dans une école professionnelle du Massachusetts, croyez-moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Welding seems like a pretty non-traditional occupational choice; is there a "
"story there?"
msgstr ""
"La soudure à l'air d'être un travail assez non traditionnel pour une fille "
"musulmane, il y a une histoire derrière?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'd be surprised actually!  Metal art has been part of Muslim traditions "
"for years, although that's not why I got into it.  I'm not a very traditional "
"girl.  My parents aren't very traditional either, but my grandparents are "
"really old fashioned and strict.  My sister came out as gay and they made her "
"life really hard; mom and dad thought she should keep it secret, but she "
"didn't believe in that.  I always loved mechanics and working with my hands, "
"so when they started harassing my parents about getting my sister and I "
"married off to nice men so we'd stop being so immoral, I decided to pick a "
"job I liked that would bother them as much as possible.  It was a good "
"choice, not only did it make them livid but I love welding.  I love the feel "
"of standing back and looking at my work, knowing I took a few chunks of scrap "
"metal and made them into something useful.  I love how it feels to make it "
"fit together perfectly.  It just puts me at peace.\n"
"\n"
"I… I do hope my grandparents are okay though.  They were old fashioned, and "
"they made choices I didn't like, but they were family and I still have sweet "
"memories of them from when I was little.  I've had to do a lot more thinking "
"about God since <the_cataclysm>, and while I'd never agree with the decisions "
"they made, I understand more why they thought they had to make them.  They "
"just wanted the whole family to share their relationship with God, in their "
"messed up way."
msgstr ""
"Vous serez surpris(e)! L'art du métal fait partie des traditions musulmanes, "
"mais ce n'est pas vraiment pourquoi je m'y suis appliquée. Je ne suis pas "
"vraiment une fille traditionnelle, mes parents non plus, mais mes "
"grandparents sont vraiment vieux jeu et stricts, ma sœur s'est révélé "
"lesbienne et ils ont rendus sa vie assez difficile, mes parents lui on "
"conseillé de garder ça secret mais elle n'a pas voulu. J'ai toujours aimé la "
"mécanique et travailler avec mes mains, donc quand ils ont commencés à "
"harceler mes parents au sujet de nous marier toute les deux à de bons hommes "
"pour arrêter d'être immorales, j'ai décidé de trouver un boulot qui les "
"dérangerait le plus possible. Devenir soudeuse était un bon choix vu que je "
"me suis rendue compte que j'adorais le travail et l'appréciation d'un travail "
"bien fait, savoir que j'ai transformé quelques morceaux de ferraille en "
"quelque chose de beau ou d'utile, l'accomplissement qui vous submerge lorsque "
"toutes les parties d'une machine s'emboitent bien.\n"
"\n"
"Je… J'espère comme même que mes grandparents vont toujours bien comme même, "
"ils étaient vieillots mais ils faisaient tout de même partie de la famille et "
"j'ai de bonnes mémoires d'enfance avec eux. J'ai eu plus de temps pour penser "
"à Dieu depuis que <the_cataclysm> est arrivé et, même si je ne serais jamais "
"d'accord avec eux sur la façon dont ils ont décidés de se comporter, je "
"comprends maintenant un peu pourquoi ils pensaient avoir besoin de nous "
"traiter comme cela, ils essayaient de forcer toute la famille de partager "
"leur propre manière d'aborder Dieu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Welding comes up a lot in my life.  Do you think you could teach me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure.  As agreed, 3 merch."
msgstr "Ok, trois merch, comme promis."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I could teach you the basics, I'll have to charge you though.  Let's "
"say, 5 merch for a teaching session, plus a bit in trade depending on how "
"in-depth you're looking for?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 merch] All right, here's your money."
msgstr "[5 merch] Ok, voilà votre argent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 merch] All right, here's your money."
msgstr "[4 merch] Ok, voilà votre argent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 merch] All right, here's your money."
msgstr "[3 merch] Ok, voilà votre argent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[BARTER] Come on, I'm serious here."
msgstr "[BARTER] Allez, je suis sérieux(se) là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[BARTER] That's still pretty steep, I risked my neck out there for your book. "
" Can't you manage a little lower?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hey, I appreciate that, but I know what I've got, and I can make good money "
"with that time.  Sorry, my price stands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, fine, you weasel.  I suppose I can manage for 3 notes.  I seriously can't "
"go lower though, we'll be using up my resources and time and I gotta pay for "
"the gas and the food somehow."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was on my way to visit my parents back in Burlington, waiting at a bus "
"station, when the evacuation notices started sounding.  I'd been a little out "
"of touch for a bit and didn't realize how bad the rioting was getting.  When "
"my bus arrived it got repurposed into an evacuation vehicle, and took me "
"here.  I… I didn't used to be very religious, it's just something I was born "
"to, but since this happened I've been thinking a lot more about God, and how "
"grateful I am for His help in surviving.  With things still so difficult, it "
"helps to know He's got some plan for me.\n"
"\n"
"Anyway, mine was the second bus to arrive, and they were just getting some "
"triage and processing stuff set up.  I was put in charge of helping with the "
"wounded, along with Uyen.  Things went a little strange later on… one of the "
"women doing triage and processing had a bit of a hang-up about particular, "
"um, colors of people being allowed into the center.  She claimed to have lost "
"our 'papers', along with a lot of other peoples'.  Thankfully because we'd "
"helped so many we were able to argue that they couldn't leave us out, but "
"there was no space left downstairs by the time we got that sorted, so here we "
"are."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things are still tense, but I've been busy lately.  Jenny's had her project "
"going and got me started helping her out with it, and for some reason that "
"seems to have been the tipping point: I'm getting chances to do a lot more "
"welding work now.  It's helping.  I feel a bit self-conscious praying in the "
"common areas, and of course, we don't go outside if we can help it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's tense here.  I know I'd feel a lot better if I had something to do with "
"my skills, or even if I just had a quiet place to pray sometimes.  I feel a "
"bit self-conscious praying in the common areas.  Jenny was talking about some "
"project ideas she had that could get me doing my job again, but I admit I'm "
"pretty nervous about going outside."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgstr "Trouvez un Koran"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid "I could use a bit of help to find a copy of the Quran."
msgstr "Je pourrais avoir besoin d'aide pour trouver une copie du Quran."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid ""
"I feel silly asking this, but here goes.  I've never been really into reading "
"holy books and stuff like that.  I usually went to the mosque on Friday, and "
"I try to pray five times a day but I hardly ever manage it.  I guess I'm not "
"a very good Muslim, but with all that's happened I would really love to have "
"a copy of the Quran to read.  This seems like a time to get back in touch "
"with God, you know?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid "Thank you.  I'll see if I can save up a little reward for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid "That's okay.  Thanks for offering."
msgstr "Ce n'est pas grave. Merci d'avoir offert."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid ""
"It's not as common as the bible, but you should be able to find copies in "
"most libraries and bookstores, or in religious buildings.  Make sure you get "
"the translated version, I can't read Arabic!"
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas aussi commun que la bible, mais vous devriez être capable d'en "
"trouver dans la plupart des bibliothéques et libraires, ou dans des bâtiments "
"religieux. Faites attention à prendre une version traduite, je ne peux pas "
"lire l'arabe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid ""
"Thank you so much.  Just having a copy to keep at hand does actually feel "
"pretty comforting.  I did a few extra rounds of chores and saved the proceeds "
"for if you managed this, here you go.  It's not much but I hope it helps."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a copy of the Quran"
msgid ""
"It's okay.  I don't know how much comfort I'd have found in an old book "
"anyway."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Garry Villeneuve"
msgstr "Garry Villeneuve"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up at you with a gaunt face.  His loose clothes and sharp cheekbones "
"suggest he recently lost a lot of weight.  \"Hi.  Hi there.\"  He scratches "
"at a patchy beard of gray stubble.  \"I'm Garry, Garry Villeneuve.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Garry."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Garry."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Garry, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Garry, enchanté·e.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*smiles at you briefly.  He looks like he hasn't been eating well.  \""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well, hello."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Garry.  What's up?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Garry.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Garry.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice to meet you too.  Are you staying here, or something?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I'm a traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nope, in fact I'm leaving right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Doing my best to keep going in the face of… everything.  Not getting far."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Before the apocalypse I was an electrician.  Boris here is my brother-in-law, "
"and we were a decent contractor team.  When the evacuations sounded, we left "
"together with our…\" he swallows and coughs before continuing, \"with our "
"families.  We got stuck into a crowded evac shelter, then onto a crowded bus. "
" Then… everything went wrong.  The bus was attacked, destroyed.  Nearly "
"everyone died.  A few of us made it back… not enough."
msgstr ""
"Avant l'apocalypse j'étais un électricien.  Boris est mon beau-frère, et nous "
"étions une assez bonne équipe.  Lorsque les appels à l'évacuation ont "
"commencés, nous sommes partis ensemble avec...\"  il avale sa salive et "
"tousse avant de continuer, \"avec nos familles.  Nous nous sommes retrouvés "
"coincés dans un abri d'évacuation bourrés, et ensuite dans un bus plein à "
"craquer.  Et ensuite... tout a commencé à s'écrouler.  Le bus a été attaqué, "
"détruit.  Presque tout le monde est mort.  Quelque uns s'en sont sortis…  pas "
"assez"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You lost someone…"
msgstr "Vous avez perdu quelqu'un…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes.  My wife, Linda… thrown from the bus.  She didn't make it.  And… and my "
"nephew, Ash, Boris and Stan's son.  We got him here, but there wasn't "
"anything we could do.\"  He gestures for a moment as if trying to explain it "
"without words, then shrugs.  \"Internal injuries."
msgstr ""
"Oui.  Ma femme, Linda... éjectée du bus.  Elle ne s'en est pas sortie.  Et... "
"et mon neveu, Ash, le fils de Boris et Stan.  On a réussi à le porter "
"jusqu'ici, mais l'on ne pouvait rien faire pour lui.\"  Il fait quelques "
"gestes pendant un moment pour essayer de l'expliquer sans utiliser de mots, "
"puis hausse ses épaules.  \"Lésions internes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you want to tell me about Linda?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about Ash."
msgstr "Dites-moi ce que vous savez au sujet d'Ash."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks unsure, then sighs softly.  \"I don't know what to say.  She was my "
"second wife; my first wife passed away about fifteen years ago.  I've gone "
"through this before, and it was bad enough then.\"  He stares at the floor "
"for a moment.  \"We don't have any touchstones anymore, you know?  I've got "
"Boris and Stan, but they can't support me, and what else is there?\"  He "
"looks back up at you, appearing to remember the conversation.  \"Sorry, you "
"were asking about Linda.  She was wonderful, always surprising me.  One of "
"those people you just couldn't predict, so much fun and full of life.  Really "
"into rock climbing.  I always used to be afraid she'd hurt herself in a "
"climbing accident.\"  He laughs, a single harsh sound more like a cough.  "
"\"Funny how life throws you curveballs.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles for a moment, his face returning to what it must have looked like "
"before everything.  \"God, that kid was funny.  Such a little nerd.  He'd "
"come bombing into any conversation to interrupt and tell you about whatever "
"his latest obsession was, didn't matter what else was going on.  We'd have to "
"remind him to go to the bathroom sometimes.\"  Garry looks around, swallowing "
"hard for a second, and wipes his hands across his face.  \"It's so damn quiet "
"here without him.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's tense here, but I don't know.  Stan, Boris and I have been pretty "
"insular.  I guess we'd better get to know some of the others here "
"eventually.\"  He looks around the room, his eyes dull.  \"It feels it should "
"be a temporary stop, but it's starting to look like we'll be here for the "
"long term.  If we live that long."
msgstr ""
"Les choses sont tendues ici, mais je ne sais pas.  Stan, Boris et moi, nous "
"sommes restés plus ou moins isolés.  Je suppose que nous ferions mieux de "
"faire connaissance avec  les autres ici maintenant que plus tard.\"  Il "
"parcoure la salle avec des yeux ternes.  \"Je pensais que ceci serait une "
"sorte d'halte momentanée, mais on dirait que nous allons être ici au long "
"terme, si nous arrivons à survivre assez longtemps pour ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Guneet Singh"
msgstr "Guneet Singh"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a young man in a white turban, surprisingly clean compared to the rest of "
"his outfit.  He turns from the window as you approach, then raises his "
"eyebrows when he sees you're a new face.  \"Oh, hello.  I don't think I've "
"seen you around before.  I'm Guneet, people call me Gunny.\""
msgstr ""
"*C'est un jeune homme coiffé d'un turban blanc, étonnamment propre par "
"rapport au reste de sa tenue. Il se détourne de la fenêtre à votre approche, "
"puis hausse les sourcils en voyant que vous êtes un nouveau visage. \"Oh, "
"bonjour. Je ne crois pas vous avoir déjà vu dans le coin. Je suis Guneet, les "
"gens m'appellent Gunny\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Gunny."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Gunny."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Gunny, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Gunny, enchanté·e.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*turns away from the window, noticing you coming close.  \""
msgstr "*se détourne de la fenêtre, remarquant que vous vous approchez. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Gunny.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Gunny. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Gunny.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Gunny.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess we're still doing that stuff?  Cool.  Nice to meet you too.  What's "
"up?"
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que nous faisons encore ce genre de choses ? C'est cool. Ravi de "
"vous rencontrer aussi. Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What's up?\"  He stares at you for a moment.  \"What a weird question.  The "
"world ended.  That's what's up.  What am I supposed to answer to that one?"
msgstr ""
"Comment vont les choses?\" Il vous fixe des yeux pendant un moment. \"Quelle "
"question bizarre.  Le monde s'est écroulé.  Voilà ce qui se passe.  Quelle "
"genre de réponse est-ce que vous vous attendiez à?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was in high school, you know.\"  Gunny jabs his thumb at his shirt, which "
"reads 'Alexander Bullock High'.  \"Most of the way through my junior year.  "
"'My story'?  I got on a bus with my parents, the bus crashed, and everyone "
"died except a few people, most of whom are crammed into this little shelter "
"now.  Who knows when we're getting out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your family all made it here?"
msgstr "Toute votre famille est arrivée ici saine et sauve?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, we did.\"  He gestures to a turbaned older man, speaking quietly with a "
"small woman a little way away.  \"Seems like it should be a great thing, "
"right?  It is.  We're super lucky.  But I can't help feel like people blame "
"us for it.  I keep wondering, y'know, 'why us'.  What makes me so special?  "
"And how can I even enjoy this, when everyone around me is hurting so bad?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there something you could do to help the others?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous faire quelque chose pour aider les autres ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"I don't have any skills.  I'm just a kid.  What am I going to "
"do?\"  Before you can answer, he shakes his head.  \"I'm being pathetic, "
"sorry.  You're right, I should see if there's something I can give back to "
"the community, maybe make my place in it.  That's a good call.\"  He "
"scratches his chin and looks out a gap in the shutters on the window.  "
"\"Thanks.\""
msgstr ""
"*hausse les épaules. \"Je n'ai aucune compétence. Je ne suis qu'un enfant. "
"Qu'est-ce que je vais faire ?\" Avant que tu puisses répondre, il secoue la "
"tête. \"Je suis pathétique, désolé. Tu as raison, je devrais voir s'il y a "
"quelque chose que je peux rendre à la communauté, peut-être y faire ma place. "
"C'est une bonne idée.\" Il se gratte le menton et regarde par "
"l'entrebâillement des volets de la fenêtre. \"Merci."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It sucks in here, there's no two ways about it"
msgstr "Ça craint ici, il n'y a pas à dire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  Still, we're starting to find a bit of a place for ourselves.  I've been "
"hanging out with Aleesha a bit, I didn't used to think we'd have a lot in "
"common but there's more than you'd think.  My mom and dad are starting to "
"relax a little too."
msgstr ""
". Pourtant, nous commençons à trouver notre place. Je traîne un peu avec "
"Aleesha, je ne pensais pas que nous aurions beaucoup de choses en commun, "
"mais il y en a plus qu'on ne le pense. Ma mère et mon père commencent aussi à "
"se détendre un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  People don't talk to us because we wear turbans and we still have each "
"other.  They think because we're still together, we didn't lose anything.  My "
"dad believes it, too, and I think my mom's on the fence."
msgstr ""
". Les gens ne nous parlent pas parce que nous portons des turbans et que nous "
"sommes toujours ensemble. Ils pensent que parce que nous sommes toujours "
"ensemble, nous n'avons rien perdu. Mon père le croit aussi, et je pense que "
"ma mère n'est pas tout à fait d'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Jenny Forcette"
msgstr "Jenny Forcette"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you working on?"
msgstr "Sur quoi travaillez-vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's everything going with that defense system?"
msgstr "Comment se passe le système de défense ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me a bit about your background."
msgstr "Parlez-moi un peu de votre parcours."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you free to teach me anything today?"
msgstr "Vous avez le temps de m'apprendre quelque chose aujourd'hui?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me anything about the other refugees here?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me dire quelque chose au sujet des autres réfugiés ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you make it here during the chaos?"
msgstr "Comment avez-vous réussi à venir ici pendant le chaos ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you think happened to the world?"
msgstr "Que pensez-vous qu'il soit arrivé au monde ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a thin woman in her early thirties, with the sort of pale, freckled skin "
"that looks like it would burn if she thought too hard about the sun.  Her "
"clothes and bearing suggest she might once have been carefully put-together, "
"but she now has the harried look of someone with too many worries and too "
"little sleep.  She looks up from a laptop and smiles as you approach.  \"Hi "
"there.  Haven't see you around here before.  I'm Jenny, Jenny Forcette.\""
msgstr ""
"*C'est une femme mince d'une trentaine d'années, à la peau pâle et parsemée "
"de taches de rousseur, qui semble prête à brûler si elle pense trop au "
"soleil. Ses vêtements et son allure suggèrent qu'elle a déjà été très "
"soignée, mais elle a maintenant l'air d'une personne qui a trop de soucis et "
"qui ne dort pas assez. Elle lève les yeux de son ordinateur portable et "
"sourit à votre approche. \"Bonjour. Je ne vous ai jamais vu dans le coin. Je "
"suis Jenny, Jenny Forcette.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice meeting you.  What are you doing on that computer?"
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous avoir rencontré.  Que faites-vous sur cet ordinateur?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice meeting you.  I'd best get going, though."
msgstr "Enchanté de vous avoir rencontré. Je ferais mieux d'y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up from her computer and gives you a quick, thin smile.  \"Hello "
"again.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle lève les yeux de son ordinateur et vous adresse un mince et rapide "
"sourire. \"Re-bonjour\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*tips the lid of her laptop closed and looks up.  \"Nice to see you again.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle referme le couvercle de son ordinateur portable et lève les yeux. "
"\"Ravi de vous revoir\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Jenny.  What are you up to these days?"
msgstr "Bonjour, Jenny. Que fais-tu ces jours-ci ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry Jenny.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Désolé·e Jenny.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm puttering around, I always have stuff on the go.\"  Jenny rubs the bridge "
"of her nose briefly, blinking fatigue from her eyes.  \"Gotta keep busy, keep "
"my mind off stuff, you know?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me?  I trained at MIT in mechanical engineering, I worked for a long time as "
"senior engineer at Marduk Thermal in Rhode Island.  It was a good job, but I "
"landed my dream gig at Boston Dynamics and moved up north to start there.\"  "
"She tips back her head and lets out a long, wistful sigh.  \"I had just "
"finished my orientation and was going to start work when the riots started.  "
"Just my damn luck."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's impressive, but there must be more to you than just your job."
msgstr "C'est impressionnant, mais vous ne devez pas vous contenter de votre travail."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You must know some great stuff.  Can you teach me anything?"
msgstr ""
"Vous devez connaître des choses extraordinaires. Pouvez-vous m'apprendre "
"quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"So, did anyone tell you there are actual no-kidding talking cyborg-robot "
"people out there now?"
msgstr ""
"Alors, quelqu'un vous a dit qu'il y a maintenant des cyborg-robots qui "
"parlent sans rire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry about your luck.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*grins and tugs at her shirt, an uncharacteristically crisp white T-shirt "
"sporting a brightly colored penguin holding a slide rule, and a rainbow "
"slogan reading 'sudo build it the way I told you to'.  \"Ha!  You must not "
"know many engineers, hey?  I guess there's more to me than engineering, but "
"most of my hobbies come back to it one way or the other.  It's not that I "
"live for my work, doing engineering for a heating company wasn't some great "
"dream, but when I got home I'd putter with the projects I wanted to do "
"instead of the ones they made me do.  You know?  And of course, I had my "
"friends and things, we'd go out or hang out and play board games and stuff.  "
"Maybe some day I'll get a board game group started up here, although there's "
"nothing wrong with the card games we've got now.  Plus I don't think "
"Zombicide would hold the same interest for me as it used to.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle sourit et tire sur sa chemise, un T-shirt blanc d'une netteté "
"inhabituelle sur lequel figure un pingouin aux couleurs vives tenant une "
"règle à calcul, avec un slogan arc-en-ciel 'sudo build it the way I told you "
"to' (sudo construisez-le comme je vous l'ai dit). \"Vous ne devez pas "
"connaître beaucoup d'ingénieurs, hein ? Je suppose que je ne suis pas "
"seulement ingénieur, mais la plupart de mes loisirs y sont liés d'une manière "
"ou d'une autre. Ce n'est pas que je vive pour mon travail, faire de "
"l'ingénierie pour une entreprise de chauffage n'était pas un grand rêve, mais "
"quand je rentrais à la maison, je m'occupais des projets que je voulais faire "
"au lieu de ceux qu'on me faisait faire. Vous voyez ? Et bien sûr, j'avais mes "
"amis et d'autres choses, on sortait ou on traînait et on jouait à des jeux de "
"société et d'autres choses. Peut-être qu'un jour, j'arriverai à créer un "
"groupe de jeux de société ici, même s'il n'y a rien de mal à jouer aux jeux "
"de cartes que nous avons maintenant. En plus, je ne pense pas que Zombicide "
"m'intéresserait autant qu'avant.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of board games do you play?"
msgstr "À quels types de jeux de société jouez-vous? "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs, looking distant.  \"I don't really like to talk about that time "
"much.  None of us do.  Short story is that I made it to one of the evacuation "
"shelters and got loaded onto a bus.  It was supposed to go to some sort of "
"FEMA support camp, but there was a roadblock on the way there.  A few people "
"just jumped out and ran for the military for protection.  They… it… it was "
"bad.  The driver managed to get us turned around and booked it, and I guess "
"they didn't chase us.  She took us back to one of the shelters and we found "
"the address for this place.  Only a few of us decided to risk it, the rest "
"stayed at the shelter to try their luck a different way.  I still wonder how "
"they did.\""
msgstr ""
"*haussant les épaules, l'air distant. \"Je n'aime pas vraiment parler de "
"cette époque. Aucun d'entre nous n'aime en parler. Pour faire court, je me "
"suis rendu dans l'un des abris d'évacuation et j'ai été embarqué dans un bus. "
"Il était censé se rendre dans une sorte de camp de soutien de la FEMA, mais "
"il y a eu un barrage sur le chemin. Quelques personnes ont sauté du bus et "
"ont couru vers l'armée pour se protéger. Ils... c'était... c'était grave. La "
"conductrice a réussi à nous faire faire demi-tour et à réserver, et je "
"suppose qu'ils ne nous ont pas poursuivis. Elle nous a ramenés à l'un des "
"abris et nous avons trouvé l'adresse de cet endroit. Seuls quelques-uns "
"d'entre nous ont décidé de prendre le risque, les autres sont restés au "
"refuge pour tenter leur chance d'une autre manière. Je me demande encore "
"comment ils ont fait.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ha!  I wonder how long that's going to be one of our go-to small talk "
"questions.  It's perfect, isn't it?  Doesn't make you talk about the worst "
"stuff but stays on theme for what's on everyone's mind.  Okay, I'll bite.  "
"Have you heard any of the really wild stories?  Giant monsters the size of "
"skyscrapers kicking over tanks and stuff, during the worst days?  I think "
"somehow our planet got moved into another dimension, probably some kind of "
"experimental process gone wrong.  During transit, some of those things came "
"across, but they left when we arrived wherever we are now.  The rules are "
"different here, and maybe we're superimposed with whatever version of Earth "
"was here to start with, and that's why we hear about aliens and other "
"unbelievable stuff out there along with the zombies.\"  She grins.  \"And "
"before you say that's implausible, bear in mind that *the dead walk now*, so "
"plausibility is off the table."
msgstr ""
"Ha ! Je me demande combien de temps encore cette question sera l'une de "
"celles que nous poserons lors de nos conversations. C'est parfait, n'est-ce "
"pas ? Elle ne vous fait pas parler des pires choses, mais reste dans le thème "
"de ce qui préoccupe tout le monde. D'accord, je mords. As-tu entendu parler "
"des histoires les plus folles ? Des monstres géants de la taille d'un "
"gratte-ciel renversant des chars d'assaut et d'autres choses, pendant les "
"pires jours ? Je pense que notre planète a été déplacée dans une autre "
"dimension, probablement à cause d'un processus expérimental qui a mal tourné. "
"Au cours de la traversée, certaines de ces choses sont apparues, mais elles "
"sont parties lorsque nous sommes arrivés là où nous sommes aujourd'hui. Les "
"règles sont différentes ici, et peut-être que nous sommes superposés à la "
"version de la Terre qui était là au départ, et c'est pourquoi nous entendons "
"parler d'extraterrestres et d'autres choses incroyables, en plus des "
"zombies.\" Elle sourit. \"Et avant que vous ne disiez que c'est "
"invraisemblable, gardez à l'esprit que *les morts marchent maintenant*, donc "
"la plausibilité n'est pas de mise."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*lets out a low whistle.  \"No, not as such.  I've heard some rumors, I "
"guess, but nothing credible.\"  She pauses, looking thoughtful.  \"I think, "
"unless you can offer me some detailed answers about who and what they are and "
"how they work, you'd better not tell me anything else.  I don't know if I "
"could handle the stress.\"  With a gulp, she pulls listlessly at her earlobe. "
" \"If you do really know some juicy tidbits though, spill.\""
msgstr ""
"*laisse échapper un petit sifflement. \"Non, pas à proprement parler. J'ai "
"entendu quelques rumeurs, je suppose, mais rien de crédible.\" Elle s'arrête, "
"l'air pensif. \"Je pense qu'à moins que vous ne puissiez m'offrir des "
"réponses détaillées sur qui et ce qu'ils sont et comment ils fonctionnent, "
"vous feriez mieux de ne rien me dire de plus. Je ne sais pas si je pourrais "
"supporter le stress.\" Avec une bouffée d'air, elle tire mollement sur le "
"lobe de son oreille. \"Si tu connais vraiment des trucs croustillants, dis-le "
"moi.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, I know they're cyborgs, from some other dimension.  I think they're "
"humans underneath the machines though.  Some of them kinda speak English."
msgstr ""
"Je sais que ce sont des cyborgs, venus d'une autre dimension. Je pense qu'il "
"y a des humains sous les machines. Certains d'entre eux parlent un peu "
"anglais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*puts her hands on her hips and glares at you.  \"I thought I made it clear I "
"wasn't willing to accept enticing tidbits of information.  What the actual "
"fuck?  Interdimensional cyborgs?  I don't want to believe you, but also, I "
"already kinda thought there might be some multidimensional hijinks going on "
"here, so I kinda do want to believe you.  They speak English though?  Are you "
"sure this isn't some kind of scam?  Are you just fucking with me?  Honestly "
"this would be a great way to fuck with me.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle met les mains sur les hanches et vous regarde fixement. \"Je pensais "
"avoir été claire sur le fait que je n'étais pas prête à accepter des "
"informations alléchantes. Qu'est-ce que c'est que ce bordel ? Des cyborgs "
"interdimensionnels ? Je n'ai pas envie de vous croire, mais j'ai déjà un peu "
"pensé qu'il y avait des trucs multidimensionnels ici, alors j'ai un peu envie "
"de vous croire. Mais ils parlent anglais ? Vous êtes sûr que ce n'est pas une "
"sorte d'arnaque ? Vous vous foutez de ma gueule ? Honnêtement, ce serait une "
"bonne façon de se foutre de ma gueule\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Show her your bionic interface.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*breathes a long, sighing curse as she examines your CBM interface.  "
"\"Holeeeeeeshiiiiiiit.  This is amazing!  Like seriously, it's not even high "
"tech.  At least not this part.  Can I see the schematics?  Can we dissect "
"you?  I'm kidding.  Unless?  No, really kidding though.  Holy shit.\"  She "
"pauses and studies you with a furrowed brow.  \"Wait, you let a strange "
"interdimensional cyborg do brain surgery on you?  Never mind, I'd totally do "
"that too.  Can you get me one of these?  No, I'd wind up taking it out and "
"dismantling it.\"  She looks you up and down.  \"Thanks.  That's incredible.  "
"It sucks that the world ended but I'm glad to know at least it ended with "
"*cyborgs*.\""
msgstr ""
"*pousse un long soupir de malédiction en examinant l'interface de votre CBM. "
"\"Holeeeeeeshiiiiiiit. C'est incroyable ! Sérieusement, ce n'est même pas de "
"la haute technologie. Du moins, pas cette partie. Je peux voir les schémas ? "
"On peut te disséquer ? Je plaisante. A moins que ? Non, je plaisante "
"vraiment. Putain de merde.\" Elle s'arrête et vous regarde en fronçant les "
"sourcils. \"Attends, tu as laissé un étrange cyborg interdimensionnel te "
"faire une opération du cerveau ? C'est pas grave, je ferais bien ça aussi. "
"Vous pouvez m'en donner un ? Non, je finirais par le sortir et le démonter.\" "
"Elle vous regarde de haut en bas. \"Elle vous regarde de haut en bas. C'est "
"incroyable. Ça craint que le monde ait pris fin, mais je suis contente de "
"savoir qu'au moins, il a pris fin avec des *cyborgs*.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*scrunches her face in thought for a moment.  \"There was a whole world out "
"there of weird board games for ultra nerdy people.  Lots of that stuff never "
"really reached mainstream.  One of the hardest parts of evacuating for me was "
"leaving my garage full of esoteric crowdfunded games I've never played.\""
msgstr ""
"*Elle s'est fait une tête pendant un moment. \"Il y avait tout un monde de "
"jeux de société bizarres pour les gens très ringards. Beaucoup de ces choses "
"n'ont jamais vraiment atteint le grand public. L'un des aspects les plus "
"difficiles de l'évacuation pour moi a été de laisser mon garage plein de jeux "
"ésotériques financés par le crowdfunding auxquels je n'ai jamais joué.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you ever thought about going back for them?"
msgstr "Avez-vous déjà pensé à retourner les chercher ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you mean stuff like D&D?"
msgstr "Vous voulez dire des choses comme D&D?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, mainly because my whole neighborhood burnt to the ground.  Some scouts "
"went by a while ago.  Nothing there for me but melted plastic miniatures and "
"thousands of hours of gameplay I'll never have."
msgstr ""
"Non, principalement parce que tout mon quartier a brûlé. Des éclaireurs sont "
"passés il y a un moment. Il n'y a rien d'autre pour moi que des figurines en "
"plastique fondues et des milliers d'heures de jeu que je n'aurai jamais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, of course I played the mandatory amount of dice based RPGs necessary to "
"graduate my engineering program,\" she grins.  \"They're fun, something like "
"that would be nice around here, but I'm not that kind of storyteller and I "
"don't think anyone else here is nerdy enough for it.\"  Jenny tips her head a "
"bit.  \"It's nice that you're asking but don't worry about me, I've got "
"recreation.\""
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, j'ai joué à la quantité obligatoire de jeux de rôle à base de dés "
"nécessaire pour obtenir mon diplôme d'ingénieur\", dit-elle en souriant. "
"\"C'est amusant, quelque chose comme ça serait bien ici, mais je ne suis pas "
"ce genre de conteur et je ne pense pas que quelqu'un d'autre ici soit assez "
"intello pour ça.\" Jenny penche un peu la tête. \"C'est bien que tu demandes, "
"mais ne t'inquiète pas pour moi, j'ai des loisirs.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you ever thought about going back for your board games?"
msgstr "Avez-vous déjà pensé à revenir en arrière pour vos jeux de société ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh.\"  She purses her lips and looks at you reluctantly.  \"I guess I can "
"teach you a bit, but you'd have to be like, my on-the-job apprentice and help "
"me get stuff done.  It'll cost you a bit depending on what you want to learn. "
" Do you know anything about electronics, computers, or mechanics already?\""
msgstr ""
"Huh\". Elle pince les lèvres et vous regarde à contrecœur. \"Je suppose que "
"je peux t'enseigner un peu, mais tu devras être comme mon apprenti sur le tas "
"et m'aider à faire des choses. Cela te coûtera un peu plus ou moins cher "
"selon ce que tu veux apprendre. Tu t'y connais déjà en électronique, en "
"informatique ou en mécanique ?\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Skill 2] I'm not a total noob."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Skill <2] No, that's why I want you to teach me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[INT 10] No, but I'm a fast learner."
msgstr "[INT 10] Non, mais j'apprends vite."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Um, you know what?  Nevermind.  What were you saying?"
msgstr "Hum, vous savez quoi ? Laisse tomber. Qu'est-ce que tu disais ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All right, fine.\"  Jenny sets aside the computer and gets up.  \"Grab some "
"tools and do as I tell you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just say the word, teach."
msgstr "Dites-moi juste ce que je dois faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&\"I'm sorry, I don't have the time to teach someone who can't pull their "
"weight, I just don't.\"  She gives you a look of genuine regret, then shrugs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  What were you saying?"
msgstr "Très bien. Qu'est-ce que tu disais ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, thanks to your help, I've been designing some turrets that would use a "
"central air system to power pneumatic rifle turrets around the center.  It's "
"a lot easier than trying to make gunpowder!\"  She shrugs quickly.  \"I'm "
"probably getting ahead of myself here, I don't think we're due to run out of "
"gunpowder for years, but I also think the design is quieter and more "
"long-term extendable."
msgstr ""
"\"Grâce à votre aide, j'ai commencé à concevoir des tourelles qui "
"utiliseraient un système d'air central pour alimenter des tourelles de fusils "
"pneumatiques autour du centre.\"  C'est beaucoup plus facile que d'essayer de "
"fabriquer de la poudre!\"  Elle hausse rapidement les épaules.  \"Je mets "
"peut être la charrue avant les bœufs, je pense pas que nous allons manquer de "
"cartouches pour quelques années au moins, mais je pense aussi que cette "
"conception est plus silencieuse et plus pratique au long terme.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"About a month ago, I got a mold for making high-caliber air rifle bullets.  "
"I've been designing some turrets that would use a central air system to power "
"pneumatic rifle turrets around the center.  It's a lot easier than trying to "
"make gunpowder!\"  She shrugs quickly.  \"I'm probably getting ahead of "
"myself here, I don't think we're due to run out of gunpowder for years, but I "
"also think the design is quieter and more long-term extendable."
msgstr ""
"\"Il y a environ un mois, j'ai trouvé un moule pour fabriquer des balles de "
"fusil à air comprimé de haut calibre.  J'ai conçu des tourelles qui "
"utiliseraient un système d'air central pour alimenter des tourelles de fusils "
"pneumatiques autour du centre.  C'est beaucoup plus facile que d'essayer de "
"fabriquer de la poudre!\"  Elle hausse rapidement les épaules.  \"Je mets "
"peut être la charrue avant les bœufs, je pense pas que nous allons manquer de "
"cartouches pour quelques années au moins, mais je pense aussi que ce concept "
"est plus silencieux et plus pratique au long terme.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I recently came into possession of this mold for making high-caliber air "
"rifle bullets.  I'm kinda working on a design that would use them to protect "
"the base.  Got a long way to go, though.  If you happen to see anything in "
"your travels about high-powered air rifles, it would help a lot."
msgstr ""
"Je suis récemment entré en possession de ce moule pour la fabrication de "
"balles de fusil à air comprimé de haut calibre. Je travaille sur un modèle "
"qui les utiliserait pour protéger la base. J'ai encore un long chemin à "
"parcourir. Si, au cours de vos voyages, vous voyez quelque chose sur les "
"carabines à air comprimé de grande puissance, cela m'aiderait beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If I see anything, I'll let you know.  Can you tell me more about your "
"project?"
msgstr ""
"Si je vois quoi que ce soit, je vous ferai savoir. Vous pouvez m'en dire plus "
"sur votre projet?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about your project."
msgstr "Racontez-moi plus au sujet de votre projet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They're pretty big.  This isn't something you'd carry around with you.  They "
"fire .30 cal bullets using compressed air that we'd make inside the basement "
"and then pipe up to individual storage tanks for the guns that would be good "
"for a few hundred shots each.  The design should be capable of auto or "
"semi-auto fire, at a range that's pretty comparable to a gunpowder-based "
"weapon.  It takes out some of the most limited parts of ranged weapons: no "
"gunpowder, no brass casings, just lead that we melt into my mold.  It's not "
"soundless, but it's not as loud as a chemical weapon.  There are tons of "
"advantages.  Only trouble is, I can't convince the Free Merchants to give me "
"the parts I need, even though it's for our own defense.\"  She grimaces.  "
"\"Being one of the 'surface people' is so frustrating.  I'm pretty sure they "
"talk about these decisions downstairs, behind our backs, and we're just not "
"part of the process and can't advocate for our own projects."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, these things are a standard .30 caliber.  They should be compatible "
"with any similar rifle barrel.  It would be pretty easy to repurpose some "
"rifle parts into large air weapons that we could use without relying on "
"gunpowder, and without so much noise.  I'm still drawing up an actual design "
"though, I have a bunch of features I want.  Ask me again in a couple weeks "
"and I'll give you some more info."
msgstr ""
"Il s'agit d'un calibre .30 standard. Ils devraient être compatibles avec "
"n'importe quel canon de fusil similaire. Il serait assez facile de réutiliser "
"certaines pièces de fusil pour en faire de grandes armes aériennes que nous "
"pourrions utiliser sans dépendre de la poudre à canon et sans faire autant de "
"bruit. Je suis encore en train de dessiner un modèle, j'ai un tas de "
"caractéristiques que je veux. Posez-moi à nouveau la question dans quelques "
"semaines et je vous donnerai plus d'informations."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there some way I can help you get the stuff you need?"
msgstr "Puis-je vous aider à obtenir ce dont vous avez besoin ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's finally ready!  The pipes are laid to the first patch of ground we'll "
"set turrets up in and I'd like for you to join me to go inspect how they are "
"working.  I'll let you know when I'm ready to go."
msgstr ""
"C'est enfin prêt ! Les tuyaux sont posés jusqu'à la première parcelle de "
"terrain où nous installerons les tourelles et j'aimerais que vous vous "
"joigniez à moi pour aller inspecter leur fonctionnement. Je vous ferai savoir "
"quand je serai prêt à partir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm really making headway.  We've done some live demonstrations with a "
"working device, and now it's just a matter of manufacturing a few of them.  "
"We should be ready for release in a week or two."
msgstr ""
"Je progresse vraiment. Nous avons fait quelques démonstrations en direct avec "
"un appareil qui fonctionne, et il ne reste plus qu'à en fabriquer "
"quelques-uns. Nous devrions être prêts à les commercialiser d'ici une semaine "
"ou deux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's getting bad.  We've been stuck in here for months, nothing changing, "
"nothing improving.  We can't go outside, we don't have enough to eat, and we "
"didn't choose to be with each other.  I don't know how long we can stay like "
"this before somebody snaps."
msgstr ""
"La situation se dégrade. Nous sommes coincés ici depuis des mois, rien ne "
"change, rien ne s'améliore. Nous ne pouvons pas sortir, nous n'avons pas "
"assez à manger et nous n'avons pas choisi d'être ensemble. Je ne sais pas "
"combien de temps on peut rester comme ça avant que quelqu'un ne craque."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's good and there's bad.  We're all pretty sick of being cooped up in "
"here for months, never knowing if there's going to be food to eat or not.  "
"It's starting to look like they're never going to let us go down to the "
"secure basement, and none of us have slept well since we were brought in.  We "
"know we've got it pretty good… we're safe, we're alive.  It's just, like, "
"what kind of life are we even living?"
msgstr ""
"Il y a du bon et du mauvais. Nous en avons tous assez d'être enfermés ici "
"depuis des mois, sans jamais savoir s'il y aura de la nourriture à manger ou "
"non. On commence à croire qu'ils ne nous laisseront jamais descendre dans le "
"sous-sol sécurisé, et aucun d'entre nous n'a bien dormi depuis qu'on nous a "
"amenés ici. Nous savons que tout va bien... nous sommes en sécurité, nous "
"sommes en vie. C'est juste que, quel genre de vie vivons-nous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's been over a month now, so I guess I'm starting to get used to it.  "
"Things were pretty rough after Sean died, but it wasn't our first big loss "
"and it won't be the last I guess.  I've made a couple friends, and in a weird "
"way we're all like family.  We were all hoping they'd let us downstairs "
"sooner than this though.  We're never quite sure if there's going to be "
"enough food to go around.  I'm really hoping I can lose myself in this "
"project.  Still haven't had a good night's sleep since <the_cataclysm>."
msgstr ""
"Cela fait plus d'un mois maintenant, alors je crois que je commence à m'y "
"habituer. Les choses ont été assez difficiles après la mort de Sean, mais ce "
"n'était pas notre première grande perte et ce ne sera pas la dernière, je "
"pense. Je me suis fait quelques amis et, bizarrement, nous sommes tous comme "
"une famille. Nous espérions tous qu'ils nous laisseraient descendre plus tôt "
"que cela. Nous ne sommes jamais sûrs qu'il y aura assez de nourriture pour "
"tout le monde. J'espère vraiment pouvoir me perdre dans ce projet. Je n'ai "
"toujours pas eu une bonne nuit de sommeil depuis <the_cataclysm>."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Living here?  Yeah, I guess I live here now.  It's… it's weird.  We're "
"crowded into this tiny space, I don't know these people, but we're sharing "
"bathrooms and we've all been through the same stuff.  It's not great.  At "
"night we can hear the <zombies> outside, and we all just lie there awake, "
"thinking the same things but too scared to talk about it."
msgstr ""
"Vous vivez ici ? Oui, je crois que je vis ici maintenant. C'est... c'est "
"bizarre. On est entassés dans ce petit espace, je ne connais pas ces gens, "
"mais on partage les salles de bains et on a tous vécu les mêmes choses. Ce "
"n'est pas génial. La nuit, on entend les <zombies> dehors, et on reste là, "
"éveillés, à penser aux mêmes choses, mais trop effrayés pour en parler."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about the Free Merchants?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet des Marchands Libres?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about Fatima?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet de Fatima?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What has made you friends with Dana, Draco, and Aleesha?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qui a rendu Dana, Draco, Aleesha et vous proches?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about the Borichenkos?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet des Borichenkos?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about the Singhs?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet des Singhs?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about the others?"
msgstr "Que pouvez-vous me dire au sujet des autres?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"For better or worse, we're a community now.  Fatima and I work together a "
"fair bit, and I consider Dana, Draco, and Aleesha my friends, and so of "
"course I've gotten to know Dana's husband Pedro too.  The Borichenkos are "
"their own sweet brand of messed up, like all of us.  The Singhs have each "
"other, and keep mostly to themselves.  Vanessa and I don't see eye to eye, "
"but I'm still glad she's here.  Uyen and Rhyzaea are always bickering about "
"leadership decisions, as if they made those kind of calls.  What did you want "
"to know?"
msgstr ""
"Pour le meilleur ou pour le pire, nous formons désormais une communauté. "
"Fatima et moi travaillons beaucoup ensemble, et je considère Dana, Draco et "
"Aleesha comme mes amis, et j'ai donc appris à connaître Pedro, le mari de "
"Dana. Les Borichenkos sont des gens un peu dérangés, comme nous tous. Les "
"Singhs sont entre eux et restent pour la plupart entre eux. Vanessa et moi ne "
"sommes pas du même avis, mais je suis quand même content qu'elle soit là. "
"Uyen et Rhyzaea sont toujours en train de se chamailler à propos des "
"décisions des dirigeants, comme si c'était eux qui prenaient ce genre de "
"décisions. Qu'est-ce que tu voulais savoir ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, there's a bunch of us.  We're starting to form a bit of a community.  "
"Fatima and I work together a fair bit, and I've been hanging out with Dana, "
"Draco, and Aleesha quite a lot.  I don't know the Borichenko bunch, the "
"Singhs, Vanessa, Uyen, or Rhyzaea quite as well, but we've talked.  What did "
"you want to know?"
msgstr ""
"Nous sommes plusieurs. Nous commençons à former une sorte de communauté. "
"Fatima et moi travaillons pas mal ensemble, et je traîne beaucoup avec Dana, "
"Draco et Aleesha. Je ne connais pas aussi bien les Borichenko, les Singh, "
"Vanessa, Uyen ou Rhyzaea, mais nous avons discuté. Que vouliez-vous savoir ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They run this place, and they don't run a charity.  We get paid for working "
"around the place, maintaining it, what have you, and we trade cash for food.  "
"The thing is, supply and demand and all… there's a lot more cash than food "
"around.  It's easier to buy a laptop than a piece of beef jerky, and there's "
"no sign of that getting better.  The balance is way off right now, a hard day "
"of work barely gets you enough to fill your belly.  I shouldn't bitch too "
"much though.  I don't know much better way to run it, although rumor is that "
"the folks living downstairs have it a lot easier than we do.  I try not to "
"think too much on that."
msgstr ""
"Ce sont eux qui gèrent cet endroit, et ils ne font pas de charité. Nous "
"sommes payés pour travailler autour de l'endroit, l'entretenir, et nous "
"échangeons de l'argent contre de la nourriture. Le problème, c'est que "
"l'offre et la demande et tout le reste... il y a beaucoup plus d'argent que "
"de nourriture. Il est plus facile d'acheter un ordinateur portable qu'un "
"morceau de bœuf séché, et il n'y a aucun signe d'amélioration. L'équilibre "
"est loin d'être atteint, une dure journée de travail permet à peine de se "
"remplir la panse. Mais je ne devrais pas trop me plaindre. Je ne connais pas "
"de meilleure façon de gérer les choses, même si la rumeur dit que les gens "
"qui vivent en bas ont la vie bien plus facile que nous. J'essaie de ne pas "
"trop y penser."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fatima's a sweety, but she's a total dork.  I know, I know, it's backwards "
"for the engineer to call the heavy-duty mechanic a nerd, but hey.  I call it "
"like it is.  She and I have been doing some odd jobs around the upstairs "
"here, fixing up old machinery and things."
msgstr ""
"Fatima est gentille, mais c'est une vraie nunuche. Je sais, je sais, c'est à "
"l'envers pour l'ingénieur de traiter le mécanicien de gros bras d'intello, "
"mais bon. Je dis les choses telles qu'elles sont. Elle et moi avons fait "
"quelques petits travaux à l'étage, réparant de vieilles machines et d'autres "
"choses."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, Dana lost her baby right after <the_cataclysm>, in a bus rollover.  She "
"was lucky to make it out alive.  She and Pedro had one of the rougher trips "
"here, I guess.  We just kinda click as friends, I'm grateful there's someone "
"else here I can really get along with.  Her husband, Pedro, is still pretty "
"shell-shocked.  He doesn't talk much.  I like him though, when he opens up "
"he's just hilarious.  Draco is just a cantankerous old fart who hasn't "
"actually got old yet, give him twenty years and he'll be there.  I like "
"grumpy people.  We also have pretty similar taste in music.  Aleesha's a "
"sweet kid, and we've all kind of adopted her, but she seems to hang out with "
"me and Dana the most.  She's a great artist, and she's full of crazy ideas.  "
"I guess I like her because of all of us, she seems to have the most hope that "
"there's a future to be had."
msgstr ""
"Dana a perdu son bébé juste après <the_cataclysm>, lors d'un renversement de "
"bus. Elle a eu de la chance de s'en sortir vivante. Pedro et elle ont eu l'un "
"des voyages les plus difficiles ici, je suppose. Nous nous entendons bien en "
"tant qu'amis, je suis reconnaissant qu'il y ait quelqu'un d'autre ici avec "
"qui je peux vraiment m'entendre. Son mari, Pedro, est encore sous le choc. Il "
"ne parle pas beaucoup. Mais je l'aime bien, quand il s'ouvre, il est "
"hilarant. Draco est un vieux schnock acariâtre qui n'a pas encore vieilli, "
"mais dans vingt ans, il sera déjà là. J'aime les gens grincheux. Nous avons "
"aussi des goûts musicaux assez similaires. Aleesha est une enfant adorable, "
"et nous l'avons tous adoptée, mais c'est avec Dana et moi qu'elle passe le "
"plus de temps. C'est une grande artiste et elle est pleine d'idées folles. Je "
"crois que je l'aime bien parce que, de nous tous, c'est elle qui semble avoir "
"le plus d'espoir en l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I didn't get to know Boris, Garry, and Stan so well for the first while.  "
"They kinda kept to themselves.  Boris and Stan had just lost their son, you "
"know.  It's pretty lucky that Garry was with them, he's Stan's little "
"brother.  Together, they're a pretty good team.  I feel bad for thinking they "
"were standoffish before.  They probably do the most to pull their weight "
"around here whenever there's work to be done."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas eu l'occasion de connaître Boris, Garry et Stan pendant les "
"premiers temps. Ils se tenaient un peu à l'écart. Boris et Stan venaient de "
"perdre leur fils. C'est une chance que Garry soit avec eux, c'est le petit "
"frère de Stan. Ensemble, ils forment une bonne équipe. Je m'en veux d'avoir "
"pensé qu'ils étaient distants avant. C'est probablement eux qui font le plus "
"d'efforts ici quand il y a du travail à faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Boris and Stan are married, I guess.  They kinda keep to themselves, they "
"seem a bit standoffish if you ask me.  Garry is Stan's brother, I think, but "
"I'm not totally sure.  He seems nice enough, but he's a man of few words.  I "
"can't get a good bead on them.  I've learned not to pry too much though."
msgstr ""
"Boris et Stan sont mariés, je suppose. Ils se tiennent un peu à l'écart, ils "
"ont l'air un peu distants si vous voulez mon avis. Garry est le frère de "
"Stan, je crois, mais je n'en suis pas tout à fait sûr. Il a l'air assez "
"gentil, mais c'est un homme peu loquace. Je n'arrive pas à les cerner. J'ai "
"appris à ne pas être trop indiscret."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Singhs are really shy, and I think they feel pretty bad about making it "
"through this together.  They're the only complete family I've seen since "
"<the_cataclysm>.  That has to feel really weird, and I think it's made them "
"stick really close together.  I think… I think they also just don't really "
"like any of us."
msgstr ""
"Les Singh sont très timides, et je pense qu'ils se sentent mal à l'aise "
"d'avoir traversé cette épreuve ensemble. C'est la seule famille complète que "
"j'ai vue depuis <the_cataclysm>. Cela doit être vraiment bizarre, et je pense "
"que cela les a poussés à rester très proches les uns des autres. Je crois "
"aussi qu'ils n'aiment aucun d'entre nous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really can't get a bead on them.  They never really talk to anyone outside "
"of their little family group, they just sit in their own spot and speak "
"Punjabi.  They always seem nice, and they do their share, they just don't "
"have any social connection."
msgstr ""
"Je n'arrive pas à les cerner. Ils ne parlent jamais à personne en dehors de "
"leur petit groupe familial, ils se contentent de s'asseoir à leur place et de "
"parler pendjabi. Ils semblent toujours gentils et font leur part, mais ils "
"n'ont aucun lien social."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Vanessa… I'm doing my best, I really am, but we just do not get along.  One "
"of these days one of us is probably going to brain the other with a tire "
"iron, and I'm just grateful I spend more time around the tire irons.  Uyen "
"and Rhyzaea are both excellent people, and I genuinely like them, but I can't "
"stand this ongoing political bullshit they've got going on.  Alonso is just "
"a… he's… there's no polite word for what he is.  A lot of the others are fine "
"with it, and okay, sure, I guess.  John is a walking stereotype, but he's a "
"great poker buddy.  I admit I kinda like him."
msgstr ""
"Vanessa... Je fais de mon mieux, vraiment, mais nous ne nous entendons pas. "
"Un jour ou l'autre, l'une d'entre nous va probablement assommer l'autre avec "
"un démonte-pneu, et je suis reconnaissante de passer plus de temps avec les "
"démonte-pneus. Uyen et Rhyzaea sont tous deux d'excellentes personnes, et je "
"les apprécie sincèrement, mais je ne supporte pas leurs conneries politiques "
"permanentes. Alonso est juste un... il est... il n'y a pas de mot poli pour "
"dire ce qu'il est. Beaucoup d'autres n'y voient pas d'inconvénient, et "
"d'accord, bien sûr, je suppose. John est un stéréotype ambulant, mais c'est "
"un bon copain de poker. J'admets que je l'aime bien."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Vanessa… well, she's nice, I guess.  I gotta say, she kinda drives me nuts, "
"but we're in this together so I try not to be too harsh.  Uyen and Rhyzaea "
"both seem to want to run the show here, but I try to stay out of those "
"politics and just focus on building stuff.  I don't see much good coming of "
"it.  Alonso is fine, he's clearly interested in me, and also in every other "
"single person here.  Not my thing, in a group this small.  John is a walking "
"stereotype, I imagine there must be more depth to him, but I haven't seen it "
"yet."
msgstr ""
"Vanessa... eh bien, elle est gentille, je suppose. Je dois dire qu'elle me "
"rend un peu fou, mais nous sommes dans le même bateau, alors j'essaie de ne "
"pas être trop dur. Uyen et Rhyzaea semblent tous deux vouloir prendre les "
"rênes, mais j'essaie de ne pas me mêler de cette politique et de me "
"concentrer sur la construction. Je ne vois pas ce qu'il y a de bon là-dedans. "
"Alonso va bien, il s'intéresse clairement à moi, et aussi à toutes les autres "
"personnes ici. Ce n'est pas mon truc, dans un groupe aussi restreint. John "
"est un stéréotype ambulant, j'imagine qu'il doit avoir plus de profondeur, "
"mais je ne l'ai pas encore vu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find reference material about air rifles for Jenny."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez des documents de référence sur les carabines à air comprimé pour "
"Jenny."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid ""
"Find reference material about air rifles.  <color_yellow>A book that has "
"'Pneumatic' in its name</color> could be the thing she wants."
msgstr ""
"Trouver des documents de référence sur les fusils à air comprimé. "
"<color_yellow>Un livre dont le nom contient \"Pneumatique\"</color> pourrait "
"être ce qu'elle recherche."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid ""
"If you happen to see anything in your travels about high-powered air rifles, "
"it would help a lot."
msgstr ""
"Si, au cours de vos voyages, vous avez vu quelque chose sur les carabines à "
"air comprimé de grande puissance, cela nous aiderait beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid "Great!  Bring it to me if you find one."
msgstr "Fantastique! Ramenez-moi en un si vous arrivez à en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid "Oh well.  Thanks anyway."
msgstr "Dommage. Merci comme même."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid ""
"Honestly I don't even have a search engine to find the name of a good book.  "
"It's the air compression part I need to know about, gun books won't help much."
msgstr ""
"Honnêtement, je n'ai même pas de moteur de recherche pour trouver le nom d'un "
"bon livre. C'est la partie compression d'air que j'ai besoin de connaître, "
"les livres sur les armes à feu ne m'aideront pas beaucoup."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid "Any sign of an air rifle book I can use?"
msgstr "Un livre sur la carabine à air comprimé serait-il disponible ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
msgid ""
"That's exactly what I need!  Here, I saved a few merch for you, I hope this "
"helps cover your troubles."
msgstr ""
"C'est exactement ce dont j'ai besoin ! Ici, j'ai sauvé quelques marchandises "
"pour vous, j'espère que cela vous aidera à couvrir vos problèmes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find an electric motor"
msgstr "Trouvez un moteur électrique"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid ""
"Yeah, if you want to risk your neck out there and bring me what I need, I'm "
"not gonna say no.  I can't, like, pay you or anything though, you know that "
"right?"
msgstr ""
"Ouais, si tu veux risquer ta peau et m'apporter ce dont j'ai besoin, je ne "
"vais pas dire non. Je ne peux pas, comme, te payer ou quoi que ce soit, tu le "
"sais, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid ""
"Before I get anything going, I'm going to need to set up a compressor.  I "
"have a lot of the stuff for that, but I need a large tank for air, and a good "
"sized electric motor - about 10 kg or so.  I'm also going to need a 60 liter "
"tank, after that."
msgstr ""
"Avant de commencer quoi que ce soit, je vais devoir installer un compresseur. "
"J'ai beaucoup de matériel pour cela, mais j'ai besoin d'un grand réservoir "
"d'air et d'un moteur électrique de bonne taille - environ 10 kg. J'aurai "
"également besoin d'un réservoir de 60 litres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid "Great!  Bring it to me when you find one."
msgstr "Fantastique! Ramenez-moi en un si vous arrivez à en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid "Oh well.  Thanks for offering anyway."
msgstr "Dommage. Merci tout de même d'avoir essayé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid ""
"Try a basic hybrid car, or maybe farm equipment that uses an electric motor.  "
"The kind on a bike would be too small, and the kind on those fancy Edison "
"sports cars is going to be too big."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid "Any sign of a motor I can use?"
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé un moteur électrique que je peux utiliser?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
msgid ""
"That's exactly what I need!  Want to talk about that tank now?  I saved a few "
"merch for you, by the way."
msgstr ""
"C'est exactement ce dont j'ai besoin ! Tu veux qu'on parle de ce réservoir "
"maintenant ? J'ai gardé quelques marchandises pour toi, au fait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgstr "Ramenez un réservoir en métal de 60L"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgid ""
"Now that I've got that motor, I can get my compressor mostly built.  I will "
"need a tank though."
msgstr ""
"Maintenant que j'ai ce moteur, je peux construire mon compresseur. Il me faut "
"cependant un réservoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgid ""
"I can get started building the compressor, but I need a large metal tank to "
"store compressed air centrally.  About 60 liters should do…"
msgstr ""
"Je peux commencer à construire le compresseur, mais j'ai besoin d'un grand "
"réservoir métallique pour stocker l'air comprimé de manière centralisée.  "
"Environ 60 litres devraient faire l'affaire…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgid ""
"It needs to be a good strong tank, like a big propane tank or something… you "
"could look at fuel storage tanks and things, as long as they're durable "
"enough.  Heck, if you get some sheet metal you could probably even weld a "
"good one together."
msgstr ""
"Il doit s'agir d'un bon réservoir solide, comme une grosse bouteille de "
"propane ou quelque chose du genre... vous pouvez envisager des réservoirs de "
"stockage de carburant et d'autres choses, tant qu'ils sont suffisamment "
"résistants. Si tu trouves de la tôle, tu pourras probablement en souder une "
"bonne."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgid "Any sign of a tank I can use?"
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé un réservoir que je peux utiliser?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
msgid ""
"Hey, this is perfect, \"tanks\" a bunch.  Okay, I'm sorry for that.  Anyway, "
"now that I've got the parts, I might be able to build a proof of concept.  "
"First I gotta get this thing up and running, and argue with the bean counters "
"about letting me draw power to run it.  Oh right, and here's some merch, "
"thanks for the help!"
msgstr ""
"Hey, c'est parfait, \"tanks\" un peu partout. D'accord, je suis désolé. Quoi "
"qu'il en soit, maintenant que j'ai les pièces, je pourrais peut-être "
"construire une preuve de concept. Il faut d'abord que je mette ce truc en "
"marche et que je discute avec les comptables pour qu'ils me laissent puiser "
"de l'énergie pour le faire fonctionner. Ah oui, et voici un peu de "
"merchandising, merci pour l'aide !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"Huh.  This isn't going to work like I thought.  Back to the drawing board I "
"guess."
msgstr ""
"Huh. Cela ne va pas fonctionner comme je le pensais. Retour à la planche à "
"dessin, je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgstr "Trouvez un manuel d'armurerie"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"Find a gunsmithing textbook for Jenny.  <color_yellow>A book with "
"'Gunsmithing' and/or 'Firearm Design' in its name</color> will do."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez un manuel d'armurerie pour Jenny. <color_yellow>Un livre avec "
"\"Armurerie\" et/ou \"Conception d'armes à feu\" dans son nom</color> fera "
"l'affaire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"I hate to admit it, but my first few tests haven't gone well.  I think I know "
"what's wrong, but I need more information."
msgstr ""
"Je n'aime pas l'admettre, mais mes premiers tests ne se sont pas bien "
"déroulés. Je pense savoir ce qui ne va pas, mais j'ai besoin de plus "
"d'informations."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"I need a good quality reference book on gunsmithing.  This isn't my area of "
"expertise, and I don't want to blow anybody up."
msgstr ""
"J'ai besoin d'un livre de référence de bonne qualité sur l'armurerie. Ce "
"n'est pas mon domaine d'expertise et je ne veux pas faire exploser quelqu'un."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"This is a bit of a tricky one.  A college library would be a good start, and "
"I imagine maybe military bases have that kind of thing?  I'm not entirely "
"sure."
msgstr ""
"C'est une question un peu délicate. La bibliothèque d'un établissement "
"d'enseignement supérieur serait un bon début, et j'imagine que les bases "
"militaires disposent peut-être de ce genre de choses ? Je n'en suis pas tout "
"à fait sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid "Any luck looking for that gunsmithing text?"
msgstr "Avez-vous réussi à trouver ce texte sur l'armurerie ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
msgid ""
"Oh yeah.  Ooooh yeah.  Now we're cookin' with gas.  Here's a bit more merch, "
"you beautiful gofer maniac."
msgstr ""
"Oh, oui. Ooooh yeah. Maintenant nous cuisinons avec du gaz. Voici un peu plus "
"de marchandise, beau maniaque de la gaffe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "John Clemens"
msgstr "John Clemens"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, John."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer John."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi John, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut John, ravi·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, John.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut John. Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice to meet you too.  I reckon' you got some questions 'bout this place."
msgstr ""
"Enchanté de vous rencontrer également. Je pense que vous avez des questions "
"sur cet endroit."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I sure do."
msgstr "Oui j'en suis sûr·e."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What can I do ya for?"
msgstr "Que puis-je faire pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My story?  Just a wanderin' cowhand, eatin' dust on the trail.  I settled "
"here for a spell after I came upon some hard times."
msgstr ""
"Mon histoire ? Juste un vacher errant, mangeant de la poussière sur la piste. "
"Je me suis installé ici pendant un certain temps après avoir connu des temps "
"difficiles."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You… you do know what's going on here, right?  With the evacuation and stuff?"
msgstr ""
"Vous… vous savez ce qui se passe ici, n'est-ce pas?  Avec l'évacuation et "
"tout ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Course I do, I ain't an idjit.  It's all the folks here c'n talk about."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je ne suis pas un idiot. C'est tout ce dont les gens ici peuvent "
"parler."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So what, uh, what happened to you?"
msgstr "Alors, qu'est-ce qui vous est arrivé ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks at you like you're in need of special help.  \"Just what I said.  I'm "
"settled down here for a spell, then goin' back on the road with my sixgun.\""
msgstr ""
"*Je vous regarde comme si vous aviez besoin d'une aide particulière. \"C'est "
"ce que j'ai dit. Je m'installe ici pour un temps, puis je repars sur la route "
"avec mon fusil.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I reckon I've done my job here.  Goan' be time to ride out into the sunset "
"soon, if'n you catch m'drift.\"  He tilts his hat melodramatically.  "
"\"Folks're comin' around to this here new world we live in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Folks don't like bein' kept from the blue sky for too long.  Cooped up like "
"cattle in a barn… we need pastures to run free, if'n y'get my drift.  'Til we "
"got 'em, it's gonna be tense in here."
msgstr ""
"Les gens n'aiment pas être tenus à l'écart du ciel bleu pendant trop "
"longtemps.  Enfermés comme du bétail dans une étable… nous avons besoin de "
"pâturages pour courir librement, si vous voyez ce que je veux dire.  Jusqu'à "
"ce qu'on les ait, ça va être tendu ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Mandeep Singh"
msgstr "Mandeep Singh"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*is a middle-aged man with a crisp turban and a large blade at his side.  He "
"meets your gaze as you approach, his expression stony.  \"Hello "
msgstr ""
"*C'est un homme d'âge moyen, coiffé d'un turban impeccable et portant une "
"grande lame au côté. Il croise votre regard lorsque vous vous approchez, son "
"expression est glaciale. \"Bonjour"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "sir"
msgstr "monsieur"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "ma'am"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  I am Mandeep Singh.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Mandeep."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Mandeep."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Mandeep, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Mandeep, enchanté·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*peers at you with his intense gaze, his face unreadable.  \"Hello again.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Mandeep.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Mandeep. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Mandeep.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Mandeep.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It is nice to meet you as well.  Can I help you with something?"
msgstr "Je suis également ravie de vous rencontrer. Puis-je vous aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I understand.  I don't know if I have many answers for you."
msgstr "Je comprends. Je ne sais pas si j'ai beaucoup de réponses à vous donner."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My story?  It is much the same as everyone's, I fear.  Loss and violence.  I "
"have not lost as much as many; by the grace of the Lord I have still got my "
"wife and son.  I could not be more grateful."
msgstr ""
"Mon histoire ? Je crains qu'elle ne soit semblable à celle de tout le monde. "
"Perte et violence. Je n'ai pas perdu autant que beaucoup d'autres ; par la "
"grâce du Seigneur, j'ai encore ma femme et mon fils. Je ne pourrais pas être "
"plus reconnaissant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about yourself.  What did you do before?"
msgstr "Parlez-moi de vous. Que faisiez-vous avant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you and your family make it here?"
msgstr "Comment vous et votre famille êtes-vous arrivés jusqu'ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*he blinks, looking a bit surprised.  \"'Before'.  It sounds so dramatic, "
"doesn't it?  I suppose drama is appropriate.  Well, in India, I was actually "
"a junior university professor, in archaeology.  When I brought my family to "
"the United States, I was to have a job at Emerson.\"  He smiles sadly.  "
"\"Things don't always work out as we hope.  Most lately, I have been driving "
"truck for UPS.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il cligne des yeux, l'air un peu surpris. \"Avant\". Ça a l'air tellement "
"dramatique, n'est-ce pas ? Je suppose que c'est approprié. En Inde, j'étais "
"en fait un jeune professeur d'université en archéologie. Lorsque j'ai emmené "
"ma famille aux États-Unis, je devais travailler à Emerson.\" Il sourit "
"tristement. \"Les choses ne se passent pas toujours comme on l'espère. "
"Dernièrement, j'ai été chauffeur de camion pour UPS.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened with your professor job?"
msgstr "Que s'est-il passé avec votre poste de professeur ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shakes his head briefly.  \"I will not bore you with tales of a past that "
"will never again matter.  Suffice to say that the offers I thought I had were "
"not what I believed them to be.  I am fortunate at least that I was able to "
"bring my family.  We made a good life for ourselves, though I often wonder "
"what it would have been had we stayed.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il secoue brièvement la tête. \"Je ne vous ennuierai pas avec les récits "
"d'un passé qui n'aura plus jamais d'importance. Il suffit de dire que les "
"offres que je pensais avoir n'étaient pas ce que je croyais. J'ai au moins la "
"chance d'avoir pu faire venir ma famille. Nous avons réussi notre vie, même "
"si je me demande souvent ce qu'elle aurait été si nous étions restés.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That is a hard question to ask a man, in these times.\"  He looks you up and "
"down carefully for a moment, shifting a little on his feet.  \"To be honest "
"with you, I made a delivery run here a few months ago to drop off some office "
"supplies.  When I saw the state the world was in, I thought perhaps this "
"would be a safer place to go than many, and so we made our way here.  It was "
"a difficult journey, but I'm sure you've heard many tales of that time, and "
"have your own.  We were nearly gunned down at a road stop, but I knew a back "
"route and managed to slip away.  There was a pickup truck with a travel "
"trailer that tried to take the back route, though, and overturned.  It nearly "
"blocked the road, and the trailer had been full of people.  Many of them were "
"now returned, and were stumbling around.  We made it through, barely, but the "
"car was damaged then.  You get the idea.\"  He sighs, rubbing his beard idly, "
"his expression flat.  \"Somehow, we made it.  What's more, all three of us "
"made it, and again made it through the disaster in the back room here.  We "
"were very lucky."
msgstr ""
"C'est une question difficile à poser à un homme, à notre époque\". Il vous "
"regarde attentivement de haut en bas pendant un moment, se déplaçant un peu "
"sur ses pieds. \"Pour être honnête avec vous, j'ai fait une livraison ici il "
"y a quelques mois pour déposer des fournitures de bureau. Quand j'ai vu "
"l'état dans lequel se trouvait le monde, j'ai pensé que ce serait peut-être "
"un endroit plus sûr que d'autres, et c'est ainsi que nous nous sommes rendus "
"ici. Ce fut un voyage difficile, mais je suis sûr que vous avez entendu de "
"nombreux récits de cette époque, et que vous avez les vôtres. Nous avons "
"failli être abattus à un arrêt routier, mais je connaissais un chemin de "
"traverse et j'ai réussi à m'enfuir. Une camionnette avec une caravane a "
"essayé de prendre le chemin inverse et s'est renversée. Elle a presque bloqué "
"la route, et la caravane était pleine de gens. Beaucoup d'entre eux étaient "
"revenus et trébuchaient. Nous avons réussi à passer, de justesse, mais la "
"voiture a été endommagée. Vous voyez ce que je veux dire. Il soupire, se "
"frotte la barbe, l'expression est plate. \"On a réussi à s'en sortir. Qui "
"plus est, nous nous en sommes sortis tous les trois, et encore une fois, nous "
"avons survécu au désastre qui s'est produit dans l'arrière-boutique. Nous "
"avons eu beaucoup de chance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Are you kidding?  That sounds like an amazing story.  What happened after you "
"got past the trailer?"
msgstr ""
"Vous plaisantez ? C'est une histoire incroyable. Que s'est-il passé une fois "
"la caravane passée ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles, very briefly, and nods.  \"Very well.  The blockage had forced us to "
"go through the woods, and our rusty old sedan was not suited to it.  We must "
"have jarred something loose, because we were not far past the trailer when "
"there was a loud bang, and the wheels stopped turning.  The engine spun and "
"the axles rattled, but it was all sound and fury, signifying nothing.  We'd "
"moved far enough from the overturned trailer to buy time, but as we got out "
"of the vehicle, we could hear their moans on the wind, drawing closer.\"  As "
"he dives into the story, Mandeep becomes more animated, his resonant accented "
"voice carrying naturally over the rolling cadence of his words.  \"I am no "
"mechanic, and even if I were, there was no time for repairs.  We took what we "
"owned and carried on on foot.  The center was not far, I knew, and at least "
"Guneet and I had our kirpan, should we be forced to defend ourselves.\"  He "
"touches the handle of the sword at his side, giving you a moment to interrupt "
"if you want."
msgstr ""
"*sourire, très brièvement, et hochement de tête. \"Très bien. Le blocage nous "
"a obligés à passer par les bois, et notre vieille berline rouillée n'était "
"pas adaptée. Nous avons dû détacher quelque chose, car nous n'étions pas loin "
"de la caravane lorsque nous avons entendu une forte détonation et que les "
"roues se sont arrêtées de tourner. Le moteur tournait et les essieux "
"s'entrechoquaient, mais ce n'était que du bruit et de la fureur, qui ne "
"signifiaient rien. Nous nous étions suffisamment éloignés de la remorque "
"renversée pour gagner du temps, mais en sortant du véhicule, nous pouvions "
"entendre leurs gémissements dans le vent, qui se rapprochaient\". Au fur et à "
"mesure qu'il s'enfonce dans son récit, Mandeep s'anime, sa voix résonnante et "
"accentuée portant naturellement sur la cadence roulante de ses mots. \"Je ne "
"suis pas mécanicien, et même si je l'étais, nous n'avions pas le temps de "
"faire des réparations. Nous avons pris ce que nous possédions et avons "
"continué à pied. Le centre n'était pas loin, je le savais, et au moins Guneet "
"et moi avions notre kirpan, au cas où nous serions obligés de nous "
"défendre.\" Il touche la poignée de l'épée qu'il porte à son côté, vous "
"laissant un moment pour l'interrompre si vous le souhaitez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Say nothing.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The roads further on were muddy: soon, we couldn't walk any further.  Our "
"pace was enough to keep us ahead of the dead, but I feared for our safety "
"should we stop.  We went on until we had no choice.  Our feet blistered in "
"shoes not meant for such a journey, and our packs weighed us down; we knew "
"that if we met any more zombies, we couldn't escape nor fight them.  At last, "
"a long-abandoned shack gave us refuge, its roof collapsed and its windows "
"boarded up.\"  He flares his nostrils.  \"I had expected some awful smell, "
"and animal dung, but to be honest, it was still surprisingly dry and dusty "
"inside.  We had a packed lunch, and feasted on cold, leftover samosa that "
"night.\"  With a little wink, he pats his belly.  \"I suppose it was the last "
"time I enjoyed my wife's home cooking, in a way.  It was hard to enjoy it.  "
"Under no circumstances could we risk a fire.  We each took a turn guarding in "
"the dark, and got what sleep we could in the cold of that old ruin.\"  "
"Glancing around at the cramped shelter room, he pauses for a moment.  \"It "
"seems almost like a memory that didn't happen, too outlandish to fit with the "
"rest of my mundane life.  The next day dawned, damp and cold, but without "
"pursuers.  By then I was confident we'd lost the zombies.\"  He gives you a "
"solemn look.  \"That is, truly, the end of this story.  Once the sun was up, "
"we made our way through the forest, onto the road, and from there it was a "
"short walk to this center."
msgstr ""
"Plus loin, les routes étaient boueuses : bientôt, nous ne pouvions plus "
"marcher. Notre rythme était suffisant pour nous permettre de devancer les "
"morts, mais je craignais pour notre sécurité si nous nous arrêtions. Nous "
"avons continué jusqu'à ce que nous n'ayons plus le choix. Nos pieds étaient "
"couverts d'ampoules dans des chaussures qui n'étaient pas faites pour un tel "
"voyage, et nos sacs nous alourdissaient ; nous savions que si nous "
"rencontrions d'autres zombies, nous ne pourrions ni les fuir ni les "
"combattre. Enfin, une cabane abandonnée depuis longtemps nous a servi de "
"refuge, son toit s'est effondré et ses fenêtres sont condamnées\". Il ouvre "
"les narines. \"Je m'attendais à une odeur nauséabonde, à des excréments "
"d'animaux, mais pour être honnête, l'intérieur était étonnamment sec et "
"poussiéreux. Nous avions emporté notre déjeuner et nous nous sommes régalés "
"de samosas froids ce soir-là.\" Avec un petit clin d'œil, il se tapote le "
"ventre. \"Je suppose que c'est la dernière fois que j'ai apprécié la cuisine "
"familiale de ma femme, d'une certaine manière. C'était difficile de "
"l'apprécier. Nous ne pouvions en aucun cas risquer un incendie. Chacun "
"montait la garde à tour de rôle dans l'obscurité et dormait comme il pouvait "
"dans le froid de cette vieille ruine.\" Il jette un coup d'œil sur la pièce "
"exiguë de l'abri et s'arrête un instant. \"Cela ressemble presque à un "
"souvenir qui n'a pas eu lieu, trop bizarre pour s'intégrer au reste de ma vie "
"banale. Le jour suivant s'est levé, humide et froid, mais sans poursuivants. "
"J'étais alors persuadé que nous avions perdu les zombies\". Il vous jette un "
"regard solennel. \"C'est vraiment la fin de cette histoire. Une fois le "
"soleil levé, nous nous sommes frayé un chemin à travers la forêt, jusqu'à la "
"route, et de là, il n'y avait qu'une courte marche jusqu'à ce centre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The situation is tense, but it seems like things are slowly improving.  This "
"place isn't home, but we're starting to become a community.  Perhaps, in "
"time, I will call some of these people friends.  At least we don't feel like "
"outsiders so much anymore."
msgstr ""
"La situation est tendue, mais il semble que les choses s'améliorent "
"lentement. Nous ne sommes pas chez nous, mais nous commençons à former une "
"communauté. Peut-être qu'avec le temps, j'appellerai certaines de ces "
"personnes des amis. Au moins, nous ne nous sentons plus autant étrangers."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It is hard for me to say.  No one is happy here.  I sense that some are "
"frustrated that my family and I have escaped the end of the world apparently "
"unscathed.  That, and perhaps some other things, have made it hard for us to "
"make close friends here."
msgstr ""
"Il m'est difficile de le dire. Personne n'est heureux ici. Je sens que "
"certains sont frustrés que ma famille et moi ayons échappé à la fin du monde, "
"apparemment indemnes. C'est pour cette raison, et peut-être pour d'autres "
"raisons, qu'il nous a été difficile de nous faire des amis proches ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Mangalpreet Singh"
msgstr "Mangalpreet Singh"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Mangalpreet."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Mangalpreet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Mangalpreet, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Mangalpreet, enchanté·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*gives you a solemn nod of recognition.  \""
msgstr "*vous fait un signe de tête solennel en guise de reconnaissance. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi there."
msgstr "Salut."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hello there."
msgstr "Oh, bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Mangalpreet."
msgstr "Bonjour Mangalpreet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Mangalpreet.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Mangalpreet.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, I'm glad to meet you too.  Will you be staying with us?  I thought they "
"were taking no more refugees."
msgstr ""
"Oui, je suis également ravie de vous rencontrer. Allez-vous rester avec nous "
"? Je croyais qu'ils n'acceptaient plus de réfugiés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm a traveler actually.  Just saying hello."
msgstr "Je suis un voyageur en fait. Je dis juste bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Is there anything you'd like to talk about?"
msgstr "Vous voulez discuter de quelque chose d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not really.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Pas vraiment.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Before the end of the world, I was the vice principal of an elementary "
"school.  Now, I'm not sure what I am.  A person without a purpose."
msgstr ""
"Avant la fin du monde, j'étais directeur adjoint d'une école primaire. "
"Maintenant, je ne sais pas trop ce que je suis. Une personne sans but."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I have my family.  I have the Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr "J'ai ma famille. J'ai le Guru Granth Sahib."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  For a while, I thought these might not be enough but… I am allowing myself "
"to hope"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  I have these things, but I do not have peace.  No one here does"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  Still, we have so much work to do to make a home here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  We are crowded, we are plagued by the sounds and the memories of the dead. "
" The situation is grim."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Pablo Nunez"
msgstr "Pablo Nunez"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Dana wanted me to be the one to let you know: they've got work for you over "
"at the ranch.  You could get out of here if you want."
msgstr ""
"Dana voulait que ce soit moi qui te fasse savoir qu'ils ont du travail pour "
"toi au ranch. Tu peux partir d'ici si tu veux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  Bye, Pablo."
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  Au revoir Pablo."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up at you with a young faced lined prematurely with concern.  \"Hi "
"there.  I'm Pablo, nice to see a new face.\""
msgstr ""
"*regarde vers vous avec un jeune visage prématurément doublé d'inquiétude. "
"\"Bonjour à tous. Je suis Pablo, content de voir un nouveau visage.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pablo, hey?  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "Pablo? Enchanté·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Pablo, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Pablo, ravi·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*dusts off his jacket and makes eye contact with you.  \""
msgstr "*Il époussette sa veste et vous regarde dans les yeux. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello, nice to see you again."
msgstr "Bonjour, je suis heureux de vous revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Pablo.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Pablo. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Pablo, nice to see you too.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We don't get many new faces around here.  How can I help you?"
msgstr "We don't get many new faces around here. How can I help you?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's been a rough time, adapting to everything that's going on.  What would "
"you like to know about?"
msgstr ""
"Cela n'a pas été facile de s'adapter à tout ce qui se passe. Qu'aimeriez-vous "
"savoir ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was an accountant before.  Just finished my CPA last year and I already had "
"a position as a manager at my firm.  Everything was looking good.  We decided "
"we were ready for a baby.  Hindsight makes us idiots, hey?"
msgstr ""
"J'étais comptable auparavant. Je venais de terminer mon CPA l'année dernière "
"et j'avais déjà un poste de manager dans mon entreprise. Tout allait bien. "
"Nous avons décidé que nous étions prêts à avoir un bébé. Le recul fait de "
"nous des idiots, hein ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you wind up in this place?"
msgstr "Comment avez-vous atterri ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dana and I were evacuated early, because of her pregnancy.  They took us to a "
"concentration center, and then we got on a bus to come here.  The bus though, "
"it was rolled over by a giant monster, and many died.  We made it out along "
"with a few others, and we kept going until we made it here.  It wasn't much "
"farther, and for some reason the monster didn't chase us, just kept tearing "
"at the bus."
msgstr ""
"Dana et moi avons été évacuées plus tôt, en raison de sa grossesse. Ils nous "
"ont emmenées dans un centre de concentration, puis nous sommes montées dans "
"un bus pour venir ici. Mais le bus a été renversé par un monstre géant, et "
"beaucoup sont morts. Nous nous en sommes sortis avec quelques autres, et nous "
"avons continué à avancer jusqu'à ce que nous arrivions ici. Ce n'était pas "
"très loin, et pour une raison quelconque, le monstre ne nous a pas "
"poursuivis, il a juste continué à déchirer le bus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about the pregnancy?"
msgstr "Qu'en est-il de la grossesse?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What happened to the other crash survivors?"
msgstr "Qu'est-il arrivé aux autres survivants de l'accident ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The doctor did what she could but after the accident and the stress of the "
"attack… No."
msgstr ""
"Le médecin a fait ce qu'il a pu, mais après l'accident et le stress de "
"l'attaque… Non."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks.  No, really, thank you.  Others have gone through so much I feel like "
"we should suck it up, but Rhy says we should let ourselves mourn properly and "
"she seems to know her stuff."
msgstr ""
"Merci. Non, vraiment, merci. Les autres ont tellement souffert que j'ai "
"l'impression que nous devrions nous résigner, mais Rhy dit que nous devrions "
"faire notre deuil correctement et elle a l'air de s'y connaître."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"From the bus?  A few of us made it in the end; the Singh family were on that "
"bus with us.  We were some of the last refugees to arrive.\"  He gestures to "
"three people gathered together a short distance away.  \"They put us into a "
"room for processing, where a bunch of the wounded were being handled as best "
"as they could manage.  They were short staffed though, and they missed one.  "
"We all thought he was just having a nap, but he wasn't,\" Pablo wipes his "
"face with his hand and pauses for a moment.  \"When he got back up as a "
"zombie, there was a huge panic.  Gunshots in a small, crowded room, and "
"trampling… it was really ugly.  We were close to the door and managed to get "
"out right away, but then a couple panicking people closed the place off and "
"left innocent people in there for what seemed like ages, calling it an "
"'outbreak'.  By the time leveler heads prevailed, there weren't many people "
"left in there to recover."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've been back to the quarantined area, cleared it out.  It was ugly back "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Je suis retourné dans la zone de quarantaine, je l'ai nettoyée. C'était moche "
"là-bas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks for that, both for taking away the constant worry about all those "
"<zombies> close at hand, and for putting those poor souls at rest at last."
msgstr ""
"Merci pour cela, à la fois pour vous débarrasser de l'inquiétude constante "
"concernant tous ces <zombies> à portée de main, et pour mettre ces pauvres "
"âmes enfin au repos."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's pretty tough here.  People have made so much effort to make things "
"better, and the group is kind of coming together, but I just don't feel like "
"I could ever belong, you know?  I need somewhere with a sky, and a little "
"privacy."
msgstr ""
"C'est assez difficile ici. Les gens ont fait tellement d'efforts pour "
"améliorer les choses, et le groupe est en train de se constituer, mais je ne "
"me sens pas à ma place, vous savez ? J'ai besoin d'un endroit avec un ciel et "
"un peu d'intimité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's pretty tough here.  We're packed into too small a location with too many "
"people.  Everyone is dealing with their own trauma.  Rhy is trying to help "
"out, but she can't be a proper counselor in these circumstances.  I don't "
"know how we're going to survive for long.  As for me, I wish I could be "
"anywhere but here.  I need to see the sky again, or I'm going to go insane."
msgstr ""
"La situation est assez difficile ici. Nous sommes entassés dans un endroit "
"trop petit avec trop de monde. Chacun doit faire face à son propre "
"traumatisme. Rhy essaie de nous aider, mais elle ne peut pas être un bon "
"conseiller dans ces circonstances. Je ne sais pas comment nous allons "
"survivre longtemps. Quant à moi, j'aimerais être n'importe où ailleurs "
"qu'ici. J'ai besoin de revoir le ciel, ou je vais devenir fou."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why not move to the Tacoma Commune?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ne pas juste rejoindre la Commune Tacoma?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got a secure base.  You and your wife could come with me."
msgstr "J'ai une base sécurisée. Vous et votre femme pourriez venir avec moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I heard about that place.  What use would they have for an accountant, "
"though?  If they have work for my wife Dana and I, I'd definitely consider it."
msgstr ""
"J'ai entendu parler de cet endroit. Mais quelle utilité auraient-ils pour un "
"comptable ? S'ils ont du travail pour ma femme Dana et moi, j'y réfléchirai "
"certainement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is amazing news!  Thank you so much!  I've talked to some of the traders "
"who have been there and I really think I can help, mostly with the manual "
"labor but also with the bookkeeping end.  It sounds so much better than this "
"place.  Thanks, my friend!  We'll get packing, and see if we can get a place "
"on the next caravan out.  It'll be a little while I'm sure, but at least our "
"child won't be born in captivity."
msgstr ""
"C'est une nouvelle extraordinaire ! Merci beaucoup ! J'ai parlé à certains "
"des commerçants qui sont passés par là et je pense vraiment que je peux "
"aider, surtout pour le travail manuel, mais aussi pour la comptabilité. Cela "
"semble tellement mieux que cet endroit. Merci, mon ami ! Nous allons faire "
"nos valises et voir si nous pouvons trouver une place dans la prochaine "
"caravane. Cela prendra un peu de temps, j'en suis sûr, mais au moins notre "
"enfant ne naîtra pas en captivité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Really?  I might consider it.  Talk to my wife, Dana.  She's put down a lot "
"more roots here, it would be up to her I think.  I'd go anywhere right now."
msgstr ""
"Vraiment ? Je pourrais y réfléchir. Parlez-en à ma femme, Dana. Elle s'est "
"beaucoup enracinée ici, c'est à elle de décider, je pense. J'irais n'importe "
"où en ce moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#. ~ Mission name
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find out if the Nunez family can find work at
#. Tacoma Ranch."
msgid "Find out if the Nunez family can find work at Tacoma Ranch."
msgstr "Allez voir si la famille Nunez peut trouver du travail au Ranch Tacoma."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/Nunez/NPC_Pablo_Tacoma.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find out if the Nunez family can find work at
#. Tacoma Ranch."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get Pablo some fire bricks."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pass a message to Jenny Forcette."
msgid "n/a"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Rhyzaea Johnny"
msgstr "Rhyzaea Johnny"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What brings you around here?  We don't see a lot of new faces."
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui vous amène ici? On ne croise pas beaucoup de nouvelles têtes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi there.  I don't think we've met before.  I'm Rhyzaea, people call me Rhy."
msgstr ""
"Bonjour. Je ne crois pas que nous ne nous soyons vu avant. Je m'appelle "
"Rhyzaea, mais tout le monde m'appelle Rhy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Rhy."
msgstr "Ravi·e de vous rencontrer Rhy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, Rhy.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Enchanté·e de vous rencontrer Rhy.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*tilts her head in recognition as you approach.  \""
msgstr ""
"*Elle incline la tête en signe de reconnaissance lorsque vous vous approchez. "
"\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Need to talk?"
msgstr "Vous voulez discuter?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Rhy.  How's it going?"
msgstr "Salut Rhy. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, what's your story?  We don't see a lot of new people back here."
msgstr ""
"Alors, quelle est votre histoire ? Nous ne voyons pas beaucoup de nouveaux "
"venus ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a curious traveler.  What's up with you?"
msgstr "Juste un voyageur curieux. Qu'en est-il de vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm doing as well as can be expected, I suppose.  Nice of you to ask."
msgstr "Je m'en sors aussi bien que possible, je suppose. C'est gentil de demander."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's a long, long story.  I'm not from around here, I'm actually from way out "
"in Western Canada.  I'd always wanted to see New England, and I was down here "
"on vacation when, well, you know.  I got evacuated, but because I'm not a US "
"citizen they weren't willing to take me downstairs.  I can understand that, "
"even if I don't like it much.  To tell you the truth I'm still coming to "
"terms with the fact that I'll probably never know how my family and my band "
"are doing."
msgstr ""
"C'est une longue, très longue histoire. Je ne suis pas d'ici, je viens en "
"fait de l'ouest du Canada. J'ai toujours voulu voir la Nouvelle-Angleterre, "
"et j'étais en vacances ici quand, eh bien, vous savez, j'ai été évacué. J'ai "
"été évacuée, mais comme je ne suis pas citoyenne américaine, on n'a pas voulu "
"m'emmener en bas. Je peux le comprendre, même si je n'aime pas trop ça. À "
"vrai dire, je n'arrive toujours pas à accepter le fait que je ne saurai "
"probablement jamais comment vont ma famille et mon groupe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about your band."
msgstr "Parlez-moi de votre groupe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a counselor actually, I worked for my band, Gitxsan.  Did a lot of "
"mental health and addictions for people that had been through some really "
"tough stuff.  Maybe not zombies eating your child level tough, but "
"surprisingly not far off.  My people have gone through some real messy crap."
msgstr ""
"J'étais conseiller en fait, je travaillais pour mon groupe, Gitxsan. Je "
"m'occupais beaucoup de santé mentale et de toxicomanie pour des gens qui "
"avaient vécu des choses très dures. Peut-être pas au niveau des zombies qui "
"mangent votre enfant, mais étonnamment pas loin. Les gens de mon groupe ont "
"traversé de vraies galères."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My band is Gitxsan, we're from Northwestern British Columbia, around the "
"Skeena River.  I'm from Hazelton, myself.  It's a beautiful place.  Tall "
"mountains, temperate rainforests… I partly came here because I love those wet "
"coastal forests, and I love exploring them in other countries.  I've been to "
"Korea and Slovenia for the same reason.  I guess I'm a bit of a forest "
"tourist?  I don't know if I'll ever see my own forest again, and the thought "
"breaks my heart."
msgstr ""
"Mon groupe s'appelle Gitxsan, nous venons du nord-ouest de la "
"Colombie-Britannique, autour de la rivière Skeena. Je suis moi-même "
"originaire d'Hazelton. C'est un endroit magnifique. De hautes montagnes, des "
"forêts pluviales tempérées... Je suis en partie venu ici parce que j'aime ces "
"forêts côtières humides, et j'aime les explorer dans d'autres pays. J'ai été "
"en Corée et en Slovénie pour la même raison. Je suppose que je suis un peu "
"une touriste de la forêt ? Je ne sais pas si je reverrai un jour ma propre "
"forêt, et cette idée me brise le cœur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My mom and dad are back in Hazelton, they live with my grandma and my older "
"brother; he took a hard knock to the head doing dumb things as a kid, and he "
"can't really take care of himself now.  I have a daughter, Angel, she's "
"sixteen and didn't want to come with me on this trip.  God help me, I can't "
"bear to think of her, she must think I'm dead."
msgstr ""
"Ma mère et mon père sont de retour à Hazelton, ils vivent avec ma grand-mère "
"et mon frère aîné ; il a reçu un coup dur à la tête en faisant des bêtises "
"quand il était enfant, et il ne peut plus vraiment s'occuper de lui "
"maintenant. J'ai une fille, Angel, qui a seize ans et qui n'a pas voulu "
"m'accompagner dans ce voyage. Que Dieu me vienne en aide, je ne peux pas "
"supporter de penser à elle, elle doit penser que je suis mort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's tense here.  Maybe it always will be.  Still, things have been getting a "
"bit better lately, and it's showing in a bit of a cascade effect.  It's hard "
"to say what will be the ongoing effects of the trauma we've been through, but "
"in the short term, people are starting to settle into whatever this new life "
"we've got is.  I hope we can keep that going."
msgstr ""
"La situation est tendue ici. Il en sera peut-être toujours ainsi. Pourtant, "
"les choses se sont un peu améliorées ces derniers temps, et cela se traduit "
"par un effet de cascade. Il est difficile de dire quels seront les effets à "
"long terme du traumatisme que nous avons subi, mais à court terme, les gens "
"commencent à s'installer dans cette nouvelle vie qui est la nôtre. J'espère "
"que nous pourrons continuer dans cette voie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There have been a lot of improvements around here, and I think the pressure "
"has gone off a bit.  There's a lot that still needs to be done, of course.  I "
"don't think we're out of the woods yet.  We've all seen things that are hard "
"to even wrap your head around; you know how that is."
msgstr ""
"Il y a eu beaucoup d'améliorations ici, et je pense que la pression est un "
"peu retombée. Il reste encore beaucoup à faire, bien sûr. Je ne pense pas que "
"nous soyons encore sortis d'affaire. Nous avons tous vu des choses qui sont "
"difficiles à comprendre, vous savez ce que c'est."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things are maybe looking up, a tiny bit.  At least there's been some positive "
"change.  Still, people up here are barely hanging on.  I've seen trauma "
"before, a lot, but this is pretty much the worst imaginable.  Everyone has "
"lost everything, with a huge dose of nightmare on top of it all.  We're "
"putting on a brave face, and a little bit of hope is going a long way."
msgstr ""
"Les choses s'améliorent peut-être, un tout petit peu. Au moins, il y a eu des "
"changements positifs. Pourtant, les gens d'ici s'accrochent à peine. J'ai "
"déjà vu des traumatismes, beaucoup, mais celui-ci est à peu près le pire que "
"l'on puisse imaginer. Tout le monde a tout perdu, avec une énorme dose de "
"cauchemar en plus. Nous faisons preuve de courage, et un peu d'espoir fait "
"beaucoup de bien."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"People up here are barely hanging on.  I've seen trauma before, a lot, but "
"this is pretty much the worst imaginable.  Everyone has lost everything, with "
"a huge dose of nightmare on top of it all.  We're putting on a brave face, "
"but without help, things are going to break, really soon."
msgstr ""
"Les gens d'ici s'accrochent à peine. J'ai déjà vu des traumatismes, beaucoup, "
"mais celui-ci est à peu près le pire que l'on puisse imaginer. Tout le monde "
"a tout perdu, avec une énorme dose de cauchemar en plus. Nous faisons bonne "
"figure, mais sans aide, les choses vont se briser, très vite."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Stan Borichenko"
msgstr "Stan Borichenko"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you want to talk about your story?"
msgstr "Voulez-vous parler de votre histoire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*seems to look past you for a while before realizing you are there.  \"Hello. "
" I'm sorry, if we've met before, I don't really remember.  I'm… I'm Stan.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il semble regarder à travers vous pendant un moment avant de s'apercevoir "
"que vous êtes là.  \"Bonjour, je suis désolé, si nous nous sommes déjà "
"rencontrés, je ne m'en souviens pas vraiment.  Je m'appelle… je m'appelle "
"Stan.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Stan, hey?  Nice to meet you."
msgstr "Stan? Enchanté·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Stan, nice to meet you.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Stan, ravi·e de vous rencontrer.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*seems to look past you for a while before realizing you are there.  \""
msgstr ""
"*Il semble vous regarder pendant un moment avant de se rendre compte que vous "
"êtes là. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hm?  Oh, hi."
msgstr "Uhm? oh, bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "…Hi."
msgstr "…Bonjour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Stan.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Stan. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi Stan.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Salut Stan.  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Huh?  Sorry, yes, nice to meet you too."
msgstr "Hein?  Désolé, oui, ravi de vous rencontrer aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem distracted."
msgstr "Vous semblez distrait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm sorry, I've been through some hard stuff.  I'm not really myself lately."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolée, j'ai traversé des moments difficiles. Je ne suis pas "
"vraiment moi-même ces derniers temps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry to hear that.  I'll leave you be."
msgstr "Je suis désolé de l'apprendre. Je vous laisse."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, I don't particularly want to talk about it, but I can I guess.  Before "
"<the_cataclysm> I was an insurance adjuster.  My husband Boris and I were "
"evacuated with my brother Garry, and from our evacuation center we caught a "
"commissioned bus out here.  The bus was attacked by a monster, we lived.  Not "
"everyone on the bus did.  We lost people dear to us, now we're stuck here "
"with little to do but think about it."
msgstr ""
"Non, je n'ai pas particulièrement envie d'en parler, mais je peux le faire. "
"Avant <the_cataclysm>, j'étais expert en assurances. Mon mari Boris et moi "
"avons été évacués avec mon frère Garry, et depuis notre centre d'évacuation, "
"nous avons pris un bus commissionné pour venir ici. Le bus a été attaqué par "
"un monstre, mais nous avons survécu. Ce n'est pas le cas de tout le monde "
"dans le bus. Nous avons perdu des personnes qui nous étaient chères, et "
"maintenant nous sommes coincés ici, avec peu de choses à faire, si ce n'est "
"penser à tout cela."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about Boris."
msgstr "Dites-moi ce que vous savez au sujet de Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about Garry."
msgstr "Dites-moi ce que vous savez au sujet de Garry."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Mostly my family and I have just been mourning.  This isn't the best place to "
"do it.  "
msgstr ""
"La plupart du temps, ma famille et moi avons fait notre deuil. Ce n'est pas "
"le meilleur endroit pour le faire. "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Still, now that we've found ways to make this community a bit of our own, I "
"feel like maybe there's a chance things will get better.  Sometimes, when "
"he's working, Boris seems like himself again and I have some hope."
msgstr ""
"Pourtant, maintenant que nous avons trouvé des moyens de faire de cette "
"communauté un peu la nôtre, j'ai l'impression qu'il y a peut-être une chance "
"que les choses s'améliorent. Parfois, quand il travaille, Boris redevient "
"lui-même et j'ai de l'espoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hope we'll have something productive to do soon; Boris, in particular, has "
"skills to contribute that might help him feel alive again."
msgstr ""
"J'espère que nous aurons bientôt quelque chose de productif à faire ; Boris, "
"en particulier, a des compétences à apporter qui pourraient l'aider à se "
"sentir à nouveau vivant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"He's a strong man.  The things we've been through… that he's been through, "
"before any of this.  If anyone can survive the loss we've seen, it's him.  "
"But he pushes it all down, "
msgstr ""
"C'est un homme fort.  Les choses que nous avons traversées… qu'il a "
"traversées, avant tout ça.  Si quelqu'un peut survivre à tout ce que nous "
"avons vu, c'est lui.  Mais il repousse tout ça, "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"if he's left with it too long.  Having work has been helping him.  Cleaning "
"up that back room might seem small, but it was a big deal for him."
msgstr ""
"s'il reste trop longtemps avec. Le fait d'avoir du travail l'a aidé. Le "
"nettoyage de l'arrière-boutique peut sembler anodin, mais c'était une grande "
"affaire pour lui."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"and if he keeps it up, I don't know how much of him will be left.  He needs "
"something to *do*.  We can't just sit here, trapped like rats in a cage "
"forever."
msgstr ""
"et s'il continue, je ne sais pas ce qu'il restera de lui. Il a besoin de "
"faire quelque chose. Nous ne pouvons pas rester assis ici, piégés comme des "
"rats dans une cage pour toujours."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"  Even more, though, having a little memory of Ash has been more than we "
"could ever have asked.  I thought it might hurt him, dwelling on those "
"memories, but instead it's given both of us some strength back."
msgstr ""
" Mais surtout, le fait d'avoir un petit souvenir d'Ash a été plus que ce que "
"nous aurions pu demander. Je pensais que ça lui ferait du mal de s'attarder "
"sur ces souvenirs, mais au contraire, ça nous a redonné de la force à tous "
"les deux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles thinly.  \"Best little brother a guy could ask for.  He's been with "
"me through everything, literally everything."
msgstr ""
"*sourire fin. \"Le meilleur petit frère qu'un homme puisse demander. Il a été "
"avec moi à travers tout, littéralement tout."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"  I wouldn't wish this world we find ourselves in on anyone, but I'm glad "
"Garry made it through with me.\"  Stan sighs, touching his neck."
msgstr ""
"  Je ne souhaite à personne ce monde dans lequel nous nous trouvons, mais je "
"suis heureux que Garry s'en soit sorti avec moi.\" Stan soupire et se touche "
"le cou."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"\"  He seems to realize where he is suddenly, and the faint smile melts.  "
"\"He's lost too much, too.\""
msgstr ""
"\" Il semble réaliser soudainement où il se trouve, et son léger sourire "
"s'estompe. \"Il a aussi perdu trop de choses.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Uyen Tran"
msgstr "Uyen Tran"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you teach me a bit about first aid?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous m'apprendre quelques choses sur les premiers secours?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too, Uyen."
msgstr "Ravi de vous rencontrer aussi Uyen."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*smiles and brushes her hair out of her eyes.  \""
msgstr "*sourire et brosse ses cheveux hors de ses yeux. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*looks you up and down with a faint smile.  \""
msgstr "*Il vous regarde de haut en bas avec un léger sourire. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*suppresses a yawn, then sees you approaching and nods with recognition.  \""
msgstr ""
"*réprime un bâillement, puis vous voit approcher et hoche la tête en signe de "
"reconnaissance. \""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Uyen.  Got a minute?"
msgstr "Salut Uyen. Vous avez une minute?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just a traveler.  Can I ask you a few things?"
msgstr "Juste un voyageur. Puis-je vous poser quelques questions ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm always good for a talk.  It gets pretty boring down here."
msgstr "Je suis toujours prêt à discuter. On s'ennuie beaucoup ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a paramedic.\"  She idly touches her forehead to brush aside a bit of "
"hair, then notices it's already tucked back.  \"I was there through some of "
"the absolute worst of it, to this day I can't tell you how I made it out.  "
"One thing led to another and I got pushed onto a bus to help take care of a "
"couple people who needed assistance for travel.  Broken arms, that kinda "
"stuff.  I got here early, I was one of the first to arrive.  Then, this woman "
"in processing 'lost' my paperwork while I was busy helping a guy with a bad "
"gash on his head.  If I hadn't made a stink about it, I'd probably be out in "
"the lobby with those poor souls that couldn't get in at all."
msgstr ""
"J'étais secouriste\". Elle se touche le front pour écarter une mèche de "
"cheveux, puis s'aperçoit qu'elle est déjà rabattue. \"J'ai vécu les pires "
"moments de la guerre, et aujourd'hui encore, je ne sais pas comment j'ai pu "
"m'en sortir. Une chose en entraînant une autre, j'ai été poussé dans un bus "
"pour aider à prendre soin de quelques personnes qui avaient besoin d'aide "
"pour voyager. Des bras cassés, ce genre de choses. Je suis arrivé tôt, "
"j'étais l'un des premiers. Puis cette femme a \"perdu\" mes papiers alors que "
"j'étais occupé à aider un homme qui avait une grave entaille à la tête. Si je "
"n'avais pas protesté, je serais probablement dans le hall d'entrée avec les "
"pauvres âmes qui n'ont pas pu entrer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You're medically trained?  Do you know if anyone's found any way to deal with "
"zombie bites?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez une formation médicale ? Savez-vous si quelqu'un a trouvé un moyen "
"de traiter les morsures de zombies ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm not sure what you mean by 'deal with'.  I've been handling zombie bites "
"the same way I handle any other bite.  Clean it and dress it, try to prevent "
"infection.  There's no, like, venom or anything.  Once the wound is cleaned "
"and dressed, it's not going to do anything special.  Zombie mouths are really "
"dirty though, so you want to make sure you do a good job cleaning it out."
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis pas sûr de ce que vous entendez par \"traiter\". J'ai traité les "
"morsures de zombies de la même manière que n'importe quelle autre morsure. Je "
"la nettoie et la panse, j'essaie d'éviter l'infection. Il n'y a pas de venin. "
"Une fois la blessure nettoyée et pansée, il n'y a rien de spécial à faire. "
"Les bouches des zombies sont vraiment sales, alors il faut s'assurer de bien "
"les nettoyer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So if the bites aren't turning people into zombies, what is?"
msgstr ""
"Donc si les morsures ne sont pas ce qui transforme des gens en zombies, "
"qu'est-ce qui le fait?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shrugs.  \"Darned if I know, that's way past my training.  I don't think "
"anyone figured it out anyway, but you'd want a doctor for ideas on that, not "
"a paramedic.  I stabilize and package patients, I don't research cures and "
"causes.\""
msgstr ""
"*hausse les épaules. \"Je ne sais pas si je le sais, c'est bien au-delà de ma "
"formation. Je ne pense pas que quelqu'un l'ait découvert de toute façon, mais "
"c'est un médecin qu'il faudrait consulter pour avoir des idées, pas un "
"secouriste. Je stabilise et emballe les patients, je ne cherche pas les "
"remèdes et les causes.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did you ever think about going into nursing or medicine?"
msgstr "Avez-vous déjà pensé à devenir infirmière ou médecin ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm going to sound like a massive stereotype here, I know, but my parents "
"always pushed hard for me to go into medicine and be a doctor.  I was still "
"thinking it over when, well,\" she gestures expansively around her.  \"Things "
"got complicated.  Honestly though, if the pay were better for being a "
"paramedic I don't know if I'd want to change at all.  I hear there's a lot of "
"burnout after a while, but I haven't seen it yet.  I really liked the work."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles slightly.  \"Everyone's got some idea, hey?  I really don't know.  It "
"seems crazy to even try to guess.  Can you believe we live in a world where "
"corpses come back to life?  There's weirder stuff out there too.  In the "
"hospital, people had all kinds of injuries and talked about seeing monsters.  "
"On the way here, I saw huge creatures in the distance, the sort of thing that "
"belongs in a kaiju movie, not stomping through suburban Worcester.\"  She "
"shrugs.  \"I guess today I'll go with simulation theory.  None of this is "
"real, we're all in a hyper-detailed computer simulation, and the creator is "
"cruel and messing with us.\"  She briefly stares into space, as though "
"looking directly into some imaginary camera.  \"Honestly I don't think any "
"scientific explanation is ever going to get close to the sheer amount of "
"mind-shattering madness around here.\""
msgstr ""
"*sourit légèrement. \"Tout le monde a une idée, hein ? Je ne sais vraiment "
"pas. C'est fou d'essayer de deviner. Pouvez-vous croire que nous vivons dans "
"un monde où les cadavres reviennent à la vie ? Il y a aussi des choses plus "
"étranges. À l'hôpital, les gens avaient toutes sortes de blessures et "
"disaient avoir vu des monstres. En venant ici, j'ai vu d'énormes créatures au "
"loin, le genre de choses qui appartiennent à un film de kaiju, et non pas à "
"la banlieue de Worcester\". Elle hausse les épaules. \"Je crois "
"qu'aujourd'hui, je vais opter pour la théorie de la simulation. Rien de tout "
"cela n'est réel, nous sommes tous dans une simulation informatique "
"hyper-détaillée, et le créateur est cruel et se moque de nous.\" Elle fixe "
"brièvement l'espace, comme si elle regardait directement une caméra "
"imaginaire. \"Honnêtement, je ne pense pas qu'une explication scientifique "
"puisse s'approcher de l'ampleur de la folie qui bouleverse l'esprit ici.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey wait, are you a fan of kaiju stuff?"
msgstr "Attendez, vous êtes un fan de kaijus?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*grins more broadly.  \"Busted!  Okay, I'm not like, a superfan.  My sister "
"was huge into it, and I kinda picked it up through her, but yeah.  I'd do "
"anything for a night on the couch with her, a copy of Pacific Rim, and a big "
"bowl of popcorn.\""
msgstr ""
"*Le sourire se fait plus large. \"Busted ! Ok, je ne suis pas une super fan. "
"Ma sœur était à fond dedans, et c'est un peu elle qui me l'a fait découvrir, "
"mais oui. Je ferais n'importe quoi pour passer une nuit sur le canapé avec "
"elle, une copie de Pacific Rim et un grand bol de pop-corn.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Maybe I could help.  There are lots of movie discs out there just collecting "
"dust, and you've got electricity."
msgstr ""
"Je pourrais peut-être vous aider. Il y a beaucoup de disques de films qui "
"prennent la poussière, et vous avez de l'électricité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, seriously.  Pacific Rim 2 though… what the heck?"
msgstr "Bon, sérieusement.  Mais Pacific Rim 2… c'est quoi ce bordel?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs and makes a waving gesture under her nose.  \"It's too bad they never "
"made a sequel.  Can you imagine?  Oh well, they'd probably have done "
"something *unconscionably stupid* like killing off Mako Mori in the first "
"act.  Good thing *that* never happened.\""
msgstr ""
"*Rire et faire un geste sous son nez. \"C'est dommage qu'ils n'aient jamais "
"fait de suite. Vous imaginez ? Ils auraient probablement fait quelque chose "
"d'incroyablement stupide, comme tuer Mako Mori dans le premier acte. "
"Heureusement que ça n'est jamais arrivé.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know, there are lots of movie discs out there just collecting dust, and "
"you've got electricity.  I could probably help you out."
msgstr ""
"Vous savez, il y a beaucoup de disques de films qui prennent la poussière, et "
"vous avez de l'électricité. Je pourrais probablement vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right.\"  Her grin fades slowly.  \"There's one ingredient you can't replace, "
"and without her, I don't…\" her voice catches.  \"Sorry.  That's a sweet "
"offer though, I really appreciate it."
msgstr ""
"C'est vrai.\"  Son sourire s'estompe lentement.  \"Il y a un ingrédient "
"impossible à remplacer, et sans elle, je ne…\" sa voix s'accroche.  "
"\"Désolée.  C'est une offre très gentille, j'apprécie vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I don't see why not.  It's always good to have more people who can do "
"it.  I'll need a bit of payment for my time, of course."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je ne vois pas pourquoi on ne le ferait pas. Il est toujours bon "
"d'avoir plus de personnes capables de le faire. J'aurai besoin d'un peu de "
"rémunération pour mon temps, bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right, let's do it!"
msgstr "Très bien, allons-y !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We've got it okay, I guess"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  Things have been getting better.  I wasn't even sure it was possible"
msgstr ". Les choses se sont améliorées. Je n'étais même pas sûr que c'était possible"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", as long as this doesn't last too long."
msgstr ", Il faut que cela ne dure pas trop longtemps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  With the back room cleared, we've had some chances to come and go, and "
"spread out a bit.  It's made a huge difference to morale.\"  She looks around "
"at the other refugees.  \"We'll have to see what the future holds."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  The situation is pretty tight, though.\"  She glances around at the "
"huddled crowds of people in the room.  \"If we're stuck here for too long "
"people are going to start getting a bit stir crazy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
msgstr "Trouvez 50 doses d'antiseptique"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
msgid ""
"Find 50 doses of antiseptic for Uyen Tran in the refugee center, in exchange "
"for <reward_count:FMCNote> merch."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez 50 doses d’antiseptiques pour Uyen Tran du centre de réfugiés pour "
"une récompense de <reward_count:FMCNote> merch."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
msgid ""
"There's the doc out front helping anyone that can pay… but for us up here, "
"money mostly goes to food.  I could do a lot for basic cuts, bruises, and "
"common stuff if I had some supplies to help out.  Could you bring me some "
"antiseptic?  Six bottles would probably be enough to last us a while."
msgstr ""
"Le médecin est là pour aider tous ceux qui peuvent payer... mais pour nous, "
"ici, l'argent sert surtout à payer la nourriture. Je pourrais faire beaucoup "
"pour les coupures, les bleus et les choses courantes si j'avais du matériel "
"pour m'aider. Pourriez-vous m'apporter de l'antiseptique ? Six flacons "
"suffiraient pour un moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 30 bandages"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid "Thanks so much.  It's a small thing but it'd be really helpful."
msgstr "Merci beaucoup. Ce n'est pas grand-chose, mais ce serait vraiment utile."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 30 bandages"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid "That's okay.  I'm sure we'll make do somehow."
msgstr "Ce n'est pas grave. Je suis sûr qu'on se débrouillera."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 30 bandages"
msgid ""
"Lots of people used to have first aid kits in their bathrooms.  I'm sure they "
"can't all have been looted."
msgstr ""
"Beaucoup de gens avaient des trousses de premiers secours dans leur salle de "
"bains. Je suis sûr qu'elles n'ont pas toutes été pillées."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 50 doses of antiseptic"
msgid ""
"Thanks so much.  Listen, I told some of the others what you were up to for us "
"and we pooled our cash to thank you.  It's not much but I hope it helps… "
"these are merch, the local money, you can trade them for goods from the shop. "
" A lot of us will take them in trade too."
msgstr ""
"Merci beaucoup. J'ai dit aux autres ce que vous avez fait pour nous et nous "
"avons mis notre argent en commun pour vous remercier. Ce n'est pas "
"grand-chose, mais j'espère que ça aidera... Ce sont des marchandises, de "
"l'argent local, que vous pouvez échanger contre des produits de la boutique. "
"Beaucoup d'entre nous sont prêts à les échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 30 bandages"
msgstr "Trouvez 30 bandages"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 30 bandages"
msgid ""
"Find 30 bandages for Uyen Tran in the refugee center, in exchange for "
"<reward_count:FMCNote> merch."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez 30 bandages pour Uyen Tran du centre de réfugiés, pour une récompense "
"de <reward_count:FMCNote> merch."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 30 bandages"
msgid ""
"There's the doc out front helping anyone that can pay… but for us up here, "
"money mostly goes to food.  I could do a lot for basic cuts, bruises, and "
"common stuff if I had some supplies to help out.  Could you bring me a few "
"extra bandages?  Thirty would probably be enough to last us a while."
msgstr ""
"Le médecin est là pour aider tous ceux qui peuvent payer... mais pour nous, "
"ici, l'argent sert surtout à payer la nourriture. Je pourrais faire beaucoup "
"pour les coupures, les bleus et les choses courantes si j'avais du matériel "
"pour m'aider. Pourriez-vous m'apporter quelques bandages supplémentaires ? "
"Trente suffiraient sans doute à nous faire tenir un moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 30 bandages"
msgid ""
"Thanks so much.  Listen, I told some of the others what you were up to for us "
"and we pooled our cash to thank you.  It's not much but I hope it helps… "
"these are merch, the local money, you can trade them for goods from the shop."
msgstr ""
"Merci beaucoup. J'ai dit aux autres ce que vous avez fait pour nous et nous "
"avons mis notre argent en commun pour vous remercier. Ce n'est pas "
"grand-chose, mais j'espère que ça aidera... Ce sont des marchandises, de "
"l'argent local, que vous pouvez échanger contre des produits de la boutique."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgstr "Trouvez 60 doses d'antidépresseurs"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid ""
"Find 60 doses of antidepressant for Uyen Tran in the refugee center, in "
"exchange for <reward_count:FMCNote> merch."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez 60 doses d'antidépresseurs pour Uyen Tran du centre de réfugiés pour "
"une récompense de <reward_count:FMCNote> merch."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid "We could still use your help…"
msgstr "Nous avons besoin de plus d'aide…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid ""
"I probably shouldn't be prescribing things, but there's a ton of people "
"needing help with sleep in here.  If you could get us some antidepressants, "
"Rhyzaea and I can probably make sure they're doled out appropriately without "
"people having to starve to pay for them.  Three month's worth - about 6 "
"bottles - would last us a little while."
msgstr ""
"Je ne devrais probablement pas prescrire quoi que ce soit, mais beaucoup de "
"personnes ici on des problèmes de sommeil. Si vous pouviez trouver des "
"antidépresseurs pour nous, Rhyzaea et moi pourrions probablement nous assurer "
"qu'ils soient distribués de façon appropriée sans que personne n'ait besoin "
"de se passer de nourriture pour en acheter. Un stock de 3 mois - un peu près "
"6 bouteilles - devrais nous durer un bon moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid ""
"Antidepressant was really common.  You can probably find it in most medicine "
"cabinets and pharmacies."
msgstr ""
"Les antidépresseurs étaient vraiment commun. Vous pouvez probablement en "
"trouvez dans la plupart des cabinets à médicaments ou dans une pharmacie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 60 doses of antidepressant"
msgid ""
"Thanks so much.  Listen, I told some of the others what you were up to for us "
"and we pooled our cash to thank you.  You've done a lot to help us out."
msgstr ""
"Merci beaucoup. J'ai dit aux autres ce que vous faisiez pour nous et nous "
"avons mis notre argent en commun pour vous remercier. Vous avez fait beaucoup "
"pour nous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Vanessa Toby"
msgstr "Vanessa Toby"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to hire out those scissors of yours."
msgstr "J'aimerais louer vos ciseaux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hmm, can we change this haircut a little please?"
msgstr "Hmm, vous pouvez changer cette coiffure un peu s'il-vous plaît?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hmm, can we change this shave a little please?"
msgstr "Hmm, peut-on changer un peu ce rasage, s'il vous plaît ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks you up and down for several seconds before speaking.  \"Oh, great.\"  "
"Her voice is husky with years of smoking, and her glare suggests it's a habit "
"she's recently given up.  \"Another new mouth to feed?  Just what we need.  "
"Well, I'm Vanessa.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il vous regarde de haut en bas pendant plusieurs secondes avant de parler. "
"\"Oh, super.\" Sa voix est rauque à cause des années de tabagisme, et son "
"regard suggère que c'est une habitude qu'elle a récemment abandonnée. "
"\"Encore une nouvelle bouche à nourrir ? C'est exactement ce dont nous avons "
"besoin. Moi, c'est Vanessa.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not a new mouth to feed, but nice to meet you too."
msgstr ""
"Je ne suis pas une nouvelle bouche à nourrir, mais je suis ravie de vous "
"rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, no.  I'm going."
msgstr "Oui, non.  J'en m'en vais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi, Vanessa.  What's up?"
msgstr "Salut Vanessa. Comment ça va?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_nevermind>  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "<end_talking_nevermind>  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well that's good.\"  She purses her lips and gives you another judgmental "
"stare.  \"If you're going to pull your own weight I guess that's an "
"improvement."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not much is up.  Not enough, in fact.  Here we are stuck in this slum pit "
"with a bunch of strangers, and all we can do is sit around staring at our "
"hands."
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a pas grand-chose de neuf. Pas assez, en fait. Nous sommes coincés "
"dans ce bidonville avec une bande d'étrangers, et tout ce que nous pouvons "
"faire, c'est rester assis à regarder nos mains."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't really want to talk about my life before this shit-show, if that's "
"what you mean.\"  She shrugs.  \"I don't need a shoulder to cry on.  I'm a "
"hairdresser, is that enough personal information for you?"
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas vraiment envie de parler de ma vie avant ce spectacle de merde, "
"si c'est ce que vous voulez dire.\" Elle hausse les épaules. \"Je n'ai pas "
"besoin d'une épaule pour pleurer. Je suis coiffeuse, c'est assez "
"d'informations personnelles pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you give me a haircut?"
msgstr "Vous pouvez me couper les cheveux?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I'm stuck in a dank shitty brick building with two dozen strangers, the "
"world's dead"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You want the sarcastic version, or the really sarcastic version?  I'm stuck "
"in a dank shitty brick building with two dozen strangers, the world's dead"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", and all anyone will talk about is this new ranch they're building, as "
"though it'll solve all our food problems"
msgstr ""
", Et tout le monde parle de ce nouveau ranch qu'ils construisent, comme s'il "
"allait résoudre tous nos problèmes alimentaires."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", and there's not enough food to go around"
msgstr ", et il n'y a pas assez de nourriture pour tout le monde"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".  At least I can do some work to keep me busy though, and the extra merch "
"does go a long way to keeping my belly full.  People like getting a good "
"haircut."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ".  Why don't you fuckin' figure it out?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can see you need one, but last time I used these shears it was to stab a "
"zombie in the face.  I don't think you'd want them in your hair.  Maybe you "
"could help me get set up properly?"
msgstr ""
"Je comprends que vous en ayez besoin, mais la dernière fois que j'ai utilisé "
"ces ciseaux, c'était pour poignarder un zombie au visage. Je ne pense pas que "
"vous voudriez les avoir dans vos cheveux. Tu pourrais peut-être m'aider à "
"m'installer correctement ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What can I do to help you out?"
msgstr "Que puis-je faire pour vous aider?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I can give you a haircut.  It'll be six merch for a haircut, or three "
"for a shave, okay?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je peux vous faire une coupe de cheveux. Ce sera six dollars pour "
"une coupe de cheveux, ou trois pour un rasage, d'accord ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 merch] Please give me a haircut."
msgstr "[6 merch] Une coupe de cheveux s'il vous plaît."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 merch] Please give me a shave."
msgstr "[3 merch] Un rasage s'il vous plaît."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, you owe me a free haircut, remember?"
msgstr "En fait, tu me dois une coupe de cheveux gratuite, tu te souviens ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you fix it to where I can grow my hair out, please?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like it if my hair didn't grow out anymore.  Can you help me with that?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you fix it to where I can grow my facial hair out, please?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'd like it if my facial hair didn't grow out anymore.  Can you help me with "
"that?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's a bit rich for my blood.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ha ha ha ha!  No."
msgstr "Ha ha ha ha!  Non."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know what I expected."
msgstr "Je ne sais pas à quoi je m'attendais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby in the refugee center"
msgstr ""
"Fabriquer un kit de coupe de cheveux de fortune pour Vanessa Toby dans le "
"centre de réfugiés"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid "If I had some equipment, I could do some hairdresser work here."
msgstr "Si j'avais le matériel ici, je pourrais probablement coiffer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid ""
"I didn't think to pack my hairdressing equipment when I was evacuated.  If "
"you could put together a basic hair cutting kit for me, I could do a bit of "
"styling for people around here.  I'll even give you a free haircut for your "
"troubles."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas pensé à emporter mon matériel de coiffure lorsque j'ai été "
"évacuée. Si vous pouviez me préparer un kit de coupe de cheveux de base, je "
"pourrais faire un peu de coiffure pour les gens d'ici. Je vous offrirai même "
"une coupe de cheveux gratuite pour votre peine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid ""
"Cool, thanks.  It'll be good to have something useful to do, and to not be "
"staring at so many shaggy slobs."
msgstr ""
"Cool, merci. Ce sera bien d'avoir quelque chose d'utile à faire, et de ne pas "
"avoir à regarder autant d'hommes hirsutes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid "Whatever, I'll keep twiddling my thumbs then."
msgstr "Peu importe, je vais continuer à me tourner les pouces."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid ""
"I don't need too much.  Scissors, a small mirror, a bit of cloth, and some "
"way to keep it all stored clean when I'm not using it, like a leather pouch "
"or something.  I can get the rest of what I need from shelter supplies."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas besoin de grand-chose. Des ciseaux, un petit miroir, un peu de "
"tissu et un moyen de ranger tout ça proprement quand je ne m'en sers pas, "
"comme une pochette en cuir ou autre. Je peux me procurer le reste de ce dont "
"j'ai besoin dans les réserves de l'abri."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid ""
"Well, this is pretty serviceable.  Heck, these scissors are nice enough that "
"I could probably inexplicably make your hair longer or a different color with "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, c'est tout à fait utilisable. Ces ciseaux sont suffisamment beaux "
"pour que je puisse, de façon inexplicable, rallonger vos cheveux ou leur "
"donner une autre couleur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Make a makeshift haircut kit for Vanessa Toby
#. in the refugee center"
msgid ""
"Seriously?  You failed to find *scissors*?  How do you tie your shoes in the "
"morning?"
msgstr ""
"Sérieusement, vous n'avez pas réussi à trouver des *ciseaux*. Vous n'avez pas "
"trouvé de *ciseaux*? Comment faites-vous pour lacer vos chaussures le matin?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sorry, but you couldn't pay me enough to go back there."
msgstr "Désolé, mais vous ne pourriez pas me payer assez cher pour que j'y retourne."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't.  Too many memories back there.  Sorry."
msgstr "Je ne peux pas. Il y a trop de souvenirs là-bas. Désolé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I wish I could, but no.  I can't face the memories."
msgstr "J'aimerais pouvoir, mais non. Je ne peux pas affronter les souvenirs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You won't get much luck asking those of us who were back there I'm afraid.  "
"Sorry."
msgstr ""
"Je crains que vous n'ayez pas beaucoup de chance en demandant à ceux d'entre "
"nous qui y étaient. Je le regrette."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is for Boris?  Yeah, Boris is has been through a lot, I'll do it for him."
msgstr "C'est pour Boris ? Oui, Boris a beaucoup souffert, je vais le faire pour lui."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It won't be pretty, but I'll see what I can do.  We'll all benefit from it "
"after all."
msgstr ""
"Ce ne sera pas très joli, mais je verrai ce que je peux faire. Nous en "
"profiterons tous après tout."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can try.  It's worth trying for Boris."
msgstr "Je peux essayer, cela vaut la peine de le faire pour Boris."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/shared_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's a big ask, for sure.  Okay, I'll see what I can do."
msgstr ""
"C'est une grande demande, c'est sûr. D'accord, je vais voir ce que je peux "
"faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a bulk trader.  Promotes production of
#. nonperishable food.
msgid "Broker"
msgstr "Courtier"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here to deliver some food supplies."
msgstr "Je suis ici pour livrer des vivres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm trying to put a cleanup crew together to tidy up the back room.  Can you "
"offer any help?"
msgstr ""
"J'essaie de constituer une équipe de nettoyage pour remettre de l'ordre dans "
"l'arrière-boutique. Pouvez-vous m'aider ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you able to buy some canning supplies?"
msgstr "Pouvez-vous acheter du matériel de mise en conserve ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I was told you had work for me?"
msgstr "On m'a dit que vous aviez du travail pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the deal with this written-on paper money you guys use?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que c'est que cette monnaie de papier écrite que vous utilisez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The refugees stuck up here seem a bit disgruntled."
msgstr "Les réfugiés coincés ici semblent un peu mécontents."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know about those beggars in the lobby?"
msgstr "Savez-vous qu'il y a des mendiants dans le hall d'entrée ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the deal with the closed-off areas of the building?"
msgstr "Qu'en est-il des zones fermées du bâtiment ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What are you going to do with that back bay area now that I've cleaned it out "
"for you?"
msgstr ""
"Qu'allez-vous faire de l'arrière-boutique maintenant que je l'ai nettoyée "
"pour vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me more about that ranch of yours."
msgstr "Dites-moi en plus au sujet de ce ranch."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What can I help you with?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que je peux faire pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yes, I can buy 500 mL or 3 L glass jars at the moment."
msgstr "Oui, je peux acheter des bocaux de 500mL ou 3L pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why cornmeal, jerky, and fruit wine?"
msgstr "Pourquoi de la farine de maïs, de la viande séchée et du vin de fruits ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, but I meant \"who are you\", like, \"what's your story?\""
msgstr ""
"D'accord, mais je voulais dire \"qui êtes-vous\", comme \"quelle est votre "
"histoire ?\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All three are easy to locally produce in significant quantities and are "
"non-perishable.  We have a local farmer or two and a few hunter types that "
"have been making attempts to provide us with the nutritious supplies.  We do "
"always need more suppliers though.  This stuff is rather cheap in bulk, so I "
"can pay a premium for any you have on you.  Canned food and other edibles are "
"handled by the merchant in the front in trade."
msgstr ""
"Ces trois produits sont faciles à produire localement en grandes quantités et "
"ne sont pas périssables. Nous avons un ou deux agriculteurs locaux et "
"quelques chasseurs qui ont tenté de nous fournir des produits nutritifs. Mais "
"nous avons toujours besoin de plus de fournisseurs. Ces produits sont plutôt "
"bon marché en vrac, je peux donc payer une prime pour tout ce que vous avez "
"sur vous. Les conserves et autres produits comestibles sont vendus par le "
"marchand d'avant"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you looking to buy anything else?"
msgstr "Vous voulez acheter quelque chose d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Very well… let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Très bien… parlons d'autre chose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm sorry, but I'm not here to make friends, I've got a job to do."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé, mais je ne suis pas là pour me faire des amis, j'ai un "
"travail à faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm actually accepting a number of different foodstuffs: beer, sugar, flour, "
"smoked meat, smoked fish, dried fruit and vegetables, cooking oil, "
"preservatives like salt and vinegar; and as mentioned before, jerky, "
"cornmeal, and fruit wine."
msgstr ""
"J'accepte en fait un certain nombre d'aliments différents : bière, sucre, "
"farine, viande fumée, poisson fumé, fruits et légumes secs, huile de cuisson, "
"conservateurs comme le sel et le vinaigre et, comme je l'ai déjà mentionné, "
"viande séchée, farine de maïs et vin de fruits."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We call them \"Free Merchant Certified Notes\".  We started signing money "
"almost as soon as we got here as a way of showing it represented actual goods "
"and services we had to trade.  Within a few days we'd organized the system, "
"and now it's been evolving into a form of cash.  Internally they're traded "
"for labor and services in exchange for food rations and other trade goods, "
"but we've been using them with suppliers we regularly trade with as well, "
"those that have faith in us."
msgstr ""
"Nous les appelons \"Free Merchant Certified Notes\". Nous avons commencé à "
"signer de l'argent dès notre arrivée pour montrer qu'il représentait les "
"biens et services que nous avions à échanger. En quelques jours, nous avons "
"organisé le système, qui a évolué vers une forme d'argent liquide. En "
"interne, ils sont échangés contre du travail et des services en échange de "
"rations alimentaires et d'autres biens commerciaux, mais nous les utilisons "
"également avec les fournisseurs avec lesquels nous commerçons régulièrement, "
"ceux qui ont confiance en nous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, it's a tough situation.  When we started out here nobody was really in "
"charge, and we let more in than we really had capacity to feed and support.  "
"When the dust settled and we'd established a little order, there were still "
"all these people upstairs waiting for a place to live, and no space.  We've "
"set up a little space for them, but it's not ideal."
msgstr ""
"Oui, c'est une situation difficile. Lorsque nous avons commencé ici, personne "
"n'était vraiment responsable et nous avons laissé entrer plus de personnes "
"que nous ne pouvions en nourrir et en soutenir. Lorsque la poussière est "
"retombée et que nous avons rétabli un peu d'ordre, il y avait encore toutes "
"ces personnes à l'étage qui attendaient un endroit pour vivre, et il n'y "
"avait pas de place. Nous avons aménagé un petit espace pour eux, mais ce "
"n'est pas idéal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do.  I don't know what you did to convince them to move out, but our supply "
"chain and I both thank you.  I hope it wasn't too unseemly."
msgstr ""
"C'est le cas. Je ne sais pas ce que vous avez fait pour les convaincre de "
"déménager, mais notre chaîne d'approvisionnement et moi-même vous remercions. "
"J'espère que ce n'était pas trop inconvenant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even once we got things sorted out, there weren't enough beds for everyone, "
"and definitely not enough supplies.  These are harsh times.  We're doing what "
"we can for those folks… at least they've got shelter."
msgstr ""
"Même une fois les choses réglées, il n'y avait pas assez de lits pour tout le "
"monde, et certainement pas assez de provisions.  Les temps sont durs.  Nous "
"faisons ce que nous pouvons pour ces personnes… au moins, elles ont un abri."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What went wrong with your staging area?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui n'a pas fonctionné dans votre zone de transit ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We didn't have great organization when we first arrived.  A few of the "
"earliest arrivals set up a triage and sorting system, with the sick and "
"infirm getting set aside to wait.  It's cruel, but we could see there was "
"only space for so many, and we didn't know what was causing people to turn "
"into zombies at the time, so we were trying to quarantine out infection.  A "
"couple folks died in there, and it escalated.  One of the first people here, "
"Jacob, had taken charge of the whole thing.  When the triage area had to be "
"evacuated he stayed behind to make sure everyone who could get out got out.  "
"It was a hell of a loss."
msgstr ""
"Nous n'étions pas très bien organisés à notre arrivée. Quelques-uns des "
"premiers arrivés ont mis en place un système de triage et de classement, les "
"malades et les infirmes étant mis de côté pour attendre. C'est cruel, mais "
"nous voyions bien qu'il n'y avait pas de place pour tout le monde, et nous ne "
"savions pas ce qui transformait les gens en zombies à l'époque, alors nous "
"essayions de mettre l'infection en quarantaine. Quelques personnes sont "
"mortes là-dedans, et la situation s'est aggravée. L'un des premiers arrivés, "
"Jacob, a pris les choses en main. Lorsque la zone de triage a dû être "
"évacuée, il est resté sur place pour s'assurer que tous ceux qui pouvaient "
"sortir sortaient. C'était une perte énorme."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, can I ask you something else?"
msgstr "Merci, puis-je vous poser une autre question ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank you for that.  We don't have any immediate plans for the area.  Once "
"it's cleaned up I suppose we'll let the people living up here decide what to "
"do with it."
msgstr ""
"Nous vous en remercions. Nous n'avons pas de projets immédiats pour cette "
"zone. Une fois qu'elle aura été nettoyée, je suppose que nous laisserons les "
"habitants décider de ce qu'il convient d'en faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You'd be better off asking the shopkeeper up front, I'm the quartermaster."
msgstr "Vous feriez mieux de demander au commerçant, je suis l'intendant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Description of mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid ""
"Deliver 50 large three-liter jars in exchange for <reward_count:FMCNote> "
"certified notes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid "I do have some work for you."
msgstr "J'ai du travail pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid ""
"You heard right.  When you brought in those canning jars, it got us thinking "
"about expanding our food storage from dehydrated to include cans.  We could "
"use some larger jars though for big stock items.  Can you bring me 50 large "
"three liter jars?  I'll pay you a Certified Note per two."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez bien entendu. Lorsque vous avez apporté ces bocaux de conserve, "
"nous avons pensé à étendre notre stockage d'aliments déshydratés aux boîtes "
"de conserve. Nous pourrions cependant utiliser des bocaux plus grands pour "
"les gros stocks. Pouvez-vous m'apporter 50 grands bocaux de trois litres ? Je "
"vous paierai une note certifiée pour deux d'entre eux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid ""
"Thank you.  Once we get a cottage industry set up with some of our "
"inhabitants, I'll be able to start buying these from you and other scavengers "
"in smaller lots.  This should be enough to test out our equipment."
msgstr ""
"Je vous remercie.  Une fois que nous aurons mis en place une industrie "
"artisanale avec certains des résidents, je pourrai commencer à acheter plus "
"de ce que vous ainsi que d'autres pilleurs avez à offrir en plus petites "
"quantités.  Ceci devrait suffire pour tester notre équipement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_broker.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle Pt. 2"
msgid ""
"Wow, that's a lot more jars than it sounded on paper.  Thanks.  Here's your "
"payment."
msgstr ""
"Wow, c'est beaucoup plus de bocaux qu'il n'y paraît sur le papier. Merci. "
"Voici votre paiement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello marshal."
msgstr "Salut capitaine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I join you guys?"
msgstr "Puis-je me joindre à vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I can do for you?"
msgstr "Je peux faire quelque chose pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you later."
msgstr "À plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is a refugee center that we've made into a sort of trading hub."
msgstr "C'est un centre de réfugiée que nous avons transformé en centre d'échange."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So are you with the government or something?"
msgstr "Vous travaillez pour le gouvernement ou quelque chose comme ça ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you trade?"
msgstr "Vous échangez quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ha ha ha, no.  Though there is Old Guard somewhere around here if you have "
"any questions relating to what the government is up to."
msgstr ""
"Ha ha ha, non. Mais il y a une vieille garde quelque part par ici si vous "
"avez des questions sur ce que fait le gouvernement."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, okay.  I'll go look for him"
msgstr "Ah, d'accord. Je vais le trouver"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Anything valuable really.  If you really want to know, go ask one of the "
"actual traders.  I'm just protection."
msgstr ""
"Tout ce qui a de la valeur en fait. Si vous voulez vraiment savoir, demandez "
"à l'un des commerçants. Je ne fais que protéger."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll go talk to them later."
msgstr "J'irais parler avec eux plus tard dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Will do, thanks!"
msgstr "Ce sera fait, merci !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's pretty blunt!"
msgstr "C'est assez brutal !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Death is pretty blunt."
msgstr "La mort est assez brutale."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So no negotiating?  No, 'If you do this quest then we'll let you in?'"
msgstr ""
"Pas de négociation ? Pas de \"Si vous faites cette quête, nous vous "
"laisserons entrer\" ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't like your attitude."
msgstr "Je n'aime pas votre attitude."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well alright then."
msgstr "Bon, d'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Then leave, you have two feet."
msgstr "Dans ce cas-là partez, vous avez deux pieds."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'd rather rearrange your face instead!"
msgstr "Je pense que je préférerais réarranger ton visage à la place !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I will."
msgstr "Je le ferait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Depends on what you want.  Go talk to a merchant if you have anything to "
"sell.  Otherwise the Old Guard liaison might have something, if you can find "
"him.  But if you're just looking for someone to put a good word in, I might "
"have something for you."
msgstr ""
"Cela dépend de ce que vous voulez. Allez parler à un marchand si vous avez "
"quelque chose à vendre. Sinon, l'agent de liaison de la Vieille Garde "
"pourrait avoir quelque chose, si vous le trouvez. Mais si vous cherchez juste "
"quelqu'un à qui parler, j'ai peut-être quelque chose pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A good word might be helpful.  What do you need?"
msgstr "Un bon mot peut être utile. De quoi avez-vous besoin ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Old Guard huh, I'll go talk to him!"
msgstr "Vieux garde, je vais aller lui parler !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are the Old Guard?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que la Veille Garde?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's just our nickname for them.  They're what's left of the federal "
"government.  Don't know how legitimate they are but they are named after some "
"military unit that once protected the president.  Their liaison is usually "
"hanging around here somewhere."
msgstr ""
"C'est juste notre surnom pour eux. Ils sont ce qu'il reste du gouvernement "
"fédéral. Je ne sais pas à quel point ils sont légitimes, mais ils ont repris "
"le nom d'une unité militaire qui eut protégé le président. Leur contact "
"traîne généralement par là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Whatever, I had another question."
msgstr "Peu importe, j'avais une autre question."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, I'll go look for him then."
msgstr "Ah, d'accord.  Je vais le trouver dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Smokes, let's go."
msgstr "Des cigarettes, c'est partit. "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid ""
"Make a friend at the refugee center by handing over around five packs - 100 "
"cigarettes."
msgstr ""
"Faites-vous un ami au centre de réfugiés en lui remettant environ cinq "
"paquets - 100 cigarettes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid "Come on man, I just need a smoke."
msgstr "Allez mec, j'ai juste besoin d'une cigarette."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid ""
"With all that's been going on, it's been more and more difficult to find a "
"smoke.  My stash has been running low for a while now.  Think you could help "
"me out here?  A few packs is all I need."
msgstr ""
"Avec tout ce qui se passe, il est de plus en plus difficile de trouver une "
"cigarette. Ma réserve s'épuise depuis un certain temps. Tu penses pouvoir "
"m'aider ? Quelques paquets, c'est tout ce dont j'ai besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid "Thanks, it's great to see someone willing to help a guy out."
msgstr "Merci, c'est super de voir que quelqu'un est prêt à aider un gars."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid "Well, I'll find someone else to do it for me."
msgstr "Ok, je trouverais probablement trouver quelqu'un d'autre pour le faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid ""
"Plenty of smokers in towns.  Gotta be some left over cigs in some of them "
"houses."
msgstr ""
"Beaucoup de fumeurs dans les villes, devrait rester une abondance de "
"cigarettes dans certaines maisons."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid "Got the smokes?"
msgstr "Vous avez les cigarettes?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Smokes, let's go."
msgid "Thanks!  I'll be sure to put in a good word for you around the center."
msgstr "Je vous remercie. Je ne manquerai pas de parler de vous en ville."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I am actually new."
msgstr "En fait, je suis nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are there any rules I should follow while inside?"
msgstr "Il y a des règles que je dois suivre à l'intérieur?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So who is everyone around here?"
msgstr "Qui est donc tout le monde ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's trade!"
msgstr "Échangeons!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks!  I will be on my way."
msgstr "Merci!  Je vais y aller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yes of course.  Just don't bring any trouble and it's all fine by me."
msgstr "Oui bien sûr. Ne ramène pas de problèmes et tout va bien pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well mostly no.  Just don't go around robbing others and starting fights and "
"you will be all set.  Also, don't go into the basement.  Outsiders are not "
"allowed in there."
msgstr ""
"En général, non. Il suffit de ne pas voler les autres et de ne pas déclencher "
"de bagarres pour que tout aille bien. N'allez pas non plus au sous-sol. Les "
"étrangers n'y sont pas autorisés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok, thanks."
msgstr "Ok, merci."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So uhhh, why not?"
msgstr "Donc euhhh, pourquoi pas?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"In short, we had a problem when a sick refugee died and turned into a zombie. "
" We had to expel the refugees and most of our surviving group now stays to "
"the basement to prevent it from happening again.  Unless you really prove "
"your worth I don't foresee any exceptions to that rule."
msgstr ""
"En bref, nous avons eu un problème lorsqu'un réfugié malade est mort et s'est "
"transformé en zombie. Nous avons dû expulser les réfugiés et la plupart des "
"survivants restent au sous-sol pour éviter que cela ne se reproduise. À moins "
"que vous ne prouviez vraiment votre valeur, je ne prévois pas d'exception à "
"cette règle."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Most are scavengers like you.  They now make a living by looting the cities "
"in search for anything useful: food, weapons, tools, gasoline.  In exchange "
"for their findings we offer them a temporary place to rest and the services "
"of our shop.  I bet some of them would be willing to organize resource runs "
"with you if you ask."
msgstr ""
"La plupart sont des pilleurs comme vous.  Ils vivent désormais de tout ce qui "
"pourrait être utile dans les villes: nourriture, armes, outils, essence.  En "
"échange de leurs trouvailles, nous leur offrons un lieu de repos temporaire "
"et les services de notre boutique.  Je parie que certains d'entre eux "
"seraient prêts à organiser des expéditions avec vous si vous demandez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the heads-up."
msgstr "Merci pour le tuyau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard2.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You are asking the wrong person, should look for our merchant by the main "
"entrance.  Perhaps one of the scavengers is also interested."
msgstr ""
"Vous vous adressez à la mauvaise personne, vous devriez chercher notre "
"marchand près de l'entrée principale. Peut-être que l'un des pilleurs est "
"également intéressé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Keep to yourself and you won't find any problems."
msgstr "Restez entre vous et vous ne rencontrerez pas de problèmes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got tips for avoiding trouble?"
msgstr "Vous avez des astuces pour éviter les ennuis?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you seen anyone who might be hiding something?"
msgstr "As-tu vu quelqu'un qui serait susceptible de cacher quelque-chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Keep your head down and stay out of my way."
msgstr "Baisse la tête et reste en dehors de mon chemin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK…"
msgstr "Ok…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Like what?"
msgstr "Comme quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not sure…"
msgstr "Je suis pas sûr…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Like they could be working for someone else?"
msgstr "Comme s'ils pouvaient travailler pour quelqu'un d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Get bent, traitor!"
msgstr "Vas te faire foutre traître!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got something to hide?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose à cacher?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I didn't mean to offend you…"
msgstr "Désolé, je ne voulais pas vous offenser…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you don't get on with your business I'm going to have to ask you to leave "
"and not come back."
msgstr ""
"Si vous ne vous occupez pas de vos affaires, je vais devoir vous demander de "
"partir et de ne pas revenir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry."
msgstr "Désolé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's it, you're dead!"
msgstr "Ça suffit, t'es mort !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I didn't mean it!"
msgstr "Je voulais pas dire ça!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You must really have a death wish!"
msgstr "Vous devez vraiment avoir envie de mourir !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard3.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We don't put-up with garbage like you, finish your business and get the hell "
"out."
msgstr "On ne tolère pas des merdes comme toi, finis ce que t'as à faire et casse-toi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Keep civil or I'll bring the pain."
msgstr "Restez civilisés ou je vous infligerai des souffrances."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just on watch, move along."
msgstr "Je suis juste de guet, circulez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello.  Welcome to our safe zone."
msgstr "Bonjour. Bienvenue dans notre zone de sécurité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good evening.  Welcome to our safe zone."
msgstr "Bonsoir à tous. Bienvenue dans notre zone de sécurité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_engineer.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_officer.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#: data/mods/No_Hope/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_Soldier.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_engineer.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_officer.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sir."
msgstr "Monsieur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Rough out there, isn't it?"
msgstr "C'est rude par ici, non?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_engineer.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_officer.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#: data/mods/No_Hope/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_Soldier.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/augustmoon_security.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_engineer.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_officer.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/UICA/ground_soldier.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ma'am"
msgstr "M'dame"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ma'am, you really shouldn't be traveling out there."
msgstr "M'dame, vous ne devriez pas vous balader par ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you get saddled with guard duty?"
msgstr "Comment vous êtes-vous retrouvé à devoir monter la garde ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Heard anything about an helicopter crash?"
msgstr "Vous avez entendu quelque chose au sujet d'un crash d'hélicoptère?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing too fancy.  We have a rota of anyone able bodied that can handle "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"Rien d'extraordinaire. Nous avons une liste de toutes les personnes valides "
"qui peuvent se débrouiller seules."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "None of your business really, is it."
msgstr "Cela ne vous regarde pas vraiment, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Gotta earn my keep."
msgstr "Je dois gagner ma vie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's honest work, and now and then I get to take a zombie down."
msgstr ""
"C'est un travail honnête, et de temps en temps, j'ai l'occasion d'abattre un "
"zombie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Talk to one of the bosses about that.  You'd have to pay me to go back there "
"though, that's gonna be a hell of a job."
msgstr ""
"Parlez-en à l'un des patrons. Mais il faudrait me payer pour que j'y "
"retourne, ça va être un sacré boulot."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have a lot of free time for that sort of thing.  Maybe talk to the "
"shopkeep, they know more about scheduling and stuff."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas vraiment beaucoup de temps libre pour ce genre de choses. Parlez "
"à Smokes, il sait plus au sujet des tâches, emplois du temps et toute ce "
"genre de trucs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nah."
msgstr "Nan."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'd rather stand around looking threatening than scrub gore out of the tiles."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que je veux plutôt me tenir debout ici et avoir l'air peu commode "
"que d'astiquer le carrelage pour en enlever le sang et les tripes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not unless you pay me.  Try the shopkeep, they can sell our services just "
"like anything else."
msgstr ""
"Pas si vous ne me payez pas. Essayez de parler à Smokes, il peut vendre nos "
"services comme il peut vendre le reste."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure yeah, I remember, I was on caravan duty when I saw it, it got caught in "
"of those weird storms, as we started driving away I heard a big splash sound."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No, sorry…"
msgstr "Non merci, désolé⋅e…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I didn't see it myself but I heard the rumors about it, apparently it crashed "
"somewhere nearby but I haven't seen any smoke or corpse."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh the helicopter?  Yeah, I tried finding the crash site around where the guy "
"said he heard the crash but I didn't find nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The crashed helicopter?  Eh, I'm pretty sure it's just a story, no one ever "
"found anything."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, yes, what a story, I almost wish I had been there to see it, almost."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah I was part of the caravan that spotted it, it was headed east then when "
"the storm broke out it got caught by some kind of creature, I heard gunshots "
"then it started flying down rapidly, I heard it crash but I'm not sure where "
"exactly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes I was told the story by the others, I'm glad I wasn't there though, I "
"hate those storms."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I dunno, I wasn't there but I overheard some guy talking about it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You know how it is, people talk, I mean sure, there was one of those weird "
"storms at the time but the helicopter story?  I don't believe it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a source of information and eventually
#. missions.  Works with the free merchant caravans.
msgid "Teamster"
msgstr "Teamster"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, have your caravans seen anything interesting out there in the wasteland?"
msgstr ""
"Vos caravanes ont remarqué quelque chose d'intéressant durant leurs "
"expéditions?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Do you know anything about a trader near the New England Church Community, "
"claims to be from here?"
msgstr ""
"Savez-vous quelque chose au sujet d'un commerçant à proximité de la "
"Communauté Chrétienne de Nouvelle-Angleterre, qui prétend être originaire "
"d'ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I've got the evidence you were looking for."
msgstr "Je pense que j'ai les preuves dont vous aviez besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I wanted to tell you about a potential new trading partner I met recently."
msgstr ""
"Je voulais vous informer d'un nouveau potentiel partenaire commercial que "
"j'ai repéré récemment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well now, a new face.  Nice ta meet ya.  I'm the one sendin' out these here "
"caravans far and wide.  What can I do ya for?"
msgstr ""
"Un nouvel arrivage? Enchanté, je suis la personne chargée d'organiser les "
"caravanes marchandes de notre organization, qu'est ce que je peux faire pour "
"vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've gotta run, nice talking to you."
msgstr "Je dois y aller, c'était un plaisir de discuter."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, got nothin' to load up just now."
msgstr "Ok, je n'ai rien à organiser pour un petit moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, sorry.  Nothin' much worth notin' out there these days, just the odd "
"scattered survivor and they usually don't want random visitors."
msgstr ""
"Non, désolé. Il n'y a pas grand-chose qui vaille la peine d'être noté de nos "
"jours, juste quelques survivants éparpillés, et ils ne veulent généralement "
"pas de visiteurs aléatoires."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Matter of fact, yeah.  Ran into a bunch of farmers.  They don't want much to "
"do with our caravans, but someone like you they might be OK with."
msgstr ""
"En fait, oui. Je suis tombé sur une bande de fermiers. Ils ne veulent pas "
"avoir affaire à nos caravanes, mais quelqu'un comme toi, ça pourrait les "
"arranger."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, a few of my caravans have come back now talkin' about this giant metal "
"castle on top of a rock, in the middle of nowhere.  They ain't been crazy "
"enough to check it out, but you could if you want."
msgstr ""
"Quelques-unes de mes caravanes sont revenues en parlant de ce gigantesque "
"château de métal situé au sommet d'un rocher, au milieu de nulle part. Ils "
"n'ont pas été assez fous pour aller le voir, mais tu peux le faire si tu veux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A few of my people have come back now talkin' about some yuppie trying to "
"start a bank that uses bullets for money.  Silly idea but the lad lives on a "
"homestead with a woman who wouldn't let my guys leave without a full belly."
msgstr ""
"Quelques-uns de mes hommes sont revenus et parlent d'un jeune qui essaie de "
"créer une banque qui utilise des balles comme monnaie. C'est une idée "
"stupide, mais le gars vit dans une ferme avec une femme qui ne laisserait pas "
"mes hommes partir sans avoir le ventre plein."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "ERROR: out of bounds on randomize_directions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that lab?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je me rendre à ce laboratoire?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that castle?"
msgstr "Comment puis-je me rendre à ce chateau?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold on, what were you saying before?"
msgstr "Attendez, que disiez-vous tout à l'heure ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_later>"
msgstr "<end_talking_leave>  <end_talking_later>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*shows you on your map where to find it.  \"That should get you there.  Good "
"luck, I 'spect you'll need it.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The teamster "
"considers for a moment"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Always lookin' for new places to trade.  What you got for me?"
msgstr ""
"Toujours à la recherche de nouveaux lieux d'échange. Qu'est-ce que tu as pour "
"moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Tell them about Rubik and the Exodii.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well now, that's a hell of a story.  Some day, I'll see if we can get out "
"there an' look into it.  Sounds like there'd be some real interestin' trade."
msgstr ""
"C'est une sacrée histoire. Un jour, je verrai si nous pouvons aller là-bas et "
"y jeter un coup d'œil. On dirait qu'il y a des échanges commerciaux très "
"intéressants."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks so much!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Mille merci!  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks so much!  I have to go ask a few others, talk to you later."
msgstr ""
"Merci beaucoup ! Je dois aller poser quelques questions à d'autres personnes, "
"à plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think they're gouging the prices for the people living there."
msgstr "Je pense qu'ils augmentent les prix pour les personnes qui y vivent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Is that so?  What makes you think that?  My accounting reports have come back "
"clean, just like everybody else."
msgstr ""
"Est-ce le cas ? Qu'est-ce qui vous fait penser cela ? Mes rapports comptables "
"ont été nettoyés, comme ceux de tout le monde."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Everything they sell I can buy for twice as less here, even a box of crackers "
"is an arm and a leg."
msgstr ""
"Tout ce qu'ils vendent, je peux l'acheter deux fois moins cher ici, même une "
"boîte de crackers coûte un bras et une jambe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess you guys are a bunch of thieves if you charge that much."
msgstr "Je suppose que vous êtes une bande de voleurs si vous demandez autant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Tell you what, if you can find some sort of evidence that proves they're "
"shafting customers and bring it to me, I'll send someone to look in to it."
msgstr ""
"Si vous trouvez une preuve qui prouve qu'ils arnaquent les clients et que "
"vous me l'apportez, j'enverrai quelqu'un pour examiner."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, you have yourself a deal."
msgstr "Ok, on a un accord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What sort of \"evidence\" did you have in mind?"
msgstr "Quelle sorte de \"preuves\" voulez-vous que je trouve?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why do you want me to do it?"
msgstr "Pourquoi voulez-vous que je fasse cela?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I have limited manpower these days, and not everyone can go off of a "
"strangers word with no supporting evidence."
msgstr ""
"Ecoutez, j'ai peu de personnel ces jours-ci, et tout le monde ne peut pas se "
"contenter d'un mot d'un étranger sans preuve à l'appui."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Makes sense, I'll find you some evidence."
msgstr "C'est logique, je trouverais ce que vous cherchez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Forget it, since you're not interested in taking this seriously."
msgstr "Oubliez cela, puisque vous n'avez pas l'intention de prendre cela au sérieux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess sales records could work, or stock lists of inventory that give a "
"discrepancy between what's sold and what money comes in."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que les registres des ventes pourraient fonctionner, ou les listes "
"d'inventaire qui donnent un écart entre ce qui est vendu et l'argent qui "
"entre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll get right to it, see you later."
msgstr "Je m'y mets, à plus tard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who would have these sorts of things?"
msgstr "Qui aurait ce genre de choses?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_later>  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "<end_talking_later>  <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, there's somebody else who works there, handles all of the money "
"management.  I'd look into them first, should be in the same spot the other "
"guy is."
msgstr ""
"Il y a quelqu'un d'autre qui travaille là-bas et qui s'occupe de la gestion "
"de l'argent. Je m'intéresserais d'abord à lui, il devrait être au même "
"endroit que l'autre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Makes sense, I'll get right to it."
msgstr "C'est logique, je m'y mets tout de suite."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not doing any of this legwork for you, figure it out on your own."
msgstr "Je ne fais pas ce travail à votre place, débrouillez-vous tout seul."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks over the papers for a moment, before pocketing them.  \"I'd say this "
"is sufficient, here's some money for your trouble.  I'll get somebody on "
"this.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks over the papers for a moment, before pocketing them.  \"This seems "
"perfectly alright to me.  I don't know what you have against them, but give "
"it up and quit wasting our time.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright then, <name_b>.  I guess that's what I get for my troubles."
msgstr "D'accord, <name_b>. Je suppose que c'est ce que j'obtiens pour mes problèmes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
msgid ""
"Ran into a bunch of farmers.  They don't want much to do with our caravans, "
"but someone like you they might be OK with."
msgstr ""
"Je suis tombé sur un groupe de fermiers. Ils ne veulent pas trop s'occuper de "
"nos caravanes, mais quelqu'un comme vous pourrait leur convenir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
msgid "Nice."
msgstr "Splendide."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that bullet bank"
msgid "Seems reasonable."
msgstr "Ça me semble raisonnable."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
msgid "Be careful.  It's rough out there."
msgstr "Soyez prudent. Les temps sont durs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that bullet bank"
msgid "Huh, go figure."
msgstr "Huh, allez savoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
msgid "It is what it is."
msgstr "Il est ce qu'il est."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that lab"
msgstr "Explorez ce laboratoire"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that lab"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that lab"
msgid ""
"There's been rumors.  Folks talkin' about some kind of secret lab, out in the "
"wilds, with survivors in it."
msgstr ""
"Il y a eu des rumeurs. Des gens parlent d'une sorte de laboratoire secret, "
"dans la nature, avec des survivants."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that scrap metal castle"
msgstr "Explorez ce château en ferraille"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
msgid ""
"A few of my caravans have come back now talkin' about this giant metal castle "
"on top of a rock, in the middle of nowhere.  They ain't been crazy enough to "
"check it out, but you could if you want."
msgstr ""
"Quelques-unes de mes caravanes sont revenues en parlant de ce gigantesque "
"château de métal au sommet d'un rocher, au milieu de nulle part. Ils n'ont "
"pas été assez fous pour y jeter un coup d'œil, mais tu peux le faire si tu "
"veux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
msgid "Your funeral."
msgstr "Ce sont vos funérailles je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that bullet bank"
msgstr "Explorer cette banque de balles"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Check out that bullet bank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that bullet bank"
msgid ""
"A few of my people have come back now talkin' about some yuppie trying to "
"start a bank that uses bullets for money.  Silly idea, but the lad lives on a "
"homestead with a woman who wouldn't let my guys leave without a full belly."
msgstr ""
"Quelques-uns de mes hommes sont revenus et parlent d'un jeune qui essaie de "
"créer une banque qui utilise des balles comme monnaie. C'est une idée "
"stupide, mais le gars vit dans une ferme avec une femme qui ne laisserait pas "
"mes hommes partir sans avoir le ventre plein."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that bullet bank"
msgid "Hopefully they are still around."
msgstr "J'espère qu'ils sont toujours là."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that bullet bank"
msgid "Don't worry about the turrets they seem friendly to people."
msgstr ""
"Ne vous inquiétez pas pour les tourelles, elles semblent amicales envers les "
"gens."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Marshal…"
msgstr "Marshal…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Citizen…"
msgstr "Citoyen…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I trade for supplies?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux échanger des choses avec vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So what are you doing right now?"
msgstr "Que faites-vous en ce moment?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never mind…"
msgstr "Peu importe…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Old Guard--that's what's left of the feds--set me up here to screen any "
"new arrivals for infection risks.  Can't be too paranoid these days.  Sad to "
"have to turn people away, but I like the assignment for the chance to get "
"news about the outside world."
msgstr ""
"La vieille garde - c'est ce qu'il reste des fédéraux - m'a installé ici pour "
"examiner les risques d'infection des nouveaux arrivants. On n'est jamais trop "
"paranoïaque de nos jours. C'est triste de devoir refuser des gens, mais "
"j'aime bien cette mission qui me permet d'avoir des nouvelles du monde "
"extérieur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of news?"
msgstr "Quelle types de nouvelles?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sightings of unusual living dead or new mutations.  The more we know about "
"what's happening, the closer we can get to a treatment or maybe even a cure.  "
"It's a long shot, but you have hope to survive."
msgstr ""
"Des observations de morts-vivants inhabituels ou de nouvelles mutations. Plus "
"nous en saurons sur ce qui se passe, plus nous nous rapprocherons d'un "
"traitement, voire d'une guérison. Les chances sont minces, mais vous avez "
"l'espoir de survivre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good luck with that…"
msgstr "Bonne chance avec ça…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is no classic zombie outbreak.  The dead seem to be getting stronger as "
"the days go on.  Some survivors too, come in here with… adaptations.  Maybe "
"they're related."
msgstr ""
"Il ne s'agit pas d'une épidémie de zombies classique.  Les morts semblent se "
"renforcer au fil des jours.  Certains survivants aussi, arrivent ici avec… "
"des adaptations.  Peut-être qu'ils sont liés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can't.  There's nothing we can spare to sell and I've got no budget to buy "
"from you.  I don't suppose you want to donate?"
msgstr ""
"Nous ne pouvons pas. Nous n'avons rien à vendre et je n'ai pas de budget pour "
"vous acheter. Je suppose que vous ne voulez pas faire de dons ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
msgid ""
"First, you need to kill <color_light_blue>any zombie</color> and extract the "
"blood from its body using the <color_light_blue>blood draw kit</color>.\n"
"Second, you need to deliver this blood to any working "
"<color_light_blue>centrifuge with a computer</color>.  Equipment like this "
"can most commonly be found at <color_light_blue>hospitals</color>, but you "
"can also try to search for it at <color_light_blue>medical labs</color>.\n"
"Third, you need to place the extracted blood on the "
"<color_light_blue>centrifuge</color> and analyze it using the "
"<color_light_blue>computer nearby</color>.  If you're successful, the data "
"will be written on an <color_light_blue>empty USB drive</color> you have to "
"provide.\n"
"Finally, you need to bring the USB drive with the data back to the "
"<color_light_blue>Doctor</color>."
msgstr ""
"Commencez par neutraliser <color_light_blue>n'importe quel zombie</color>, "
"ensuite effectuer une extraction du sang de zombies à l'aide du "
"<color_light_blue>kit de prélèvement sanguin</color>. \n"
"Dans un second temps, transmettez le sang extrait à une "
"<color_light_blue>centrifugeuse fonctionnelle équipée d'un "
"ordinateur</color>, qui peut être située dans des "
"<color_light_blue>installations hospitalières</color> ou des "
"<color_light_blue>laboratoires médicaux</color>.\n"
"Dans un troisième temps, analysez les échantillons de sang à l'aide de "
"<color_light_blue>l'ordinateur associé</color> à la "
"<color_light_blue>centrifugeuse</color>. En cas de réussite, enregistrez les "
"données sur une <color_light_blue>clé USB vierge</color> fournie par "
"l'équipe.\n"
"Et enfin, remettez la clé USB contenant les données au "
"<color_light_blue>Docteur</color>."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
msgid ""
"We don't have the equipment for real analysis here so it'll need to be done "
"in the field.  I need you to get a fresh sample of zombie blood, take it to a "
"hospital, and perform a centrifuge analysis of it.  I've been authorized to "
"reward the completion of this job with 30 merch, a sizeable sum of the local "
"currency."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
msgid ""
"Excellent.  Take this blood draw kit; once you've found a zombie corpse, use "
"it to extract blood from the body, then take it to a hospital for analysis."
msgstr ""
"Excellent. Prenez ce kit de prélèvement sanguin ; une fois que vous aurez "
"trouvé un cadavre de zombie, utilisez-le pour extraire le sang du corps, puis "
"amenez l'échantillon à l'hôpital pour analyse."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Download Workstation Data"
msgstr "Télécharger les données du poste de travail"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
msgid ""
"The medical software didn't just analyze the blood, it triggered a government "
"alert.  Medical staff was under orders to immediately drive any matching "
"samples to the nearest laboratory.  That must mean the government knew!  We "
"have the destination address.  Go there, get in, and bring back any records "
"you can download off a computer.  Like last time, I can compensate you, and "
"the Old Guard saw enough promise in this assignment to spare a larger sum of "
"60 merch.  I'm sure you're also free to lay claim to any valuables you might "
"find at the target location."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
msgid "Great!  I've mapped out a route to the address."
msgstr "C'est génial ! J'ai tracé un itinéraire jusqu'à l'adresse."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgid "Can't blame you, but come back if you change your mind."
msgstr "Je ne peux pas vous en vouloir, mais revenez si vous changez d'avis."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
msgid ""
"If the laboratory is locked, maybe you can find an id card from employees who "
"died in the evacuation.  Also brush up on your computer skills, any computers "
"will have some security on them.  Bring back anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"Si le laboratoire est fermé à clé, vous pourrez peut-être trouver une carte "
"d'identité des employés décédés lors de l'évacuation. Améliorez également vos "
"connaissances en informatique, car tous les ordinateurs sont protégés. "
"Rapportez tout ce que vous trouverez sur une clé USB."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid "Have you completed your mission?"
msgstr "Avez-vous accompli votre mission ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
msgid "Thanks!  This data looks damaged, but maybe I can make something out of it."
msgstr ""
"Merci! Ces données ont l'air endommagées, mais je pourrais peut être en faire "
"quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Download Encryption Codes"
msgstr "Téléchargez les Codes de Chiffrement"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
msgid ""
"Unfortunately the data you got was incomplete and mostly encrypted.  There "
"may be a way to get encryption codes, though.  I found a complaint by the "
"infosec team that they were unable to deliver critical security updates to "
"one research site.  It was some kind of more restricted secondary site hidden "
"beneath a town, they weren't allowed in.  That means it should have unsecured "
"computers we can get the codes from.  I couldn't secure any funding for this "
"due to a lack of obvious results, but if you believe in this enough, maybe we "
"can convince them otherwise?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
msgid ""
"Great!  I've mapped out a route, it should look like a normal house.  Bring "
"back anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"Super ! J'ai tracé un itinéraire, ça devrait ressembler à une maison normale. "
"Ramenez tout ce que vous trouvez sur une clé USB."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
msgid "Expect the lab to be locked as usual."
msgstr "Attendez-vous à ce que le laboratoire soit fermé comme d'habitude."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
msgid ""
"Wonderful!  Now I just need to get an undamaged, complete archive, and we can "
"really figure out what happened."
msgstr ""
"Merveilleux ! Il ne me reste plus qu'à obtenir des archives complètes et "
"intactes, et nous pourrons vraiment comprendre ce qui s'est passé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Download Research Archives"
msgstr "Télécharger les archives de la recherche"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
msgid ""
"So there looks to be months, maybe years of experiments, and that data set "
"must be huge.  Database servers massive enough to house it would overheat "
"running on emergency power.  But I did find communications from a lab that "
"had some kind of freezing portal open during the Cataclysm, sending "
"everything to subzero temperatures.  I bet the archives inside that lab are "
"still working.  The Old Guard didn't seem very convinced, but still ended up "
"providing 100 merch for this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
msgid ""
"Great!  I've mapped out a route.  Bundle up, it gets colder the deeper you go "
"and it looks like the archives were on the fourth basement level."
msgstr ""
"C'est très bien ! J'ai tracé un itinéraire. Habillez-vous bien, il fait de "
"plus en plus froid au fur et à mesure que vous descendez et il semble que les "
"archives se trouvaient au quatrième sous-sol."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
msgid ""
"That lab is going to start freezing and just get colder the deeper you go.  "
"You'll really need special equipment to survive that far down.  Bring back "
"anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"Ce laboratoire va commencer à geler et à devenir de plus en plus froid au fur "
"et à mesure que vous vous enfoncez. Vous aurez vraiment besoin d'un "
"équipement spécial pour survivre à cette profondeur. Ramenez tout ce que vous "
"trouverez sur une clé USB."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
msgid "Thanks!  This is a lot of data to go through."
msgstr "Merci ! Il y a beaucoup de données à examiner."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgstr "Trouvez les Tunnels de Laboratoire"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgid ""
"In the data we found a major contract for tunneling and train equipment, "
"ordered eight months ago.  It's the best lead we have.  Here's the address of "
"the government lab where the equipment was delivered.  I want you to go "
"there, find the tunnels that they dug, and download everything you can about "
"the train network.  On the other hand, our sponsors were extremely impressed "
"in getting this far without their direction, and would like to apologize by "
"supporting this mission with a whole 300 merch!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgid "So glad for your help."
msgstr "Je me réjouis de votre aide."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgid ""
"The equipment was rated for 50 feet underground, so that tunnel entrance is "
"going to be deeper inside a lab than a normal subway.  Fifty feet would mean "
"maybe four stories down.  Bring back anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"L'équipement a été conçu pour une profondeur de 15 mètres, de sorte que "
"l'entrée du tunnel sera plus profonde à l'intérieur d'un laboratoire que dans "
"un métro normal. 15 mètres signifie peut-être quatre étages plus bas. Ramenez "
"tout ce que vous trouvez sur une clé USB."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgid ""
"Fantastic!  I should be able to reconstruct what cargo moved between which "
"labs.  I wonder what was really going on down there."
msgstr ""
"Fantastique ! Je devrais pouvoir reconstituer les cargaisons qui ont circulé "
"entre les différents laboratoires. Je me demande ce qui se passait vraiment "
"là-dessous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/NPC_Smokes.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as shopkeeper with missions.  Faction
#. critical.  Real name: Gavin Wheeler
msgid "Smokes"
msgstr "Smokes"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Unknown Recipient"
msgstr "Destinataire Inconnu"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Unknown Recipient"
msgid ""
"Deliver the FEMA hard drive to the strange group that Smokes mentioned.  "
"Return to the evacuation center when the data's been delivered."
msgstr ""
"Livrer le disque dur de la FEMA à l'étrange groupe mentionné par Smokes. "
"Retourner au centre d'évacuation lorsque les données ont été livrées."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
msgid "Got the hard drive delivered?"
msgstr "Vous avez livré le disque dur?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
msgid ""
"Oh, good.  I'm glad you're alright; I had no idea what to make of them.  "
"Well, one less thing to worry about."
msgstr ""
"Oh, c'est bien. Je suis content que vous alliez bien ; je ne savais pas quoi "
"en penser. Eh bien, une chose de moins à s'inquiéter."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
msgid ""
"At least you came back alive.  Don't sweat it too much - it's no skin off my "
"back.  If they want it that bad, they can come get another copy themselves."
msgstr ""
"Au moins, tu es revenu vivant. Ne vous en faites pas trop, ce n'est pas une "
"peau de chagrin. S'ils le veulent tant que ça, ils peuvent venir chercher un "
"autre exemplaire eux-mêmes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Clear Back Bay"
msgstr "Vider le Garage à l'Arrière"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid ""
"Clear out the barricaded back area in the refugee center and lay the former "
"leader of the Free Merchants to rest, in exchange for the local currency: "
"Free Merchant certified notes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid ""
"If you really want to lend a hand we could use your help clearing out the "
"dead in the back bay.  Fearful of going outside during the first days of the "
"Cataclysm we ended up throwing our dead and the zombies we managed to kill in "
"the sealed back bay.  Our promising leader at the time even fell… he turned "
"into something different.  Kill all of them and make sure they won't bother "
"us again.  We can't pay much, besides some of our own internal money which "
"isn't good for that much yet, but it would help us to reclaim the bay.  "
"<color_red>If you accept, I'll tell the guards to immediately take down the "
"barricade in the back.  You should only accept if you're ready to do this "
"now.</color>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid "Please be careful, we don't need any more deaths."
msgstr "S'il vous plait, soyez prudent, nous n'avons pas besoin de plus de morts."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Red.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Area"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Lost in the Woods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Protect the cattle"
msgid ""
"Come back when you get a chance, we really need to start reclaiming the "
"region."
msgstr ""
"Revenez quand vous en aurez l'occasion, nous devons vraiment commencer à "
"reprendre cette région."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
msgid "If you can, get a friend or two to help you."
msgstr "Si vous pouvez, prenez un ou deux amis pour vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid "Will they be bothering us any longer?"
msgstr "Est-ce qu'ils vont nous ennuyer encore longtemps ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid ""
"Thank you, having that big of a threat close to home was nerve wracking.  "
"Here's some of our local certified notes, we've been paying these to our "
"workers in exchange for supplies.  They're getting some value in the center "
"as a trade item, I'm afraid they're all we have to spare at the moment."
msgstr ""
"Merci, une menace aussi importante à proximité de chez nous était très "
"éprouvante pour les nerfs. Voici quelques-uns de nos billets certifiés "
"locaux, nous les avons payés à nos travailleurs en échange de fournitures. "
"Ils ont une certaine valeur au centre en tant qu'objet d'échange, mais je "
"crains que ce soit tout ce dont nous disposons pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Name of the monster group "GROUP_REFUGEE_BOSS_ZOMBIE" placed on map
#. update on start of mission "Clear Back Bay"
msgid "Sean McLaughlin"
msgstr "Sean McLaughlin"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Missing Caravan"
msgstr "Caravane manquante"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Missing Caravan"
msgid ""
"Investigate the last known location of a disappeared scavenger trading party, "
"and eliminate any bandits or raiders in the vicinity in exchange for "
"<reward_count:FMCNote> certified notes."
msgstr ""
"Enquêtez sur le dernier emplacement connu d'un groupe de pilleurs disparus et "
"éliminez les pillards ou quoi que ce soit d'autre présents dans les environs "
"en échange de <reward_count:FMCNote> notes certifiées."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
msgid ""
"This is a bit more involved than the last request, we recently lost a "
"scavenger party coming to trade with us and would like you to investigate.  "
"We strongly suspect a raider band or horde caught them off-guard.  I can give "
"you the coordinates of their last radio message but little else.  In either "
"case, deal with the threat so that the scavengers can continue to pass "
"through in relative safety.  The best reward I can offer is a claim to the "
"supplies they were carrying, plus thirty certified notes - that's our own "
"internal money, good for trading and such."
msgstr ""
"Cette demande est un peu plus complexe que la précédente.  Nous avons "
"récemment perdu un groupe de pilleurs qui venait faire du commerce avec nous "
"et nous aimerions que vous enquêtiez.  Nous soupçonnons fortement une bande "
"de pillards ou une horde zombies de les avoir pris au dépourvu.  Je peux vous "
"donner les coordonnées de leur dernier message radio, mais pas grand-chose "
"d'autre.  Quel que soit le cas, occupez vous de la menace pour que les "
"pilleurs puissent continuer à passer en toute sécurité.  La meilleure "
"récompense que je puisse offrir est un droit sur les provisions qu'ils "
"transportaient ainsi que trente billets certifiés - c'est notre monnaie "
"interne, bonne pour les échanges et autres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
msgid "Our community survives on trade, we appreciate it."
msgstr "Nous apprécions, notre communauté survis grâce au marchandage."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
msgid ""
"Thank you, the world is a better place without them.  Two of our more skilled "
"individuals accepted the assistance of the Old Guard in setting up an outpost "
"while you were out.  We didn't have many other options, refugees are still "
"streaming in and we don't know what else to do with our limited food supply.  "
"If you get a chance, you should see if they need your assistance in the "
"future…"
msgstr ""
"Merci, le monde est meilleur sans eux. Deux de nos membres les plus "
"compétents ont accepté l'aide de la vieille garde pour établir un avant-poste "
"pendant votre absence. Nous n'avions pas beaucoup d'autres options, les "
"réfugiés continuent d'affluer et nous ne savons pas quoi faire d'autre avec "
"nos réserves de nourriture limitées. Si vous en avez l'occasion, vous devriez "
"voir s'ils ont besoin de votre aide à l'avenir..."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgstr "Récupérer le prospectus"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid ""
"Visit the farming commune and bring the foreman's prospectus back to the "
"refugee center, for <reward_count:FMCNote> certified notes."
msgstr ""
"Visit the farming commune and bring the foreman's prospectus back to the "
"refugee center, for <reward_count:FMCNote> certified notes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid ""
"We recently set out some skilled people to start an outpost, to secure us "
"some food supplies in a safer location.  The new outpost that we've started "
"could use your assistance.  I need you to get the foreman's prospectus before "
"we begin to send additional refugees to the farming commune.  Consult with "
"the foreman to get more detailed tasks.  We've got 50 Certified Notes for you "
"if you can do this for us."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons récemment envoyé quelques personnes qualifiées pour créer un "
"avant-poste, afin de nous assurer des réserves de nourriture dans un endroit "
"plus sûr. Le nouvel avant-poste que nous avons créé aurait besoin de votre "
"aide. J'ai besoin que vous obteniez le prospectus du contremaître avant que "
"nous commencions à envoyer des réfugiés supplémentaires dans la commune "
"agricole. Consultez le contremaître pour obtenir des tâches plus détaillées. "
"Nous avons 50 notes certifiées pour vous si vous pouvez faire cela pour nous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid "I'm sure the outpost will expand quickly with your assistance."
msgstr "Je suis sûr que la commune s'établira rapidement avec votre assistance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid "Just follow your map."
msgstr "Suivez simplement la carte."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid "Do you have the prospectus?"
msgstr "Vous avez le prospectus ? "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgid ""
"With this we'll be able to convince others to invest in the commune.  Thank "
"you, here's your money.  We also managed to get a manual crank hooked up to "
"the garage in the back, so feel free to make use of that - you've been a "
"great help to us."
msgstr ""
"Avec ceci nous serons capable de convaincre d'autres intérêts d'investir dans "
"la commune. Merci, voilà votre paiement. Nous avons aussi réussi à installer "
"une manivelle dans le garage à l'arrière, vous nous avez été d'une grande "
"aide, donc si vous avez un véhicule à entreposer, vous êtes libre de le "
"laisser entre nos mains."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Solar Power"
msgstr "Énergie Solaire"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Solar Power"
msgid ""
"Deliver 10 solar panel arrays to help the Free Merchants set up a renewable "
"power grid, in exchange for a handsome reward."
msgstr ""
"Livrez 10 groupes de panneaux photovoltaïques aux Marchands Libres afin que "
"ceci puissent installer un réseau électrique renouvelable dans le centre de "
"réfugiés en échange d'une récompense considérable."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
msgid ""
"We are starting to build new infrastructure here and would like to get a few "
"new electrical systems online… unfortunately our existing system relies on an "
"array of something called RTGs.  Running generators isn't a viable option "
"underground, of course.  We have a big flat roof up top, and if we had a few "
"solar panel arrays we could use them to top up our usage.  We could pay you "
"pretty handsomely to bring us, say, ten solar panel arrays?"
msgstr ""
"Nous sommes en train de construire de l'infrastructure ici et nous aimerions "
"ajouter quelques systèmes électriques additionnels mais malheureusement notre "
"réseau électrique actuel tourne sur une batterie de GTRs. Utiliser des "
"générateurs à essence dans le sous-sol est bien sûr hors de question et de "
"toute manière nous n'avons pas vraiment assez de carburant pour que ceci soit "
"une solution viable. Nous avons par contre un large toit plat, et quelques "
"panneaux photovoltaïques seraient probablement assez pour combler la demande "
"de nos rénovations. Nous serions prêts à vous payez une récompense "
"considérable si vous nous rameniez disons… dix groupes de panneaux "
"photovoltaïques?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
msgid "If you can do this for us our survival options would vastly increase."
msgstr ""
"Si vous pouvez faire ceci pour nous nos chances de survie seront grandement "
"accrues."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
msgid "Solar panel arrays are pretty common on solar farms and on rooftops."
msgstr ""
"Les groupes de panneaux photovoltaïques sont assez faciles à trouver sur les "
"toits de bâtiments variés ou dans une ferme solaire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
msgid ""
"Great, I know it isn't much but we hope to continue to expand thanks to your "
"help."
msgstr ""
"Fantastique, je sais que ce n'est pas beaucoup, mais nous espérons pouvoir "
"être capable de continuer à améliorer les choses ici avec votre aide."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "In a Pickle"
msgstr "Dans le pétrin"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "In a Pickle"
msgid ""
"Deliver 100 0.5 L glass jars to the Free Merchants to kickstart their food "
"storage plans."
msgstr ""
"Livrez 100 bocaux en verre de 0.5L aux Marchands Libres pour les aider à "
"lancer leur plan de stockage de nourriture à long terme."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
msgid ""
"While we've managed to secure day to day food supplies, it's very much hand "
"to mouth.  Our reserves would barely last a few days if something kept our "
"people locked in.  We need a stockpile to avoid that.  Thanks to our outpost "
"we have a bit of meat and vegetables coming in, but we need a better way to "
"preserve them.  Some of our people know enough about food canning that if we "
"had a good stock of canning jars, we could make pickles and canned meats to "
"get us set for the winter.  I'll pay you a premium rate if you can bring us "
"around a hundred jars to get us started."
msgstr ""
"Jusqu'ici nous avons réussi à trouver et acheter assez de nourriture pour "
"vivre au jour le jour, mais ceci est plus précaire que la majorité veut, nos "
"réserves ne dureront pas longtemps si quelque chose garde nos caravanes au "
"centre pour plus de quelque jours, et nous avons besoin d'un stockage de "
"nourriture à long terme pour parer à cette éventualité. Grâce à la commune "
"nous avons un peu de viande et de légumes arrivant assez régulièrement en "
"plus de nos échanges, mais nous devons trouver un moyen de les conserver plus "
"longtemps. Plusieurs personnes ici ont les connaissances nécessaire pour "
"mariner cet influx, mais nous avons besoin d'un bon stock de bocaux avant "
"qu'ils puissent faire ceci et nous donner assez de provisions pour passer "
"l'hiver. Je serais prêt à vous payer au dessus du marché si vous pouviez nous "
"liver 100 bocaux pour lancer ce projet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
msgid "It'll take a load off my shoulders if I can finally stop worrying about this."
msgstr ""
"Ce serait un poids levé de mes épaules si je pouvez finalement arrêter de me "
"soucier de ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
msgid ""
"We'll hold for the moment, but I'll get an ulcer if I have to keep worrying.  "
"If you reconsider let me know."
msgstr ""
"On devrait être capable de tenir pour l'instant, mais je vais avoir un ulcère "
"si je continue de me soucier de ça, donc dites-moi si vous voulez "
"reconsidérer mon offre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
msgid ""
"That's one less thing to worry about.  Glad to have someone like you on our "
"side.  Here's 25 merch, and the broker will buy any further glass jars you "
"can find - at a reduced price, we can't keep up the premium rate.  Actually, "
"the broker was saying they had some jobs like this for you, and that it might "
"be easier to just go straight through their office if you want more work."
msgstr ""
"C'est une chose de moins à garder en tête. Je suis content d'avoir quelqu'un "
"comme vous de notre côté. Voilà 25 merch, et le courtier achètera tout bocaux "
"de plus que vous pouvez lui amener - à un prix plus bas bien sûr, nous ne "
"pouvons pas continuer à les acheter à un prix aussi fort. Maintenant que j'y "
"pense, le courtier me disait qu'il aurait probablement d'autre boulots comme "
"celui-ci pour vous, et que ce serait probablement plus facile si vous alliez "
"le voire directement dans son bureau si vous voulez plus de travail."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, we had an odd group come by maybe two days after the power grid went "
"off.  Two armed guards wearing brown uniforms, and what looked like a "
"government doctor, had a hazmat suit on.  Everyone had masks they never took "
"off.  They looked organized… maybe a military remnant from somewhere close by."
msgstr ""
"Un groupe étrange est venu nous voir deux jours après la coupure du réseau "
"électrique. Deux gardes armés portant des uniformes bruns, et ce qui semblait "
"être un médecin du gouvernement, qui portait une combinaison de protection "
"contre les matières dangereuses. Tout le monde portait des masques qu'ils "
"n'enlevaient jamais. Ils avaient l'air organisés... peut-être un reste de "
"l'armée d'un endroit proche."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What were they here for?"
msgstr "Ils étaient là pour quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The doctor paid us in advance to get some old FEMA info from our computers "
"here, and told us to deliver the data to an isolated building afterwards.  We "
"still haven't done that.  I'm half worried it might have been some kind of "
"trap, or trick."
msgstr ""
"Le médecin nous a payés à l'avance pour récupérer de vieilles informations de "
"la FEMA sur nos ordinateurs ici, et nous a demandé de livrer les données dans "
"un bâtiment isolé par la suite. Nous ne l'avons toujours pas fait. J'ai peur "
"qu'il s'agisse d'un piège ou d'une ruse."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where's that building at, exactly?"
msgstr "Il est où exactement ce bâtiment?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem right to be suspicious."
msgstr "Vous avez probablement raison de vous méfier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I could share the dropoff location if you want to bring the drive there for "
"us, but whatever's there, I'm not sure it's worth all the trouble.  I'll "
"reward you for your trouble."
msgstr ""
"Je pourrais partager le lieu de dépôt si vous voulez y amener le véhicule "
"pour nous, mais quoi qu'il en soit, je ne suis pas sûr que cela vaille la "
"peine de se donner tant de mal. Je vous récompenserai pour votre peine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems fine to me.  I'll take your drive for you."
msgstr "Cela me va.  Je peut vous prendre votre disque dur."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I can see why you haven't done it yet.  Hold that thought for now."
msgstr ""
"En fait, je comprends pourquoi vous ne l'avez pas encore fait. Gardez cette "
"idée en tête pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was hoping you'd say that.  It's an old isolated building not too far from "
"here; you should probably just leave the drive to whoever's there and be on "
"your way.  And like I said, be careful approaching the place.  I wouldn't "
"like leading you straight into your death."
msgstr ""
"J'espérais que vous diriez cela. C'est un vieux bâtiment isolé pas très loin "
"d'ici ; vous devriez probablement laisser la conduite à qui que ce soit et "
"partir. Et comme je l'ai dit, soyez prudent en approchant de l'endroit. Je ne "
"voudrais pas vous mener tout droit à la mort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't worry, I'll be careful.  I'll let you know when it's done."
msgstr ""
"Ne vous inquiétez pas, je serai prudent. Je te ferai savoir quand ce sera "
"fait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sure I'll manage."
msgstr "Je suis sûr·e que je vais pouvoir me débrouiller."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hmm.\"  Smokes looks thoughtful, rubbing his chin.  \"Well, most of the "
"people downstairs aren't willing to come up for things like that, and a lot "
"of folks that are up here have a lot of bad memories from that.  You could "
"try asking around some of the people we have upstairs, but it'll be tough.  "
"If you have some merch you could spare, though, I could get some people off "
"guard duty and into your little crew for some hazard pay.  You might also "
"have luck asking the Old Guard rep in the southwest bay, near the library - I "
"hear they've got some volunteers lately."
msgstr ""
"Hmm.\" Smokes prend un air pensif et se frotte le menton. \"Eh bien, la "
"plupart des gens d'en bas ne sont pas prêts à monter pour ce genre de choses, "
"et beaucoup de gens d'en haut en ont gardé de mauvais souvenirs. Tu pourrais "
"essayer de demander à des gens de l'étage, mais ce sera difficile. Si vous "
"avez un peu de marchandise à offrir, je pourrais faire sortir quelques "
"personnes de leur service de garde et les intégrer à votre petite équipe, "
"moyennant une prime de risque. Vous pourriez aussi demander au représentant "
"de la vieille garde dans la baie sud-ouest, près de la bibliothèque - j'ai "
"entendu dire qu'ils avaient quelques volontaires ces derniers temps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 merch] Five merch for someone sounds fair to me."
msgstr "[5 merch] Cinq merch pour une personne de plus m'a l'air d'être un bon marché."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[10 merch] How about ten merch to do it?"
msgstr "[10 merch] Qu'est ce que dix merch pourrait m'offrir?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the advice.  Maybe I'll come back with some more merch."
msgstr "Merci pour vos conseils. Je reviendrai peut-être avec d'autres produits."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's enough to get someone off guard duty, yeah.  Hand it here and I'll set "
"it up.\"  The money exchanges hands.  \"Right.  I haven't updated this list "
"in a while, so some people are still assigned to watch the back bay, which is "
"technically a free shift now.  I'll let one of them know about what's up and "
"they can spend the time helping to clean up back there.  Hope it helps."
msgstr ""
"C'est suffisant pour faire sortir quelqu'un du service de garde, oui. "
"Donnez-le moi et je vais le mettre en place.\" L'argent change de main. "
"\"C'est vrai. Je n'ai pas mis à jour cette liste depuis un moment, donc "
"certaines personnes sont toujours assignées à la surveillance de la baie "
"arrière, qui est techniquement un poste libre maintenant. Je vais informer "
"l'un d'entre eux de ce qui se passe et ils pourront passer du temps à aider à "
"nettoyer l'arrière-boutique. J'espère que cela vous aidera."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Woah, you're really intent, hey?  That's a lot for most people here.\"  The "
"money exchanges hands.  \"That's enough to get two people off guard duty for "
"an afternoon, even with all the ugliness back there.  And you know what?  "
"I'll help out, too, so make that three.  I can appreciate someone who's "
"willing to put their money where their mouth is."
msgstr ""
"Woah, vous avez vraiment l'intention, hé ? C'est beaucoup pour la plupart des "
"gens ici.\" L'argent change de main. \"C'est assez pour permettre à deux "
"personnes de ne pas être de garde pendant un après-midi, même avec toute la "
"laideur qu'il y a derrière. Et vous savez quoi ? Je donnerai aussi un coup de "
"main, alors ça fait trois. Je peux apprécier quelqu'un qui est prêt à joindre "
"le geste à la parole."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you very much!"
msgstr "Merci beaucoup!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks at you cautiously.  \"He hasn't been bothering you, has he?  Dave's "
"usually pretty harmless.\""
msgstr ""
"*regarde avec circonspection.  \"Il ne vous a pas dérangé, n'est-ce pas?  "
"Dave est généralement assez inoffensif.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"He wants permission to build himself a little shelter outside of your lobby, "
"somewhere out of the way.  He'd need access to your washrooms and things, but "
"you could clear him out of this space."
msgstr ""
"Il demande la permission de se construire un petit abri à l'extérieur de "
"votre hall d'entrée, quelque part à l'écart. Il aurait besoin d'accéder à vos "
"toilettes et autres, mais vous pourriez le faire sortir de cet espace."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, sounds great on paper, but *where*?  We aren't swimming in real estate "
"here, the place is seriously overcrowded.  And I won't have him living out of "
"a soggy cardboard box on the doorstep, it's an even worse look than the lobby."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, cela semble très bien sur le papier, mais *où* ? Nous ne nageons "
"pas dans l'immobilier ici, l'endroit est sérieusement surpeuplé. Et je ne "
"veux pas qu'il vive dans une boîte en carton détrempée sur le pas de la "
"porte, c'est encore pire que le hall d'entrée."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What about the rooftop?  There's a stair access there, I can see it from "
"outside, and he'd probably be able to do a bit of a lookout job."
msgstr ""
"Et sur le toit ? Il y a un escalier pour y accéder, je peux le voir de "
"l'extérieur, et il pourrait probablement faire un peu le guet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rubs his chin.  \"It's probably technically a fire hazard, but there's not "
"much to light up there besides what Dave brings.  And a few of the guards are "
"pretty attached to him, so we could maybe send folks up to keep an eye on him "
"and make sure he's doing okay.  That wouldn't interfere with comings and "
"goings, either.\"  He pauses a moment, looking at his ledger as if it "
"contains answers.  \"You know what?  Sure.  If Dave is okay with it, I can "
"talk the others into letting him have rooftop access to build himself a "
"little shelter, as long as he continues to keep it clean up there like he has "
"in here.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il se frotte le menton. \"C'est probablement un risque technique d'incendie, "
"mais il n'y a pas grand-chose à allumer là-haut à part ce que Dave apporte. "
"Et quelques gardes sont assez attachés à lui, alors on pourrait peut-être "
"envoyer des gens pour garder un œil sur lui et s'assurer qu'il va bien. Cela "
"n'interférerait pas avec les allées et venues, non plus.\" Il s'arrête un "
"instant, regardant son registre comme s'il contenait des réponses. \"Il "
"s'arrête un instant et regarde son registre comme s'il contenait des "
"réponses. Bien sûr. Si Dave est d'accord, je peux convaincre les autres de "
"lui laisser l'accès au toit pour qu'il se construise un petit abri, à "
"condition qu'il continue à le garder propre comme il l'a fait ici.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks.  I'll go let him know."
msgstr "Merci. Je vais aller le lui dire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*looks up.  \"Hey.\""
msgstr "*regarde vers le haut. \"Hey.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*waves you over.  \"I haven't seen you before.  Welcome to our little homely "
"house.\""
msgstr ""
"*Jvous fait signe de venir. \"Je ne vous ai jamais vu auparavant. Bienvenue "
"dans notre petite maison.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you?  This is a refugee center, right?"
msgstr "Qui êtes vous? Ceci est un centre de réfugiés non?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I wonder if you've heard "
"anything about it, maybe from some of the traders coming through?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis à la recherche d'un bâtiment spécifique et étrange.  Je voulais juste "
"savoir si vous en aviez entendu parler, peut-être d'un des marchands passant "
"par ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hope it helps."
msgstr "J'espère que ça aidera."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Give me second to write that down… okay, done."
msgstr "Donnez-moi une seconde pour l'écrire… ok, c'est fait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You know where to find me."
msgstr "Vous savez où me trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Next shipment should arrive in around <interval>."
msgstr "Le prochain envoi devrait arriver vers <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stick around for <interval>, there will surely be something you'd like."
msgstr ""
"Restez dans les parages pendant <interval>, il y aura sûrement quelque chose "
"qui vous plaira."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, I will make sure to check back.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Before you ask, we're full.  You're right about the refugee part, but we're "
"way over capacity right now.  We don't have the food or space to take on "
"anyone else.\"  He softens a little.  \"As for me, I do a lot of things here, "
"but mostly I keep tabs on our supplies.  You can call me Smokes, or Gavin; "
"whichever you prefer.  I also trade with people from outside, like you.  If "
"you're in the market for hardware, we're selling, and if you have food, we "
"are very much buying.  Anyways, uh, what can I do for you"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"?\"\n"
"\n"
"Liam looks around at the crowded room, speaking in a soft voice for just your "
"ears.  \"Can't honestly believe people are trying to crowd in here.  They're "
"all so scared, this is a death trap."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "?"
msgstr "?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got some time to talk?"
msgstr "Vous avez un peu de temps pour discuter?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I just wanted to look around.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Lay it on me."
msgstr "Mettez-le-moi sur le dos."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alright, shoot."
msgstr "D'accord, tirez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Something on your mind?"
msgstr "Quelque chose vous tracasse?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I talk to you about that fellow over there in the dinosaur suit?"
msgstr "Puis-je vous parler de ce type qui porte un costume de dinosaure ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "'Sorry, we're full'?  Do you greet everyone like that?"
msgstr "\"Désolé, nous sommes complets\" ? Accueillez-vous tout le monde comme ça ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You're having trouble with food?"
msgstr "Vous avez des problèmes de nourriture?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned you were selling hardware?"
msgstr "Vous avez mentionné que vous vendez des outils et des matériaux?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with these people in the lobby?  Are they with you?"
msgstr ""
"Qu'est-ce qui se passe avec ces personnes dans le hall d'entrée ? Sont-ils "
"avec vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I took care of your beggar problem."
msgstr "Je me suis occupé de votre problème de mendicité."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with these 'Free Merchant certified notes'?"
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez m'en dire plus au sujet de ces \"billets certifiés par les "
"Marchants Libres\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking for work.  Can I do anything for the center?"
msgstr "Je cherche du travail. Puis-je faire quelque chose pour le centre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you interested in buying any processed lumber?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'une source de bois d'œuvre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does this center need any metal?"
msgstr "Ce centre à besoin de métal?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you interested in any chemical supplies?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'une source de produits chimiques?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, unfortunately.  They're folks that wanted to join us, but we're too full "
"and we don't have enough to share.  Most people leave and look for their own "
"place when we turn them down, but these ones… didn't.  We've been trying to "
"find them a safe place, but there's a shortage of those these days, for "
"reasons I'm sure you can guess.  Until then, we're letting them crash here as "
"long as they don't mess the place up."
msgstr ""
"Non, malheureusement. Ce sont des gens qui voulaient se joindre à nous, mais "
"nous sommes trop pleins et nous n'avons pas assez à partager. La plupart des "
"gens partent et cherchent un endroit à eux lorsque nous les refusons, mais "
"ceux-là... ne l'ont pas fait. Nous avons essayé de leur trouver un endroit "
"sûr, mais il y a une pénurie ces jours-ci, pour des raisons que vous pouvez "
"certainement deviner. En attendant, nous les laissons s'installer ici tant "
"qu'ils ne mettent pas le bazar."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Social 1] If I could look into clearing them out of here, would you be able "
"to pay me back?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why haven't they gone anywhere else?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ne sont-ils pas allés ailleurs ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Couldn't you get them out?  Your guards are well-armed."
msgstr "Vous ne pouvez pas les faire sortir ? Vos gardes sont bien armés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Best of luck."
msgstr "Bonne chance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know, why don't you ask them?  I haven't pried, but where else do "
"they have to go?  You've seen how bad it is out there.  We don't have the "
"space for them, but it won't kill us to give them some shelter as long as "
"they aren't too much of a drain on resources"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Don't you guys have, like, scavengers and things?\"  Liam sounds like he's "
"trying not to get irritated with Smokes.  \"Can't these guys help out in some "
"way in exchange for food?  It seems insane to just keep them sitting in your "
"entry way.\"\n"
"\n"
"Smokes gives him a long-suffering look.  \"Like I said, ask them.  We can't "
"take them in, though.  It's not just them.  We've had to turn away dozens of "
"people, if we started making exceptions we'd be dead meat.  These guys are "
"just the ones who didn't try their luck out there, they've got their reasons "
"I guess.  I don't like this any more than you do."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Jesus, man, we aren't monsters.  I'm sure we could get them out if we really "
"needed to, yeah, but why would we do that?  We need to be stringent with who "
"we take on, that's true, but forcing out people in need isn't a great way to "
"convince anyone that we're reliable allies.  The world doesn't run on good "
"faith, but it's damn well nicer to live in because of it."
msgstr ""
"Bon sang, on n'est pas des monstres. Je suis sûr que nous pourrions les faire "
"sortir si nous en avions vraiment besoin, oui, mais pourquoi le ferions-nous "
"? Nous devons faire preuve de rigueur dans nos choix, c'est vrai, mais ce "
"n'est pas en expulsant des gens dans le besoin que nous convaincrons qui que "
"ce soit que nous sommes des alliés fiables. Le monde ne fonctionne pas sur la "
"bonne foi, mais il est bien plus agréable à vivre grâce à cela."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We don't have a lot to share, but… well, I guess it's not safe for them.  At "
"best, it's a health hazard waiting to happen.  We could pay you in merch if "
"you can clear them out without anyone getting hurt, yeah."
msgstr ""
"Nous n'avons pas grand-chose à partager, mais... je suppose que ce n'est pas "
"sûr pour eux. Au mieux, c'est un risque pour la santé. Nous pourrions vous "
"payer en marchandises si vous pouviez les débarrasser sans que personne ne "
"soit blessé, oui."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  What's merch?"
msgstr "Je vais voir ce que je peux faire. Qu'est ce que de la \"merch\"?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No guarantees, but I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "Aucune garantie, mais je vais voir ce que je peux faire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I appreciate it a lot, getting them somewhere safe.  I hope that's what you "
"did, anyway.  In any case, having the lobby clear is a big help.  Even with "
"the uh, cardboard guy still around, he's a lot easier to handle alone."
msgstr ""
"J'apprécie beaucoup que vous les mettiez en sécurité. J'espère que c'est ce "
"que vous avez fait, en tout cas. En tout cas, le fait que le hall d'entrée "
"soit dégagé m'aide beaucoup. Même si le gars en carton est toujours là, il "
"est beaucoup plus facile à gérer seul."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I do believe we discussed a reward?"
msgstr "Je me rappelle qu'on s'était mis d'accord sur une récompense?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just glad to help."
msgstr "Je suis heureux d'avoir pu aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"And so we did.\"  Smokes reaches under their table, counts out some money, "
"and slides it through a slot in the glass.  \"Here's five merch a head for "
"the folks you found a new home for.  We won't forget it"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
".\"\n"
"\n"
"Luo puts her hands on her hips.  \"You're getting *paid* for… ah, fuck it.  I "
"should be pissed, but honestly I'm so glad to be out of this place, I can't "
"even be mad.  That's really saying something, coming from me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not as much as I'd like, I'm afraid.  Most of these shelters seemed to have "
"been designed to make people *feel* safer, not to actually keep them safe.  "
"Our radio equipment is terrible… I don't think it was even meant to be used "
"seriously.  I've heard some talk of hordes."
msgstr ""
"Pas autant que je le souhaiterais, je le crains. La plupart de ces abris "
"semblent avoir été conçus pour que les gens se sentent plus en sécurité, et "
"non pour qu'ils le soient réellement. Notre équipement radio est terrible... "
"Je ne pense pas qu'il ait été conçu pour être utilisé sérieusement. J'ai "
"entendu parler de hordes."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hordes?"
msgstr "Des hordes?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Tools, to be precise.  The basement and the storage rooms had way more than "
"we need, and a lot of people brought their own when they were evacuating.  "
"There's more than we could ever use, so we'll be happy to sell them at a very "
"fair price.  Nothing in the way of radios, so you'll have to look somewhere "
"else for that."
msgstr ""
"Des outils, pour être précis. Le sous-sol et les salles de stockage en "
"contenaient bien plus que nous n'en avons besoin, et de nombreuses personnes "
"ont apporté les leurs lors de l'évacuation. Il y en a plus que nous ne "
"pourrons jamais utiliser, nous serons donc heureux de les vendre à un prix "
"très raisonnable. Il n'y a pas de radios, vous devrez donc chercher ailleurs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait, basement?  I didn't know this place had a basement."
msgstr "Un sous-sol? Je ne savais pas que cet endroit avait un sous-sol."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Mind if I take a look at your stock?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux jeter un œil sur votre stock?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Radios?  That seems awfully specific."
msgstr "Des radios?  C'est une demande assez spécifique."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to know."
msgstr "Bon à savoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've had some issues with scavengers.  Apparently a big part of the "
"marketing for these shelters was high-end radio equipment that they could use "
"to keep in touch with each other, and a lot of the people we've traded with "
"have asked about it.  Not that we don't have any radios, mind you, but "
"they're all absolutely awful.  Even if we *could* spare any, they'd be "
"useless to anyone that actually needed it - not much point in lugging around "
"a ham radio that can't pick up anything more than a mile away."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons eu quelques problèmes avec les charognards. Apparemment, une "
"grande partie du marketing pour ces abris était un équipement radio haut de "
"gamme qu'ils pouvaient utiliser pour rester en contact les uns avec les "
"autres, et beaucoup de gens avec qui nous avons échangé nous ont posé des "
"questions à ce sujet. Ce n'est pas que nous n'ayons pas de radios, mais elles "
"sont toutes absolument horribles. Même si nous pouvions en avoir, elles "
"seraient inutiles pour ceux qui en auraient vraiment besoin - il n'y a pas "
"vraiment d'intérêt à se trimballer avec une radio amateur qui ne capte rien à "
"plus d'un kilomètre de distance."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes we are.  The center had a good stock of those awful soy bars, but between "
"all of us, it went fast.  We're making do with what we can skim off the edge "
"of towns, but mostly we rely on trade from people like you.  Speaking of, "
"we'll pay top dollar for anything preserved - canned, salted, dried, "
"whatever.  Just talk to the broker in the back."
msgstr ""
"Oui, c'est vrai. Le centre avait un bon stock de ces horribles barres de "
"soja, mais entre nous tous, c'est parti très vite. Nous nous débrouillons "
"avec ce que nous pouvons trouver aux abords des villes, mais nous comptons "
"surtout sur le commerce de gens comme vous. À ce propos, nous sommes prêts à "
"payer le prix fort pour tout ce qui est conservé - en conserve, salé, séché, "
"etc. Il suffit de parler au courtier à l'arrière."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't see that many of you around."
msgstr "Je ne voit pas beaucoup d'entre vous dans les environs."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Listen, buddy.  We were putting away some of the last food you gave us and "
"noticed it was… off.  Okay I'll cut the shit- It was people.  I don't know "
"how you got it, or what you did, but we aren't taking any chances.  You are "
"not welcome here anymore.  <color_red>I'll give you one minute</color> to "
"fuck off and never come back."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "But I-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, we could use some around here for repairs and whatnot.  What are the "
"terms?"
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, nous pourrions en utiliser pour les réparations et autres.  Quelles "
"sont les conditions?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, how about 250 merch for 100 pounds of…"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que ça vous dit 250 merch pour 45 kilos de…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Chemicals?  I'm sure we could find some use for them, and we are in need of "
"medical supplies.  What's the offer?"
msgstr ""
"Des produits chimiques? Je suis sûr que ça pourrait nous être utile, et nous "
"avons vraiment besoin de matériel médical. Quelle est l'offre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, how about 300 merch for 10 liters of…"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que ça vous dit 300 merch pour 10 litres de…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  Smokes listens"
msgstr ""
"&Vous décrivez l'entrepôt le mieux que vous pouvez et Smokes écoute "
"attentivement"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then shakes his head.  \"Not ringing a bell, I think I'd remember if I'd "
"heard about something like that.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then nods slowly.  \"This sounds a bit familiar, I remember a scavenger "
"coming through a while ago with a weird story about a place like that.  Might "
"be nothing though.\""
msgstr ""
", puis hoche de la tête lentement.  \"Ça me rappelle quelque chose, je me "
"souviens d'un pilleur étant passé par ici il y a un bon moment avec une "
"histoire bizarre concernant un endroit ressemblant à cela.  Mais de tout ce "
"que je sais, cela pourrait être une fausse piste."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A lot of the time, yes.  Our address is on the info boards of most of the "
"evac shelters around here, and people keep showing up that we have to turn "
"away.  It gets easier when you have something you can read off a script."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds a little cruel."
msgstr "Ça semble un peu cruel."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Cannibal + Uncaring] Wait, I thought you were having food problems."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*shrugs.  \"Did you need something else?\""
msgstr "*haussant les épaules. \"Vous aviez besoin d'autre chose ?\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*bristles.  \"I know, alright?  I do.  I hate it too.  But we are packed to "
"the gills right now, and the only way we're going to stay alive is if we keep "
"our gates closed fast.  I don't know what made the scavengers out there so "
"ruthless, but some of us have had to kill our own kids.  Please show some "
"consideration.\""
msgstr ""
" \"Je sais, d'accord?  Je sais.  Je déteste ça aussi.  Mais nous sommes "
"pleins à craquer pour le moment, et la seule façon de rester en vie, c'est de "
"fermer nos portes.  Je ne sais pas ce qui rends les pilleurs si cruel, mais "
"certains d'entre nous ont dû tuer leurs propres enfants.  S'il vous plaît, "
"faites preuve d'un peu de considération.\""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We are.  That's why we're turning people away."
msgstr "C'est le cas. C'est pourquoi nous refusons des gens."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm saying you're giving up a potential source of meat."
msgstr "Je dis que vous renoncez à une source potentielle de viande."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<end_talking_nevermind>  Don't know where I was going with that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can't tell if you're joking or not, but that is seriously fucked up, and I "
"don't want to hear another word about it.  Okay?"
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas si tu plaisantes ou non, mais c'est vraiment n'importe quoi, "
"et je ne veux plus en entendre parler. D'accord ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright, I'm sorry.  Bad joke."
msgstr "D'accord, d'accord, je suis désolé. Mauvaise blague."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not much to say.  What did you want to hear?"
msgstr "Pas grand-chose à dire. Que vouliez-vous entendre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How'd you end up here?"
msgstr "Comment avez-vous atterri ici ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Smokes?  That's quite a name."
msgstr "Smokes?  C'est un sacré nom."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I'm Gavin, like I said.  I was a fireman before <the_cataclysm>, and I "
"was also on duty when everything fell apart.  I'd rather not go into detail, "
"but other than that, I wasn't really much to write home about.  My family was "
"Irish, I never married, and I liked woodworking.  I volunteered to take "
"inventory of what the center had when I got off the bus, one thing leads to "
"another, and now I'm here."
msgstr ""
"Je suis Gavin, comme je l'ai dit. J'étais pompier avant <the_cataclysm>, et "
"j'étais aussi de service quand tout s'est effondré. Je préfère ne pas entrer "
"dans les détails, mais à part ça, je n'avais pas grand-chose à me mettre sous "
"la dent. Ma famille était irlandaise, je ne me suis jamais marié et j'aimais "
"travailler le bois. Je me suis porté volontaire pour faire l'inventaire de ce "
"que le centre avait quand je suis descendu du bus, une chose en entraînant "
"une autre, et maintenant je suis ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rolls his eyes.  \"Tell me about it.  My actual name is Gavin, which I think "
"I told you.  I used to be a firefighter, and people started recognizing me "
"because of the helmet.  Someone called me 'smokes' because of it, and it "
"stuck.  I hate it.  I've never even touched a cigarette.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il roule des yeux. \"Parle-moi de ça. Mon vrai nom est Gavin, je crois que "
"je vous l'ai déjà dit. J'étais pompier, et les gens ont commencé à me "
"reconnaître à cause de mon casque. Quelqu'un m'a appelé 'smokes' à cause de "
"ça, et c'est resté. Je déteste ça. Je n'ai jamais touché une cigarette\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[PER 8] If you hate it, then why are you smiling?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can't say I blame you."
msgstr "Je ne peut pas vraiment vous en vouloir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"Well, I think it's ridiculous, but I guess I don't mind it that "
"much.  I figure it's all in good fun, and people could really use the laugh "
"these days, y'know?  I'm sure they'd stop if I asked.  The helmet is like… a "
"badge of office, at this point.  You can call me Smokes if you really want.\""
msgstr ""
"*rires. \"Je trouve ça ridicule, mais ça ne me dérange pas tant que ça. Je me "
"dis que c'est pour le plaisir et que les gens ont bien besoin de rire en ce "
"moment, vous savez ? Je suis sûr qu'ils arrêteraient si je leur demandais. Le "
"casque est comme... un insigne de fonction, à ce stade. Vous pouvez m'appeler "
"Smokes si vous le voulez vraiment\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, merch.  They're just paper notes we've started using for local cash.  We "
"started out paying each other with dollar bills, but there's so much paper "
"money out there that it's just useless now.  For our internal use, we started "
"certifying bills that represent food and labor in the center here.  We "
"started trading them internally, and then they started circling around, and "
"now other people have started adopting them, too."
msgstr ""
"Oh, des marchandises. Ce sont juste des billets de banque que nous avons "
"commencé à utiliser comme monnaie locale. Nous avons commencé à nous payer "
"les uns les autres avec des billets d'un dollar, mais il y a tellement de "
"papier-monnaie que c'est devenu inutile. Pour notre usage interne, nous avons "
"commencé à certifier des billets qui représentent la nourriture et le travail "
"dans le centre ici. Nous avons commencé à les échanger en interne, puis ils "
"ont commencé à circuler, et maintenant d'autres personnes ont commencé à les "
"adopter aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but the last thing we need is another mouth to feed.  Most of us "
"lack any real survival skills, so keeping our group small enough to survive "
"on the food we trade for is the main thing keeping us alive."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé, mais la dernière chose dont nous avons besoin, c'est d'une "
"autre bouche à nourrir. La plupart d'entre nous n'ont pas de réelles "
"compétences en matière de survie, alors garder notre groupe suffisamment "
"petit pour survivre grâce à la nourriture que nous échangeons est la "
"principale chose qui nous maintient en vie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can pull my own weight!"
msgstr "Je peux porter mon propre poid!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Maybe out there alone, or with a small group, but enough to feed a few dozen "
"other people that aren't helping you?  That just isn't a risk we're willing "
"to take right now.  If you want to trade us supplies or donate something, "
"you're more than welcome to, and it'd be a huge help, but right now, we're "
"far past our comfort zone as it is."
msgstr ""
"Peut-être seul, ou avec un petit groupe, mais suffisamment pour nourrir "
"quelques douzaines d'autres personnes qui ne vous aident pas ? Ce n'est tout "
"simplement pas un risque que nous sommes prêts à prendre pour l'instant. Si "
"vous voulez échanger des fournitures ou faire un don, vous êtes les bienvenus "
"et cela nous aiderait énormément, mais pour l'instant, nous avons déjà "
"dépassé notre zone de confort."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No way in hell.  I'm not going to risk the safety of dozens of people just "
"for some ass.  If you're that desperate, go talk to Alonso."
msgstr ""
"Pas question. Je ne vais pas risquer la sécurité de dizaines de personnes "
"juste pour un cul. Si vous êtes si désespéré, allez parler à Alonso."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The center has a pretty large lower floor, behind metal doors that were made "
"to stand up to basically anything - bombs, radiation, you name it.  Place is "
"basically a vault.  Most of our population is living in there; only people "
"who we think are combat-capable stay up here.  Bear in mind, we started off "
"with a few buses of office workers and soccer moms.  If worst comes to worst, "
"they'll stand a chance if things go bad up here."
msgstr ""
"Le centre dispose d'un étage inférieur assez vaste, derrière des portes "
"métalliques conçues pour résister à n'importe quoi - bombes, radiations, etc. "
"L'endroit est en fait une chambre forte. La majeure partie de notre "
"population vit à l'intérieur ; seules les personnes que nous jugeons aptes au "
"combat restent à l'intérieur. N'oubliez pas que nous avons commencé avec "
"quelques bus d'employés de bureau et de mères de famille. Au pire, ils auront "
"une chance si les choses tournent mal ici."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get down there?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce que je peux me rendre en bas?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can't share that.  We're taking security extremely seriously right now.  "
"The guards downstairs are well-armed, and they've got orders to immediately "
"apprehend anyone they don't recognize.  We want to keep those people as safe "
"we can until either we have more space up here or we've got some room inside "
"the fence for them to live."
msgstr ""
"Je ne peux pas partager cela. Nous prenons la sécurité très au sérieux en ce "
"moment. Les gardes en bas sont bien armés, et ils ont reçu l'ordre "
"d'appréhender immédiatement toute personne qu'ils ne reconnaissent pas. Nous "
"voulons garder ces personnes en sécurité jusqu'à ce que nous ayons plus "
"d'espace ici ou que nous ayons de l'espace à l'intérieur de la clôture pour "
"qu'elles puissent vivre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I suppose that makes sense."
msgstr "Je suppose que c'est logique."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why spend so much effort keeping it locked down?  I thought you mentioned "
"they weren't able to help."
msgstr ""
"Pourquoi dépenser autant d'efforts pour le verrouiller ? Je croyais que vous "
"aviez dit qu'ils n'étaient pas en mesure de vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If I could go down there, I could help bring them supplies.  Food, medicine…"
msgstr ""
"Si je pouvais y aller, je pourrais les aider à se ravitailler.  De la "
"nourriture, des médicaments…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just because they're not boots on the ground doesn't mean they aren't "
"helping.  In fact, I'd say that a lot of them are our most important people.  "
"They keep the power running, for one thing.  And even if they weren't "
"helping, look at it this way: all of us are scared, and almost all of us have "
"lost someone from all this.  We aren't going to throw our own to the wolves."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas parce qu'ils ne sont pas sur le terrain qu'ils ne nous aident "
"pas. En fait, je dirais que beaucoup d'entre eux sont les personnes les plus "
"importantes pour nous. Ils font fonctionner l'électricité, pour commencer. Et "
"même s'ils n'aidaient pas, il faut voir les choses sous cet angle : nous "
"avons tous peur, et nous avons presque tous perdu quelqu'un à cause de tout "
"cela. Nous n'allons pas jeter les nôtres aux loups."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I appreciate the offer, I really do, but I'm sorry.  The basement is "
"off-limits to outsiders, and we're not in the market for new recruits right "
"now.  Maybe once we're in a better spot there might be some room to think "
"about it, but right now I can't justify just giving you free reign down there."
msgstr ""
"J'apprécie l'offre, vraiment, mais je suis désolé. Le sous-sol est "
"hors-limite à toute personne de l'extérieur, et nous ne sommes pas intéressés "
"à recruter pour l'instant. Peut-être que si nous arrivons à stabiliser "
"légèrement notre situation il y aurait un peu de place pour y penser, mais "
"pour l'instant il n'est pas possible de justifier de vous donner carte "
"blanche en bas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.  Someone came through this way a while back saying he had tried to "
"drive into Syracuse after the outbreak.  Didn't even make it downtown before "
"he ran into a wall of zombies that he said could stop a tank.  He hightailed "
"it out, but he said there were several thousand at least.  I guess when you "
"get a bunch of them together, they end up making enough noise to attract "
"everyone in the neighborhood.  Thankfully, we haven't had a mob like that "
"pass by here, because I'm not sure the fence would do much to keep them out."
msgstr ""
"Oui. Quelqu'un est passé par là il y a quelque temps en disant qu'il avait "
"essayé d'aller à Syracuse en voiture après l'épidémie. Il n'a même pas "
"atteint le centre-ville avant de se heurter à un mur de zombies qui, selon "
"lui, aurait pu arrêter un char d'assaut. Il s'est sauvé, mais il a dit qu'il "
"y avait au moins plusieurs milliers de zombies. Je suppose que lorsqu'ils "
"sont nombreux, ils finissent par faire assez de bruit pour attirer tout le "
"monde dans le quartier. Heureusement, nous n'avons jamais vu passer une telle "
"foule, car je ne suis pas sûr que la clôture puisse les empêcher d'entrer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Other than those people with the hard drive, none that I know of.  Scavengers "
"share some odd things, but we can't exactly go check for ourselves.  The "
"teamster in the back bay might have some pointers, though, if you really want "
"to know."
msgstr ""
"À part les gens qui ont le disque dur, je n'en connais aucun.  Les pilleurs "
"partagent des choses bizarres, mais nous ne pouvons pas vraiment aller "
"vérifier par nous-mêmes.  Le routier à l'arrière pourrait avoir un idée "
"cependant si vous voulez vraiment savoir."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Things were rough at first, and our policy of taking everyone we could caused "
"a lot of strife later on.  Right now, we just want to get enough trade going "
"keep ourselves afloat.  We might have to turn people away, but we've found "
"that they're usually willing to trade with us, which is our only real source "
"of food right now.  We're trying to turn that into a business model.  Doesn't "
"matter who you are, we'll trade with you as long as you don't bring trouble."
msgstr ""
"Les choses ont été difficiles au début, et notre politique consistant à "
"prendre tous ceux que nous pouvions a causé beaucoup de conflits par la "
"suite. Pour l'instant, nous voulons simplement obtenir suffisamment "
"d'échanges pour nous maintenir à flot. Il se peut que nous devions refuser "
"des gens, mais nous avons constaté qu'ils sont généralement prêts à commercer "
"avec nous, ce qui est notre seule véritable source de nourriture pour "
"l'instant. Nous essayons d'en faire un modèle économique. Peu importe qui "
"vous êtes, nous ferons du commerce avec vous tant que vous n'apportez pas "
"d'ennuis."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about when the goods dry up?  Won't that happen eventually?"
msgstr ""
"Qu'en est-il lorsque les marchandises se tarissent ? Cela ne finira-t-il pas "
"par arriver ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Here's hoping it works out."
msgstr "Espérons que tout se passera bien."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right now, it's the best way we have to make sure that everyone gets what "
"they need.  Long-term viability of business models is what people in suits "
"used to do back before all this, and we see where that got them.  Barter is "
"the only thing keeping us from starving, so we're going to keep doing it as "
"long as it works or until we can start producing our own food."
msgstr ""
"Pour l'instant ceci est la meilleure façon que nous avons de faire en sorte "
"que tout le monde ait ce que dont ils ont besoin. La viabilité au long terme "
"des modèles commerciaux est ce que les personnes en costard faisant avant "
"tout ceci, et voyez où cela les a mené. Le troc et l'échange est la seule "
"chose qui nous empêche de mourir de faim, donc nous allons continuer à faire "
"ceci jusqu'à ce que cela arrête de fonctionner ou que nous soyons capable de "
"produire notre propre nourriture."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't think we have a figurehead right now, I think?  If we do, I don't "
"know about it.  For the most part, we all have our own responsibilities and "
"that works to keep us all fed as a group.  I'm the front man for outsiders, "
"the broker keeps tabs on our food, so on and so forth.  We've had some town "
"hall style talks in the cafeteria about setting up a democracy, but there's "
"nothing solid on that right now."
msgstr ""
"Je ne pense pas que nous ayons une figure de proue pour l'instant. Si c'est "
"le cas, je ne le sais pas. Pour l'essentiel, nous avons tous nos propres "
"responsabilités et cela nous permet de rester nourris en tant que groupe. Je "
"suis l'homme de paille pour les étrangers, le courtier surveille notre "
"nourriture, etc. Nous avons eu quelques discussions à la cafétéria sur la "
"mise en place d'une démocratie, mais il n'y a rien de concret pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a unique trader and potential mission
#. provider.
msgid "Makayla Sanchez"
msgstr "Makayla Sanchez"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a unique trader and potential mission
#. provider.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Arsonist"
msgstr "Pyromane"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Job description of "Arsonist" NPC class
msgid "I'm just watching the world burn."
msgstr "Je regarde le monde brûler."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That sure is a shiny badge you got there!"
msgstr "C'est un beau badge que vous avez là!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Heh, you look important."
msgstr "Vous avez l'air d'être quelqu'un d'important."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm actually new."
msgstr "Je suis nouveau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any jobs for me?"
msgstr "Vous avez un job à me donner?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with your ears?"
msgstr "Quel est le problème avec vos oreilles?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are you doing these days?"
msgstr "Comment allez-vous ces jours-ci ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Guess that makes two of us.  Well, kind of.  I don't think we're open, "
"though.  Full up as hell; it's almost a crowd downstairs.  Did you see the "
"trader at the entrance?  There's the one to ask."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que nous sommes deux. Enfin, en quelque sorte. Je ne pense pas que "
"nous soyons ouverts. C'est plein comme l'enfer ; il y a presque une foule en "
"bas. Vous avez vu le commerçant à l'entrée ? C'est à lui qu'il faut demander."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sucks…"
msgstr "Ça craint…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, there's a guy downstairs who got a working pneumatic cannon.  It shoots "
"metal like… like a cannon without the bang.  Cost-efficient as hell.  And "
"there's no shortage of improvised weapons you can make.  The big thing "
"though, seems to be continuing construction of fortifications.  Very few of "
"those monsters seem to be able to break through a fence or wall constructed "
"with the stuff."
msgstr ""
"Il y a un gars en bas qui a un canon pneumatique en état de marche. Il tire "
"du métal comme... comme un canon sans la détonation. C'est très économique. "
"Et les armes improvisées ne manquent pas. Le plus important, cependant, "
"semble être de continuer à construire des fortifications. Très peu de ces "
"monstres semblent capables de franchir une clôture ou un mur construit avec "
"ce matériau."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing optimistic, at least.  Had a pal on the road with a ham radio, but "
"she's gone and so is that thing.  Kaput."
msgstr ""
"Rien d'optimiste, en tout cas. J'avais une amie sur la route qui possédait "
"une radio amateur, mais elle est partie et son appareil aussi. Kaput."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing optimistic?"
msgstr "Rien d'optimiste?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Most of the emergency camps have dissolved by now.  The cities are mobbed, "
"the forests crawling with glowing eyes and zombies.  Some insane shit out "
"there, and everyone with a radio seems to feel like documenting their last "
"awful moments."
msgstr ""
"La plupart des camps de réfugiés se sont désagrégés, les villes sont "
"envahies, les forêts pullulent zombies et de choses aux yeux brilliants. "
"Beaucoup de choses cinglées dehors, et on dirait que tout les gens possédant "
"une radio ont envie de documenter leurs horribles derniers moments."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I feel bad for asking."
msgstr "Je me sens mal de demander."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know.  I mean, if you can make yourself useful.  But that's become a "
"real hazy thing nowadays.  It depends who you ask.  The merchant definitely "
"doesn't want me here when I'm not selling, but… some people get away with it."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas. Je veux dire, si vous pouvez vous rendre utile. Mais c'est "
"devenu très flou de nos jours. Cela dépend à qui vous demandez. Le marchand "
"ne veut surtout pas que je sois là quand je ne vends pas, mais... certains "
"s'en sortent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Same way you got yours, I bet.  Keep quiet about it, some people here look "
"down on people like us."
msgstr ""
"De la même façon que vous avez eu le vôtre, je parie. Ne le dites pas, "
"certaines personnes ici détestent les gens comme nous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ssh.  Some people in here hate… mutations.  This was an accident."
msgstr "Ssh.  Certaines personnes ici détestent… les mutations.  C'était un accident."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry to ask."
msgstr "Désolé(e) d'avoir demandé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I burn down buildings and sell the Free Merchants the materials.  No, "
"seriously.  If you've seen burned wreckage in place of suburbs or even see "
"the pile of rebar for sale, that's probably me.  They've kept me well off in "
"exchange, I guess."
msgstr ""
"Je brûle les bâtiments et je vends les matériaux aux marchands libres. Non, "
"sérieusement. Si vous avez vu des épaves brûlées à la place des banlieues ou "
"même un tas de barres d'armature à vendre, c'est probablement moi. Ils m'ont "
"bien aidé en échange, je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll buy."
msgstr "J'achète."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who needs rebar?"
msgstr "Qui a besoin de barres d'armatures?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Supply the arsonist"
msgstr "Approvisionnez la pyromane"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "Bring the arsonist 120 units of commercial fertilizer."
msgstr "Apportez à la pyromane 120 unités d'engrais commercial."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "I could use some help getting some materials."
msgstr "J'aurais besoin d'aide pour obtenir du matériel."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid ""
"I could use some help getting some materials.  Molotovs are nice for burning "
"down buildings but aren't all that for keeping yourself safe.  If you could "
"get me 120 units of commercial fertilizer I could make something a lot more "
"potent."
msgstr ""
"J'aurais besoin d'aide pour trouver de l'équipement. Les cocktails Molotov "
"sont bon pour brûler des bâtiments mais ne sont pas idéals niveau sécurité. "
"Si vous pouviez me trouver 120 unités d'engrais commercial je pourrais "
"fabriquer quelque chose de beaucoup plus puissant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "Oh, merci beaucoup, mon ami.  Vous ne le regretterez pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "Think it over."
msgstr "Réfléchissez-y."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid ""
"Commercial fertilizer tends to be made from ammonium nitrate, which is also "
"usable as an explosive.  Try looking for some around the abandoned farms."
msgstr ""
"Les engrais commerciaux sont généralement fabriqués à partir de nitrate "
"d'ammonium, qui peut également être utilisé comme explosif. Essayez d'en "
"trouver dans les fermes abandonnées."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "Did you find any fertilizer?  Are you sure this is the ammonium nitrate kind?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez trouvé de l'engrais? Vous êtes sûr(e) que ceci est le genre au "
"nitrate d'ammonium?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid ""
"This is great!  I'll get to work making something of this.  You can have some "
"of my Molotovs, I won't need quite so many now."
msgstr ""
"C'est super! Je vais me mettre au boulot et commencer a utiliser ce que vous "
"venez de me donner. Vous pouvez prendre quelque uns de mes cocktails Molotov, "
"je n'en aurais plus autant besoin maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "I guess I could convince the shelter to sell me some."
msgstr "Je pense que je pourrais convaincre le refuge de m'en vendre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
msgid "Damn.  Perhaps I wasn't the only one who thought of this."
msgstr "Bon sang de bonsoir. Je ne suis peut-être pas le seul à y avoir pensé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I made some nice things with that ammonium nitrate you got me.  Want to trade?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai fait de belles choses avec le nitrate d'ammonium que tu m'as offert. Tu "
"veux faire un échange ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You… smelled me?"
msgstr "Tu m'as senti ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got anything for sale?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose à vendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got any survival advice?"
msgstr "Vous avez des conseils de survie ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "O…kay…?"
msgstr "O…k…?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I trade food here in exchange for a place to crash and general supplies.  "
"Well, more specifically I trade food that isn't stale chips and flat cola."
msgstr ""
"J'y échange de la nourriture contre un endroit où dormir et des fournitures "
"générales. Plus précisément, j'échange de la nourriture qui n'est pas "
"constituée de chips rassis et de cola plat."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, so you hunt?"
msgstr "Oh, vous chassez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not really, just trying to lead my life."
msgstr "Pas vraiment, j'essaie juste de mener ma vie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yep.  Whatever game I spot, I bag and sell the meat and other parts here.  "
"Got the occasional fish and basket full of wild fruit, but nothing comes "
"close to a freshly-cooked moose steak for supper!"
msgstr ""
"Oui. Quel que soit le gibier que je repère, j'emballe et je vends la viande "
"et les autres parties ici. J'ai parfois du poisson et un panier rempli de "
"fruits sauvages, mais rien ne vaut un steak d'élan fraîchement cuit pour le "
"dîner !"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great, now my mouth is watering…"
msgstr "Super, maintenant j'ai l'eau à la bouche…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, just bagged a fresh batch of meat.  You may want to grill it up before "
"it gets too, uh… 'tender'."
msgstr ""
"Bien sûr, je viens d'emballer un nouveau lot de viande.  Vous allez peut-être "
"vouloir la faire griller avant qu'elle ne devienne trop, euh… \"tendre\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Feed a man a fish, he's full for a day.  Feed a man a bullet, he's full for "
"the rest of his life."
msgstr ""
"Nourrissez un homme avec un poisson, il sera rassasié pour un jour. "
"Nourrissez un homme d'une balle, il sera rassasié pour le reste de sa vie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Spot your prey before something nastier spots you."
msgstr "Repérez votre proie avant que quelque chose de plus menaçant vous repère."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Jabberwock is real, don't listen to what anybody else says.  If you see "
"it, RUN."
msgstr ""
"Le Jabberwock est réel, n'écoutez pas ce que disent les autres. Si vous le "
"voyez, fuyez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Zombified animals aren't good for eating, but sometimes you might find usable "
"fur on 'em."
msgstr ""
"La viande d'un animal zombifié n'est définitivement pas comestible, mais vous "
"pourriez probablement extraire un peu de fourrure pas trop décomposée d'un de "
"leurs cadavres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A steady diet of cooked meat and clean water will keep you alive forever, but "
"your taste buds and your colon may start to get angry at you.  Eat a piece of "
"fruit every once in a while."
msgstr ""
"Un régime consistant uniquement de viande cuite et d'eau propre peut vous "
"garder en bonne forme longtemps, mais votre colon et vos papilles vont "
"commencer à se plaindre au bout d'un moment, donc n'hésitez pas à manger des "
"fruits et des légumes de temps en temps."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Smoke crack to get more shit done."
msgstr "Fume du crack pour dépoter plus."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Watch your back out there."
msgstr "Faites attention à vos arrières."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "Representative"
msgstr "Représentant"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way I can join the 'Old Guard'?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il un moyen de rejoindre la \"vieille garde\" ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got some questions for you about those weird robots."
msgstr "J'ai quelques questions à vous poser sur ces étranges robots."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I can already tell you what you want to know about those 'robots'."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que je peux déjà vous dire ce que vous voulez savoir sur ces "
"\"robots\"."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does the Old Guard need anything?"
msgstr "La Vieille Garde a besoin de quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I wanted to ask you something about that offer."
msgstr "Je voulais vous demander quelque chose à propos de cet offre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the region's federal liaison.  Most people here call us the 'Old Guard' "
"and I rather like the sound of it.  Despite how things currently appear, the "
"federal government was not entirely destroyed.  After the outbreak I was "
"chosen to coordinate civilian and militia efforts in support of military "
"operations."
msgstr ""
"Je suis l'agent de liaison fédéral de la région. La plupart des gens ici nous "
"appellent la \"vieille garde\" et j'aime bien cette appellation. Malgré les "
"apparences, le gouvernement fédéral n'a pas été entièrement détruit. Après "
"l'épidémie, j'ai été choisi pour coordonner les efforts des civils et des "
"milices en soutien aux opérations militaires."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So what are you actually doing here?"
msgstr "Du coup, que faites-vous ici en réalité ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I ensure that the citizens here have what they need to survive and protect "
"themselves from raiders.  Keeping some form of law is going to be the most "
"important element in rebuilding the world.  We do what we can to keep the "
"'Free Merchants' here prospering and in return they have provided us with "
"spare men and supplies when they can."
msgstr ""
"Je veille à ce que les citoyens d'ici aient ce qu'il faut pour survivre et se "
"protéger des pillards. Le maintien d'une certaine forme de droit sera "
"l'élément le plus important de la reconstruction du monde. Nous faisons ce "
"que nous pouvons pour que les \"marchands libres\" prospèrent et, en retour, "
"ils nous fournissent des hommes et du matériel lorsqu'ils le peuvent."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there a catch?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il un piège ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything more to it?"
msgstr "Y a-t-il quelque chose de plus ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hmmm…"
msgstr "Hmmm…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There isn't much pushed out by public relations that I'd actually believe.  "
"From what I gather, communication between the regional force commands is "
"almost non-existent.  What I do know is that the 'Old Guard' is currently "
"based out of the 2nd Fleet and patrols the Atlantic coast trying to provide "
"support to the remaining footholds."
msgstr ""
"Il n'y a pas grand-chose que je croirais dans les relations publiques. "
"D'après ce que j'ai compris, la communication entre les commandements des "
"forces régionales est pratiquement inexistante. Ce que je sais, c'est que la "
"\"vieille garde\" est actuellement basée au sein de la 2e flotte et qu'elle "
"patrouille le long de la côte atlantique pour tenter d'apporter un soutien "
"aux derniers points d'appui."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The 2nd Fleet?"
msgstr "La 2ième Flotte?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about the footholds."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't know much about how it formed but it is the armada of military and "
"commercial ships that's floating off the coast.  They have everything from "
"supertankers and carriers to fishing trawlers… even a few NATO ships.  Most "
"civilians are offered a cabin on one of the liners to retire to if they serve "
"as a federal employee for a few years."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais pas trop comment elle s'est formée, mais c'est l'armada de navires "
"militaires et commerciaux qui flotte au large de la côte. Il y a de tout, des "
"superpétroliers aux transporteurs en passant par les chalutiers de pêche... "
"et même quelques navires de l'OTAN. La plupart des civils se voient offrir "
"une cabine sur l'un des paquebots pour prendre leur retraite s'ils sont "
"fonctionnaires fédéraux pendant quelques années."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They may just be propaganda but apparently one or two cities were successful "
"in 'walling themselves off.'  Around here I was told that there were a few "
"places like this one but I couldn't tell you where."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est peut-être que de la propagande, mais il semble qu'une ou deux villes "
"aient réussi à \"s'emmurer\". Dans le coin, on m'a dit qu'il y avait quelques "
"endroits comme celui-ci, mais je ne pourrais pas vous dire où."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You can't actually join unless you go through a recruiter.  We can usually "
"use help though, ask me from time to time if there is any work available.  "
"Completing missions as a contractor is a great way to make a name for "
"yourself among the most powerful men left in the world."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne pouvez pas vous inscrire à moins de passer par un recruteur. Mais "
"nous avons souvent besoin d'aide, demandez-moi de temps en temps s'il y a du "
"travail disponible. Remplir des missions en tant qu'entrepreneur est un "
"excellent moyen de se faire un nom parmi les hommes les plus puissants du "
"monde."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Actually, I've met them.  They seem open to trade and things.  Thought you "
"might want to know."
msgstr ""
"Je les ai déjà rencontrés. Ils ont l'air ouverts aux échanges et à la "
"diplomatie. Je pensais juste que vous apprécierez de savoir ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, that's interesting.  It's not something I'm in a position to do "
"something about, but you might want to take that information to one of the "
"teamsters for the Free Merchants.  Maybe that's a way we could establish some "
"friendlier relationships."
msgstr ""
"C'est intéressant. Je ne suis pas en mesure de faire quelque chose, mais vous "
"pourriez transmettre cette information à l'un des membres de l'équipe des "
"marchands libres. C'est peut-être un moyen d'établir des relations plus "
"amicales."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good idea.  I'll go do that."
msgstr "Bonne idée. Je vais aller faire ça."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Huh, maybe.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Uh, peut être.  <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, well.  In that case, I would be interested in hearing what you know about "
"them.  I can relay it to command.  Let's see what I have to trade… how about "
"some antibiotics from our stores?  You can never have too many of them out "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Oh, bien sûr. Dans ce cas, j'aimerais savoir ce que vous savez sur eux. Je "
"peux le transmettre au commandement. Voyons ce que j'ai à échanger... Que "
"diriez-vous de quelques antibiotiques de nos magasins ? Il n'y en a jamais "
"trop."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've met them.  They seem open to trade and things.  Not hostile, at "
"least not to me."
msgstr ""
"Oui, je les ai rencontrés. Ils semblent ouverts au commerce et à d'autres "
"choses. Ils ne sont pas hostiles, du moins pas à mon égard."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to think about it.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but I can't leave my post here, and I just don't have the human "
"resources even for a project like that."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolé, mais je ne peux pas laisser mon poste ici, et je n'ai même "
"pas les ressources humaines pour un tel projet."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, thanks anyway…"
msgstr "Merci quand même..."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's your lucky day: I just made contact with a couple volunteers like "
"yourself, and that's exactly the sort of project I can put them to."
msgstr ""
"C'est votre jour de chance : Je viens d'entrer en contact avec un couple de "
"bénévoles comme vous, et c'est exactement le genre de projet que je peux leur "
"confier."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, that's great news!"
msgstr "Merci, ce sont de bonnes nouvelles!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Kill Bandits"
msgstr "Tuez les Bandits"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid ""
"A pair of bandits have been preying on locals, based out of a nearby cabin.  "
"Ensure they meet a bitter end along with any associates, but watch out for "
"traps around their hideout."
msgstr ""
"Une paire de bandits s'en prend aux habitants de la région depuis une cabane "
"voisine. Veillez à ce qu'ils connaissent une fin amère, ainsi que leurs "
"complices, mais surveillez les pièges autour de leur repaire."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid ""
"I don't like sending untested men into the field but if you have stayed alive "
"so far you might have some skills.  There are at least a pair of bandits "
"squatting in a local cabin, anyone who preys upon civilians meets a quick "
"end… execute both of them for their crimes.  Complete this and the Old Guard "
"will consider you an asset in the region."
msgstr ""
"Je n'aime pas envoyer des hommes non testés sur le terrain, mais si vous êtes "
"restés en vie jusqu'à présent, vous avez peut-être quelques compétences. Il y "
"a au moins deux bandits qui squattent une cabane locale, tous ceux qui "
"s'attaquent aux civils connaissent une fin rapide... exécutez-les tous les "
"deux pour leurs crimes. Terminez cela et la Vieille Garde vous considérera "
"comme un atout dans la région."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid "Contractor, I welcome you aboard."
msgstr "Entrepreneur, je vous souhaite la bienvenue à bord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid "The States will remain a wasteland unless good men choose to save it."
msgstr ""
"Les États-Unis resteront une terre en friche, à moins que des hommes de bonne "
"volonté ne choisissent de les sauver."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid "They might suspect you are coming, keep an eye out for traps."
msgstr ""
"Ils peuvent se douter que vous arrivez, gardez l'œil ouvert pour repérer les "
"pièges."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
msgid ""
"The Old Guard thanks you for eliminating the criminals.  You won't be "
"forgotten."
msgstr ""
"La vieille garde vous remercie d'avoir éliminé les criminels. Vous ne serez "
"pas oubliés."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Deal with Informant"
msgstr "Neutralisez la Taupe"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid ""
"The Hell's Raiders bandit group may have an informant working inside the "
"Refugee Center.  Investigate and bring them to justice without arousing any "
"suspicions."
msgstr ""
"Le groupe des Pillards de l'Enfer a peut-être un⸱e informateur⸱rice au sein "
"du Centre de Réfugiés.  Menez l'enquête et livrez-le⸱a à la justice sans "
"éveiller de soupçons."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid ""
"This task is going to require a little more persuasive skill.  I believe the "
"Hell's Raiders have an informant here to monitor who comes and goes.  I need "
"you to find out who it is and deal with them without letting anyone else know "
"of my suspicions.  We normally allow the Free Merchants to govern themselves "
"so I would hate to offend them."
msgstr ""
"Cette tâche va demander un peu plus de talent de persuasion.  Je crois que "
"les Pillards de l'Enfer ont un⸱e informateur⸱rice ici qui surveille les "
"allées et venues.  J'ai besoin que vous trouviez de qui il s'agit et que vous "
"vous en occupiez sans que personne d'autre ne soit au courant de mes "
"soupçons.  Nous laissons normalement les Marchands Libres se gouverner "
"eux-mêmes, je ne voudrais pas les offenser."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid "Thank you, please keep this discreet."
msgstr "Merci de rester discret."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid "Come back when you get a chance, we could use a few good men."
msgstr ""
"Revenez quand vous en aurez l'occasion, nous aurions besoin de quelques bons "
"éléments."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid "If they draw first blood their friends are less likely to blame you…"
msgstr ""
"S'ils sont les premiers à faire couler le sang, leurs amis seront moins "
"enclins à vous blâmer…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid "You deal with the rat?"
msgstr "Vous avez neutralisé la taupe?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Deal with Informant"
msgid "Thank you, I'll do the explaining if anyone else asks about it."
msgstr "Merci, j'expliquerai si quelqu'un d'autre me pose la question."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Source of Robots"
msgstr "Trouvez la Source des Robots Étranges"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid ""
"Go to the supposed source of the weird robots marked on your map and report "
"back to the Old Guard representative what you've seen."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid "Got a weird one for you this time…"
msgstr "J'en ai une bizarre pour vous cette fois-ci…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid ""
"I don't usually hear much from command, but we got a message by radio "
"recently.  You might be the right choice to look into it for me.  There've "
"been reports of weird robots and things wandering around since things went "
"south.  Dunno how, but apparently command tracked down what they think is the "
"source.  They want someone to go check out who is making these, and if we can "
"get any tech or assistance from them.  This is strictly recon, you "
"understand: could be a hostile entity, so do not engage directly.  Report "
"back to me when you've found out something."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid "Thanks, once you know who it is, report back to me and I'll pass that on."
msgstr ""
"Merci, dès que vous saurez de qui il s'agit, signalez-le moi et je le "
"transmettrai."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid ""
"Come back when you get a chance, if there's any chance these things are on "
"our side, we need all the help we can get."
msgstr ""
"Revenez dès que vous en avez l'occasion, s'il y a une chance que ces choses "
"soient de notre côté, nous avons besoin de toute l'aide possible."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid ""
"If you see any weird machines around, do not engage.  Sneak away, I'd say.  "
"They seem to be hostile to zombies, but that doesn't mean they can tell you "
"aren't one."
msgstr ""
"Si vous voyez des machines bizarres dans les parages, ne vous engagez pas. "
"Fuyez en douce, je dirais. Elles semblent hostiles aux zombies, mais cela ne "
"veut pas dire qu'elles peuvent savoir que vous n'en êtes pas un."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Red.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Area"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Lost in the Woods"
msgid "Great work, wasn't sure what I was sending you after."
msgstr "Bon travail, je n'étais pas sûr de ce que je vous envoyais."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid ""
"That's a shame, a damn shame.  Wish you could have learned more.  Thanks for "
"trying."
msgstr ""
"C'est dommage, vraiment dommage. J'aurais aimé que vous puissiez en apprendre "
"davantage. Merci d'avoir essayé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Source of Robots"
msgid "Damn… let's hope we can try again sometime."
msgstr "Espérons que nous pourrons réessayer un jour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Secure Trade Route"
msgstr "Sécurisez la Route Commerciale"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Secure Trade Route"
msgid ""
"One of the Free Merchants silently disappeared while escorting a trade "
"caravan.  Whoever or whatever is responsible must be quick and quiet - "
"investigate the trade route and eliminate the threat."
msgstr ""
"L'un des marchands libres a disparu silencieusement alors qu'il escortait une "
"caravane commerciale. Le responsable, quel qu'il soit, doit être rapide et "
"discret : il doit enquêter sur la route commerciale et éliminer la menace."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
msgid ""
"There is another monster troubling the merchants but this time it isn't "
"human… at least I don't think.  Guy just disappeared while walking behind a "
"packed caravan.  They didn't hear any shots but I suppose some raider may "
"have been real sneaky.  Check out the area and report anything you find."
msgstr ""
"Un autre monstre vient troubler les marchands, mais cette fois il n'est pas "
"humain... du moins je ne le crois pas. Le type a disparu alors qu'il marchait "
"derrière une caravane bondée. Ils n'ont pas entendu de coups de feu, mais je "
"suppose qu'un pilleur a pu être très sournois. Vérifiez la zone et signalez "
"tout ce que vous trouvez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Red.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Area"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Lost in the Woods"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Protect the cattle"
msgid "Thanks, keeping the people safe is what we try and do."
msgstr "Merci, nous essayons d'assurer la sécurité de la population."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Red.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Area"
msgid ""
"Search the bushes for any trace?  I'm not an expert tracker but you should be "
"able to find something."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez cherché des traces dans les buissons ? Je ne suis pas un expert en "
"pistage, mais vous devriez pouvoir trouver quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgstr "Assassinez le Chef des Pillards de l'Enfer"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid ""
"The Old Guard have located a Hell's Raiders encampment that is coordinating "
"attacks on the Free Merchants.  Pay them a visit and execute the area "
"leadership."
msgstr ""
"La Veille Garde a localisé le camp des Pillards de l'Enfer coordonnant les "
"attaques contre les Marchands Libres.  Payez leur une visite et exécutez "
"leurs chefs de file."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid ""
"I've located a Hell's Raiders encampment in the region that appears to be "
"coordinating operations against the Free Merchants.  We know almost nothing "
"about the command structure in the 'gang' so I need to send someone in to "
"decapitate the leadership.  The raid will be held under orders of the U.S. "
"Marshals Service and by agreeing to the mission you will become a marshal, "
"swearing to assist the federal government in regaining order."
msgstr ""
"J'ai localisé un camp des Hell Raiders qui à l'air de coordonner les "
"opérations du gang contre les Marchands Libres. Nous ne savons presque rien "
"sur leur structure de commande donc j'ai besoin de quelqu'un à envoyer pour "
"décapitez leurs chefs de file. L'opération sera menée sous l'autorité du U.S. "
"Marshals Service, en acceptant cette mission, vous acceptez de devenir un "
"marshal, et jurez d'assister le gouvernement fédéral à rétablir la paix et "
"l'ordre."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid ""
"Now repeat after me… I do solemnly swear that I will support and defend the "
"Constitution of the United States against all enemies, foreign and domestic… "
"that I will bear true faith and allegiance to the same… that I take this "
"obligation freely, without any mental reservation or purpose of evasion… and "
"that I will well and faithfully discharge the duties of the office on which I "
"am about to enter.  To establish justice, insure domestic tranquility, "
"provide for the common defense, promote the general welfare and secure the "
"blessings of liberty.  So help me God.  Congratulations Marshal, don't forget "
"your badge and gun.  As a marshal all men or women assisting you are "
"considered deputy marshals so keep them in line."
msgstr ""
"Répétez après moi… Je jure solennellement que je soutiendrai et défendrai la "
"Constitution des Etats-Unis contre tous les ennemis, étrangers et domestiques "
"; que je lui porterai une foi et une allégeance véritables ; que je prends "
"cette obligation librement, sans aucune réserve mentale ou intention "
"d'évasion ; et que je remplirai bien et fidèlement les devoirs de la fonction "
"que je suis sur le point d'exercer. D'établir la justice, d'assurer la "
"tranquillité intérieure, de pourvoir à une défense commune, de développer le "
"bien-être général et d'assurer les bienfaits de la liberté: Que Dieu me "
"vienne en aide. Félicitations Marshal, n'oubliez pas votre badge et votre "
"arme. En tant que marshal, tout compagnon que vous ayez seront considérés vos "
"députés, donc faites-les se tenir à carreaux."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid ""
"I'd recommend having two deputies… it would be a death trap if a single man "
"got surrounded."
msgstr ""
"Je recommanderais d'avoir deux adjoints… ce serait un piège mortel si un "
"homme seul se retrouvait encerclé."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid "Has the leadership been dealt with?"
msgstr "Vous vous avez éliminés les chefs de file?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Assassinate Raider Leader"
msgid ""
"Marshal, you continue to impress us.  We may have some hope of long term "
"survival yet thanks to you."
msgstr ""
"Marshal, vous continuez de nous impressionner. Nous gardons un bon espoir "
"pour notre survie à long terme grace à vous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Install radio repeater mod"
msgstr "Installer le module répéteur radio"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"The Old Guard wishes to expand their range of communications to get in touch "
"with other survivors in the Wasteland.  Find a Radio Station and install a "
"repeater mod via its terminal."
msgstr ""
"La Vieille Garde souhaite étendre ses moyens de communication pour entrer en "
"contact avec d'autres survivants dans le Wasteland. Trouvez une station radio "
"et installez un module répéteur via son terminal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "I don't need anything major for now, Marshal.  Well, except…"
msgstr "Je n'ai besoin de rien de majeur pour l'instant, Marshal.  Enfin, sauf…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"For now, the perimeter of the Refugee Center is free of threats.  That means "
"we can afford to divert our attention to others in need of help.  However, "
"our communication with the wasteland is lacking at best and nonexistent at "
"worst.  We need to broaden our reach to intercept and send radio broadcasts.  "
"Unfortunately Radio Towers are out of the question to widen our broadcasts, "
"as the emergency grid for them is out of action.  However, Radio Stations in "
"towns or urban areas should still have some juice left.  I want you to "
"install something called a \"radio repeater mod\" in these stations that can "
"broaden their reach and allow them to pick weaker signals.  Sadly, I have "
"neither these devices nor a manual for them at my disposal.  You'll need to "
"find instructions and assemble them yourself.  Are you up for this task?"
msgstr ""
"Pour l'instant, le périmètre du Centre pour les réfugiés est libre de toute "
"menace. Cela signifie que nous pouvons nous permettre de détourner notre "
"attention vers d'autres personnes qui ont besoin d'aide. Cependant, nos "
"communications avec le terrain vague sont au mieux insuffisantes, au pire "
"inexistantes. Nous devons élargir notre champ d'action afin d'intercepter et "
"d'envoyer des émissions radio. Malheureusement, les tours radio sont hors de "
"question pour élargir nos émissions, car le réseau d'urgence pour ces tours "
"est hors service. Cependant, les stations de radio situées dans les villes ou "
"les zones urbaines devraient avoir encore un peu de jus. Je veux que vous "
"installiez dans ces stations ce que l'on appelle un \"modulateur de répéteur "
"radio\" qui peut élargir leur portée et leur permettre de capter des signaux "
"plus faibles. Malheureusement, je ne dispose ni de ces appareils ni de leur "
"mode d'emploi. Vous devrez donc trouver des instructions et les assembler "
"vous-même. Êtes-vous prêt pour cette tâche ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"As I said, I have no repeaters or manuals at my disposal.  But you might want "
"to try you chances in Libraries or maybe other survivors.  Godspeed, Marshal."
msgstr ""
"Comme je l'ai dit, je n'ai pas de répétiteurs ou de manuels à ma disposition. "
"Mais vous pourriez tenter votre chance dans les bibliothèques ou peut-être "
"auprès d'autres survivants. Bonne chance, Marshal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"Come back when you get a chance Marshal.  We really need get in touch with "
"rest of the region."
msgstr ""
"Revenez dès que vous en avez l'occasion, Marshal. Nous avons vraiment besoin "
"d'entrer en contact avec le reste de la région."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"As I recommended, libraries would be a good start.  Or any place that sells "
"books and manuals, really."
msgstr ""
"Comme je l'ai recommandé, les bibliothèques seraient un bon début. Ou tout "
"autre endroit qui vend des livres et des manuels, en fait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "Have you set up a repeater yet, Marshal?"
msgstr "Avez-vous déjà installé un répéteur, Marshal ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"Thank you for the good work, Marshal.  It's not much but please accept these "
"supplies to compensate.  Come back to me if you are willing to install more."
msgstr ""
"Merci pour votre travail, Marshal. Ce n'est pas grand-chose, mais je vous "
"prie d'accepter ces fournitures en guise de compensation. Revenez me voir si "
"vous voulez en installer d'autres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"Huh; that's weird, the boys at comms say that they didn't really see an "
"improvement.  Well, if you want to try again, come to me.  Maybe this time "
"it'll work."
msgstr ""
"C'est bizarre, les gars des communications disent qu'ils n'ont pas vraiment "
"vu d'amélioration. Eh bien, si vous voulez réessayer, venez me voir. "
"Peut-être que cette fois ça marchera."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "That's a damn shame…  You can come back anytime if you want to try again."
msgstr ""
"C'est vraiment dommage…  Vous pouvez revenir à tout moment si vous voulez "
"réessayer."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "We need more help…"
msgstr "Nous avons besoin de plus d'aide…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"We need more repeaters to expand our range and ability of our communications. "
" You know the drill Marshal, find or assemble a radio repeater mod and set it "
"up in a Radio Station.  Radio Towers are still off the table."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons besoin de plus de répéteurs pour étendre la portée et la capacité "
"de nos communications. Vous connaissez la marche à suivre, Marshal, trouvez "
"ou assemblez un module répéteur radio et installez-le dans une station radio. "
"Les tours radio ne sont toujours pas à l'ordre du jour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "Stay safe, Marshal."
msgstr "Restez en sécurité, Marshal."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"You can find the Radio Stations in towns or urban centers.  I still have no "
"repeater mod available Marshal.  However you can craft one yourself, if you "
"find the manual.  Try libraries or bookstores if you still don't have one."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez trouver les stations de radio dans les villes ou les centres "
"urbains. Je n'ai toujours pas de module répéteur disponible Marshal. "
"Cependant, vous pouvez en fabriquer un vous-même, si vous trouvez le manuel. "
"Essayez les bibliothèques ou les librairies si vous n'en avez toujours pas."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"Good work, Marshal.  Here's some supplies for your next venture.  Come back "
"to me if you are willing to install more."
msgstr ""
"Bon travail, Marshal. Voici quelques fournitures pour votre prochaine "
"aventure. Revenez me voir si vous voulez en installer d'autres."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid ""
"Huh, that's weird, the boys at comms say that they didn't really see an "
"improvement.  Well, if you want to try again, come to me.  Maybe this time "
"it'll work."
msgstr ""
"C'est bizarre, les gars des communications disent qu'ils n'ont pas vraiment "
"vu d'amélioration. Si tu veux réessayer, viens me voir. Peut-être que cette "
"fois, ça marchera."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Install radio repeater mod"
msgid "Oh well, you can try again anytime."
msgstr "Vous pouvez réessayer à tout moment."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Wait.  Before you go, I got an offer for you if you're interested."
msgstr ""
"Attendez.  Avant que vous partiez, j'ai une offre à vous proposer si vous "
"êtes intéressé⋅e."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything else I should know?"
msgstr "Je devrais savoir quelque chose d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about the cargo."
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui était à bord?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A helicopter crashed in the region not long ago, at first I thought it was "
"just a rumor, caravan guards talking about some crash nearby, but then I got "
"a visit from a couple of Old Guard people looking for a lost helicopter, one "
"of them got quite drunk one night and shared some interesting details, turns "
"out it was an Old Guard heli coming back from way out west with quite the "
"cargo, and I know where you can find it.  That's all you're getting for free "
"though, I'd like to see some return on investment on that bottle you "
"understand."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm not buying anything without some proof."
msgstr "Je ne vais rien acheter sans une preuve."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why sell the info instead of retrieving the cargo yourself?  What happened to "
"the old guard investigation?  How can you be sure that it wasn't looted "
"already?  This sounds sketchy as hell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[50 merch] Fine."
msgstr "[50 merch] D'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Failure explanation for NPC dialogue response
msgid "You don't have enough."
msgstr "Vous n'avez pas assez."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He crosses his arms.  \"Fine.  Go talk to the guards, that crash was all the "
"talk among them for a while.  Look, I'm not trying to do you over, I wouldn't "
"risk my reputation and my job for a handful of cash, feel free to tell "
"everyone in the center that I'm a liar sending people to their death for a "
"quick buck if you find out that I lied.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&He sighs.  \"Well, let's just say that the location of the helicopter "
"doesn't make the retrieval of the cargo…trivial.  Apparently the higher-ups "
"at the Old Guard agreed that it was too hard and too far to be worth.  It "
"wasn't transporting Jesus, just valuable cargo.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes actually.  The scout told me that he saw something weird down at the "
"lake.  Translucent shapes swimming close to the surface from time to time.  "
"I'm sure it has something to do with the weird storm that brought the "
"helicopter down."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Alright, give me your map I'll show you the location."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I had other questions."
msgstr "J'avais d'autres questions."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The cargo?  That's the kind of optional information worth a small supplement."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"This wasn't the deal and you're starting to wear my nerves thin asshole, tell "
"me or I'll make you pick your teeth off the floor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come on, you already got what you wanted, are you really trying to fleece me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[25 merch] This better be worth."
msgstr "[25 merch] Ça à intérêt à valoir la peine."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"& He tenses and grits his teeth for a moment before regaining his composure.  "
"\"No, we both know you won't.  Let's pretend this never happened, offer's "
"still up.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine…"
msgstr "D'accord…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What are you talking about, I'm not \"fleecing\" anyone, you're free to make "
"the retrieval with the information you have, all I'm offering is purely "
"optional information for a reasonable price."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fine.  The heli was transporting a few sets of those combat exoskeletons back "
"from a DoubleTech testing site way out west, the ones they were showing on TV "
"before all this, I'm sure a guy like you could put those to good use.  I "
"won't risk my life for one but if you succeed and would like to trade them "
"you know where to find me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find the sunken helicopter"
msgstr "Trouvez l'hélicoptère noyé"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find the sunken helicopter"
msgid ""
"You got the location of a sunken helicopter, all that's left to do is find a "
"way to get there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a partner for hire.
msgid "Merc"
msgstr "Mercenaire"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_drugs.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NC_ANCILLA_GRUNT.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Independents/GENERIC/nc_solo.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Independents/GENERIC/nc_solo.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ An experienced survivor doing low importance work for Hub 01, or working
#. under another ancillary. Has no access to Hub 01s custom gear.
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Independent mercenaries with high quality combat gear and augments.
msgid "Mercenary"
msgstr "Mercenaire"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Job description of "Mercenary" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Hub Mercenary" NPC class
msgid "Fighting for the all-mighty dollar."
msgstr "Se battre pour le tout-puissant dollar."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any tips for surviving?"
msgstr "Des astuces de survie?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What would it cost to hire you?"
msgstr "Combien ça coûterait de vous embaucher ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm just a hired hand.  Someone pays me and I do what needs to be done."
msgstr "Je ne suis qu'un employé. Quelqu'un me paie et je fais ce qui doit être fait."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you have to fight your way out of an ambush, the only thing that is going "
"to save you is having a party that can return fire.  People who work alone "
"are easy pickings for monsters and bandits."
msgstr ""
"Si vous devez vous sortir d'une embuscade, la seule chose qui vous sauvera "
"sera d'avoir un groupe capable de riposter. Les personnes qui travaillent "
"seules sont des proies faciles pour les monstres et les bandits."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I suppose I should hire a party then?"
msgstr "Je suppose que je devrais engager une personne pour l'occasion ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm currently waiting for a customer to return… I'll make you a deal though, "
"750 merch will cover my expenses if I get a small cut of the loot."
msgstr ""
"J'attends actuellement le retour d'un client… Mais je vous propose un marché: "
"750 merch couvrira mes frais si je reçois une petite part du butin."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What the heck is a merch?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qu'un produit dérivé ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might be back."
msgstr "Je serais peut être de retour."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[750 merch] You have a deal."
msgstr "[750 merch] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Merch is what they call dollar bills around here.  Free Merchant Credit Notes "
"or something.  If you want to buy stuff around here and you don't want to "
"barter away your guns, you need merch."
msgstr ""
"Merch est ce qu'on appelle ici des billets d'un dollar. Des notes de crédit "
"gratuites ou quelque chose comme ça. Si tu veux acheter des choses ici et que "
"tu ne veux pas troquer tes armes, tu as besoin de marchandises."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I see.  Let's try this again from the start."
msgstr "Je vois. Recommençons depuis le début."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, how much merch do I need?"
msgstr "D'accord, de combien de marchandises ai-je besoin ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, thanks for the info.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I guess you're the boss."
msgstr "C'est vous le boss…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_scavenger_mercenary.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glad to have you aboard."
msgstr "Je suis heureux de vous compter parmi nous."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey there.  Do you work here, or what?"
msgstr "Bonjour à tous. Vous travaillez ici, ou quoi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Me?  No, I'm just passing through, how about you?"
msgstr "Moi ? Non, je ne fais que passer, et vous ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Work here?  No, of course not.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seen anything interesting out there?"
msgstr "Vous avez vu quelque chose d'intéressant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not much, just passing through.  Have a good day."
msgstr "Pas grand-chose, je ne fais que passer. Bonne journée."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You looking for a traveling companion?  I could use someone to watch my back."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Come to think of it, yeah.  The other day, I met this weird old man in the "
"woods.  Obsessed with rabbits.  He seemed like a nice fellow, open to "
"visitors, if you'd like I can send you his way to trade."
msgstr ""
"En y repensant, oui. L'autre jour, j'ai rencontré un vieil homme bizarre dans "
"les bois. Obsédé par les lapins. Il avait l'air d'un type sympa, ouvert aux "
"visiteurs, si tu veux je peux t'envoyer sur son chemin pour échanger."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I could point you to some acquaintances of mine that have a farm, they're "
"decent folk, if you have goods to trade.  Be careful around them, I get a "
"vibe like they don't like visitors too much, and honestly it makes me nervous "
"that they made it through this so together.  Kinda of ominous, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Je pourrais vous indiquer des connaissances qui ont une ferme, ce sont des "
"gens honnêtes, si vous avez des marchandises à échanger. Soyez prudent avec "
"eux, j'ai l'impression qu'ils n'aiment pas trop les visiteurs, et "
"honnêtement, ça me rend nerveux qu'ils aient réussi à traverser tout ça "
"ensemble. C'est un peu inquiétant, vous savez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, show me where to find this guy."
msgstr "Bien sûr, montrez-moi où trouver ce type."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm always open to meet new survivors.  Where are these acquaintances of "
"yours?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis toujours prête à rencontrer de nouveaux survivants. Où sont vos "
"connaissances ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Weird.  I guess I could check that out too, sure."
msgstr "C'est bizarre. Je pense que je pourrais vérifier cela aussi, bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ah, yeah, I've heard of that too.  It's a weird world out there, hey?"
msgstr "Ah, oui, j'en ai entendu parler aussi. C'est un monde étrange, hein ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, here, I'll draw you up a little map."
msgstr "Bien sûr, je vais vous dessiner une petite carte."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks!  What's your story?"
msgstr "Merci ! Quelle est votre histoire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks!  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, I have people of my own to look out for.  I can't leave them in the "
"lurch."
msgstr ""
"Désolé, j'ai des gens dont je dois m'occuper. Je ne peux pas les laisser en "
"plan."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They could come along too."
msgstr "Ils pourraient venir aussi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't I come back to your hideout?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ne reviendrais-je pas dans ta cachette ?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It doesn't really work that way.  They're back in safety, and I've got to go "
"check in with them with some supplies.  You know how it is, not everyone is "
"suited to risk travel these days."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas vraiment comme ça que ça marche. Ils sont de retour en sécurité, "
"et je dois aller les voir pour leur apporter des provisions. Vous savez ce "
"que c'est, tout le monde n'est pas fait pour les voyages à risque de nos "
"jours."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_visiting_scavenger.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Look, I don't know a better way to put this.  I don't know you, I can't bring "
"some random back with me.  For all I know you're a cannibal psycho or "
"something.  We all saw too much of that during <the_cataclysm>.  Me and mine, "
"we're not looking to expand our tribe just now, OK?"
msgstr ""
"Ecoute, je ne connais pas de meilleure façon de le dire. Je ne te connais "
"pas, je ne peux pas ramener un inconnu avec moi. Pour ce que j'en sais, tu es "
"un psychopathe cannibale ou quelque chose comme ça. On en a tous trop vu "
"pendant <the_cataclysm>. Moi et les miens, on ne cherche pas à agrandir notre "
"tribu pour l'instant, OK ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the surface of Hub 01 as an external mercenary.
msgid "Cranberry Foster"
msgstr "Cranberry Foster"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the surface of Hub 01 as an external mercenary.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Hub Mercenary"
msgstr "Mercenaire du Hub"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Better keep our eyes on the road."
msgstr "Mieux vaut garder les yeux sur la route."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*looks at you expectantly."
msgstr "*regarde vers vous avec impatience."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Better be careful around here."
msgstr "Mieux vaut être prudent par ici."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Got something to say?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose à dire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I charge hourly, y'know."
msgstr "Je facture à l'heure, vous savez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey."
msgstr "Salut."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to see you."
msgstr "Ça fait du bien de vous voir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Did I scare you off the first time?"
msgstr "Vous ai-je effrayé la première fois ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi again, other person."
msgstr "Rebonjour à l'autre personne."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*waves."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&There's a person reclined on the sofa here.  They're very tall, with their "
"legs reaching to the other armrest, and they're wearing a set of Hub 01's "
"modular armor.  An environmental suit in blue-and-brown is crumpled in a "
"misshapen heap on the floor near the table, and leaning against the far "
"armrest is a rifle looking like nothing you've seen before.\n"
"\n"
"They look up towards you as you come through the door and wave a hand.  "
"\"Placeholder text.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Did you just say \"placeholder text\" out loud?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Uh… okay.  Who are you?"
msgstr "Euh… ok.  Qui êtes-vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About those jobs…"
msgstr "À propos de vos boulots…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want help with something else?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'aide pour autre chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's set up a combat strategy."
msgstr "Mettons au point une stratégie de combat."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Good to have some company."
msgstr "Ça fait du bien d'avoir de la compagnie."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Have something to say?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose à dire?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Did you want something?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*waits expectantly."
msgstr "*attend avec impatience."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So what's going on?"
msgstr "Que se passe-t-il donc ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything on your mind?"
msgstr "Quelque chose vous tracasse?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was <the_cataclysm> like for you?"
msgstr "Comment était <the_cataclysm> pour vous?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want help with something?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'aide pour faire quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you know about our employers?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que vous savez au sujet de nos employeurs?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That gun isn't like anything I've ever seen.  What am I looking at?"
msgstr ""
"Ce pistolet ne ressemble à rien de ce que j'ai pu voir. Qu'est-ce que je "
"regarde ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the deal with your gun again?"
msgstr "Quel est le problème avec votre arme ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've helped you out now.  Do you think you could vouch for me with our "
"employers?"
msgstr ""
"Je vous ai aidé. Pensez-vous pouvoir vous porter garant pour moi auprès de "
"nos employeurs ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How can I get a gun like that?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que je peux trouver une arme comme celle-ci?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I just realized, we've been in touch for a while now and I don't actually "
"know; are you a man or a woman?"
msgstr ""
"Je viens de me rendre compte que nous sommes en contact depuis un certain "
"temps et que je ne sais pas si vous êtes un homme ou une femme."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About the gold you wanted…"
msgstr "Au sujet de l'or que vous vouliez…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know what I was expecting."
msgstr "Je ne sais pas à quoi je m'attendais."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Cool."
msgstr "Cool."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I sure did.  Sorry, just a stupid icebreaker.  Old habits and all that.\"  "
"They sit up.  \"What's up?"
msgstr ""
"Je l'ai fait. Désolé, c'était juste pour briser la glace. Les vieilles "
"habitudes et tout ça.\" Ils se redressent. \"Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who exactly are you?"
msgstr "Qui êtes-vous exactement?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I thought I was the only one working for the people here."
msgstr "Je pensais que j'était le/la seul(e) travaillant pour le Hub."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just saying hi.  I'll be on my way now."
msgstr "Je ne fait que dire bonjour. Je vais m'en aller maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just the same as you.  Some nobody doing dirty work for scraps.  Uh, no "
"offense."
msgstr ""
"Tout comme vous. Une personne qui fait du sale boulot pour des miettes. Sans "
"vouloir vous offenser."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "None taken.  I guess that makes two of us."
msgstr "Aucune n'a été prise. Je suppose que nous sommes deux."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, never mind."
msgstr "Enfin, peu importe."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess so.\"  They beam sheepishly.  \"Uh, call me Cranberry.  Cran is fine "
"too.  It's nice to meet someone else from here.  I guess having some company "
"for once wouldn't be awful."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que oui\". Ils affichent un air penaud. \"Appelez-moi Cranberry. "
"Cran, c'est bien aussi. C'est sympa de rencontrer quelqu'un d'autre d'ici. Je "
"suppose qu'avoir un peu de compagnie pour une fois n'est pas si mal."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I guess I could stay for a while."
msgstr "Je suppose que je pourrais rester ici un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I have some places to be right now.  Good to meet you."
msgstr ""
"En fait, je dois me rendre à quelques endroits en ce moment. Enchanté de vous "
"rencontrer."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not a whole lot, really.  They made me track down and destroy some government "
"documents a while back.  Obviously I read them first, but it wasn't much.  As "
"far as I know, this place had an experimental computer network before "
"everything went to hell.  What's going on in there now is anybody's guess."
msgstr ""
"Pas grand-chose, en fait. Ils m'ont fait rechercher et détruire des documents "
"gouvernementaux il y a quelque temps. Évidemment, je les ai lus d'abord, mais "
"ce n'était pas grand-chose. Pour autant que je sache, cet endroit disposait "
"d'un réseau informatique expérimental avant que tout ne parte en vrille. "
"Personne ne sait ce qui s'y passe aujourd'hui."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold on, government documents?"
msgstr "Attendez, des documents gouvernementaux?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Computer network?"
msgstr "Un système informatique?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Strange bedfellows…"
msgstr "Étranges compagnons de lit…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah!  Crazy shit.  They sent me to an office building to find a folder with "
"a certain serial and get rid of it.  They didn't even care what was on it.  "
"By the time I got there, though, the building was pretty much a wreck.  The "
"folder had been sitting in a puddle for God knows how long, and there was "
"nothing even remotely legible by then."
msgstr ""
"Oui, c'est ça ! C'est dingue. Ils m'ont envoyé dans un immeuble de bureaux "
"pour trouver un dossier avec un certain numéro de série et m'en débarrasser. "
"Ils ne se souciaient même pas de ce qu'il y avait dessus. Mais quand je suis "
"arrivé, le bâtiment était une véritable épave. Le dossier était resté dans "
"une flaque d'eau pendant Dieu sait combien de temps, et il n'y avait plus "
"rien de lisible, même de loin."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's what the news said, anyway.  It was only about a 20-minute trip from "
"my apartment and sometimes I'd drive past it, so I was curious and I did some "
"research into it.  The only info I could find about it online said that it "
"was a NASA lab for computer research, but that was probably bullshit.  I "
"mean, do you see any NASA logos?  Sure, we got huge steel doors and 15-foot "
"concrete walls, but not a logo in sight.  The building probably goes "
"underground, right?  It's way too small to be a whole laboratory up here."
msgstr ""
"C'est en tout cas ce que disaient les journaux. Il n'y avait qu'une vingtaine "
"de minutes de trajet depuis mon appartement et il m'arrivait de passer "
"devant, alors j'étais curieuse et j'ai fait quelques recherches à ce sujet. "
"Les seules informations que j'ai pu trouver en ligne disaient qu'il "
"s'agissait d'un laboratoire de recherche informatique de la NASA, mais "
"c'était probablement des conneries. Voyez-vous des logos de la NASA ? Bien "
"sûr, il y a d'énormes portes en acier et des murs en béton de 5 mètres, mais "
"pas un logo en vue. Le bâtiment est probablement souterrain, n'est-ce pas ? "
"C'est bien trop petit pour être un laboratoire entier ici."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just trying to get some rest.  I don't have anywhere else to stay, so they "
"let me sleep on the couch out here as long as I keep my gun handy."
msgstr ""
"J'essaie juste de me reposer. Je n'ai nulle part où loger, alors ils me "
"laissent dormir sur le canapé, à condition que je garde mon arme à portée de "
"main."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They don't let you in to sleep?"
msgstr "Ils ne vous laissent pas rentrer pour dormir?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dude, I wish.  It sounds like there's different people on the mic at "
"different times, but all of them give me the same spiel: nobody's allowed in "
"right now.  I guess I shouldn't raise a fuss about it, honestly.  All being "
"considered, this compound is pretty safe, and the couch ain't so bad."
msgstr ""
"J'aimerais bien. On dirait qu'il y a différentes personnes au micro à "
"différents moments, mais toutes me disent la même chose : personne n'est "
"autorisé à entrer pour l'instant. Je suppose que je ne devrais pas en faire "
"tout un plat, honnêtement. Tout compte fait, cette enceinte est assez sûre, "
"et le canapé n'est pas si mal."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You sound frustrated about it."
msgstr "Vous semblez frustré par ça."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Now that you mention it, it does seem rather strange."
msgstr "Maintenant que vous le dites, cela semble assez étrange."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thinking I should go hunt something soon…"
msgstr "Je pense que je devrais bientôt aller chasser quelque chose…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just wondering if things will get better someday."
msgstr "Je me demande juste si les choses vous aller mieux un jour."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hmm?  Nothing, I guess I just like resting in this place.  I feel good today."
msgstr ""
"Hmm ? Rien, je crois que j'aime me reposer dans cet endroit. Je me sens bien "
"aujourd'hui."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Wondering if the whole world is like this now.  It has to be, right?  I was "
"watching some foreign news channels when everything was going down, and it "
"sounded like things were just as bad there…"
msgstr ""
"Je me demande si le monde entier est comme ça maintenant.  Ce doit être le "
"cas, non?  J'ai regardé des chaînes d'information étrangères lorsque tout "
"s'est effondré, et j'ai eu l'impression que les choses allaient tout aussi "
"mal là-bas…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just vibing."
msgstr "Juste des vibrations."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*picks the gun up and shows it to you from a few different angles.  You've "
"never seen anything like it; it has a steel body with composite blue "
"furniture, and looks lightweight and cutting-edge.  It features a modern "
"hybrid scope, built-in attachments, and a strange quick-release button on the "
"side.  The magazine looks like something for an assault rifle, but the "
"magazine well itself is strangely designed and seems to be fitted with an "
"adapter to make the magazine actually fit.\n"
"\n"
"\"Whatcha think?\""
msgstr ""
"*Il prend l'arme et vous la montre sous différents angles. Vous n'avez jamais "
"rien vu de tel ; il a un corps en acier avec un meuble en composite bleu, et "
"semble léger et à la pointe de la technologie. Il est équipé d'une lunette "
"hybride moderne, d'accessoires intégrés et d'un étrange bouton de "
"déverrouillage rapide sur le côté. Le chargeur ressemble à celui d'un fusil "
"d'assaut, mais le logement du chargeur lui-même est étrangement conçu et "
"semble être équipé d'un adaptateur pour que le chargeur puisse s'y loger."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is that a custom Hub rifle?"
msgstr "Est-ce un fusil customisé du Hub que je vois?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where'd you find that thing?"
msgstr "Où est-ce que vous avez trouvé ce truc?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sweet piece of salvage."
msgstr "Une belle pièce de récupération."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's from our employers.  Apparently, it's a custom platform they make for "
"field agents.  It's got quick swap barrels for 9mm, the standard NATO "
"cartridges, and shotgun shells too.  It's great for if you're on a long field "
"mission and run out of ammo.  A lot of dudes bit the dust on their way home "
"from the gun store with a box of nine-mil.  I guess it's better them than us; "
"they don't need it now."
msgstr ""
"Il provient de nos employeurs. Apparemment, il s'agit d'une plateforme "
"personnalisée qu'ils fabriquent pour les agents de terrain. Elle est équipée "
"de canons à changement rapide pour le 9 mm, les cartouches standard de l'OTAN "
"et les cartouches de fusil de chasse. C'est idéal pour les missions de longue "
"durée où l'on est à court de munitions. Beaucoup de gars ont mordu la "
"poussière en rentrant de l'armurerie avec une boîte de 9 mm. Je suppose que "
"c'est mieux pour eux que pour nous ; ils n'en ont plus besoin maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Damn.  Where can I get one of those?"
msgstr "Wow.  Où est-ce que je peux me dégoter l'une de ses armes?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You'll have to work that out with the intercom.  They seem stingy with them."
msgstr ""
"Vous allez devoir négocier ça avec l'intercom. Ils ont l'air d'être assez "
"pingres avec ceux-ci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As promised earlier, I'll let the Hub know that you're worth manufacturing "
"some proper gear for.  Let 'em know that I sent you next time you talk with "
"them and I'm sure they'll help you."
msgstr ""
"Comme promis plus tôt, je vais informer le Hub que tu mérites qu'on fabrique "
"du bon équipement pour toi. Dis-leur que c'est moi qui t'envoie la prochaine "
"fois que tu leur parles, et je suis sûr qu'ils t'aideront."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do owe you one.  Tell you what: I'll let the Hub know that you're worth "
"manufacturing some proper gear for.  Let 'em know that I sent you next time "
"you talk with them and I'm sure they'll help you."
msgstr ""
"C'est vrai que je vous doit une faveur. Vous savez quoi, dites au Hub que je "
"pense que vous valez la peine de fabriquer pour vous de l'équipement de haute "
"qualité la prochaine fois que vous leur parlez, et ceci devrait probablement "
"leur faire considérer sérieusement votre requête."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'll have to work it out with the intercom.  I don't want to vouch for "
"someone I don't really know."
msgstr ""
"Vous allez devoir négocier ça avec l'intercom, je ne vais pas donner ma "
"garantie pour le bénéfice de quelqu'un que je ne connais pas vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I can do to change your mind?"
msgstr "Quelque chose que je peux faire pour vous faire changer d'avis?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Once we finish up this job, I'll vouch for you.  Pinkie promise."
msgstr ""
"Une fois que nous aurons fini ce boulot, je porterais garantie pour vous. "
"Promis juré."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "*goes quiet.  They chew their lip, looking off towards a point in space."
msgstr ""
"*Le silence se fait. Ils se mordent la lèvre, regardant au loin vers un point "
"dans l'espace."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry.  Too personal?"
msgstr "Je suis désolé(e). Trop personnel?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, it can wait."
msgstr "Ça peut peu être attendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, no!  It's fine, promise.  It's just been a hot minute, and I'm trying to "
"remember it.  It's been a while.  You sure you want to hear it?"
msgstr ""
"Non, non! C'est parfaitement ok, je promets. Ça c'est juste passé il y a "
"tellement longtemps, et j'essaie de me rappeler ce qui c'est passé "
"exactement. Vous êtes sûr(e) que vous voulez que je vous raconte cela?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sure."
msgstr "Je suis sûr(e)."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might not have the time.  Hold that thought for later."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai probablement pas le temps, mais j'aimerais garder l'opportunité de "
"faire ceci plus tard si cela vous va."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*stares at a point at the wall, thinking.  Their wedding ring glints on their "
"left hand."
msgstr ""
"* fixe un point sur le mur, en réfléchissant. Leur alliance brille sur leur "
"main gauche."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Wait.]"
msgstr "[Attendre.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"…Alright.  Well.  For starters, I lived alone in an apartment, and I didn't "
"have any family or relatives I really cared about, so things were a lot "
"easier for me than they could have been."
msgstr ""
"…D'accord.  Eh bien…  Pour commencer, je vivais seul dans un appartement, et "
"je n'avais pas de famille ou de proches auxquels je tenais vraiment, donc les "
"choses étaient beaucoup plus faciles pour moi qu'elles n'auraient pu l'être."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Listen.]"
msgstr "[Écouter.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I've never really been a prepper, but I was into conspiracy theories.  Not as "
"a participant, just as an observer.  I think information spread is "
"interesting.\"  They pause.  \"I think it was in early March that I started "
"thinking something was wrong.  Like, the riots were bad beforehand, right?  "
"And that just seemed like normal unrest.  But then suddenly you're seeing it "
"happening in other countries where the normal explanations don't work.  So I "
"dug deeper, and once I did, I realized that this had been happening since "
"January, and getting worse since then.  That was when I started to take it "
"seriously."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai jamais vraiment été un \"complotiste\", mais j'aimais les théories du "
"complot. Pas en tant que participant, mais en tant qu'observateur. Je pense "
"que la diffusion de l'information est intéressante.\" Ils font une pause. "
"\"Je pense que c'est au début du mois de mars que j'ai commencé à penser que "
"quelque chose n'allait pas. Par exemple, les émeutes étaient déjà mauvaises "
"avant, n'est-ce pas ? Et cela semblait être une agitation normale. Mais "
"soudain, cela se produit dans d'autres pays où les explications habituelles "
"ne fonctionnent pas. J'ai donc creusé un peu plus, et une fois que j'ai "
"creusé, j'ai réalisé que cela se produisait depuis janvier, et que cela "
"s'aggravait depuis. C'est à ce moment-là que j'ai commencé à prendre les "
"choses au sérieux."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"But like, I was a park ranger.  I wasn't exactly making six figures, and you "
"know how bad rent was.  I couldn't buy a ton of canned food, but what I "
"*could* do is can things myself.  Not in tin cans, but in jars; the old way.  "
"So every paycheck, I'd use a little bit to buy one or two big glass jars, and "
"on the weekends I'd spend a few hours filling them up with food and sealing "
"them.  I started brushing up at the range too.  Proud gun owner, baby."
msgstr ""
"Mais j'étais garde forestier. Je ne gagnais pas vraiment un salaire à six "
"chiffres, et vous savez à quel point le loyer était cher. Je ne pouvais pas "
"acheter des tonnes de conserves, mais ce que je pouvais faire, c'était mettre "
"des choses en conserve moi-même. Pas dans des boîtes de conserve, mais dans "
"des bocaux, à l'ancienne. À chaque paie, j'utilisais un peu d'argent pour "
"acheter un ou deux grands bocaux en verre et, le week-end, je passais "
"quelques heures à les remplir de nourriture et à les sceller. J'ai aussi "
"commencé à me perfectionner au stand de tir. Je suis fière d'être "
"propriétaire d'une arme à feu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What food were you canning?"
msgstr "Quel genre de nourriture est-ce que vous mettiez en conserve?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I bought fruit and veggies from the store for my greens, but I figured those "
"didn't really have enough calories for the long-term, so I hunted.  To be "
"more accurate, I poached in the park I worked at.  It was never anything "
"huge; I had to be able to conceal this stuff, remember.  But we were on a "
"shoestring budget as it is and we never had the people we needed, so it was "
"trivial to bag an animal using a rifle from one of the ranger stations.  I'd "
"dress the carcass, then leave it in a place that I could either bring with me "
"in my truck that day or come back later to sneak it out.  I never got caught. "
" I'm not proud of it, but I'm not really ashamed of it, either.  Besides, "
"venison is great."
msgstr ""
"J'ai acheté des fruits et des légumes au magasin pour mes légumes verts, mais "
"je me suis dit qu'ils ne contenaient pas assez de calories pour le long "
"terme, alors j'ai chassé. Pour être plus précis, j'ai braconné dans le parc "
"où je travaillais. Ce n'était jamais quelque chose d'énorme ; je devais être "
"capable de dissimuler ce genre de choses, souvenez-vous. Mais notre budget "
"était déjà très limité et nous n'avons jamais eu le personnel nécessaire. Il "
"était donc facile de capturer un animal à l'aide d'un fusil depuis l'un des "
"postes de gardes forestiers. J'habillais la carcasse, puis je la laissais "
"dans un endroit que je pouvais soit emporter avec moi dans mon camion ce "
"jour-là, soit revenir plus tard pour la sortir en cachette. Je ne me suis "
"jamais fait prendre. Je n'en suis pas fier, mais je n'en ai pas honte non "
"plus. En outre, la venaison est excellente."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"So I figured that this wasn't going to be a problem a few months down the "
"line, right?  Just a flash in the pan.  I had my emergency stock of food in "
"case things went bad for a little while.  Best case scenario, I never have to "
"worry about it, things go back to normal after a bit, and I save some money "
"on groceries for a while.  And I wanted to keep doing this for a few more "
"weeks, but…"
msgstr ""
"Je me suis donc dit que cela n'allait pas poser de problème dans quelques "
"mois, n'est-ce pas ? Ce n'était qu'un feu de paille. J'avais mon stock de "
"nourriture d'urgence au cas où les choses tourneraient mal pendant un petit "
"moment. Dans le meilleur des cas, je n'ai jamais à m'en préoccuper, les "
"choses reviennent à la normale après un certain temps et j'économise de "
"l'argent sur les courses pendant un certain temps. Je voulais continuer à "
"faire cela pendant quelques semaines encore, mais..."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "But what?"
msgstr "Mais quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"March 30th happened.\"  Cranberry seems shaken, and talks a little louder for "
"a second.  \"You remember that video, right?  That was what set off alarm "
"bells in my head.  That shit was fucking scary.  And at that point I "
"realized, okay, I think things are about to get bad and this is for real."
msgstr ""
"Le 30 mars est arrivé\". Cranberry semble ébranlé et parle un peu plus fort "
"pendant une seconde. \"Vous vous souvenez de cette vidéo, n'est-ce pas ? "
"C'est ce qui a déclenché l'alarme dans ma tête. Cette merde était vraiment "
"effrayante. C'est à ce moment-là que j'ai réalisé que les choses allaient mal "
"tourner et que c'était pour de vrai."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't remember the video."
msgstr "Je ne me souvient pas de cette vidéo."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Whoo-ee, someone was living under a rock, huh?  It was all over the news.  "
"Video on YouTube, it was a livestream of one of the riots in Minneapolis.  A "
"mom was…\"  They hesitate.  \"I don't want to go into detail, but it was real "
"bad.  Real bad.  That's what set off people panicking."
msgstr ""
"Quelqu'un vivait sous une pierre, hein ? C'était dans tous les journaux. Une "
"vidéo sur YouTube, c'était un livestream d'une des émeutes à Minneapolis. Une "
"mère était...\" Ils hésitent. \"Je ne veux pas entrer dans les détails, mais "
"c'était vraiment grave. Très grave. C'est ce qui a déclenché la panique chez "
"les gens."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"People started freaking out.  I did, too.  I don't know how bad things got "
"elsewhere, but shit was flying off the shelves where I lived.  Empty racks at "
"grocery stores everywhere you looked.  I had enough food for a few weeks, so "
"it wasn't a problem for me, but it still shook me up bad.  Every day some "
"horrible new shit was happening somewhere in the world, and things got just "
"worse and worse.  Then that insanity with Rhode Island happened, and once the "
"national emergency came out, I knew that okay, this is happening, it's "
"actually happening.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Did you know that I was still going to work that entire time?  I don't "
"know, it just felt meditative.  I lived in a pretty rural area, so there "
"wasn't the kind of chaos in the cities and congestion on the roads.  I could "
"just take a side road there and have a day of quiet.  Just the woods and "
"whoever else actually bothered to show up that day.  The park closed for "
"visitors closed a day or two before the state of emergency, and it was really "
"peaceful, being there alone."
msgstr ""
"Les gens ont commencé à paniquer. Moi aussi. Je ne sais pas à quel point la "
"situation s'est détériorée ailleurs, mais là où j'habitais, la marchandise "
"s'envolait des rayons. Les rayons des épiceries étaient vides partout. "
"J'avais assez de nourriture pour quelques semaines, ce n'était donc pas un "
"problème pour moi, mais cela m'a quand même beaucoup secoué. Chaque jour, il "
"se passait quelque chose d'horrible quelque part dans le monde, et les choses "
"allaient de mal en pis. Puis la folie de Rhode Island est arrivée, et une "
"fois que l'urgence nationale a été annoncée, j'ai su que c'était en train de "
"se produire, que c'était vraiment en train de se produire\".\n"
"\n"
"\"Saviez-vous que j'allais toujours travailler pendant tout ce temps ? Je ne "
"sais pas, j'avais l'impression de méditer. Je vivais dans une région assez "
"rurale, il n'y avait donc pas le chaos des villes et les embouteillages sur "
"les routes. Je pouvais simplement prendre une route secondaire et passer une "
"journée tranquille. Il n'y avait que les bois et tous ceux qui se donnaient "
"la peine de venir ce jour-là. Le parc a été fermé aux visiteurs un jour ou "
"deux avant l'instauration de l'état d'urgence, et c'était vraiment paisible "
"d'y être seul."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Then the portals happened, and you know the rest from there.  Two days later, "
"the world was over.  There was a lot of chaos in my complex.  I just nailed "
"shut my front door, drew all the curtains, kept my shotgun loaded, and "
"probably slept maybe ten hours total that week.  I don't know if there was "
"someone up in the sky watching over me, but if there was, I sure as hell owe "
"them big time."
msgstr ""
"Puis les portails sont apparus, et vous connaissez la suite. Deux jours plus "
"tard, le monde était fini. Le chaos régnait dans mon complexe. J'ai cloué ma "
"porte d'entrée, tiré tous les rideaux, gardé mon fusil chargé et j'ai "
"probablement dormi dix heures au total cette semaine-là. Je ne sais pas si "
"quelqu'un dans le ciel veillait sur moi, mais si c'est le cas, je lui suis "
"redevable."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I kind of lost track of the days.  Every day was the same; eat, check the "
"barricades, look on the Internet, play some games with the sound off to try "
"and distract myself.  I filled up my bathtub, and once the water went out, "
"I'd drink from there with a lifestraw when I needed to hydrate.  Meal "
"planning got easier after I was down to just my canned stuff.  The Internet "
"didn't stay on for long, though, which I guess was a blessing because of how "
"many people were sharing their fear and awful experiences in real time.  I "
"did that routine every day until that emergency broadcast came through that "
"no help was coming, and then I knew it was over."
msgstr ""
"J'ai un peu perdu le fil des jours. Chaque jour était le même : manger, "
"vérifier les barricades, regarder sur Internet, jouer à des jeux avec le son "
"éteint pour essayer de me distraire. Je remplissais ma baignoire et, une fois "
"que l'eau était coupée, je buvais de l'eau à l'aide d'une barre de vie "
"lorsque j'avais besoin de m'hydrater. La planification des repas est devenue "
"plus facile une fois que je n'avais plus que mes conserves. L'Internet n'a "
"pas fonctionné longtemps, ce qui a été une bénédiction, car beaucoup de gens "
"partageaient leurs peurs et leurs expériences terribles en temps réel. J'ai "
"suivi cette routine tous les jours jusqu'à ce qu'un message d'urgence "
"m'annonce qu'aucune aide n'arrivait, et j'ai alors su que c'était fini."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It took a bit for me to muster the nerve to leave, but I wanted to.  Had to "
"see, y'know?  It was… a shock, zombies just walking in the parking lot.  "
"Like, sure, I could look out the window, but it feels different up close.  I "
"had my knife handy, and I didn't want to make too much noise, so that's what "
"I used.  I stabbed one of my dead neighbors in the neck that day.\"  They "
"smile wistfully.  \"I threw up on my shoes after the first one, but it got "
"easier."
msgstr ""
"Il m'a fallu un peu de temps pour trouver le courage de partir, mais j'en "
"avais envie. Il fallait que je voie, tu vois ? C'était... un choc, les "
"zombies marchant juste dans le parking. Bien sûr, je pouvais regarder par la "
"fenêtre, mais de près, c'est différent. J'avais mon couteau à portée de main, "
"et je ne voulais pas faire trop de bruit, alors c'est ce que j'ai utilisé. "
"J'ai poignardé un de mes voisins morts dans le cou ce jour-là\". Ils sourient "
"avec nostalgie. \"J'ai vomi sur mes chaussures après la première fois, mais "
"c'est devenu plus facile."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My truck was still there, and was on half a tank of gas.  I thought, okay, "
"this isn't gonna be easy, but I can pack my food and the things I need to "
"take with me into the truck, and then drive to that building I know about "
"that was so reinforced.\"  They gesture around them.  \"This building.  The "
"Hub.  So I got some stuff into a bugout bag in the cabin and filled up the "
"truck bed, and off I went.  The roads were bad, but I'm not a bad driver.  "
"Zombies are slow."
msgstr ""
"Mon camion était toujours là, et il ne lui restait que la moitié du réservoir "
"d'essence. Je me suis dit, d'accord, ça ne va pas être facile, mais je peux "
"mettre ma nourriture et les choses que j'ai besoin d'emporter dans le camion, "
"et ensuite conduire jusqu'à ce bâtiment que je connais et qui a été tellement "
"renforcé.\" Ils font un geste autour d'eux. \"Ce bâtiment. Le Hub. J'ai donc "
"mis quelques affaires dans un sac de survie dans la cabine, j'ai rempli la "
"benne du camion et je suis parti. Les routes étaient mauvaises, mais je ne "
"suis pas un mauvais conducteur. Les zombies sont lents."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And the rest is history."
msgstr "Et le reste appartient à l'histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If only, huh?  No, not quite.  About five miles away I hit a bad pothole and "
"skidded off the road and got stuck.  That's not a problem on its own, but a "
"few minutes into trying to get it unstuck, I saw a big furrow of dirt coming "
"towards me and decided, you know what, maybe I should get off the side of the "
"road.  So I grab my bugout bag from the cabin and a little food from the bed, "
"and I book it onto the road.  Now, I don't know what this thing was, but it "
"hit the truck from below and *flipped it over*.  That was enough to make me "
"say 'Nope, I can go on foot.'"
msgstr ""
"Si seulement, hein ? Non, pas tout à fait. À environ huit kilomètres de là, "
"j'ai heurté un nid-de-poule, je suis sorti de la route et je me suis retrouvé "
"coincé. Ce n'est pas un problème en soi, mais quelques minutes après avoir "
"essayé de le dégager, j'ai vu un grand sillon de terre venir vers moi et j'ai "
"décidé, vous savez quoi, que je devrais peut-être quitter le bord de la "
"route. J'ai donc pris mon sac de survie dans la cabane et un peu de "
"nourriture dans le lit, et je me suis engagé sur la route. Je ne sais pas ce "
"qu'était cette chose, mais elle a frappé le camion par en dessous et l'a fait "
"basculer. Cela a suffi à me faire dire : \" Non, je peux y aller à pied \"."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It took me a few days from there.  I had a heavy load, and it was slow going. "
" I slept on the road the first night because I was so freaked out by what I "
"saw, but the day after I got the nerves to walk through the woods.  I had a "
"tent, so it wasn't so bad.  Every now and then, I'd run into a zombie, or a "
"wrecked car that still had some of them buckled in.  I left my shotgun behind "
"in the truck, so I got better at using the knife.  It gets easier, y'know?"
msgstr ""
"Il m'a fallu quelques jours à partir de là. J'avais un lourd fardeau et j'ai "
"mis du temps à avancer. J'ai dormi sur la route la première nuit parce que "
"j'étais tellement effrayé par ce que je voyais, mais le jour suivant, j'ai eu "
"le courage de marcher dans les bois. J'avais une tente, alors ce n'était pas "
"si mal. De temps en temps, je tombais sur un zombie ou sur une voiture "
"accidentée dans laquelle certains étaient encore attachés. J'ai laissé mon "
"fusil de chasse dans le camion, alors je me suis amélioré dans l'utilisation "
"du couteau. C'est de plus en plus facile, vous savez ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A while later, I made it here.  The gate was open, so I just walked right in. "
" I tried the intercom, but nobody answered, which I'm sure you had happen to "
"you, too.  Then I realize: this building is super reinforced, unlocked, and "
"seems abandoned now.  Why don't I just stay here?  So I set up my stuff in "
"this here lobby and I spend the night there.  Then I try the intercom again."
msgstr ""
"Un peu plus tard, je suis arrivé ici. La porte était ouverte, alors je suis "
"entré directement. J'ai essayé l'interphone, mais personne n'a répondu, ce "
"qui, j'en suis sûr, vous est arrivé à vous aussi. Je me suis alors rendu "
"compte que ce bâtiment était super renforcé, qu'il n'était pas fermé à clé et "
"qu'il semblait abandonné. Pourquoi ne pas rester ici ? J'installe donc mes "
"affaires dans ce hall et j'y passe la nuit. Puis j'essaie à nouveau "
"l'interphone."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Did they answer that time?"
msgstr "Ont-ils répondu cette fois-ci ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Hoo boy, yes they did, and let me tell you, they were not happy campers about "
"me crashing on their couch.  Now, these people don't tell me who they are, "
"but they tell me to get off the premises immediately.  I wasn't having that.  "
"I had been through hell and come out the other end, and I don't remember what "
"I said to them, but it was along the lines of 'I have nowhere to go, and your "
"building is nice and cozy, so if you want me to leave, you can come out here "
"and make me.'\"  They laugh.  \"They weren't expecting me to bite back.  So I "
"turn off the intercom and I go eat lunch.  When I go back again, the first "
"thing they ask is if I want a job."
msgstr ""
"Et laissez-moi vous dire qu'ils n'étaient pas contents que je m'installe sur "
"leur canapé. Ces personnes ne m'ont pas dit qui elles étaient, mais elles "
"m'ont demandé de quitter les lieux immédiatement. Je n'étais pas d'accord. "
"J'avais vécu l'enfer et j'en étais sorti par l'autre bout, et je ne me "
"souviens pas de ce que je leur ai dit, mais c'était du genre 'Je n'ai nulle "
"part où aller, et votre bâtiment est agréable et confortable, alors si vous "
"voulez que je parte, vous pouvez venir ici et me forcer'\". Ils rient. \"Ils "
"ne s'attendaient pas à ce que je réplique. J'ai donc éteint l'interphone et "
"je suis allé manger. Lorsque j'y retourne, la première chose qu'ils me "
"demandent, c'est si je veux un emploi."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just like that?"
msgstr "Juste comme ça?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, no.  It was obvious they just wanted to get rid of me, but I decided I "
"wanted to show that I was useful.  They tell me to find a crashed drone "
"somewhere in the surrounding area and bring it back here.  No directions, of "
"course.  Y'know, go find this drone in the middle of the woods, it'll be "
"easy.  But I had some tools in my bag, right?  And yours truly has repaired "
"some drones in the park service.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"So it takes me a whole-ass afternoon, but I find their stupid drone stuck "
"in a tree.  I can see the camera's still on, so I pick it up and I tell the "
"lens: 'Hey, you want me to fix it too?'  And I do.  It was just a cracked "
"frame and the wiring to the rotors was sliced up.  The propellers themselves "
"were fine.  So I bring it out of the woods and turn it off.  Then I open up "
"the casing, solder up the wires, and use superglue to hold the frame "
"together, which wasn't perfect, but I figured it'd hold until it got back "
"home.  Then I turned it back on, and wouldn't you know, it immediately starts "
"up and sits there for a minute, like 'What the fuck?  Why am I working "
"again?'  And then it flies away, and I walk my smug ass back home."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien, non. Il était évident qu'ils voulaient juste se débarrasser de moi, "
"mais j'ai décidé de montrer que j'étais utile. Ils me disent de trouver un "
"drone écrasé quelque part dans les environs et de le ramener ici. Pas "
"d'instructions, bien sûr. Vous savez, trouvez ce drone au milieu des bois, ce "
"sera facile. Mais j'avais des outils dans mon sac, non ? Et votre serviteur a "
"réparé quelques drones dans le service des parcs.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Il m'a fallu tout un après-midi, mais j'ai trouvé leur stupide drone coincé "
"dans un arbre. Je vois que la caméra est encore allumée, alors je la ramasse "
"et je dis à l'objectif : 'Hé, tu veux que je la répare aussi ?'. Et c'est ce "
"que je fais. C'était juste un cadre fissuré et le câblage des rotors était "
"coupé. Les hélices elles-mêmes étaient en bon état. Je l'ai donc sorti de la "
"forêt et je l'ai éteint. J'ouvre ensuite le boîtier, je soude les fils et "
"j'utilise de la superglue pour maintenir le cadre ensemble, ce qui n'était "
"pas parfait, mais je me suis dit que ça tiendrait jusqu'à ce qu'il rentre à "
"la maison. Je l'ai ensuite rallumé et, comme par hasard, il a immédiatement "
"démarré et est resté là pendant une minute, à se demander \"Qu'est-ce que "
"c'est que ce bordel ? Pourquoi est-ce que je fonctionne à nouveau ? Puis il "
"s'est envolé et j'ai raccompagné mon petit cul à la maison."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And *now* the rest is history."
msgstr "Et *maintenant*, le reste appartient à l'histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You got it.\"  Cranberry grins.  \"I ask them if their drone got home in one "
"piece, and it did.  They said that my work wasn't bad at all and did a little "
"impromptu interview asking where I learned my skills and how I got to the "
"building.  I got the canned intro of 'we underestimated your usefulness', and "
"like you say, the rest is history.  Now we're here."
msgstr ""
"Vous l'avez.\" Cranberry sourit. \"Je leur ai demandé si leur drone était "
"rentré chez lui en un seul morceau, et c'est le cas. Ils ont dit que mon "
"travail n'était pas mal du tout et ont fait une petite interview impromptue "
"en me demandant où j'avais appris mes compétences et comment j'étais arrivé "
"dans le bâtiment. J'ai eu droit à l'introduction en conserve \"nous avons "
"sous-estimé votre utilité\" et, comme vous le dites, le reste appartient à "
"l'histoire. Maintenant, nous sommes ici."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's quite the story.  You seem to be feeling pretty good, in spite of the "
"world ending."
msgstr ""
"C'est toute une histoire. Vous semblez vous sentir bien, malgré la fin du "
"monde."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess I am, yeah.  It feels nice to be putting all my skills to use instead "
"of working an underpaid job to walk around the same woods flying a quadcopter "
"around and being a glorified PR rep to cranky parents who are only at the "
"park because they promised their kids they'd go.  Mind you, I'd still go back "
"to it if I could.\"  Their expression falters a little.  \"We all had our "
"struggles, but things are different now, you know?  We get to worry about the "
"future in a whole new way; an existential way that we never had to consider "
"before, not really.  Sure, there was the occasional nuke scare, but as a "
"society, we had things pretty good.  Unless the dead stop getting back up, I… "
"don't think things are going to ever go back to normal.\"\n"
"\n"
"Cranberry pauses for a moment, then shakes it off.  \"But… right now, I'm "
"feeling at peace with everything, despite it all.  Maybe I'm just in shock, "
"and it'll all come crashing down one of these days.  Things might get worse, "
"and they may never get better.  But I feel alright.  And I think that's "
"enough for me."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que c'est le cas, oui. C'est agréable d'utiliser toutes mes "
"compétences au lieu d'avoir un emploi sous-payé pour me promener dans les "
"mêmes bois en faisant voler un quadcoptère et en étant un représentant en "
"relations publiques glorifié pour des parents grincheux qui ne sont au parc "
"que parce qu'ils ont promis à leurs enfants d'y aller. Remarquez, j'y "
"retournerais quand même si je le pouvais\". Leur expression s'assombrit un "
"peu. \"Nous avons tous eu des difficultés, mais les choses sont différentes "
"aujourd'hui, vous savez ? Nous devons nous préoccuper de l'avenir d'une toute "
"nouvelle manière, une manière existentielle que nous n'avons jamais eu à "
"considérer auparavant, pas vraiment. Bien sûr, il y avait de temps en temps "
"une peur nucléaire, mais en tant que société, nous étions plutôt bien lotis. "
"À moins que les morts ne cessent de se relever, je... ne pense pas que les "
"choses reviendront un jour à la normale.\"\n"
"\n"
"Cranberry s'arrête un instant, puis se reprend. \"Mais... pour l'instant, je "
"me sens en paix avec tout, malgré tout. Peut-être que je suis juste en état "
"de choc, et que tout s'écroulera un de ces jours. Les choses pourraient "
"empirer et ne jamais s'améliorer. Mais je me sens bien. Et je pense que cela "
"me suffit."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you for telling me."
msgstr "Merci de m'avoir raconté ça."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*smiles at you, genuine and warm.  \"It feels nice to tell it.  You're "
"welcome.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il vous sourit, sincère et chaleureux. \"Ça fait du bien de le raconter. De "
"rien.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Spend a while in silence.]"
msgstr "(Passer un moment en silence.)"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, that's a bit personal.  Like, you seem alright, but that's kind of "
"heavy stuff, y'know?  Maybe I can tell you another time."
msgstr ""
"Je suis désolée, c'est un peu personnel. Tu as l'air d'aller bien, mais c'est "
"un peu lourd, tu sais ? Peut-être que je pourrai te le dire une autre fois."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I guess I am, yeah.  Feels like a stupid fetch quest.\"  They suddenly pause. "
" \"Hey.  If you happen across any gold out in the world, I'll pay you to "
"bring it back for me.  Right now my assignment stipulates eight scrip per "
"kilo, and I'd be willing to give you all of that.  I just want something else "
"to do.  Just maybe don't mention it to the intercom, alright?  This is "
"supposed to be my job."
msgstr ""
"Je suppose que oui. J'ai l'impression de faire une quête stupide.\" Ils "
"s'arrêtent soudain. \"Hé, si vous trouvez de l'or dans le monde, je vous "
"paierai pour que vous me le rameniez. Pour l'instant, ma mission prévoit huit "
"scripts par kilo, et je serais prêt à vous donner tout ça. Je veux juste "
"faire autre chose. Ne le dites pas à l'interphone, d'accord ? C'est censé "
"être mon travail."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You got it.  I'll let you know if I find any gold."
msgstr "Vous l'avez. Je vous ferai savoir si je trouve de l'or."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually, I don't think I have time for that, sorry."
msgstr "En fait, je ne pense pas avoir le temps pour cela, désolé."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks a lot."
msgstr "Merci beaucoup"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Got some gold for me?"
msgstr "Vous avez de l'or pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[200 gold] Here's a batch for you."
msgstr "[200 gold] Voici un lot pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have 200 gold for you right now."
msgstr "Je n'ai pas 200 unités d'or pour vous pour le moment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I appreciate it.  Here's the scrip; don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr "J'apprécie. Voici votre récompense; ne dépensez pas tout au même endroit."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Honestly, sometimes I feel like an ATM."
msgstr ""
"Honnêtement, j'ai parfois l'impression d'être un distributeur automatique de "
"billets."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks.  I never thought I'd get exhausted of carrying pure gold around, but "
"here we are."
msgstr ""
"Merci. Je n'aurais jamais cru que je me lasserais un jour de transporter de "
"l'or pur, mais nous y sommes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Exchanging my money for goods and services.  Just as the founding fathers "
"intended."
msgstr ""
"J'échange mon argent contre des biens et des services. Comme le voulaient les "
"pères fondateurs."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Active Noise Control"
msgstr "Source de la nuissance"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid ""
"Investigate Hub 01's radio tower, discover the source of the interference, "
"and fix the problem."
msgstr ""
"Enquêtez sur la tour radio du Hub 01, découvrez la source de l'interférence "
"et résolvez le problème."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid ""
"Well… a little while ago, I set up a radio transmitter in the radio tower not "
"far from here, but apparently it's stopped transmitting.  If you're willing "
"to back me up while I check it out, I'll owe you a favor."
msgstr ""
"Eh bien... il y a quelque temps, j'ai installé un émetteur radio dans la tour "
"radio située non loin d'ici, mais apparemment, il a cessé d'émettre. Si vous "
"voulez bien me soutenir pendant que je vérifie, je vous dois une faveur."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
msgid "Alright, let's be off.  You don't mind taking point, right?"
msgstr "Très bien, allons-y. Ça ne vous dérange pas de faire le point, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid "Well, thanks for offering."
msgstr "Merci de votre offre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid ""
"I'm sure we'll figure it out once there.  Bring a good weapon and some ammo "
"just in case, if you can; no idea what insanity <the_cataclysm> has brought "
"us this time."
msgstr ""
"Je suis sûr que nous trouverons une solution une fois sur place. Apportez une "
"bonne arme et quelques munitions au cas où, si vous le pouvez ; on ne sait "
"pas quelle folie <the_cataclysm> nous a apporté cette fois-ci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid "You think we fixed the problem?"
msgstr "Vous pensez que nous avons résolu le problème ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid ""
"Sure seems like it.  What even was that…?  Eh, doesn't matter.  Let's go back "
"to the Hub; hopefully the tower's working now."
msgstr ""
"On dirait bien.  Qu'est-ce que c'était…?  Peu importe.  Retournons au Hub; "
"j'espère que la tour fonctionne maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
msgid "*frowns at you.  \"I've been with you this whole time, dude.  C'mon."
msgstr ""
"*fronce les sourcils. \"J'ai été avec toi tout ce temps, mec. Je suis avec "
"toi depuis tout ce temps, mec."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return to Hub 01"
msgstr "Retournez au Hub 01"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Return to Hub 01"
msgid ""
"With the source of the radio tower's interference fixed, return to Hub 01 "
"with Cranberry."
msgstr ""
"Une fois la source d'interférence de la tour radio réparée, retournez au Hub "
"01 avec Cranberry."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
msgid "Let's get back home."
msgstr "Rentrons à la maison."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
msgid "Hey, you have a map, don't you?  You can use mine, if you need."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez une carte, n'est-ce pas ? Vous pouvez utiliser la mienne, si vous "
"en avez besoin."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
msgid "Thanks a lot for having my back.  Like I said, I owe you one."
msgstr "Merci beaucoup de m'avoir soutenu. Comme je l'ai dit, je vous en dois une."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Ulysses_Rourke.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A cold ex-mercenary from a third world country you have never heard of
#. before.  Third in charge after Melchior and Director Cohen.
msgid "U. Rourke"
msgstr "U. Rourke"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Ulysses_Rourke.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ A cold ex-mercenary from a third world country you have never heard of
#. before.  Third in charge after Melchior and Director Cohen.
msgid "Head of Security"
msgstr "Chef de la Sécurité"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Ulysses_Rourke.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Needs his own unique background.
msgid "Head of security"
msgstr "Chef de la sécurité"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Ulysses_Rourke.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#. ~ Job description of "Head of security" NPC class
#. ~ Needs his own unique background.
#. ~ Job description of "Hub Security" NPC class
msgid "I'm part of the Hub security team."
msgstr "Je fais partie de l'équipe de sécurité du Hub."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A generic guard for Hub 01.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Hub Security"
msgstr "Sécurité du Hub"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_robofac_generic_security.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Keep it civil, merc."
msgstr "Restez courtois, Merc."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A free merchant caravanner that temporarily supplies the hq with
#. foodstuff.
msgid "Free Merchant"
msgstr "Marchand Libre"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ This is a unique NPC who doesn't get randomly selected background traits
msgid "Caravaneer"
msgstr "Caravanier"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Job description of "Caravaneer" NPC class
#. ~ This is a unique NPC who doesn't get randomly selected background traits
msgid "I'm the owner of a trade caravan."
msgstr "Je suis le chef d'une caravane marchande."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Still plenty of outlaws in the roads, perhaps you should tend to your job, "
"marshal…"
msgstr ""
"Il y a encore beaucoup de hors-la-loi sur les routes, vous devriez peut-être "
"vous occuper de votre travail, marshal…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You see anything you want, marshal?"
msgstr "Quelque chose vous tente marshal?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, a U.S. marshal, how quaint."
msgstr "Oh, un U.S. marshal, comme c'est pittoresque."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome…"
msgstr "Bonjour…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_FORGE_MERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Here to trade, I hope?"
msgstr "Ici pour échanger, j'espère ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Safe travels, scavenger."
msgstr "Bon voyage, pilleur·se."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When is the next shipment?"
msgstr "Quand aura lieu le prochain chargement?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I keep to my own business, and you keep to yours, marshal.  Seems like a fair "
"deal?"
msgstr ""
"Je m'occupe de mes affaires et vous vous occupez des vôtres, marshal. Cela "
"semble être un accord équitable ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have been supplying this lab here with food from a few hunting and farming "
"communities nearby.  The roads are tough and dangerous, but it makes good "
"money, and beats scavenging the cities for scraps."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons approvisionné ce laboratoire en nourriture provenant de quelques "
"communautés de chasseurs et d'agriculteurs des environs. Les routes sont "
"difficiles et dangereuses, mais cela rapporte beaucoup d'argent, et c'est "
"mieux que d'aller chercher des restes dans les villes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keep safe, then."
msgstr "Soyez prudents."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Around <interval>, if the caravan doesn't run into trouble."
msgstr "Vers <interval>, si la caravane ne rencontre pas d'ennuis."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/ROBOFAC_SURFACE_FREEMERCHANT.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the info, bye."
msgstr "Merci pour l'information, au revoir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NC_ANCILLA_GRUNT.json
#. ~ Job description of "Mercenary" NPC class
#. ~ An experienced survivor doing low importance work for Hub 01, or working
#. under another ancillary. Has no access to Hub 01s custom gear.
msgid "Fighting in the name of Hub 01 and money, mostly money."
msgstr "Combat au service d'Hub 01 et de l'argent, principalement pour l'argent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid ""
"Ahh but if you want suggestions and are one for craft beers, I certainly "
"suggest having some old world brew before it all goes flat or sour."
msgstr ""
"Ahh mais si vous voulez des suggestions et que vous êtes un adepte des bières "
"artisanales, je vous suggère certainement de prendre un peu de bière du vieux "
"monde avant que tout ne devienne plat ou aigre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid ""
"Speaking off, Cranberry here brought me a whole cask of Cabernet a few days "
"ago.  So if red wines are your thing I can offer that by the gallon."
msgstr ""
"En parlant de ça, Cranberry m'a ramené un tonneau entier de Cabernet il y a "
"quelque jours. Donc si les vins rouges sont votre vice je peux vous en offrir "
"des litres et des litres."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid ""
"Just bought some of this new \"Free Whiskey\" from the caravaneer up above.  "
"It's vile if you ask me, but it packs a good punch.  A real drink of the "
"apocalypse I suppose."
msgstr ""
"J'ai juste acheté un peu de ce \"Whisky Libre\" d'un chef de caravane qui "
"c'est pointé en haut.  C'est affreux si vous me demandez, mais ça vous "
"nettoie bien les boyaux.  Une bonne liqueur de l'apocalypse je suppose."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid "The water I boiled from a pool by the rails, so I don't suggest you get some."
msgstr ""
"L'eau que j'ai bouillie provenait d'une piscine située près des rails, je ne "
"vous conseille donc pas d'en prendre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid ""
"And you can also try chatting with some of the other patrons if networking is "
"your thing."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez aussi essayer de discuter avec d'autres clients, si le réseautage "
"est votre truc."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid "Also have some old world sodas if alcohol isn't your kind of thing."
msgstr ""
"J'ai aussi des sodas du monde d'avant si l'alcool n'est pas votre tasse de "
"thé."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid "Not much fruit juice to make fancy drinks, but I can scrounge up some still."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai plus beaucoup de jus de fruit pour faire des cocktails, mais je crois "
"que je peut fouiller un peu pour en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid "Can also sell some dry foods if you want to stock for a trip somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Je peux aussi vous vendre des aliments secs si vous êtes en train de préparer "
"une expédition vers quelque part."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgid "Also good for a chat if you don't want anything."
msgstr "C'est aussi un bon moyen de discuter si vous ne voulez rien."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ah great to see you around."
msgstr "Ah, c'est un plaisir de vous voir dans les parages."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How goes the surface?  All dead and walkey still?"
msgstr "Comment va la surface ? Tout est mort et tout marche encore ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Should hang around one of these days, help me out in the bar for a change, "
"what do you say, eh?"
msgstr ""
"Je devrais rester dans le coin un de ces jours, m'aider au bar pour changer, "
"qu'en dites-vous, hein ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, what can I do for you today?"
msgstr "Que puis-je faire pour vous aujourd'hui ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Feel free to lounge around, and ask if there's anything you need."
msgstr ""
"N'hésitez pas à vous détendre et à demander si vous avez besoin de quelque "
"chose."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Welcome to the Terminal, scavenger, longest standing underground bar in the "
"state.  Feel free to ask if you need something."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenue au Terminal, scavenger, le plus ancien bar clandestin de l'état. "
"N'hésitez pas à demander si vous avez besoin de quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let me see what you keep behind the counter."
msgstr "Laissez-moi voir ce que vous gardez derrière le comptoir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you have on tap?"
msgstr "Qu'avez-vous en stock ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "There should be a package for me here."
msgstr "Il devrait y avoir un paquet pour moi ici."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any good rumors?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll be going…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If what you want are jobs and opportunities, you'll probably be better off "
"asking to my other patrons.  Have regulars from well across the state, I'm "
"sure some can offer what you want.\"\n"
"\n"
" \"Really, I just tend the bar and don't ask many questions.  Things tend "
"work out better that way."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll ask around, thank you."
msgstr "Je me renseignerai, merci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Just the best spirits the whole of New England has to offer.  Well the best "
"we've managed to loot so far at least.\n"
"\n"
" <ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"
msgstr ""
"Juste les meilleurs crus que la Nouvelle Angleterre a à offrir.  Ou du moins "
"les meilleurs qu'on a réussi à trouver pour l'instant.\n"
"\n"
" <ANCILLA_barkeep_suggestion>"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just some water."
msgstr "Juste de l'eau."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$2] Just some water."
msgstr "[$2] Juste de l'eau."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$3] I'll take a beer"
msgstr "[$3] Je veux bien une bière."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$3] Get me a cup of red wine"
msgstr "[$3] Un coupe de vin rouge s'il vous plaît."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$3] I'll take a shot of rum"
msgstr "[$3] Un shot de rhum, si possible."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[$3] I'll take a shot of whiskey"
msgstr "[$3] Un shot de whisky."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_bartender.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second thought, don't bother."
msgstr "En y réfléchissant bien, ce n'est pas la peine."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_BARKEEP.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh yes of course, think this should be all, well that's all there is anyhow."
msgstr ""
"Oh oui, bien sûr, je pense que cela devrait être tout, enfin c'est tout ce "
"qu'il y a de toute façon."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Doc.  Stevens"
msgstr "Doc Stevens"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Ancilla Doctor"
msgstr "Docteur Auxiliaire"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Job description of "Ancilla Doctor" NPC class
#. ~ Job description of "Mercurial Medical Agent" NPC class
msgid "I try to keep this gang in one piece.  It's a full time job."
msgstr ""
"J'essaie de garder ce groupe en un seul morceau. C'est un travail à plein "
"temps."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Try not to touch anything.  Keeping this place clean is a full time job."
msgstr ""
"Essayez de ne toucher à rien. Garder cet endroit propre est un travail à "
"plein temps."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Did you know you can lose a medical license over tax fraud?  Couldn't be me."
msgstr ""
"Vous savez que quelqu'un peut perdre sa license médicale pour cause de fraude "
"fiscale?  Bien sûr ce n'est pas mon cas."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You try to use the autodoc alone and I'll let it carve you up.  I'm not "
"kidding."
msgstr ""
"Vous essayez d'utiliser l'autodoc par vous même et je le laisserai vous "
"dépecer.  Je ne blague pas."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Clinic is open, yes.  If you need medical assistance, I'm your man."
msgstr ""
"La clinique est ouverte, oui. Si vous avez besoin d'une assistance médicale, "
"je suis votre homme."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you help me with some bionics?"
msgstr "Vous pourriez m'aider avec des implants bioniques?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could use your medical assistance."
msgstr "J'ai besoin de votre aide médicale."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need to trade some medical supplies."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'échanger pour des fournitures médicales."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_woodcutter1.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Come back later, I need to take care of a few things first."
msgstr "Revenez plus tard, je dois m'occuper de certaines choses avant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can take a look at you or your companions if you have any injuries.  It'll "
"cost you, of course."
msgstr ""
"Je peux vous examiner, vous ou vos compagnons, si vous avez des blessures. "
"Cela vous coûtera de l'argent, bien sûr."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC, 30m] I need you to patch me up."
msgstr "[4 POH, 30m] J'ai besoin que vous me raccommodiez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 HGC, 1h] I need you to patch my friends up."
msgstr "[8 POH, 1h] J'ai besoin que vous raccommodiez mes compagnons."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_nurse.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I should be fine."
msgstr "Ça devrait aller pour moi."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, what are you looking for?"
msgstr "Bien sûr, qu'est ce que vous cherchez?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I was wondering if you could install a cybernetic implant…"
msgstr "Je me demandais si vous pouviez installer un implant cybernétique…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I was wondering if you could install a cybernetic implant in my friend here…"
msgstr ""
"Je me demandais si il serait possible pour vous d'installer un implant "
"cybernétique dans l'un des mes compagnons…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need help removing an implant…"
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'aide pour retirer un implant…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need help removing an implant from one of my friends…"
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'aide pour retirer un implant d'un de mes compagnons…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh no, I was wondering if you knew where to get some."
msgstr "Oh non, je me demandais si vous saviez où en trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Now some protocol tests for brain damage.  Please stare at the light over "
"there…"
msgstr ""
"Maintenant, quelques protocoles pour tester les lésions cérébrales.  Fixez la "
"lumière là-bas…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It might take some days for your nervous system to adapt.  Come back if you "
"experience any concerning symptoms like…"
msgstr ""
"Il se peut que votre système nerveux mette quelques jours à s'adapter.  "
"Revenez si vous ressentez des symptômes inquiétants comme…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I suggest you take it easy for a few days now."
msgstr "Je vous suggère de vous ménager pendant quelques jours."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Augustmoon_Salvors/augustmoon_doctor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Take it easy now, or come back soon.  All the same to me."
msgstr "Calmez-vous maintenant, ou revenez bientôt. Pour moi, c'est la même chose."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you want to carve up cyborg corpses, find someone at the bar, not me."
msgstr ""
"Si vous voulez découper des cadavres de cyborg, trouvez quelqu'un au bar, pas "
"moi."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_DOCTOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It takes resources to keep this show running: disinfectant, antibiotics, "
"anesthetics, so on.  I'll give you a great price if you bring any of those."
msgstr ""
"Il faut des ressources pour faire fonctionner ce spectacle : désinfectants, "
"antibiotiques, anesthésiques, etc. Je vous ferai un bon prix si vous apportez "
"l'un de ces produits."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Independents/salvor_camp_solo.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Independents/salvor_camp_solo.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic Mercenary Guard for the ancilla hq.
#. ~ A generic mercenary for decorative purposes.
msgid "mercenary"
msgstr "mercenaire"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We'll protect our own, marshal."
msgstr "Nous protégerons les nôtres, marshal."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Make sure you don't get in trouble, officer."
msgstr "Assurez-vous de ne pas avoir d'ennuis, monsieur l'agent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't let me see you snooping around."
msgstr "Ne me laisse pas te voir fouiner."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay out of trouble, right?"
msgstr "Ne pas s'attirer d'ennuis, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How do you like that boot, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, oh, umm.  Yes, Sir?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nothing to report, Sir!"
msgstr "Rien à signaler!"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey boss."
msgstr "Salut boss."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Great to see you back in base."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Here's hoping I get out of guard duty soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Got anything good?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose d'intéressant?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "On an errand from the box?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Up and at them again?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Up for a drink when my shift ends?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well I can't complain much, money and free food for standing around with a "
"gun?\n"
"\n"
"Sure looks like a steal nowadays."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you don't have any business here, you better get going."
msgstr "Si vous n'avez rien à faire ici, vous feriez mieux de partir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Terminal is down there, please move along."
msgstr "Le terminal est en bas, veuillez avancer."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please head right down, scavenger."
msgstr "Descendez, s'il vous plaît, pilleur·se."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are you here to do anything?"
msgstr "Vous êtes ici pour faire quelque chose?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you are looking for the Terminal, it's in the first basement, right down "
"the stairs and to the left."
msgstr ""
"Si vous cherchez le terminal, il se trouve au premier sous-sol, en bas des "
"escaliers et à gauche."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way I can join your team?"
msgstr "Il y a moyen pour moi de rejoindre votre équipe?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Me?  Just standing around, looking scary.  Think I'm doing a good job?\n"
"\n"
"Don't answer that."
msgstr ""
"Moi ? Je reste là, à avoir l'air effrayant. Tu penses que je fais du bon "
"boulot ?\n"
"\n"
"Ne répondez pas à cette question."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just making sure people don't ask stupid questions."
msgstr "Je fait juste en sorte que personne ne pose des questions stupides."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm just on watch, move along."
msgstr "Je suis juste de garde, circulez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Getting paid for standing around.  And you are getting in the way."
msgstr ""
"Je reçois ma paie lorsque je reste debout et aux aguets, et vous êtes en "
"train de gênez ça."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A few of us joined up to make this a safe house, and it's just my turn "
"watching the gates."
msgstr ""
"Quelques-uns d'entre nous se sont associés pour faire de cette maison un lieu "
"sûr, et c'est à mon tour de surveiller les portes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Just go down to the Terminal if you want in."
msgstr "Dirigez vous juste vers le Terminal si vous voulez entrer."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/NPC_ANCILLA_HQ_GUARD.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well you certainly look like you could.  Try ringing the box in the bunker "
"across the street, or see if someone in the Terminal has a need for help."
msgstr ""
"Vous avez l'air de pouvoir le faire. Essayez d'appeler la boîte du bunker de "
"l'autre côté de la rue, ou voyez si quelqu'un dans le terminal a besoin "
"d'aide."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Offer to buy the anchor for 1 HGC."
msgstr "Offrez d'acheter l'ancre pour 2 POH."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, what's that thing for anyways?"
msgstr "D'ailleurs, à quoi sert ce truc ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, I don't think I can help you."
msgstr "Désolé(e), je ne pense pas que je peux vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, see you around then."
msgstr "Je vous verrai plus tard dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Take the anchor."
msgstr "Prendre l'ancre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Take the anchor and leave the coin.  Do we have a deal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_anchor_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just leave, this isn't right at all."
msgstr "Partez, ce n'est pas bien du tout."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&A pair of veteran mercenaries share stories between bouts of heavy drinking. "
" You could probably join them if you wanted to."
msgstr ""
"Une paire de mercenaires vétérans en train de partager des histoires entre "
"des tournées de liqueur forte. Vous pourriez probablement vous joindre à eux "
"si vous le vouliez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Join and hear them out for a while.]"
msgstr "[Joignez-vous à eux et écoutez-les pour un moment.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Join them in their heavy drinking.]"
msgstr "[Joignez-vous à leur beuverie.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Join them with a story of your own.]"
msgstr "[Joignez-vous à eux et racontez-leur une de vos histoires.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Just move along.]"
msgstr "(Passez votre chemin.)"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The veterans seem happy to have you, and you listen as the older mercenary "
"narrates <merc_story>.\n"
"\n"
"You all share some drinks while going over the details and as the "
"conversation winds down."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You share increasingly embellished stories about your exploits as you dare "
"each other into downing series of eye-watering drinks."
msgstr ""
"Vous vous racontez des histoires de plus en plus enjolivées sur vos exploits "
"et vous vous mettez au défi d'avaler des séries de boissons qui vous mettent "
"l'eau à la bouche."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Bar… barshender!  We… we?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&As you sit, the older mercenary continues their narration of <merc_story>.\n"
"\n"
"When their tale reaches conclusion, you stop to consider what sort of story "
"you could tell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Recall that time when you rescued a farmer's son from a citadel full of alien "
"horrors."
msgstr ""
"Remémorez la fois où vous avez secouru le fils d'un fermier d'une citadelle "
"remplie d'horreurs d'un autre monde."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell them about your hunting of a pyramidal robot using a prototype energy "
"rifle."
msgstr ""
"Racontez-leur la fois où vous avez chassé une sorte de robot pyramidal avec "
"un prototype de fusil à énergie."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Recall the time you were tricked into fighting against distorted versions of "
"yourself while lost in a place beyond time."
msgstr ""
"Remémorez la fois où vous avez forcé(e) à combattre des versions de "
"vous-mêmes distordues perdu(e) au milieu d'un endroit au-delà du temps et de "
"l'espace."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell about your slaying of an insectile horror after getting trapped within "
"its lair."
msgstr "Racontez votre combat dans la tanière d'une horreur insectoïde. "

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Recall the long story of how you agreed to help the remnants of the Federal "
"Government."
msgstr ""
"Remémorez la longue histoire de comment et pourquoi vous avez décidé d'aider "
"les vestiges du Gouvernement Fédéral."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell them about the horrors uncovered by the mining expeditions of New "
"England."
msgstr ""
"Dites-leur quelles sortes d'horreurs les équipes de mineurs de la Nouvelle "
"Angleterre ont rencontré."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell them about the horrors wandering in these very same subway tunnels."
msgstr ""
"Dites-leur quel genre d'horreurs rôdent dans les tunnels de métro des grandes "
"villes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Recall that time when you used a tactical nuclear weapon."
msgstr "Remémorez la fois ou vous avez utilisé une arme nucléaire tactique."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Try to gross each other out with tales of mutant butchery."
msgstr ""
"Essayez de vous dégouter les uns les autres avec des histoires de dissections "
"de mutant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Speak about the alien construct you found while lost in an endless sea of "
"black glass."
msgstr ""
"Parlez de le structure étrange que vous avez trouvé, perdu dans un océan "
"infini de verre noir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell them the story of how you were trapped in an infinitely looping "
"corridor, fighting the warped remnants of the researchers there and somehow "
"the damned corridor itself.  And at the end of the day, you're not even sure "
"the headache was worth it."
msgstr ""
"Racontez leur comment vous vous êtes retrouvé·e piégée dans un couloir infini "
"à combattre ce qui restait des chercheurs aussi coincés à l'intérieur ainsi "
"que d'une manière ou d'une autre le couloir même.  Et au final vous n'êtes "
"pas vraiment sûr·e si tout ça valait la migraine énorme que cela vous a causé."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Tell them the story of how you dived into and were forced to fight for your "
"life within a disgusting, toxic hellscape made from the un-living innards of "
"some crushed zombie monstrosity.  All so the intercom could have some damned "
"HDD back."
msgstr ""
"Racontez-leur comment vous avez plongé et avez été forcé de lutter pour votre "
"vie dans un paysage d'enfer dégoûtant et toxique, fait des entrailles non "
"vivantes d'une monstruosité zombie écrasée. Tout cela pour que l'interphone "
"puisse récupérer un maudit disque dur."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[LIE] Just make something up."
msgstr "[MENTIR] Vous inventez juste quelque chose."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&While the veterans indulge your storytelling, they clearly seem not too "
"pleased nor impressed by your tale."
msgstr ""
"&Bien que les vétérans se prêtent à votre récit, ils ne semblent "
"manifestement pas très satisfaits ni impressionnés par votre histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, ugh…  I should be going now…"
msgstr "Bon ben, bleurgh… Je devrais y aller…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You make some small talk and share a pair of drinks after finishing your "
"story."
msgstr ""
"&Vous faites un brin de causette et partagez une paire de verres après avoir "
"terminé votre histoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The clearly drunk mercenaries hail you as minor celebrity and invite you to "
"a pair of rounds when your tale is finished."
msgstr ""
"&Les mercenaires, manifestement ivres, vous saluent comme une petite "
"célébrité et vous invitent à une paire de rondes lorsque votre récit est "
"terminé."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah I guess it really did happen just like that."
msgstr "Oui, je suppose que c'est vraiment arrivé comme ça."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The veterans eagerly accept your challenge, and none of you can really "
"stomach the prospect of more drinks after the first pair of tales."
msgstr ""
"&Les vétérans acceptent volontiers votre défi, et aucun d'entre vous ne peut "
"vraiment supporter la perspective d'autres boissons après la première paire "
"d'histoires."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The expressions on both the mercs' faces are a mix of confusion and visceral "
"disgust as you relate your tale.  Finally, the younger mercenary blurts out, "
"\"None of us wanted to touch that contract since the intercom was being so "
"shifty about it.\"  \"You're my kind of free-range lunatic!\"  The older "
"mercenary interjects.  \"I'll drink to that!\"."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, that was certainly an…  interesting experience."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The veteran's expressions turn to a mixture of awe and fear as your tale "
"nears conclusion, the younger mercenary is finally after a long  \"We heard "
"someone had gone and completed that death trap contract, but I still couldn't "
"believe it.\"  \"You're a damn madman!\"  The older mercenary interjects in "
"agreement.  \"I'll drink to that!\"."
msgstr ""
"&L'expression du vétéran se transforme en un mélange d'admiration et de peur "
"à mesure que votre récit approche de sa conclusion, le plus jeune mercenaire "
"est finalement après un long \"Nous avons entendu que quelqu'un était allé "
"remplir ce contrat de piège mortel, mais je n'arrivais toujours pas à y "
"croire\". \"Vous êtes un sacré fou !\" Le mercenaire le plus âgé intervient "
"en signe d'approbation. \"Je vais boire à ça !\"."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah looking back I really don't know why I did it."
msgstr "Avec le recul, je ne sais vraiment pas pourquoi je l'ai fait."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_chatting_veterans.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC
#. "EOC_BEM_BEM_CHATTING_VETERANS_DRUNK_MESSAGE"
msgid "<ANCILLA_BAR_HANGOVER>"
msgstr "<ANCILLA_BAR_HANGOVER>"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_drugs.json
#. ~ Job description of "Mercenary" NPC class
msgid "Drug running for the name of Hub 01 and money, mostly money."
msgstr ""
"Transporte des drogues et produits chimiques au service d'Hub 01 et de "
"l'argent, principalement pour l'argent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_drugs.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, let see what you offer."
msgstr "Voyons ce que vous avez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#. ~ Job description of "Mercenary" NPC class
msgid "Fighting for the name of Hub 01 and money, mostly money."
msgstr "Combat au service d'Hub 01 et de l'argent, principalement pour l'argent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You find the gun runner intently assessing the swirling smoke of a stale "
"cigarette.  <mypronoun> barely acknowledges your approach.  \"Let's cut it "
"short, I have come upon an excess supply of exotic weaponry and let's say "
"that it would be expedient for it to disappear and you seem like just the "
"kind of person I'm looking for.\" .\n"
"\n"
"<mypronoun> hands you an inventory list, loosely annotated in a piece of "
"graph paper.\n"
"\n"
"\"No harm in looking right?"
msgstr ""
"&Vous trouvez le porteur d'arme en train d'évaluer intensément la fumée "
"tourbillonnante d'une cigarette éventée. <mypronoun> reconnaît à peine votre "
"approche. \"Pour faire court, je suis tombé sur un surplus d'armes exotiques "
"et disons qu'il serait opportun qu'elles disparaissent et vous semblez être "
"exactement le genre de personne que je recherche.\".\n"
"\n"
"<mypronoun> vous remet une liste d'inventaire, vaguement annotée sur une "
"feuille de papier millimétré.\n"
"\n"
"\"Il n'y a pas de mal à regarder, n'est-ce pas ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_gunrunner.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, let's see what you have to offer."
msgstr "Bien sûr, voyons ce que vous avez à offrir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm just looking for my next job.  So if you can't help with that, I rather "
"we be on our own separate ways."
msgstr ""
"Je cherche juste mon prochain emploi. Si vous ne pouvez pas m'aider, je "
"préfère que nous suivions chacun notre chemin."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well then, what does it cost to hire you."
msgstr "Dans ce cas-là, que me couterait-il de vous embaucher?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ha I prefer the cheerful sort anyways."
msgstr "Ha, je préfère le genre joyeux de toute façon."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well whatever."
msgstr "Peu importe."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_hireable.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[12 HGC] You have a deal."
msgstr "[12 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Fleshmonger"
msgstr "Marchand de chair"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Fleshmonger"
msgid ""
"Deposit a human sample in a pit within the dead drop location.  Pick up your "
"reward at the Terminal once that's done."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not in the mood for a talk, sorry."
msgstr "Je ne suis pas d'humeur à discuter, désolé."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh yes.  I actually have one right here."
msgstr "Oh, oui. En fait, j'en ai un ici même."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might be."
msgstr "C'est possible."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, but I might be looking to buy some."
msgstr "Non, mais il ce peut que je sois intéressé(e) à en acheter."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, not at all."
msgstr "Non, pas du tout."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Most I can give is two gold coins.  I've arranged a drop in the nearby woods, "
"put the goods there and you can get your cash with the barkeep here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It'll get done."
msgstr "Cela se fera."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not interested after all?"
msgstr "Vous n'êtes finalement pas intéressé ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 HGC] Its a deal."
msgstr "[5 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, just let me find the cash."
msgstr "Absolument, donnez-moi juste un peu pour trouver l'argent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No deal."
msgstr "Pas d'accord."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_human_sample.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<mypronoun> quickly removes the offending piece of meat from your hand and "
"places two golden coins on the table, apparently unshaken by the prospect of "
"meeting someone who casually visits bars while carrying cuts of human flesh.  "
"\"Now if you please, I have a meal to get rid of.\" <mypronoun> says, between "
"poorly masked bouts of nausea."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "\"God\"-Slayer"
msgstr "Tueur de \"Dieu\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Description of mission ""God"-Slayer"
msgid ""
"A traumatized mercenary has claimed to have seen what you assume to be a "
"powerful monster.  Maybe you should investigate this for the benefit of "
"everyone."
msgstr ""
"Un mercenaire traumatisé affirme avoir vu ce que vous supposez être un "
"monstre puissant. Peut-être devriez-vous enquêter pour le bien de tous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You see one more traumatized face, all too many and too frequent for any "
"help to be worthwhile."
msgstr ""
"&Vous voyez un visage traumatisé de plus, tous trop nombreux et trop "
"fréquents pour qu'une aide soit utile."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Attempt a friendly approach."
msgstr "Tentez une approche amicale."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Leave the traveler to their trauma."
msgstr "Laissez le voyageur à son traumatisme."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&<mypronoun> seems completely lost to the present, but you can't help but "
"notice <mypossesivepronoun> gear is caked with mud and broken twigs.  It "
"doesn't look like you'll be getting much conversation from this one."
msgstr ""
"&<mypronoun> semble complètement perdu dans le présent, mais vous ne pouvez "
"pas vous empêcher de remarquer que l'équipement de <mypronoun> est couvert de "
"boue et de brindilles cassées. Vous n'avez pas l'air d'avoir beaucoup de "
"conversation avec lui."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Press on in search of a reaction."
msgstr "Poursuivre la recherche d'une réaction."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Try to find someone more interested in conversation."
msgstr "Essayez de trouver quelqu'un de plus intéressé par la conversation."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Show your map to the mercenary, and have them mark where they saw this "
"\"god\"."
msgstr ""
"Montrez votre carte au mercenaire et demandez-lui de marquer l'endroit où il "
"a vu ce \"dieu\"."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah I'm sure I have seen that one too.  Try to stay safe."
msgstr "Oui, je suis sûr que j'ai vu celle-là aussi. Essayez de rester en sécurité."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_jabberwock.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&<mypronoun> silently points at your maps with a trembling hand."
msgstr "&<mypronoun> pointe silencieusement vos cartes d'une main tremblante."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] Its a deal."
msgstr "[4 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Offer to buy them for 2 coins."
msgstr "Offrir de l'acheter pour 2 pièces."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Huh where do you get those from"
msgstr "Vous les avez trouvées où?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure whatever, two coins and its all yours."
msgstr "Ok, peu importe, donnez-moi deux pièces et c'est à vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] Its a deal then."
msgstr "[2 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, it looks like I don't actually have two coins right now…"
msgstr "Oh, il semblerait que je n'aie pas deux pièces pour l'instant…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "See you around then."
msgstr "À bientôt donc."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well that'd be telling.  Suffice to say that a few friends found them, and "
"none of us are into the lab-dive business."
msgstr ""
"Je garde mes sources secrètes, disons juste que quelques amis et moi les ont "
"trouvées quelque part et qu'aucun d'entre nous ne veut risquer sa peau dans "
"un laboratoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_keycard_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Not a bargain bin kid, the price's the price."
msgstr "Pas de marchandage, le prix nommé est le prix point barre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 HGC] It's a deal."
msgstr "[3 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Offer to buy it for 2 coins."
msgstr "Offrir de l'acheter pour 2 pièces."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't even know what that is."
msgstr ""
"Je ne sais même pas ce que cette chose est, pourquoi est-ce que je payerais "
"autant pour l'avoir?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure whatever, two coins and it's all yours."
msgstr "Ok, peu importe, donnez moi juste deux pièces et tout est à vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] It's a deal then."
msgstr "[2 POH] Marché conclu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"A 'nanofabricator template', it seems, no idea what it's good for, but it "
"sure looks valuable.  Are you buying it or not?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/BEM_template_seller.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well I'm sure someone who values it will come around, thanks for hearing the "
"pitch anyways."
msgstr ""
"Je suis sûr que quelqu'un qui l'apprécie viendra, mais merci de m'avoir "
"écouté."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ These are all random people you met in a bar once, the fact that they
#. don't have names is meant to emphasize the transient nature of the
#. conversations you have with them
msgid "the enterprising gunrunner"
msgstr "le trafiquant d'armes entreprenant"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ EOC-specific, should not spawn outside of trigger events.
msgid "cyborg rescue"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ EOC-specific, should not spawn outside of trigger events.
msgid "kicking cyborg"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the drinking veteran"
msgstr "le buveur vétéran"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the pill pusher"
msgstr "le trafiquant de pilules"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the traumatized traveler"
msgstr "le voyageur traumatisé"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the shady mercenary"
msgstr "le mercenaire louche"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the disconsolate mercenary"
msgstr "le mercenaire inconsolable"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the cheerful mercenary"
msgstr "le mercenaire joyeux"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_ancilla_npcs/BAR_ENCOUNTER_MERCENARIES/NPC_BEMS.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
msgid "the ID forger"
msgstr "le faussaire"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Andrea Dzvonko"
msgstr "Andrea Dzvonko"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
msgid "software engineer"
msgstr "ingénieure en logiciel"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Andrea Dzvonko is a software engineer with a limited understanding of how
#. melchior actually functions.
msgid "Hub 01 Software Engineer"
msgstr "Ingénieure en Logiciel d'Hub 01"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 Software Engineer" NPC class
#. ~ Andrea Dzvonko is a software engineer with a limited understanding of how
#. melchior actually functions.
msgid "I work for Hub 01 as a software engineer."
msgstr "Je travaille pour Hub 01 en tant qu'ingénieure en logiciel."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Woah, you must be that new person they told us about.  I can't really believe "
"you're here.  I'm Andrea.  Dr. Dzvonko in the old days, but that seems silly "
"now."
msgstr ""
"Woah, tu dois être la nouvelle personne dont ils nous ont parlé. Je n'arrive "
"pas à croire que vous êtes ici. Je m'appelle Andrea. Dr. Dzvonko dans le "
"temps, mais ça semble idiot maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who the fuck are you?  How did you get down here?  Security!"
msgstr "Who the fuck are you? How did you get down here? Security!"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hold on, hold on.  I'm not here to hurt anyone, and there aren't enough of us "
"left to just start fighting."
msgstr ""
"Attendez, attendez. Je ne suis pas là pour faire du mal à qui que ce soit, et "
"nous ne sommes pas assez nombreux pour commencer à nous battre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Andrea_Dzvonko.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you too."
msgstr "Je suis aussi enchanté·e de faire votre connaissance."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Darla Novak"
msgstr "Darla Novak"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
msgid "building maintenance"
msgstr "entretien des bâtiments"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Keeps melchior from boiling to death and you from
#. choking on stale bunker air.
msgid "Hub 01 HVAC maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 HVAC maintenance" NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Keeps melchior from boiling to death and you from
#. choking on stale bunker air.
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 Server Maintenance" NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Resident dungeon master.
msgid "I'm part of Hub 01's maintenance crew."
msgstr "Je fait partie de l'équipe de maintenance d'Hub 01."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Darla_Novak.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, hey.  The rumors were true, there really is someone new around.  Nice to "
"meet you, call me Darla."
msgstr ""
"Oh, hey. Les rumeurs étaient vraies, il y a vraiment quelqu'un de nouveau "
"dans le coin. Enchanté, appelez-moi Darla."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Jonathan Farrier"
msgstr "Jonathan Farrier"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "assistant"
msgstr "assistant"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Trucker and now general handyman.  Used to work as a cargo driver for a
#. company supplying Hub 01, is only inside the lab by chance.
msgid "Hub 01 Assistant"
msgstr "Assistant d'Hub 01"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ Job description of "Hub 01 Assistant" NPC class
#. ~ Trucker and now general handyman.  Used to work as a cargo driver for a
#. company supplying Hub 01, is only inside the lab by chance.
msgid "I do miscellaneous jobs within Hub 01."
msgstr "J'accomplit des tâches diverses à l'intérieur d'Hub 01."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Jonathan_Farrier.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aw, hey, you must be that new blood runnin' jobs up top.  So, they finally "
"let you down, eh?  My name's Jon, Jon Farrier.  Nice to meet you, real nice."
msgstr ""
"Aw, hey, vous devez être le nouveau sang qui fait tourner la machine au "
"sommet. Alors, ils t'ont finalement laissé tomber, hein ? Je m'appelle Jon, "
"Jon Farrier. Ravi de vous rencontrer, vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
msgid "Sunil Narayana"
msgstr "Sunil Narayana"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "server maintenance"
msgstr "entreteneur de serveurs"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ HVAC maintenance.  Resident dungeon master.
msgid "Hub 01 Server Maintenance"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_basement_npcs/NPC_Sunil_Narayana.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oooh, the NEW person.  So, you're not just some rumor they cooked up as a "
"team building exercise.  I'm Sunil, welcome to the underground."
msgstr ""
"Oooh, la NOUVELLE personne. Donc, tu n'es pas juste une rumeur qu'ils ont "
"inventée pour renforcer l'esprit d'équipe. Je suis Sunil, bienvenue dans le "
"métro."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "the intercom"
msgstr "l'intercom"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Refusal reason for a shop item group
msgid "You're not yet qualified to buy this"
msgstr "Vous n'êtes pas encore qualifié(e) pour acheter ceci"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Refusal reason for a shop item group
msgid "You need to earn an HWP first"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin d'obtenir une HWP avant cela"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Reason for a shopkeeper blacklist entry
msgid "Will not buy back their own gear"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom is silent."
msgstr "L'intercom reste silencieux."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom crackles on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom's red LED blinks on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom says something unintelligible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&An intercom is embedded into the wall here, just next to the card reader.  "
"It's a metal box about as big as a dinner plate, with a speaker shaped like a "
"downwards curve and a large camera prominently featured in the center.  You "
"see a single metal button with a dark LED next to it.  The intercom is silent."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Identify yourself before the intercom.]"
msgstr "[Identifiez-vous devant l'intercom.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Press the button.]"
msgstr "[Appuyer sur le bouton.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Bang on the metal door.]"
msgstr "[Frapper la porte en métal.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hello again.  Brought us anything good?"
msgstr "Rebonjour. Vous avez quelque chose pour nous?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh, hi.  Doing okay?"
msgstr "Euh, bonjour. Vous allez bien?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How's that armor working?"
msgstr "Comment fonctionne cette armure ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sorry, I didn't catch that."
msgstr "Désolé, je n'avais pas compris."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "-ello?  Hello?\"  [Thump thump.]  \"Oh, there we go."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The voice on the intercom is humming a tune."
msgstr "&La voix de l'interphone fredonne un air."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What's up with the interference in this thing?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qui se passe avec les interférences dans ce truc ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Speak slowly and clearly.  Please."
msgstr "Veuillez parler lentement et clairement s'il vous plaît."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Say again?"
msgstr "Répétez?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, do you need something?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yes, mercenary?"
msgstr "Oui mercenaire?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Mercenary."
msgstr "Mercenaire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Say it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Get with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Make it quick."
msgstr "Faite vite."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't loiter."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't do anything stupid."
msgstr "Ne faites pas quelque chose stupide."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ugh, I hate intercom duty… oh, um.  Hello."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please don't bother us senselessly."
msgstr "Veuillez ne pas nous déranger sans raison."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If/you speak to/understand… you/me. Yes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's discuss contracts."
msgstr "Discutons de contrats."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything fancier you can sell?"
msgstr "Vous vendez des choses plus intéressantes?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's discuss prototypes."
msgstr "Discutons de prototypes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The traders at the refugee center asked me to deliver this drive of FEMA data…"
msgstr ""
"Les commerçants du centre de réfugiés m'ont demandé de leur remettre ce "
"disque de données de la FEMA…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned portal storms.  What are those?"
msgstr ""
"Vous avez mentionné des tempêtes dimensionnelles.  Qu'est ce qu'elles sont "
"exactement?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Listen, something happened earlier.  The world got… bad.  Things felt very "
"wrong.  Do you know anything about what that was?"
msgstr ""
"Écoutez, il s'est passé quelque chose tout à l'heure.  Le monde est devenu… "
"contre nature.  Les choses allaient très mal.  Vous savez ce que c'était?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have some portal storm recordings."
msgstr "J'ai des enregistrements de tempête dimensionnelle."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have found more of those golden robots, can you make anything of them yet?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What the hell were you testing out there?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce que vous étiez en train de tester là-bas?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your scientist was wearing some kind of armor.  What is it?"
msgstr "Votre scientifique portait une sorte d'armure. Qu'est-ce que c'est ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I found this in the collapsed tower with the other data.  Is it useful to "
"your people?  [Hand over the UHMWPE nanofabricator template.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I saw that your mercs have specialty rifles.  Would I be able to get one of "
"those?"
msgstr ""
"J'ai vu que vous mercenaires ont des fusils spéciaux. Est ce qu'il serait "
"possible que j'en reçoive un?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think one of your operatives has vouched for my competency.  I'd like one "
"of those rifles."
msgstr ""
"Je crois que l'un de vos agents s'est porté garante de mon niveau de "
"compétence. J'aimerais l'un de ces fusils."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, about that protective gear?"
msgstr "Au sujet de cette tenue de protection?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mentioned you had a map of the area?"
msgstr "Vous avez mentionné que vous aviez une carte des environs?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I need some gear to outfit my crew, I think five sets of police riot armor "
"would do the trick."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm here and I've got the goods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cost of the armor plus everything left in the tower."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom crackles with static as it turns on.  The LED next to the "
"button lights up a bright red, and the camera lens whirs as it focuses on "
"you.  There is no immediate response."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Hello?"
msgstr "…Bonjour?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Um, can anyone hear me?"
msgstr "Euh, quelqu'un m'entend?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Tap the camera lens.]  Look, I know someone's listening.  What is this place?"
msgstr ""
"[Tapoter la lentille de caméra.] Ok, je sais que quelqu'un est en train "
"d'écouter, qu'est-ce que cet endroit?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The merchant at the refugee center sent me.  You were looking for a hard "
"drive from them?"
msgstr ""
"Le marchand du centre de réfugiés m'a envoyé(e). Vous leur aviez demandé un "
"certain disque dur?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that hard drive…"
msgstr "Au sujet du disque dur…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The traders mentioned you were looking for help."
msgstr ""
"Les marchands ont mentionné que vous étiez à la recherche  de personnes pour "
"accomplir certaines choses pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom hisses.  A voice of indeterminate sex speaks flatly.  \"I don't "
"know who you are or how you got to this location, but we have nothing to gain "
"from one another.  If you have a reason to be here, then please state your "
"business.  Otherwise, please leave the area.\""
msgstr ""
"&L'interphone siffle. Une voix de sexe indéterminé s'exprime platement. \"Je "
"ne sais pas qui vous êtes ni comment vous êtes arrivés ici, mais nous n'avons "
"rien à gagner l'un de l'autre. Si vous avez une raison d'être ici, veuillez "
"en faire part. Sinon, veuillez quitter les lieux.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a delivery from the Free Merchants.  You requested a hard drive from "
"them."
msgstr "J'ai une livraison des Marchands Libres, vous leur avez demandé un disque dur."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wait, what?"
msgstr "Attendez, quoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You do realize that the front door is just open?"
msgstr "Vous vous rendez compte que la porte d'entrée est ouverte?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's the apocalypse out here!  Please just let me in!"
msgstr "C'est l'apocalypse ici ! S'il vous plaît, laissez-moi entrer !"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm just looking for valuables.  Maybe we can trade?"
msgstr "Je cherche juste des objets de valeur. On peut peut-être faire un échange ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Look, there must be something we can work out."
msgstr "Ecoutez, il doit bien y avoir quelque chose que nous pouvons trouver."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well truth be told, this encounter ain't quite so random."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I promise you, there is nothing you can do for us.  Now leave, before I'm "
"forced to-\"  They stop suddenly.  You hear a short, muffled conversation "
"from the other end.  There's a brief pause.  \"Alright.  We might be able to "
"gain some mutual benefit.  It's a dangerous task, but if you complete it then "
"we would be willing to open up limited trading access."
msgstr ""
"Je vous promets qu'il n'y a rien que vous puissiez faire pour nous. "
"Maintenant, partez, avant que je ne sois obligé de...\" Ils s'arrêtent "
"brusquement. On entend une courte conversation étouffée à l'autre bout du "
"fil. Il y a une brève pause. \"D'accord. Nous pourrions peut-être en tirer un "
"avantage mutuel. C'est une tâche dangereuse, mais si vous l'accomplissez, "
"nous serons prêts à vous ouvrir un accès commercial limité."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Risk my neck for the privilege of trading with you?  Maybe another time."
msgstr ""
"Risquez ma peau pour le privilège d'échanger avec vous? Peut être un autre "
"jour."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are listening…\n"
"\n"
"You detect a slight elevation in their voice, with a start you realize they "
"are nervous."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Actually I was just joking.  Our meeting is indeed a fortunate accident but "
"now that I have your attention would you be interested in trading in some "
"goods?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Some mercenaries I met mentioned this place, said its a good place to find "
"some work and possibly some valuable post-apocalyptic gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You guys aren't as slick as you think.  You think no one's gonna notice a "
"pristine looking meteorological station in the middle of nowhere with not a "
"potted plant out of place?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not without significantly advanced surveillance tech most of which were "
"either decommissioned or destroyed post cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Actually a bunch of high tech dudes HAVE scouted out this place and wanted me "
"to check it out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I am in tight with a bunch of inter-dimensional travellers who observed this "
"base and sent me out to investigate this place."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I see and do you have more information regarding these interested parties?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not really."
msgstr "Pas vraiment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Not much actually but I do know they have pretty sweet looking technology as "
"I saw them having advanced machinery everywhere.  Nothing like I've ever seen."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We need more information on these folks, we will be making covert visual "
"contact ourselves but for obvious reasons we can't get inside information "
"without alerting these guys.  That's where you come in…we want you to gather "
"as much information on these people without raising any suspicions and bring "
"it back to us.  Most importantly find who they are and why are they here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  I'll be back with the juicy details."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know man sounds kind of dangerous.  What can I expect in return?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Absolutely not, these guys are far more powerful than me and one wrong move "
"will get me killed, besides I'm no rat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Inter-dimensional travellers you say?  What kind of tech do these beings "
"operate?  And how were you able to communicate with them?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright listen up."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Information doesn't come cheap my friend."
msgstr "Les informations ne sont pas bon marché."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've said more than I ought to have.  I'm leaving."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii.  "
"These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated machinery "
"to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  They do understand English to a "
"certain extent and when talking they use a strange dialect they like to call "
"Anglic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii "
"and they use a mix of futuristic and ancient technology the latter being "
"mostly due to their last landing place being a ancient battlefield of some "
"sort.  These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated "
"machinery to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  While their choice for "
"personal defense was more along the lines of ancient gear like spears and "
"swords.  They do understand English to a certain extent and when talking they "
"use a strange dialect they like to call Anglic."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii.  "
"These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated machinery "
"to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  They do understand English to a "
"certain extent and when talking they use a strange dialect they like to call "
"Anglic.  They are here to mine this place of any useful metal, gather any "
"tech they deem worth saving and maybe even grab a couple of survivors to join "
"their ranks before they move out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"They are a race of inter-dimensional beings who call themselves the Exodii "
"and they use a mix of futuristic and ancient technology the latter being "
"mostly due to their last landing place being a ancient battlefield of some "
"sort.  These guys are more metal than man in my opinion and use automated "
"machinery to do their fighting and heavy lifting.  However their choice for "
"personal defense was more along the lines of ancient gear like spears and "
"swords.  They do understand English to a certain extent and when talking they "
"use a strange dialect they like to call Anglic.  They are here to mine this "
"place of any useful metal, gather any tech they deem worth saving and maybe "
"even grab a couple of survivors to join their ranks before they move out."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you for bringing this information to us…"
msgstr "Merci de nous fournir ces informations…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's talk reward."
msgstr "Parlons récompense."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"No problem, if you ask me to choose between us and cyborg tyrants, you best "
"believe I ain't betraying my race.  It's unnatural you know?  Please let me "
"know if there is anything else I can do for you guys."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"For your services rendered we can either offer you some riot gear armor or "
"the USP 9x19mm pistol with compatible magazines."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds equitable to me be back with that information in a jiff"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's too little for a whole lot of risk.  I'll pass on this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Deal!  Now listen close."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take the riot armor."
msgstr "J'aimerais l'armure anti-émeutes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take the USP."
msgstr "J'aimerais l'USP."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Ah its you.  Mind giving your fellow American information regarding possible "
"terrorist cyborgs?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know what?  I've changed my mind.  I'll do your dirty work.  Give me some "
"time to chat up these folks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Please… I stopped being an American the moment the government left us to fend "
"for ourselves."
msgstr ""
"S'il vous plaît… j'ai cessé d'être un·e américain·e le moment où notre "
"gouvernement nous a laissé nous débrouiller nous-même."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fine.  I'll tell you about these inter-dimensional beings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is something else that has come up on our side which requires some "
"field agents.  Would you like to hear about it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds like you have work for me?  Count me in."
msgstr "On dirait que vous avez du boulot pour moi?  Je suis partant·e."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe not right now."
msgstr "Peut-être pas maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Right.  Your handling of this situation was exemplary, and it's clear to us "
"that we greatly underestimated our potential for mutual benefit.  If you are "
"interested, we are willing to offer you more work going forward, and all of "
"it will have proper compensation from now on."
msgstr ""
"C'est vrai. Votre gestion de la situation a été exemplaire, et il est clair "
"pour nous que nous avons largement sous-estimé notre potentiel d'avantages "
"mutuels. Si vous êtes intéressé, nous sommes prêts à vous offrir plus de "
"travail à l'avenir, et tout cela sera rémunéré correctement à partir de "
"maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "And the trading we agreed on?"
msgstr "Et la permission d'échanger avec vous que vous m'aviez promise?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly.  I've just finished speaking with a certain individual, who has "
"authorized you limited access to a selection of our internal stores.  We will "
"provide you with pay for contracts in the form of tokens to be used as an "
"exchange currency, which you can then trade for goods.  We are also amenable "
"to bartering in exchange for supplies that are currently difficult for us to "
"obtain from outside the facility."
msgstr ""
"Certainement. Je viens de m'entretenir avec un certain individu, qui vous a "
"autorisé à avoir un accès limité à une sélection de nos magasins internes. "
"Nous vous fournirons des contrats rémunérés sous la forme de jetons à "
"utiliser comme monnaie d'échange, que vous pourrez ensuite échanger contre "
"des marchandises. Nous sommes également disposés à faire du troc en échange "
"de fournitures qu'il nous est actuellement difficile d'obtenir de l'extérieur."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll keep that in mind.  Let's get down to business."
msgstr "Je m'en souviendrai. Passons aux choses sérieuses."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We look forward to working with you."
msgstr "Nous nous réjouissons de travailler avec vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank you.  This might be of use benefit to us, but we will need at least a "
"day to read the contents of the template.  Please speak with us again once "
"we've had time."
msgstr ""
"Nous vous remercions. Cela pourrait nous être utile, mais nous aurons besoin "
"d'au moins une journée pour lire le contenu du modèle. Veuillez nous "
"recontacter une fois que nous aurons eu le temps de le faire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Very well."
msgstr "Très bien."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see you then."
msgstr "Je vous verrai alors."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom's tray wordlessly slides open."
msgstr "&Le plateau de l'interphone s'ouvre sans bruit."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom erupts into static.  Then, it resolves into a voice.  It clears "
"its throat, then speaks slowly and carefully.  \"Understood.  There is a tray "
"embedded beneath the intercom.  Please place the drive into it.\"  On cue, a "
"small portion of the wall beneath the intercom slides out along rails, "
"revealing a large tray several inches deep.  \"You are welcome to leave "
"afterwards.\""
msgstr ""
"&L'interphone devient statique. Puis une voix se fait entendre. Elle "
"s'éclaircit la gorge, puis parle lentement et prudemment. \"Compris. Il y a "
"un plateau encastré sous l'interphone. Veuillez y placer le lecteur.\" Au "
"moment voulu, une petite partie du mur sous l'interphone glisse le long de "
"rails, révélant un grand plateau de plusieurs centimètres de profondeur. "
"\"Vous pouvez partir après.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Hand over the FEMA data.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hold on, who are you?  And what do you want with the data?"
msgstr "Attendez, qui êtes-vous ? Et que voulez-vous faire de ces données ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What am I getting out of this?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que j'en retire ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, forgot to grab the drive.  I'll return with it."
msgstr "Désolé, j'ai oublié de prendre le disque. Je reviendrai avec."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Ask Gavin."
msgstr "Demandez à Gavin."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The tray slides shut.  \"Thank you.\"  The intercom turns off without "
"another word."
msgstr "&Le plateau se referme. \"Merci\". L'interphone s'éteint sans un mot de plus."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh!  Good.  We had written that off as a non-starter.  Just drop it into the "
"tray and we'll bring it in."
msgstr ""
"Oh ! Bien. Nous l'avions considéré comme un échec. Déposez-le dans le bac et "
"nous l'apporterons."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have the drive with me right now; I'll give it to you when I have it."
msgstr ""
"Je n'ai pas le disque avec moi en ce moment ; je vous le donnerai quand je "
"l'aurai."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you.  Was there anything else you needed?"
msgstr "Merci. Vous avez besoin de quoi que ce soit d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That question has… a complicated answer."
msgstr "Cette question a… une réponse compliquée."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to hear it."
msgstr "J'aimerais l'entendre."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Later, then."
msgstr "À plus tard dans ce cas-là."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Understand that I'm not an expert about this.\"  The voice sighs.  You hear "
"the person on the other side typing on a keyboard for several seconds.  \"I "
"will explain it as best I can, but again, I'm not a professional.  Whatever "
"caused the apocalypse, it… broke something about the way our world works.  "
"I'm sure you've noticed that 'normal' physics don't always apply anymore.  We "
"are, as of right now, uncertain if our models were wrong, or if this is "
"something fundamentally different to our reality.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"From what we've observed, these events are what happen at the peak of a "
"cyclical effect.  This is gross oversimplification, and I don't know the "
"science behind it, but… I guess the simplest way to think of it is that 'our' "
"reality is moving closer and further from this other place, or model, or so "
"on.  Like a yo-yo.  When these two things are closest together, we get portal "
"storms.  Otherwise, things are… I wouldn't say normal, not anymore, but they "
"are as close to normal as we get now.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Reading a footnote here… we're looking to gather data about these storms "
"using a device developed specifically for the purpose.  I'll add that to your "
"contracts list, if you want to know more about it."
msgstr ""
"\"Veuillez comprendre que je ne suis en aucun cas un expert sur ce sujet.\" "
"La voix soupire et vous pouvez entendre la personne de l'autre coté de "
"l'intercom taper sur un clavier pendant quelques secondes. \"Je vais essayer "
"de vous l'expliquer le mieux possible, mais de nouveau, je ne suis pas une "
"professionnelle. La chose qui à provoquée cette apocalypse, a... "
"fondamentalement brisé quelque chose dans le fonctionnement de notre réalité. "
"Je suis sûre que vous avez déjà pu vous rendre compte que les lois physiques "
"\"normales\" ne sont plus inviolables partout depuis. Nous sommes, pour "
"l'instant, incertains si nos modèles sont simplement erronés ou si quelque "
"chose de fondamental à été altéré par le Cataclysme.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"De ce que nous avons pu observer, ces \"tempêtes\" sont la manifestation "
"d'un effet cyclique. Ceci est une simplification grossière, et je ne sais pas "
"toute sur la science derrière cette conclusion, mais… je suppose que la façon "
"la plus facile de visualiser cela est d'imaginer que notre réalité se "
"rapproche et s'éloigne de ce qui a causé le Cataclysme - comme un yo-yo. "
"Lorsque les deux sont au plus proche, un tempête dimensionnelle se manifeste. "
"En temps normal, les choses restent, non, pas normales, cela n'est plus "
"possible maintenant, mais aussi normales que possible.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"On me dit que notre département de recherche aurait besoin d'un agent "
"extérieur pour relever des données lors d'une tempête dimensionnelle. "
"J'ajoute cela à la liste de contrats disponibles, au cas où cela vous "
"intéresse.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are there any warning signs?"
msgstr ""
"Y a-t-il des signes annonciateurs qu'une tempête est sur le point de se "
"déclencher?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there any way to stay safe during one?"
msgstr "Existe-t-il un moyen de rester en sécurité lors d'un tel événement ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That sounds pretty bad.  Is this going to get worse?"
msgstr "Cela semble assez grave. La situation va-t-elle empirer ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How can you know all this?"
msgstr "Comment pouvez-vous savoir tout cela ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything useful I could find in one of these storms?"
msgstr ""
"Il y a quelque chose d'utile que je pourrais trouver durant l'une de ces "
"tempêtes?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you for the information."
msgstr "Merci pour l'information."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"In a way.  In the days and hours leading up to one of these events, you may "
"see things that are obviously out of place, or that don't make sense.  This "
"is most clear during the nighttime, but you can see it during the day, too.  "
"If this happens once, take note of it.  If it happens again, be ready for "
"anything."
msgstr ""
"D'une certaine manière. Dans les jours et les heures qui précèdent l'un de "
"ces événements, vous pouvez voir des choses qui ne sont manifestement pas à "
"leur place ou qui n'ont pas de sens. C'est plus évident la nuit, mais vous "
"pouvez aussi le constater le jour. Si cela se produit une fois, prenez-en "
"note. Si cela se reproduit, soyez prêt à tout."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes and no.  When something like this is going on, the storm is going to "
"affect you one way or another, but being outside is much more dangerous.  If "
"you can, find a solid shelter.  Stay as far away from the outer walls as you "
"can.  Being underground is probably a good idea.  There are likely "
"undocumented psychological effects; use your best judgment and your common "
"sense."
msgstr ""
"Oui et non. Lorsqu'un tel événement se produit, la tempête vous affectera "
"d'une manière ou d'une autre, mais il est beaucoup plus dangereux d'être à "
"l'extérieur. Si vous le pouvez, trouvez un abri solide. Restez aussi loin que "
"possible des murs extérieurs. Il est probablement préférable d'être sous "
"terre. Il y a probablement des effets psychologiques non documentés ; faites "
"preuve de discernement et de bon sens."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, it seems likely.  This isn't exactly something we can measure "
"with traditional instruments, but observation has shown that they're not "
"likely to get better.  By far the strongest so far was at the start of the "
"Cataclysm, and while we cannot accurately predict what the future holds, our "
"projections are not optimistic.  I wish I could tell you anything else, but I "
"would advise you get used to seeing them going forward."
msgstr ""
"Malheureusement, cela semble probable. Ce n'est pas exactement quelque chose "
"que nous pouvons mesurer avec des instruments traditionnels, mais "
"l'observation a montré qu'ils ne sont pas susceptibles de s'améliorer. C'est "
"au début du cataclysme qu'elles ont été les plus fortes, et bien que nous ne "
"puissions pas prédire avec précision ce que l'avenir nous réserve, nos "
"prévisions ne sont pas optimistes. J'aimerais pouvoir vous dire autre chose, "
"mais je vous conseille de vous habituer à les voir à l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have a vested interest in determining how these events will influence the "
"future of the planet - as should you.  Most of the equipment inside of this "
"facility has remained in working order, and although the Internet no longer "
"exists in a functional way, we still have a plethora of information that was "
"stored locally prior to <the_cataclysm>.  We are monitoring and documenting "
"these portal storms, and we will continue to do so for the foreseeable future."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons un intérêt direct, tout comme vous, de déterminer comment ces "
"événements influencerons le futur de notre planète. La majorité de ce qui est "
"dans notre établissement à été préparé pour faire face à cette crise, et bien "
"que l'Internet ait disparu, nous avons accès à une quantité bien plus que "
"suffisante de données qui furent stockées avant le début du <the_cataclysm>. "
"Nous surveillons et analysons ces tempêtes de portail, et continuerons de "
"faire de même à l’avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Potentially.  We recently came into possession of a video taken during the "
"first days of <the_cataclysm> using a home camcorder.  We have ruled out "
"possible tampering, and conclude that the recording is legitimate.  It "
"depicts an entity that appeared to rapidly change shape, but responded "
"especially strongly to human presence.  Eventually, the entity reshaped "
"itself into a small object, which the author of the recording claimed had "
"anomalous properties.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Subsequent entities of this type have failed to manifest during remote "
"observation of the phenomenon.  We hypothesize that, if they do exist at all, "
"they may only appear in response to human presence.  While we consider the "
"hypothesis too dangerous and too uncertain to test using our own resources, "
"we would be eager to hear the results if you attempted to do so yourself."
msgstr ""
"Potentiellement. Nous sommes récemment entrés en possession d'une vidéo prise "
"au cours des premiers jours de <the_cataclysm> à l'aide d'un caméscope "
"domestique. Nous avons exclu toute possibilité de falsification et conclu que "
"l'enregistrement est légitime. Il montre une entité qui semble changer "
"rapidement de forme, mais qui réagit particulièrement fortement à la présence "
"humaine. Finalement, l'entité s'est transformée en un petit objet qui, selon "
"l'auteur de l'enregistrement, avait des propriétés anormales.\n"
"\n"
"\"Les entités de ce type qui ont suivi ne se sont pas manifestées lors de "
"l'observation à distance du phénomène. Nous émettons l'hypothèse que, si "
"elles existent, elles n'apparaissent qu'en réponse à une présence humaine. "
"Bien que nous considérions cette hypothèse comme trop dangereuse et trop "
"incertaine pour être testée avec nos propres ressources, nous serions "
"impatients d'entendre les résultats si vous tentiez de le faire vous-même."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've been working on specialized gear for potential agents in the field, "
"given the hardware we have available.  Given the risks we've observed from "
"here, it seemed astute.  It seems we still have some work to do."
msgstr ""
"Nous avons travaillé sur des équipements spécialisés pour les agents "
"potentiels sur le terrain, compte tenu du matériel dont nous disposons. Etant "
"donné les risques que nous avons observés d'ici, cela semblait astucieux. Il "
"semble que nous ayons encore du travail à faire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[INT 10] The pieces seemed warped.  Whatever you're using to reinforce the "
"armor isn't strong enough."
msgstr ""
"[INT 10] Les composants ont l'air déformés. Quoi que ce soit que vous "
"utilisez pour renforcer l'armure, ce n'est manifestement pas assez solide."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom goes quiet for a moment.  You hear a brief exchange on the "
"other end, and then the microphone squeals as the voice gets closer again.  "
"\"As additional payment for helping resolve the situation, feel free to keep "
"the modular defense system.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have "
"been iterating on supplementary pieces that we would be willing to trade to "
"you.\""
msgstr ""
"&L'interphone se tait un instant. Vous entendez un bref échange à l'autre "
"bout du fil, puis le microphone grince lorsque la voix se rapproche à "
"nouveau. \"En guise de paiement supplémentaire pour avoir aidé à résoudre la "
"situation, n'hésitez pas à garder le système de défense modulaire. La "
"plateforme d'armure de base est solide, et nous avons développé des pièces "
"supplémentaires que nous serions prêts à vous échanger.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've always wanted to be a lab rat."
msgstr "J'ai toujours voulu(e) être un rat de laboratoire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you say so."
msgstr "Si vous le dites."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've solved that issue with our more recent prototypes.\"  There is a brief "
"pause.  \"You seem like a good candidate.  We will transfer over the "
"additional pieces to complete that prototype set, with the goal of collecting "
"additional field data.  The core armor platform is solid, and we have been "
"iterating on supplementary pieces we would be willing to trade to you.  Any "
"feedback on their performance would be appreciated."
msgstr ""
"\"Nous avons trouvé une solution à ce problème avec nos prototypes plus "
"récents\" L'intercom pause pour un moment.  \"Vous avez l'air d'être un·e "
"candidat·e approprié·e.  Nous vous transférons les pièces additionnelles "
"complétant les pièces que vous possédez déjà, avec pour mission pour vous de "
"collecter plus de données sur le terrain.  Ce que vous possédiez déjà est "
"satisfaisant, et nous avons développé des pièces supplémentaires utilisant "
"les résultats que vous nous avez fournis comme inspiration que nous serions "
"disposés d'échanger avec vous.  Vos commentaires sur la performance de "
"celles-ci serait apprécié.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hopefully it serves me better than the good doctor."
msgstr "J'espère qu'il me servira mieux que le bon docteur."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We'll see what happens."
msgstr "Nous verrons ce qui se passera."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was a modified Wraitheon chassis, with a custom AI.  We'd hoped that it "
"would interact with the outside world for us, but you know how well that "
"went.  That particular line of study is now on hiatus, given that the project "
"lead… well, you know."
msgstr ""
"C'était un chassis Wraitheon modifié doté d'une IA customisée. Nous avions un "
"espoir de réussir à l'utiliser pour intéragir avec le monde extérieur pour "
"nous, mais vous savez bien que ceci ne s'est pas passé comme prévu. Cette "
"ligne d'étude est maintenant en hiatus, principalement par ce que la personne "
"en charge du projet est... morte."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right."
msgstr "Ok."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We have no other disposable equipment right now.  You'll have to come back in "
"<interval>."
msgstr ""
"Nous n'avons pas d'autre équipement jetable pour le moment. Vous devrez "
"revenir dans <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "No. Come back in <interval>."
msgstr "Non. Revenez dans <interval>."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What would you like to discuss?"
msgstr "De quoi voulez-vous discuter ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back from the convoy.  [Hand over the hard case.]"
msgstr "Je reviens du convoi. [Remettez la mallette.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm back from LIXA.  [Hand over the data.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I found it.  I found your template.  [Hand over the silicon photonics "
"template.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The weapon worked!  [Hand over the inactive trifacet.]"
msgstr "L'arme a fonctionnée! [Rendre le trifacette inactif.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I found the robot, but…  [Hand over the trifacet remains.]"
msgstr "J'ai trouvé le robot, mais… [Rendre le trifacette détruit.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Return to sender]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Light retrieval]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Iron Safari]"
msgstr "[Contrat: Safari Métallique]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Hazard Meteorology]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Contract: Data Retrieval]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I need a new NRE recorder."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'un nouvel enregistreur NRE."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any more work for me right now?"
msgstr "Vous avez des contrats pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Unfortunate, but not unfixable.  As before, we are willing to provide a "
"replacement in exchange for an NRE microphone."
msgstr ""
"C'est regrettable, mais ce n'est pas irrémédiable. Comme précédemment, nous "
"sommes prêts à fournir un remplacement en échange d'un microphone NRE."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hook me up.  [Hand over the NRE microphone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is an NRE microphone, and where can I find it?"
msgstr "Qu'est ce qu'un microphone de NRE, et où puis-je en trouver?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On second thought, I'll get back to you on that."
msgstr "Après réflexion, je reviendrai vers vous à ce sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The microphone is a static version of the same device used in the recorder, "
"mounted on a tripod.  The glass ampoule is larger, but should look roughly "
"the same in design.  They may be somewhat scarce given the current state of "
"the world, but I would advise you to look inside of research labs.  Subway "
"lines may be a good place to start."
msgstr ""
"Le microphone est une version statique du même dispositif que celui utilisé "
"dans l'enregistreur, monté sur un trépied. L'ampoule de verre est plus "
"grande, mais devrait avoir à peu près le même design. Elles sont peut-être un "
"peu rares étant donné l'état actuel du monde, mais je vous conseille de "
"chercher à l'intérieur des laboratoires de recherche. Les lignes de métro "
"peuvent être un bon point de départ."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You fold up the microphone's legs, stuff it awkwardly into the tray, and "
"slide it shut.  A few moments later, it slides open again, revealing a "
"replacement NRE recorder.\n"
"\n"
"\"Try not to lose this one.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Give me a moment to look at your file… here we are.  Valid assignments are "
"turning up empty at the moment.  I'm afraid we have no open contracts for you."
msgstr ""
"Laissez-moi le temps de consulter votre dossier… voilà.  Le système ne montre "
"aucune tâche disponible pour le moment.  Je crains que nous n'ayons pas de "
"contrats ouverts pour vous."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return Field Data"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Return Field Data"
msgid ""
"Investigate a nearby field and return with Dr. Prado and the robot prototype "
"she was testing.  Failing that, retrieve the I/O recorder stored within the "
"robot.  If the robot remains operational, avoid direct confrontation and use "
"EMP grenades to disable it."
msgstr ""
"Explorez un champ voisin et revenez avec le Dr. Prado et le prototype de "
"robot qu'elle testait. À défaut, récupérez l'enregistreur d'entrées/sorties "
"stocké dans le robot. Si le robot reste opérationnel, évitez la confrontation "
"directe et utilisez des grenades EMP pour le mettre hors d'état de nuire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One of our scientists recently left the building to perform a field test of a "
"prototype robot, but failed to return.  We have not been able to contact "
"them.  Your job would be to investigate the testing site, and return with her "
"and the prototype.  Failing that, return with the data recorder that was "
"attached to our prototype."
msgstr ""
"L'un de nos scientifiques a récemment quitté le bâtiment pour effectuer un "
"test sur le terrain d'un prototype de robot, mais n'est pas revenu. Nous "
"n'avons pas réussi à la contacter. Votre tâche consisterait à enquêter sur le "
"site d'essai et à revenir avec elle et le prototype. À défaut, revenez avec "
"l'enregistreur de données qui était attaché à notre prototype."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems trivial.  Is there a catch?"
msgstr "Cela à l'air trivial. Quel est le problème?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is.  If the robot is operational, it's very likely to be hostile and "
"extremely dangerous.  I don't recommend fighting it directly.  Dr. Prado left "
"the building with a handful of EMP grenades.  If you can locate those "
"grenades, use them to disable the prototype instead."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll do it.  Where is the test site?"
msgstr "Je vais le faire. Où se trouve le site d'essai ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Extremely dangerous?  What kind of danger should I expect?"
msgstr "Extrêmement dangereux?  À quel sorte de danger devraist-je m'attendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll pass on getting killed today, thanks."
msgstr "Je ne me ferai pas tuer aujourd'hui, merci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's built with experimental combat programming and some heavy-duty armor.  "
"Despite the armor, it's pretty nimble, so unless you've got a vehicle don't "
"expect to outrun it.  We decided to hold off on adding long-range weapons "
"until we finished the initial field testing, so if you can keep your "
"distance, you should be safe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can handle it.  Where is the test site?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'll pass."
msgstr "Je pense que je vais passer."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Very close by.\"  The voice lists off some relative coordinates.  \"Good luck."
msgstr "Très proche.\" La voix énumère des coordonnées relatives. \"Bonne chance."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're back.  Do you have anything to report?"
msgstr "Vous êtes de retour. Avez-vous quelque chose à signaler ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Your scientist was dead, but I disabled the prototype.  Is this what you were "
"looking for?  [Hand over the prototype I/O recorder.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not yet.  I'll get back to it."
msgstr "Pas encore.  Je m'y remets."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom is silent for a few seconds while the tray slides back in.  "
"\"Yes it is.  It's unfortunate that only the data was salvageable, but you "
"have our thanks for returning it nonetheless.\""
msgstr ""
"&L'interphone reste silencieux pendant quelques secondes, le temps que le "
"plateau se remette en place. \"Oui, c'est bien cela. Il est regrettable que "
"seules les données aient pu être récupérées, mais nous vous remercions de "
"nous les avoir rendues.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I've done my part.  What now?"
msgstr "Ok, j'ai fait ma part.  Qu'avez-vous pour moi?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Is \"unfortunate\" how you usually describe someone being eviscerated by a "
"robot?"
msgstr ""
"Est-ce que le mot \"regrettable\" est quelque chose que vous utilisez souvent "
"pour décrire l'éviscération de quelqu'un par un robot?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Dr. Prado knew the risks, and she chose to follow through with the test "
"anyway.  Her death is cause for sadness, and it will affect us, but you "
"didn't even know her.  At least now, something of her work will remain."
msgstr ""
"Le Dr Prado connaissait les risques, et elle a choisi de poursuivre le test "
"malgré tout. Sa mort nous attriste et nous affecte, mais vous ne l'avez même "
"pas connue. Au moins maintenant, quelque chose de son travail restera."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The voice hesitates.  \"About that.  Give me a moment.\"  After a pause, you "
"hear muffled back-and-forth conversation.  You can't make out what's being "
"said, but you can make out at least two other distinct voices."
msgstr ""
"&La voix hésite. \"A ce propos. Donnez-moi un moment.\" Après une pause, vous "
"entendez une conversation étouffée qui va et vient. Vous ne pouvez pas "
"comprendre ce qui se dit, mais vous pouvez distinguer au moins deux autres "
"voix distinctes."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Return to sender"
msgstr "Retour à l'expéditeur"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Return to sender"
msgid ""
"Find the corpse of a Hub 01's AI researcher and retrieve the hard case they "
"brought with them during the evacuation."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez le cadavre d'un chercheur en IA du Hub 01 et récupérez la mallette "
"qu'il avait emportée avec lui lors de l'évacuation."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"When the portal storms started, the government issued an evacuation order for "
"critical personnel and sent convoys to retrieve them, with our head of AI "
"research among the recalled.  We recently discovered that he died when the "
"convoy transferring him was ambushed in the initial chaos, but his corpse and "
"belongings might remain intact enough to benefit from his research.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We want you to travel to the convoy and locate the body, if possible.  His "
"evacuation protocol included retrieving and storing as much of the data from "
"his facility as possible, to be stored in a code-locked hard case.  If this "
"hard case is present, retrieve it, and bring it back here.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We offer the standard hazard pay of 4 HGC for this contract."
msgstr ""
"\"Lors ce que les tempêtes dimensionnelles ont commencées, le gouvernement a "
"donné un ordre d'évacuation pour des personnes d'importance critiques et a "
"envoyé des convois armés pour les sécuriser, parmi eux, notre chef de "
"recherche sur les IA. Nous avons récemment appris que celui-ci est mort lors "
"ce que son convoi a souffert une ambuche durant le chaos initial, mais son "
"corps et ses affaires personnelles sont probablement toujours assez intacts "
"pour nous permettre d'accéder aux données de sa recherche.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous voulons que vous vous déplaciez jusqu'à ce convoi et localisiez son "
"corps si possible. Le protocole d'évacuation avait comme ordre pour lui de "
"rassembler autant de données que possibles de son laboratoire avant d'être "
"escorter, et de l'entroposer dans une valise sécurisée. Si cette valise est "
"toujours sur les lieux, ramenez-la à nous.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous sommes prêts à vous payer 4 POH pour ce contrat, en accordance avec "
"notre prime de risque standard.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take it.  Where's the convoy?"
msgstr "J'accepte le contrat. Où est le convoi?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What should I expect to go up against?"
msgstr "À quoi devrais-je m'attendre?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who was this person, and what do they look like?"
msgstr "Qui était cette personne, et à quoi ressemblait-elle?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What else do you have available?"
msgstr "Vous avez quelque chose d'autre de disponible?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The convoy was composed of vehicles and personnel from the US Army, and it "
"was heavily armed.  Our surveillance of the area has shown that the majority "
"of the slain military personnel have revived, including one wearing a light "
"combat exoskeleton.  Resistance will be heavy, but if possible, you may be "
"able to locate and retrieve the hard case, then exfiltrate without direct "
"combat as long as you can outpace the undead there.  Otherwise, bring a rifle "
"and plenty of ammo."
msgstr ""
"Le convoi était composé de véhicules et de soldats de l'armée américaine "
"lourdement armés. Nos drones de surveillance déployés dans les environs nous "
"ont permis de déterminer que la majorité de ces soldats sont maintenant "
"réanimés, y compris un d'eux qui opérait un exosquelette de combat léger. La "
"lutte nécessaire pour sécuriser les données sera probablement dure, mais vous "
"pourriez probablement courir plus rapidement que la majorités des zombies si "
"vous trouvez la valise assez rapidement. Si vous êtes incapable de faire "
"cela, une arme à feu et beaucoup de balles sont votre meilleure option."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Officially speaking, they were a senior DARPA researcher.  Their corpse "
"should stick out; it's likely the only one not wearing camouflage.  That's "
"all you need to know."
msgstr ""
"De façon officielle, il était considéré comme un chercheur senior de DARPA. "
"Son corps devrait être assez distinctif dû au fait qu'il devrait être le seul "
"n'étant pas en uniforme camouflage. Vous n'avez pas besoin de savoir plus."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It was ambushed on the road.\"  The intercom recites a series of coordinates. "
" \"Report back with the hard case.  If the researcher brought it with him, it "
"will be intact; have no doubt about that."
msgstr ""
"Il est tombé dans une embuscade sur la route.\" L'interphone récite une série "
"de coordonnées. \"Faites votre rapport avec la valise. Si le chercheur l'a "
"apportée avec lui, elle sera intacte, n'en doutez pas."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom's tray slides shut.\n"
"\n"
"\"This is the case; thank you.  Transferring the stipulated amount now.\"  "
"The tray slides back open with your payment.  \"As an additional form of "
"payment, you have been given clearance to receive a map of the area around "
"this site, to assist in your work.  The standing price is 1 HGC; please "
"inform us if you'd like to follow up on that offer going forward."
msgstr ""
"&Le plateau de l'interphone se referme.\n"
"\n"
"\"C'est le cas, merci. Je transfère maintenant le montant stipulé.\" Le "
"plateau s'ouvre à nouveau avec votre paiement. \"En guise de paiement "
"supplémentaire, vous avez reçu l'autorisation de recevoir une carte des "
"environs de ce site, pour vous aider dans votre travail. Le prix courant est "
"de 1 HGC ; veuillez nous informer si vous souhaitez donner suite à cette "
"offre à l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[PER 8] The original markings on that case had been scratched out.  Who did "
"it really belong to?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm interested in that map."
msgstr "Cette carte m'intéresse."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Light retrieval"
msgstr "Récupération de la lumière"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Light retrieval"
msgid ""
"Reach the collapsed tower basement, and search the ruins for a photonic "
"circuitry template.  The intercom warned you about heavy enemy presence, and "
"of the existence of a hazardous environment."
msgstr ""
"Rejoignez le sous-sol de la tour effondrée et fouillez les ruines à la "
"recherche d'un modèle de circuit photonique. L'intercom vous a averti d'une "
"forte présence ennemie et de l'existence d'un environnement dangereux."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Our facility once sourced advanced photonic circuitry from a nearby robotics "
"manufacturer.  Their building suffered major damage during the portal storms, "
"and collapsed almost entirely.  However, preliminary scouting reveals that "
"the basement prototyping lab likely remains intact.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We ask you to investigate the ruins, and if possible, retrieve a template "
"for the fabrication of said photonic circuitry.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 8 HGC, the standard heightened-hazard "
"rate.  We are also willing to provide you with a set of protective gear at a "
"considerable discount upon acceptance of the contract."
msgstr ""
"Notre installation s'approvisionnait autrefois en circuits photoniques "
"avancés auprès d'un fabricant de robots voisin. Le bâtiment a subi "
"d'importants dégâts lors des tempêtes du portail et s'est presque entièrement "
"effondré. Cependant, les premiers repérages révèlent que le laboratoire de "
"prototypage situé au sous-sol est probablement intact.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous vous demandons d'enquêter sur les ruines et, si possible, de récupérer "
"un modèle pour la fabrication de ces circuits photoniques.\n"
"\n"
"\"L'exécution de ce contrat vous donne droit à 8 HGC, le taux standard de "
"dangerosité accrue. Nous sommes également disposés à vous fournir un ensemble "
"d'équipements de protection à un prix très avantageux dès l'acceptation du "
"contrat."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's do this, then.  Transfer the location."
msgstr "Je suppose que je vais m'y mettre.  Transférez les coordonnées."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where is this manufacturer?"
msgstr "Où se trouve ce fabricant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You mention hazard pay.  What dangers are there?"
msgstr "Vous mentionnez la prime de risque. Quels sont les risques encourus ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't believe I'm cleared to-\"  You hear brief chatter.  \"Apologies; I "
"was mistaken.  The manufacturer was, technically speaking, kept secret from "
"the public.  As a result, it operated using an office tower as a front, and "
"was located underground.  An elevator in the back of the building led to the "
"basement, but it was likely destroyed in the damage - as a result, you will "
"need to find a way down yourself.  While there were stairs as well, it's "
"highly likely that they have been destroyed.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We advise bringing a way to safely enter and exit the lower level; a "
"grappling hook would work well for this purpose.  Given the damage, the "
"elevator shaft itself probably remains intact, and would be your likeliest "
"point of entry to the underground portion of the building."
msgstr ""
"Je ne crois pas être autorisé à...\" Vous entendez un bref bavardage. \"Mes "
"excuses ; je me suis trompé. Le fabricant était, techniquement parlant, tenu "
"secret du public. Par conséquent, il opérait en utilisant une tour de bureaux "
"comme façade, et était situé sous terre. Un ascenseur à l'arrière du bâtiment "
"menait au sous-sol, mais il a probablement été détruit par les dégâts. Il y "
"avait également des escaliers, mais il est fort probable qu'ils aient été "
"détruits.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous vous conseillons d'apporter un moyen d'entrer et de sortir du niveau "
"inférieur en toute sécurité ; un grappin conviendrait parfaitement à cet "
"effet. Compte tenu des dégâts, la cage d'ascenseur elle-même est probablement "
"intacte, et serait votre point d'entrée le plus probable dans la partie "
"souterraine du bâtiment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"About that.\"  You hear papers shuffling.  \"Our drones are unable to "
"approach the structure too closely, as a large amount of interference "
"prevents surveillance, but long-distance measurements reveal a high "
"concentration of toxic compounds in the air, as well as densely-clustered "
"heat signatures.  We expect a high concentration of undead, and other dangers "
"are likely."
msgstr ""
"A propos de ça\". On entend un bruit de papier. \"Nos drones ne peuvent pas "
"s'approcher trop près de la structure, car une grande quantité "
"d'interférences empêche la surveillance, mais les mesures à longue distance "
"révèlent une forte concentration de composés toxiques dans l'air, ainsi que "
"des signatures thermiques densément regroupées. Nous nous attendons à une "
"forte concentration de morts-vivants, et d'autres dangers sont probables."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Toxic compounds?"
msgstr "Composés toxiques?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about these heat signatures."
msgstr "Expliquez-moi l'histoire au sujet des signatures thermiques."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "\"Other dangers\" is a little vague.  Do you have anything more substantial?"
msgstr ""
"\"Autres dangers\", c'est un peu vague comme avertissement. Vous avez des "
"infos plus substantielles?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Back to the contract itself…"
msgstr "Retournons au contrat…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Correct.  The source of the chemicals is unknown, as is the exact "
"composition; only trace amounts are present in the air itself.  We can, "
"however, extrapolate that something within the ruins is creating highly "
"poisonous emissions.  We do not know how strong these emissions will become, "
"or what form they will take."
msgstr ""
"Correct. La source de ces produits chimiques n'est pas confirmé, l'exacte "
"composition de l'émanation n'étant pas non plus confirmée. Nous pouvons par "
"contre extrapoler que quelque chose dans les ruines produit des émissions "
"hautement toxiques. Nous ne sommes pas sure de l'intensité de ces émissions, "
"si celles-ci augmenteront en force, ou quelle formes elles prendront."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"At the moment, their origin is unclear.  The temperature profile of the "
"building is highly unusual, despite the damage, and is much denser than "
"wandering hordes observed through remote scouting.  A large amount of heat "
"consistent with an extremely high density of organisms appears to be "
"emanating from the basement itself.  We are, unfortunately, in the dark about "
"the cause of this density.  We would advise you remain observant and note "
"down any abnormalities."
msgstr ""
"Pour l'instant, leur origine n'est pas claire. Le profil de température du "
"bâtiment est très inhabituel, malgré les dégâts, et il est beaucoup plus "
"dense que les hordes errantes observées lors des repérages à distance. Une "
"grande quantité de chaleur correspondant à une densité extrêmement élevée "
"d'organismes semble émaner du sous-sol lui-même. Nous ne connaissons "
"malheureusement pas la cause de cette densité. Nous vous conseillons de "
"rester observateur et de noter toute anomalie."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be specific, there have been anomalous readings that we are unable to "
"explain.  Seismic disturbances have been recorded emanating from the ruins, "
"with a magnitude ranging from two to four, and periodic vocalizations have "
"been documented to exceed 150 decibels.  We are uncertain why or how these "
"phenomena are created."
msgstr ""
"Plus précisément, il y a eu des relevés anormaux que nous sommes incapables "
"d'expliquer. Des perturbations sismiques ont été enregistrées en provenance "
"des ruines, avec une magnitude allant de deux à quatre, et des vocalisations "
"périodiques dépassant 150 décibels ont été documentées. Nous ne savons pas "
"exactement pourquoi ni comment ces phénomènes se produisent."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The more I hear about this, the worse it sounds."
msgstr "Plus j'en entends parler, plus cela me paraît grave."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Did you have any other concerns?"
msgstr "Avez-vous d'autres préoccupations?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Your hesitation is understandable.  Unfortunately, we have already taken all "
"possible measures to obtain data and information remotely, but we are unable "
"to develop our understanding further without a physical presence."
msgstr ""
"Votre hésitation est compréhensible. Malheureusement, nous avons déjà pris "
"toutes les mesures possibles pour obtenir des données et des informations à "
"distance, mais nous ne pouvons pas développer davantage notre compréhension "
"sans une présence physique."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent.  Thank you very much.\"  The intercom recites a series of "
"coordinates.  \"Exercise a great deal of caution.  We do not know what the "
"conditions on the ground are like.  Use your best judgment.  As before, we "
"are willing to offer you protective gear, if you would like it."
msgstr ""
"C'est excellent. Merci beaucoup.\" L'interphone récite une série de "
"coordonnées. \"Soyez très prudents. Nous ne connaissons pas les conditions au "
"sol. Faites preuve de discernement. Comme précédemment, nous sommes prêts à "
"vous offrir des équipements de protection, si vous le souhaitez."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I would like that gear, yes.  Tell me about it."
msgstr "J'aimerais avoir ce matériel, oui. Parlez-m'en."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fantastic.\"  The intercom's tray slides shut, and then opens shortly "
"afterwards with your payment.  \"You have our thanks and our payment."
msgstr ""
"Fantastique.\" Le plateau de l'interphone se referme, puis s'ouvre peu après "
"avec votre paiement. \"Vous avez nos remerciements et notre paiement."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have any idea what I just went through?"
msgstr "Avez-vous la moindre idée de ce que je viens de vivre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You certainly gave me a run for my money, I'll say that much."
msgstr ""
"Vous m'en avez fait voir de toutes les couleurs, c'est le moins que l'on "
"puisse dire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As we discussed during acceptance of the contract, we were aware of hazardous "
"ground conditions, but we were unable to deduce further information other "
"than what was available through long-range sensing.  If you would like to "
"provide a description of the hazards present, we are willing to document them."
msgstr ""
"Comme nous en avons discuté lors de l'acceptation du contrat, nous étions "
"conscients des conditions dangereuses du sol, mais nous n'avons pas été en "
"mesure de déduire d'autres informations que celles disponibles grâce à la "
"détection à longue portée. Si vous souhaitez fournir une description des "
"risques présents, nous sommes disposés à les documenter."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Detail the conditions at the collapsed tower and its basement.  This will "
"advance time by ten minutes.]"
msgstr ""
"[Détaillez les conditions de la tour effondrée et de son sous-sol. Cela fera "
"avancer le temps de dix minutes]."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Let them know how bad that mission REALLY was.]"
msgstr "[Faites-leur savoir à quel point cette mission était VRAIMENT mauvaise]."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…Just forget it.  Let's never speak of this again."
msgstr "…Oublions cela.  N'en parlons plus jamais."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Over the course of several minutes, you explain what happened at the ruins: "
"the zombie presence and gigantic tendrils on the surface, and the biological "
"infestation completely taking over the basement, as well as the hostile "
"threats encountered therein.  The voice periodically interjects with "
"questions or statements; the whole time, you hear the sounds of typing on a "
"keyboard.\n"
"\n"
"\"We would like to extend our thanks for your detailed report.  It is clear "
"to us that the threat level present at the manufacturer was far higher than "
"we had originally anticipated, and your performance in the situation was "
"exemplary.  Should you desire further contract work, we will bear these facts "
"in mind, and ensure that the threat prognoses of your future assignments are "
"adequately assessed.\""
msgstr ""
"&Pendant plusieurs minutes, vous expliquez ce qui s'est passé dans les ruines "
": la présence de zombies et de gigantesques vrilles à la surface, "
"l'infestation biologique qui a complètement envahi le sous-sol, ainsi que les "
"menaces hostiles qui s'y trouvent. La voix intervient périodiquement pour "
"poser des questions ou faire des déclarations ; pendant tout ce temps, vous "
"entendez le son de la frappe sur un clavier.\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous tenons à vous remercier pour votre rapport détaillé. Il est clair pour "
"nous que le niveau de menace présent chez le fabricant était bien plus élevé "
"que ce que nous avions initialement prévu, et votre performance dans cette "
"situation a été exemplaire. Si vous souhaitez travailler sur d'autres "
"contrats, nous garderons ces faits à l'esprit et veillerons à ce que les "
"pronostics de menace de vos futures missions soient évalués de manière "
"adéquate.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's fine.  At least now we know for the future."
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas grave. Au moins, nous savons maintenant ce qu'il en est pour "
"l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, yeah.  You're welcome."
msgstr "Oui oui, de rien."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's never do that again."
msgstr "Ne recommençons plus jamais."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The intercom waits patiently."
msgstr "&L'intercom attends patiemment."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Description, huh?  Where to begin?  Let's start with the giant mob of zombies "
"that was infesting the building.  Oh, and there were also horrors full of "
"toxic gas that exploded when I got near them or killed one, so I was "
"constantly choking on fumes the whole time."
msgstr ""
"Description, hein ? Par où commencer ? Commençons par la foule géante de "
"zombies qui infestait le bâtiment. Oh, et il y avait aussi des horreurs "
"pleines de gaz toxiques qui explosaient lorsque je m'en approchais ou que "
"j'en tuais une, ce qui fait que j'étais constamment en train d'étouffer sous "
"les vapeurs."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That makes-"
msgstr "Cela fait…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, but that's not all!  They were coming from a pair of giant fucking "
"tentacles coming out of the ground like a monster movie that were constantly "
"roaring and shaking the whole building, and toxic exploding spiders kept "
"crawling off and shooting poison darts at me until I got away or stopped the "
"tentacles themselves, which wasn't easy because the entire building had come "
"down around them."
msgstr ""
"Mais ce n'est pas tout ! Ils provenaient d'une paire de putains de tentacules "
"géants qui sortaient du sol comme dans un film de monstres et qui ne "
"cessaient de rugir et de secouer tout le bâtiment, et des araignées toxiques "
"explosives continuaient de ramper et de me lancer des fléchettes empoisonnées "
"jusqu'à ce que je m'échappe ou que j'arrête les tentacules elles-mêmes, ce "
"qui n'était pas facile parce que tout le bâtiment s'était effondré autour "
"d'elles."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Stop talking.]"
msgstr "[Arrêtez de parler.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What do you mean by-"
msgstr "Que voulez-vous dire par…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Then it took me half an hour to find the way down, because there were holes "
"in the floor everywhere, and when I finally did, I was in the insides of a "
"goddamn flesh pit with flooding up to my ankles, and to complement the "
"innards hanging from the ceiling that I couldn't see through the gas that "
"would throw me ten feet and make me start drowning, there were dozens of "
"people fused together in lumps everywhere, and did I mention the poison gas?  "
"Because they were full of it too, and so everything reeked and it felt like "
"being in a giant fucking intestine full of people."
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, j'ai mis une demi-heure à trouver le chemin pour descendre, parce "
"qu'il y avait des trous dans le sol partout, et quand je l'ai enfin trouvé, "
"je me suis retrouvé à l'intérieur d'un putain de puits de chair avec de l'eau "
"jusqu'aux chevilles, et pour compléter les entrailles suspendues au plafond "
"que je ne pouvais pas voir à cause du gaz qui me projetterait à trois mètres "
"et me ferait commencer à me noyer, il y avait des douzaines de personnes "
"fusionnées en morceaux partout, et est-ce que j'ai mentionné le gaz "
"empoisonné ? Parce qu'ils en étaient pleins aussi, et donc tout empestait et "
"j'avais l'impression d'être dans un putain d'intestin géant rempli de gens."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please slow down-"
msgstr "Veuillez ralentir…"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"And after ALL THAT, I find your manufacturing lab on the other end of this "
"thing straight out of a fever dream nightmare, and after ALL THAT, I find "
"your photonics, and then I have to get ALL THE WAY out of the ENTIRE "
"ZOMBIE-INFESTED TOWN so I could bring you your stupid fucking template.  Are "
"you happy now?"
msgstr ""
"Après tout cela, je trouve votre laboratoire de fabrication à l'autre bout de "
"ce truc tout droit sorti d'un cauchemar, et après tout cela, je trouve votre "
"photonique, et ensuite je dois sortir de toute la ville infestée de zombies "
"pour pouvoir vous apporter votre putain de modèle stupide. Tu es content "
"maintenant ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&The voice on the other side of the intercom is silent with disbelief."
msgstr "&La voix de l'autre côté de l'interphone est muette d'incrédulité."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"…Uh.  We are- thank you for finding the photonics.  We will, ah, make sure "
"that the threat conditions of your future contracts are adequately assessed.  "
"Um.  Thank you."
msgstr ""
"…Euh.  Nous sommes -- merci d'avoir trouvé les circuits photoniques.  Nous "
"allons, ah, nous assurer que le niveau de danger de vos futurs contrats soie "
"correctement évaluée.  Euh…  Merci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Iron Safari"
msgstr "Safari Métallique"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Iron Safari"
msgid ""
"Disable and retrieve the unusual robot by <color_yellow>successfully stunning "
"it with the prototype rifle provided,</color> then <color_yellow>quickly "
"running up and deactivating the robot before it recovers from the "
"stun</color>.  You can keep shooting it while it's stunned to prolong the "
"time until it is active again.  You can intercept the robot indicated by Hub "
"01, or find an inactive robot somewhere else.  <color_yellow>You'll need some "
"experience in electronics or mechanics to disable it</color>."
msgstr ""
"Désactivez et récupérez le robot inhabituel en <color_yellow>réussissant à "
"l'assommer avec le prototype de fusil fourni,</color> puis <color_yellow>en "
"courant rapidement et en désactivant le robot avant qu'il ne se remette de "
"l'assommoir</color>. Vous pouvez continuer à lui tirer dessus pendant qu'il "
"est assommé pour prolonger le délai avant qu'il ne soit à nouveau actif. Vous "
"pouvez intercepter le robot indiqué par le Hub 01, ou trouver un robot "
"inactif ailleurs. <color_yellow>Vous aurez besoin d'un peu d'expérience en "
"électronique ou en mécanique pour le désactiver</color>."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One of our scout drones spotted a partially-malfunctioning robot of "
"unconventional make while tracking an anomalous radiation spike close by.  We "
"project that much knowledge could be gained from a close examination of this "
"subject, and you would be tasked to retrieve it for us intact.  We will equip "
"you with a prototype rifle and instructions on how to use it and deactivate "
"the robot, if you accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"The success of this contract requires that the subject be brought back in "
"an inactive state, and *not* destroyed.  A ruined robot is of no scientific "
"value.  We emphasize that you use the prototype to complete this task; an EMP "
"blast would likely destroy the subject outright.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Completion of this contract awards 2 HGC, and you will be able to keep the "
"prototype and the equipment used to operate it."
msgstr ""
"L'un de nos drones d'observation a repéré un robot partiellement défectueux "
"de fabrication non conventionnelle alors qu'il suivait un pic de radiation "
"anormal à proximité. Nous pensons qu'un examen approfondi de ce sujet "
"pourrait nous apporter beaucoup de connaissances, et vous serez chargé de le "
"récupérer intact pour nous. Si vous acceptez, nous vous fournirons un "
"prototype de fusil et des instructions sur la façon de l'utiliser et de "
"désactiver le robot\".\n"
"\n"
"\"Le succès de ce contrat exige que le sujet soit ramené dans un état "
"inactif, et *non* détruit. Un robot en ruine n'a aucune valeur scientifique. "
"Nous insistons sur le fait que vous devez utiliser le prototype pour "
"accomplir cette tâche ; une explosion IEM détruirait probablement le sujet.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"L'achèvement de ce contrat attribue 2 HGC, et vous pourrez conserver le "
"prototype et l'équipement utilisé pour le faire fonctionner."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got a deal.  I'll track down your robot."
msgstr "Vous avez un marché. Je traquerai votre robot."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about this prototype."
msgstr "Dites-moi en plus au sujet de ce prototype."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What is this robot, and what does it look like?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce que ce robot et à quoi ressemble-t-il ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you'll give me a moment…\"  You hear the sounds of typing.  \"Its working "
"name is the hm12.  It functions similarly to a laser, but is specifically "
"designed to incapacitate robots without harming their internals.  Once a "
"subject is stunned, it can be manually deactivated.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"A shot will only stun the robot if you manage to hit its main sensory "
"array, which will rely on your aim.  After a stunning shot, you might proceed "
"to the deactivation attempts by examining the robot from up close."
msgstr ""
"Si vous voulez bien m'accorder un moment...\" On entend des bruits de frappe. "
"\"Son nom de travail est le hm12. Son fonctionnement est similaire à celui "
"d'un laser, mais il est spécialement conçu pour neutraliser les robots sans "
"endommager leur structure interne. Une fois le sujet assommé, il peut être "
"désactivé manuellement.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Un tir n'étourdira le robot que si vous parvenez à toucher son réseau "
"sensoriel principal, ce qui dépendra de votre visée. Après un tir "
"étourdissant, vous pouvez procéder aux tentatives de désactivation en "
"examinant le robot de près."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We are as of yet uncertain of its origin and purpose.  Its body most closely "
"resembles a pyramid on what we believe are three sets of legs for mobility.  "
"It is lightly armed, and has attacked our cam-spy drones using high-voltage "
"electric discharge.  We theorize that this is most likely for deterrence, and "
"not to cause direct harm.  Nonetheless, we need to emphasize that its full "
"capabilities are unknown, and we do not know how it will react when "
"confronted with a living threat."
msgstr ""
"Nous sommes encore incertains de son origine et de sa fonction. Son corps "
"ressemble le plus à une pyramide sur ce que nous pensons être trois ensembles "
"de jambes pour la mobilité. Il est légèrement armé et a attaqué nos drones "
"espions à l'aide de décharges électriques à haute tension. Nous pensons qu'il "
"s'agit probablement d'un moyen de dissuasion et non d'une attaque directe. "
"Néanmoins, nous devons insister sur le fait que toutes ses capacités sont "
"inconnues et que nous ne savons pas comment il réagira lorsqu'il sera "
"confronté à une menace vivante."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Lovely.  Just a moment; we will transfer the prototype and handling "
"procedures, which includes information of its last recorded location.\"\n"
"\n"
"The intercom tray thumps several times as objects are placed into it.  After "
"about a minute, it slides open, revealing a slender weapon that looks a bit "
"like a radar gun, a tool battery, a sheaf of papers in a binder, and a UPS.  "
"\"The hm12 draws power from a connected UPS.  Please remember to bring the "
"specimen back *intact* - battered salvage is of no use to us.  To safely "
"perform the task of deactivation, please review the provided documentation, "
"and pay special attention to the procedures detailed in subsections IV and "
"VII."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom tray quickly slides shut.\n"
"\n"
"\"We expected nothing less.  We hope you found the prototype's performance to "
"be satisfactory.\""
msgstr ""
"&Le plateau de l'interphone se referme rapidement.\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous n'en attendions pas moins. Nous espérons que vous avez trouvé les "
"performances du prototype satisfaisantes\"."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Will this weapon work on other robots, as well?"
msgstr "Cette arme fonctionnera-t-elle également sur d'autres robots ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The handling procedures you gave me seemed to predate the Cataclysm.  How "
"long had that robot been here?"
msgstr ""
"Les procédures de manipulation que vous m'avez données semblent antérieures "
"au Cataclysme. Depuis combien de temps ce robot est-il là ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We believe so; it underwent intensive internal tests on existing and "
"theoretical models before giving it to you.  UGVs, autonomous CROWS units, "
"manhacks, and other robots should all be possible to neutralize by using the "
"weapon, although we advise great caution; the weapon is short-ranged, and was "
"not designed to target distant enemies."
msgstr ""
"Nous le pensons ; elle a fait l'objet de tests internes intensifs sur des "
"modèles existants et théoriques avant de vous être remise. Les UGV, les "
"unités autonomes CROWS, les manhacks et autres robots devraient tous pouvoir "
"être neutralisés à l'aide de l'arme, bien que nous recommandions la plus "
"grande prudence ; l'arme a une courte portée et n'a pas été conçue pour "
"cibler des ennemis éloignés."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Pardon me.\"  The voice briefly turns away from the microphone and asks "
"something.  \"Very well.  I am cleared to tell you that it appeared near the "
"beginning of the portal storms, and during this time, it was logged and "
"documented.  No attempt was ever made to retrieve it before the government "
"collapsed.  That is all I am able to share with you at this time."
msgstr ""
"Excusez-moi\". La voix se détourne brièvement du microphone et demande "
"quelque chose. \"Très bien. Je suis autorisé à vous dire qu'il est apparu "
"vers le début des tempêtes de portail, et pendant cette période, il a été "
"enregistré et documenté. Aucune tentative n'a été faite pour le récupérer "
"avant que le gouvernement ne s'effondre. C'est tout ce que je peux vous dire "
"pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The intercom tray quickly slides shut.  After a pause, the voice on the "
"other end sighs.\n"
"\n"
"\"…we requested that the subject remain intact.  This outcome is… "
"unfortunate.  We will process the specimen, but it is unlikely that it will "
"yield usable information as to its purpose.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"You may keep the prototype.  You are dismissed.\""
msgstr ""
"&Le plateau de l'interphone se referme rapidement. Après une pause, la voix à "
"l'autre bout du fil soupire.\n"
"\n"
"\"...nous avons demandé que le sujet reste intact. Ce résultat est... "
"malheureux. Nous allons traiter le spécimen, mais il est peu probable qu'il "
"fournisse des informations utilisables quant à son objectif.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Vous pouvez garder le prototype. Vous pouvez vous retirer.\""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, alright."
msgstr "Ok, ok."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Hazard Meteorology"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Hazard Meteorology"
msgid ""
"Use the NRE recorder to collect information during a portal storm event.  "
"You'll need to <color_yellow>stay outside and carry the recorder for around 6 "
"minutes until you hear a sharp beep</color> to collect sufficient data.  "
"Generate a printout by activating the NRE recorder and offer it to Hub 01 to "
"finish the mission."
msgstr ""
"Utilisez l'enregistreur NRE pour collecter des informations lors d'une "
"tempête sur le portail. Vous devrez <color_yellow>rester à l'extérieur et "
"porter l'enregistreur pendant environ 6 minutes jusqu'à ce que vous entendiez "
"un bip aigu</color> pour collecter suffisamment de données. Générez une "
"impression en activant l'enregistreur NRE et offrez-le au Hub 01 pour "
"terminer la mission."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As we mentioned before, our research into the portal storm phenomena requires "
"that we obtain additional data to verify our own local measurements.  "
"Recording this data will require you to carry a scientific instrument called "
"an NRE recorder on your person while outside in the storm for around six "
"minutes.  The recording instrument will be provided at no cost if you choose "
"to accept.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are willing to offer 1 HGC for each standard-length recording.  "
"Higher-quality data may be obtained by collecting more data before printing a "
"report, and as a result, we are willing to provide higher pay for better "
"recordings."
msgstr ""
"Comme nous l'avons mentionné précédemment, nos recherches sur les phénomènes "
"de tempêtes portails exigent que nous obtenions des données supplémentaires "
"pour vérifier nos propres mesures locales. L'enregistrement de ces données "
"nécessitera que vous portiez sur vous un instrument scientifique appelé "
"enregistreur NRE pendant que vous serez à l'extérieur dans la tempête pendant "
"environ six minutes. L'instrument d'enregistrement vous sera fourni "
"gratuitement si vous l'acceptez\".\n"
"\n"
"\"Nous sommes prêts à offrir 1 HGC pour chaque enregistrement de longueur "
"standard. Des données de meilleure qualité peuvent être obtenues en "
"collectant davantage de données avant l'impression d'un rapport et, par "
"conséquent, nous sommes disposés à offrir une rémunération plus élevée pour "
"de meilleurs enregistrements."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, why not?  Let's do some science."
msgstr "Bien sûr, pourquoi pas?  Faisons un peu de science."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How does the recorder work?"
msgstr "Comment est-ce que l'enregistreur fonctionne?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How will I know when I've been outside long enough?"
msgstr "Comment saurai-je si je suis resté(e) à l'extérieur assez longtemps?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do I need to physically hold the recorder in my hand?"
msgstr "J'ai besoin de tenir l'enregistreur dans mes mains?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If I lose the recorder or break it, what should I do?"
msgstr "Si je perds l'enregistreur ou le casse, que devrais-je faire?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Once the storm starts, it should be enough to walk outside while carrying the "
"NRE, as the recording requires no particular actions on your part.  Research "
"insist on the fact that you must personally carry the NRE on your person to "
"take accurate measurements, so leaving it outside while you take shelter "
"won't work.  I'd explain the synchronistic relations that demand this, but I "
"didn't really understand that part myself… oh, and you might want to obtain a "
"high-caliber firearm before attempting to take the measurements.  Just in "
"case things start leaking into uhm… prime."
msgstr ""
"Une fois que la tempête à commencée, il devrait être suffisant pour vous de "
"juste marcher à l'extérieur avec enregistreur NRE sur vous, celui-ci "
"s'allumant automatiquement sans aucune intervention de votre part. Nos "
"chercheurs insistent que vous avez besoin de porter l'enregistreur sur vous "
"pour que celui-ci soit capable d'enmagasiner des données utiles, donc just le "
"laisser dehors et rester bien à l'abri n'est pas une option. Je vous "
"expliquerais les équations et théorèmes qui nécessitent que vous vous "
"risquiez autant, mais je ne suis pas sûr de totalement comprendre moi-même… "
"Oh, et vous allez probablement vouloir obtenir une arme à feu à large calibre "
"avant d'essayer d'accomplir cette prise de données, juste au cas où des... "
"choses commencent à pénétrer à travers la réalité. "

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The recorder will beep once it has recorded enough data for a report.  The "
"longer you stay outside, however, the higher the quality and quantity of the "
"data will be.  While you are only expected to obtain the minimum viable "
"report that the NRE can produce, we are willing to offer increased pay for "
"higher-quality recordings."
msgstr ""
"L'enregistreur bipera lorsqu'il aura emagasiner assez de données pour un "
"rapport complet, mais si vous restez dehors plus longtemps, ses données "
"deviendront plus précises et précieuses. Bien qu'il ne soit attendu de vous "
"que de faire le minimum signalé par le bip, nous serions disposés à payer une "
"prime pour des enregistrements de plus haute qualité."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You do not.  All that is required is that you have it somewhere on your "
"person; it will function equally well inside of a bag as it would in your own "
"hands.  Your preferred method of carrying the instrument will be enough to "
"collect data as long as it is directly carried on your person."
msgstr ""
"Ceci n'est pas nécessaire. Tout ce qui est requis de vous est de l'avoir "
"quelque part sur vous, l'enregistreur étant capable de fonctionner dans votre "
"sac que dans vos mains. Votre choix d'où le porter est totalement libre à "
"condition qu'il soit toujours directement sur vous, le laisser dans un "
"véhicule n'est donc pas une option par exemple."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The recorder is not irreplaceable, but it is constructed using delicate "
"components that are now in short supply.  In the event that the device is "
"rendered nonfunctional, we are willing to provide a replacement at an "
"equivalent cost.  Specifically, if you can locate an NRE microphone, which "
"can be located in certain laboratories, then we are willing to provide a "
"replacement recorder in exchange for it."
msgstr ""
"L'enregistreur n'est pas irremplaçable, mais sa fabrication requiert des "
"composants délicats maintenant en quantités limitées. Si votre exemplaire est "
"endommagé irrémédiablement, nous sommes prêts à vous en fournir un "
"remplacement pour un coût équivalent, de plus, si vous trouvez un microphone "
"NRE durant vos fouilles, nous vous fourniront un remplacement sans frais en "
"échange."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Transferring the recorder now.\"  The intercom tray slides open, revealing a "
"hefty, barebones device and a light battery to accompany it.  \"Please "
"remember to exercise caution; the effects of portal storms on human "
"physiology are poorly understood."
msgstr ""
"Transfert de l'enregistreur maintenant.\" Le plateau de l'intercom s'ouvre, "
"révélant un appareil lourd et dépouillé, accompagné d'une batterie légère. "
"\"Les effets des tempêtes de portail sur la physiologie humaine sont mal "
"connus."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Data Retrieval"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Data Retrieval"
msgid ""
"Reach the LIXA facility, and search the area for anything of interest.  The "
"intercom warned you about a number of undead aboveground, and the high "
"probability of more underground."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"During the Cataclysm, we lost contact with one of our sister sites, LIXA.  "
"Aerial surveillance indicates that the facility's inhabitants are deceased, "
"and beyond the now-zombified security detail, the site should be sparsely "
"populated.  We want you to enter the facility and make a copy of what they "
"were researching on the provided thumb drive.  Additionally, we will be "
"providing you with a keycard that should at the very least get you in the "
"front door.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We're offering a standard 5 HGC for successful retrieval of the data.  If "
"that isn't enough of an incentive, we do have a manifest from before we lost "
"contact with the facility showing a handful of specialized powered suits in "
"inventory.  You are free to take any that are left."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Alright, I'll see if I can't get that data for you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What can you tell me about what they were doing there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What does LIXA even mean?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If I lose the ID card or the memory stick, what should I do?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"All I can tell you is that they were conducting cutting-edge research related "
"to-\" The intercom abruptly cuts off for several seconds before coming back "
"on, the voice sounding apologetic, \"Sorry, but as it turns out I'm not at "
"liberty to divulge that information.  What I can do however is recommend you "
"bring an NRE recorder with you if you still have one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's an acronym that stands for Laser Interferometer eXodimensional resonance "
"Assay."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, the ID card wouldn't strictly speaking be necessary if you were to find "
"some way of breaching the facility's security doors.\" The voice pauses for a "
"moment, \"But that said we only have the one ID card, so unless you're "
"confident you can get in without it, please don't lose it.  As for the memory "
"stick I would highly recommend you not lose that as portable drives with the "
"required hardware security modules to interface with secure terminals are in "
"short supply these days.  However there may very well be some on-site for you "
"to scavenge if you're lucky."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Transferring the items now.\"  The intercom tray slides open, revealing an ID "
"card for the facility and what looks like a USB thumb drive.  \"Again: please "
"take care not to lose either of these since we can't exactly make more of "
"them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"[Detail the conditions at the research facility.  This will advance time by "
"ten minutes.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Let them know how much of a trainwreck THIS one was.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&Over the course of several minutes, you calmly detail the events at the "
"facility: the unexpected zombie presence underground, the anomalous nature of "
"the experiment floor, and the encounter with the warped and hostile research "
"staff trapped in the corridor.  Throughout, the voice interjects with "
"questions, the sounds of typing filling the pauses.\n"
"\n"
"\"We appreciate your thorough report,\" the voice finally responds.  \"Your "
"handling of the circumstances was commendable considering the anomalous and "
"unpredictable nature of the facility.  If you seek further contract work, "
"rest assured, we'll take into account the potential for anomalous "
"circumstances in future assignments and relay them accordingly.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Hoo boy, where do I even begin with this one?  Let's start with the fact that "
"your intel was about as useful as a screen door on a submarine!  "
"\"Sparsely-populated,\" my ass!  How did you lot miss the goddamn zombie mosh "
"pit down the open elevator shaft!?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We're sorry but-"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, ho ho ho ho ho no friend you do not get to talk right now.  When I "
"FINALLY got down to the experiment floor, you know what I found?  The entire "
"corridor was turned into a two-dimensional image!  What were they even DOING "
"that turned an entire section of the building INTO A HAUNTED VIDEO GAME "
"PORTAL PAINTING!?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I SAID SHUT UP!  It teleported me to an infinitely looping corridor!  "
"INFINITELY!  LOOPING!  CORRIDOR!  I mean, fuck, you ever see one of those "
"Escher paintings?  It's like that, only you don't just see the surface of "
"what you're looking at, you see EV-ER-Y-THING, and friend let me tell you "
"getting a first-hand look at the inside of my digestive system was *not* "
"pretty.  Oh, and did I mention the light?  Yeah, when some of the laser tubes "
"got broken, they spat out light THAT HURT!  A LOT!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You know why they got broken?  I was fighting the insane remnants of the "
"research staff!  They were climbing the walls, spitting light!  And then "
"there was the corridor itself somehow!  I fought the goddamn building!  I've "
"had nightmares that made more sense than fighting that thing!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh… Yeah, sorry.  I'll, um… I'll make a note to try and see if we can't get "
"any better information for your future contracts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pay Back The Riot Gear to Hub 01"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I appreciate the credit.  I've got your payment now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to give it some thought."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'y réfléchir un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "[thanks bro this will be very interesting where's the tower?]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[tell them where scout tower is]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What project would you like to know about?"
msgstr "De quel projet voulez-vous des nouvelles?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you decoded the disk?"
msgstr "Vous avez décodé le disque?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 HGC] I'd like to buy the rest of the armor set now."
msgstr "[6 POH] J'aimerais acheter le reste de l'armure."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to request a Hybrid Weapons Platform."
msgstr "J'aimerais demander une plateforme d'armes hybrides."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How goes work on the HWP?"
msgstr "Comment se passe le travail sur le HWP ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'd like to request a set of armor."
msgstr "J'aimerais réquisitionner une armure."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How is my ordered armor going?"
msgstr "Comment se porte l'armure que j'ai commandée ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I would like you to upgrade my modular defense system."
msgstr "J'aimerais que vous amélioriez mon système de défense modulaire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"My phase immersion suit has taken a serious beating.  Could someone repair it "
"for me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "My RM13 combat armor has taken some damage.  Could someone repair it for me?"
msgstr ""
"Mon armure de combat RM13 a été endommagée. Vous avez quelqu'un qui pourrait "
"me la réparer?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I salvaged this combat exoskeleton.  Do you think you could repair it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How are my armor repairs coming?"
msgstr "Mes réparations d'armure avancent bien?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've found this piece of XEDRA tech; it seems to offer some kind of "
"protection.  I'm curious what you all can make of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any progress on the anchor?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Any progress on the Hub anchor?"
msgstr "Du progrès sur l'ancre?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've found a rifle chambered for a caliber I don't recognize.  Do you think "
"you could make an HWP adapter for it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you finished work on that exotic conversion kit?"
msgstr "Vous avez fini votre kit de conversion exotique?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"At the moment, no.  While you are no doubt proficient, distribution of "
"prototype equipment is so far restricted to trusted field agents.  Were "
"someone else from the organization to vouch for your competency, we may "
"consider extending access."
msgstr ""
"Pour l'instant, non. Bien que vous soyez sans aucun doute compétent, la "
"distribution de l'équipement prototype est jusqu'à présent limitée aux agents "
"de terrain de confiance. Si quelqu'un d'autre de l'organisation se portait "
"garant de vos compétences, nous pourrions envisager d'élargir l'accès."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, Foster gave you quite a recommendation.  Very well - I will authorize "
"you access to our prototype fabrication services for agents in the field.  "
"This includes the Hybrid Weapons Platform, alongside the ability to order "
"spare or replacement parts for your field gear."
msgstr ""
"Oui, Foster vous a fait une belle recommandation. Très bien - je vais vous "
"autoriser à accéder à nos services de fabrication de prototypes pour les "
"agents sur le terrain. Cela inclut la plateforme d'armes hybrides, ainsi que "
"la possibilité de commander des pièces de rechange ou de remplacement pour "
"votre équipement de terrain."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great.  What exactly is this 'Hybrid Weapons Platform', anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Platform is complete.  As a reminder, the HWP will not function as a "
"weapon without a conversion kit installed.  Transferring the requested items "
"now.\"\n"
"\n"
"The tray shakes as several heavy objects are dropped into it, and it slides "
"open.  Inside: the Hybrid Weapons Platform.  On its own, it doesn't look like "
"much; it resembles the body of a service rifle without a stock or barrel, "
"colored in sleek black with blue highlights around the magazine well.  Small "
"yellow arrows and inscriptions are present at certain points, highlighting "
"the fasteners used to assemble the thing in earnest.  Accompanying the "
"Platform itself is a series of four bundles of parts for it, each held "
"together using velcro strips and tagged by caliber.  A drawstring nylon bag, "
"embroidered with the Hub's logo and filled with proprietary tools, completes "
"the whole package.\n"
"\n"
"All in all, not a bad deal.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you require magazines of any given caliber, we are willing to "
"provide them through standard requisitions.  We hope you find its performance "
"to be satisfactory."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Work is still ongoing.  These things can take time."
msgstr "Nous travaillons encore dessus, ces choses prennent du temps."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll spare you the marketing pitch.  The Hybrid Weapons Platform - or more "
"commonly the HWP - is a weapons platform capable of supporting multiple "
"calibers via the use of quick-release adapters.  On its own, the platform "
"does nothing; each adapter, however, allows it to chamber and fire a "
"different type of round.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Each new HWP is printed to order.  Materials will require eight HGC up "
"front, and fabrication will take seven days."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 HGC] A week is fine."
msgstr "[8 POH] Une semaine d'attente me va."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about the adapters.  Does it come with any?"
msgstr "Parlez-moi des adaptateurs. Est-il livré avec des adaptateurs ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "A week feels like an eternity these days.  Why the wait?"
msgstr "Une semaine semble être une éternité de nos jours. Pourquoi attendre ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why should I use this over something like a rifle that doesn't need "
"proprietary parts?"
msgstr ""
"Pourquoi l'utiliser plutôt qu'un fusil qui n'a pas besoin de pièces "
"exclusives ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Adapters are standalone conversion kits, and can be swapped in the field "
"without any tools, though it will take a minute or so.  The factory standard "
"includes adapters for the following calibers… 5.56 NATO, 7.62 NATO, 9mm "
"Parabellum, and 12-gauge shotshell.  Two loaded magazines are also provided "
"for each of these calibers, and additional empty magazines can be purchased "
"through trade.  A maintenance kit with the necessary tools to service the "
"Platform is also provided."
msgstr ""
"Les adaptateurs sont des kits de conversion autonomes, qui peuvent être "
"échangés sur le terrain sans aucun outil, même si cela prend environ une "
"minute. La norme d'usine comprend des adaptateurs pour les calibres suivants "
": 5.56 NATO, 7.62 NATO, 9mm Parabellum, et 12-gauge shotshell. Deux chargeurs "
"chargés sont également fournis pour chacun de ces calibres, et des chargeurs "
"vides supplémentaires peuvent être achetés dans le commerce. Un kit de "
"maintenance contenant les outils nécessaires à l'entretien de la plate-forme "
"est également fourni."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"As before, each Platform is made to order.  This is a slow process for "
"several reasons.  First, the parts must be printed to spec; this takes a "
"great degree of precision, and so the process is lengthy.  The remainder of "
"the week is spent running reliability tests as each conversion kit finishes "
"production.  I understand that it isn't an ideal option, but I believe the "
"quality of the product is worth that investment."
msgstr ""
"Comme auparavant, chaque plate-forme est fabriquée sur commande. Il s'agit "
"d'un processus lent pour plusieurs raisons. Tout d'abord, les pièces doivent "
"être imprimées selon les spécifications, ce qui demande une grande précision, "
"et le processus est donc long. Le reste de la semaine est consacré à des "
"tests de fiabilité au fur et à mesure que la production de chaque kit de "
"conversion s'achève. Je comprends que ce n'est pas l'option idéale, mais je "
"pense que la qualité du produit vaut cet investissement."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I believe the answer to that question to be twofold.  First, a maintenance "
"kit is included with each new Platform that includes the tools required to "
"service it, including a diagram of the weapon's construction.  Second, even "
"if you would prefer to use the weapon only for a specific purpose, we are "
"able to manufacture and provide high-capacity drum magazines far exceeding "
"the capacity of widely-available analogues.  We expect this to be a "
"significant boon to your ability to use the Platform in a variety of "
"environments and situations, as high-capacity magazines can be difficult or "
"dangerous to find in the new world."
msgstr ""
"Je pense que la réponse à cette question est double. Premièrement, chaque "
"nouvelle plate-forme est accompagnée d'un kit d'entretien comprenant les "
"outils nécessaires à son entretien, ainsi qu'un schéma de construction de "
"l'arme. Deuxièmement, même si vous préférez utiliser l'arme uniquement dans "
"un but spécifique, nous sommes en mesure de fabriquer et de fournir des "
"chargeurs à tambour de grande capacité, dépassant de loin la capacité des "
"armes analogues largement disponibles. Nous pensons que cela vous permettra "
"d'utiliser la plate-forme dans une grande variété d'environnements et de "
"situations, car les chargeurs de grande capacité peuvent être difficiles ou "
"dangereux à trouver dans le nouveau monde."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Excellent.  Report back in seven days' time, and your Platform will be ready."
msgstr ""
"Excellent. Faites-nous un rapport dans sept jours et votre plate-forme sera "
"prête."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Excellent.  We will begin work shortly.  Report back in 24 hours for pickup."
msgstr ""
"Excellent.  Nous commencerons le travail sous peu.  Revenez dans 24 heures "
"pour récupérer votre commande."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes we have!  The disk contained the configuration necessary to print our "
"armors with a much more resilient composite than was previously available to "
"us, without sacrificing any maneuverability.  As a form of payment, we are "
"willing to provide you with the first functional models of the armor at a "
"good price - six HGC.  While that may seem steep, the materials used are very "
"high-end, and six coins just barely covers the production cost alone.  If you "
"are unwilling or incapable of filling that price now, the offer will remain "
"available indefinitely - just let us know when you'd like it.\n"
"\n"
"\"Should you find anything else of interest in the world, please bring it to "
"us.  We would be happy to collaborate like this again in the future."
msgstr ""
"Oui, nous l'avons fait ! Le disque contenait la configuration nécessaire pour "
"imprimer nos armures avec un composite beaucoup plus résistant que celui dont "
"nous disposions auparavant, sans sacrifier la maniabilité. En guise de "
"paiement, nous sommes prêts à vous fournir les premiers modèles fonctionnels "
"de l'armure à un bon prix - six HGC. Ce prix peut sembler élevé, mais les "
"matériaux utilisés sont très haut de gamme, et six pièces couvrent à peine le "
"coût de production. Si vous ne souhaitez pas ou ne pouvez pas payer ce prix "
"maintenant, l'offre restera valable indéfiniment - il vous suffit de nous "
"faire savoir quand vous le souhaitez.\n"
"\n"
"\"Si vous trouvez quelque chose d'intéressant dans le monde, n'hésitez pas à "
"nous l'apporter. Nous serions heureux de collaborer à nouveau de la sorte à "
"l'avenir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not yet.  The contents are very strongly encrypted, so simply pulling the "
"data is impossible.  Work is underway to deduce the correct access key, but "
"even with our facilities, it will take some time."
msgstr ""
"Pas encore. Le contenu est très fortement crypté, de sorte qu'il est "
"impossible d'extraire simplement les données. Des travaux sont en cours pour "
"déduire la clé d'accès correcte, mais même avec nos installations, cela "
"prendra du temps."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[6 HGC] Let's see what this armor is capable of."
msgstr "[6 POH] Voyons si cette armure en valait la peine."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Understood.  The parts will finish fabrication in 24 hours, once you hand "
"over the stipulated HGC.  Depending on our currently available selection, the "
"price will range from 2 to 4 HGC for non-specialty equipment."
msgstr ""
"Je comprends. La fabrication des pièces sera achevée dans les 24 heures, une "
"fois que vous nous aurez remis les HGC stipulés. En fonction de notre "
"sélection actuelle, le prix variera entre 2 et 4 HGC pour les équipements non "
"spécialisés."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[3 HGC] I'd like to request a replacement Modular Defense System."
msgstr "[3 POH] Je voudrais un remplacement pour mon système de défense modulaire."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] I'd like to request a set of prototype armor."
msgstr "[2 POH] J'aimerais un ensemble d'armure prototype."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of turnout armor."
msgstr "[4 POH] J'aimerais un ensemble d'armure ignifugée."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of ballistic armor."
msgstr "[4 POH] J'aimerais un ensemble d'armure pare-balles."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[4 HGC] I'd like to request a set of kinetic armor."
msgstr "[4 POH] J'aimerais un ensemble d'armure pare-chocs."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[12 HGC] I'd like to request a set of soldier armor."
msgstr "[12 POH] J'aimerais un ensemble d'armure de soldat."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, we've finished printing the requested armor pieces.  Transferring to you "
"now."
msgstr ""
"Oui, nous avons fini d'imprimer les pièces d'armure demandées. Nous vous les "
"transférons maintenant."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The parts are still being printed.  Please be patient."
msgstr ""
"Les pièces sont encore en cours d'impression. Nous vous demandons d'être "
"patient."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sweet, thanks."
msgstr "Merci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "The repairs and tuneup are complete.  Should be good as new or better."
msgstr ""
"Les réparations et la mise au point sont terminées. Il devrait être comme "
"neuf ou mieux."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly; for a fee of ten coins, repairs and adjustments could be completed "
"in two weeks.  We'll also pull suit metrics and haptic data to better "
"understand the situation on the ground.  I'd ask you to make sure everything "
"has been removed from the suit before giving it to us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&The camera starts scanning the armor, after a moment the intercom cracks "
"back to life.  \"This technology is currently not within our database, we can "
"probably repair it but we'll need to reverse-engineer it first.  We estimate "
"the repairs to take around a month and a half, and they'll have an increased "
"fee of 12 coins.  Please make sure everything has been removed from the suit "
"before giving it to us.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[10 HGC] Alright."
msgstr "[10 POH] Ok."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[12 HGC] Fine."
msgstr "[12 POH] Je suppose que ça vaux la dépense."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yes, that is within our capabilities.  For ten coins, repairs and adjustments "
"can be completed by tomorrow; we will recharge the internal battery as well.  "
"Please note that if you have made any modifications to the armor, it will be "
"reverted to factory standard as part of the repairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Certainly, it'll cost you 10 coins and should be ready in two weeks.  "
"Remember to take off any attachments and batteries before turning it in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"One moment,\" the respondent audibly leaves for a moment and after a short "
"period the intercom cracks with life.  \"We have never attempted repairs on a "
"military exoskeleton, we will have to reverse-engineer it first, expect this "
"to take around a month and a half, it will also cost you 12 coins.  Please "
"make sure to take off any attachments and batteries before turning it in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We will begin work shortly.  Report back in two weeks for pickup."
msgstr ""
"Nous commencerons le travail sous peu.  Revenez dans deux semaines pour "
"récupérer votre commande."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We will begin work shortly.  Report back in around one and a half months for "
"pickup."
msgstr ""
"Nous commencerons le travail sous peu.  Revenez dans environ un mois et demi "
"pour récupérer votre commande."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Interesting.  If you could provide us the item, we could direct research on "
"it for a standard work week for a fee of two HGC; after that, we will let you "
"know if any progress has been made and return the item as-is.  Please remove "
"any batteries or other attachments before providing it."
msgstr ""
"Intéressant. Si vous pouviez nous fournir l'objet, nous pourrions mener des "
"recherches dessus pendant une semaine de travail normale pour une somme de "
"deux HGC ; ensuite, nous vous ferons savoir si des progrès ont été réalisés "
"et nous vous rendrons l'objet en l'état. Veuillez retirer les piles et autres "
"accessoires avant de nous fournir l'objet."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC, anchor] See you in five days."
msgstr "[2 POH, ancre] Je reviendrait dans cinq jours."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We've made some notable progress.  The anchor itself appears to provide some "
"degree of protection from extradimensional phenomena, and we believe that we "
"can integrate it into our current modular armor system.  This will, however, "
"make it heavier and less portable.  The armor will remain wearable outside of "
"metal armor, although it will be a more snug fit than the anchor alone would "
"have been.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"We are returning the anchor now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Very well; we will need one coin for materials costs, as well as the anchor "
"itself and the modular defense system you wish to combine it with.  As usual, "
"I encourage you to remove everything from the pockets before handing them "
"over for processing.  We'll need one day for construction and one day to "
"verify efficacy."
msgstr ""
"Très bien, nous aurons besoin d'une pièce pour le coût des matériaux, ainsi "
"que de l'ancre elle-même et du système de défense modulaire auquel vous "
"souhaitez l'associer. Comme d'habitude, je vous encourage à retirer tout ce "
"qui se trouve dans les poches avant de les remettre pour traitement. Nous "
"aurons besoin d'un jour pour la construction et d'un jour pour vérifier "
"l'efficacité."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 HGC, anchor, MDS] I'll see you in two days."
msgstr "[1 POH, ancre, SDM] Je reviendrait dans deux jours."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The anchor has been integrated into the harness.  Thank you as always for "
"your contributions to our research and technology."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Lovely.  Research will begin within the next few hours."
msgstr "Charmant. Les recherches commenceront dans les prochaines heures."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The combination should be a fairly simple matter.  Return in two days to pick "
"up the finished product."
msgstr ""
"La combinaison devrait être assez simple. Revenez dans deux jours pour "
"récupérer le produit fini."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excuse me for a moment.\"  The intercom turns off abruptly.  It comes back on "
"after roughly a minute, and when it speaks again, another voice is on the "
"other side, speaking carefully.\n"
"\n"
"\"Yes… the Exodii.  We have yet to make contact, but we are keenly interested "
"in their capabilities and technology.  If you were to provide us with, say, "
"five rounds, in addition to the rifle itself and a magazine suitable for it, "
"we believe we would be able to replicate the parts.  We expect it to take "
"three days of research.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Please note that the requested materials will not be returned, as they are "
"likely to be damaged during research."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 12.3ln, PA md. 68 magazine, PA md. 68] Is this what you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[5 12.3ln, PS md. 71z magazine, PS md. 71z] Is this what you need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why not contact them directly?"
msgstr "Pourquoi ne pas les contacter directement?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've met them already.  They seem friendly; if you'd like to reach out to "
"them yourself, I'm sure that they could help."
msgstr ""
"Je les ai déjà rencontrés. Ils ont l'air sympathiques ; si vous souhaitez les "
"contacter vous-même, je suis sûr qu'ils pourront vous aider."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"While the Exodii seem benign, our experience with extradimensional life thus "
"far has been… unpleasant, shall we say, given the current state of the world. "
" We find it wise to approach with an abundance of caution.  We are incapable "
"of knowing the true agenda and capabilities of this group, and we believe "
"that understanding some degree of how they operate will allow us to make "
"contact in a more educated way."
msgstr ""
"Bien que les Exodii semblent inoffensifs, notre expérience de la vie "
"extradimensionnelle a été jusqu'à présent... désagréable, dirons-nous, compte "
"tenu de l'état actuel du monde. Nous pensons qu'il est sage d'approcher avec "
"une abondance de prudence. Nous sommes incapables de connaître les véritables "
"intentions et capacités de ce groupe, et nous pensons qu'une certaine "
"compréhension de leur mode de fonctionnement nous permettra d'entrer en "
"contact de manière plus éclairée."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Have you, now?  We are pleased to hear.  However, we still believe that "
"approaching with an excess of wariness is a wise choice.  We feel that it "
"would behoove us to understand more about this group before we approach "
"directly, and so for the time being, understanding more about their "
"general-use technology is our preferred course of action."
msgstr ""
"Et maintenant ? Nous sommes heureux de l'apprendre. Cependant, nous "
"continuons de penser qu'il est sage d'aborder ce groupe avec un excès de "
"méfiance. Nous pensons qu'il est préférable de mieux connaître ce groupe "
"avant de l'approcher directement. Pour l'instant, nous préférons donc nous "
"renseigner sur leur technologie générale."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Brilliant!!  Just brilliant.  Thank you very much.  Please contact us again "
"in three days.  Thank you!\"\n"
"\n"
"The voice abruptly disconnects.  When the intercom comes back on, it's the "
"original voice again.  \"Was there anything else?"
msgstr ""
"Brillant ! Tout simplement génial. Merci beaucoup. Veuillez nous recontacter "
"dans trois jours. Merci !\"\n"
"\n"
"La voix se déconnecte brusquement. Lorsque l'interphone se rallume, c'est à "
"nouveau la voix d'origine. \"Y a-t-il autre chose ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem very… excited about this."
msgstr "Vous avez l'air vraiment… enthousiaste à ce sujet."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The Cataclysm has illuminated hitherto unknown facts about our universe.  The "
"opportunity to research - and perhaps understand - technology from not only "
"another world, but another dimension entirely, is an exceptionally promising "
"field of study.  Now more than ever is our continued delving into this field "
"of study paramount; while our focus has shifted rather abruptly, we believe "
"that if there is ever any chance of understanding or even reversing "
"<the_cataclysm>, it would come from studies like this."
msgstr ""
"Le cataclysme a mis en lumière des faits jusqu'alors inconnus sur notre "
"univers. La possibilité de rechercher - et peut-être de comprendre - une "
"technologie provenant non seulement d'un autre monde, mais aussi d'une autre "
"dimension, est un domaine d'étude exceptionnellement prometteur. Aujourd'hui "
"plus que jamais, il est primordial que nous continuions à explorer ce domaine "
"d'étude ; bien que notre objectif ait changé de façon plutôt abrupte, nous "
"pensons que si nous avons une chance de comprendre ou même d'inverser "
"<the_cataclysm>, c'est grâce à des études comme celle-ci."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The project was a success!  The ammo is fairly rudimentary, but ultimately "
"proved simple to manufacture, and has lent itself well to large magazines.  "
"We will transfer a copy of the conversion kit in a moment; it is capable of "
"accepting specialized magazines that we have just begun to produce ourselves. "
" Thank you for allowing us this opportunity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Given the context of your assignment, we are willing to sell you a set of our "
"protective gear - a gas mask and an environmental suit - at a considerable "
"discount.  We will part with it for two exchange coins.\"  The intercom waits "
"expectantly.  \"Actually, hold on, we might not have one in your size…"
msgstr ""
"Compte tenu du contexte de votre mission, nous sommes disposés à vous vendre "
"un ensemble de nos équipements de protection - un masque à gaz et une "
"combinaison environnementale - à un prix très avantageux. Nous nous en "
"séparerons contre deux pièces d'échange\". L'interphone attend avec "
"impatience. \"En fait, attendez, nous n'en avons peut-être pas à votre "
"taille..."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[2 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr "[2 POH] Marché conclu!"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What will it do for me?"
msgstr "Qu'est-ce qu'il peut faire pour moi ?"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have to give it a thought."
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'y réfléchir un peu."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What the gas mask does should be obvious; we'll provide you with a cartridge, "
"of course.  The environment suit is full-body, and protects you from water, "
"harmful radiation, and environmental hazards.  It's also rated to protect "
"from electric shocks of up to twelve thousand volts.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Bear in mind that the suit isn't armor.  It will keep you safe from the "
"environment, but it's just Nomex and it won't protect you from anything "
"stronger than a punch.  The modular defense system is designed to fit over "
"it, so I'd urge you to bring them both if fighting is unavoidable."
msgstr ""
"La fonction du masque à gaz devrait être évidente ; nous vous fournirons une "
"cartouche, bien sûr. La combinaison environnementale couvre tout le corps et "
"vous protège de l'eau, des radiations nocives et des risques "
"environnementaux. Elle est également conçue pour protéger contre les chocs "
"électriques allant jusqu'à douze mille volts\".\n"
"\n"
"\"Gardez à l'esprit que la combinaison n'est pas une armure. Elle vous "
"protégera de l'environnement, mais ce n'est que du Nomex et elle ne vous "
"protégera pas de quelque chose de plus fort qu'un coup de poing. Le système "
"de défense modulaire est conçu pour s'adapter par-dessus, alors je vous "
"conseille vivement d'apporter les deux si le combat est inévitable."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To assist your operations, we are willing to sell you a map of the local "
"area, as surveyed by our cam-spy drones.  Its standing price is 1 HGC."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[1 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr "[1 POH] Marché conclu!"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent; please deposit the printouts in the intercom's tray.  We'll issue "
"a reward based on the quality of your recordings."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a NRE anomaly printout.]"
msgstr "[Déposer un imprimé d'anomalie de NRE.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a long NRE printout.]"
msgstr "[Déposer un long imprimé de NRE.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit an NRE printout.]"
msgstr "[Déposer un imprimé de NRE.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deposit a short NRE printout.]"
msgstr "[Déposer un imprimé de NRE court.]"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That would be all."
msgstr "Ceci est tout."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Extrapolating trends from these recordings has become difficult.  Research "
"has requested we only accept higher quality data from now on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&\"Thank you.\"  The recording changes hands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Excellent; this should be enough to work with.  Here's your agreed-upon "
"reward.\"  The tray slides shut, and quickly reopens with your payment.  "
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "&\"Excellent.\"  The recording changes hands."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Great!  This looks like a very high-quality recording.  Because this data is "
"much better, we are willing to pay five times what we paid for the base data "
"collected.\"  The tray slides shut, and quickly reopens with your payment.  "
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""
"Fantastique! Ceci a l'air d'être un enregistrement de très haute qualité. Ces "
"données étant de bien meilleure qualité, nous sommes disposés à payer cinq "
"fois ce que nous avons payer pour un enregistrement de qualité ordinaire.\" "
"Le tiroir se referme puis se rouvre rapidement avec votre paiement à "
"l'intérieur. \"Vu votre performance et notre besoin constant de nouvelles "
"données, vous êtes le/la bienvenu(e) à garder l'enregistreur pour des "
"enregistrements ultérieurs que nous serions plus que désireux de vous payer "
"pour acquérir."

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Fantastic.\"  The recording changes hands.  \"At this rate, we'll have some "
"real results soon."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Uh… please allow me a second to check this in.\"  The tray slides shut, and "
"the intercom turns off.  Roughly a minute later, it turns back on.  \"Well, "
"it looks like this is a real treasure trove of information.  In fact, you've "
"made quite an impression on R&D, and probably just saved us a few weeks of "
"research at the least.  They demanded you be given a pretty significant "
"accomplishment bonus, so… well, there you go.\"  The tray slides open, "
"revealing an impressive pile of coins.\n"
"\n"
"\"Given your performance and our constant need for new data, you are free to "
"keep the recorder for further use.  We are willing to pay for any future data "
"that you're able to record."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There is an infinite supply of the stuff but I guess from us you can get it "
"clean and undamaged.  That'll be $400."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[8 HGC] Deal!"
msgstr "[8 POH] Marché conclu!"

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm a little tight on funds right now.  Can we work out a buy now pay later "
"deal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So we'd need a sweeter deal than just the money if we did this."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can pay you what I owe in cash and looted gear."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"If you give me this deal you can have all the alien corpses, their stuff and "
"their tower"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well it might be more interesting than straight gear.  Tell us when it's "
"available for inspection.  We expect you back in 20 days or less."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "20 days then for payment."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Much obliged."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Beautiful; please put them into loading area.  We'll issue a reward depending "
"on what you managed to scavenge."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken trifacet.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken triakis drone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken monolith.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a broken delta drone.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Drag in broken quadraphract leg.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Drag in broken quadraphract.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated trifacet.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated triakis.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated monolith.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[Deliver a deactivated delta.]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We already have a similar model in better condition but this one is useful as "
"a reference."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We can probably gain some insight from studying this unit, but  it appears "
"seriously damaged."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That is quite a lot of broken metal, let's hope R&D can at least salvage some "
"materials."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We don't need all of your glossy scrap."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We witnessed it as a part of larger construct."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm impressed you managed to drag it inside.  We gonna need to fix the lift "
"after this one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I believe we already have similar model already but is nice to have more, it "
"will allow us be more active in our research."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh what an interesting piece.  R&D will have a field day with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I assume you were trying to figure out limits of the hm12.  I guess they are "
"right here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_trades.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I doubt we can get a lot of information from this drone but thanks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "scrapper"
msgstr "ferrailleur"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Haven't seen another face in quite a while.  Not a living one, at least.  "
"State your business.  Maybe you got some use for some of this scrap metal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Pleasure to see you again, <name_g>."
msgstr "Un plaisir de vous revoir <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why stay here of all places?"
msgstr "Pourquoi rester ici de tous les endroits possibles?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I wonder if you've come across "
"it in your travels?"
msgstr ""
"Je suis à la recherche d'un bâtiment spécifique et étrange.  Je me demande si "
"vous l'auriez peut être vu durant vos déplacements?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I know I worked in salvage, but I don't remember much else about it.  I just "
"remember finding this place and deciding to stay here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I held a modest job here as a scrap yard worker.  Business was fair "
"most days, but when <the_cataclysm> hit, I decided to head out here.  With "
"all the craziness going on in the cities and whatnot, I decided to just stay "
"here for while.  I figure someone might find a use for the leftover metal "
"lying around, so I started selling it to anyone who passed by."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, this place had some barbed wire, metalworking tools, and plenty of "
"supplies.  I made the walls myself.  I didn't know of anywhere else to go "
"either."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Like I said, I came out here when the dead got pissed off.  This place had "
"some barbed wire, metalworking tools, and plenty of stuff to make weapons out "
"of.  Even the walls are my own making."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Think I could stay here?"
msgstr "Je peux rester ici?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I'm fine with it.  There's a spare bed in the shed next door for anyone "
"who needs it.  Just don't hog it.  Someone else might come along."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The scrap trader "
"nods along, listening"
msgstr ""
"&Vous décrivez l'entrepôt du mieux que vous pouvez.  Le marchand de ferraille "
"hoche de la tête, écoutant attentivement"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then shrugs.  \"No, sorry, not ringing any bells.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then raises one eyebrow.  \"Not making any promises, but I did catch just a "
"glimpse of a weird building one time that might be what you're looking for.\""
msgstr ""
", puis lève un sourcil.  \"Je ne promets rien, mais j'ai jeté un coup d'œil "
"une fois sur quelque chose d'étrange qui pourrait ressembler à ça.\""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure thing.  I've got a few things on hand.  What'll ya have?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's take a look at your stock."
msgstr "Laissez moi jeter un coup d'œuil à ce que vous avez en stock."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Anything else you need?"
msgstr "Vous avez besoin de quelque chose d'autre?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Find anything good?"
msgstr "Vous avez trouvé quelque chose d'intéressant?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I have another look?"
msgstr "Est-ce que je peux jeter un autre coup d'œil?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nope, although I have a really good claim by the river.  Gonna go fetch them "
"soon, be right back in <interval>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, good luck."
msgstr "Eh bien, bonne chance."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgstr "Trouvez 25 Magnétrons"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Obtain 25 magnetrons in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr "Trouvez 25 magnétrons de pour obtenir un crédit chez le marchand de ferraille."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "I need help…"
msgstr "J'ai besoin d'aide…"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid ""
"Since business is increasing around here, I've decided to start selling more "
"specialized metal.  Problem is, I can't separate the metal out.  Fortunately, "
"I found some old schematics on a machine for this sort of thing.  If you "
"could get me 25 magnetrons, I can melt down the sorted stuff into bars.  I "
"can quickly pay you in raw materials."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid ""
"Magnetrons can be found in microwaves.  An apartment block should have tons "
"of them."
msgstr ""
"Les magnétrons sont l'un des composants des micro-ondes. Une tour "
"d'appartements devrait en avoir une grande quantité."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Do you have the magnetrons?"
msgstr "Vous avez les magnétrons?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
msgid "Wonderful!  I'll start the smelting as soon as possible."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess I'll do it myself."
msgstr "Dommage. Je suppose que je devrais le faire moi-même."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgstr "Obtenez 300 Unités de Charbon de Bois"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid "Obtain 300 lumps of charcoal in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid ""
"That machine I put together is working wonderfully, but the generator is "
"nearly out of juice.  If you could get me 300 lumps of charcoal, I'll pay you "
"however I can."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid ""
"Its fairly simple to make some.  I don't know where you could find any, "
"though."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
msgid "Do you have the charcoal?"
msgstr "Vous avez le charbon de bois?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Wonderful!  This should do for a while."
msgstr "Merveilleux!  Ceci devrait être suffisant pour l'instant."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgstr "Trouvez 100 Unités de Pâte de Soudure"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Obtain 100 solder in exchange for credit with the scrap merchant."
msgstr ""
"Trouvez 100 unités de fil à souder en échange de crédit avec le marchand de "
"ferraille."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid ""
"That machine I put together needs some repairs on it, but I'm out of solder.  "
"If you could get me about 100 spools, I'll pay you for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "An electronics store might have some."
msgstr "Un magasin d'électroménager devrait peut être en avoir."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Do you have the solder?"
msgstr "Vous avez le fil de soudure?"

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Establish trade relations between the scrapper and a refugee center, and "
"bring back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr ""
"Établissez un accord d'échange entre le marchand de ferraille et le centre de "
"réfugiés, et ramenez un contrat signé."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"I was out scavenging recently, and I found one of those old evac shelters.  "
"Turns out the computer was still on and had an address for a refugee center.  "
"I figure they might want some spare metal, so I need you to go over there and "
"strike a deal with them."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Establish trade relations between the scrapper and some artisans."
msgstr "Établissez une relation commerciale entre le ferrailleur et les artisans."

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Business has been booming since you made a deal with that refugee center.  "
"The last caravan that came by here mentioned something about a blacksmith "
"down some old road.  Sounds like another business opportunity, so I need you "
"to go over there and make a deal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"It should be pretty simple making the contract, but I'd recommend taking a "
"car over there myself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "What did they say about the agreement?"
msgstr "Qu'on ils dit au sujet de l'accord?"

