#: data/json/snippets/dimensional_exploration.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "log_immersion27"
msgid "IMMERSION LOG: 27A, INCIDENT REPORT"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/dimensional_exploration.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "log_immersion27"
msgid ""
"\n"
"IMMERSION LOG: 27A\n"
"\n"
"INCIDENT REPORT:\n"
"\n"
"SUMMARY:\n"
"Unforeseen EM interference source forced the team to remain in-phase between "
"prime and sub-scape 27.  Expedition members reported observing a "
"spheroid-entity ('PE-01') moving beneath the typically opaque t-substrate.  "
"Interference readings and expedition testimony implies the PE-01 was a potent "
"EM radiation source, and the origin of the interference.  After 30 min, PE-01 "
"receded and the expedition was aborted in accordance of procedure EMER-12.  "
"The expedition team suffered no injuries during the incident.\n"
"\n"
"It's become clear we have greatly underestimated the risk posed by phase "
"immersions.  Engineering has been tasked with designing a new, improved "
"protection suite, and has shown promising advances.  Updated emergency "
"procedures are in-progress.\n"
"\n"
"Refer to file EXO-I-271 for full report."
msgstr ""
"\n"
"JOURNAL D'IMMERSION: 27A\n"
"\n"
"RAPPORT D'INCIDENT:\n"
"\n"
"SOMMAIRE:\n"
"\n"
"Interférences électromagnétiques imprévues ont forcés l'équipe à rester en "
"phase entre dimension prime et sous-dimension 27. Les membres de l'expédition "
"ont signaler la présence d'un entité sphéroïde (\"PE-01\") se déplaçant en "
"dessous du typiquement opaque substrat-t. Les interférences produites et les "
"témoignages de l'expédition suggèrent que PE-01 est une puissante source de "
"radiation électromagnétique et l'origine des interférences. Après 30 minutes, "
"PE-01 s'est retiré et l'expédition fût rappelée en accordance avec la "
"procédure EMER-12. L'équipe d'expédition n'a souffert aucune blessures durant "
"l'incident.\n"
"\n"
"Il est devenu clair que nous avons largement sous-estimé le risque posé par "
"ses immersions. Le département d'ingénierie a été assigné à la production "
"d'une nouvelle combinaison de protection et a déjà montré plusieurs avancées "
"prometteuses. Une mise à jour des procédures d'urgence est en cours.\n"
"\n"
"Consultez dossier EXO-I-271 pour le rapport complet."

#: data/json/snippets/dimensional_exploration.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "artifact_scp"
msgid "AI-012-PA \"Bakelite Phone\" CONTAINMENT PROCEDURE"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/dimensional_exploration.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "artifact_scp"
msgid ""
"\n"
"DESIGNATION AI-012-PA\n"
"\"Bakelite Phone\"\n"
"\n"
"CONTAINMENT PROCEDURE:\n"
"The object should be kept within an anechoic chamber.  Chamber should be "
"actively monitored in case of ████████ emission leakage.\n"
"\n"
"DESCRIPTION/PARATRONICS:\n"
"An Ericsson ED 702 Bakelite phone, red variant.  The original rotary dial has "
"been replaced by a Bakelite copy of a Yage Y103d spherical doorknob.\n"
"The phone remains fully operational, and even when unconnected to a "
"functional landline, █████████████████████ █████████████████████████████████ "
"████████████.\n"
"Organic matter reacts adversely to such emissions, and the following effects "
"have been observed during live tests: disorientation and fugue states, "
"████████████████████████████████, disintegration, ████████████████ followed "
"by death.\n"
"\n"
"BACKGROUND:\n"
"Recovered during immersion ███ within a manifested copy of ███ █████ office.  "
"The object appearance and paratronic effects are believed to be an imprint of "
"the popular perception surrounding the ██████████/██████ ███████, even "
"although such ███████ never existed in this shape."
msgstr ""

