#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"As you starts to cut through the thick outer crust of the mi-go, you note "
"that it's even tougher than you would have expected."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"The smell emanating from the mi-go as you cut it open is pungent, like a "
"chemical factory gone horribly wrong.  You're forced to take short breaks to "
"recover from nausea."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"You note that the ichorous blood of this creature is unlike any similar stuff "
"you've ever encountered or even heard of.  It's not only the odd color - pink "
"like pepto bismol - but also its texture.  Somehow it is both oily and "
"sticky, and the viscosity seems to change as you work with it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"Nothing seems right with this creature.  The texture of the muscles is off.  "
"Are these even muscles, or are they long stringy organs of some kind?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"You note that what pass for bones in this body have alien shapes and are "
"joined up in ways unlike anything from Earth.  A few times you see intricate "
"interlocking patterns that hold a strange beauty, though it's somewhat "
"lessened by the incredibly terrible smell."
msgstr ""
"Vous notez que ce qui à l'air d'être un squelette interne dans cet organisme "
"a une disposition complètement différente de toute créature issue de cette "
"planète. Vous observez à plusieurs reprises des assemblages intriqués "
"possédant une élégance étrange, un peu ternie par l'odeur chimique "
"envahissante que la carcasse dégage."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest>"
msgid ""
"What should go for tendons in this creature aren't joined to the bones in any "
"way you've seen before.  Instead of a single tendon connecting two end "
"points, there are instead a range of smaller connections between slightly "
"different locations.  On further study you wonder if these are indeed "
"tendons, or perhaps some kind of nerve or signalling structure.  Later, you "
"find similar things wrapped around what you think might be a sensory organ."
msgstr ""
"Ce qui sert de tendons dans cette créature est relié à l’endosquelette d'une "
"manière que vous n'avez jamais observée auparavant. Au lieu d'un seul tendon "
"connectant deux morceaux d'os, ceux-ci sont arrangés en une succession de "
"connections entre morceaux de tendons de différentes longueurs. Après plus "
"d'investigation sur ce sujet vous vous demandez si ceux-ci sont en effet des "
"tendons, ou peut-être une sorte de structure nerveuse ou un autre type de "
"système de relais de signaux. Vous passez encore plus de temps à remonter le "
"long de ce réseau et parvenez à trouver une toile de ces fibres enroulées "
"autour de ce que vous présumez être un organe sensoriel."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"You cannot find a single heart in the mi-go.  Instead, there seem to be "
"multiple copies of something that presumably acts as a heart spread out all "
"over the body.  At least you think it acts as a heart, given how it is "
"connected to what should be blood vessels."
msgstr ""
"Vous n'arrivez pas à trouver quelque chose ressemblant à un cœur à "
"l'intérieur du mi-go, juste plusieurs copies de quelque chose ayant l'air de "
"fonctionner comme une sorte de cœur à travers la carcasse. Du moins vous "
"pensez que ceux-ci ont une fonction analogue à un cœur, vu que ceux-ci sont "
"connectés à ce qui à l'air d'être un système circulatoire."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"Something that looks like it fills a role similar to blood vessels, assuming "
"the pink ichor is in fact blood, form a central plexus that doesn't make much "
"sense to you.  It's impossibly complex, a tiny road map of shockingly tough "
"tubules in a pattern that almost looks like it spells a word in some "
"unknowable language."
msgstr ""
"Il y a quelque chose à l'intérieur ayant l'air de servir de tuyautage pour ce "
"qui à l'air d'être un système sanguin si vous assumez que l'ichor rose est en "
"effet une sorte de sang. Les vaisseaux variés convergent vers une sorte de "
"plexus central ayant une morphologie extrêmement étrange et complexe, un "
"labyrinthe de tubules extraordinairement coriaces formant ce que vous "
"pourriez jurer est une sorte de message utilisant un language vous révoltant "
"instinctivement."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"The creature contains a lot of tissue that probably are organs of one kind of "
"another, but there is no guessing what function they are meant to perform."
msgstr ""
"Cette créature contient beaucoup de tissus que vous supposez être des sortes "
"d'organes, mais vous n'avez même pas une hypothèse plausible au sujet de la "
"fonction de la plupart."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"You think you've found something like a lung: a lot of small orifices all "
"over the body connecting short sections of tubing to organs of spongy tissue, "
"so it might take in air (or water?) through one orifice, extract oxygen from "
"the medium, and \"exhale\" it through the tubing at the other side of the "
"organ.  Just as you feel a sense of understanding something at last, you "
"realize that these organs aren't connected to the ichor system at all, and in "
"fact seem to be drier and more leathery than the rest of the creature."
msgstr ""
"Vous pensez avoir trouvé quelque chose ressemblant à un système pulmonaire, "
"une multitude de petits orifices auxquels sont attachées des sections de tube "
"courtes les connectant à des amas de tissu spongieux, permettant à cette "
"organisme de remplir ceux-ci avec de l'air (ou de l'eau?) à travers un "
"orifice et expirer à travers un autre tube. Juste lorsque vous pensez que "
"vous commencez enfin à comprendre au moins une chose au sujet de cette "
"monstruosité, vous vous rendez compte que ce système n'a pas l'air d'être "
"connecté du tout au système circulatoire ichoreux, et que le tout à l'air "
"bien trop sec et imperméable pour servir comme surface d'échange gazeux."

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"You think you have found the creature's voice box, but you cannot be sure, "
"given its design which leaves you unable to figure out how it would actually "
"work.  It reminds you a bit of an old-fashioned bellows, if a bellows were "
"sky-blue, spongy, and smelled like rotten ammonia."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"There are tough networks of fibers that could be nerves in this thing, but if "
"so, you can't confirm that they lead to any centralized brain.  On the other "
"hand, they could be structural, or muscular.  It's very hard to tell."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"You thought you found its brain, at least until you found another one, and "
"then yet another one, of a different size and shape.  Needless to say, the "
"structure of these organs means nothing to you.  Also, the one in the head is "
"one of the smaller ones."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"It does not seem to have anything resembling eyes, at least not any "
"lens-based design, unless the structure would be too tiny for you to see with "
"the naked eye while everything is covered with blood."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/snippets/mi-go_anatomy.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<mi-go_harvest_deeper>"
msgid ""
"The mi-go's antennae seem to be of different types, but you can't determine "
"what the purpose of any of them is."
msgstr ""

