"Probablement le seul moyen pratique de déplacer ceci sans briser votre dos."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/stowed_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "tied-down golden monolith"
msgstr "monolithe doré ligoté"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/stowed_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "tied-down golden monolith"
msgid ""
"An alien construct, secured to the roof for transportation.  Hopefully it "
"won't reanimate on next road bump."
msgstr ""
"Une machine étrange ayant été ligotée au toit d'un véhicule pour être "
"transportée.  Espérons que celle-ci ne se réanimera pas au premier "
"nid-de-poule."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "vehicle tank (2 L)"
msgstr "réservoir de véhicule (2L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (2 L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (10 L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (20 L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (60 L)"
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for "
"the vehicle's engine, the engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank "
"when the engine is on.  If filled with water, you can access the water from a "
"water faucet, if one is installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber "
"hose to siphon liquids out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir destiné à contenir des liquides. S'il est rempli du carburant "
"approprié pour le moteur du véhicule, celui-ci prélèvera automatiquement le "
"carburant du réservoir lorsque le moteur sera en marche. S'il est rempli "
"d'eau, vous pouvez accéder à l'eau à partir d'un robinet, s'il y en a un dans "
"le véhicule. Vous pouvez également utiliser un tuyau en caoutchouc pour "
"siphonner les liquides d'un réservoir."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "vehicle tank (10 L)"
msgstr "réservoir de véhicule (10L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "vehicle tank (20 L)"
msgstr "réservoir de véhicule (20L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "vehicle tank (60 L)"
msgstr "réservoir de véhicule (60L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "refrigerated tank (60 L)"
msgid ""
"A 60 L refrigerated tank.  When turned on, it will cool the liquid inside, "
"extending the time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir réfrigéré de 60L.  Si celui-ci est connecté à un système "
"électrique, il sera capable de garder au froid les liquides contenus à "
"l'intérieur, repoussant les dates de péremption."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "refrigerated tank (100 L)"
msgid ""
"A 100 L refrigerated tank.  When turned on, it will cool the liquid inside, "
"extending the time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir réfrigéré de 100L.  Si celui-ci est connecté à un système "
"électrique, il sera capable de garder au froid les liquides contenus à "
"l'intérieur, repoussant les dates de péremption."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "heated tank (60 L)"
msgstr "réservoir chauffé (60L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heated tank (60 L)"
msgid ""
"A 60 L heated tank.  When turned on, it will prevent the contents from "
"freezing."
msgstr ""
"Un réservoir chauffé de 60L.  Si celui-ci est connecté à un système "
"électrique, il sera capable d'empêcher les liquides contenus à l'intérieur de "
"geler."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "external tank (100 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe (100L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "external tank (100 L)"
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted outside the vehicle's walls and "
"armor.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If "
"filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (100 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe sur toit (100L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "external tank (200 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe (200L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (200 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe sur toit (200L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "wooden barrel (100 L)"
msgstr "tonneau en bois (100L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden barrel (100 L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "steel drum (100 L)"
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted inside the cargo or passenger "
"space.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If "
"filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "fuel bunker"
msgid "A bin for holding solid fuel."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "small pressurized tank"
msgstr "petit réservoir pressurisé"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "small pressurized tank"
msgid "A tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un réservoir conçu pour garder des gaz sous pression."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "medium pressurized tank"
msgstr "réservoir pressurisé moyen"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "medium pressurized tank"
msgid "A medium tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un réservoir de taille moyenne conçu pour garder des gaz sous pression."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "large pressurized tank"
msgstr "large réservoir pressurisé"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "large pressurized tank"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "XL pressurized tank"
msgid "A large tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un large réservoir conçu pour garder des gaz sous pression."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "XL pressurized tank"
msgstr "réservoir pressurisé XL"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "external aluminum tank (100 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe en aluminium (100L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "roof-mounted external aluminum tank (100 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe sur toit en aluminium (100L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "external aluminum tank (200 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe en aluminium (200L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "roof-mounted external aluminum tank (200 L)"
msgstr "réservoir externe sur toit en aluminium (200L)"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "mounted electric forge"
msgstr "forge électrique installée"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric forge"
msgid ""
"An electric forge for metalworking, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  With "
"a hammer and other tools, you could use this for metalworking.  If you "
"attempt to craft an item that needs a forge, you will be given the option of "
"selecting it as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Une forge électrique pour les projets de métallurgie alimentée par les "
"batteries du véhicule y étant attaché.  Avec un marteau et quelques autres "
"outils vous pourriez utiliser ceci pour forger ou réparer quelque chose.  "
"Vous aurez l'option de l'utiliser comme outil si vous êtes à proximité et une "
"recette demande une forge."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "mounted electric kiln"
msgstr "four électrique installé"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric kiln"
msgid ""
"A electric kiln for baking brick or clay, powered by the vehicle's batteries. "
" You could use this to harden bricks or clay.  If you attempt to craft an "
"item that needs a kiln, you will be given the option of selecting it as a "
"tool."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "mounted electric oil press"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric oil press"
msgid "A heavy-duty press used to create vegetable oil from nuts or seeds."
msgstr ""
"Une large et solide presse utilisée pour extraire des huiles végétales à "
"partir de noix ou de graines."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "door lock set"
msgid_plural "door lock sets"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of "door lock set"
msgid ""
"Some wires and gears for connecting door handles and an unlocking knob to a "
"latching mechanism, and a sturdy lock to go on the outer surface.  It is "
"meant to be installed in a vehicle door or hatch."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "binoculars"
msgstr "jumelles"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "binoculars"
msgid "Binoculars secured near the seat."
msgstr "Une paire de jumelles attachées au siège."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "concrete mixer drum"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "concrete mixer drum"
msgid "A plastic 100-liter drum of a portable concrete mixer."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "yoke and harness"
msgid "Attach this part to a beast of burden to allow it to pull your vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Attachez cette pièce à une bête de somme pour lui permettre de tirer votre "
"véhicule."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "reinforced yoke and harness"
msgid ""
"Attach this part to a beast of burden to allow it to pull your vehicle.  This "
"one is reinforced with heavy chains and steel."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "cart handle"
msgstr "poignée de chariot"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cart handle"
msgid "A metal handle, a creature with hands could use it to push a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Une poignée en métal, une créature avec des mains pourrait l'utiliser pour "
"pousser le véhicule."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "bed"
msgid "A small but comfortable bed."
msgstr "Un petit lit mais néanmoins assez comfortable."

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Vehicle part name
msgid "handle"
msgstr "guidon"

#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "handle"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden handle"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "light wooden handle"
