#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/tools.json
#. ~ Description of "atompot"
msgid ""
"Rivtech's premiere self-heating kitchen appliance, complete with lid, "
"hand-crafted with the power of the atom to reach any temperature in thirty "
"seconds.  As bulky as it is, its plutonium power source means that it can be "
"used to cook an absurd amount of meals without ever worrying about running "
"low on power.  Unsurprisingly, sales weren't particularly good because of the "
"prospect of irradiating your food, but internal shielding ensures that only "
"trace amounts find their way into the center."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/items/tools.json
#. ~ Description of "atomic coffeemaker"
msgid ""
"A Curie-G coffeemaker, made by CuppaTech.  It famously uses a radioactive "
"generator to heat water for coffee.  Normally the water is heated using "
"energy stored in a capacitor, and makes ordinary coffee.  However, as a "
"special feature, water from the RTG containment area can be used, giving the "
"coffee a very special kick.  The Curie-G is illegal in most countries."
msgstr ""
"Ceci est une machine à café Curie-G, un produit de CuppaTech. Cet appareil "
"est célèbre pour son utilisation d'un générateur radioactif miniature utilise "
"pour réchauffer l'eau insérée dans son reservoir. De façon normale, l'eau "
"chauffée est gardée a distance du réacteur. mais la Curie-G a une fonction "
"additionnelle permettant à ceux qui veulent ajouter une touche particulière à "
"leur cafe d'utiliser l'eau du reservoir de refroidissement du réacteur. La "
"machine à café Curie-G est interdite à la vente dans la majorité des systèmes "
"colonisés."

