msgstr "hiss!"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Sentinel-lx"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Sentinels-lx"
msgstr[0] "Sentinelle-lx Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Sentinelles-lx Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Sentinelles-lx Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Sentinel-lx"
msgid ""
"Its exterior plates are sable and gold, this luxurious variant of a Wraitheon "
"drone was once kept as a bodyguard by society's wealthiest.  Still with its "
"wrist sword extended, it resembles an ancient knight, standing an eternal "
"watch."
msgstr ""
"Ses armatures extérieures sont en zibeline et en or. Cette variante luxueuse "
"d'un drone Wraitheon servait autrefois de garde du corps aux personnes les "
"plus fortunées de la société. Toujours avec son épée de poignet déployée, il "
"ressemble à un ancien chevalier qui monte une garde éternelle."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Targeting sound of special attack of monster "Wraitheon Sentinel-lx"
msgid "\"Dispatching hostile with lethal force.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bloodhound drone"
msgid_plural "bloodhound drones"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bloodhound drone"
msgid ""
"A small, spiked quadcopter robot equipped with a high-power spotlight.  This "
"automated seeker drone was originally designed to harry and harass fugitives "
"while maintaining visual contact for other pursuers."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "ENIAC Seneschal"
msgid_plural "ENIAC Seneschals"
msgstr[0] "Sénéchal ENIAC"
msgstr[1] "Sénéchaux ENIAC"
msgstr[2] "Sénéchaux ENIAC"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "ENIAC Seneschal"
msgid ""
"One of the many cheaper models produced by ENIAC.  It is supposedly "
"multi-purpose, and equipped with several tools to facilitate this; however, "
"it is commonly used for janitorial work."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "TsKBEM Likvidator"
msgid_plural "TsKBEM Likvidators"
msgstr[0] "Likvidator TsKBEM"
msgstr[1] "Likvidators TsKBEM"
msgstr[2] "Likvidators TsKBEM"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "TsKBEM Likvidator"
msgid ""
"A now ancient industrial robot line first made by the Soviet TsKBEM, and "
"still in use thanks to its easily obtained fabrication schematics.  Built to "
"operate within nuclear reactors and waste repositories, the Likvidator is "
"assembled around an armored bipedal chassis that mounts several heavy "
"manipulator arms.  Legend claims it was originally designed after a nuclear "
"disaster during early space-age Earth."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "ENIAC Famulus"
msgid_plural "ENIAC Famuli"
msgstr[0] "Famulus ENIAC"
msgstr[1] "Famuli ENIAC"
msgstr[2] "Famuli ENIAC"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "ENIAC Famulus"
msgid ""
"A top of the line luxury model, the Famulus is a humaniform robot, derived "
"from Wraitheon schematics with slight alterations to give it a more human "
"appearance.  Designed to be a robotic servant, its AI tailored for the needs "
"of each customer, it is arguably one of the few commercial robots to pass the "
"Turing test."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "TsKBEM Udarnik"
msgid_plural "TsKBEM Udarniks"
msgstr[0] "Udarnik TsKBEM"
msgstr[1] "Udarniks TsKBEM"
msgstr[2] "Udarniks TsKBEM"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "TsKBEM Udarnik"
msgid ""
"A highly customizable light industrial and agricultural robot.  Its original "
"design dates back to the ancient Soviet Union; the aptly named Udarnik "
"\"shock worker\" was the trigger behind the automation revolution, and with "
"subsequent adaptations, became the workhorse of early human space "
"colonization.  Although outdated by modern standards, the Udarnik is still "
"commonly seen in frontier worlds - thanks to its easily obtainable "
"fabrication schematics.\n"
"\n"
"This particular version is equipped with a mix of construction and heavy "
"cargo-handling tools and was likely involved in the construction of colony "
"buildings."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rampant Udarnik"
msgid_plural "rampant Udarniks"
msgstr[0] "Udarnik erratique"
msgstr[1] "Udarniks erratiques"
msgstr[2] "Udarniks erratiques"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rampant Udarnik"
msgid ""
"An erratic and dangerous Udarnik that mistakenly attempts to hammer "
"everything on its sights.  Although this corrupted robot is not built for "
"combat, its sheer size and hydraulic strength make it extremely dangerous up "
"close."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
#. ~ Its in Russian.  Not a typo.
msgid "TsKBEM Zenit"
msgid_plural "TsKBEM Zenit"
msgstr[0] "Zenit TsKBEM"
msgstr[1] "Zenits TsKBEM"
msgstr[2] "Zenits TsKBEM"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "TsKBEM Zenit"
msgid ""
"An ancient security drone intended to safeguard extractive outposts in "
"hostile environments.  Its construction vaguely recalls an alien crustacean, "
"with a single sensory oculus and four spade-like legs mounted underneath a "
"disk of space-ship grade armor.  Zenit units can mount a wide variety of "
"\"deterrent\" weapon modules, and its difficult to tell what this rogue unit "
"is capable of."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "TsKBEM Brandspojt"
msgid_plural "TsKBEM Brandspojts"
msgstr[0] "Brandspojt TsKBEM"
msgstr[1] "Brandspojts TsKBEM"
msgstr[2] "Brandspojts TsKBEM"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "TsKBEM Brandspojt"
msgid ""
"An old and decidedly uncommon firefighter robot of Soviet design.  Crab-like "
"in form, its back mounts a squat water tank beneath a turreted water cannon.  "
"While effective for its original function, the design lacks the flexibility "
"of others from the TsKBEM, and most Brandspojt units still in existence are "
"museum pieces."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Croplord 2SPL"
msgid_plural "Croplord 2SPLs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Croplord 2SPL"
msgid ""
"Twin linked rotors allow this ubiquitous EINAC drone to comfortably hover "
"above fields and deploy pesticides at prodigious rates.  They have no ability "
"to detect humans within their work areas and will readily disperse lethal "
"pesticides near them."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "Croplord 2SPL"
msgid "The Croplord crashes into the ground."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "faulty surgical droid"
msgid_plural "faulty surgical droids"
msgstr[0] "droïde chirurgien défectueux"
msgstr[1] "droïdes chirurgiens défectueux"
msgstr[2] "droïdes chirurgiens défectueux"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "faulty surgical droid"
msgid ""
"A free roaming medical robot capable of administering powerful anesthetics "
"and performing complex surgical operations, usually in that order.  Faulty "
"bio-diagnostic programs resulted in numerous lawsuits before the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rat snatcher"
msgid_plural "rat snatchers"
msgstr[0] "robot dératiseur"
msgstr[1] "robots dératiseurs"
msgstr[2] "robots dératiseurs"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rat snatcher"
msgid ""
"A small and flimsy hexapod drone that relies on sheer speed to hunt rats and "
"other small pests.  It has either gone rampant or been maliciously "
"reprogrammed."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "grab-bot"
msgid_plural "grab-bots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "grab-bot"
msgid ""
"A salvaged skitterbot repurposed to grab onto and immobilize enemies.  It's "
"meant to work in a pack."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pest hunter"
msgid_plural "pest hunters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pest hunter"
msgid ""
"A salvaged skitterbot refitted with an 8mm integrated firearm.  The robot's "
"small size precludes rapid-fire, due to recoil, and requires the use of "
"lightweight caseless ammo."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "UICA Imaginifer MP"
msgid_plural "UICA Imaginifer MP"
msgstr[0] "policier militaire ACIU Imaginifer"
msgstr[1] "policiers militaires ACIU Imaginifer"
msgstr[2] "policiers militaires ACIU Imaginifer"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "UICA Imaginifer MP"
msgid ""
"A supposedly non-combat refit of Wraitheon's Imaginifer series, outfitted for "
"crowd control and riot suppression.  This unit is outfitted with a beanbag "
"shotgun and a taser and has been painted in the white and blue scheme of "
"UICA's military police."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ No ammo sound of special attack of monster "UICA Imaginifer MP"
msgid "click click!"
msgstr "click click!"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Imaginifer"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Imaginifers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Imaginifer"
msgid ""
"Imaginifers are Wraitheon Industries standard military humaniforms, company "
"parlance for an android designed to seamlessly integrate into standard "
"infantry units.  Although originally designed for UICA's expeditionary forces "
"they are now commonly employed by any faction that can afford them.  This "
"particular unit seems to belong to the Company itself.\n"
"\n"
"Wraitheon humaniforms are designed to take full advantage of a humanoid "
"shape, not to look human; programmed for game theory, not for sapience."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Hashashiyyin"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Hashashiyyins"
msgstr[0] "Hashashiyyin Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Hashashiyyins Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Hashashiyyins Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Hashashiyyin"
msgid ""
"An imaginifer variant of unorthodox design, the Hashashiyyin dispenses with "
"most of its armor in favor of active-camo systems and a lightweight, more "
"agile frame.  Commonly employed in scouting and counter-sniping roles.  This "
"unit is equipped for close range ambush, and weilds a 35x50mm dart gun."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Suppressor"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Suppressors"
msgstr[0] "Suppresseur Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Suppresseurs Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Suppresseurs Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Suppressor"
msgid ""
"Looking more like a tank than a robot, the Suppressor is built to deal with "
"vehicles (including tanks) and personnel alike.  Equipped with a 40mm grenade "
"launcher, it can easily dispatch anything in its path."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Fulgent"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Fulgent"
msgstr[0] "Fulgent Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Fulgents Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Fulgents Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Fulgent"
msgid ""
"An autonomous anti-personnel weapons platform, mounting a laser on an "
"insectoid chassis.  The Fulgent designation excels at 'controlling' riots and "
"(sometimes simultaneously) putting down potential freedom fighters."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Irradiant"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Irradiants"
msgstr[0] "Irradiant Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Irradiants Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Irradiants Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Irradiant"
msgid ""
"An autonomous anti-armor weapons platform, mounting a 5kg plasma railgun over "
"an insectoid chassis.  The Irradiant designation excels at ambush and "
"midrange combat, where it can leverage its superior agility and reduced "
"sensor profile to successfully engage technologically advanced foes."
msgstr ""
"Plate-forme d'armes anti-blindées autonome, dotée d'un ÉlectroCanon à plasma "
"de 5 kg sur un châssis insectoïde. La désignation Irradiant excelle dans les "
"embuscades et les combats de moyenne portée, où elle peut tirer parti de son "
"agilité supérieure et de son profil de détection réduit pour engager avec "
"succès des ennemis technologiquement avancés."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "Wraitheon Irradiant"
msgid "The Irradiant emits a chilling robotic shrill as it fires its plasma railgun."
msgstr ""
"L'Irradiant émet une stridulation robotique glaciale lorsqu'il tire avec son "
"ÉlectroCanon à plasma."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Targeting sound of special attack of monster "Wraitheon Irradiant"
msgid "the climbing pitch of a charging plasma railgun"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Isohypsa"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Isohypsas"
msgstr[0] "Isohypsa Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Isohypsas Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Isohypsas Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Isohypsa"
msgid ""
"A bulky aerial drone that mounts an advanced AI overwatch unit within it "
"bulbous carapace-like armor.  As an autonomous drone control platform, the "
"Isohypsa is principally meant to coordinate and enhance the combat "
"capabilities of simpler Wraitheon robots in lieu of human operators."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "Wraitheon Isohypsa"
msgid "The Isohypsa emits a rapid sequence of sibilant tones!"
msgstr "L'Isohypsa émets une séquence rapide de sons sibyllins!"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Kabura-ya"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Kabura-ya"
msgstr[0] "Kabura-ya Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Kabura-yas Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Kabura-yas Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Kabura-ya"
msgid ""
"A microplane drone designed to seek enemy personnel before detonating at "
"close range."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Wraitheon Frequency"
msgid_plural "Wraitheon Frequencies"
msgstr[0] "Disrupteur Wraitheon"
msgstr[1] "Disrupteurs Wraitheon"
msgstr[2] "Disrupteurs Wraitheon"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Wraitheon Frequency"
msgid ""
"An autonomous weapons platform, made to disrupt or disable electronics - "
"especially other robots - with an electromagnetic pulse."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "shock-mine"
msgid_plural "shock-mines"
msgstr[0] "mine éléctrocuteuse"
msgstr[1] "mines éléctrocuteuses"
msgstr[2] "mines éléctrocuteuses"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "shock-mine"
msgid ""
"A bulky device that will constantly discharge electricity in a small radius "
"around it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "eyebot"
msgid_plural "eyebots"
msgstr[0] "eyebot"
msgstr[1] "eyebots"
msgstr[2] "eyebots"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "eyebot"
msgid ""
"A quadcopter drone largely comprised of a high-resolution camera lens and a "
"speaker, this robot hovers above the ground, documenting the carnage and "
"mayhem around it.  While it is no longer able to report to a central "
"authority, it's likely that some of its automated alert systems are still "
"functional, given that the thing seems to have an operational charging "
"station somewhere."
msgstr ""
"Un drone quadricoptère largement composé d'une lentille de caméra à haute "
"résolution et d'un haut-parleur. Ce robot plane à quelques mètres du sol, "
"documentant le carnage et le chaos tout autour de lui. Bien qu'il ne soit "
"plus capable de rendre compte à ses supérieurs, il est probable que "
"quelques-uns de ses systèmes d'alerte automatiques fonctionnent toujours, vu "
"que le fait que celui-ci soit encore fonctionnel suggère qu'il possède une "
"station de recharge opérationnelle dans les environs."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "police bot"
msgid_plural "police bots"
msgstr[0] "robot policier"
msgstr[1] "robots policiers"
msgstr[2] "robots policiers"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "police bot"
msgid ""
"One of the many models of armored law enforcement robots employed shortly "
"before the collapse of civilization.  Solar powered like many other robots, "
"it maintains its programmed pursuit of law and order, propelled on a trio of "
"omni wheels."
msgstr ""
"Un des nombreux modèles de robots blindé de maintien de l'ordre employés peu "
"avant la chute de la civilisation. Doté d'une alimentation solaire, comme de "
"nombreux autres robots, il continue à exécuter son programme de maintien de "
"l'ordre sur son trio de roues omni-directionnelles.   "

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "riot control bot"
msgid_plural "riot control bots"
msgstr[0] "robot anti-émeutes"
msgstr[1] "robots anti-émeutes"
msgstr[2] "robots anti-émeutes"

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "riot control bot"
msgid ""
"A nonviolent riot-control bot, designed to suppress riots and make mass "
"arrests of those participating.  Though its relaxation gas is by far its "
"best-known weapon, it carries a blinding spotlight and a low-powered stungun "
"for self-defense--in addition to a supply of electronic handcuffs."
msgstr ""
"Un robot anti-émeutes non violent. Conçu pour neutraliser des groupes entiers "
"d'émeutiers et les arrêter en masse. Son gaz relaxant est son arme "
"principale, il possède également une grenade flash, un pistolet paralysant et "
"des menottes électroniques."

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "STEED"
msgid_plural "STEEDs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of monster "STEED"
msgid ""
"Found on nearly every frontier planet, the ubiquitous TSKBEM STEED (Surface "
"Traversing Equine Emulating Drone) is an incredibly rugged quadrupedal "
"machine based on old Earth horses and mules.  Capable of crossing the "
"roughest terrain, powered by a compact atomic reactor, generous storage "
"capacity, light armor, and a lifetime warranty, the STEED is a priceless tool "
"for prospectors and homesteaders.  This version has been ruggedized against "
"Salus IV's extreme cold, but does not keep you warm while riding."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Feed message of monster "STEED"
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The %s activates as you swipe the registry key.  A nearly inaudible hum is "
"the only indication the STEED is active."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "broken STEED"
msgid_plural "broken STEEDs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Description of "broken STEED"
msgid ""
"A broken STEED, it looks beyond repair.  At least the atomic core shielding "
"should be intact."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "UICA Irradiant"
msgid_plural "UICA Irradiants"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Aftershock/mobs/robots.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/monsters/robots.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "UICA Regulator"
msgid_plural "UICA Regulators"
msgstr[0] "Régulateur UICA"
msgstr[1] "Régulateurs UICA"
msgstr[2] "Régulateurs UICA"

