msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Tome of the Hollow Earth"
msgid ""
"This large dusty spellbook seems perpetually, well, dusty.  It contains a "
"considerable amount of earthly power."
msgstr ""
"Ce grimoire énorme et poussiéreux à l'air de rester perpétuellement, eh bien, "
"poussiéreux.  Vous ressentez une quantité de pouvoir terrestre considérable "
"s'en émanant."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Memoirs of the Champion of Earth"
msgid_plural "copies of Memoirs of the Champion of Earth"
msgstr[0] "Les Mémoires du Champion de la Terre"
msgstr[1] "copies de Les Mémoires du Champion de la Terre"
msgstr[2] "copies de Les Mémoires du Champion de la Terre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Memoirs of the Champion of Earth"
msgid ""
"A book written by someone obviously very self-absorbed who describes himself "
"as \"Chosen of Gaia, the Only Champion of Terra\".  Despite his arrogance, "
"his mastery in combining different earthshaper's abilities as described in "
"the book make him an accomplished sorcerer worth learning from."
msgstr ""
"Un livre écrit par quelqu'un évidemment extrêmement nombriliste se nommant "
"\"Élu de Gaïa, le Champion Unique de Terra\".  Malgré son arrogance, la "
"maîtrise de différents pouvoirs de façonneur de terre et la capacité à les "
"mêler efficacement étant décrites à travers les pages de cette ouvrage font "
"de lui un sorcier talentueux que vous feriez mieux de suivre l'exemple."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "One Spell is All You Need!"
msgid_plural "copies of One Spell is All You Need!"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "One Spell is All You Need!"
msgid ""
"This advertising booklet promotes one spell that allows you to create a "
"different tool for different purposes.  Surprisingly, it works as the book "
"says - you can change the shape of your tool, depending on your needs."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Tome of Magical Movement"
msgid_plural "copies of The Tome of Magical Movement"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Tome of Magical Movement"
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This small lightweight book seems to almost not entirely exist, let's say it "
"97% does.  It contains Magus spells focused on movement."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Smudged Scroll"
msgid_plural "Smudged Scrolls"
msgstr[0] "Parchemin Barbouillé"
msgstr[1] "Parchemins Barbouillés"
msgstr[2] "Parchemins Barbouillés"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Smudged Scroll"
msgid ""
"This looks like someone was designing a new spell, but spilled a mug of "
"coffee on it and crumpled it up in anger.  You can tell that it will "
"definitely cast something, but you can't be sure that it will work very well."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
msgid_plural "copies of Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Necromantic Minions for Dummies"
msgid ""
"This book details various ways of summoning an undead minion to fight for "
"you.  They all appear to disappear after a short time, crumbling to dust."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Fundamentals of Technomancy"
msgid_plural "copies of Fundamentals of Technomancy"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Fundamentals of Technomancy"
msgid ""
"This thick manual instructs the spellcaster on manipulating and empowering "
"various forms of matter and energy."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
msgid_plural "copies of Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Complete Idiot's Guide to Technomancy"
msgid ""
"This colorful guide, full of diagrams and cartoons, teaches a couple of very "
"basic Technomancy spells for the not-so-bright pupils."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
msgid_plural "copies of Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Technomancy and the Electromagnetic Spectrum"
msgid ""
"This lab reference material book is thick and overflowing with information on "
"combining magic with EM radiation."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Mage-Engineer's Practical Guide"
msgid_plural "copies of The Mage-Engineer's Practical Guide"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Mage-Engineer's Practical Guide"
msgid ""
"This is a heavy, university thaumaturgical-program-level guidebook.  It "
"discusses the various practical applications of magic in repairwork and "
"engineering, with a focus on immediately-usable techniques instead of airy "
"theoretical approaches."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Liminal Pathways"
msgid_plural "copies of Liminal Pathways"
msgstr[0] "Sentiers Liminaires"
msgstr[1] "copies de Sentiers Liminaires"
msgstr[2] "copies de Sentiers Liminaires"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Liminal Pathways"
msgid ""
"A famous animist grimoire from early modernity.  Its cryptic passages "
"describe and map connections between the spiritual world and ours."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Runic Tablet shard"
msgid_plural "Runic Tablet shards"
msgstr[0] "éclat de tablette runique"
msgstr[1] "éclats de tablette runique"
msgstr[2] "éclats de tablette runique"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Runic Tablet shard"
msgid ""
"A small tablet of blackened stone, apparently cut from a much larger slab.  "
"Golden runes glow over its surface, and slowly shift into intelligible "
"sentences when you stare at them."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
msgid_plural "copies of Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Geospatial Systems: The Lie Of Linearity"
msgid ""
"This book outlines in great detail how time and space are wibbly-wobbly and "
"non-Euclidean.  It also appears to have a dozen different coordinate systems "
"that it uses nearly interchangeably, which makes it hard to follow.  There's "
"lots of jargon, but with intense study you can probably learn a thing or two "
"about portals."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Forbidden Tome"
msgid_plural "Forbidden Tomes"
msgstr[0] "Tome Proscrit"
msgstr[1] "Tomes Proscrits"
msgstr[2] "Tomes Proscrits"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Forbidden Tome"
msgid ""
"A very, very old and heavy tome of various spells lost to the ages, either "
"for good reason, or simply through the passage of time.  There are very few "
"copies in existence, usually owned by those of great power, and yet all of "
"them seem to have the last dozen pages or so torn out, in haste."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Transcendence of the Human Condition"
msgid_plural "copies of Transcendence of the Human Condition"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Transcendence of the Human Condition"
msgid ""
"The Human is the only creature that seeks to improve himself.  This study "
"examines different spells that can heighten various senses temporarily, in "
"hopes to discover a more permanent solution."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
msgid_plural "copies of Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Wherever You've Gone, There You Can Be"
msgid ""
"A very sarcastically-written guide to using magic to get into and out of "
"places you absolutely are not supposed to be."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
msgid_plural "copies of It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "It's the End of the World, But You'll Feel Fine"
msgid ""
"This thick paperback book is a collection of the proper magical preparations "
"to survive various disasters.  Unfortunately, the zombie apocalypse section "
"doesn't account for everything that's gone wrong in the Cataclysm, but "
"there's still a lot of useful knowledge here."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Elven Path"
msgid ""
"Written by the elven archdruid Tylindel Melithilarahd over 500 years ago, "
"this weighty tome was considered *the* most important book of the Harmonist "
"druidic movement up until just before the Cataclysm.  Archdruid "
"Melithilarahd's death in 2016 ended his overt patronage of his own works, "
"allowing other writers to attempt to make their mark, especially younger "
"elves who did not have such a strident anti-modern attitude.  In addition to "
"all the philosophical essays about the importance of living in harmony with "
"nature and allowing plants to grow where they will are several plant-based "
"druidic spells."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Lazy Mage's How-to Guide"
msgid_plural "copies of The Lazy Mage's How-to Guide"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Lazy Mage's How-to Guide"
msgid ""
"A thin book full of spells designed to help the practitioner short-cut having "
"to actually do any work.  Considering the effort involved in studying magic, "
"you're not sure any actual time is being saved."
msgstr ""
"Un petit livre de sorts censés aider l'apprenti éviter de vraiment "
"travailler. Considérant l'effort nécessaire pour étudier la magie dés le "
"départ, vous n'êtes pas sûr(e) que ceci puisse faire gagner du temps à qui "
"que ce soit."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Arcano-hiking for Fun"
msgid_plural "copies of Arcano-hiking for Fun"
msgstr[0] "Se Divertir avec la Rando Arcanique"
msgstr[1] "copies de Se Divertir avec la Rando Arcanique"
msgstr[2] "copies de Se Divertir avec la Rando Arcanique"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Arcano-hiking for Fun"
msgid ""
"A thin book about the usefulness of magic in hiking, such as keeping clean, "
"keeping the weather good, staying dry, and otherwise avoiding all the "
"problems of the mundane outdoors."
msgstr ""
"Un petit libre traitant de l'utilité de la magie pour les randonneurs, pour "
"rester propre, sec et une myriade d'autre problèmes que quelqu'un pourrait "
"rencontrer au milieu de la cambrousse."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Effects of Technological Progress on Magic"
msgid_plural "copies of The Effects of Technological Progress on Magic"
msgstr[0] "Les Effets du Progrès Technologique sur la Magie"
msgstr[1] "copies de Les Effets du Progrès Technologique sur la Magie"
msgstr[2] "copies de Les Effets du Progrès Technologique sur la Magie"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Effects of Technological Progress on Magic"
msgid ""
"A thick book about the history of magic's interactions with technology.  It "
"delves deeply into why technological solutions have mostly replaced magic in "
"daily life even though mages can have immense personal power: the "
"incompatibility of Control and Harmony schools, the technological ease-of-use "
"from the end-user perspective, and even the way some nations' legal systems "
"have worked to discourage magic use so as to prevent individuals from "
"attaining too much power."
msgstr ""
"Un livre épais ayant pour sujet l'histoire de la relation entre la magie et "
"le progrès technologique.  Aborde de façon exhaustive pourquoi les solutions "
"technologiques ont remplacées la magie dans la majorité de la vie quotidienne "
"malgré le fait que les mages soient capables d'atteindre une vaste quantité "
"de pouvoir personnel en discutant de l'incompatibilité des écoles de pensée "
"du Contrôle et de l'Harmonie, la praticité de la technologie pour "
"l'utilisateur et la création de systèmes légaux dans certaines nations pour "
"administrer et rendre comptables les magiciens."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Home Mage's Healthcare Manual"
msgid_plural "copies of The Home Mage's Healthcare Manual"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Home Mage's Healthcare Manual"
msgid ""
"A reference book for the practical use of magic in healing the sort of wounds "
"that are likely to occur at home: burns from cooking, scraped knees, cuts "
"from knives, bruises, colds and the flu, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid ""
"Travels Among the Ljósálfar: Their Customs, Food, Lifestyle, Celebrations, "
"and Ceremonies"
msgid_plural ""
"copies of Travels Among the Ljósálfar: Their Customs, Food, Lifestyle, "
"Celebrations, and Ceremonies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Travels Among the Ljósálfar: Their Customs, Food,
#. Lifestyle, Celebrations, and Ceremonies"
msgid ""
"An old 19th-century travelogue, detailing the author's travels among the "
"elven tribes of northern Greenland.  The section about the midwinter festival "
"and the northern lights is particularly detailed."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Storm Chasing In Complete Safety"
msgid_plural "copies of Storm Chasing In Complete Safety"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Storm Chasing In Complete Safety"
msgid ""
"A description of weather patterns, geological formations in particularly "
"storm-prone areas, essays from well-known storm chasers, proper equipment and "
"safety, how to keep dry, and a way to use magic to completely avoid any "
"possible danger from the storm itself.  The book does explicitly warn that if "
"a tree falls on you, you're on your own, though, so the title seems to be "
"more than half marketing."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Fashion Over Function: A Thaumaturgical Guide to Wearing Whatever, Whenever"
msgid_plural ""
"copies of Fashion Over Function: A Thaumaturgical Guide to Wearing Whatever, "
"Whenever"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Fashion Over Function: A Thaumaturgical Guide to Wearing
#. Whatever, Whenever"
msgid ""
"A thin guide to using magic to avoid extremes of both hot and cold, allowing "
"you to design your wardrobe around always looking good rather than having to "
"account for summer's heat or winter's chill."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "A Cat Cafe at Home!"
msgid_plural "copies of A Cat Cafe at Home!"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "A Cat Cafe at Home!"
msgid ""
"A very thin book, filled with glossy photos, about how to use druidic magic "
"to call up cats whenever you are feeling lonely, if you can't afford one, or "
"if you live in a place that doesn't normally allow pets.  The people in the "
"photos watching half-a-dozen cats play sure look happy."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Save Water and Time, with Magic!"
msgid_plural "copies of Save Water and Time, with Magic!"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Save Water and Time, with Magic!"
msgid ""
"This very thin booklet about the ecological benefits of using magic instead "
"of a mundane morning cleaning routine.  At the bottom of the back cover is an "
"abstract logo of two people holding both hands with a tree growing through "
"the resulting circle, and the words \"Gaia's Children\" beneath it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Mystic Survival in the End Times"
msgid_plural "copies of Mystic Survival in the End Times"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Mystic Survival in the End Times"
msgid ""
"A somewhat alarmist book about the ways to survive after the collapse of "
"civilization, using simple magic to deal with common problems.  Sadly, there "
"are no anti-zombie combat spells within."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Landscaping with Earthshaping"
msgid_plural "copies of Landscaping with Earthshaping"
msgstr[0] "Le Paysagiste Façonneur de Terre"
msgstr[1] "copies de Le Paysagiste Façonneur de Terre"
msgstr[2] "copies de Le Paysagiste Façonneur de Terre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Landscaping with Earthshaping"
msgid ""
"A guide to using earthshaping magic to shortcut the backbreaking work of "
"digging and hauling needed to redo one's yard."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Limitations of the Mana Economy"
msgid_plural "copies of The Limitations of the Mana Economy"
msgstr[0] "Les Limitations de l'Économie Magique"
msgstr[1] "copies de Les Limitations de l'Économie Magique"
msgstr[2] "copies de Les Limitations de l'Économie Magique"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Limitations of the Mana Economy"
msgid ""
"A study of the inherent non-scalability of magical solutions to problems, "
"touching on the difficulty of producing crystallized mana in the quantities "
"needed for industrial use, the long time period necessary for magical "
"materials like orichalcum, mithril, or crimsonite to reach reliability, the "
"way that earthshaping and druidism specifically require wilderness for some "
"of their spells, and the way that an average mage exhausts their mana pool "
"within fifteen minutes of working on any major project without extensive "
"study and training."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Make Your Own Special Effects"
msgid_plural "copies of Make Your Own Special Effects"
msgstr[0] "Comment Faire Ses Propres Effets Spéciaux"
msgstr[1] "copies de Comment Faire Ses Propres Effets Spéciaux"
msgstr[2] "copies de Comment Faire Ses Propres Effets Spéciaux"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Make Your Own Special Effects"
msgid ""
"A guide to using magic to create practical special effects, whether for a "
"birthday celebration, house party, or simply for your own amusement."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Gardening the Druidic Way"
msgid_plural "copies of Gardening the Druidic Way"
msgstr[0] "Jardiner comme les Druides"
msgstr[1] "copies de Jardiner comme les Druides"
msgstr[2] "copies de Jardiner comme les Druides"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Gardening the Druidic Way"
msgid ""
"A reference tome for using magic to garden in a \"organic, traditional, "
"earth-centered way\", as the back cover states."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Let No Wall Stand in Your Way!"
msgid_plural "copies of Let No Wall Stand in Your Way!"
msgstr[0] "Ne Laissez Aucun Mur se Dresser Devant Vous!"
msgstr[1] "copies de Ne Laissez Aucun Mur se Dresser Devant Vous!"
msgstr[2] "copies de Ne Laissez Aucun Mur se Dresser Devant Vous!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Let No Wall Stand in Your Way!"
msgid ""
"This book claims to be an aid to people who always forget their keys or need "
"to get into their car quickly, but the selection of spells seems pretty "
"suspicious to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "A Study of Nethereum Incursions"
msgid_plural "copies of A Study of Nethereum Incursions"
msgstr[0] "copie de Une Étude sur les Incursions du Néant"
msgstr[1] "copies de Une Étude sur les Incursions du Néant"
msgstr[2] "copies de Une Étude sur les Incursions du Néant"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "A Study of Nethereum Incursions"
msgid ""
"An academic book about the history of known Nethereum incursions, including "
"the 1908 Tunguska incident, the disappearance of the army of Cambyses, "
"various dancing plagues, the earthquake that destroyed the kingdom of "
"Mgarzhbag, the Week Without Sun in the 7th century, and more, along with a "
"variety of speculation about possible other historical and pre-historical "
"incursions."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Born of a Gale: A Taxonomy of Air and Weather Spirits"
msgid_plural "copies of Born of a Gale: A Taxonomy of Air and Weather Spirits"
msgstr[0] "Nés d'une Bourrasque: Une Taxonomie des Esprits Aériens et Météorologiques"
msgstr[1] ""
"copies de Nés d'une Bourrasque: Une Taxonomie des Esprits Aériens et "
"Météorologiques"
msgstr[2] ""
"copies de Nés d'une Bourrasque: Une Taxonomie des Esprits Aériens et "
"Météorologiques"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Born of a Gale: A Taxonomy of Air and Weather Spirits"
msgid ""
"A formal study of the various sylphs, anemoi, shedim, hytersprites, hyades, "
"ame-onna, and other spirits associated with air, wind, or weather."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Akyâluaban and Ghâzkhud are words from a fictional language and should
#. not be translated.
msgid "Akyâluaban: the Book of the Living Stone"
msgid_plural "copies of Akyâluaban: the Book of the Living Stone"
msgstr[0] "Akyâluaban: le Livre de la Pierre Vivante"
msgstr[1] "copies de l'Akyâluaban: le Livre de la Pierre Vivante"
msgstr[2] "copies de l'Akyâluaban: le Livre de la Pierre Vivante"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Akyâluaban: the Book of the Living Stone"
msgid ""
"A copy of a religious text from the Ghâzkhud dwarven religion.  Amidst the "
"prayers and songs and meditations on the ancestors and the earth and the "
"stones are some spells, though pious traditional ghâzkhudians would react "
"with shock if you called them that."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Magical Method of Tidying Up"
msgid_plural "copies of The Magical Method of Tidying Up"
msgstr[0] "Faire le Ménage Magiquement"
msgstr[1] "copies de Faire le Ménage Magiquement"
msgstr[2] "copies de Faire le Ménage Magiquement"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Magical Method of Tidying Up"
msgid ""
"This obvious cash-in book does have some actual practical spells amongst all "
"the philosophical-sounding essays about the importance of cleanliness."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Healing Power of Nature"
msgid_plural "copies of The Healing Power of Nature"
msgstr[0] "Le Pouvoir de Guérison de la Nature"
msgstr[1] "copies de Le Pouvoir de Guérison de la Nature"
msgstr[2] "copies de Le Pouvoir de Guérison de la Nature"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "The Healing Power of Nature"
msgid ""
"A description of the various ways to use natural herbs and plants to fuel "
"magical healing.  There is a lot of useful knowledge of here if you sift "
"through the book and filter out the various chapters about the dangers of "
"allopathic medicine and modern post-industrial lifestyles."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Now You See We: Technomantic Transit In Action"
msgid_plural "copies of Now You See We: Technomantic Transit In Action"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Now You See We: Technomantic Transit In Action"
msgid ""
"A book about how technomancy, usually thought of as being based around "
"electricity and human enhancement, somehow also encompasses quick moment but "
"only when holograms are involved.  At least half the book is descriptions of "
"experiments performed by research thaumaturges to find the exact boundaries "
"of technomancy when movement is involved."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Magical Mishaps: When Spells Go Wrong"
msgid_plural "copies of Magical Mishaps: When Spells Go Wrong"
msgstr[0] "Mésaventures Magiques: Lorsque les Sorts Tournent Mal"
msgstr[1] "copies de Mésaventures Magiques: Lorsque les Sorts Tournent Mal"
msgstr[2] "copies de Mésaventures Magiques: Lorsque les Sorts Tournent Mal"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Magical Mishaps: When Spells Go Wrong"
msgid ""
"A series of stories of the various ways magic can go wrong if the wrong "
"ingredients, words, or gestures are used.  A lot of the stories are merely "
"funny, like the magus who in trying to alter the Sorcerer's Hand spell caused "
"music to follow her everywhere she went, but there's the occasional real "
"tragedy mixed in as a cautionary tale."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Intermittent Fasting Using Biomancy"
msgid_plural "copies of Intermittent Fasting Using Biomancy"
msgstr[0] "Le Jeûne Intermittent à l'Aide de la Biomancie"
msgstr[1] "copies de Le Jeûne Intermittent à l'Aide de la Biomancie"
msgstr[2] "copies de Le Jeûne Intermittent à l'Aide de la Biomancie"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "Intermittent Fasting Using Biomancy"
msgid ""
"A guide to using biomancy to perform extreme intermittent fasting, eating an "
"enormous amount of food only once every 2-5 days, depending on the mage's "
"skill.  The book is filled with both glossy photos of extremely fit, "
"beautiful people and warnings to make sure that your stomach isn't full when "
"the spell wears off."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "A Year of Living Without Magic"
msgid_plural "copies of A Year of Living Without Magic"
msgstr[0] "Vivre un An Sans Magie"
msgstr[1] "copies de Vivre un An Sans Magie"
msgstr[2] "copies de Vivre un An Sans Magie"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
#. ~ Description of "A Year of Living Without Magic"
msgid ""
"A guide to living without any magic at all, including ways to perform tasks "
"that were traditionally performed with magic, such as starting fires, tending "
"minor wounds, cooking and preserving food, doing laundry, and so on.  "
"Somewhat hypocritically, it does include a dispelling spell in the back of "
"the book."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/spellbooks.json
