msgstr "%1$s marmonne des mots et se déplace plus rapidement."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "forge born"
msgid_plural "forge born"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "forge born"
msgid ""
"The most elaborate, gaudy and overwrought clockwork creature that you've ever "
"seen.  Each one has its face designed in a mask displaying a single emotion.  "
"Blades extend from the wrists in combat."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goblin forgemaster"
msgid_plural "goblin forgemasters"
msgstr[0] "maître de forge gobelin"
msgstr[1] "maîtres de forge gobelins"
msgstr[2] "maîtres de forge gobelins"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goblin forgemaster"
msgid ""
"A goblin like none you've ever seen before.  He directs workers and "
"automatons with confidence and style."
msgstr ""
"Un gobelin comme vous n'avez jamais vu auparavant, ordonnant ses ouvriers et "
"automates en toute confiance et panache."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lizardfolk forgemaster"
msgid_plural "lizardfolk forgemasters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lizardfolk forgemaster"
msgid ""
"Lizardfolk rarely live outside of their tribes.  This one has found freedom "
"and purpose beyond serving their draconic masters."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "gracken forgemaster"
msgid_plural "gracken forgemasters"
msgstr[0] "maître de forge gracken"
msgstr[1] "maîtres de forge gracken"
msgstr[2] "maîtres de forge gracken"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "gracken forgemaster"
msgid ""
"This is some form of eldritch monstrosity; an uncouth black being with "
"smooth, oily, skin and unpleasant horns that curve inward toward each other.  "
"Tall and thin, the shadows cling unnaturally to its vaguely defined humanoid "
"form as it shuffles along, its hands twitching and spasming so rapidly as to "
"appear a little more than a black blur of claws.  This one politely asks you "
"to mind your step as this is a working environment."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "forge demon"
msgid_plural "forge demons"
msgstr[0] "démon de la forge"
msgstr[1] "démons de la forge"
msgstr[2] "démons de la forge"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "forge demon"
msgid ""
"The first thing you notice is that this creature has five arms.  The next is "
"that it walks on three legs.  It walks amongst the vault until it notices you "
"then throws itself at the walls screaming bloody murder.  Its mere presence "
"fills you with an unfathomable dread."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "vengeance spirit"
msgid_plural "vengeance spirits"
msgstr[0] "esprit vengeur"
msgstr[1] "esprits vengeurs"
msgstr[2] "esprits vengeurs"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "vengeance spirit"
msgid ""
"It looks like a will-o-the-wisp, darting back and forth, until it catches "
"sight of its prey.  When the sickly green balefires light up inside the "
"eyeholes of a skull, the mouth opens and a deep moan vibrates up through the "
"legs of those standing nearby."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "vengeance spirit"
msgid "The spirit flickers and reappears!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "forge worker"
msgid_plural "forge workers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "forge worker"
msgid ""
"A squat humanoid that looks quite sturdily built.  They style their hair in "
"mohawks and other strange fashions that seem to be dictated by what parts of "
"their skin aren't scarred from burns.  Their clothes are designed to protect "
"them from the intense environment they work in."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "forge hound"
msgid_plural "forge hounds"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/forgedwellers.json
#. ~ Description of monster "forge hound"
msgid "A metallic hound steps out of a nearby angle and growls at you.  Run!!!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goblin warrior"
msgid_plural "goblin warriors"
msgstr[0] "guerrier goblin"
msgstr[1] "guerriers goblins"
msgstr[2] "guerriers goblins"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goblin warrior"
msgid ""
"A goblin, but like something out of history.  Over the dirty, tattered "
"remnants of their street clothes, they're wearing improvised armor and "
"carrying a heavy club.  They look at you like a wolf seeing a particularly "
"juicy hunk of lamb."
msgstr ""
"Un gobelin, mais une caricature obscène tirée droit d'un pamphlet de "
"démagogue spéciste maniant une lourde massue et portant des morceaux "
"hétéroclites d'armure improvisée au dessus de lambeaux de ses vêtements du "
"quotidien.  Son attitude vous suggère que vous n'êtes pas grand chose de plus "
"à ses yeux qu'un gros morceau de viande pour dîner."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits your %2$s with a cudgel!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe votre %2$s avec sa massue!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits <npcname>'s %2$s with a cudgel!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe le/la %2$s de <npcname> avec sa massue!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goblin slinger"
msgid_plural "goblin slingers"
msgstr[0] "frondeur gobelin"
msgstr[1] "frondeurs gobelins"
msgstr[2] "frondeurs gobelins"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goblin slinger"
msgid ""
"A goblin, but like something out of history.  Over the dirty, tattered "
"remnants of their street clothes, they're wearing improvised armor and "
"carrying a sling with a pouch for extra stones.  They look at you like a wolf "
"seeing a particularly juicy hunk of lamb."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "goblin slinger"
msgid "The goblin slings a rock at you!"
msgstr "Le goblin utilise sa fronde et vous vise avec une pierre!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/orcs.json
#. ~ No ammo sound of special attack of monster "goblin slinger"
#. ~ No ammo sound of special attack of monster "orc archer"
msgid "grunting"
msgstr "grognement"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goblin leader"
msgid_plural "goblin leaders"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goblin leader"
msgid ""
"A goblin, slightly larger than the others and bearing a weapon with more "
"craftsmanship.  The goblins around them scurry to obey their orders."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits your %2$s with their spear!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe votre %2$s avec sa lance!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits <npcname>'s %2$s with their spear!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe le/la %2$s de <npcname> avec sa lance!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "goblin thornweaver"
msgid_plural "goblin thornweavers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "goblin thornweaver"
msgid ""
"A goblin in tattered clothing, muttering to themselves.  Occasionally, they "
"wave a hand and an eldritch viridian glow trails after it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and your %2$s is surrounded by a cloud of "
"scratching thorns!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and <npcname>'s %2$s is surrounded by a cloud of "
"scratching thorns!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and you narrowly avoid a cloud of scratching "
"thorns!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and <npcname> narrowly avoids a cloud of "
"scratching thorns!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and your %2$s is surrounded by a cloud of "
"scratching thorns, but they do no damage."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s chatters words of magic and <npcname>'s %2$s is surrounded by a cloud of "
"scratching thorns, but they do no damage."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "goblin thornweaver"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s waves their hands and %1$s is surrounded in greenish vapors."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "warg"
msgid_plural "wargs"
msgstr[0] "warg"
msgstr[1] "wargs"
msgstr[2] "wargs"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "warg"
msgid ""
"An enormous wolf, a meter and a half high at the shoulder, as large as a "
"young horse.  Tamed wargs were common as pets before the Cataclysm, but this "
"one looks anything but tame."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Feed message of monster "warg"
#, c-format
msgid ""
"The %s approaches you, acknowledging your ancient bond, and eats the meat you "
"offer."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bugbear"
msgid_plural "bugbears"
msgstr[0] "bugbear"
msgstr[1] "bugbears"
msgstr[2] "bugbears"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bugbear"
msgid ""
"An enormous gray-green humanoid, over two meters tall with thick fur at their "
"joints and long, tufted ears, this creature no longer has much resemblance to "
"a goblin other than the color.  Despite their size, they move in almost "
"complete silence and hold a long bladed weapon in their hand."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/orcs.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits your %2$s with their blade!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe votre %2$s avec sa lame!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/orcs.json
#. ~ Monster attack message
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s hits <npcname>'s %2$s with their blade!"
msgstr "%1$s frappe le/la %2$s de <npcname> avec sa lame!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bugbear stalker"
msgid_plural "bugbear stalkers"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/goblin.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bugbear stalker"
msgid ""
"An enormous gray-green humanoid, over two meters tall with thick fur at their "
"joints and long, tufted ears, this creature no longer has much resemblance to "
"a goblin other than the color.  Despite their size, they move in almost "
"complete silence and hold a long spear in their hand.  Strangely, you can "
"only see them when you're looking directly at them; when in the corner of "
"your vision they simply fade from sight."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "clay golem"
msgid_plural "clay golems"
msgstr[0] "golem d'argile"
msgstr[1] "golems d'argile"
msgstr[2] "golems d'argile"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Description of monster "clay golem"
msgid ""
"A large, humanoid golem made from clay.  Its proportions are off and it seems "
"fragile."
msgstr ""
"Un golem de la taille et forme d'un large humanoïde conçu à partir d'argile. "
"Ses proportions sont fausses et il à l'air fragile."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "plastic golem"
msgid_plural "plastic golems"
msgstr[0] "golem de plastique"
msgstr[1] "golems de plastique"
msgstr[2] "golems de plastique"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Description of monster "plastic golem"
msgid ""
"Traditionally, making a golem is a months-long process involving hand tools "
"and precision craftsmanship.  A stone golem is as much a work of art as it is "
"a magical device.  The advent of 3D printing made it easy to get into the "
"golem-making hobby, and plastic golems have soared in popularity."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "stone golem"
msgid_plural "stone golems"
msgstr[0] "golem de pierre"
msgstr[1] "golems de pierre"
msgstr[2] "golems de pierre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Description of monster "stone golem"
msgid "A large, humanoid golem made from stone.  Its fists look similar to rockets."
msgstr ""
"Un golem de la taille et forme d'un large humanoïde conçu à partir de pierre. "
"Ses poings ont l'air redoutable."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "iron golem"
msgid_plural "iron golems"
msgstr[0] "golem de fer"
msgstr[1] "golems de fer"
msgstr[2] "golems de fer"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Description of monster "iron golem"
msgid ""
"A large, humanoid golem made from iron.  Some sort of noxious gas seems to be "
"seeping from its mouth."
msgstr ""
"Un golem de la taille et forme d'un large humanoïde conçu à partir de fer. "
"Une sorte de gaz toxique s'échappe en fumeroles de sa bouche."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "earthshaper's golem"
msgid_plural "earthshaper's golems"
msgstr[0] "golem de façonneur de terre"
msgstr[1] "golems de façonneur de terre"
msgstr[2] "golems de façonneur de terre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/golems.json
#. ~ Description of monster "earthshaper's golem"
msgid ""
"This golem is easy to separate from other golems - the metallic earthshaper's "
"emblem shines on its smooth body, and it's eyes and hands are made out of "
"amethyst."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Yule cat"
msgid_plural "Yule cats"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Yule cat"
msgid ""
"Magical beast from Icelandic folklore, known for their catlike appearance and "
"their hobby of eating Workshop Elves."
msgstr ""
"Une bête magique à l'apparence féline issue du folklore islandais. Aime bien "
"croquer sur des lutins d'ateliers."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Yule cat cub"
msgid_plural "Yule cat cubs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Yule cat cub"
msgid ""
"The child of a Yule cat, this catlike creature looks as if it poses no threat "
"to you, but looks can be deceiving."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "workshop elf"
msgid_plural "workshop elves"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Description of monster "workshop elf"
msgid ""
"Magical humanoids who are known for working in workshops, wearing green, and "
"being proficient at making toys."
msgstr ""
"Un humanoïde magique connu pour son labeur dans des ateliers polaires, ses "
"habits verts et son aptitude à fabriquer des jouets."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "leprechaun"
msgid_plural "leprechauns"
msgstr[0] "leprechaun"
msgstr[1] "leprechauns"
msgstr[2] "leprechauns"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/holiday_magiclysm.json
#. ~ Description of monster "leprechaun"
msgid "Mischievous shoemakers who wear green and love pulling pranks on mortals."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lizardfolk warrior"
msgid_plural "lizardfolk warriors"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lizardfolk warrior"
msgid ""
"A tall, powerful, reptilian humanoid with a muscular tail whose skin is "
"covered in dark gray-green scales.  They are tribal and tend to be found in "
"caves and near water, especially in areas inhabited by dragons and wyrms.  "
"They aren't particularly hostile, though they don't care for outsiders and "
"are highly dangerous when provoked.  While they usually prefer to fight with "
"their greatclubs, they are equally ferocious with their sharp teeth and claws."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lizardfolk hunter"
msgid_plural "lizardfolk hunters"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lizardfolk hunter"
msgid ""
"The hunter is a smaller lizardfolk than a warrior, but equally as deadly, "
"with their lithe figures and accurate javelin throws."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "lizardfolk hunter"
msgid "The hunter hurls a barbed javelin at you!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lizardfolk shaman"
msgid_plural "lizardfolk shamans"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lizardfolk shaman"
msgid ""
"Lizardfolk are very intelligent and cunning, but magical ability is a rare "
"quality.  Shamans are chosen from the tribe during childhood, when magical "
"abilities mark the fate of the young tribesman.  Not much is known about the "
"initiation ritual they must undergo, but few survive the experience.  Shamans "
"are druidic spellcasters that can use the forces of nature to battle enemies, "
"as well as summoning assistance when needed."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lizardfolk chieftain"
msgid_plural "lizardfolk chieftains"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lizardfolk chieftain"
msgid ""
"Among the lizardfolk, ambition is a rare quality.  Chieftains earn their "
"place by exhibiting unusually high levels of ambition, often mistaken by "
"outsiders as excessive, brutal violence.  This chief is the largest and "
"strongest member of its tribe and carries a fierce trident to compliment its "
"teeth and claws."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_reptile_amphibian.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "crocodile"
msgid_plural "crocodiles"
msgstr[0] "crocodile"
msgstr[1] "crocodiles"
msgstr[2] "crocodiles"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/lizardfolk.json
#. ~ Description of monster "crocodile"
msgid ""
"A once-and-future lizardfolk shaman, this large crocodile no longer has any "
"hint of any humanoid characteristics and looks very, very dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go fleshwarper"
msgid_plural "mi-go fleshwarpers"
msgstr[0] "mélangeur de chair mi-go"
msgstr[1] "mélangeurs de chair mi-go"
msgstr[2] "mélangeurs de chair mi-go"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go fleshwarper"
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of ribbed, "
"membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and it moves "
"with an uncanny fluidity on its many legs.  Its flesh occasionally ripples, "
"as though something inside was squirming and trying to get free."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go fleshwarper"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s's numerous antennae move rhythmically for a moment."
msgstr ""
"Les nombreuses antennes du %1$s se déplacent en un rythme distinct pendant un "
"moment."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go fleshwarper"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s's numerous antennae twitch in all directions for a moment."
msgstr ""
"Les nombreuses antennes du %1$s se trémoussent dans toutes les directions "
"pendant un moment."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go fleshwarper"
#, c-format
msgid "As %1$s touches %3$s, the flesh warps and twists!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mi-go nethermancer"
msgid_plural "mi-go nethermancers"
msgstr[0] "néantmancien mi-go"
msgstr[1] "néantmanciens mi-go"
msgstr[2] "néantmanciens mi-go"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go nethermancer"
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of ribbed, "
"membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and it moves "
"with an uncanny fluidity on its many legs.  Its carapace is covered in "
"regular patterns which occasionally shift as you look at them before settling "
"into a new configuration."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go nethermancer"
#, c-format
msgid ""
"%1$s twitches its antennae at %3$s and %3$s is lifted up and pulled towards "
"them!"
msgstr ""
"%1$s trémousse ses antennes vers %3$s et %3$s est soudainement soulévé·e vers "
"lui!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/monsters/mi_go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go nethermancer"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go lightbringer"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go mindrender"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s's numerous antennae sync their movements for a brief moment."
msgstr ""
"Les nombreuses antennes du %1$s se synchronisent avec ses mouvements un bref "
"moment."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go nethermancer"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s's numerous antennae weave in a complicated pattern."
msgstr "Les nombreuses antennes du %1$s tissent un motif complexe."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mi-go.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go nethermancer"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s numerous antennae point directly at %3$s."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "animated blade"
msgid_plural "animated blades"
msgstr[0] "lame animée"
msgstr[1] "lames animées"
msgstr[2] "lames animées"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Description of monster "animated blade"
msgid ""
"A conjured glowing longsword that darts and dodges around, slicing and "
"cutting your foes into small pieces."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Description of monster "animated blade"
msgid ""
"A conjured glowing longsword that darts and dodges around, slicing and "
"cutting enemies into small pieces."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Description of monster "hologram"
msgid "Hologram copy of you."
msgstr "Une copie holographique de vous."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "watcher spirit"
msgid_plural "watcher spirits"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Description of monster "watcher spirit"
msgid ""
"A summoned watcher spirit, translucent and barely visible.  It gazes all "
"around itself."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/mics.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "watcher spirit"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s dissipates in a gust of wind!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "owlbear"
msgid_plural "owlbears"
msgstr[0] "hibours"
msgstr[1] "hibours"
msgstr[2] "hibours"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "owlbear"
msgid ""
"The horrible owlbear is probably the result of genetic experimentation by "
"some insane wizard.  These creatures inhabit the tangled forest regions of "
"every temperate clime, as well as subterranean labyrinths.  They are ravenous "
"eaters, aggressive hunters, and evil tempered at all times.  They attack prey "
"on sight and will fight to the death."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "black pudding"
msgid_plural "black puddings"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "black pudding"
msgid ""
"Writhing, sticky, black sludge undulates across the ground.  A faint sizzling "
"sound comes from the ground beneath it as it lurches toward you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "black pudding"
#, c-format
msgid "The black pudding burns %3$s with acid!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "krabgek"
msgid_plural "krabgeks"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "krabgek"
msgid ""
"A large baleful eye peers out from the darkness, its gleam hinting at a weird "
"intelligence and unnerving malevolence.  The eye oozes some pinkish liquid, "
"and the weirdly humanoid figure is covered in sharp blue-black triangular "
"plates."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "krabgek"
#, c-format
msgid "The krabgek gazes at %3$s!"
msgstr "Le krabgek fixe %3$s du regard!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "hunllef lamb"
msgid_plural "hunllef lambs"
msgstr[0] "agneau hunllef"
msgstr[1] "agneaux hunllef"
msgstr[2] "agneaux hunllef"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "hunllef lamb"
msgid ""
"The offspring of the Hunllef rams are much more docile but still have wicked "
"looking horns like their parents."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "hunllef ram"
msgid_plural "hunllef rams"
msgstr[0] "bélier hunllef"
msgstr[1] "béliers hunllef"
msgstr[2] "béliers hunllef"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "hunllef ram"
msgid ""
"Hunllef rams, also known as Nightmare Sheep, are a particularly vicious breed "
"of sheep suspected to be from another plane of existence.  Both males and "
"females display deadly horns and a willingness to use them on most other "
"creatures that come near them.  They are the most biddable source of "
"parabolan wool and often take a protective stance towards other sheep, so "
"some farmers will risk life and limb to keep them."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "owlbear cub"
msgid_plural "owlbear cubs"
msgstr[0] "hibourson"
msgstr[1] "hiboursons"
msgstr[2] "hiboursons"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bulette"
msgid_plural "bulettes"
msgstr[0] "bulette"
msgstr[1] "bulettes"
msgstr[2] "bulettes"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bulette"
msgid ""
"The bulette (or landshark) was the result of a mad wizard's experimental "
"cross breeding of a snapping turtle and armadillo with infusions of demons' "
"ichor.  They range temperate climates feeding on horses, men, and most other "
"flesh.  The stupid bulette is irascible and always hungry, and they fear "
"nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "will-o-wisp"
msgid_plural "will-o-wisps"
msgstr[0] "feu follet"
msgstr[1] "feux follets"
msgstr[2] "feux follets"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "will-o-wisp"
msgid ""
"Will-o'-wisps can be yellow, white, green, or blue.  They are easily mistaken "
"for lanterns, especially in the foggy marshes and swamps where they reside."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "will-o-wisp"
#, c-format
msgid "%1$s glitters in an eerie pattern."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "troll"
msgid_plural "trolls"
msgstr[0] "troll"
msgstr[1] "trolls"
msgstr[2] "trolls"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "troll"
msgid ""
"A monstrous, green-skinned humanoid, almost three meters tall but as thin as "
"the average human.  Trolls are renowned for their thick hides and natural "
"regenerative ability."
msgstr ""
"Une créature humanoïde monstrueuse à la peau verdâtre, atteignant presque "
"trois mètres de hauteur mais ayant la même corpulence que la personne "
"moyenne. Les trolls sont réputés pour leur peau épaisse et leur capacité de "
"régénération incroyable."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "rock troll"
msgid_plural "rock trolls"
msgstr[0] "troll de pierre"
msgstr[1] "trolls de pierre"
msgstr[2] "trolls de pierre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "rock troll"
msgid ""
"A monstrous, gray-skinned humanoid, almost three meters tall but as thin as "
"the average human.  Rock trolls have rocky skin that's almost impervious to "
"hand weapons, but they turn to stone in the sunlight."
msgstr ""
"Une créature humanoïde monstrueuse à la peau grise, atteignant presque trois "
"mètres de hauteur mais ayant la même corpulence que la personne moyenne. Les "
"trolls de pierre ont une peau rocheuse presque impossible à pénétrer avec une "
"arme de mêlée et une capacité de régénération incroyable, mais ceux-ci ont "
"désespérément peur de la lumière du soleil capable de les figer en une statue "
"de pierre."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "rock troll"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s turns to stone."
msgstr "Le %s se transforme en pierre."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "sea troll"
msgid_plural "sea trolls"
msgstr[0] "troll marin"
msgstr[1] "trolls marins"
msgstr[2] "trolls marins"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "sea troll"
msgid ""
"A monstrous, green-skinned humanoid, almost three meters tall but as thin as "
"the average human.  Sea trolls are just as mean and dangerous as trolls on "
"land, but they can also swim and breathe in water."
msgstr ""
"Une créature humanoïde monstrueuse à la peau verte, atteignant presque trois "
"mètres de hauteur mais ayant la même corpulence que la personne moyenne. Les "
"trolls marins sont aussi méchants et dangereux que les trolls normaux sur "
"terre, mais ajoutent à cela une capacité à respirer sous l'eau et nager."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "stirge"
msgid_plural "stirges"
msgstr[0] "strige"
msgstr[1] "striges"
msgstr[2] "striges"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "stirge"
msgid ""
"This horrid flying creature looks like a cross between a large bat and "
"oversized mosquito."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "shrieker"
msgid_plural "shriekers"
msgstr[0] "hurleur"
msgstr[1] "hurleurs"
msgstr[2] "hurleurs"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "shrieker"
msgid ""
"A shrieker is a human-sized mushroom that emits a piercing screech to drive "
"off creatures that disturb it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "frog"
msgid_plural "frogs"
msgstr[0] "grenouille"
msgstr[1] "grenouilles"
msgstr[2] "grenouilles"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "frog"
msgid ""
"A conspicuously average American bullfrog.  You better keep prince charming "
"away from it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "lemure"
msgid_plural "lemures"
msgstr[0] "lémure"
msgstr[1] "lémures"
msgstr[2] "lémures"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "lemure"
msgid ""
"A lemure resembles a molten mass of flesh with a vaguely humanoid head and "
"torso."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "winter wolf"
msgid_plural "winter wolves"
msgstr[0] "loup d'hiver"
msgstr[1] "loups d'hiver"
msgstr[2] "loups d'hiver"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "winter wolf"
msgid ""
"A pure white dire wolf.  If you squint, you can see a faint mist surrounding "
"its coat, and ice shards slowly descend from its breath."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "loup garou"
msgid_plural "loup garous"
msgstr[0] "loup garou"
msgstr[1] "loup garous"
msgstr[2] "loup garous"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "loup garou"
msgid ""
"Previously thought extinct outside of rural Quebec and Louisiana this cursed "
"creature has been known to breed with true wolves when it isn't madly "
"destroying any signs of humanity in its territory.  These once normal men, "
"women, elves and dwarves are now forever cursed to roam the wilderness as "
"four legged avatars of destruction; giant, rabid, maddened wolves that never "
"know peace when they can smell or see the creations of the mortal races.  "
"Immortal until killed it would be difficult to remember they were once mortal "
"until cutting beneath the fur shows meat that somehow remembers a different "
"life."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fiery nightmare"
msgid_plural "fiery nightmares"
msgstr[0] "cauchemar ardent"
msgstr[1] "cauchemars ardents"
msgstr[2] "cauchemars ardents"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fiery nightmare"
msgid ""
"A colossal figure which seems to consist entirely of shadows engulfed in "
"flames.  Their immense dark wings extend from wall to wall.  Two eyes that "
"resemble burning coals are gazing down on you with hatred.  In one hand they "
"hold a huge sword, in the other a many thonged whip, both glowing with "
"red-hot flames."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "teravolt"
msgid_plural "teravolts"
msgstr[0] "teravolt"
msgstr[1] "teravolts"
msgstr[2] "teravolts"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "teravolt"
msgid "A small energy sphere that slowly floats towards the target."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "teravolt"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s explode, creating a giant cloud of sparks."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "razor butterfly"
msgid_plural "razor butterflies"
msgstr[0] "papillon rasoir"
msgstr[1] "papillons rasoir"
msgstr[2] "papillons rasoir"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/elementals.json
#. ~ Description of monster "razor butterfly"
#. ~ Description of monster "skyglass butterfly"
msgid ""
"A large, brightly colored butterfly with crystalline wings, fluttering "
"incongruously through the air.  This one seems to be patterned with orange "
"runes, and its wings look razor-sharp."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "electric demon"
msgid_plural "electric demons"
msgstr[0] "démon électrique"
msgstr[1] "démons électriques"
msgstr[2] "démons électriques"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "electric demon"
msgid ""
"Small, pure electric elemental that jumps from target to target, attacking "
"anything and everything in their sight bar the caster."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "electric demon"
#, c-format
msgid "A %s explode!"
msgstr "Un(e) %s explose!"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "thunder pillar"
msgid_plural "thunder pillars"
msgstr[0] "pilier de tonnerre"
msgstr[1] "piliers de tonnerre"
msgstr[2] "piliers de tonnerre"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "thunder pillar"
msgid ""
"They look like a giant floating stone shard, but are actually an intelligent "
"creature that can use electric branches as their own bodies."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "thunder pillar"
msgid "The pillar weaves electricity around themself!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "ankheg"
msgid_plural "ankhegs"
msgstr[0] "ankheg"
msgstr[1] "ankhegs"
msgstr[2] "ankhegs"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "ankheg"
msgid ""
"A huge, segmented, burrowing insect, two meters long and pale greenish-yellow "
"in color."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "ankheg"
#, c-format
msgid "The ankheg spits a stream of acid at %3$s!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "otyugh"
msgid_plural "otyughs"
msgstr[0] "otyugh"
msgstr[1] "otyughs"
msgstr[2] "otyughs"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "otyugh"
msgid ""
"An enormous, bulbous body dominated by a toothy maw, with three tentacles "
"extending from the top.  Two tentacles are tipped with grasping filaments and "
"the last has several dark spots that might be eyes.  It smells indescribably "
"foul."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "catoblepas"
msgid_plural "catoblepases"
msgstr[0] "catoblepas"
msgstr[1] "catoblepas"
msgstr[2] "catoblepas"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "catoblepas"
msgid ""
"A terrible stench is the first sign of this monster's presence.  It has an "
"ox-like body and warthog-like head, with a neck almost as long as a "
"giraffe's.  It keeps its head low to the ground, but there's something odd "
"about its eyes."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "catoblepas"
#, c-format
msgid "The catoblepas looks at %3$s!"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "mossling"
msgid_plural "mosslings"
msgstr[0] "moussinet"
msgstr[1] "moussinets"
msgstr[2] "moussinets"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Description of monster "mossling"
msgid ""
"A dog-sized mass of lichen and plant matter, ambling about on a series of "
"short limbs.  It looks around the forest floor for fallen leaves to eat."
msgstr ""
"Un amas de lichen et de matière végétale de la taille d'un chien, se "
"déplaçant sur un grand nombre de petites pattes et cherchant le sol de la "
"forêt pour des feuilles mortes à manger."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "mossling"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s collapses into a pile of moss."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dryad"
msgid_plural "dryads"
msgstr[0] "dryade"
msgstr[1] "dryades"
msgstr[2] "dryades"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dryad"
msgid ""
"You would have thought this was a tree until it suddenly moved.  It is "
"human-shaped and human-sized, but with wood for skin and leaves for hair.  It "
"regards you impassively."
msgstr ""
"Vous auriez pu jurer que ceci était un arbre avec qu'elle commence à bouger. "
"Elle, dû au fait que sa silhouette est vaguement féminine et de la taille "
"d'un être humain possédant une peau d'écorce et une chevelure de feuilles. "
"Elle vous regarde impassiblement."

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "dryad"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s collapses into splinters."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "brackenwight"
msgid_plural "brackenwights"
msgstr[0] "tumulus végétal"
msgstr[1] "tumuli végétaux"
msgstr[2] "tumuli végétaux"

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Description of monster "brackenwight"
msgid ""
"An animate pile of moss, leaves, sticks, and other forest detritus, towering "
"almost three meters high.  Three pits near the top with a lambent green glow "
"might be eyes.  It slowly walks on massive limbs."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "brackenwight"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s collapses into a massive pile of leaves and sticks."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Magiclysm/monsters/nature_spirits.json
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "brackenwight"
#, c-format
