#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_phavian_private"
msgid "Note on the back of a schedule printout"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_phavian_private"
msgid ""
"I don't want one of those assignments ever again.  They call themselves "
"\"Offworld Acquisitions\" but do you know what they actually do?  They're "
"butchers!  I can only sit through so many lectures about how \"only humans "
"have human rights\" before I want to just start trying to adjust their "
"thought processes.  Give me an hour alone in a room with each one of them and "
"they'll never want to hurt a fly.\n"
"\n"
"Mark my words, those maniacs are making enemies that we can't afford to make. "
" We don't know everything that's out there beyond the gates and it's pure "
"luck we haven't made contact with a civilization that wants to hunt US for "
"something WE have.  Unless we have and some of those immersion teams that "
"went missing were actually captured.  They're playing with fire and we're all "
"going to get burned."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
msgid "Re: CE225"
msgstr "Re: CE225"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
msgid ""
"As instructed, we brought L85 to the subject's location and subjected it to "
"increasingly-higher-lumen concentrations, all to no effect.  We got up to 50K "
"lumens with no effect other than making everyone except L85 and (footage "
"later showed) the subject blind briefly.  The subject simply laughed.\n"
"\n"
"It wasn't laughing when we took it down the hall and threw it into the room "
"with the open windows, though."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_telepathy"
msgid "incident report: 223741"
msgstr "rapport d'incident: 223741"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_telepathy"
msgid ""
"At 0411 this morning, a GLASS ANVIL mathematician seconded to XEDRA-40 "
"discovered an anomaly in one of the returning immersion teams during a "
"routine random security scan.  While monitoring Dr. Mahika Mittal, the "
"mathematician suddenly screamed and grabbed their head before collapsing to "
"the floor.  In the ensuing confusion, Dr. Mittal attempted to grab Sgt "
"Adams's rifle before making a gesture and \"causing the temperature in the "
"room to drop to freezing\".  Following this, Dr. Mittal grabbed Dr. McDowell "
"and dragged him back through the still-open dive aperture just before it "
"closed.  An attempt to reopen the aperture to the previous destination was "
"unsuccessful at producing a stable connection; further efforts are ongoing.\n"
"\n"
"When awakened, mathematician U72 stated that during her attempt to make "
"contact she felt \"Something cold, icy, like a glacier.  Inhuman.  It wasn't "
"Dr. Mahika, it was something that looked like her, or had taken her place "
"or…I don't know.\"  When told that Dr. Mittal had escaped, U72 was emphatic "
"that it (she only ever used the word it) had to be captured for study and to "
"prevent similar incidents from happening again.\n"
"\n"
"Questioning of the other dive team members is ongoing.  None of them said Dr. "
"Mittal showed any suspicious behavior either before or during the dive."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_vitakinesis"
msgid "a partial interview transcript"
msgstr "une transcription partielle de réunion"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/mod_interactions/xedra_evolved/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_vitakinesis"
msgid ""
"\"…summary of your sensations, please.\"\n"
"M33: \"Uh, okay.  Well, it's hard to describe this, you know, but a "
"normal…sorry, sorry, a standard person has a kind of glow to them.  If "
"they're sick, or tired, or injured in some way, it affects the glow.  "
"[REDACTED]…oh, sorry, I mean, uh, the CE473 had that same glow but it was "
"muted\"\n"
"Interviewer: \"Muted?\"\n"
"M33: \"Like, the glow was just…lower, you know?  Like she was sick or "
"something, but she wasn't.  I couldn't find anything wrong with her at all.  "
"I did a full scan, as much as I could, you know, and she was in perfect "
"health.  Better, even.  The, uh, CE473 is in her mid-40s?\"\n"
"Interviewer: \"That's correct.\"\n"
"M33: \"I never would have believed that if I wasn't told it.  She doesn't "
"just look good for her age, she's physically younger.\"\n"
"Interviewer: \"What was your impression of the subject on your second "
"examination?\"M33: \"Oh, at the end of the day?  Well, I'm not sure how to "
"describe it, she was…red.\"\n"
"Interviewer: \"What do you mean by that?\"\n"
"M33: \"Yeah, like she was even paler than usual and there were these kind of "
"red streaks.  And it felt, uh…\"\n"
"*fifteen second pause*\n"
"\n"
"Interviewer: \"Please continue.  Your impressions are very important to the "
"success of the experiment.\"\n"
"*six second pause*\n"
"M33: \"Hungry.  It felt hungry.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/monsters/amalgamations.json
