#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_biokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for biokinetic study is BURNT NOVEMBER.  Designation
#. for use in combat is VERDANT HAND
msgid ""
"They wanted me to keep a logbook of my daily exercise but I don't understand "
"the point.  I run, I lift, I sleep, that's about all these have me do here.  "
"What, they want \"5:40 a.m.: 30 reps 250 lbs, run 20 minutes, 100 burpees (10 "
"sets)\" blah blah who cares?  That shit doesn't matter.  We're all trapped "
"here and things are going to hell and we got some kind of poison in our "
"bodies that's going to bring us back when we die so we can eat brains.\n"
"\n"
"Well, fine, here's my log: 6:05 a.m.: 50 reps 400 lbs, sprint 10 minutes, 200 "
"pull-ups, triple somersault from a standing start.  Put me in the Olympics "
"right now."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_biokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for biokinetic study is BURNT NOVEMBER.  Designation
#. for use in combat is VERDANT HAND
msgid "The VERDANT HAND combat protocols"
msgstr "Les protocoles de combat MAIN VERDOYANTE"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_biokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for biokinetic study is BURNT NOVEMBER.  Designation
#. for use in combat is VERDANT HAND
msgid ""
"They demanded that I include that title on this report even though it's "
"pretentious as hell.  This isn't some superweapon that will change the face "
"of modern warfare, it's just a better form of hand-to-hand combat.  They "
"can't dodge bullets.  They can't punch through brick walls.  They can't do "
"that movie thing where the hero hits a bad guy and the bad guy goes flying "
"twenty feet.  They're just faster and stronger and hit harder, all good "
"things, but they aren't going to beat someone with a gun.  There's a reason "
"we invented guns and why functional martial arts training is about defending "
"yourself and getting away, not about going on the offense.\n"
"\n"
"So is it worth training people?  That's the wrong question.  This isn't a "
"codified martial art, it's just using dimensional metaphysics to enhance "
"existing methods of combat.  A VERDANT HAND candidate will be better at Muay "
"Thai than anyone who hasn't gone through BURNT NOVEMBER but they still need "
"the actual martial arts training.  This is just another tool.  I'm not sure "
"why there's so much focus on this, to be honest.  With the cost of retrieving "
"materials, surely we could spend that money better elsewhere.  Modern warfare "
"does not rely on single superheroes winning battles."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid "Notes scribbled on notebook paper"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid ""
"I'm looking up at the sky.  I can see the same constellations on Earth, but "
"they're shimmering somehow, like there's a haze or a fog or something between "
"us.  Then, the stars start to slowly go out.  Not in a wave, but "
"randomly--one here, one there, faster and faster until the entire sky was "
"dark.  Then the moon disappeared as well and everything went black.\n"
"\n"
"I'm standing on the edge of a cliff.  Below me is the churning sea, the "
"waters black under the stormclouds.  The sea rises slowly as rain falls in "
"sheets, lightning striking the waters.  They break over the edge of the "
"cliff, then over my head.  I drown.\n"
"\n"
"I am standing in a forest.  The trees rustle all around me and the birds "
"sing, and then clouds pass over the sun.  The sun dims and then starts to go "
"black.  It's an eclipse.  The light fades and all the birdsong dies.  I stand "
"in pitch blackness with the rustle of leaves around me."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid "testing report N2-8129"
msgstr "rapport de test N2-8129"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid ""
"Subject O21 was placed blindfolded in a completely dark room with a deck of "
"shuffled playing cards, instructed to remove the blindfold, and asked to sort "
"them in standard order: clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades, each in numerical "
"order.  Task was completed in 6:03 with 18/52 cards in the proper order and "
"minor to major ordering errors in all other cards.  Subject was then asked to "
"drink from the coffee cup in the room.  Cup was placed on a shelf above the "
"door to prevent movement around the room from discovering it, but task was "
"completed in 1:14, with the only difficulty being subject's height (158 cm) "
"making it harder to reach the shelf.  Subject was then asked to cross the "
"room to the table, pick up the paper, and read the sequence of numbers "
"written on it.  Subject was unable to do so, only correctly reciting the "
"first two digits.\n"
"\n"
"Experiment does uphold the thesis that successful NOBLE HORIZON "
"mathematicians perceive their surroundings through means other than light.  "
"As O21 was unable to read the document, their sense is not \"sight\" as such. "
" Further experimentation to determine its limits is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid "COLD BELOW progress report"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"After all of the time and money I wish I had more promising news to report.  "
"Netherum mathematics is an inexact science, as you well know, so it's very "
"hard to find a protocol that will work the same every time.  Melchior has the "
"advantage of processing speed but our mathematicians have to put in the "
"hours, but they can make connections Melchior cannot because he can only work "
"with the data he's given, whereas NOBLE HORIZON provides new data.  But, "
"unpredictably.  We've discovered any number of immersion destinations where "
"the physical laws are so different even the probes wouldn't work, much less a "
"dive team.  The majority of them, even BURNT NOVEMBER wouldn't be sufficient "
"to sustain a diver.  There's no value in exotic materials that will probably "
"not survive the transition.\n"
"\n"
"On the other hand, COLD BELOW did discover Plane 398RG and we got quite a few "
"awakenings out of it before testing was prohibited.  And on the other other "
"hand, they found 9472P where the entire world's biomass had been assimilated "
"by XE157 and we lost the entire dive team because XE157 ignored the probes.  "
"It's like that bell curve meme where Melchior is in the middle and COLD BELOW "
"is both ends.  If only we had a better way to get the far side."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid "GRAY DAWN vs. NOBLE HORIZON testing"
msgstr "test AUBE GRISE vs HORIZON NOBLE"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid ""
"In the interests of testing Dr. Al-Masri's hypothesis, we assembled a group "
"of NOBLE HORIZON and GRAY DAWN mathematicians and had them both attempt to "
"conduct a simple number guessing game.  Melchior provided a six-digit number "
"and both teams attempted to guess it.  GRAY DAWN were competitive when the "
"number was overseen by a third party, as expected, but when both teams were "
"provided with a terminal interface and instructed to enter their guesses, "
"GRAY DAWN scored no better than chance.  On the other hand, NOBLE HORIZON "
"consistently managed to guess at least three digits and successfully guessed "
"the entire six-digit sequence twice (out of ten total sequences).  This "
"disparity was maintained when both groups were placed in empty rooms, "
"instructed to write down their guesses on a sheet of paper, and place it into "
"a box before leaving the room.  Finally, NOBLE HORIZON attained a better than "
"chance score on the final test, when both groups were instructed to guess the "
"sequence before Melchior was asked to provide a sequence.\n"
"\n"
"This leads to two conclusions.  The first is that the alarmists are wrong; "
"Melchior is not secretly harboring a genius intellect and plotting to control "
"XEDRA from within, it is a computer, capable of processing vast amounts of "
"data and using Netherum mathematics to process that data much faster than "
"would otherwise be possible.  The second is that while GRAY DAWN requires a "
"specific source from which to attain new information, NOBLE HORIZON does not. "
" Even in situations where no information transfer would be possible, such as "
"the final two testing scenarios, NOBLE HORIZON still had a better-than-chance "
"rate of correctly determining the sequence."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid "Note on official XEDRA stationary"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_clairsentience"
#. ~ Phavian designation for clairsentience study is NOBLE HORIZON.  Phavian
#. designation for use of clairsentience to find appropriate portal targets
#. for immersion dives is COLD BELOW
msgid ""
"Dr Richardson,\n"
"Last night, both J99 and V27 approached me with a concern.  As is consistent "
"with NOBLE HORIZON protocol, they have been keeping a dream journal and "
"noticed during the weekly meeting that a few nights ago they had exactly the "
"same dream, down to the smallest details.  You can find the exact details in "
"the weekly report but the gist of it was a giant hand reaching out of the sky "
"and covering the entire Earth and squeezing the Earth until it cracked.  "
"Looking back through previous journals, I found that W88 and P61 had similar "
"dreams within the last week.  I'm still trying to track down if there was a "
"\"patient zero\", so to speak, and if this is some kind of contagious imagery "
"or there is some other obvious explanation, but in the meantime, I'm baffled. "
" NOBLE HORIZON visions are usually filtered through the individual psyche of "
"the mathematician, and I have no explanation for why in this case multiple "
"mathematicians would exhibit the exact same manifestation.\n"
"\n"
"I'm going to get to the bottom of this.  We already have bad morale after "
"947188 and this is not going to help.\n"
"John Goldberg\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid "testing report R2-1711"
msgstr "rapport de test R2-1711"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The testing mathematician was provided with a standard smartphone and "
"instructed to turn on and leave on the flashlight, share their location with "
"multiple provided addresses, and repeatedly delete and re-download several "
"very large testing files (each over 10gb in size).  During breaks, the phone "
"was left streaming HD movies over the cellular network.\n"
"\n"
"Results were very consistent; while the phone's battery rapidly drained while "
"unattended, despite not being connected to power, the battery slowly refilled "
"when the phone was being handled by T47, often reaching or being close to "
"100% when the time came for a break.\n"
"\n"
"Following this, the experiment was modified to have T47 sit and read a book "
"in the same room, but never approach closer than two meters to the phone, "
"which was again set to stream HD movies over the cellular network.  The phone "
"discharged its battery and shut off completely within four hours.  Further "
"testing shows the approximate range of the effect (in T47's case) to be 8 "
"centimeters from their body and that barriers (both conductive and "
"non-conductive) do not impede the effect in any way.  Attempts to use a "
"multimeter to directly measure the strength of the effect were inconclusive, "
"as it changed rapidly up to several times per second and often the multimeter "
"simply could not register any current at all.  I have already submitted a "
"request for further testing to determine the exact parameters of the effect, "
"include its strength and the full variety of devices subject to it, and will "
"submit an update with my results as soon as I have them.\n"
"-Charlotte Manning\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid "re: power"
msgstr "re: énergie"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid ""
"I did some work on your proposal to power the facility using RUBY LOOP in the "
"event of continued disruptions over a long timescale and I can say that it's "
"just not going to work.  Sure, a RUBY LOOP guy can keep their phone running "
"basically forever, but it can't scale up.  We final have the data on those "
"caloric expenditures and yes, I know they don't add up and nothing makes "
"sense, but the \"how much they need to eat\" and the \"how much power they "
"output\" lines do not ever cross no matter what we try.  And yes, I know "
"you're going to bring up A80, but even though she can now throw lightning "
"bolts like an X-man her efficiency rating on power generation is not actually "
"that high among RUBY LOOP mathematicians.  And no, before you ask, hooking up "
"a lightning rod and having her just blast it repeatedly wouldn't generate "
"enough power either.  I thought of it and we did try it, but no dice.\n"
"\n"
"We're going to have to hope that COBALT THORN comes through if we're stuck in "
"here for too long."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid "note on the back of a testing report"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid ""
"\"Double double toil and trouble\n"
"\"little Jenny wants to play\n"
"\"flash of lightning very frightening\n"
"\"Thunder drive our fears away\n"
"\"Shadows waiting not abating\n"
"\"Hope to all who fear the dark\n"
"\"Shines a light in dark of night\n"
"\"Ever glowing one bright spark\"\n"
"A smear of blood and scorch marks hide any further words that may have been "
"written."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid "AAR ID# Q85-77"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid ""
"Immediately after immersion into 471XE, the dive team confirmed probe "
"observations that despite not being in any kind of chamber or underground, "
"there were no visible light sources anywhere.  Sgt Simmons ordered the team "
"to turn on their flashlights, and after doing so the team almost immediately "
"came under attack by multiple XE338 entities.  Due to 471XE's effects on "
"Netherum energy, Sgt Simmons ordered V78 to deter the attack using "
"mathematics and the dive team formed a defensive formation while V78 fended "
"off the XE338 attackers with repeated bolts of lightning.  While the attacks "
"were effective, the light itself seemed to function as a deterrent and the "
"dive team was able to withdraw through the aperture in short order with only "
"Dr. Rodriguez suffering any injuries that required more than first aid.\n"
"\n"
"Based on this incident, further travel to 471XE is prohibited without a "
"CRYPTIC FORGE mathematician present and backed up by several high-powered "
"light sources."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid "I am the One"
msgstr "Je suis l'Élu"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_electrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for electrokinetic study is RUBY LOOP
msgid ""
"I flow through the data and watch the patterns stream around me.  I turn and "
"choose between them.  A confidential email exchange, perhaps.  A receipt from "
"a delivery.  A junk email for performance enhancement.  The secret plans of "
"XEDRA management.  All is laid bare before my electronic gaze.  Passwords do "
"not even slow me down.  I hear the voices of the satellites as they chatter "
"in ones and zeroes.  I am a true inhabitant of the digital age, at home on "
"the waves of the sea of information.\n"
"\n"
"*Handwritten below in red are the words, \"Refer I32 for psychological "
"evaluation.\"*"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for photokinetic study is CRYPTIC FORGE
msgid "incident report: 884001"
msgstr "rapport d'incident: 884001"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for photokinetic study is CRYPTIC FORGE
msgid ""
"At 1405 during a routine CRYPTIC FORGE test, mathematician A34 reported "
"feeling \"strange, I don't know what\" and immediately afterwards all "
"monitoring and testing equipment ceased transmitting.  Security responded "
"immediately and found A34 uninjured inside the testing room, though they were "
"forced to cut through the door since the electronic lock had failed.  "
"Subsequent investigation of network footage revealed that when attempting to "
"radiation-sterilize various vegetables, A34 had somehow triggered an "
"electromagnetic pulse.  When interviewed after the incident, A34 stated that, "
"\"the energy just kept building and building and I guess it had to go "
"somewhere.\"\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, due to the lockdowns and the prohibitive cost, as well as the "
"disruptions it would cause other experiments and daily operations in general, "
"any form of electromagnetic hardening is impractical.  Dr. Al-Masri has "
"floated the possibility of attempting to train other CRYPTIC FORGE "
"mathematicians to provide a control in case of an EMP, but at the moment, "
"this is only theoretical as no mathematician has demonstrated the conscious "
"abilty to produce one.  I'm sorry to say that for the moment, all we can do "
"is hope it doesn't happen again."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for photokinetic study is CRYPTIC FORGE
msgid "testing report C8-3434"
msgstr "rapport de test C8-3434"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_photokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for photokinetic study is CRYPTIC FORGE
msgid ""
"How does CRYPTIC FORGE control darkness?  Darkness is not a thing, there are "
"no \"skotons\" that they could emit to cancel out existing light, but that "
"seems to the casual observer what is happening.\n"
"\n"
"B81 was instructed to cancel the light within a one-meter area in the center "
"of the testing chamber.  The lights were extinguished and blackout curtains "
"hung over all observation windows.  The area was first exposed to candlelight "
"(12 lumens), showing a distinct border of the area.  A flashlight (350 "
"lumens) was trained on the area as well, with a similar effect, though the "
"directional light from the flashlight was sufficient to demonstrate that "
"light did not penetrate the area.  A high-powered flashlight (6000 lumens) "
"shown from the corner illuminated most of the testing area and clearly "
"delineated the borders of the area, as well as casting a shadow on the wall "
"opposite of the light source.  Finally, the blackout curtains were removed "
"and, after instructing B81 to close their eyes, a floodlight (118K lumens) "
"was shone on the area, again to no effect.\n"
"\n"
"The initial hypothesis, that CRYPTIC FORGE is somehow suppressing or allowing "
"photons to \"jump\" through the area, is incorrect.  Assuming that "
"conservation of energy is still in effect (since, without assuming that we "
"have no basis to determine anything), it is instead possible that the photons "
"are somehow absorbed by the affected area in a way that does not inhibit "
"movement, in the same way that space seems mostly empty but large amounts of "
"radiation are absorbed by cosmic dust.  Unfortunate that we don't have access "
"to a particle accelerator to test various particles' interactions with the "
"effect.\n"
"\n"
"I have already submitted a proposal to test CRYPTIC FORGE's ability to block "
"microwaves, radio waves, X-rays, and other elements of the electromagnetic "
"spectrum, and am waiting on successful procurement of the necessary "
"equipment.\n"
"Adam Brenner\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid "testing report O3-5523"
msgstr "rapport de test O3-5523"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid ""
"Z87 was instructed to kindle a flame above their palm, doing so successfully "
"after approximately ten seconds of effort.  Measurements showed the "
"temperature near the flame to exceed 200°C, though Z87 showed no discomfort "
"despite his proximity.  Following instruction of testing authority, subject "
"maintained the flame for 11 minutes and 38 seconds before it dissipated.  A "
"second test showed similar results, though on this second attempt, Z87 could "
"only maintain the flame for 7 minutes and 8 seconds.  While the fire burned "
"with no apparent need for fuel, oxygen concentration measurements taken "
"before, during, and after the test showed that the oxygen content of the room "
"did decrease in line with the apparent size of the flame."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid "Medicinal use of COPPER PRIME"
msgstr "Utilisation médicinale de CUIVRE PRIMAIRE"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid ""
"Despite folk wisdom and popular belief, cauterization is ineffective at "
"stopping bleeding or controlling infection compared to nearly any other "
"method.  However, controlled electrocautery is used in modern medicine; can "
"COPPER PRIME show similar levels of effectiveness?\n"
"\n"
"PROCEDURE: Animal testing was done on six cows in order to provide a "
"sufficient volume of blood, since mouse or monkey subjects would be "
"insufficient.  Three mathematicians were used, each augmented with a matrix "
"crystal, to conduct the tests.  Each cow was immobilized and had a series of "
"wounds inflicted using a standard surgical scalpel.\n"
"\n"
"RESULTS: While it was possible to stop bloodflow from non-lacerating wounds "
"and non-arterial bleeding (mathematicians consistently failed to stop "
"arterial bleeding), results were less than promising.  Two cows died "
"immediately after the testing from blood loss and two of the remaining cows "
"showed signs of infection in several of the cuts, showing a higher "
"contamination ratio than electrocautery.  While better than a hot iron, "
"COPPER PRIME is not of high enough effectiveness to consider using for wound "
"treatment, and especially not if SMOKE USHER is available."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid "testing report O5-8346"
msgstr "rapport de test O5-8346"

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"As you requested, I gathered three COPPER PRIME mathematicians for the "
"experiment.  We took them to the walk-in freezer, and provided them with "
"standard physician's examination gowns, ushered them in, and told them to "
"individually knock on the door when they felt ready to come out.  Minimum "
"time was 45 minutes, after which B22 knocked and asked to exit.  The longest "
"was 3 hours, though since I31 reported symptoms of frostbite the following "
"day, he obviously did not follow experimental protocols to exit as soon as he "
"felt significant discomfort.  I admit that some of the fault lies with me, "
"however--I should have chosen a more objective criteria to request exit.  For "
"the next experiment, I intend to equip the mathematicians with temperature "
"monitors and instruct them to leave when their internal body temperature "
"drops to 33.5°.\n"
"\n"
"I'll have a full report written up in the next few days\n"
"-Jacob Sanchez\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid "V44, experiment impressions"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_pyrokinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for pyrokinetic study is COPPER PRIME.
msgid ""
"Write down my impressions of Netherum mathematics?  How do you describe sight "
"to a blind man?  How do you describe a symphony to a deaf person?  Well, "
"alright, I'll try.\n"
"\n"
"I've heard some of the body people say that they have full awareness, like "
"they're concentrating on every part of their body at once, but that's not "
"what it's like for me.  It's more like focusing on something so hard you lose "
"awareness of your surroundings.  I pick a point in space and I concentrate, "
"and it's like I'm being sucked into it.  I just push on it.  I'm not sure how "
"I can describe it better than that, I push on it with my mind and it starts "
"moving, and when I'm aware of the world again, it's on fire.\n"
"\n"
"World on fire.  If I ever get to write about this, that's what I'll call the "
"book.\n"
"\n"
"The researchers ask me how I know how much energy to add, or how I "
"concentrate, and I just know.  There's a reason we call it \"awakening.\"  I "
"don't even need to think about it, really.  Despite the name it's not like "
"mathematics, where you have to figure out 9 time 34 and carry the 3 and so "
"on, it's like riding a bicycle.  Once I got used to how it worked, I can just "
"do it.  It takes seconds, sometimes less.  I just have to put myself into the "
"right frame of mind and the fire comes.\n"
"\n"
"Not sure how useful that is, but it's what it's like."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_telekinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for telekinetic study is JUNIPER GOLD.  Phavian
#. designation for telekinetic study for use in combat is ONYX LIGHTNING
msgid "It's all just motion"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_telekinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for telekinetic study is JUNIPER GOLD.  Phavian
#. designation for telekinetic study for use in combat is ONYX LIGHTNING
msgid ""
"Why is there a distinction between pyrokinesis and telekinesis at all?  Fire "
"isn't a fundamental element, it's the result of heat which is the result of "
"molecular motion.  There's no conceptual reason why a pyrokinetic couldn't "
"make all the molecules of an object move in a particular direction, producing "
"motion of the entire object, or a telekinetic couldn't produce a more chaotic "
"motion that resulted in the object's energy increasing.  Furthermore, in no "
"test has a telekinetic been able to move part of an object unless that part "
"is designed for motion; pulling a lever is possible, but breaking a plate in "
"half is not.  And a pyrokinetic cannot apply the reverse and slow down an "
"object's molecules to reduce heat unless that object is on fire.\n"
"\n"
"My theory is that it's all psychological.  We've all grown up with modern "
"culture and stories about what psychics are \"supposed\" to be capable of, "
"and so the matrix crystals and Netherum mathematics shape the candidates' "
"abilities toward those pre-determined pathways.  If we could get a SMOKE "
"USHER mathematician from an uncontacted tribe, maybe they'd be able to induce "
"diseases in their targets or steal their soul, in accordance with that "
"tribe's beliefs and practices about supernatural powers.  But since our "
"candidates come from a culture where pyrokinesis and telekinesis are separate "
"things and geokinesis or osteokinesis are very rare to nonexistent in "
"fiction, the former result from awakenings and the latter do not.\n"
"\n"
"I would like to formally request a wider variety of cultural backgrounds for "
"our project candidates to test this theory."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_telekinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for telekinetic study is JUNIPER GOLD.  Phavian
#. designation for telekinetic study for use in combat is ONYX LIGHTNING
msgid "re: the Third"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "lab_file_telekinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for telekinetic study is JUNIPER GOLD.  Phavian
#. designation for telekinetic study for use in combat is ONYX LIGHTNING
msgid ""
"Sarah,\n"
"I read your email and you're right--it's not a law anymore if we have such an "
"easily-demonstrable counterexample.  \"Newton's Third Conjecture\" doesn't "
"have the same ring to it but seems more accurate.  We've done a lot of "
"experiments to find some sort of consequences for the TKs and so far there's "
"nothing other than the standard metabolic cost.  Netherum mathematics is "
"work, but the mechanism of the force is unclear.  We've already tried both a "
"scale and water displacement and neither of them showed any measurable "
"counterforce.  That leaves a few possibilities:/n1)There is no counterforce.  "
"That breaks classical mechanics in half but frankly we're already at that "
"point anyway.\n"
"2)The counterforce is exerted elsewhere, such as the Netherum.  This is "
"basically just handwavium, \"well, we can't see it but it must be out "
"there.\"  Must it?  Plus then the counterforce isn't actually acting on the "
"origin point anyway unless you buy Dr. Ho's ridiculous \"The soul is a Nether "
"construct\" theory.\n"
"3)The counterforce applies in some way we aren't looking for, like, I don't "
"know, DNA damage or other microscopic-level areas.  We already had "
"comprehensive checkups and didn't find anything, but we're not entirely sure "
"what we're looking for.\n"
"\n"
"\"we're not entirely sure what we're looking for\" is basically the theme of "
"this whole project, honestly.  It's amazing we've discovered as much as we "
"have.\n"
"\n"
"-Neha"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/MindOverMatter/snippets/snippets_new.json
#. ~ Name of a snippet in category "lab_file_telekinesis"
#. ~ Phavian designation for telekinetic study is JUNIPER GOLD.  Phavian
#. designation for telekinetic study for use in combat is ONYX LIGHTNING
