msgid "notes about the cryptid"
msgid_plural "notes about the cryptids"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_lore.json
#. ~ Description of "notes about the cryptid"
msgid ""
"The notes you have taken about the cryptid you're hunting.\n"
"Also known as the mongolian death worm, the Olgoi-khorkhoi is a massive "
"acid-spewing burrowing worm.  Finding acid-resistant gear will prove useful "
"to survive the encounter.  According to most of the credible stories you've "
"read, the lethal poison covering its skin is nothing but exaggerations."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_lore.json
#. ~ Description of "notes about the cryptid"
msgid ""
"The notes you have taken about the cryptid you're hunting.\n"
"The man of the Nineteenth Hour is peaceful for most of the day but becomes "
"incredibly violent against those who are still awake when he enters his "
"active phase.  Some stories tell that his presence shields those who are "
"sleeping against everything that could disturb their sleep."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_lore.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "old leather-bound journal"
msgid_plural "old leather-bound journal"
msgstr[0] "vieux journal relié en cuir"
msgstr[1] "vieux journaux reliés en cuir"
msgstr[2] "vieux journaux reliés en cuir"

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_lore.json
#. ~ Description of "old leather-bound journal"
msgid ""
"This handwritten book contains the detailed yet disorganized notes of a "
"vampire who found how to consume other vampires for power.  Reading it might "
"tell you how to do it, if it is what you want."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_recipes.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Report: LAUGHING DANCER metallurgy"
msgid_plural "copies of Report: LAUGHING DANCER metallurgy"
msgstr[0] "copie du Rapport : LAUGHING DANCER métallurgie"
msgstr[1] "copies du Rapport : LAUGHING DANCER métallurgie"
msgstr[2] "copies du Rapport : LAUGHING DANCER métallurgie"

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/book_recipes.json
#. ~ Description of "Report: LAUGHING DANCER metallurgy"
msgid ""
"A series of documents discussing the properties of the armor and weapons used "
"by a group or organization only referred to as \"LAUGHING DANCER\".  Some of "
"these described specifications don't seem physically possible."
msgstr ""
"Une série de documents discutant des propriétés des armures et des armes "
"utilisées par un groupe ou une organisation uniquement désigné sous le nom de "
"'LAUGHING DANCER'. Certaines de ces spécifications ne semblent pas "
"physiquement possibles."

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Esoteric Investigations Weekly"
msgid_plural "issues of Esoteric Investigations Weekly"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "Esoteric Investigations Weekly"
msgid ""
"A magazine for occult investigators.  These types of magazines proliferated "
"in the decade prior to the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Noon"
msgid_plural "issues of The Noon"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "The Noon"
msgid ""
"A tabloid paper with a rather unusually out-of-this-world articles even for "
"tabloids' standard, ranging from something like an article about morticians "
"selling the deceased's 'dreams' to the government to a sensational headline "
"about a half-bat half-human boy causing 40-car pileup in the highway while "
"driving away from police pursuit.  While most thought of The Noon as an "
"amusing but otherwise mostly fake news paper in the past, the Cataclysm might "
"bring the articles' presumably fake facts to light."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Holmesian Guide to Magickal Practice"
msgid_plural "copies of The Holmesian Guide to Magickal Practice"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "The Holmesian Guide to Magickal Practice"
msgid ""
"It's big and heavy, but full of great information about esoteric "
"investigations."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Scraggy-Boo and the Mystery Crew"
msgid_plural "copies of Scraggy-Boo and the Mystery Crew"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "Scraggy-Boo and the Mystery Crew"
msgid ""
"A guide for teens interested in pursuing occult knowledge.  Readers often "
"speak of encountering a guide in their dreams of a Russian Sheepdog, who "
"introduces himself as Scraggy-Boo."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Escaping the Black Iron Prison"
msgid_plural "copies of Escaping the Black Iron Prison"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "Escaping the Black Iron Prison"
msgid ""
"A hardbound book detailing numerous rituals and thought modifications in "
"order to teach its readers how to break the shackles of mundanity."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Out-of-place manuscript"
msgid_plural "Out-of-place manuscript"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "Out-of-place manuscript"
msgid ""
"This book always feels like it shouldn't be where it is.  Its texts are "
"incoherent and illogical, but they promise to help you understand something.  "
"Reading a few words from its pages is enough to give you a headache."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Lies"
msgid_plural "copies of Lies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Description of "Lies"
msgid ""
"A haphazardly-written book filled with ramblings about something it calls "
"\"the Lies\".  You feel threatened by this book, uneasy at the thought of "
"having it on your person, but parsing its texts could give you insight on how "
"things truly are.\n"
"Only the first third of the pages are filled with text, and the last written "
"page is splattered in red."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_READ_BOOK_LIES"
msgid "Fortunately, you lack the deductive abilities to understand this book."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_READ_BOOK_LIES_REAL"
msgid "You begin your read, for better or worse."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_READ_BOOK_LIES_REAL"
msgid "Rejoice, for you have no reason to read this book anymore."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in effect in EoC
#. "EOC_DEDUCTION_FROM_BOOK_LIES"
msgid ""
"You gained almost no knowledge from this session.  Maybe if you read more, "
"you will gain more."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in effect in EoC
#. "EOC_DEDUCTION_FROM_BOOK_LIES"
msgid "You gained a decent amount of knowledge from this read."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/items/books_deduction.json
