#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_meeting1>"
msgid ""
"*, your old friend, looks up at you in shock.  At his feet lies a corpse, its "
"head almost completely blown off by the shotgun that drops limply from Liam's "
"fingers as you approach.  \"I swear, dude, this is not what it looks like.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Not what it looks like?  It looks like you just blew someone's head off, "
"Liam.  Holy shit, is that… Chris?  Did you kill Chris?"
msgstr ""
"Ce n'est pas ce que je crois?  On dirait que tu viens d'exploser la tête de "
"quelqu'un, Liam.  Putain de merde, c'est… Chris?  Tu as tué Chris?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No!  Dammit, no!\"  Liam looks briefly panicked, then his eyes widen.  \"I "
"have something for this, hold on.\"  He reaches to the sofa behind him, "
"slowly, keeping his hands away from the shotgun on the floor.  \"Look.  Chris "
"left a note.\"  Liam holds up the paper, in Chris' clear handwriting.  You "
"can just make it out: it reads somewhat like a suicide note, and realization "
"starts to dawn.  Liam nods, seeing you start to understand.  \"Chris got bit "
"while we were on our way here.  We tried to treat it, I did everything I "
"could think of, but the infection got worse and worse.  Chris told me to just "
"turn my back, but I couldn't do that.  We had a pact.  You know that.\"  "
"Liam's eyes are red rimmed, and he wipes them with a sleeve.  \"I stayed here "
"until… until the transition.  We wrote this letter and a bunch more, stuff "
"for Chris's family, if we can find them, you know?"
msgstr ""
"Non!  Bon sang, non!»  Liam semble brièvement paniqué, puis ses yeux "
"s'écarquillent.  «J'ai quelque chose pour ça, attends.»  Il tend le bras vers "
"le canapé derrière lui, lentement, en gardant ses mains éloignées du fusil à "
"pompe posé sur le sol.  «Regarde. Chris a laissé un mot.»  Liam tend le "
"papier, écrit de la main de Chris.  Vous pouvez juste la déchiffrer: elle "
"ressemble à une lettre de suicide, et vous commencez à prendre conscience de "
"la situation.  Liam acquiesce, voyant que vous commencez à comprendre.  "
"«Chris s'est fait mordre alors que nous étions en route.  On a essayé de le "
"soigner, j'ai fait tout ce que j'ai pu, mais l'infection s'est aggravée.  "
"Chris m'a dit de lui tourner le dos, mais je ne pouvais pas le faire.  Nous "
"avions un pacte.  Tu le sais.»  Les yeux de Liam sont cerclés de rouge et il "
"les essuie d'un revers de manche.  «Je suis resté ici jusqu'à... jusqu'à la "
"transition.  On a écrit cette lettre et un tas d'autres, des trucs pour la "
"famille de Chris, si on peut les trouver, tu vois?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So Chris turned into a zombie right in front of you?"
msgstr "Chris s'est donc transformé en zombie devant toi?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Wait.  Zombies?  I knew things were going to shit, but are you telling me "
"it's really zombies?"
msgstr ""
"Attends.  Des zombies?  Je savais que les choses allaient mal, mais tu es en "
"train de me dire que c'est vraiment des zombies?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.\"  Liam wipes his face again, and flops down on the couch.  \"I thought "
"there'd be more time between passing out and getting back up, I was going to "
"do this outside.  God damn, that was the hardest thing I've ever done.\"  He "
"looks up at you, his face drained, across the body of one of your oldest "
"friends.  \"Fucking hell.  You're alive.  You made it here.  I'm sorry for "
"the rough introduction, I should be hugging you right now.  You're not bit or "
"anything?"
msgstr ""
"Oui.\"  Liam s'essuie à nouveau le visage et s'écroule sur le canapé.  \"Je "
"pensais qu'il y aurait plus de temps entre l'évanouissement et le corps se "
"relevant, j'allais faire ça dehors.  Bon sang, c'est la chose la plus "
"difficile que j'aie jamais faite.\"  Il vous regarde, le visage vidé, à "
"travers le corps d'un de vos plus vieux amis.  \"Putain de merde.  Tu es "
"vivant·e.  Tu as réussi à venir ici.  Je suis désolé pour cette introduction "
"brutale, je devrais être en train de te serrer dans mes bras.  Tu n'es pas "
"mordu·e ou quoi que ce soit d'autre?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I'm fine.  Want to get this cleaned up?"
msgstr "Non, ça va. Tu veux qu'on nettoie ça?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Bit?  Like, the whole classic 'one bite and you're done' zombie movie stuff?"
msgstr ""
"Une morsure?  Comme le genre de \"une morsure et c'est fini\" des films de "
"zombies classiques?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah.  You probably heard some wacky shit on the news, hey?  I heard all "
"kinds of garbage, anything from evil mushrooms to interdimensional monsters, "
"but no.  It's zombies, classic fucking zombies.  I'm still struggling with it "
"myself."
msgstr ""
"Oui, c'est vrai.  Tu as probablement entendu des trucs bizarres aux infos, "
"hein?  J'ai entendu toutes sortes de conneries, des champignons maléfiques "
"aux monstres interdimensionnels, mais non.  Ce sont des zombies, des putains "
"de zombies classiques.  J'ai encore du mal à m'y faire moi-même."

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You got it.  I know, it feels really contrived, doesn't it?  It's exactly "
"like the old movies in every way, like someone had designed it to be.  I "
"don't know if it's every bite or what, but Chris just had one that barely "
"broke the skin and you see where that ended up.  Took about three days.  My "
"advice is, we don't let these things teeth anywhere near our skin.  They're "
"pretty clumsy bastards, though.  They definitely can't just nibble you as "
"they go by, they've gotta grab you first.  Unfortunately, seems like they're "
"pretty fuckin' good at that.  Once you get grabbed, best bet is to go full "
"ham on the zombie grabbing you with everything you've got, and try to shake "
"loose, but honestly it's better to not get grabbed."
msgstr ""
"Tu comprends.  Je sais, ça semble vraiment inventé, n'est-ce pas?  C'est "
"exactement comme dans les vieux films, comme si quelqu'un l'avait conçu.  Je "
"ne sais pas si c'est à chaque morsure ou quoi, mais Chris en avait une qui a "
"à peine percé la peau et tu vois où ça a fini.  Cela a pris environ trois "
"jours.  Mon conseil est de ne pas laisser ces choses s'approcher de notre "
"peau.  Ce sont des bâtards assez maladroits.  Ils ne peuvent pas se contenter "
"de te mordre au passage, il faut d'abord qu'ils t'attrapent.  "
"Malheureusement, il semble qu'ils soient très doués pour cela.  Une fois que "
"tu as été attrapé·e, le mieux est de t'acharner sur le zombie qui t'attrape "
"avec tout ce que tu as, et d'essayer de te libérer, mais honnêtement, c'est "
"mieux de ne pas être attrapé·e."

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, no bites.  I'm fine.  Want to get this cleaned up?"
msgstr "Pas de morsure.  Je vais bien.  Tu veux qu'on nettoie ça?"

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*lets out a long sigh and nods.  \"Let's get poor Chris outside for a proper "
"burial to start.  I can't tell you how glad I am to see you.\""
msgstr ""
"*Il pousse un long soupir et acquiesce.  \"Emmenons Chris dehors pour qu'il "
"soit enterré comme il se doit.  Je ne peux pas te dire à quel point je suis "
"content de te voir.\""

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm glad to see you too, Liam.  Wish it was a better situation.  Let's do "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Je suis content·e de te voir aussi, Liam.  J'aimerais que la situation soit "
"meilleure.  Allons-y."

#: data/mods/classic_zombies/npcs/liam_follower.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<talk_snippet_modded_liam_Friends4ever>"
msgid ""
"Aww, of course.  No matter what happens, you're always you and I'm always me, "
"right?  We've been through worse than this.\"  He pauses, his brow furrowed.  "
"\"Well, okay, maybe we haven't.  But we've stuck through it all for so many "
"years, what's a little undead apocalypse gonna change?  Hell, I think we're "
"in for one of those classic buddy-buddy zombie movie experiences, like, uh, "
"Dawn of the Dead.\"  He pauses.  \"Maybe not that one.  Night of the Living "
"Dead?\"  He pauses again.  \"Zombieland, maybe.  Who cares.  You're my "
"family, more than my birth family ever was."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Dark Days Ahead"
msgstr "Dark Days Ahead"

#: data/mods/dda/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Dark Days Ahead"
msgid "Core content for Cataclysm-DDA"
msgstr "Contenu principal pour Cataclysm-DDA"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Tutorial"
msgid "Tutorial for Cataclysm-DDA"
msgstr "Tutoriel pour Cataclysm-DDA"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "dummy"
msgid_plural "dummies"
msgstr[0] "mannequin d'entraînement"
msgstr[1] "mannequins d'entraînement"
msgstr[2] "mannequins d'entraînement"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Description of monster "dummy"
msgid "This dummy serves for only one purpose - to teach players how to hit monsters."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/monsters.json
#. ~ Death message of monster "dummy"
#, c-format
msgid "The %s is destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/overmap_terrain.json
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
msgid "tutorial room"
msgstr "pièce du tutorial"

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Welcome to the Cataclysm tutorial!  As you play, pop-ups like this one will "
"appear to guide you through the basic game actions.\n"
"\n"
"At any time, you can press <keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Keybindings menu</color> to view or modify the controls for "
"the game or specific menu that you are in.\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <keybind:POPUP_WAIT:QUIT> will close the pop-up."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The character in the center of the screen represents you.  By default, you "
"can move around using the <color_yellow>numpad</color>, "
"<color_yellow>vikeys</color>, or the <color_yellow>arrow keys</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Movement Controls:\n"
"North: <keybind:UP>\n"
"South: <keybind:DOWN>\n"
"West: <keybind:LEFT>\n"
"East: <keybind:RIGHT>\n"
"Northwest: <keybind:LEFTUP>\n"
"Northeast: <keybind:RIGHTUP>\n"
"Southwest: <keybind:LEFTDOWN>\n"
"Southeast: <keybind:RIGHTDOWN>\n"
"Wait in place: <keybind:pause>\n"
"\n"
"You can also use <keybind:SELECT> to select the location you want to move, "
"and then press it again to confirm the movement.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the door to the east."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You're standing next to a closed door.  To open it, either walk into it, or "
"press <keybind:open> and then a movement key.  Using <keybind:open> will also "
"let you open windows, gates, fences, safes and more."
msgstr ""
"Vous êtes à côté d'une porte fermée. Pour l'ouvrir, marcher simplement à "
"travers ou appuyez sur <keybind:open> puis une touche directionnelle. "
"Utiliser <keybind:open> vous permet aussi d'ouvrir fenêtres, portails, "
"barrières, coffre-forts et un bon nombre d'autres choses."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can close an opened door by pressing <keybind:close> and then a movement "
"key.  Closing doors behind you can often slow down crowds of monsters greatly."
msgstr ""
"Vous pouvez fermer une porte ouverte en appuyant sur <keybind:close> puis sur "
"une touche de mouvement pour choisir la case sur laquelle la porte est "
"présente. Fermer une porte derrière vous ralentira la plupart des "
"poursuivants."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Most monsters will have to smash their way through a closed door.  If a door "
"is locked or partially broken, you can smash it by pressing <keybind:smash> "
"and then a movement key."
msgstr ""
"La plupart des monstres ne sont pas assez intelligent pour ouvrir une porte "
"et devront la détruire pour passer. Si la porte est verrouillée ou bloquée, "
"vous pouvez la détruire en appuyant sur <keybind:smash> puis une touche de "
"mouvement pour choisir quelle case vous voulez frapper."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can smash through windows by pressing <keybind:smash> and then a movement "
"key.  A smashed window takes a long time to climb through, and it's possible "
"to hurt yourself on the broken glass, but it's a good last-ditch escape "
"route.  Smashing a broken window again will clear the glass so you can move "
"through it safely, although it will still be quite slow.  Almost everything "
"can be smashed, given you have enough strength or are doing enough damage."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just stepped on a space with one or more items.  If you wish to pick it "
"up, press <keybind:pickup>.  To select the tile directly underneath you, "
"press <keybind:pause>.\n"
"\n"
"In the <color_light_cyan>Pickup</color> menu, press:\n"
"<keybind:RIGHT> to select the items you wish to pick up\n"
"<keybind:LEFT> to deselect\n"
"<keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm\n"
"\n"
"Note that you don't need to stand directly on the space with items to pick "
"them up, you can pick them up when standing near them.\n"
"\n"
"If the item is too big to fit in any of your pockets, or is a weapon that you "
"want to wield, you can press <keybind:wield> to wield it from the ground or "
"from the <color_light_cyan>Pickup</color> menu.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please pick up the <color_light_cyan>baseball "
"bat</color> you're standing on and move to the door to the south."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"There is a display rack next to you with a steel spear lying on it.  You can "
"press <keybind:wield> to directly wield an item, without the need of picking "
"it up first.  Pressing <keybind:wield> will open the <color_light_cyan>Wield "
"item</color> menu.  Select the item you want to wield and confirm by pressing "
"<keybind:CONFIRM>.\n"
"\n"
"As you have no free space in your inventory, you will have to drop the "
"<color_light_cyan>baseball bat</color> on the ground before you can wield the "
"spear.\n"
"\n"
"If you wish to free your hands (i.e. wield nothing), press <keybind:wield> "
"and select your currently wielded item.  Alternatively, you could drop the "
"wielded item by pressing <keybind:drop> and selecting your currently wielded "
"item.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please wield the spear and move to the counters "
"west of you."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a type of clothing!  To wear clothing, press "
"<keybind:wear> and then select an item.  To take off clothing, press "
"<keybind:take_off>, or simply take it off and drop it in one action by "
"pressing <keybind:drop>."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a good weapon!  To wield a weapon, press "
"<keybind:wield>, then pick what to wield.  To wield nothing, either drop your "
"weapon with <keybind:drop>, or press <keybind:wield> to put it away."
msgstr ""
"L'objet que vous venez de ramasser est une bonne arme!  Pour manier une arme, "
"appuyez sur <keybind:wield> puis choisissez ce que vous voulez manier.  Pour "
"ne rien tenir, poser votre arme au sol en appuyant sur <keybind:drop> ou sur "
"<keybind:wield> pour la ranger dans votre inventaire."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a comestible!  To eat a comestible, press "
"<keybind:eat>.  Comestibles are items you can use up, like food, drink, "
"pills, etc.  Most food expires eventually, so be careful.  Some comestibles, "
"especially drugs, can cause subtle, long-term effects."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a tool!  To activate a tool, press "
"<keybind:apply>.  Some tools have a set charge, which can be reloaded once "
"depleted.  Others are single-use items, and still others are reusable."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is a firearm!  Guns are very powerful weapons but "
"they require ammunition.  Firearms have many special attributes.  Most modify "
"the damage done by their ammunition.  They also have dispersion, which "
"affects their chance to hit.  Some guns are semi-automatic, while others can "
"fire a burst.  Some firearms (mainly bows and other muscle-powered weapons) "
"have a range, which is added on top of the ammo's range when firing."
msgstr ""
"L'objet que vous venez de ramasser est une arme à feu! Les armes à feu sont "
"très puissantes mais nécessitent des munitions. Les armes à feu ont de "
"nombreux attributs. La plupart modifient les dommages causés par les "
"munitions. Elles ont aussi une dispersion, qui affecte la chance de toucher. "
"Certaines armes sont semi-automatique, tandis que d'autres peuvent tirer des "
"rafales. Certaines armes à feu (principalement les arcs et autres armes qui "
"fonctionnent par vos muscles) ont une portée qui est ajoutée à la portée des "
"munitions."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"The item you just picked up is ammunition, used with a gun.  It has many "
"special attributes.  The damage value is the maximum done on a standard hit; "
"a critical hit or headshot will do much more damage.  Some monsters or NPCs "
"will wear armor which reduces the damage from gunfire; a high armor-pierce "
"value will reduce this effect.  The range is the maximum range the ammo can "
"achieve, and the dispersion affects its chance to hit."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that provides physical protection.  "
"There are three types of damage that clothing defends against: "
"<color_light_cyan>bashing</color>, <color_light_cyan>cutting</color>, and "
"<color_light_cyan>ballistic</color>.  Most monsters deal bashing damage, but "
"cutting is often the more deadly of the two.  Not many enemies deal ballistic "
"damage; among them are some robots, turrets, and non-playable characters "
"(NPCs)."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that provides ample storage space.  "
"This will allow you to carry more stuff, but be aware that there is also a "
"limit on the weight you can carry which depends on your strength.  The item "
"you put on also encumbered your torso.  This will make combat a little more "
"difficult.  To check encumbrance, press <keybind:player_data>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the corridor to the north and wear "
"all clothing you find on the racks."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just put on an article of clothing that protects against the environment. "
" The most common and important are respiratory devices, which will protect "
"you against smoke, airborne toxins or organisms, and other common hazards.  "
"However, they also make it a little harder to breathe when running, so you'll "
"move more slowly.  To check your encumbrance, press <keybind:player_data>."
msgstr ""
"Vous venez d'enfiler un vêtement ou une pièce d'armure qui vous protège de "
"l'environnement. Le type le plus commun et important sont les appareils "
"respiratoires vous protégeant de la fumée, des toxines, et d'autres dangers. "
"En contre partie il est difficile de respirer en courant avec, ceci vous "
"ralentissant. Appuyez sur <keybind:player_data> pour vérifier votre niveau "
"d'encombrement."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"If you press <keybind:inventory> and then the letter of your weapon, you'll "
"see its combat stats.  Bashing damage ignores most armor, but varies greatly "
"and requires strength.  Cutting damage is a fixed amount, but is blocked by "
"armor.  The To-hit bonus affects your chances of hitting.  The amount of time "
"it takes to swing your melee weapon depends on both its size and weight; "
"small, compact weapons are the fastest."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Hitting a monster will stun it briefly, allowing you to escape or get in "
"another attack.  Your dexterity and melee skills are used to determine "
"whether an attack hits, while strength affects damage."
msgstr ""
"Toucher un monstre peut l'assomer brièvement, vous permetant de vous échapper "
"ou de lui asséner un autre coup. Votre dextérité et votre compétence de mêlée "
"déterminent vos chances de toucher, et votre force affecte la quantité de "
"dégâts produite."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Looks like you suddenly felt pain.  The pain status is indicated on the "
"sidebar and also in the <keybind:player_data> menu.\n"
"\n"
"Small amounts of pain are tolerable, but as it gets worse your stats will "
"drop and you will move much slower.  To reduce pain, take painkillers like "
"<color_light_cyan>codeine</color> on the rack nearby (by activating it with "
"<keybind:apply>), or simply wait it out."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"When you kill a monster it will often leave behind a corpse.  Corpses can be "
"important sources of food, but you must butcher them by standing on the "
"corpse and pressing <keybind:butcher>.  You'll need a bladed weapon in your "
"inventory, preferably a small, very sharp one.  An unskilled butcher may only "
"get a few pieces of meat, or none at all.  Note that many monsters, such as "
"zombies, leave tainted meat, unsuitable for consumption."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"That drug you just took is a <color_light_cyan>painkiller</color>.  "
"Painkillers are very important to keep on hand, as pain both penalizes your "
"stats and makes you slower.  Be careful though, as the stronger painkillers "
"can make you woozy, and some are even addictive.\n"
"\n"
"Please also note that painkillers don't work the moment you take them.  They "
"need some time to start working, and you don't need to take another dose "
"right now if you don't see the immediate effect.  Just wait, and sooner or "
"later the pain will start going away."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"That drug you just took placed an effect on you.  To check your effects, "
"press <keybind:player_data>.  Most only last a short while, while others, "
"like chronic disease, last until cured by some other means."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just drank a bottle of water, reducing your thirst level and reducing the "
"water level in the bottle.  You'll probably want to drop empty bottles, or "
"you might want to save them to refill from a water source later."
msgstr ""
"Vous venez de boire une bouteille d'eau, ce qui réduit votre niveau de soif "
"ainsi que le niveau d'eau de la bouteille. Vous voudrez probablement jeter "
"les bouiteilles vides, ou les garder pour les remplir plus tard."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You just activated a grenade!  You probably want to throw it.  To throw an "
"item, press <keybind:throw> and then select the item to throw.  The maximum "
"range depends on your strength and the object's weight and size.  Throwing "
"isn't very good in most combat situations, but if you've got some fire power…"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This thing here on the floor is a <color_light_cyan>trap</color>.  Traps are "
"permanent until set off, and can be an important defensive tactic, "
"particularly when sleeping in unsafe territory.  Try stepping on the bubble "
"wrap.  Don't worry, it's harmless, but it will make some noise.  There are "
"other types of traps that will cause varying amounts of damage or even "
"teleport you, so watch your step carefully."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Finally, to fire a gun, press <keybind:fire>. You'll automatically target the "
"last monster you shot at, or the closest monster to you.  You can change your "
"target with the <color_yellow>movement keys</color>, or cycle through "
"monsters with <keybind:TARGET:PREV_TARGET> and <keybind:TARGET:NEXT_TARGET>.  "
"Select the <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> as a target and press "
"<keybind:fire> to fire a single shot.  With many guns, you can change the "
"fire mode to burst or full auto by pressing <keybind:select_fire_mode>.\n"
"\n"
"There are detailed instructions on how to aim and fire in the "
"<color_light_cyan>Aiming and firing</color> menu, so make sure to check it "
"carefully.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please fire a couple of times at the dummy and move "
"to the corridor to the west."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Firing your gun will increase your recoil level.  You can see its level in "
"the <color_light_cyan>Aiming and firing</color> menu (by pressing "
"<keybind:fire>).  Generally speaking, the more damaging the ammo, the worse "
"the recoil.  Recoil severely reduces your chance to hit, but you can "
"eliminate recoil by pausing (<keybind:pause>) for a turn.  High strength "
"reduces recoil, so weak characters might want to stick to .22 or 9x19mm guns."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This is a staircase leading down.  To go downstairs, step onto the staircase "
"and press the <keybind:LEVEL_DOWN> key.  Similarly, to go upstairs, stand on "
"the staircase leading up and press the <keybind:LEVEL_UP> key."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"It's dark down here!  Without a source of light, you'll be limited to seeing "
"only one space in any direction.  You'll encounter darkness while underground "
"or at night.  Press <keybind:LEVEL_UP> to go back upstairs, and look around "
"for a flashlight."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"It's dark down here!  Fortunately, you have a "
"<color_light_cyan>flashlight</color>.  Press <keybind:apply> and then select "
"your flashlight to turn it on."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"From a water source like this, you can fill any containers you might have.  "
"Examine the dispenser by pressing <keybind:examine>.  Next, press "
"<color_yellow>'c'</color> to fill a container, then select the "
"<color_light_cyan>plastic bottle</color> to put the water into.\n"
"\n"
"The Examine command (<keybind:examine>) can be used for interacting with many "
"types of terrain and furniture.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please fill the plastic bottle with water, drink a "
"little of it (by pressing <keybind:eat> and selecting <color_light_cyan>clean "
"water</color>), and then move to the corridor to the north."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"This door is locked.  There are several ways to deal with locked doors "
"(lockpicking and prying being the most common), but right now you don't have "
"the necessary tools at hand.  Instead, you can simply bash it with your "
"<color_light_cyan>baseball bat</color> by pressing <keybind:smash> and then "
"selecting the direction.\n"
"\n"
"Note that not every door can be bashed down.  Some doors will require more "
"strength than you have or a stronger weapon.  If you're not seeing any damage "
"being done after a few swings, an alternative approach might be needed.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please smash the door."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"Bashing things is hard work that will deplete your stamina.  You can see how "
"much stamina you have on the sidebar.  The less stamina you have, the slower "
"your movement and most actions will be.  To restore stamina, you need only to "
"wait.  You can press <keybind:wait> to open the <color_light_cyan>Wait for "
"how long</color> menu and select the amount of time you want to wait.  Select "
"option <color_light_cyan>Wait until you catch your breath</color> to fully "
"restore all lost stamina.\n"
"\n"
"Be careful about doing too many strenuous activities as you will build up "
"your weariness over time, which will stack movement and action penalties on "
"top of your stamina cost.  You can watch your <color_light_cyan>Weary "
"Transition</color> in the sidebar as you are performing longer activities to "
"see their effect on  your weariness.  To reduce your weariness, you just need "
"to rest or do less strenuous activities for a while."
msgstr ""
"Frapper des choses est dur et fera baisser votre endurance. Vous pouvez voir "
"votre niveau d'endurance restante sur votre barre latérale. Moins vous avez "
"d'endurance, plus vos mouvements et la plupart des actions deviendront lents. "
"Pour récupérer votre endurance, vous n'avez besoin que d'attendre sans rien "
"faire. Vous pouvez appuyer sur <keybind:wait> pour ouvrir le menu "
"<color_light_cyan> \"Attendre pour combien de temps</color> et sélectionner "
"la durée que vous voulez attendre. Sélectionnez l'option "
"<color_light_cyan>Attendre jusqu'à ce que vous rattrapiez votre "
"souffle</color> pour récupérer toute l'endurance que vous avez perdue.\n"
"\n"
"Faites attention à ne peut en faire trop, les activité fatigantes vous "
"rendant de plus en plus épuisé(e) séparément de votre niveau d'endurance, "
"ceci ajoutant des pénalités de plus en plus écrasantes à vos mouvements et "
"actions. Vous pouvez observer votre <color_light_cyan>Niveau "
"d'Épuisement</color> sur votre barre latérale s'empirer lorsque vous "
"accomplissez des activités longues et fatigantes. Pour réduire votre niveau "
"d'épuisement, vous n'avez besoin que de vous reposer en dormant ou en "
"accomplissant des activités moins fatigantes comme la lecture."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/snippets.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "tutorial_messages"
#. ~ These use hardcoded calls
msgid ""
"You can put the <color_light_cyan>steel spear</color> in the "
"<color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> to free your hands.  Press "
"<keybind:apply> to open the <color_light_cyan>Use item</color> menu, then "
"select the spear strap, then select the spear, and finally press "
"<keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please put the <color_light_cyan>steel "
"spear</color> in the <color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> and move down the "
"corridor."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_LOOK"
msgid ""
"You can also use the mouse to see things around you.  The "
"<color_light_cyan>Mouse view</color> window will appear on the sidebar, and "
"you'll be able to get information on the terrain, monsters, and items in the "
"world around you.  Alternatively, you can press <keybind:look> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Look Around</color> window."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_MOVEMENT_MODES"
msgid ""
"Most of the time your character will be walking when you move.  But sometimes "
"it's useful to change your movement mode to something else.\n"
"\n"
"There are four movement modes:\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Walking</color>: default mode, average movement speed, "
"stamina draining speed, and noise\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Running</color>: <color_light_green>move much "
"faster</color>, but will <color_light_red>drain your stamina quickly</color>\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Crouching</color>: will make your character "
"<color_light_green>less visible to monsters</color> by allowing you to hide "
"behind some obstacles, <color_light_red>decreased movement speed</color> and "
"<color_light_green>noise</color>\n"
"<color_light_cyan>Prone</color>: <color_light_green>even less "
"visibility</color> to monsters, <color_light_red>even less movement "
"speed</color> and <color_light_green>noise</color>\n"
"\n"
"Pressing <keybind:open_movement> will open the <color_light_cyan>Movement "
"Mode</color> menu, which allows you to switch the mode at any time.  There "
"are extra keybindings that can be set to switch to each mode individually for "
"convenience.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please move to the end of the corridor."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_MONSTER_SIGHTED"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> standing before you.  Let's attack "
"it.  To do this, simply move into it.\n"
"\n"
"After you've dealt with it, please move to the door behind it."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_REACH_ATTACK"
msgid ""
"There is another <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> standing behind the "
"counters.  Most melee weapons require standing directly adjacent to your "
"target in order to hit it.\n"
"\n"
"Fortunately, some long weapons such as spears are able to perform reach "
"attack with a range of 2 or 3, so if you have one, you don't need to climb "
"onto the counters to stand next to the dummy.  The <color_light_cyan>steel "
"spear</color> has a range of 2, so you can hit the dummy right over the "
"counters.  To use the reach attack, press the <keybind:fire> key.  Once you "
"select your target, press <keybind:CONFIRM> to confirm.\n"
"\n"
"After you've dealt with the dummy, please move to the corridor to the south."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_HOLSTERS_WEAR"
msgid ""
"Always wielding a <color_light_cyan>steel spear</color> in your hands might "
"be inconvenient.  Fortunately, there is a <color_light_cyan>spear "
"strap</color> lying on the rack nearby.  You can wear it by pressing "
"<keybind:wear>.\n"
"To take off any worn item, you can press <keybind:take_off>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please wear the spear strap."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_GUN_LOAD"
msgid ""
"In the next room you'll find a row of racks with a gun, a magazine for it, "
"and ammo for it.  To be able to fire a gun, you'll need to insert a magazine "
"with ammo in it.  Press <keybind:reload_item> to open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Reload item</color> menu and put ammo in the magazine, and "
"then press <keybind:reload_item> once again to insert a magazine into a gun.\n"
"\n"
"If you wish to unload your gun, possibly to change ammunition types, press "
"<keybind:unload>."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_INVENTORY"
msgid ""
"Cataclysm uses a container-based inventory.  Putting something into your "
"inventory requires wearing some clothing or container with pockets that are "
"big enough to hold it.  The <color_light_cyan>spear strap</color> is one "
"example of such containers.  Pockets have finite dimensions, so you can't put "
"an item that has more volume or is longer than a pocket.\n"
"\n"
"To view your inventory, press <keybind:inventory>.  You'll see that you have "
"only your worn clothes, of which only your jeans have 4 small pockets.  "
"Select your jeans and press <keybind:CONFIRM> to see their description and "
"amount of pockets.  To scroll through the description, press "
"<keybind:PAGE_UP> and <keybind:PAGE_DOWN>.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, move to the western rack and wear (<keybind:wear>) "
"the <color_light_cyan>backpack</color> to increase the available capacity of "
"your inventory."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_FLASHLIGHT"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>flashlight</color> and a "
"<color_light_cyan>medium battery</color> lying on the rack.  Flashlights are "
"very useful tools as they allow you to see in the dark.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please reload the flashlight by pressing "
"<keybind:reload_item>.  Take it with you and move to the stairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_INTERACT"
msgid ""
"There is a <color_light_cyan>water dispenser</color> around the corner.  Pick "
"up the <color_light_cyan>plastic bottle</color> from the rack and proceed to "
"the dispenser."
msgstr ""
"Il y a une <color_light_cyan>fontaine à eau</color> après le prochain coin. "
"Ramassez la <color_light_cyan>bouteille en plastique</color> laissée sur "
"l'étagère et déplacez-vous vers la fontaine."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_REMOTE_USE"
msgid ""
"A <color_light_cyan>flashlight</color> is a good thing to have, but it drains "
"its battery quickly, so it won't last very long.  A much better solution for "
"long-lasting lighting is a <color_light_cyan>gasoline lantern</color>.  "
"Reload the lantern with <color_light_cyan>gasoline</color> "
"(<keybind:reload_item>) and then activate it (<keybind:apply>) while standing "
"nearby.  A <color_light_cyan>lighter</color> will help you to fire the "
"lantern.\n"
"\n"
"Some tools (such as lamps, dehydrators, bathroom scales etc) don't need to be "
"picked up before activating and allow remote use.\n"
"\n"
"After you light the lantern, you can safely turn off your flashlight to "
"conserve its energy; the lit lantern will give you enough light for any "
"actions and will last much longer.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please light the lantern and then move to the "
"corridor to the east."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_CRAFTING_FOOD"
msgid ""
"Looks like you're hungry!  The hunger status is indicated on the sidebar.  "
"Let's make a <color_light_cyan>peanut butter sandwich</color> from "
"<color_light_cyan>peanut butter</color> and "
"<color_light_cyan>crackers</color> on the counter next to the wall.\n"
"\n"
"To make food, you need to use the <color_light_cyan>Crafting</color> menu.  "
"Press <keybind:craft> to open the menu.  Press <keybind:NEXT_TAB> and "
"<keybind:PREV_TAB> to toggle crafting categories and select the "
"<color_light_cyan>FOOD</color> category.  From there, select peanut butter "
"sandwich and press <keybind:CONFIRM> to start crafting.\n"
"\n"
"Note that you don't need to stand directly near the counter to be able to "
"craft.  The <color_light_cyan>crafting radius</color> is 6 tiles, so while "
"you're standing no farther than 6 tiles from any crafting components and "
"tools, your character is able to still get them in order to use them.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please craft the peanut butter sandwich and then "
"eat it by pressing <keybind:eat>."
msgstr ""
"On dirait que vous avez faim! Votre état de faim est indiqué sur votre barre "
"latérale. Fabriquons un <color_light_cyan>sandwich au beurre de "
"cacahuètes</color> à partir de <color_light_cyan>beurre de cacahuètes</color> "
"et des <color_light_cyan>crackers</color> présents sur le comptoir à côté du "
"mur.\n"
"\n"
"Pour fabriquer de la nourriture, vous avez besoin d'utiliser le menu de "
"<color_light_cyan>Fabrication</color>. Appuyez sur <keybind:craft> pour "
"ouvrir le menu. Appuyez sur <keybind:NEXT_TAB> et <keybind:PREV_TAB> pour "
"activer les catégories de fabrication et sélectionnez la catégorie "
"<color_light_cyan>NOURRITURE</color>. De là, sélectionner le sandwich au "
"beurre de cacahuètes et appuyez sur <keybind:CONFIRM> pour commencer à le "
"fabriquer.\n"
"\n"
"Notez que vous n'avez pas besoin de vous tenir juste à côté du comptoir pour "
"y fabriquer quelque chose, le <color_light_cyan>rayon de fabrication</color> "
"étant de 6 cases, ceci voulant dire que si vous ne vous tenez pas à plus de 6 "
"cases des ingrédients ou outils d'une recette de fabrication, votre "
"personnage est toujours capable d'y accéder.\n"
"\n"
"Pour continuer le tutoriel, veuillez fabriquer le sandwich au beurre de "
"cacahuètes puis le manger en appuyant sur <keybind:eat>."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_CONSTRUCTION"
msgid ""
"In the next room, you can find a <color_light_cyan>paint brush</color> and "
"several cans of <color_light_cyan>paint</color>.  You can use them to paint "
"the wall in your preferred color.  To do this, open the "
"<color_light_cyan>Construction</color> menu by pressing <keybind:construct> "
"and toggling the categories with <keybind:LEFT> and <keybind:RIGHT>.  Find "
"the <color_light_cyan>Decorative</color> category and select one of the "
"options to paint the wall.\n"
"\n"
"To continue the tutorial, please paint some walls and move further south."
msgstr ""
"Dans la prochaine pièce, vous trouverez un <color_light_cyan>pinceau</color> "
"et plusieurs pots de <color_light_cyan>peinture</color>. Vous pouvez utiliser "
"ces objets pour peindre le mur de votre couleur préférée. Pour faire ceci, "
"ouvrez votre menu de <color_light_cyan>Construction</color> en appuyant sur "
"<keybind:construct> et en activant les catégories en appuyant sur "
"<keybind:LEFT> et <keybind:RIGHT>. Naviguez vers la catégorie "
"<color_light_cyan>Décorations</color> et sélectionnez l'une de vos options "
"pour peindre le mur.\n"
"\n"
"Pour continuer le tutoriel, veuillez peindre quelques murs et ensuite vous "
"déplacer vers le sud."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_THROWING"
msgid ""
"There are 10 <color_light_cyan>baseballs</color> lying on the floor.  You "
"might not need all 10, or you might not have enough space in your pockets.  "
"To pick up a specific amount of items, press <keybind:pickup>, select the "
"stack of items, and type a number on the keyboard (Multiple numbers can be "
"used for large stacks).  Finish the selection with "
"<keybind:INVENTORY:TOGGLE_ENTRY>.  The cursor should change to a "
"<color_light_cyan>#</color> symbol.\n"
"\n"
"You can throw a baseball at the <color_light_cyan>dummy</color> in the end of "
"the corridor by pressing <keybind:throw>.\n"
"\n"
"To complete the tutorial, throw some baseballs at the dummy and then move to "
"the end of the corridor to the north."
msgstr ""
"Il y a 10 <color_light_cyan>balles de baseball</color> sur le sol. Vous "
"n'aurez peut être pas besoin des 10, ou vous n'avez peut être pas assez de "
"place dans vos poches. Pour ramasser un nombre spécifique d'objets, appuyez "
"sur <keybind:pickup>, sélectionnez le tas d'objets et appuyez sur un chiffre "
"(une combinaison de multiples nombres peut être utilisée pour les grands "
"nombres d'objets). Achevez la sélection en appuyant sur "
"<keybind:INVENTORY:TOGGLE_ENTRY>. Le curseur devrait changer vers le symbole "
"suivant <color_light_cyan>#</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Vous pouvez jeter une balle de baseball vers le "
"<color_light_cyan>mannequin</color> au bout du couloir en appuyant sur "
"<keybind:throw>.\n"
"Pour compléter le tutoriel, lancez des balles de baseball sur le mannequin et "
"bouger ensuite vers la fin du couloir ou nord."

#: data/mods/dda_tutorial/traps.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_LESSON_FINALE"
msgid ""
"Congratulations!  You have completed the tutorial.  Here is some last-minute "
"advice.\n"
"\n"
"You can press <keybind:action_menu> to open the <color_light_cyan>Action "
"menu</color>.  It provides a convenient way to access various actions.\n"
"\n"
"Not sure what keys you can press in a given menu?  Press the "
"<keybind:HELP_KEYBINDINGS> to open the <color_light_cyan>Keybindings</color> "
"menu.  It allows you to view the existing keybindings and modify them to your "
"liking.  Sometimes there will be lesser used or convenience actions without a "
"default keybinding, which you can also set.\n"
"\n"
"You can continue exploring the tutorial rooms, or you can exit the tutorial "
"by pressing <keybind:save>.  This will save your game and exit to the main "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Antivirals Before You Die!"
msgstr "Trouvez des Antiviraux Avant de Mourir!"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in effect in EoC "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
#. ~ Player message in false effect in EoC "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid "You take an antiviral."
msgstr "Vous prenez un médicament antiviral."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid "You seem to be feeling a little better, but the prickling sensation remains."
msgstr ""
"Vous semblez vous sentir un peu mieux, mais la sensation de picotement "
"demeure."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid ""
"You no longer feel uncomfortably itchy, but your skin is still concerningly "
"pale."
msgstr ""
"Vous ne ressentez plus de démangeaisons inconfortables, mais votre peau est "
"toujours d'une pâleur inquiétante."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effect_on_conditions.json
#. ~ Player message in nested effect in then statement in false effect in EoC
#. "EOC_CONSUMED_ANTIVIRAL"
msgid ""
"Some of the lesions on your skin have begun to heal, but the itchiness "
"remains."
msgstr ""
"Certaines des lésions de votre peau ont commencé à guérir, mais les "
"démangeaisons persistent."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Pallor"
msgstr "Pâleur"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Itchy pale skin"
msgstr "Peau pâle et démangeante"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "zombie_virus"
msgid "Necrotic skin"
msgstr "Peau Nécrotique"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Pallor"
msgid "Your skin is pale and there are dark spots around your eyes."
msgstr "Votre peau est devenue pâle et vous avez des tâches noires dans votre vision."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Itchy pale skin"
msgid ""
"Your skin is pale and there are dark spots around your eyes.  You feel a "
"constant itching sensation, like your skin could fall off at any moment."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Necrotic skin"
msgid ""
"Your skin is pale and covered in gross sores.  It's like your skin is rotting "
"right off your body."
msgstr ""
"Votre peau est pâle et couverte de plaies suintantes. Vous avez l'impression "
"que votre peau est en train de se décomposer."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/effects.json
#. ~ Apply message of effect type "Pallor, Itchy pale skin, Necrotic skin"
msgid "An ominous prickling feeling reverberates through your body."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "antivirals"
msgid_plural "antivirals"
msgstr[0] "antiviraux"
msgstr[1] "antiviraux"
msgstr[2] "antiviraux"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ Description of "antivirals"
msgid ""
"An anti-viral medication that inhibits the development of certain viruses.  "
"One dose lasts 16 hours.  Could this, by some miracle, work against whatever "
"the zombies are carrying?"
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/items.json
#. ~ "description" action message of item "antivirals"
msgid "Reduces the effect of certain viral infections."
msgstr "Réduit les effets de certaines infections virales."

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/modinfo.json
#. ~ MOD name
msgid "Deadly Zombie Virus"
msgstr "Virus Zombie Mortel"

#: data/mods/deadly_bites/modinfo.json
#. ~ Description of MOD "Deadly Zombie Virus"
msgid ""
"Bites from zombies have a chance to inflict a permanent fatal illness.  Find "
"and consume antivirals to stave off the disease."
msgstr ""

#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_monsters.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "hook kangaroo"
msgid_plural "hook kangaroos"
msgstr[0] "kangourou raptor zombifié"
